msgid "Applications"
msgstr "Iarratais"

msgid ""
"Django contains a registry of installed applications that stores "
"configuration and provides introspection. It also maintains a list of "
"available :doc:`models </topics/db/models>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá clárlann feidhmchlár suiteáilte i Django a stórálann cumraíocht agus a "
"sholáthraíonn ionchraíocht. Coinníonn sé liosta de na samhlacha atá ar fáil "
"freisin: doc: `samhlach` </topics/db/models>."

msgid ""
"This registry is called :attr:`~django.apps.apps` and it's available "
"in :mod:`django.apps`:"
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ar an gclárlann seo: attr: `~django.apps.apps` agus tá sé ar fáil "
"in:mod: `django.apps`:"

msgid "Projects and applications"
msgstr "Tionscadail agus iarratais"

msgid ""
"The term **project** describes a Django web application. The project Python "
"package is defined primarily by a settings module, but it usually contains "
"other things. For example, when you run  ``django-admin startproject "
"mysite`` you'll get a ``mysite`` project directory that contains a "
"``mysite`` Python package with ``settings.py``, ``urls.py``, ``asgi.py`` and "
"``wsgi.py``. The project package is often extended to include things like "
"fixtures, CSS, and templates which aren't tied to a particular application."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an téarma**tionscad** cur síos ar fheidhmchlár gréasáin Django. "
"Sainmhínítear pacáiste an tionscadail Python go príomha ag modúl socruithe, "
"ach de ghnáth bíonn rudaí eile ann. Mar shampla, nuair a reáchtáil tú "
"``django-admin startproject mysite`` gheobhaidh tú eolaire tionscadail "
"``mysite`` ina bhfuil pacáiste Python ``mysite`` le `settings.py``, "
"`urls.py``, `asgi.py`` agus ``wsgi.py``. Is minic a leathnaítear an pacáiste "
"tionscadail chun rudaí cosúil le daingneáin, CSS agus teimpléid nach bhfuil "
"ceangailte le feidhmchlár áirithe a áireamh."

msgid ""
"A **project's root directory** (the one that contains ``manage.py``) is "
"usually the container for all of a project's applications which aren't "
"installed separately."
msgstr ""
"Is iondúil gurb é fréamhsheoltóir tionscadail** (an ceann ina bhfuil "
"`manage.py` ') an coimeádán d'iarratais uile tionscadail nach bhfuil "
"suiteáilte ar leithligh."

msgid ""
"The term **application** describes a Python package that provides some set "
"of features. Applications :doc:`may be reused </intro/reusable-apps/>` in "
"various projects."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an téarma**iarratas** cur síos ar phacáiste Python a sholáthraíonn "
"roinnt sraith gnéithe. Iarratais: doc: `Is féidir é a athúsáid' i "
"dtionscadail éagsúla. </intro/reusable-apps/>"

msgid ""
"Applications include some combination of models, views, templates, template "
"tags, static files, URLs, middleware, etc. They're generally wired into "
"projects with the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting and optionally with "
"other mechanisms such as URLconfs, the :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` setting, or "
"template inheritance."
msgstr ""
"I measc na bhfeidhmchláir tá teaglaim de mhúnlaí, tuairimí, teimpléid, "
"clibeanna teimpléad, comhaid statacha, URLanna, middleware, srl. De ghnáth "
"déantar iad a sreangú isteach i dtionscadail leis an socrú:: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS` agus go roghnach le meicníochtaí eile mar URLConfs, an "
"socrú: `MIDDLEWARE` nó oidhreacht teimpléad."

msgid ""
"It is important to understand that a Django application is a set of code "
"that interacts with various parts of the framework. There's no such thing as "
"an ``Application`` object. However, there's a few places where Django needs "
"to interact with installed applications, mainly for configuration and also "
"for introspection. That's why the application registry maintains metadata in "
"an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance for each installed application."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach a thuiscint gur sraith cód é feidhmchlár Django a "
"idirghníomhaíonn le codanna éagsúla den chreat. Níl aon rud den sórt sin ann "
"mar réad ``Feidhmchláir`. Mar sin féin, tá cúpla áit ann ina gcaithfidh "
"Django idirghníomhú le feidhmchláir suiteáilte, go príomha le haghaidh "
"cumraíochta agus freisin le haghaidh ionbhreithniú. Sin an fáth go "
"gcoinníonn clárlann an fheidhmchláir meiteashonraí in an:class: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig` sampla do gach feidhmchlár suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"There's no restriction that a project package can't also be considered an "
"application and have models, etc. (which would require adding it "
"to :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`)."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon srian ann nach féidir pacáiste tionscadail a mheas mar iarratas "
"freisin agus go mbeadh samhlacha aige, srl. (rud a d'éilfeadh é a chur "
"chuig: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`)."

msgid "Configuring applications"
msgstr "Iarratais a chumrú"

msgid ""
"To configure an application, create an ``apps.py`` module inside the "
"application, then define a subclass of :class:`AppConfig` there."
msgstr ""
"Chun feidhmchlár a chumrú, cruthaigh modúl ``apps.py`` taobh istigh den "
"fheidhmchlár, ansin sainmhínigh fo-aicme de:class: `AppConfig` ann."

msgid ""
"When :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains the dotted path to an application "
"module, by default, if Django finds exactly one :class:`AppConfig` subclass "
"in the ``apps.py`` submodule, it uses that configuration for the "
"application. This behavior may be disabled by "
"setting :attr:`AppConfig.default` to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"When: Setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` tá an cosán poncanach chuig modúl "
"feidhmchláir, de réir réamhshocraithe, má aimsíonn Django go díreach fo-"
"aicme ceann:class: `AppConfig` sa fho-mhodúl ``apps.py``, úsáideann sé an "
"chumraíocht sin don fheidhmchlár. Féadfar an t-iompar seo a dhíchumasú trí "
"shocrú: attr: `AppConfig.default` go ``False``."

msgid ""
"If the ``apps.py`` module contains more than one :class:`AppConfig` "
"subclass, Django will look for a single one where :attr:`AppConfig.default` "
"is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá níos mó ná fo-aicme amháin: class: `AppConfig` sa modúl ``apps.py``, "
"cuardóidh Django ceann amháin ina bhfuil: attr: `AppConfig.default` ``True``."

msgid ""
"If no :class:`AppConfig` subclass is found, the base :class:`AppConfig` "
"class will be used."
msgstr ""
"Má aimsítear fo-aicme no:class: `AppConfig`, úsáidfear an rang base: class: "
"`AppConfig`."

msgid ""
"Alternatively, :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` may contain the dotted path to a "
"configuration class to specify it explicitly::"
msgstr ""
"De rogha air sin, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh an cosán poncaithe chuig rang "
"cumraíochta ag :setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` chun é a shonrú go sainráite::"

msgid "For application authors"
msgstr "Maidir le húdair iarratais"

msgid ""
"If you're creating a pluggable app called \"Rock ’n’ roll\", here's how you "
"would provide a proper name for the admin::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá aip inphlugáilte á chruthú agat ar a dtugtar “Rock 'n' roll”, seo "
"conas a chuirfeá ainm ceart ar fáil don riarachán:"

msgid ""
"``RockNRollConfig`` will be loaded automatically "
"when :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains ``'rock_n_roll'``. If you need to "
"prevent this, set :attr:`~AppConfig.default` to ``False`` in the class "
"definition."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaítear ``RocknrollConfig`` go huathoibríoch nuai:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS` tá ```rock_n_roll'``. Más gá duit é seo a chosc, "
"socraí:attr: `~appconfig.default` go ``False`` sa sainmhíniú ranga."

msgid ""
"You can provide several :class:`AppConfig` subclasses with different "
"behaviors. To tell Django which one to use by default, "
"set :attr:`~AppConfig.default` to ``True`` in its definition. If your users "
"want to pick a non-default configuration, they must replace "
"``'rock_n_roll'`` with the dotted path to that specific class in "
"their :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat fo-aicmí roinnt: class: `AppConfig` a sholáthar le "
"hiompraíochtaí éagsúla. Chun insint do Django cén ceann atá le húsáid de "
"réir réamhshocraithe, socraí:attr: `~AppConfig.default` go ``True`` ina "
"sainmhíniú. Más mian le d'úsáideoirí cumraíocht neamh-réamhshocraithe a "
"roghnú, ní mór dóibh ``rock_n_roll'`` a chur in ionad leis an gcosán ponctha "
"chuig an rang sonrach sin ina socrú: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"The :attr:`AppConfig.name` attribute tells Django which application this "
"configuration applies to. You can define any other attribute documented in "
"the :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` API reference."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn an tréith: Attr: `AppConfig.name` do Django cén feidhmchlár a "
"bhaineann an chumraíocht seo leis. Is féidir leat aon tréith eile a "
"dhoiciméadaithe sa tagairt API: class: `~django.apps.appconfig` a shainiú."

msgid ""
":class:`AppConfig` subclasses may be defined anywhere. The ``apps.py`` "
"convention merely allows Django to load them automatically "
"when :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains the path to an application module "
"rather than the path to a configuration class."
msgstr ""
":class: Is féidir fo-aicmí `AppConfig` a shainiú áit ar bith. Ní cheadaíonn "
"an choinbhinsiún `apps.py` ach do Django iad a luchtú go huathoibríoch "
"nuai:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` tá an cosán chuig modúl feidhmchláir seachas "
"an cosán chuig rang cumraíochta."

msgid ""
"If your code imports the application registry in an application's "
"``__init__.py``, the name ``apps`` will clash with the ``apps`` submodule. "
"The best practice is to move that code to a submodule and import it. A "
"workaround is to import the registry under a different name::"
msgstr ""
"Má allmhairíonn do chód clárlann an iarratais i ``__init__.py`` iarratais, "
"beidh an t-ainm `apps`` ag teacht leis an bhfo-mhodúl ``apps``. Is é an "
"cleachtas is fearr ná an cód sin a bhogadh chuig fo-mhodúl agus é a "
"iompórtáil. Is é an réiteach ná an clárlann a iompórtáil faoi ainm difriúil::"

msgid "For application users"
msgstr "Do úsáideoirí feidhmchláir"

msgid ""
"If you're using \"Rock ’n’ roll\" in a project called ``anthology``, but you "
"want it to show up as \"Jazz Manouche\" instead, you can provide your own "
"configuration::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá “Rock 'n' roll” á úsáid agat i dtionscadal ar a dtugtar ``anthology "
"``, ach ba mhaith leat go dtaispeánfaidh sé suas mar “Jazz Manouche” ina "
"ionad sin, is féidir leat do chumraíocht féin a sholáthar:"

msgid ""
"This example shows project-specific configuration classes located in a "
"submodule called ``apps.py``. This is a convention, not a "
"requirement. :class:`AppConfig` subclasses may be defined anywhere."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an sampla seo ranganna cumraíochta sonracha tionscadail atá "
"suite i bhfo-mhodúl ar a dtugtar ``apps.py``. Is coinbhinsiún é seo, ní "
"riachtanas. :class: Is féidir fo-aicmí `AppConfig` a shainiú áit ar bith."

msgid ""
"In this situation, :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` must contain the dotted path to "
"the configuration class because it lives outside of an application and thus "
"cannot be automatically detected."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, ní mór go mbeadh an cosán poncaithe chuig an rang cumraíochta "
"ag :setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` toisc go gcónaíonn sé lasmuigh d'iarratas agus "
"dá bhrí sin ní féidir é a bhrath go huathoibríoch."

msgid "Application configuration"
msgstr "Cumraíocht feidhmchláir"

msgid ""
"Application configuration objects store metadata for an application. Some "
"attributes can be configured in :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` subclasses. "
"Others are set by Django and read-only."
msgstr ""
"Stóráil rudaí cumraíochta feidhmchláir meiteashonraí d'fheidh Is féidir "
"roinnt tréithe a chumrú in:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` fo-aicmí. Tá "
"daoine eile leagtha síos ag Django agus léite amháin."

msgid "Configurable attributes"
msgstr "tréithe inchumraithe"

msgid "Full Python path to the application, e.g. ``'django.contrib.admin'``."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán Python chuig an bhfeidhmchlár, m.sh. "
"```django.contrib.admin'``."

msgid ""
"This attribute defines which application the configuration applies to. It "
"must be set in all :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` subclasses."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an tréith seo cén feidhmchlár a bhaineann an chumraíocht leis. "
"Caithfear é a shocrú i ngach:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` fo-aicmí."

msgid "It must be unique across a Django project."
msgstr "Caithfidh sé a bheith uathúil ar fud tionscadal Django."

msgid "Short name for the application, e.g. ``'admin'``"
msgstr "Ainm gearr don iarratas, m.sh. ````admin'``"

msgid ""
"This attribute allows relabeling an application when two applications have "
"conflicting labels. It defaults to the last component of ``name``. It should "
"be a valid Python identifier."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an tréith seo feidhmchlár a athlipéadú nuair a bhíonn lipéid "
"contrártha ag dhá iarratas. Tá sé réamhshocraithe go dtí an chomhpháirt "
"deireanach de ``ainm ``. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé ina aitheantóir bailí Python."

msgid ""
"Changing this attribute after migrations have been applied for an "
"application will result in breaking changes to a project or, in the case of "
"a reusable app, any existing installs of that app. This is because "
"``AppConfig.label`` is used in database tables and migration files when "
"referencing an app in the dependencies list."
msgstr ""
"Mar thoradh ar an tréith seo a athrú tar éis imirce a chur i bhfeidhm ar "
"iarratas beidh athruithe briste ar thionscadal nó, i gcás aip in-athúsáidte, "
"aon shuiteálacha atá ann cheana den aip sin. Tá sé seo toisc go n-úsáidtear "
"``AppConfig.label`` i dtáblaí bunachar sonraí agus comhaid imirce agus tú ag "
"tagairt do aip sa liosta spleáchais."

msgid "Human-readable name for the application, e.g. \"Administration\"."
msgstr "Ainm inléite don duine don iarratas, m.sh. “Riarachán”."

msgid "This attribute defaults to ``label.title()``."
msgstr "Tá an tréith seo réamhshocraithe go ``label.title () ``."

msgid ""
"Filesystem path to the application directory, e.g. ``'/usr/lib/pythonX.Y/"
"dist-packages/django/contrib/admin'``."
msgstr ""
"Conair an chórais chomhaid chuig an eolaire feidhmchláir, m.sh. ``'/usr/lib/"
"pythonx.y/dist-packages/django/contrib/admin'``."

msgid ""
"In most cases, Django can automatically detect and set this, but you can "
"also provide an explicit override as a class attribute on "
"your :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` subclass. In a few situations this is "
"required; for instance if the app package is a `namespace package`_ with "
"multiple paths."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, is féidir le Django é seo a bhrath agus a shocrú go "
"huathoibríoch, ach is féidir leat athshlánú follasach a sholáthar mar "
"thréith ranga ar d'fho-aicme: `~django.apps.appconfig`. I gcúpla cás tá sé "
"seo ag teastáil; mar shampla más 'pacáiste spás ainmneacha`_ é an pacáiste "
"aip le cosáin iolracha."

msgid ""
"Set this attribute to ``False`` to prevent Django from selecting a "
"configuration class automatically. This is useful when ``apps.py`` defines "
"only one :class:`AppConfig` subclass but you don't want Django to use it by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an tréith seo go `False`` chun Django a chosc ó rang cumraíochta a "
"roghnú go huathoibríoch. Tá sé seo úsáideach nuair a shainmhíníonn "
"``apps.py`` ach fo-aicme amháin: class: `AppConfig` ach níl tú ag iarraidh "
"Django é a úsáid de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Set this attribute to ``True`` to tell Django to select a configuration "
"class automatically. This is useful when ``apps.py`` defines more than "
"one :class:`AppConfig` subclass and you want Django to use one of them by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an tréith seo go `True`` chun a rá le Django rang cumraíochta a "
"roghnú go huathoibríoch. Tá sé seo úsáideach nuair a shainmhíníonn "
"``apps.py`` níos mó ná fo-aicme amháin: class: `AppConfig` agus ba mhaith "
"leat Django ceann acu a úsáid de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid "By default, this attribute isn't set."
msgstr "De réir réamhshocraithe, níl an tréith seo socraithe."

msgid ""
"The implicit primary key type to add to models within this app. You can use "
"this to keep :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` as the primary key type "
"for third party applications."
msgstr ""
"An príomh-chineál eochair intuigthe le cur le samhlacha laistigh den aip "
"seo. Is féidir leat é seo a úsáid chun: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` "
"a choinneáil mar an príomhchineál eochair d'iarratais tríú páirtí."

msgid "By default, this is the value of :setting:`DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, is é seo an luach de:setting: `DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`."

msgid "Read-only attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe léite amháin"

msgid ""
"Root module for the application, e.g. ``<module 'django.contrib.admin' from "
"'django/contrib/admin/__init__.py'>``."
msgstr ""
"<module 'django.contrib.admin' from 'django/contrib/admin/__init__.py'>Modúl "
"fréimhe don fheidhmchlár, m.sh. ``."

msgid ""
"Module containing the models, e.g. ``<module 'django.contrib.admin.models' "
"from 'django/contrib/admin/models.py'>``."
msgstr ""
"<module 'django.contrib.admin.models' from 'django/contrib/admin/"
"models.py'>Modúl ina bhfuil na samhlacha, m.sh. ``."

msgid ""
"It may be ``None`` if the application doesn't contain a ``models`` module. "
"Note that the database related signals such "
"as :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` "
"and :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` are only emitted for "
"applications that have a ``models`` module."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith ``None`` mura bhfuil modúl ``samhlacha ``san "
"iarratas. Tabhair faoi deara nach n-astaítear comharthaí a bhaineann leis an "
"mbunachar sonraí mar: data: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_migrate` "
"agus:data: `~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` ach le haghaidh "
"feidhmchláir a bhfuil modúl ``models`` acu."

msgid "Methods"
msgstr "Modhanna"

msgid ""
"Returns an iterable of :class:`~django.db.models.Model` classes for this "
"application."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé athrá arís de: class: `~django.db.models.model` ranganna don "
"fheidhmchlár seo."

msgid "Requires the app registry to be fully populated."
msgstr "Éilíonn clárlann an aip a bheith daonra go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"Returns the :class:`~django.db.models.Model` with the given ``model_name``. "
"``model_name`` is case-insensitive."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé sean:class: `~django.db.models.model` leis an ``model_name`` a "
"thugtar. Tá ``model_name`` neamh-íogair ó cháis."

msgid "Raises :exc:`LookupError` if no such model exists in this application."
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe:exc: `LookuPerror` mura bhfuil samhail den sórt sin ann san "
"iarratas seo."

msgid ""
"Requires the app registry to be fully populated unless the ``require_ready`` "
"argument is set to ``False``. ``require_ready`` behaves exactly as "
"in :meth:`apps.get_model()`."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn clárlann an aip a bheith daonra go hiomlán mura bhfuil an argóint "
"`requeri_ready`` socraithe go ``False``. Iompraíonn ``requi_ready`` go "
"díreach mar atá in:meth: `apps.get_model () `."

msgid ""
"Subclasses can override this method to perform initialization tasks such as "
"registering signals. It is called as soon as the registry is fully populated."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le fo-aicmí an modh seo a shárú chun tascanna tosaithe a dhéanamh "
"mar chomharthaí a chlárú. Tugtar air chomh luath agus a bhíonn an chlárlann "
"daonra go hiomlán."

msgid ""
"Although you can't import models at the module-level "
"where :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` classes are defined, you can import "
"them in ``ready()``, using either an ``import`` statement "
"or :meth:`~AppConfig.get_model`."
msgstr ""
"Cé nach féidir leat samhlacha a iompórtáil ag an leibhéal modúl ina bhfuil "
"aicmí: class: `~django.apps.appconfig` sainmhínithe, is féidir leat iad a "
"iompórtáil i `ready () ``, ag baint úsáide as ráiteas ``import`` nó:meth: "
"`~AppConfig.get_model`."

msgid ""
"If you're registering :mod:`model signals <django.db.models.signals>`, you "
"can refer to the sender by its string label instead of using the model class "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag clárú: mod: `comharthaí samhail <django.db.models.signals>`, is "
"féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh don seoltóir trína lipéad teaghrán in ionad "
"an rang samhail féin a úsáid."

msgid "Example::"
msgstr "Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Although you can access model classes as described above, avoid interacting "
"with the database in your :meth:`ready()` implementation. This includes "
"model methods that execute queries "
"(:meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save()`, :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.delete()`, "
"manager methods etc.), and also raw SQL queries via "
"``django.db.connection``. Your :meth:`ready()` method will run during "
"startup of every management command. For example, even though the test "
"database configuration is separate from the production settings, ``manage.py "
"test`` would still execute some queries against your **production** database!"
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar ranganna samhail mar a thuairiscítear "
"thuas, seachain idirghníomhú leis an mbunachar sonraí i do chur i bhfeidhm: "
"meth: `ready () `. Áirítear leis seo modhanna samhail a fhorghníomhaíonn "
"ceisteanna (:meth: `~django.db.models.model.save () `, :meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.delete ()`, modhanna bainisteora srl.), agus "
"freisin ceisteanna SQL amh trí `django.db.connection``. Rith do mhodh: Meth: "
"`ready () `le linn tosú gach ordaithe bainistíochta. Mar shampla, cé go "
"bhfuil cumraíocht an bhunachar sonraí tástála ar leithligh ó na socruithe "
"táirgeachta, chuirfeadh ``manage.py test`` roinnt ceisteanna fós i gcoinne "
"do bhunachar sonraí **táirgeach**!"

msgid ""
"In the usual initialization process, the ``ready`` method is only called "
"once by Django. But in some corner cases, particularly in tests which are "
"fiddling with installed applications, ``ready`` might be called more than "
"once. In that case, either write idempotent methods, or put a flag on your "
"``AppConfig`` classes to prevent rerunning code which should be executed "
"exactly one time."
msgstr ""
"Sa ghnáthphróiseas tionscnaíochta, ní ghlaonn Django ar an modh `réidh ``ach "
"uair amháin. Ach i roinnt cásanna cúinne, go háirithe i dtástálacha atá ag "
"feiceáil le feidhmchláir suiteáilte, d'fhéadfaí “réidh” a ghlaoch níos mó ná "
"uair amháin. Sa chás sin, scríobh modhanna idempotent, nó cuir bratach ar "
"d'aicmí ``AppConfig` chun cosc a chur ar chód athreáchtáil ar chóir a "
"fhorghníomhú go díreach uair amháin."

msgid "Namespace packages as apps"
msgstr "Pacáistí spás ainmneacha mar aipeanna"

msgid ""
"Python packages without an ``__init__.py`` file are known as \"namespace "
"packages\" and may be spread across multiple directories at different "
"locations on ``sys.path`` (see :pep:`420`)."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar “pacáistí spás ainmneacha” ar phacáistí Python gan comhad "
"``__init__.py`` agus féadfar iad a scaipeadh ar fud eolairí iolracha ag "
"áiteanna éagsúla ar `sys.path`` (féach: pep: `420`)."

msgid ""
"Django applications require a single base filesystem path where Django "
"(depending on configuration) will search for templates, static assets, etc. "
"Thus, namespace packages may only be Django applications if one of the "
"following is true:"
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn feidhmchláir Django cosán chórais comhaid bonn amháin ina ndéanfaidh "
"Django (ag brath ar chumraíocht) cuardach ar theimpléid, sócmhainní "
"statacha, srl. Mar sin, ní fhéadfaidh pacáistí spás ainmneacha a bheith ina "
"bhfeidhmchláir Django ach má tá ceann díobh seo a leanas fíor:"

msgid ""
"The namespace package actually has only a single location (i.e. is not "
"spread across more than one directory.)"
msgstr ""
"Níl ach suíomh amháin ag an bpacáiste spás ainmneacha i ndáiríre (ie níl sé "
"scaipthe thar níos mó ná eolaire amháin.)"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` class used to configure the application "
"has a :attr:`~django.apps.AppConfig.path` class attribute, which is the "
"absolute directory path Django will use as the single base path for the "
"application."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: attr: `~django.apps.appconfig` tréith aicme: `~django.apps.appconfig` "
"a úsáidtear chun an feidhmchlár a chumrú: `~django.apps.path` tréith aicme, "
"arb é an cosán eolaire iomlán a úsáidfidh Django mar an bonn aonair don "
"fheidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"If neither of these conditions is met, Django will "
"raise :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured`."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcomhlíontar ceachtar de na coinníollacha seo, ardóidh Django: exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ImProperlyConfigured`."

msgid "Application registry"
msgstr "Clárlann iarratais"

msgid ""
"The application registry provides the following public API. Methods that "
"aren't listed below are considered private and may change without notice."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an clárlann feidhmchláir an API poiblí seo a Meastar go bhfuil "
"modhanna nach bhfuil liostaithe thíos príobháideacha agus féadfaidh siad "
"athrú gan fógra."

msgid ""
"Boolean attribute that is set to ``True`` after the registry is fully "
"populated and all :meth:`AppConfig.ready` methods are called."
msgstr ""
"Tréith Boolean atá socraithe go ``True`` tar éis don chlárlann a bheith "
"daonra go hiomlán agus tugtar gach modh: meth: `AppConfig.ready`."

msgid "Returns an iterable of :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instances."
msgstr "Filleann sé cásanna in-athraithe de:class: `~django.apps.appconfig`."

msgid ""
"Returns an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` for the application with the "
"given ``app_label``. Raises :exc:`LookupError` if no such application exists."
msgstr ""
"Tugann tuairisce:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` don iarratas leis an "
"``app_label`` a thugtar. Ardaithe:exc: `LookuPerror` mura bhfuil aon "
"fheidhmchlár den sórt sin ann."

msgid ""
"Checks whether an application with the given name exists in the registry. "
"``app_name`` is the full name of the app, e.g. ``'django.contrib.admin'``."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann an bhfuil iarratas leis an ainm tugtha sa chlárlann. Is é "
"``app_name`` ainm iomlán an aip, m.sh. ```django.contrib.admin'``."

msgid ""
"Returns the :class:`~django.db.models.Model` with the given ``app_label`` "
"and ``model_name``. As a shortcut, this method also accepts a single "
"argument in the form ``app_label.model_name``. ``model_name`` is case-"
"insensitive."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé sean:class: `~django.db.models.model` leis an ``app_label`` agus "
"``model_name`` a thugtar. Mar aicearra, glacann an modh seo le argóint "
"amháin sa fhoirm ``app_label.model_name``. Tá ``model_name`` cás-neamh-"
"íogair."

msgid ""
"Raises :exc:`LookupError` if no such application or model exists. "
"Raises :exc:`ValueError` when called with a single argument that doesn't "
"contain exactly one dot."
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe:exc: `LookuPerror` mura bhfuil aon fheidhmchlár nó samhail den sórt "
"sin ann. Ardaithe:exc: `ValueError` nuair a ghlaonn sé le argóint amháin "
"nach bhfuil ponc amháin go díreach ann."

msgid ""
"Requires the app registry to be fully populated unless the ``require_ready`` "
"argument is set to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn clárlann an aip a bheith daonra go hiomlán mura bhfuil an argóint "
"`requeri_ready`` socraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"Setting ``require_ready`` to ``False`` allows looking up models :ref:`while "
"the app registry is being populated <app-loading-process>`, specifically "
"during the second phase where it imports models. Then ``get_model()`` has "
"the same effect as importing the model. The main use case is to configure "
"model classes with settings, such as :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL`."
msgstr ""
"<app-loading-process>Má shocraíonn ``requi_ready`` go `False``, is féidir "
"samhlacha a lorg suas: ref: `agus clárlann an aip á dhaonrú `, go sonrach le "
"linn an dara céim ina n-allmhairíonn sé samhlacha. Ansin tá an éifeacht "
"chéanna ag ``get_model () ``agus an tsamhail a allmhairiú. Is é an "
"príomhchás úsáide ná ranganna samhail a chumrú le socruithe, mar "
"shampla:setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL`."

msgid ""
"When ``require_ready`` is ``False``, ``get_model()`` returns a model class "
"that may not be fully functional (reverse accessors may be missing, for "
"example) until the app registry is fully populated. For this reason, it's "
"best to leave ``require_ready`` to the default value of ``True`` whenever "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Nuair is é ``requi_ready`` `False``,, get_model () ``filleann ``get_model "
"()`` aicme samhail nach bhféadfadh a bheith feidhmiúil go hiomlán "
"(d'fhéadfadh rochtainí droim a bheith in easnamh, mar shampla) go dtí go "
"mbeidh clárlann an aip daonra go hiomlán. Ar an gcúis seo, is fearr "
"``requi_ready`` a fhágáil go luach réamhshocraithe ``True`` nuair is féidir."

msgid "Initialization process"
msgstr "Próiseas tionscnaíochta"

msgid "How applications are loaded"
msgstr "Conas a luchtaítear feidhmchláir"

msgid ""
"When Django starts, :func:`django.setup()` is responsible for populating the "
"application registry."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thosaíonn Django, :func: `django.setup () `atá freagrach as clárlann "
"an fheidhmchláir a líonadh."

msgid "Configures Django by:"
msgstr "Cumraíonn Django ag:"

msgid "Loading the settings."
msgstr "Ag luchtú na socruithe."

msgid "Setting up logging."
msgstr "Logáil a chur ar bun."

msgid ""
"If ``set_prefix`` is True, setting the URL resolver script prefix "
"to :setting:`FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME` if defined, or ``/`` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``set_prefix`` Fíor, socraigh an réimír script réiteach URL "
"to:setting: `FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME` má tá sé sainmhínithe, nó ``/`` ar shlí eile."

msgid "Initializing the application registry."
msgstr "An clárlann iarratais a thionscnamh."

msgid "This function is called automatically:"
msgstr "Tugtar an feidhm seo go huathoibríoch:"

msgid "When running an HTTP server via Django's ASGI or WSGI support."
msgstr ""
"Agus freastalaí HTTP á reáchtáil agat trí thacaíocht ASGI nó WSGI Django."

msgid "When invoking a management command."
msgstr "Agus ordú bainistíochta á ghairm agat."

msgid ""
"It must be called explicitly in other cases, for instance in plain Python "
"scripts."
msgstr ""
"Caithfear é a ghlaoch go sainráite i gcásanna eile, mar shampla i "
"scripteanna Python simplí."

msgid ""
"The application registry is initialized in three stages. At each stage, "
"Django processes all applications in the order of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear clárlann an iarratais a thionscnamh i dtrí chéim. Ag gach céim, "
"próiseálann Django gach feidhmchlár san ordó:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "First Django imports each item in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr "Allmhairíonn Django ar dtús gach mír in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"If it's an application configuration class, Django imports the root package "
"of the application, defined by its :attr:`~AppConfig.name` attribute. If "
"it's a Python package, Django looks for an application configuration in an "
"``apps.py`` submodule, or else creates a default application configuration."
msgstr ""
"Más rang cumraíochta feidhmchláir é, allmhairíonn Django pacáiste fréimhe an "
"fheidhmchláir, atá sainmhínithe ag a tréith: attr: `~AppConfig.name`. Más "
"pacáiste Python é, lorgaíonn Django cumraíocht feidhmchláir i bhfo-mhodúl "
"`apps.py`, nó cruthaíonn sé cumraíocht feidhmchláir réamhshocraithe eile."

msgid "*At this stage, your code shouldn't import any models!*"
msgstr "* Ag an gcéim seo, níor chóir do chód aon mhúnlaí a iompórtáil! *"

msgid ""
"In other words, your applications' root packages and the modules that define "
"your application configuration classes shouldn't import any models, even "
"indirectly."
msgstr ""
"Is é sin le rá, níor cheart do phacáistí fréimhe d'iarratais agus na modúil "
"a shainmhíníonn do ranganna cumraíochta feidhmchláir aon mhúnlaí a "
"allmhairiú, fiú"

msgid ""
"Strictly speaking, Django allows importing models once their application "
"configuration is loaded. However, in order to avoid needless constraints on "
"the order of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, it's strongly recommended not import "
"any models at this stage."
msgstr ""
"Go docht, ceadaíonn Django samhlacha a allmhairiú nuair a luchtar a "
"gcumraíocht feidhmchlá Mar sin féin, d'fhonn srianta gan ghá a sheachaint ar "
"an ord de:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, moltar go láidir gan aon mhúnlaí a "
"allmhairiú ag an gcéim seo."

msgid ""
"Once this stage completes, APIs that operate on application configurations "
"such as :meth:`~apps.get_app_config()` become usable."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh an chéim seo críochnaithe, éiríonn APIs a oibríonn ar "
"chumraíochtaí feidhmchláir mar: meth: `~apps.get_app_config () `inúsáidte."

msgid ""
"Then Django attempts to import the ``models`` submodule of each application, "
"if there is one."
msgstr ""
"Ansin déanann Django iarracht an fo-mhodúl ``samhlacha ``de gach feidhmchlár "
"a allmhairiú, má tá ceann ann."

msgid ""
"You must define or import all models in your application's ``models.py`` or "
"``models/__init__.py``. Otherwise, the application registry may not be fully "
"populated at this point, which could cause the ORM to malfunction."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór duit na samhlacha go léir i `models.py`` nó ``models/__init__.py`` "
"d'iarratais a shainiú nó a allmhairiú. Seachas sin, b'fhéidir nach mbeadh an "
"chlárlann iarratais daonra go hiomlán ag an bpointe seo, rud a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith ina chúis le mífhe"

msgid ""
"Once this stage completes, APIs that operate on models such "
"as :meth:`~apps.get_model()` become usable."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh an chéim seo críochnaithe, éiríonn APIs a oibríonn ar mhúnlaí "
"mar: meth: `~apps.get_model () `inúsáidte."

msgid ""
"Finally Django runs the :meth:`~AppConfig.ready()` method of each "
"application configuration."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh ritheann Django an modh: meth: `~AppConfig.ready () `de gach "
"cumraíocht feidhmchláir."

msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr "Fabhtcheartú"

msgid ""
"Here are some common problems that you may encounter during initialization:"
msgstr ""
"Seo roinnt fadhbanna coitianta a d'fhéadfadh teacht ort le linn tionscnaimh:"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.exceptions.AppRegistryNotReady`: This happens when "
"importing an application configuration or a models module triggers code that "
"depends on the app registry."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.exceptions.AppregistryNotReady`: Tarlaíonn sé seo "
"nuair a iompórtáil cumraíocht feidhmchláir nó modúl samhlacha a spreagann "
"cód a bhraitheann ar chlárlann an aip."

msgid ""
"For example, :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext()` uses the app "
"registry to look up translation catalogs in applications. To translate at "
"import time, you need :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy()` "
"instead. (Using :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext()` would be a bug, "
"because the translation would happen at import time, rather than at each "
"request depending on the active language.)"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, :func: `~django.utils.translation.gettext () `úsáideann "
"clárlann an aip chun catalóga aistriúcháin a lorg in iarratais. Chun aistriú "
"ag am allmhairithe, ní mór duit: func: "
"`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy () `ina ionad. (Bheadh fabht ag "
"baint úsáid:func: `~django.utils.translation.gettext () `, toisc go dtarlódh "
"an t-aistriúchán ag am allmhairithe, seachas ar gach iarratas ag brath ar an "
"teanga ghníomhach.)"

msgid ""
"Executing database queries with the ORM at import time in models modules "
"will also trigger this exception. The ORM cannot function properly until all "
"models are available."
msgstr ""
"Spreagfaidh an eisceacht seo freisin fiosrúcháin bunachar sonraí a "
"fhorghníomhú leis an ORM ag am allmhairithe i modúil Ní féidir leis an ORM "
"feidhmiú i gceart go dtí go mbeidh gach samhail ar fáil."

msgid ""
"This exception also happens if you forget to call :func:`django.setup()` in "
"a standalone Python script."
msgstr ""
"Tarlaíonn an eisceacht seo freisin má dhéanann tú dearmad glaoch ar: func: "
"`django.setup () `i script Python neamhspleách."

msgid ""
"``ImportError: cannot import name ...`` This happens if the import sequence "
"ends up in a loop."
msgstr ""
"``ImportError: ní féidir ainm a allmhairiú... ``Tarlaíonn sé seo má "
"chríochnaíonn an seicheamh allmhairithe i lúb."

msgid ""
"To eliminate such problems, you should minimize dependencies between your "
"models modules and do as little work as possible at import time. To avoid "
"executing code at import time, you can move it into a function and cache its "
"results. The code will be executed when you first need its results. This "
"concept is known as \"lazy evaluation\"."
msgstr ""
"Chun deireadh a chur le fadhbanna den sórt sin, ba cheart duit spleáchais "
"idir do mhodúil samhlacha a íoslaghdú agus an oibre is lú agus is féidir a "
"dhéanamh ag am Chun an cód a fhorghníomhú ag am allmhairithe a sheachaint, "
"is féidir leat é a bhogadh isteach i bhfeidhm agus a thorthaí a Cuirfear an "
"cód i bhfeidhm nuair a theastaíonn a thorthaí uait ar dtús. Tugtar "
"“meastóireacht leisciúil” ar an gcoincheap seo."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.admin`` automatically performs autodiscovery of ``admin`` "
"modules in installed applications. To prevent it, change "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` to contain "
"``'django.contrib.admin.apps.SimpleAdminConfig'`` instead of "
"``'django.contrib.admin'``."
msgstr ""
"Déanann ``django.contrib.admin`` uathoibríoch modúil ``admin ``in iarratais "
"suiteáilte. Chun é a chosc, athraigh do th:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` chun go "
"mbeidh ```django.contrib.admin.apps.simpleAdminConfig'`` in ionad "
"``'django.contrib.admin'``."

msgid ""
"``RuntimeWarning: Accessing the database during app initialization is "
"discouraged.`` This warning is triggered for database queries executed "
"before apps are ready, such as during module imports or in "
"the :meth:`AppConfig.ready` method. Such premature database queries are "
"discouraged because they will run during the startup of every management "
"command, which will slow down your project startup, potentially cache stale "
"data, and can even fail if migrations are pending."
msgstr ""
"``RuntimeWarning: Tá sé díspreagtha ar rochtain a fháil ar an mbunachar "
"sonraí le linn tionscnaíodh aipeanna. ``Cuirtear an rabhadh seo a spreagadh "
"le haghaidh ceisteanna bunachar sonraí a fhorghníomhú sula mbeidh aipeanna "
"réidh, mar shampla le linn allmhairí modúl nó sa modh: `AppConfig.ready`. "
"Cuirtear díspreagadh ar cheisteanna bunachar sonraí roimh am den sórt sin "
"toisc go rithfidh siad le linn tosú gach ordaithe bainistíochta, rud a "
"mhoilliú ar thosú do thionscadail, a d'fhéadfadh sonraí seasta a thaisceadh, "
"agus a d'fhéadfadh go dteipeann fiú má"

msgid ""
"For example, a common mistake is making a database query to populate form "
"field choices::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, botún coitianta ná ceist bunachar sonraí a dhéanamh chun "
"roghanna réimse foirme a líonadh:"

msgid ""
"In the example above, the query from ``Country.objects.all()`` is executed "
"during module import, because the ``QuerySet`` is iterated over. To avoid "
"the warning, the form could use a :class:`~django.forms.ModelChoiceField` "
"instead::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, déantar an cheist ó `Country.Objects.all () ``a "
"fhorghníomhú le linn allmhairiú modúl, toisc go ndéantar an `QuerySet` a "
"athrá. Chun an rabhadh a sheachaint, d'fhéadfadh an fhoirm a:class: "
"`~django.forms.ModelChoiceField` a úsáid ina ionad:"

msgid ""
"To make it easier to find the code that triggered this warning, you can make "
"Python :ref:`treat warnings as errors <python:warning-filter>` to reveal the "
"stack trace, for example with ``python -Werror manage.py shell``."
msgstr ""
"Chun é a dhéanamh níos éasca an cód a spreag an rabhadh seo a aimsiú, is "
"féidir leat Python: ref: `rabhaidh a chóireáil mar earráidí <python:warning-"
"filter>`chun an rian cruach a nochtadh, mar shampla le ``python -Werror "
"manage.py shell``."

msgid "System check framework"
msgstr "Creat seiceála an chórais"

msgid ""
"The system check framework is a set of static checks for validating Django "
"projects. It detects common problems and provides hints for how to fix them. "
"The framework is extensible so you can easily add your own checks."
msgstr ""
"Is sraith seiceálacha statacha é creat seiceála an chórais chun tionscadail "
"Django a bhailíochtú. Braithíonn sé fadhbanna coitianta agus soláthraíonn sé "
"leideanna maidir le conas iad a shocrú. Tá an creat inleathnaithe ionas gur "
"féidir leat do sheiceálacha féin a chur leis go héasca."

msgid ""
"For details on how to add your own checks and integrate them with Django's "
"system checks, see the :doc:`System check topic guide </topics/checks>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas do sheiceálacha féin a chur leis agus iad "
"a chomhtháthú le seiceálacha córais Django, féach in:doc: `Treoir ábhair "
"seice</topics/checks> ála córas`."

msgid "API reference"
msgstr "Tagairt API"

msgid "``CheckMessage``"
msgstr "``Seiceachtaireacht ``"

msgid ""
"The warnings and errors raised by system checks must be instances of "
"``CheckMessage``. An instance encapsulates a single reportable error or "
"warning. It also provides context and hints applicable to the message, and a "
"unique identifier that is used for filtering purposes."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh na rabhaidh agus na hearráidí arna ardú ag seiceálacha córais a "
"bheith ina gcásanna de “seiceachtaireacht seiceála”. Cuimsíonn cás earráid "
"nó rabhadh amháin a thuairiscithe. Soláthraíonn sé comhthéacs agus leideanna "
"is infheidhme maidir leis an teachtaireacht, agus aitheantóir uathúil a "
"úsáidtear chun críocha scagtha."

msgid "Constructor arguments are:"
msgstr "Is iad na hargóintí tógála:"

msgid "``level``"
msgstr "``leibhéil ``"

msgid ""
"The severity of the message. Use one of the predefined values: ``DEBUG``, "
"``INFO``, ``WARNING``, ``ERROR``, ``CRITICAL``. If the level is greater or "
"equal to ``ERROR``, then Django will prevent management commands from "
"executing. Messages with level lower than ``ERROR`` (i.e. warnings) are "
"reported to the console, but can be silenced."
msgstr ""
"Déine na teachtaireachta. Úsáid ceann de na luachanna réamhshainithe: "
"`DEBUG`, `INFO``, `RABHADH ``, `ERROR``, `CRITICAL``. Má tá an leibhéal níos "
"mó nó comhionann le ``ERROR`, ansin cuirfidh Django cosc ar orduithe "
"bainistíochta ó fhorghníomhú. Tuairiscítear teachtaireachtaí le leibhéal "
"níos ísle ná ``ERROR`` (ie rabhaidh) don chonsól, ach is féidir iad a thostú."

msgid "``msg``"
msgstr "``msg``"

msgid ""
"A short (less than 80 characters) string describing the problem. The string "
"should *not* contain newlines."
msgstr ""
"Sreang gairid (níos lú ná 80 carachtar) ag cur síos ar an bhfadhb. Níor "
"chóir go mbeadh línte nua sa teaghrána*."

msgid "``hint``"
msgstr "```Cinn``"

msgid ""
"A single-line string providing a hint for fixing the problem. If no hint can "
"be provided, or the hint is self-evident from the error message, the hint "
"can be omitted, or a value of ``None`` can be used."
msgstr ""
"Sreang aon-líne a sholáthraíonn leid chun an fhadhb a shocrú. Mura féidir "
"aon leid a sholáthar, nó mura bhfuil an leid féin-soiléir ón teachtaireacht "
"earráide, is féidir an leid a fhágáil, nó is féidir luach ``None`` a úsáid."

msgid "``obj``"
msgstr "```Obj``"

msgid ""
"Optional. An object providing context for the message (for example, the "
"model where the problem was discovered). The object should be a model, "
"field, or manager or any other object that defines a ``__str__()`` method. "
"The method is used while reporting all messages and its result precedes the "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Rud a sholáthraíonn comhthéacs don teachtaireacht (mar shampla, an "
"tsamhail inar aimsíodh an fhadhb). Ba chóir go mbeadh an réad ina mhúnla, "
"réimse, nó bainisteoir nó aon rud eile a shainmhíníonn modh ``__str__ () `. "
"Úsáidtear an modh agus gach teachtaireacht á thuairisciú agus bíonn a "
"thoradh roimh an teachtaireacht."

msgid "``id``"
msgstr "``id``"

msgid ""
"Optional string. A unique identifier for the issue. Identifiers should "
"follow the pattern ``applabel.X001``, where ``X`` is one of the letters "
"``CEWID``, indicating the message severity (``C`` for criticals, ``E`` for "
"errors and so). The number can be allocated by the application, but should "
"be unique within that application."
msgstr ""
"Sreang roghnach. Aitheantóir uathúil don tsaincheist. Ba chóir "
"d'aitheantóirí an patrún ``Applabel.x001`` a leanúint, áit a bhfuil `X`` "
"ceann de na litreacha ``CEWID``, ag léiriú déine na teachtaireachta (``C`` "
"do chriticiúla, `E`` le haghaidh earráidí agus mar sin). Is féidir leis an "
"iarratas an uimhir a leithdháileadh, ach ba chóir go mbeadh sé uathúil "
"laistigh den iarratas sin"

msgid ""
"There are subclasses to make creating messages with common levels easier. "
"When using them you can omit the ``level`` argument because it is implied by "
"the class name."
msgstr ""
"Tá fo-ranganna ann chun teachtaireachtaí a chruthú le leibhéil choiteanna a "
"dhéanamh níos éasca. Agus iad á úsáid agat is féidir leat an argóint "
"``leibhéil ``a fhágáil toisc go bhfuil ainm an ranga intuigthe air."

msgid "Builtin tags"
msgstr "Clibeanna Builtin"

msgid "Django's system checks are organized using the following tags:"
msgstr ""
"Eagraítear seiceálacha córais Django ag baint úsáide as na clibeanna seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid "``admin``: Checks of any admin site declarations."
msgstr "``admin``: Seiceálacha ar aon dearbhú láithreáin riaracháin."

msgid "``async_support``: Checks asynchronous-related configuration."
msgstr "``async_support``: Seiceálann cumraíocht asincrónach a bhaineann leis."

msgid "``caches``: Checks cache related configuration."
msgstr "``caches``: Seiceálann cumraíocht a bhaineann le taisce."

msgid "``compatibility``: Flags potential problems with version upgrades."
msgstr ""
"``comhoiriúnacht``: Brataíonn fadhbanna féideartha le huasghrádú leagan."

msgid "``commands``: Checks custom management commands related configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``database``: Checks database-related configuration issues. Database checks "
"are not run by default because they do more than static code analysis as "
"regular checks do. They are only run by the :djadmin:`migrate` command or if "
"you specify configured database aliases using the ``--database`` option when "
"calling the :djadmin:`check` command."
msgstr ""
"``database``: Seiceálann saincheisteanna cumraíochta a bhaineann le bunachar "
"sonraí. Ní reáchtáiltear seiceálacha bunachar sonraí de réir réamhshocraithe "
"toisc go ndéanann siad níos mó ná anailís chód statach mar a dhéanann Ní "
"reáchtáiltear iad ach leis an ordú:djadmin: `migrate` nó má shonraíonn tú "
"ainmneacha bunachar sonraí cumraithe ag baint úsáide as an rogha ``--"
"database`` agus tú ag glaoch ar an ordú:djadmin: `check`."

msgid "``files``: Checks files related configuration."
msgstr "``files``: Seiceálann cumraíocht a bhaineann le comhaid."

msgid "``models``: Checks of model, field, and manager definitions."
msgstr ""
"``samhlacha ``: Seiceálacha ar shainmhínithe samhail, réimse agus "
"bainisteoir."

msgid "``security``: Checks security related configuration."
msgstr "``slándála``: Seiceálann cumraíocht a bhaineann le slándáil."

msgid "``signals``: Checks on signal declarations and handler registrations."
msgstr ""
"``comhartha``: Seiceálacha ar dhearbhuithe comhartha agus ar chlárúcháin "
"láimhseálaithe."

msgid "``sites``: Checks :mod:`django.contrib.sites` configuration."
msgstr "``sites``: Seiceálacha: MOD: cumraíocht `django.contrib.sites`."

msgid ""
"``staticfiles``: Checks :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` configuration."
msgstr ""
"``staticfiles``: Seiceálacha: MOD: cumraíocht `django.contrib.staticfiles`."

msgid "``templates``: Checks template related configuration."
msgstr "``templates``: Seiceálann cumraíocht a bhaineann le teimpléad."

msgid "``translation``: Checks translation related configuration."
msgstr "``translation``: Seiceálann cumraíocht a bhaineann le haistriúchán."

msgid "``urls``: Checks URL configuration."
msgstr "``urls``: Seiceálann cumraíocht URL."

msgid "Some checks may be registered with multiple tags."
msgstr "Is féidir roinnt seiceálacha a chlárú le clibeanna iolracha."

