msgid "Support for custom link text was added."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model reference"
msgstr "Tagairt múnla"

msgid ""
"The **models** section of the ``admindocs`` page describes each model that "
"the user has access to along with all the fields, properties, and methods "
"available on it. Relationships to other models appear as hyperlinks. "
"Descriptions are pulled from ``help_text`` attributes on fields or from "
"docstrings on model methods."
msgstr ""

msgid "A model with useful documentation might look like this::"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar mhúnla le cáipéisíocht úsáideach:"

msgid ""
"Access was restricted to only allow users with model view or change "
"permissions."
msgstr ""

msgid "View reference"
msgstr "Féach tagairt"

msgid ""
"Each URL in your site has a separate entry in the ``admindocs`` page, and "
"clicking on a given URL will show you the corresponding view. Helpful things "
"you can document in your view function docstrings include:"
msgstr ""
"Tá iontráil ar leithligh ag gach URL ar do shuíomh sa leathanach "
"`admindocs`, agus cliceáil ar URL ar leith taispeánfar an radharc "
"comhfhreagrach duit. I measc na rudaí cabhracha is féidir leat a dhoiciméadú "
"i docstrings feidhm amharc tá:"

msgid "A short description of what the view does."
msgstr "Cur síos gairid ar an méid a dhéanann an dearcadh."

msgid ""
"The **context**, or a list of variables available in the view's template."
msgstr ""
"An **comhthéacs**, nó liosta d'athróg atá ar fáil i dteimpléad an amharc."

msgid "The name of the template or templates that are used for that view."
msgstr "Ainm an teimpléid nó na teimpléid a úsáidtear don radharc sin."

msgid "Template tags and filters reference"
msgstr "Clibeanna teimpléad agus tagairt scagair"

msgid ""
"The **tags** and **filters** ``admindocs`` sections describe all the tags "
"and filters that come with Django (in fact, the :ref:`built-in tag reference "
