"MySQL, Spatialite"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``GEOMETRYCOLLECTION`` or a ``MULTI`` geometry object from the "
"geometry column. This is analogous to a simplified version of "
"the :class:`Union` aggregate, except it can be several orders of magnitude "
"faster than performing a union because it rolls up geometries into a "
"collection or multi object, not caring about dissolving boundaries."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé réad geoiméadachta ``GEOMETRYCOLLECTION`` nó réad geoiméadais "
"``MULTI`` ón gcolún geoiméadrach. Tá sé seo cosúil le leagan simplithe den "
"chomhiomlán: aicme: `Union`, ach amháin gur féidir leis a bheith roinnt "
"orduithe méide níos tapa ná aontas a dhéanamh toisc go rollaíonn sé "
"geoiméadraí i mbailiúchán nó ilréad, gan cúram faoi theorainneacha a "
"thuaslagadh."

msgid "MySQL 8.0.24+ support was added."
msgstr "Cuireadh tacaíocht MySQL 8.0.24+ leis."

msgid "``Extent``"
msgstr "``Faoi láimhse``"

msgid ""
"*Availability*: `PostGIS <https://postgis.net/docs/ST_Extent.html>`__, "
"Oracle, SpatiaLite"
msgstr ""
"< https://postgis.net/docs/ST_Extent.html>*Infhaighteacht*: `PostGIS`__, "
"Oracle, Spatialite"

msgid ""
"Returns the extent of all ``geo_field`` in the ``QuerySet`` as a 4-tuple, "
"comprising the lower left coordinate and the upper right coordinate."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais méid na `geo_field`` go léir sa ``QuerySet`` mar 4-tuple, "
"lena n-áirítear an comhordanáid íochtarach ar chlé agus an comhordanáid "
"uachtarach ar dheis."

msgid "``Extent3D``"
msgstr "``Extent3D``"

msgid "*Availability*: `PostGIS <https://postgis.net/docs/ST_3DExtent.html>`__"
msgstr ""
"< https://postgis.net/docs/ST_3DExtent.html>*Infhaighteacht*: `PostGis`__"

msgid ""
"Returns the 3D extent of all ``geo_field`` in the ``QuerySet`` as a 6-tuple, "
"comprising the lower left coordinate and upper right coordinate (each with "
"x, y, and z coordinates)."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé méid 3D gach ``geo_field`` sa `QuerySet`` mar thúpla 6, lena n-"
"áirítear an comhordanáid íochtarach ar chlé agus an comhordanáid uachtarach "
"ar dheis (gach ceann acu le comhordanáidí x, y, agus z)."

msgid "``MakeLine``"
msgstr "``Makeline``"

msgid ""
"*Availability*: `PostGIS <https://postgis.net/docs/ST_MakeLine.html>`__, "
"SpatiaLite"
msgstr ""
"< https://postgis.net/docs/ST_MakeLine.html>*Infhaighteacht*: `PostGis`__, "
"Spatialite"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``LineString`` constructed from the point field geometries in the "
"``QuerySet``. Currently, ordering the queryset has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé ``Linestring`` a tógadh ó na geoiméadrachtaí réimse pointe sa "
"``QuerySet``. Faoi láthair, níl aon éifeacht ag ordú an tacar fiosrúcháin."

msgid ""
"*Availability*: `PostGIS <https://postgis.net/docs/ST_Union.html>`__, "
"Oracle, SpatiaLite"
msgstr ""
"< https://postgis.net/docs/ST_Union.html>*Infhaighteacht*: `PostGIS`__, "
"Oracle, Spatialite"

msgid ""
"This method returns a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GEOSGeometry` object "
"comprising the union of every geometry in the queryset. Please note that use "
"of ``Union`` is processor intensive and may take a significant amount of "
"time on large querysets."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh seo a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.geosgeometry` réad a "
"chuimsíonn aontas gach geoiméadair sa tacar fiosrúcháin. Tabhair faoi deara "
"le do thoil go bhfuil úsáid “Union” dian ar phróiseálaí agus go bhféadfadh "
"sé go dtógfadh sé go leor ama ar cheisteanna móra."

msgid ""
"If the computation time for using this method is too expensive, consider "
"using :class:`Collect` instead."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an t-am ríomhaireachta chun an modh seo a úsáid ró-daor, smaoinigh ar: "
"class: `Collect` a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid ""
"*See* `OpenGIS Simple Feature Specification For SQL <https://portal.ogc.org/"
"files/?artifact_id=829>`_, at Ch. 2.1.13.2, p. 2-13 (The Dimensionally "
"Extended Nine-Intersection Model)."
msgstr ""
"* Féach* Sonraíocht Gné Simplí OpenGIS Do SQL`_ < https://portal.ogc.org/"
"files/?artifact_id=829>, ag Ch. 2.1.13.2, lch. 2-13 (An tSamhail Crossnódh "
"Naoi Leathnaithe Toiseach)."

msgid ""
"*See* `SDO_RELATE documentation <https://docs.oracle.com/en/ database/oracle/"
"oracle-database/18/spatl/spatial-operators-reference.html# GUID-97C17C18-"
"F05E-49B4-BE11-E89B972E2A02>`_, from the Oracle Spatial and Graph "
