msgid ""
"This document explores the details of the GeoDjango Model API.  Throughout "
"this section, we'll be using the following geographic model of a `ZIP "
"code`__ and of a `Digital Elevation Model`__ as our examples::"
msgstr ""
"Scrúdaíonn an doiciméad seo sonraí an API Múnla GeoDjango. Le linn na roinn "
"seo, beimid ag úsáid an tsamhail gheografach seo a leanas de `cód ZIP`__ "
"agus de `Múnla Airde Digit`__ mar ár samplaí:"

msgid "Spatial Field Types"
msgstr "Cineálacha Réimse spású"

msgid ""
"Spatial fields consist of a series of geometry field types and one raster "
"field type. Each of the geometry field types correspond to the OpenGIS "
"Simple Features specification [#fnogc]_. There is no such standard for "
"raster data."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i réimsí spásúla sraith cineálacha réimse geoiméadrachta agus "
"cineál réimse raster amháin. Freagraíonn gach ceann de na cineálacha réimse "
"geoiméadair do shonraíocht Gnéithe Simple OpenGIS [#fnogc] _. Níl aon "
"chaighdeán den sórt sin ann do shonraí raster."

msgid "The base class for geometry fields."
msgstr "An bunaicme do réimsí geoiméadrachta."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.Point`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.point`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.LineString`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.lineString`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.Polygon`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.polygon`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiPoint`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.multipoint`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiLineString`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.multilineString`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.MultiPolygon`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.multipolygon`."

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.geos.GeometryCollection`."
msgstr "Stórais a: aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.geos.geometryCollection`."

msgid "``RasterField``"
msgstr "``Rasterfield``"

msgid "Stores a :class:`~django.contrib.gis.gdal.GDALRaster`."
msgstr "Stórais a:aicme: `~django.contrib.gis.gdal.gdalraster`."

msgid "``RasterField`` is currently only implemented for the PostGIS backend."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirtear `Rasterfield ``i bhfeidhm faoi láthair ach amháin don chúltaca "
"PostGIS."

msgid "Spatial Field Options"
msgstr "Roghanna Réimse spásúla"

msgid ""
"In addition to the regular :ref:`common-model-field-options` available for "
"Django model fields, spatial fields have the following additional options. "
"All are optional."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na rialt:ref: `common-model-field-options` atá ar fáil do "
"réimsí samhail Django, tá na roghanna breise seo a leanas ag réimsí spásúla. "
"Tá gach ceann roghnach."

msgid ""
"Sets the SRID [#fnogcsrid]_ (Spatial Reference System Identity) of the "
"geometry field to the given value. Defaults to 4326 (also known as "
"`WGS84`__, units are in degrees of longitude and latitude)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an SRID [#fnogcsrid] _ (Aitheantas Córais Tagartha Spásúil) an "
"réimse geoiméadrach don luach a thugtar. Réamhshocraithe go 4326 (ar a "
"dtugtar `WGS84`__ freisin, tá aonaid i gcéimeanna fadmhéad agus "
"domhanleithead)."

msgid "Selecting an SRID"
msgstr "SRID a roghnú"

msgid ""
"Choosing an appropriate SRID for your model is an important decision that "
"the developer should consider carefully.  The SRID is an integer specifier "
"that corresponds to the projection system that will be used to interpret the "
"data in the spatial database. [#fnsrid]_  Projection systems give the "
"context to the coordinates that specify a location.  Although the details of "
"`geodesy`__ are beyond the scope of this documentation, the general problem "
"is that the earth is spherical and representations of the earth (e.g., paper "
"maps, web maps) are not."
msgstr ""
"Is cinneadh tábhachtach é SRID iomchuí a roghnú do do mhúnla ar chóir don "
"fhorbróir machnamh go cúramach. Is sonraitheoir sláireach é an SRID a "
"fhreagraíonn don chóras teilgean a úsáidfear chun na sonraí sa bhunachar "
"sonraí spásúil a léirmhíniú. [#fnsrid] _ Tugann córais teilgean an "
"comhthéacs do na comhordanáidí a shonraíonn suíomh. Cé go bhfuil sonraí "
"`geodesy`__ thar raon feidhme na doiciméadaithe seo, is í an fhadhb "
"ghinearálta ná go bhfuil an domhan sféarúil agus nach bhfuil léiriúcháin ar "
"an domhan (m.sh., léarscáileanna páipéir, léarscáileanna gréasáin)."

msgid ""
"Most people are familiar with using latitude and longitude to reference a "
"location on the earth's surface.  However, latitude and longitude are "
"angles, not distances. In other words, while the shortest path between two "
"points on a flat surface is a straight line, the shortest path between two "
"points on a curved surface (such as the earth) is an *arc* of a `great "
"circle`__. [#fnthematic]_  Thus, additional computation is required to "
"obtain distances in planar units (e.g., kilometers and miles).  Using a "
"geographic coordinate system may introduce complications for the developer "
"later on. For example, SpatiaLite does not have the capability to perform "
"distance calculations between geometries using geographic coordinate "
"systems, e.g. constructing a query to  find all points within 5 miles of a "
"county boundary stored as WGS84. [#fndist]_"
msgstr ""
"Tá eolas ag mórchuid na ndaoine ar domhanleithead agus domhanfhad a úsáid "
"chun tagairt a dhéanamh do shuíomh ar dhromchla an domhain. Mar sin féin, is "
"uillinneacha iad domhanleithead agus domhanfhad, ní achair. Is é sin le rá, "
"cé gur líne dhíreach an cosán is giorra idir dhá phointe ar dhromchla "
"cothrom, is é an cosán is giorra idir dhá phointe ar dhromchla cuartha (mar "
"shampla an talamh) ná *arc* de `ciorcal mór`__. [#fnthematic] _ Dá bhrí sin, "
"teastaíonn ríomh breise chun achair a fháil in aonaid phlanar (m.sh., "
"ciliméadar agus míle). D'fhéadfadh córas comhordaithe geografach a úsáid "
"deacrachtaí a thabhairt don fhorbróir níos déanaí. Mar shampla, níl sé de "
"chumas ag SpatiaLite ríomhanna achair a dhéanamh idir geoiméadraí ag baint "
"úsáide as córais chomhordaithe geografacha, m.sh. ceist a thógáil chun gach "
"pointe a aimsiú laistigh de 5 míle ó theorainn chontae atá stóráilte mar "
"WGS84. [#fndist] _"

msgid ""
"Portions of the earth's surface may projected onto a two-dimensional, or "
"Cartesian, plane.  Projected coordinate systems are especially convenient "
"for region-specific applications, e.g., if you know that your database will "
"only cover geometries in `North Kansas`__, then you may consider using "
"projection system specific to that region.  Moreover, projected coordinate "
"systems are defined in Cartesian units (such as meters or feet), easing "
"distance calculations."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar codanna de dhromchla an domhain a réamh-mheas ar eitleán "
"déthoiseach, nó Cartesian. Tá córais chomhordaithe réamh-mheasta áisiúil go "
"háirithe d'fheidhmchláir atá sonrach le réigiún, m.sh., má tá a fhios agat "
"nach gclúdóidh do bhunachar sonraí ach geoiméadraí i `Kansas Thuaidh `__, "
"ansin féadfaidh tú smaoineamh ar chóras teilgean a úsáid Thairis sin, "
"sainmhínítear córais chomhordaithe réamh-mheasta in aonaid Cairtesian (mar "
"mhéadair nó cosa), ag maolú ríomhanna achair."

msgid ""
"If you wish to perform arbitrary distance queries using non-point geometries "
"in WGS84 in PostGIS and you want decent performance, enable "
"the :attr:`GeometryField.geography` keyword so that :ref:`geography database "
"type <geography-type>` is used instead."
msgstr ""
"<geography-type>Más mian leat ceisteanna achair treallacha a dhéanamh ag "
"baint úsáide as geoiméadraí neamh-phointe i WGS84 i PostGIS agus ba mhaith "
"leat feidhmíocht mhaith, cumasaigh an eochairfhocal: attr: "
"`Geometryfield.geography` ionas go n-úsáidtear: ref: `cineál bunachar sonraí "
"tíreolaíochta `ina ionad."

msgid "Additional Resources:"
msgstr "Acmhainní Breise:"

msgid ""
"`spatialreference.org`__: A Django-powered database of spatial reference "
"systems."
msgstr ""
"`spatialreference.org`__: Bunachar sonraí faoi thiomáint Django de chórais "
"tagartha spásúla."

msgid ""
"`The State Plane Coordinate System`__: A website covering the various "
"projection systems used in the United States.  Much of the U.S. spatial data "
"encountered will be in one of these coordinate systems rather than in a "
"geographic coordinate system such as WGS84."
msgstr ""
"`An Córas Comhordaithe Pléanna Stáit`__: Suíomh Gréasáin a chlúdaíonn na "
"córais teilgean éagsúla a úsáidtear sna Stáit Aontaithe. Beidh cuid mhaith "
"de shonraí spásúla na SA a bhíonn i gceann de na córais chomhordaithe seo "
"seachas i gcóras comhordaithe geografach mar WGS84."

msgid "``spatial_index``"
msgstr "``Innéacsa_spáis``"

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``True``.  Creates a spatial index for the given geometry field."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True``. Cruthaíonn innéacs spásúil don réimse "
"geoiméadrach ar leith."

msgid ""
"This is different from the ``db_index`` field option because spatial indexes "
"are created in a different manner than regular database indexes.  "
"Specifically, spatial indexes are typically created using a variant of the R-"
"Tree, while regular database indexes typically use B-Trees."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo difriúil ón rogha réimse `db_index ``toisc go gcruthaítear "
"innéacsanna spásúla ar bhealach difriúil ná innéacsanna bunachar sonraí "
"rialta. Go sonrach, cruthaítear innéacsanna spásúla de ghnáth ag baint "
"úsáide as leagan den R-Tree, agus is gnách go n-úsáideann innéacsanna "
"bunachar sonraí rialta B-Crainn."

msgid "Geometry Field Options"
msgstr "Roghanna Réimse Céim"

msgid ""
"There are additional options available for Geometry fields. All the "
"following options are optional."
msgstr ""
"Tá roghanna breise ar fáil do réimsí Geoiméadra. Tá na roghanna seo a leanas "
"go léir roghnach."

msgid "``dim``"
msgstr "```dim``"

msgid ""
"This option may be used for customizing the coordinate dimension of the "
"geometry field.  By default, it is set to 2, for representing two-"
"dimensional geometries.  For spatial backends that support it, it may be set "
"to 3 for three-dimensional support."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an rogha seo a úsáid chun toise comhordaithe an réimse "
"geoiméadrach a shaincheapadh. De réir réamhshocraithe, tá sé socraithe go 2, "
"chun geoiméadraí déthoiseach a léiriú. Maidir le cúltaca spásúla a thacaíonn "
"leis, féadfar é a shocrú go 3 le haghaidh tacaíochta tríthoiseach."

msgid ""
"At this time 3D support is limited to the PostGIS and SpatiaLite backends."
msgstr ""
"Ag an am seo tá tacaíocht 3D teoranta do na cúltaca PostGIS agus Spatialite."

msgid "``geography``"
msgstr "``Geografa``"

msgid ""
"If set to ``True``, this option will create a database column of type "
"geography, rather than geometry.  Please refer to the :ref:`geography type "
"<geography-type>` section below for more details."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe ar ``True``, cruthóidh an rogha seo colún bunachar sonraí "
"de chineál tíreolaíochta, seachas geoiméadracht. Féach an roinn:ref: `cineál "
"tíreolaíochta <geography-type>`thíos le do thoil le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"Geography support is limited to PostGIS and will force the SRID to be 4326."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht tíreolaíochta teoranta do PostGIS agus cuirfidh sé iallach ar "
"an SRID a bheith 4326."

msgid "Geography Type"
msgstr "Cineál Tíreolaíochta"

msgid ""
"The geography type provides native support for spatial features represented "
"with geographic coordinates (e.g., WGS84 longitude/latitude). "
"[#fngeography]_ Unlike the plane used by a geometry type, the geography type "
"uses a spherical representation of its data.  Distance and measurement "
"operations performed on a geography column automatically employ great circle "
"arc calculations and return linear units.  In other words, when "
"``ST_Distance`` is called on two geographies, a value in meters is returned "
"(as opposed to degrees if called on a geometry column in WGS84)."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an cineál tíreolaíochta tacaíocht dúchasach do ghnéithe spásúla "
"a léirítear le comhordanáidí geografacha (m.sh., fad/domhanleithead WGS84) "
"[#fngeography] _ Murab ionann agus an eitleán a úsáideann cineál "
"geoiméadrach, úsáideann an cineál tíreolaíochta léiriú sféarúil dá shonraí. "
"Fostaíonn oibríochtaí achair agus tomhais a dhéantar ar cholún tíreolaíochta "
"ríomhanna stua ciorcail iontacha agus aonaid líneacha ar ais Is é sin le rá, "
"nuair a ghlaofar ``ST_distance`` ar dhá gheograíocht, cuirtear luach i "
"méadar ar ais (seachas céimeanna má ghairtear ar cholún geoiméadais i WGS84)."

msgid ""
"Because geography calculations involve more mathematics, only a subset of "
"the PostGIS spatial lookups are available for the geography type. "
"Practically, this means that in addition to the :ref:`distance lookups "
"<distance-lookups>` only the following additional :ref:`spatial lookups "
"<spatial-lookups>` are available for geography columns:"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhfuil níos mó matamaitice i gceist le ríomhanna tíreolaíochta, níl "
"ach fo-thacar de na cuardaigh spásúla PostGIS ar fáil don chineál "
"tíreolaíochta. <spatial-lookups>Go praiticiúil, <distance-lookups>ciallaíonn "
"sé seo nach bhfuil ach na cuardach breise seo a leanas: ref: `cuardaigh "
"spásúla `ar fáil do cholúin tíreolaíochta, i dteann:ref: `cuardach achair`:"

msgid ""
"If you need to use a spatial lookup or aggregate that doesn't support the "
"geography type as input, you can use "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Cast` database function to convert "
"the geography column to a geometry type in the query::"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit cuardach spásúil nó comhiomlán a úsáid nach dtacaíonn leis an "
"gcineál tíreolaíochta mar ionchur, is féidir leat feidhm bhunachar sonraí: "
"class: `~django.db.Models.functions.cast a úsáid chun an colún tíreolaíochta "
"a thiontú go cineál geoiméadrach san fhiosrúchán:"

msgid ""
"For more information, the PostGIS documentation contains a helpful section "
"on determining `when to use geography data type over geometry data type "
"<https://postgis.net/docs/"
"using_postgis_dbmanagement.html#PostGIS_GeographyVSGeometry>`_."
msgstr ""
"< https://postgis.net/docs/"
"using_postgis_dbmanagement.html#PostGIS_GeographyVSGeometry>Le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise, tá rannán cabhrach sa dhoiciméadú PostGIS maidir le "
"cinneadh a dhéanamh ar `cathain a úsáidfear cineál sonraí tíreolaíochta thar "
"chineál sonraí geoiméad"

msgid ""
"OpenGIS Consortium, Inc., `Simple Feature Specification For SQL <https://"
"www.ogc.org/standard/sfs/>`_."
msgstr ""
"OpenGIS Consortium, Inc., `Sonraíocht Gné Simplí Do SQL`_. < https://"
"www.ogc.org/standard/sfs/>"

msgid ""
"*See id.* at Ch. 2.3.8, p. 39 (Geometry Values and Spatial Reference "
"Systems)."
msgstr ""
"*Féach id.* ag Ch. 2.3.8, lch. 39 (Luachanna Coiméadrachta agus Córais "
"Tagartha Spásúla)."

msgid ""
"Typically, SRID integer corresponds to an EPSG (`European Petroleum Survey "
"Group <https://epsg.org/>`_) identifier.  However, it may also be associated "
"with custom projections defined in spatial database's spatial reference "
"systems table."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, freagraíonn sláimhir SRID d'aitheantóir EPSG (`G< https://"
"epsg.org/> rúpa Suirbhéireachta Peitriliam Eorpai`_). Mar sin féin, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith bainteach freisin le réamh-mheastacháin saincheaptha "
"a shainmhínítear i dtábla córais tagartha spásúla"

msgid ""
"Terry A. Slocum, Robert B. McMaster, Fritz C. Kessler, & Hugh H. Howard, "
"*Thematic Cartography and Geographic Visualization* (Prentice Hall, 2nd "
"edition), at Ch. 7.1.3."
msgstr ""
"Terry A. Slocum, Robert B. McMaster, Fritz C. Kessler, & Hugh H. Howard, "
"*Cartografaíocht Téamach agus Amharc Geografach* (Halla Prentice, 2ú "
"eagrán), ag Ch. 7.1.3."

msgid "This limitation does not apply to PostGIS."
msgstr "Ní bhaineann an teorannú seo le PostGIS."

msgid ""
"Please refer to the `PostGIS Geography Type <https://postgis.net/docs/"
"using_postgis_dbmanagement.html#PostGIS_Geography>`_ documentation for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Féach do thoil do dhoiciméadú `Cineál Tíreolaíochta PostGIS `_ le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh son< https://postgis.net/docs/"
"using_postgis_dbmanagement.html#PostGIS_Geography> raí."

msgid "OGR Inspection"
msgstr "Cigireacht OGR"

msgid "``GeoJSON`` Serializer"
msgstr "``GeoJson`` Serializer"

msgid ""
"GeoDjango provides a specific serializer for the `GeoJSON`__ format. "
"See :doc:`/topics/serialization` for more information on serialization."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn GeodJango serializer sonrach don fhormáid `GeoJson`__. Féach: "
"doc: `/topics/sraitheoireacht `le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise ar "
"shraitheadh."

msgid ""
"The ``geojson`` serializer is not meant for round-tripping data, as it has "
"no deserializer equivalent. For example, you cannot use :djadmin:`loaddata` "
"to reload the output produced by this serializer. If you plan to reload the "
"outputted data, use the plain :ref:`json serializer <serialization-formats-"
"json>` instead."
msgstr ""
"Níl an serializer ``geojson`` i gceist le haghaidh sonraí timpeall cruinn, "
"toisc nach bhfuil aon choibhéis díshealaithe aige. Mar shampla, ní féidir "
"leat: djadmin: `loaddata` a úsáid chun an t-aschur a tháirgeann an "
"serializer seo a athluchtú. <serialization-formats-json>Má tá sé ar intinn "
"agat na sonraí aschuir a athluchtú, bain úsáid as an plain: ref: `json "
"serializer `ina ionad."

msgid ""
"In addition to the options of the ``json`` serializer, the ``geojson`` "
"serializer accepts the following additional option when it is called by "
"``serializers.serialize()``:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le roghanna an serializer ``json``, glacann an serializer "
"``geojson`` leis an rogha breise seo a leanas nuair a ghlaonn "
"``serializers.serialize () ``air:"

msgid ""
"``geometry_field``: A string containing the name of a geometry field to use "
"for the ``geometry`` key of the GeoJSON feature. This is only needed when "
"you have a model with more than one geometry field and you don't want to use "
"the first defined geometry field (by default, the first geometry field is "
"picked)."
msgstr ""
"``geoimetry_field``: Sreang ina bhfuil ainm réimse geoiméadrach le húsáid le "
"haghaidh eochair ``geoiméadr`` den ghné GeoJSON. Ní theastaíonn sé seo ach "
"nuair a bhíonn samhail agat le níos mó ná réimse céiméadra amháin agus nach "
"dteastaíonn uait an chéad réimse geoiméadrach sainmhínithe a úsáid (de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, roghnaítear an chéad réimse geoiméadrach)."

msgid ""
"``id_field``: A string containing the name of a field to use for the ``id`` "
"key of the GeoJSON feature. By default, the primary key of objects is used."
msgstr ""
"``id_field``: Sreang ina bhfuil ainm réimse le húsáid le haghaidh eochair "
"``id`` den ghné GeoJSON. De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáidtear príomh-eochair "
"na rudaí."

msgid ""
"``srid``: The SRID to use for the ``geometry`` content. Defaults to 4326 "
"(WGS 84)."
msgstr ""
"``srid``: An SRID le húsáid don ábhar ``geoiméadrach`. Réamhshocraithe go "
"4326 (WGS 84)."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`fields <subset-of-fields>` option can be used to limit fields that "
"will be present in the ``properties`` key, as it works with all other "
"serializers."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an rogha: Ref: `réimsí <subset-of-fields>`a úsáid chun réimsí a "
"bheidh i láthair san eochair ``properties` a theorannú, toisc go n-oibríonn "
"sé le gach sraitheoir eile."

msgid "Would output::"
msgstr "Aschur a bheadh::"

msgid ""
"When the ``fields`` parameter is not specified, the ``geojson`` serializer "
"adds a ``pk`` key to the ``properties`` dictionary with the primary key of "
"the object as the value."
msgstr ""
"Nuair nach sonraítear an paraiméadar ``fields ``, cuireann an sraitheoir "
"``geojson`` eochair `pk`` leis an bhfoclóir ``properties` le príomh-eochair "
"an réada mar an luach."

msgid "Geographic Sitemaps"
msgstr "Léarscáil Láithreáin Geografacha"

msgid ""
"KML is an XML language focused on geographic visualization [#]_. "
"``KMLSitemap`` and its compressed counterpart ``KMZSitemap`` allow you to "
"present geolocated data in a machine-readable format."
msgstr ""
"Is teanga XML é KML atá dírithe ar léirshamhlú geografach [#] _. Ligeann "
"``KMLSitemap`` agus a mhacasamhail comhbhrúite ``KMZSitemap`` duit sonraí "
"geolocaithe a chur i láthair i bhformáid inléite le meaisín."

msgid "Reference"
msgstr "Tagairt"

msgid "``KMLSitemap``"
msgstr "``KMLSiteMap``"

msgid "``KMZSitemap``"
msgstr "``KMZsitemap``"

msgid "https://www.ogc.org/standard/kml/"
msgstr "https://www.ogc.org/standard/kml/"

msgid "Testing GeoDjango apps"
msgstr "Aipeanna GeodJango a thástáil"

msgid ""
"Included in this documentation are some additional notes and settings "
"for :ref:`testing-postgis` users."
msgstr ""
"San áireamh sa doiciméadú seo tá roinnt nótaí agus socruithe breise "
"d'úsáideoirí: ref: `testing-postgis`."

msgid ""
"The settings below have sensible defaults, and shouldn't require manual "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Tá réamhshocruithe ciallmhar ag na socruithe thíos, agus níor cheart go "
"dteastaíonn suíomh láimhe"

msgid "``POSTGIS_VERSION``"
msgstr "``LEAGAN_POSTGIS``"

msgid ""
"When GeoDjango's spatial backend initializes on PostGIS, it has to perform "
"an SQL query to determine the version in order to figure out what features "
"are available. Advanced users wishing to prevent this additional query may "
"set the version manually using a 3-tuple of integers specifying the major, "
"minor, and micro version numbers for PostGIS. For example, to configure for "
"PostGIS X.Y.Z you would use::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thosaíonn cúltaca spásúil GeodJango ar PostGIS, caithfidh sé ceist "
