"shampla:"

msgid "Index transforms"
msgstr "Athraíonn innéacs"

msgid ""
"Index transforms index into the array. Any non-negative integer can be used. "
"There are no errors if it exceeds the :attr:`size <ArrayField.size>` of the "
"array. The lookups available after the transform are those from "
"the :attr:`base_field <ArrayField.base_field>`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn Innéacs innéacs isteach san eagar. Is féidir aon sláimhir neamh-"
"dhiúltach a úsáid. Níl aon earráidí ann má sháraíonn sé an: attr: `méid "
"<ArrayField.size>`den eagar. <ArrayField.base_field>Is iad na cuardaigh atá "
"ar fáil tar éis an claochlú iad siúd ó:attr: `base_field `. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL uses 1-based indexing for array fields when writing raw SQL. "
"However these indexes and those used in :lookup:`slices <arrayfield.slice>` "
"use 0-based indexing to be consistent with Python."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann PostgreSQL innéacsú 1-bhunaithe do réimsí eagar agus SQL amh á "
"scríobh. Mar sin féin úsáideann na hinnéacsanna seo agus iad siúd a "
"úsáidtear in:lookup: `sliseanna <arrayfield.slice>`innéacsú 0-bhunaithe chun "
"a bheith comhsheasmhach le Python."

msgid "Slice transforms"
msgstr "Athraitheann sliseanna"

msgid ""
"Slice transforms take a slice of the array. Any two non-negative integers "
"can be used, separated by a single underscore. The lookups available after "
"the transform do not change. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tógann claochruithe slisní slisní slisní slisná den eagar. Is féidir aon dhá "
"shláimhir neamh-dhiúltach a úsáid, scartha le béim amháin. Ní athraíonn na "
"cuardaigh atá ar fáil tar éis an claochlú. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL uses 1-based indexing for array fields when writing raw SQL. "
"However these slices and those used in :lookup:`indexes <arrayfield.index>` "
"use 0-based indexing to be consistent with Python."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann PostgreSQL innéacsú 1-bhunaithe do réimsí eagar agus SQL amh á "
"scríobh. Mar sin féin úsáideann na slisní seo agus iad siúd a úsáidtear "
"in:lookup: `innéacsanna <arrayfield.index>`innéacsú 0-bhunaithe chun a "
"bheith comhsheasmhach le Python."

msgid "Multidimensional arrays with indexes and slices"
msgstr "Eagraí ilthoiseach le hinnéacsanna agus slisní"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL has some rather esoteric behavior when using indexes and slices "
"on multidimensional arrays. It will always work to use indexes to reach down "
"to the final underlying data, but most other slices behave strangely at the "
"database level and cannot be supported in a logical, consistent fashion by "
"Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt iompraíochta sách esoteric ag PostgreSQL nuair a úsáidtear "
"innéacsanna agus slisní ar eagair ilthoiseach. Oibreoidh sé i gcónaí "
"innéacsanna a úsáid chun na sonraí bunúsacha deiridh a bhaint amach, ach "
"iompraíonn an chuid is mó de na slisní eile go aisteach ar leibhéal an "
"bhunachar sonraí agus ní féidir le Django tacú leo ar bhealach loighciúil, "
"comhsheasmhach."

msgid "``HStoreField``"
msgstr "``HStorefield``"

msgid ""
"A field for storing key-value pairs. The Python data type used is a "
"``dict``. Keys must be strings, and values may be either strings or nulls "
"(``None`` in Python)."
msgstr ""
"Réimse chun péirí luacha eochair a stóráil. Is é ``dict`` an cineál sonraí "
"Python a úsáidtear. Caithfidh eochracha a bheith ina teaghráin, agus "
"d'fhéadfadh luachanna a bheith ina teaghráin nó neamhaill (``None ``i "
"Python)."

msgid "To use this field, you'll need to:"
msgstr "Chun an réimse seo a úsáid, beidh ort:"

msgid "Add ``'django.contrib.postgres'`` in your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr "Cuir ``django.contrib.postgres'`` i d:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
":ref:`Set up the hstore extension <create-postgresql-extensions>` in "
"PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
":ref: `Socraigh an síneadh hstore <create-postgresql-extensions>`i "
"PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"You'll see an error like ``can't adapt type 'dict'`` if you skip the first "
"step, or ``type \"hstore\" does not exist`` if you skip the second."
msgstr ""
"Feicfidh tú earráid mar ``ní féidir an cineál 'dict' a oiriúnú má scipeann "
"tú an chéad chéim, nó ```cineál “hstore” ann ``má scipeann tú an dara ceann."

msgid ""
"On occasions it may be useful to require or restrict the keys which are "
"valid for a given field. This can be done using "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.validators.KeysValidator`."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith úsáideach na heochracha atá bailí do "
"réimse ar leith a cheangal nó a shrianadh. Is féidir é seo a dhéanamh ag "
"baint úsáide as an:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.validators.keysValidator`."

msgid "Querying ``HStoreField``"
msgstr "Ag fiosrú ``hStorefield``"

msgid ""
"In addition to the ability to query by key, there are a number of custom "
"lookups available for ``HStoreField``."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis an gcumas ceist a dhéanamh de réir eochair, tá roinnt "
"cuardaigh saincheaptha ar fáil do ``hStorefield`."

msgid "We will use the following example model::"
msgstr "Úsáidfimid an tsamhail sampla seo a leanas::"

msgid "Key lookups"
msgstr "Cuardaigh eochair"

msgid "To query based on a given key, you can use that key as the lookup name:"
msgstr ""
"Chun fiosrú bunaithe ar eochair ar leith, is féidir leat an eochair sin a "
"úsáid mar ainm an chuardaigh:"

msgid "You can chain other lookups after key lookups:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat cuardaigh eile a shlánú tar éis na príomhchuardaigh:"

msgid "or use ``F()`` expressions to annotate a key value. For example:"
msgstr ""
"nó bain úsáid as abairtí ``F () ``chun príomhluach a anótáil. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"If the key you wish to query by clashes with the name of another lookup, you "
"need to use the :lookup:`hstorefield.contains` lookup instead."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an eochair is mian leat a cheistiú trí chomhraic le hainm cuardaigh "
"eile, ní mór duit an cuardach: lookup: `hstorefield.contains` a úsáid ina "
"ionad."

msgid ""
"Key transforms can also be chained "
"with: :lookup:`contains`, :lookup:`icontains`, :lookup:`endswith`, :lookup:`iendswith`, :lookup:`iexact`, :lookup:`regex`, :lookup:`iregex`, :lookup:`startswith`, "
"and :lookup:`istartswith` lookups."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na hathruithe eochair a shlánú freisin le: :lookup: "
"`contains`, :lookup: `icontains`, :lookup: `endswith`, :lookup: "
"`iendswith`, :lookup: `iexact`, :lookup: `regex`, :lookup: "
"`iregex`, :lookup: `startswith`, agus:lookup: Cuardaigh `istartswith`."

msgid ""
"Since any string could be a key in a hstore value, any lookup other than "
"those listed below will be interpreted as a key lookup. No errors are "
"raised. Be extra careful for typing mistakes, and always check your queries "
"work as you intend."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhféadfadh aon teaghrán a bheith ina eochair i luach hstore, "
"léirmhínífear aon chuardach seachas iad siúd atá liostaithe thíos mar "
"eochair chuardach. Ní ardaítear aon earráidí. Bí cúramach thar a bheith "
"cúramach maidir le botúin clóscríobh, agus seiceáil i gcónaí go n-oibríonn "
"do chuid"

msgid ""
"The :lookup:`contains` lookup is overridden "
"on :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.HStoreField`. The returned "
"objects are those where the given ``dict`` of key-value pairs are all "
"contained in the field. It uses the SQL operator ``@>``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an cuardach: lookup: `contains` ar:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.hStorefield`. Is iad na rudaí a thugtar ar "
"ais iad na rudaí ina bhfuil an ``dict`` tugtha de phéirí eochairluacha go "
"léir sa réimse. Úsáideann sé an oibreoir SQL ``@> ``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"This is the inverse of the :lookup:`contains <hstorefield.contains>` lookup "
"- the objects returned will be those where the key-value pairs on the object "
"are a subset of those in the value passed. It uses the SQL operator ``<@``. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an inbhéar den chuardach: lookup: `conté <hstorefield.contains>`- "
"is iad na rudaí a chuirtear ar ais iad na rudaí ina bhfuil na péirí luacha "
"eochair ar an réad ina fho-thacar de na rudaí sa luach a rith. Úsáideann sé "
"an oibreoir SQL ``<@``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``has_key``"
msgstr "``a_eochair``"

msgid ""
"Returns objects where the given key is in the data. Uses the SQL operator ``?"
"``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé rudaí ar ais ina bhfuil an eochair a thugtar sna sonraí. Úsáideann "
"an t-oibreoir SQL ``? ``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``has_any_keys``"
msgstr "```aon_eochair``"

msgid ""
"Returns objects where any of the given keys are in the data. Uses the SQL "
"operator ``?|``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé rudaí ar ais ina bhfuil aon cheann de na heochracha a thugtar sna "
"sonraí. Úsáideann an t-oibreoir SQL ``? |``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``has_keys``"
msgstr "``hais_eochair``"

msgid ""
"Returns objects where all of the given keys are in the data. Uses the SQL "
"operator ``?&``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé rudaí ar ais ina bhfuil na heochracha a thugtar go léir sna "
"sonraí. Úsáideann an t-oibreoir SQL ``? & ``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``keys``"
msgstr "``eochracha ``"

msgid ""
"Returns objects where the array of keys is the given value. Note that the "
"order is not guaranteed to be reliable, so this transform is mainly useful "
"for using in conjunction with lookups "
"on :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.ArrayField`. Uses the SQL "
"function ``akeys()``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé rudaí ar ais ina bhfuil an raon eochracha an luach tugtha. Tabhair "
"faoi deara nach ráthaítear go mbeidh an t-ordú iontaofa, mar sin tá an "
"claochlú seo úsáideach go príomha le húsáid i gcomhar le cuardaigh ar:class: "
"`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.arrayfield`. Úsáideann sé an fheidhm SQL "
"``akeys () ``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``values``"
msgstr "``luacha``"

msgid ""
"Returns objects where the array of values is the given value. Note that the "
"order is not guaranteed to be reliable, so this transform is mainly useful "
"for using in conjunction with lookups "
"on :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.fields.ArrayField`. Uses the SQL "
"function ``avals()``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé rudaí ar ais ina bhfuil an raon luachanna an luach a thugtar. "
"Tabhair faoi deara nach ráthaítear go mbeidh an t-ordú iontaofa, mar sin tá "
"an claochlú seo úsáideach go príomha le húsáid i gcomhar le cuardaigh "
"ar:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.fields.arrayfield`. Úsáideann sé an "
"fheidhm SQL ``avals () ``. Mar shampla:"

msgid "Range Fields"
msgstr "Réimsí Raon"

msgid ""
"There are five range field types, corresponding to the built-in range types "
"in PostgreSQL. These fields are used to store a range of values; for example "
"the start and end timestamps of an event, or the range of ages an activity "
"is suitable for."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúig chineál réimse réimse ann, a fhreagraíonn do na cineálacha raon "
"ionsuite i PostgreSQL. Úsáidtear na réimsí seo chun raon luachanna a "
"stóráil; mar shampla stampaí ama tosaigh agus deireadh imeachta, nó an raon "
"aoiseanna a bhfuil gníomhaíocht oiriúnach dóibh."

msgid ""
"All of the range fields translate to :ref:`psycopg Range objects "
"<psycopg:adapt-range>` in Python, but also accept tuples as input if no "
"bounds information is necessary. The default is lower bound included, upper "
"bound excluded, that is ``[)`` (see the PostgreSQL documentation for details "
"about `different bounds`_). The default bounds can be changed for non-"
"discrete range fields (:class:`.DateTimeRangeField` "
"and :class:`.DecimalRangeField`) by using the ``default_bounds`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Aistríonn gach ceann de na réim <psycopg:adapt-range>sí raon chuig: ref: "
"`psycopg Range earraí `i Python, ach glacann siad le tuples mar ionchur mura "
"bhfuil aon fhaisnéis teorainneacha riachtanach. Is é an réamhshocrú ceann "
"íochtarach san áireamh, ceann uachtarach eisiata, is é sin ``[)`` (féach "
"doiciméadú PostgreSQL le haghaidh sonraí faoi `teorainneacha éagsúla`_). Is "
"féidir na teorainneacha réamhshocraithe a athrú do réimsí raon neamh-scoite "
"(:class: `.DateTimeRangeField` agus:class: `.decimalRangeField`) tríd an "
"argóint ``default_limits ``a úsáid."

msgid "PostgreSQL normalizes a range with no points to the empty range"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A range with equal values specified for an included lower bound and an "
"excluded upper bound, such as ``Range(datetime.date(2005, 6, 21), "
"datetime.date(2005, 6, 21))`` or ``[4, 4)``, has no points. PostgreSQL will "
"normalize the value to empty when saving to the database, and the original "
"bound values will be lost. See the `PostgreSQL documentation for details "
"<https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/rangetypes.html#RANGETYPES-IO>`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "``IntegerRangeField``"
msgstr "``Réimse Iomlána``"

msgid ""
"Stores a range of integers. Based on "
"an :class:`~django.db.models.IntegerField`. Represented by an ``int4range`` "
"in the database and a "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange`` in Python."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann sé raon sláimhreacha. Bunaithe ar: aicme: "
"`~Django.db.Models.IntegerField`. Léirítear ag ``int4range`` sa bhunachar "
"sonraí agus ``Django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.numericRange`` i "
"Python."

msgid ""
"Regardless of the bounds specified when saving the data, PostgreSQL always "
"returns a range in a canonical form that includes the lower bound and "
"excludes the upper bound, that is ``[)``."
msgstr ""
"Beag beann ar na teorainneacha a shonraítear agus na sonraí á shábháil, "
"filleann PostgreSQL raon i gcónaí i bhfoirm chanónach a chuimsíonn an ceann "
"íochtarach agus a eisiann an ceann uachtarach, is é sin ``[)``."

msgid "``BigIntegerRangeField``"
msgstr "``BigIntegerRangeField``"

msgid ""
"Stores a range of large integers. Based on "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.BigIntegerField`. Represented by an "
"``int8range`` in the database and a "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange`` in Python."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann sé raon sláimhreacha móra. Bunaithe ar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.BigIntegerField`. Léirítear ag ``int8range`` sa bhunachar "
"sonraí agus ``Django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.numericRange`` i "
"Python."

msgid "``DecimalRangeField``"
msgstr "``Deimalrangefield``"

msgid ""
"Stores a range of floating point values. Based on "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.DecimalField`. Represented by a ``numrange`` in "
"the database and a "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange`` in Python."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann sé raon luachanna pointe ar snámh. Bunaithe ar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DecimalField`. Léirítear ag ``numrange`` sa bhunachar "
"sonraí agus ``django.db.backends.postgreSQL.Psycopg_any.numericRange`` i "
"Python."

msgid ""
"Optional. The value of ``bounds`` for list and tuple inputs. The default is "
"lower bound included, upper bound excluded, that is ``[)`` (see the "
"PostgreSQL documentation for details about `different bounds`_). "
"``default_bounds`` is not used for "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange`` inputs."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Luach `teorainneacha ``le haghaidh ionchuir liosta agus tuple. Is "
"é an réamhshocrú ceann íochtarach san áireamh, ceann uachtarach eisiata, is "
"é sin ``[)`` (féach doiciméadú PostgreSQL le haghaidh sonraí faoi "
"`teorainneacha éagsúla`_). Ní úsáidtear ``default_bounds`` le haghaidh "
"ionchuir ``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.numericRange``."

msgid "``DateTimeRangeField``"
msgstr "``DataTimerangeField``"

msgid ""
"Stores a range of timestamps. Based on "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`. Represented by a ``tstzrange`` "
"in the database and a "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateTimeTZRange`` in Python."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann sé raon stampaí ama. Bunaithe ar a:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField`. Léirítear ag ``tstzrange`` sa bhunachar "
"sonraí agus ``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateTimetzRange`` i "
"Python."

msgid ""
"Optional. The value of ``bounds`` for list and tuple inputs. The default is "
"lower bound included, upper bound excluded, that is ``[)`` (see the "
"PostgreSQL documentation for details about `different bounds`_). "
"``default_bounds`` is not used for "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateTimeTZRange`` inputs."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Luach `teorainneacha ``le haghaidh ionchuir liosta agus tuple. Is "
"é an réamhshocrú ceann íochtarach san áireamh, ceann uachtarach eisiata, is "
"é sin ``[)`` (féach doiciméadú PostgreSQL le haghaidh sonraí faoi "
"`teorainneacha éagsúla`_). Ní úsáidtear ``default_bounds`` le haghaidh "
"ionchuir ``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateTimetzRange``."

msgid "``DateRangeField``"
msgstr "``Daterangefield``"

msgid ""
"Stores a range of dates. Based on a :class:`~django.db.models.DateField`. "
"Represented by a ``daterange`` in the database and a "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateRange`` in Python."
msgstr ""
"Stórálann sé raon dátaí. Bunaithe ar a:class: `~django.db.models.datefield`. "
"Léirítear ag ``daterange`` sa bhunachar sonraí agus "
"``Django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.daterange`` i Python."

