msgid "Context variables"
msgstr "Athróga comhthéacs"

msgid ""
"When customizing the templates for "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.index` "
"and :func:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap` views, you can rely on "
"the following context variables."
msgstr ""
"Agus na teimpléid á shaincheapadh le haghaidh tuairimí: func: "
"`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.index` agus:func: "
"`~django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap`, is féidir leat brath ar na "
"hathróga comhthéacs seo a leanas."

msgid ""
"The variable ``sitemaps`` is a list of objects containing the ``location`` "
"and ``lastmod`` attribute for each of the sitemaps. Each URL exposes the "
"following attributes:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an t-athróg ``sitemaps ``liosta de na rudaí ina bhfuil an tréith "
"``suíomh`` agus ``lastmod`` do gach ceann de na léarscáileanna láithreáin. "
"Nochtann gach URL na tréithe seo a leanas:"

msgid "``location``: The location (url & page) of the sitemap."
msgstr "``láithreach``: Suíomh (url & leathanach) an léarscáileáin."

msgid ""
"``lastmod``: Populated by the :meth:`~Sitemap.get_latest_lastmod` method for "
"each sitemap."
msgstr ""
"``lastmod``: Daonraithe ag an modh: meth: `~SiteMap.get_Latest_LastMod` do "
"gach léarscáil an léarscáileáin."

msgid "Sitemap"
msgstr "Láithreán Gréasáin"

msgid ""
"The variable ``urlset`` is a list of URLs that should appear in the sitemap. "
"Each URL exposes attributes as defined in "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sitemaps.Sitemap` class:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an t-athróg `urlset`` liosta de URLanna ba chóir a bheith le feiceáil "
"sa léarscáil an léarscáileáin. Nochtann gach URL tréithe mar a "
"shainmhínítear san aicme:class: `~django.contrib.sitemaps.siteMap`:"

msgid "``alternates``"
msgstr "``malartach``"

msgid "``changefreq``"
msgstr "``Changefreq``"

msgid "``item``"
msgstr "``Míre``"

msgid "``lastmod``"
msgstr "``lasmod``"

msgid "``location``"
msgstr "``suíomh``"

msgid "``priority``"
msgstr "``tosaíocht ``"

msgid ""
"The ``alternates`` attribute is available when :attr:`~Sitemap.i18n` "
"and :attr:`~Sitemap.alternates` are enabled. It is a list of other language "
"versions, including the optional :attr:`~Sitemap.x_default` fallback, for "
"each URL. Each alternate is a dictionary with ``location`` and ``lang_code`` "
"keys."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith ``alternates`` ar fáil nuai:attr: `~SiteMap.I18n` agus:attr: "
"`~SiteMap.Alternates` cumasaithe. Is liosta de leaganacha teanga eile é, "
"lena n-áirítear an fillback roghnaí:attr: `~SiteMap.x_default`, do gach URL. "
"Is foclóir é gach malartach le heochracha ``láithreach`` agus ``lang_code``."

msgid ""
"The ``item`` attribute has been added for each URL to allow more flexible "
"customization of the templates, such as `Google news sitemaps`_. Assuming "
"Sitemap's :attr:`~Sitemap.items()` would return a list of items with "
"``publication_data`` and a ``tags`` field something like this would generate "
"a Google News compatible sitemap:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireadh an tréith ``earra`` le haghaidh gach URL chun saincheapadh níos "
"solúbtha a cheadú ar na teimpléid, mar shampla `láithreáin nuachta Google "
"`_. Ag glacadh le Sitemap 's:attr: `~SiteMap.items () `a thabharfadh liosta "
"míreanna a thabhairt ar ais le `publication_data ``agus réimse ``tags`` rud "
"éigin mar seo léarscáil láithreán gréasáin atá comhoiriúnach le Google News:"

msgid "The \"sites\" framework"
msgstr "An creat “láithreáin”"

msgid ""
"Django comes with an optional \"sites\" framework. It's a hook for "
"associating objects and functionality to particular websites, and it's a "
"holding place for the domain names and \"verbose\" names of your Django-"
"powered sites."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le creat roghnach “suíomhanna”. Is crúca é chun rudaí agus "
"feidhmiúlacht a cheangal le láithreáin ghréasáin áirithe, agus is áit "
"shealbhaithe é d'ainmneacha fearainn agus ainmneacha “fhíorúla” do "
"shuíomhanna faoi thiomáint Django."

msgid ""
"Use it if your single Django installation powers more than one site and you "
"need to differentiate between those sites in some way."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid é má chumhachtaíonn do shuiteáil Django aonair níos mó ná suíomh "
"amháin agus ní mór duit idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir na suíomhanna sin ar "
"bhealach éigin."

msgid "The sites framework is mainly based on this model:"
msgstr "Tá creat na suíomhanna bunaithe go príomha ar an tsamhail seo:"

msgid ""
"A model for storing the ``domain`` and ``name`` attributes of a website."
msgstr ""
"Múnla chun tréithe ``fearainn ```agus ``ainm ``a stóráil de láithreán "
"gréasáin."

msgid ""
"The fully qualified domain name associated with the website. For example, "
"``www.example.com``."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm fearainn láncháilithe a bhaineann leis an suíomh Gréasáin. Mar "
"shampla, ``www.example.com``."

msgid "A human-readable \"verbose\" name for the website."
msgstr "Ainm “fhíorúil” inléite don duine don láithreán gréasáin."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`SITE_ID` setting specifies the database ID of "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object associated with that "
"particular settings file. If the setting is omitted, "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` function will "
"try to get the current site by comparing "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site.domain` with the host name from "
"the :meth:`request.get_host() <django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>` method."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an socrú: Setting: `SITE_ID` ID bunachar sonraí an réad: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a bhaineann leis an gcomhad socruithe "
"áirithe sin. <django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>Má fhágtar an socrú, "
"déanfaidh an fheidhm:func: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` iarracht an suíomh reatha "
"a fháil trí chomparáid idir an:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site.domain` leis an ainm óstach ón modh:meth: "
"`request.get_host () `."

msgid ""
"How you use this is up to you, but Django uses it in a couple of ways "
"automatically via a couple of conventions."
msgstr ""
"Is fútsa atá an chaoi a n-úsáideann tú é seo, ach úsáideann Django é ar "
"chúpla bealach go huathoibríoch trí chúpla coinbhinsiún."

msgid "Example usage"
msgstr "Úsáid samplach"

msgid "Why would you use sites? It's best explained through examples."
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth a n-úsáideann tú suíomhanna? Is fearr é a mhíniú trí shamplaí."

msgid "Associating content with multiple sites"
msgstr "Ábhar a cheangal le suíomhanna iolracha"

msgid ""
"The LJWorld.com_ and Lawrence.com sites were operated by the same news "
"organization -- the Lawrence Journal-World newspaper in Lawrence, Kansas. "
"LJWorld.com focused on news, while Lawrence.com focused on local "
"entertainment. But sometimes editors wanted to publish an article on *both* "
"sites."
msgstr ""
"Bhí na suíomhanna LJworld.com_ agus Lawrence.com á oibriú ag an eagraíocht "
"nuachta céanna - nuachtán Lawrence Journal-World i Lawrence, Kansas. Dhírigh "
"LJworld.com ar nuacht, agus dhírigh Lawrence.com ar siamsaíocht áitiúil. Ach "
"uaireanta bhí eagarthóirí ag iarraidh alt a fhoilsiú ar* an bheirt "
"suíomhanna."

msgid ""
"The naive way of solving the problem would be to require site producers to "
"publish the same story twice: once for LJWorld.com and again for "
"Lawrence.com. But that's inefficient for site producers, and it's redundant "
"to store multiple copies of the same story in the database."
msgstr ""
"Ba é an bealach naif chun an fhadhb a réiteach ná a cheangal ar tháirgeoirí "
"láithreáin an scéal céanna a fhoilsiú faoi dhó: uair amháin le haghaidh "
"LJworld.com agus arís do Lawrence.com. Ach tá sé sin neamhéifeachtach do "
"tháirgeoirí láithreáin, agus tá sé iomarcach cóipeanna iolracha den scéal "
"céanna a stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"A better solution removes the content duplication: Both sites use the same "
"article database, and an article is associated with one or more sites. In "
"Django model terminology, that's represented by "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` in the ``Article`` model::"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann réiteach níos fearr deireadh leis an dúbailt ábhair: Úsáideann an "
"dá shuíomh an bunachar sonraí alt céanna, agus tá baint ag alt le suíomh "
"amháin nó níos mó. I dtéarmaíocht samhail Django, léirítear é sin ag a: "
"class: `~Django.db.Models.ManyTomanyField` sa tsamhail ``Article``:"

msgid "This accomplishes several things quite nicely:"
msgstr "Cuireann sé seo roinnt rudaí i gcrích go deas:"

msgid ""
"It lets the site producers edit all content -- on both sites -- in a single "
"interface (the Django admin)."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé do tháirgeoirí an láithreáin gach ábhar a chur in eagar - ar an "
"dá shuíomh - i gcomhéadan amháin (riarachán Django)."

msgid ""
"It means the same story doesn't have to be published twice in the database; "
"it only has a single record in the database."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé nach gá an scéal céanna a fhoilsiú faoi dhó sa bhunachar "
"sonraí; níl ach taifead amháin aige sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"It lets the site developers use the same Django view code for both sites. "
"The view code that displays a given story checks to make sure the requested "
"story is on the current site. It looks something like this::"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé d'fhorbróirí láithreáin an cód amharc Django céanna a úsáid don "
"dá shuíomh. Seiceálann an cód amharc a thaispeánann scéal ar leith chun a "
"chinntiú go bhfuil an scéal iarrtha ar an suíomh reatha. Breathnaíonn sé rud "
"éigin mar seo:"

msgid "Associating content with a single site"
msgstr "Ábhar a cheangal le suíomh amháin"

msgid ""
"Similarly, you can associate a model to "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` model in a many-to-one "
"relationship, using :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, is féidir leat samhail a cheangal leis an "
"tsamhail:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` i gcaidreamh go leor le "
"duine, ag baint úsáid:class: `~django.db.models.foreignKey`."

msgid ""
"For example, if an article is only allowed on a single site, you'd use a "
"model like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, mura gceadaítear alt ach ar shuíomh amháin, úsáideann tú "
"samhail mar seo:"

msgid "This has the same benefits as described in the last section."
msgstr ""
"Tá na buntáistí céanna aige seo mar a thuairiscítear sa chuid deireanach."

msgid "Hooking into the current site from views"
msgstr "Ag dul isteach sa suíomh reatha ó thuairimí"

msgid ""
"You can use the sites framework in your Django views to do particular things "
"based on the site in which the view is being called. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat creat na suíomhanna i do thuairimí Django a úsáid chun rudaí "
"áirithe a dhéanamh bunaithe ar an suíomh ina bhfuil an radharc á ghlaoch. "
"Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"It's fragile to hard-code the site IDs like that, in case they change. The "
"cleaner way of accomplishing the same thing is to check the current site's "
"domain::"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé leochaileach IDanna an láithreáin mar sin a chódú crua, i gcás go n-"
"athraíonn siad. Is é an bealach níos glaine chun an rud céanna a chur i "
"gcrích ná fearann an láithreáin reatha a sheiceáil:"

msgid ""
"This has also the advantage of checking if the sites framework is installed, "
"and return a :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` instance if "
"it is not."
msgstr ""
"Tá an buntáiste aige seo freisin a sheiceáil an bhfuil creat na suíomhanna "
"suiteáilte, agus a: class: `~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestsite` "
"sampla a thabhairt ar ais mura bhfuil sé."

msgid ""
"If you don't have access to the request object, you can use the "
"``get_current()`` method of the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` "
"model's manager. You should then ensure that your settings file does contain "
"the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting. This example is equivalent to the previous "
"one::"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil rochtain agat ar an réad iarratais, is féidir leat an modh "
"``get_current () ``de bhainisteoir an tsamhail:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a úsáid. Ba cheart duit a chinntiú ansin "
"go bhfuil an socrú: setting: `SITE_ID` i do chomhad socruithe. Tá an sampla "
"seo coibhéiseach leis an gceann roimhe seo:"

msgid "Getting the current domain for display"
msgstr "An fearainn reatha a fháil le taispeáint"

msgid ""
"LJWorld.com and Lawrence.com both have email alert functionality, which lets "
"readers sign up to get notifications when news happens. It's pretty basic: A "
"reader signs up on a web form and immediately gets an email saying, \"Thanks "
"for your subscription.\""
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhmiúlacht foláirimh ríomhphoist ag LJworld.com agus Lawrence.com "
"araon, a ligeann do léitheoirí clárú chun fógraí a fháil nuair a tharlaíonn "
"nuacht. Tá sé bunúsach go leor: Síníonn léitheoir suas ar fhoirm gréasáin "
"agus faigheann sé ríomhphost láithreach ag rá, “Go raibh maith agat as do "
"shíntiús.”"

msgid ""
"It'd be inefficient and redundant to implement this sign up processing code "
"twice, so the sites use the same code behind the scenes. But the \"thank you "
"for signing up\" notice needs to be different for each site. By "
"using :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` objects, we can abstract "
"the \"thank you\" notice to use the values of the current "
"site's :attr:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site.name` "
"and :attr:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site.domain`."
msgstr ""
"Bheadh sé neamhéifeachtach agus iomarcach an cód próiseála sínithe seo a "
"chur i bhfeidhm faoi dhó, mar sin úsáideann na suíomhanna an cód céanna "
"taobh thiar de na radhairc. Ach caithfidh an fógra “go raibh maith agat as "
"síniú” a bheith difriúil do gach suíomh. Trí rudaí:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a úsáid, is féidir linn an fógra “go "
"raibh maith agat” a thiomsú chun luachanna an láithreáin reatha a úsáid: "
"attr: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site.name` agus:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site.domain`."

msgid "Here's an example of what the form-handling view looks like::"
msgstr "Seo sampla den chuma atá ar an radharc láimhseála foirme:"

msgid ""
"On Lawrence.com, this email has the subject line \"Thanks for subscribing to "
"lawrence.com alerts.\" On LJWorld.com, the email has the subject \"Thanks "
"for subscribing to LJWorld.com alerts.\" Same goes for the email's message "
"body."
msgstr ""
"Ar Lawrence.com, tá an líne ábhair ag an ríomhphost seo “Go raibh maith agat "
"as liostáil le foláirimh lawrence.com.” Ar LJworld.com, tá an t-ábhar ag an "
"ríomhphost “Go raibh maith agat as liostáil le foláirimh LJworld.com.” Téann "
"an rud céanna le comhlacht teachtaireachta an ríomhphoist."

msgid ""
"Note that an even more flexible (but more heavyweight) way of doing this "
"would be to use Django's template system. Assuming Lawrence.com and "
"LJWorld.com have different template directories (:setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-"
"DIRS>`), you could farm out to the template system like so::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur bealach níos solúbtha fós (ach níos troma) chun é seo "
"a dhéanamh ná córas teimpléad Django a úsáid. Ag glacadh leis go bhfuil "
"eolairí teimpléad éagsúla ag Lawrence.com agus LJworld.com (:setting: `DIRS "
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>`), d'fhéadfá feirm a dhéanamh amach chuig an gcóras "
"teimpléid mar sin:"

msgid ""
"In this case, you'd have to create :file:`subject.txt` "
"and :file:`message.txt` template files for both the LJWorld.com and "
"Lawrence.com template directories. That gives you more flexibility, but it's "
"also more complex."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, bheadh ort comhaid teimpléad:file: `subject.txt` agus:file: "
"`message.txt` a chruthú d'eolairí teimpléad LJworld.com agus Lawrence.com "
"araon. Tugann sé sin níos mó solúbthachta duit, ach tá sé níos casta freisin."

msgid ""
"It's a good idea to exploit the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` "
"objects as much as possible, to remove unneeded complexity and redundancy."
msgstr ""
"Is smaoineamh maith é leas a bhaint as na rudaí:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a oiread agus is féidir, chun castacht "
"agus iomarcaíocht neamhriachtanach a bhaint."

msgid "Getting the current domain for full URLs"
msgstr "An fearainn reatha a fháil le haghaidh URLanna iomlána"

msgid ""
"Django's ``get_absolute_url()`` convention is nice for getting your objects' "
"URL without the domain name, but in some cases you might want to display the "
"full URL -- with ``https://`` and the domain and everything -- for an "
"object. To do this, you can use the sites framework. An example:"
msgstr ""
"Tá coinbhinsiún ``get_absolute_url () ``Django go deas chun URL d'earraí a "
"fháil gan an t-ainm fearainn, ach i gcásanna áirithe b'fhéidir gur mhaith "
"leat an URL iomlán a thaispeáint - le ``https: //`` agus an fearainn agus "
"gach rud - do réad. Chun seo a dhéanamh, is féidir leat creat na láithreáin "
"a úsáid. Sampla:"

msgid "Enabling the sites framework"
msgstr "Creat na láithreáin a chumasú"

msgid "To enable the sites framework, follow these steps:"
msgstr "Chun creat na láithreáin a chumasú, lean na céimeanna seo:"

msgid ""
"Add ``'django.contrib.sites'`` to your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr "Cuir ``django.contrib.sites'`` le do shocrú: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "Define a :setting:`SITE_ID` setting::"
msgstr "Sainmhínigh a: socrú: `SITE_ID` socrú::"

msgid "Run :djadmin:`migrate`."
msgstr "Rith: DjaDmin: `imirce `."

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.sites`` registers "
"a :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` signal handler which "
"creates a default site named ``example.com`` with the domain "
"``example.com``. This site will also be created after Django creates the "
"test database. To set the correct name and domain for your project, you can "
"use a :ref:`data migration <data-migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"``django.contrib.sites`` cláraíonn a:data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_migrate` láimhseálaí comhartha a chruthaíonn "
"suíomh réamhshocraithe darb ainm ``example.com`` leis an bhfearann "
"``example.com``. Cruthófar an suíomh seo freisin tar éis Django an bunachar "
"sonraí tástála a chruthú. <data-migrations>Chun an t-ainm agus an fearainn "
"ceart a shocrú do do thionscadal, is féidir leat a:ref: `imirce sonraí `a "
"úsáid."

msgid ""
"In order to serve different sites in production, you'd create a separate "
"settings file with each ``SITE_ID`` (perhaps importing from a common "
"settings file to avoid duplicating shared settings) and then specify the "
"appropriate :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` for each site."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn freastal ar shuíomhanna éagsúla i dtáirgeadh, chruthófá comhad "
"socruithe ar leithligh le gach ``SITE_ID` (b'fhéidir allmhairiú ó chomhad "
"socruithe coiteann chun socruithe roinnte a dhúbailt) agus ansin sonraigh an "
"oiriúna:envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` do gach suíomh."

msgid "Caching the current ``Site`` object"
msgstr "An réad reatha ```Láithreach`` a chaitheamh a chaitheamh"

msgid ""
"As the current site is stored in the database, each call to "
"``Site.objects.get_current()`` could result in a database query. But Django "
"is a little cleverer than that: on the first request, the current site is "
"cached, and any subsequent call returns the cached data instead of hitting "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"De réir mar a stóráiltear an suíomh reatha sa bhunachar sonraí, d'fhéadfadh "
"ceist bunachar sonraí a bheith mar thoradh ar gach glao chuig "
"`site.objects.get_current () `. Ach tá Django beagán níos cliste ná sin: ar "
"an gcéad iarratas, cuirtear an suíomh reatha a chosc, agus filleann aon "
"ghlao ina dhiaidh sin na sonraí taiscéadaithe in ionad an bunachar sonraí a "
"bhualadh."

msgid ""
"If for any reason you want to force a database query, you can tell Django to "
"clear the cache using ``Site.objects.clear_cache()``::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ceist bunachar sonraí a chur i bhfeidhm ar chúis ar bith, is "
"féidir leat a rá le Django an taisce a ghlanadh ag baint úsáide as "
"`Site.Objects.clear_cache () ``:"

msgid "The ``CurrentSiteManager``"
msgstr "An ``Currentsitemanager``"

msgid ""
"If :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` plays a key role in your "
"application, consider using the "
"helpful :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` in your "
"model(s). It's a model :doc:`manager </topics/db/managers>` that "
"automatically filters its queries to include only objects associated with "
"the current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ról lárnach ag: Class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` i "
"d'iarratas, smaoinigh ar an gcabhrach: class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentsiteManager` a úsáid i do mhúnla (í). "
"Is samhail é: doc: `bainisteor` a scagann a cheisteanna go huathoibríoch "
"chun </topics/db/managers> rudaí a bhaineann leis an reatha: class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a áireamh."

msgid "Mandatory :setting:`SITE_ID`"
msgstr "Riachtanas: Socrú: `SITE_ID`"

msgid ""
"The ``CurrentSiteManager`` is only usable when the :setting:`SITE_ID` "
"setting is defined in your settings."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an `CurrentSiteManager`` inúsáidte ach nuair a shainmhínítear an "
"socrúit:setting: `SITE_ID` i do shocruithe."

msgid ""
"Use :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` by adding it "
"to your model explicitly. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid:Class: `~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentSiteManager` tríd é a "
"chur le do mhúnla go sainráite. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"With this model, ``Photo.objects.all()`` will return all ``Photo`` objects "
"in the database, but ``Photo.on_site.all()`` will return only the ``Photo`` "
"objects associated with the current site, according to "
"the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting."
msgstr ""
"Leis an tsamhail seo, cuirfidh `Photo.Objects.all () ``gach rud ``Photo`` ar "
"ais sa bhunachar sonraí, ach ní thabharfaidh ``Photo.on_site.all () ``ach na "
"rudaí ``Photo`` a bhaineann leis an suíomh reatha ar ais, de réir an "
"socruithe: `SITE_ID`."

msgid "Put another way, these two statements are equivalent::"
msgstr "Cuir bealach eile, tá an dá ráiteas seo coibhéiseach:"

msgid ""
"How did :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` know "
"which field of ``Photo`` was the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site`? "
"By default, :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` looks "
"for a either a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` called ``site`` or "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` called ``sites`` to filter on. "
"If you use a field named something other than ``site`` or ``sites`` to "
"identify which :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` objects your "
"object is related to, then you need to explicitly pass the custom field name "
"as a parameter to :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` "
"on your model. The following model, which has a field called ``publish_on``, "
"demonstrates this::"
msgstr ""
"Cén chaoi a raibh a fhios ag :class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentsiteManager` cén réimse de ``Photo "
"``a bhí an:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site`? De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, féachann :class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentSiteManager` ceachtar a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey` ar a dtugtar ``site`` nó a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField` ar a dtugtar ``sites`` le scagadh air. "
"Má úsáideann tú réimse darb ainm rud éigin seachas ``site`` nó ``sites`` "
"chun a aithint cé na ruda:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a "
"bhfuil baint ag do réad leis, ansin ní mór duit ainm an réimse saincheaptha "
"a rith mar pharaiméadar chuig:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentsiteManager` ar do mhúnla. Léiríonn "
"an tsamhail seo a leanas, a bhfuil réimse aige ar a dtugtar ``publish_on``, "
"seo:"

msgid ""
"If you attempt to "
"use :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager` and pass a "
"field name that doesn't exist, Django will raise a ``ValueError``."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú iarracht a úsáid:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.managers.currentSiteManager` agus ainm réimse nach "
"bhfuil ann a chur ar aghaidh, ardóidh Django ``ValueError``."

msgid ""
"Finally, note that you'll probably want to keep a normal (non-site-specific) "
"``Manager`` on your model, even if you "
"use :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager`. As explained "
"in the :doc:`manager documentation </topics/db/managers>`, if you define a "
"manager manually, then Django won't create the automatic ``objects = "
"models.Manager()`` manager for you. Also note that certain parts of Django "
"-- namely, the Django admin site and generic views -- use whichever manager "
"is defined *first* in the model, so if you want your admin site to have "
"access to all objects (not just site-specific ones), put ``objects = "
"models.Manager()`` in your model, before you "
"define :class:`~django.contrib.sites.managers.CurrentSiteManager`."
msgstr ""
"Mar fhocal scoir, tabhair faoi deara gur dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh "
"“Bainisteoir” gnáth (neamh-shonrach don láithreán) a choinneáil ar do "
"mhúnla, fiú má úsáideann tú: class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.Managers.CurrentSiteManager`. Mar a mhínítear in:doc: "
"`doiciméadú bainisteora”, má shain</topics/db/managers> mhíníonn tú "
"bainisteoir de láimh, ansin ní chruthóidh Django an bainisteoir uathoibríoch "
"``objects = Models.manager ()` duit. Tabhair faoi deara freisin go n-"
"úsáideann codanna áirithe de Django - eadhon, suíomh riaracháin Django agus "
"tuairimí cineálacha - cibé bainisteoir a shainmhínítear *chéad* sa tsamhail, "
"mar sin más mian leat go mbeadh rochtain ag do shuíomh riaracháin ar gach "
"rud (ní amháin cinn suíomh-shonrach), cuir ``objects = Models.manager () `i "
"do mhúnla, sula sainmhíníonn tú: "
"`~django.contrib.current.sites.managers.tSiteManager`."

msgid "Site middleware"
msgstr "Láithreán Middleware"

msgid "If you often use this pattern::"
msgstr "Má úsáideann tú an patrún seo go minic::"

msgid ""
"To avoid repetitions, "
"add :class:`django.contrib.sites.middleware.CurrentSiteMiddleware` "
"to :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`. The middleware sets the ``site`` attribute on "
"every request object, so you can use ``request.site`` to get the current "
"site."
msgstr ""
"Chun athrá a sheachaint, cuir: class: "
"`django.contrib.sites.middleware.currentsiteMiddleware` chuig:setting: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`. Socraíonn an middleware an tréith ``suite`` ar gach réad "
"iarratais, ionas gur féidir leat ``request.site`` a úsáid chun an suíomh "
"reatha a fháil."

msgid "How Django uses the sites framework"
msgstr "Conas a úsáideann Django creat na suíomhanna"

msgid ""
"Although it's not required that you use the sites framework, it's strongly "
"encouraged, because Django takes advantage of it in a few places. Even if "
"your Django installation is powering only a single site, you should take the "
"two seconds to create the site object with your ``domain`` and ``name``, and "
"point to its ID in your :setting:`SITE_ID` setting."
msgstr ""
"Cé nach bhfuil sé ag teastáil go n-úsáideann tú creat na suíomhanna, "
"spreagtar go láidir é, toisc go mbaineann Django leas as i gcúpla áit. Fiú "
"mura bhfuil do shuiteáil Django ag cumhachtú ach suíomh amháin, ba cheart "
"duit an dá soicind a thógáil chun réad an láithreáin a chruthú le do "
"``fearainn`` agus `ainm ``, agus díriú ar a ID i do shuíomh: `SITE_ID`."

msgid "Here's how Django uses the sites framework:"
msgstr "Seo mar a úsáideann Django creat na suíomhanna:"

msgid ""
"In the :mod:`redirects framework <django.contrib.redirects>`, each redirect "
"object is associated with a particular site. When Django searches for a "
"redirect, it takes into account the current site."
msgstr ""
"Sa chreat: mod: `atreoruithe <django.contrib.redirects>`, tá baint ag gach "
"réad atreoraithe le suíomh áirithe. Nuair a chuardaíonn Django atreorú, "
"cuireann sé an suíomh reatha san áireamh."

msgid ""
"In the :mod:`flatpages framework <django.contrib.flatpages>`, each flatpage "
"is associated with a particular site. When a flatpage is created, you "
"specify its :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site`, and "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.FlatpageFallbackMiddleware` "
"checks the current site in retrieving flatpages to display."
msgstr ""
"Sa chreat: mod: `flatpages <django.contrib.flatpages>`, tá baint ag gach "
"leathanach cothrom le suíomh áirithe. Nuair a chruthaítear leathanach "
"cothrom, sonraíonn tú ai:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site`, agus "
"seiceálann seiceál:class: "
"`~django.contrib.flatpages.middleware.flatpageFallBackmiddleware` an suíomh "
"reatha chun leathanaigh réidh a aisghabháil le taispeáint."

msgid ""
"In the :mod:`syndication framework <django.contrib.syndication>`, the "
"templates for ``title`` and ``description`` automatically have access to a "
"variable ``{{ site }}``, which is "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object representing the "
"current site. Also, the hook for providing item URLs will use the ``domain`` "
"from the current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object if you "
"don't specify a fully-qualified domain."
msgstr ""
"Sa chreat sindiciúcháin: mod:<django.contrib.syndication>, tá rochtain go "
"huathoibríoch ag na teimpléid le haghaidh ``title`` agus ``description`` ar "
"athróg ``{{site}}``, arb é an:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` "
"réad a léiríonn an láithreán reatha. Chomh maith leis sin, úsáidfidh an "
"crúca chun URLanna míreanna a sholáthar an réad ``fearainn ``ón réad "
"reatha:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` mura sonraíonn tú fearann "
"láncháilithe."

msgid ""
"In the :mod:`authentication framework "
"<django.contrib.auth>`, :class:`django.contrib.auth.views.LoginView` passes "
"the current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` name to the template "
"as ``{{ site_name }}``."
msgstr ""
"Sa chreat:mod: `fíordheimhniúcháin <django.contrib.auth>`, :class: "
"`django.contrib.auth.views.loginView` téann an t-ainm reatha:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` chuig an teimpléad mar ``{{site_name}}``."

msgid ""
"The shortcut view (``django.contrib.contenttypes.views.shortcut``) uses the "
"domain of the current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object when "
"calculating an object's URL."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an dearcadh aicearra "
"(``django.contrib.contenttypes.views.shortcut``) réad reatha: class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` agus URL réada á ríomh."

msgid ""
"In the admin framework, the \"view on site\" link uses the "
"current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` to work out the domain "
"for the site that it will redirect to."
msgstr ""
"Sa chreat riaracháin, úsáideann an nasc “amharc ar an láithreán” an "
"reatha:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` chun an fearainn don "
"láithreán a atreoróidh sé chuig a oibriú amach."

msgid "``RequestSite`` objects"
msgstr "``Iarrata`` rudaí"

msgid ""
"Some :doc:`django.contrib </ref/contrib/index>` applications take advantage "
"of the sites framework but are architected in a way that doesn't *require* "
"the sites framework to be installed in your database. (Some people don't "
"want to, or just aren't *able* to install the extra database table that the "
"sites framework requires.) For those cases, the framework provides "
"a :class:`django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` class, which can be "
"used as a fallback when the database-backed sites framework is not available."
msgstr ""
"Baineann roinnt: doc: feidhmchláir `django.contrib` </ref/contrib/index> "
"leas as creat na láithreáin ach déantar iad a ailtiriú ar bhealach nach gá "
"uir* creat na suíomhanna atá le suiteáil i do bhunachar sonraí. (Níl daoine "
"áirithe ag iarraidh, nó níl* in* an tábla bunachar sonraí breise a éilíonn "
"creat na láithreáin a shuiteáil.) Maidir leis na cásanna sin, soláthraíonn "
"an creat aicme a:class: `django.contrib.sites.requests.requestsite`, ar "
"féidir é a úsáid mar fhilleadh nuair nach bhfuil creat na suíomhanna "
"tacaíochta le bunachar sonraí ar fáil."

msgid ""
"A class that shares the primary interface "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` (i.e., it has ``domain`` and "
"``name`` attributes) but gets its data from a "
"Django :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object rather than from a database."
msgstr ""
"Aicme a roinneann an príomh-chomhéadan de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` (ie, tá tréithe ``domain`` agus ``ainm "
"``aige) ach a fhaigheann a chuid sonraí ó réad django:class: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest` seachas ó bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Sets the ``name`` and ``domain`` attributes to the value "
"of :meth:`~django.http.HttpRequest.get_host`."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn na tréithe ```ainm ``agus `domain`` don luach de:meth: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest.get_host`."

msgid ""
"A :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` object has a similar "
"interface to a normal :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object, "
"except its :meth:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite.__init__()` "
"method takes an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object. It's able to "
"deduce the ``domain`` and ``name`` by looking at the request's domain. It "
"has ``save()`` and ``delete()`` methods to match the interface "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site`, but the methods "
"raise :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"A: Class: `~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestSite` tá comhéadan cosúil "
"le réad gnáth:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site`, seachas a: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestSite. Tógann an modh __init__ () "
"`réad: aicme: `~django.http.httpRequest`. Tá sé in ann an ``fearainn`` agus "
"``ainm ``a bhaint amach trí fhéachaint ar fhearann an iarratais. Tá modhanna "
"``save () ``agus ``delete ()`` aige chun comhéadan de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.models.site` a mheaitseáil, ach ardaíonn na modhanna: "
"exc: `NotImplementeDerror`."

msgid "``get_current_site`` shortcut"
msgstr "Aicearra ``get_current_site``"

msgid ""
"Finally, to avoid repetitive fallback code, the framework provides "
"a :func:`django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site` function."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, chun cód titim athchleachtach a sheachaint, soláthraíonn an "
"creat feidhm a:func: `django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site`."

msgid ""
"A function that checks if ``django.contrib.sites`` is installed and returns "
"either the current :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` object or "
"a :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` object based on the "
"request. It looks up the current site based on :meth:`request.get_host() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>` if the :setting:`SITE_ID` setting is not "
"defined."
msgstr ""
"Feidhm a sheiceálann an bhfuil ``django.contrib.sites`` suiteáilte agus a "
"thugann an rud reatha: class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` nó "
"a:class: `~django.contrib.sites.requestsite` réad reatha bunaithe ar an "
"iarratas. Breathnaíonn sé suas ar an suíomh reatha bunaithe ar:meth: "
"`request.get_host () <django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>`mura sainmhínítear "
"an socrú:setting: `SITE_ID`."

msgid ""
"Both a domain and a port may be returned by :meth:`request.get_host() "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>` when the Host header has a port "
"explicitly specified, e.g. ``example.com:80``. In such cases, if the lookup "
"fails because the host does not match a record in the database, the port is "
"stripped and the lookup is retried with the domain part only. This does not "
"apply to :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` which will "
"always use the unmodified host."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh fearann agus calafort araon a chur ar ais ag: meth: "
"`request.get_host () <django.http.HttpRequest.get_host>`nuair a bhíonn "
"calafort sonraithe go sainráite ag an gceannteideal Óstach, m.sh. "
"``example.com:80``. I gcásanna den sórt sin, má theipeann ar an cuardach "
"toisc nach n-oireann an t-óstach taifead sa bhunachar sonraí, déantar an "
"calafort a dhíriú agus déantar an cuardach a athbhreithniú leis an gcuid "
"fearainn amháin. Ní bhaineann sé seo le:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.requests.requestsite` a úsáidfidh an t-óstach neamh-"
"mhodhnaithe i gcónaí."

msgid "The ``staticfiles`` app"
msgstr "An aip `staticfiles``"

msgid ""
"``django.contrib.staticfiles`` collects static files from each of your "
"applications (and any other places you specify) into a single location that "
"can easily be served in production."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` comhaid statacha ó gach ceann de "
"d'iarratais (agus aon áiteanna eile a shonraíonn tú) i suíomh amháin is "
"féidir a sheirbheáil go héasca i dtáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"For an introduction to the static files app and some usage examples, "
"see :doc:`/howto/static-files/index`. For guidelines on deploying static "
"files, see :doc:`/howto/static-files/deployment`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh réamhrá ar an aip comhaid statacha agus roinnt samplaí úsáide, "
"féach: doc: `/howto/static-files/index `. Le haghaidh treoirlínte maidir le "
"comhaid statacha a imscaradh, féach:doc: `/howto/static-files/imscaradh `."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`staticfiles settings <settings-staticfiles>` for details on the "
"following settings:"
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `socruithe staticfiles <settings-staticfiles>`le haghaidh sonraí "
"faoi na socruithe seo a leanas:"

msgid ":setting:`STORAGES`"
msgstr ":socrú: `STÓRÁLAÍ`"

msgid ":setting:`STATIC_ROOT`"
msgstr ":socrú: `STATIC_ROOT`"

msgid ":setting:`STATIC_URL`"
msgstr ":socrú: `STATIC_URL`"

msgid ":setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `STATICFILES_DIRS`"

msgid ":setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS`"
msgstr ":setting: `STATICFILES_FINDERS`"

msgid "``django.contrib.staticfiles`` exposes three management commands."
msgstr "Nochtann ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` trí ordú bainistíochta."

msgid "``collectstatic``"
msgstr "``Collectstatic``"

msgid "Collects the static files into :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`."
msgstr "Bailíonn sé na comhaid statacha in:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"Duplicate file names are by default resolved in a similar way to how "
"template resolution works: the file that is first found in one of the "
"specified locations will be used. If you're confused, "
"the :djadmin:`findstatic` command can help show you which files are found."
msgstr ""
"Réitear ainmneacha comhaid dúblacha de réir réamhshocraithe ar bhealach "
"cosúil leis an gcaoi a n-oibríonn réiteach teimpléid: úsáidfear an comhad a "
"fhaightear den chéad uair i gceann de na háiteanna Má tá mearbhall ort, is "
"féidir leis an ordú:djadmin: `findstatic` cabhrú leat cé na comhaid atá le "
"fáil a thaispeáint duit."

msgid ""
"On subsequent ``collectstatic`` runs (if ``STATIC_ROOT`` isn't empty), files "
"are copied only if they have a modified timestamp greater than the timestamp "
"of the file in ``STATIC_ROOT``. Therefore if you remove an application "
"from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, it's a good idea to use "
"the :option:`collectstatic --clear` option in order to remove stale static "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Ar rith ``collectstatic`` ina dhiaidh sin (mura bhfuil ``STATIC_ROOT`` "
"folamh), ní chóipeáiltear comhaid ach amháin má tá stampa ama modhnaithe acu "
"níos mó ná stampa ama an chomhaid i `STATIC_ROOT``. Dá bhrí sin má bhaineann "
"tú feidhmchlár ó:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, is smaoineamh maith an "
"roghna:option: `collectstatic --clear` a úsáid chun comhaid statacha seasta "
"a bhaint."

msgid ""
"Files are searched by using the :setting:`enabled finders "
"<STATICFILES_FINDERS>`. The default is to look in all locations defined "
"in :setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS` and in the ``'static'`` directory of apps "
"specified by the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"<STATICFILES_FINDERS>Cuardaítear comhaid trí:setting: `aimsitheoirí "
"cumasaithe `a úsáid. Is é an réamhshocrú ná breathnú i ngach áit a "
"shainmhínítear in:setting: `STATICFILES_DIRS` agus san eolaire ``'static'` "
"d'aipeanna a shonraítear leis an socrú: `SETTING: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command calls "
"the :meth:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage.post_process` "
"method of the ``staticfiles`` storage backend from :setting:`STORAGES` after "
"each run and passes a list of paths that have been found by the management "
"command. It also receives all command line options "
"of :djadmin:`collectstatic`. This is used by "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` "
"by default."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn an t-ordú bainistíochta: DjaDmin: `collectstatic` ar an modh: `meth: "
"`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.staticfilesStorage.post_process` ar an "
"modh cúltaca stórála `staticfiles`` ó:setting: `STORAGES` tar éis gach rith "
"agus rith liosta cosáin a aimsíodh ag an ordú bainistíochta. Faigheann sé "
"freisin gach rogha líne ordaithe de:djadmin: `collectstatic`. Úsáidtear é "
"seo ag an:class: "
"`~django.contrib.staticFiles.Storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` de réir "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"By default, collected files receive permissions "
"from :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` and collected directories receive "
"permissions from :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`. If you would "
"like different permissions for these files and/or directories, you can "
"subclass either of the :ref:`static files storage classes <staticfiles-"
"storages>` and specify the ``file_permissions_mode`` and/or "
"``directory_permissions_mode`` parameters, respectively. For example::"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, faigheann comhaid bailithe ceadanna ó:setting: "
"`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` agus faigheann eolairí bailithe ceadanna "
"ó:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`. Más mian leat ceadanna "
"éagsúla do na comhaid agus/nó na heolairí seo, is féidir leat ceachtar de na "
"haicmí stórála comhaid statacha: ref: a fho-aicmiú agus na paraiméadair "
"`<staticfiles-storages>file_permissions_mode`` agus/nó "
"``directory_permissions_mode`` a shonrú, faoi seach. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Then set the ``staticfiles`` storage backend in :setting:`STORAGES` setting "
"to ``'path.to.MyStaticFilesStorage'``."
msgstr ""
"Ansin socraigh an cúltaca stórála ``staticfiles`` in:setting: `STORAGES` "
"socrú go ```Path.to.myStaticFilesStorage``."

msgid "Some commonly used options are:"
msgstr "Is iad roinnt roghanna a úsáidtear coitianta:"

msgid "Do NOT prompt the user for input of any kind."
msgstr "NÁ spreag an t-úsáideoir le haghaidh ionchur de chineál ar bith."

msgid ""
"Ignore files, directories, or paths matching this glob-style pattern. Use "
"multiple times to ignore more. When specifying a path, always use forward "
"slashes, even on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Déan neamhaird ar chomhaid, eolairí nó cosáin a mheaitseann leis an bpatrún "
"stíl Úsáid arís agus arís eile chun neamhaird a dhéanamh de Agus cosán á "
"shonrú agat, bain úsáid as slashes ar aghaidh i gcónaí, fiú ar Windows."

msgid "Do everything except modify the filesystem."
msgstr "Déan gach rud seachas an córas comhaid a mhodhnú."

msgid ""
"Clear the existing files before trying to copy or link the original file."
msgstr ""
"Glanaigh na comhaid atá ann cheana sula ndéanann tú iarracht an comhad "
"bunaidh a chóipeáil nó"

msgid "Create a symbolic link to each file instead of copying."
msgstr "Cruthaigh nasc siombalach le gach comhad in ionad cóipeáil."

msgid ""
"Don't call "
"the :meth:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage.post_process` "
"method of the configured ``staticfiles`` storage backend "
"from :setting:`STORAGES`."
msgstr ""
"Ná glaoigh ar an modh: meth: "
"`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.staticFilesStorage.post_process` ar an "
"gcúltaca stórála ``staticfiles`` cumraithe ó:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"Don't ignore the common private glob-style patterns ``'CVS'``, ``'.*'`` and "
"``'*~'``."
msgstr ""
"Ná déan neamhaird ar na patrúin choitianta i stíl glob príobháideacha "
"``'CVS'``, ```.*'`` agus ```*~'``."

msgid "For a full list of options, refer to the commands own help by running:"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh liosta iomlán roghanna, féach ar na horduithe cabhair féin trí "
"rith:"

msgid "Customizing the ignored pattern list"
msgstr "An liosta patrún a neamhaird a shaincheapadh"

msgid ""
"The default ignored pattern list, ``['CVS', '.*', '*~']``, can be customized "
"in a more persistent way than providing the ``--ignore`` command option at "
"each ``collectstatic`` invocation. Provide a "
"custom :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` class, override the "
"``ignore_patterns`` attribute of this class and replace "
"``'django.contrib.staticfiles'`` with that class path in "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an liosta patrún réamhshocraithe a neamhaird, ``['CVS', '.*', "
"'*~']``, a shaincheapadh ar bhealach níos leanúnach ná an rogha ordaithe ``--"
"ignore`` a sholáthar ag gach iontráil ``collectstatic``. Cuir aicme "
"saincheapa:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` ar fáil, athsháraigh tréith "
"``ignore_patterns`` den rang seo agus cuir ``django.contrib.staticfiles'` in "
"ionad an cosán ranga sin i do shuíomh: `INSTALLED_APPS`:"

msgid "``findstatic``"
msgstr "``findstatic``"

msgid "Searches for one or more relative paths with the enabled finders."
msgstr ""
"Cuardaigh cosáin choibhneasta amháin nó níos mó leis na faighteoirí "
"cumasaithe."

msgid ""
"By default, all matching locations are found. To only return the first match "
"for each relative path, use the ``--first`` option:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, faightear gach suíomh meaitseála. Chun an chéad "
"chluiche a thabhairt ar ais amháin do gach cosán coibhneasta, bain úsáid as "
"an rogha ``--first``:"

msgid ""
"This is a debugging aid; it'll show you exactly which static file will be "
"collected for a given path."
msgstr ""
"Is cúnamh dífhabhtaithe é seo; taispeánfaidh sé duit go díreach cén comhad "
"statach a bhailfear le haghaidh cosán ar leith."

msgid ""
"By setting the ``--verbosity`` flag to 0, you can suppress the extra output "
"and just get the path names:"
msgstr ""
"Trí bhratach ``--verbosity`` a shocrú go 0, is féidir leat an t-aschur "
"breise a chur faoi chois agus ainmneacha na cosáin a fháil:"

msgid ""
"On the other hand, by setting the ``--verbosity`` flag to 2, you can get all "
"the directories which were searched:"
msgstr ""
"Ar an láimh eile, tríd an bhratach ``--verbosity`` a shocrú go 2, is féidir "
"leat na heolairí go léir a cuardaíodh a fháil:"

msgid "``runserver``"
msgstr "``Runserver``"

msgid ""
"Overrides the core :djadmin:`runserver` command if the ``staticfiles`` app "
"is :setting:`installed<INSTALLED_APPS>` and adds automatic serving of static "
"files. File serving doesn't run through :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`."
msgstr ""
"<INSTALLED_APPS>Sáraíonn an t-ordú core: djadmin: `runserver` más é an aip "
"`staticfiles``: setting: `suiteáil` agus cuireann sé freastal uathoibríoch "
"comhaid statacha leis. Ní ritheann seirbhísiú comhad trí:setting: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`."

msgid "The command adds these options:"
msgstr "Cuireann an t-ordú na roghanna seo leis:"

msgid ""
"Use the ``--nostatic`` option to disable serving of static files with "
"the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` app entirely. This option "
"is only available if the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` app "
"is in your project's :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an rogha ``--nostatic`` chun freastal comhaid statacha a dhíchumasú "
"leis an aip: doc: `staticfiles` go hiomlán </ref/contrib/staticfiles>. Níl "
"an rogha seo ar fáil ach amháin má tá an aip: doc: `staticfiles` i do shocrú "
"tionscadal: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` </ref/contrib/staticfiles>."

msgid "Example usage:"
msgstr "Úsáid sampla:"

msgid ""
"Use the ``--insecure`` option to force serving of static files with "
"the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` app even if "
"the :setting:`DEBUG` setting is ``False``. By using this you acknowledge the "
"fact that it's **grossly inefficient** and probably **insecure**. This is "
"only intended for local development, should **never be used in production** "
"and is only available if the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` "
"app is in your project's :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an rogha ``--insecure`` chun comhaid statacha a sheirbheáil a chur i "
"bhfeidhm leis an aip: doc: `staticfiles` fiú más é an socrú:setting: `DEBUG` "
"`False`` </ref/contrib/staticfiles>. Trí úsáid a bhaint as seo admhaíonn tú "
"go bhfuil sé thar a bheith neamhéifeachtúil** agus is dócha go bhfuil sé "
"neamhchinnteach**. Níl sé seo beartaithe ach d'fhorbairt áitiúil, níor "
"cheart é a úsáid riamh i dtáirgeach** agus níl sé ar fáil ach amháin má tá "
"an aip: doc: `staticfiles` i socrú do thionscad:setting: `</ref/contrib/"
"staticfiles> INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"``--insecure`` doesn't work "
"with :class:`~.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage`."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibríonn ``--insecure`` le:class: `~.storage.manifestStaticFilesStorage`."

msgid "Storages"
msgstr "Stórálaí"

msgid "``StaticFilesStorage``"
msgstr "``Stóráil Comhad Static``"

msgid ""
"A subclass of the :class:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage` "
"storage backend that uses the :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` setting as the base "
"file system location and the :setting:`STATIC_URL` setting respectively as "
"the base URL."
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme den chúltaca stórála:class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.filesystemStorage` a úsáideann an socrú:setting: "
"`STATIC_ROOT` mar shuíomh an chórais chomhaid bonn agus an socrú: "
"`STATIC_URL` faoi seach mar an bunURL."

msgid ""
"If this method is defined on a storage, it's called by "
"the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command after each run and gets "
"passed the local storages and paths of found files as a dictionary, as well "
"as the command line options. It yields tuples of three values: "
"``original_path, processed_path, processed``. The path values are strings "
"and ``processed`` is a boolean indicating whether or not the value was post-"
"processed, or an exception if post-processing failed."
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhínítear an modh seo ar stóráil, glaonn an t-ordú bainistíochta: "
"djadmin: `collectstatic` air tar éis gach rith agus cuirtear ar na stórais "
"agus na gcosáin áitiúla comhaid a aimsítear mar fhoclóir, chomh maith leis "
"na roghanna líne ordaithe. Tugann sé bealaí de thrí luach: ``original_path, "
"processsed_path, processsed``. Is teaghráin iad na luachanna cosáin agus is "
"boolean é “próiseáilte” a léiríonn cibé an raibh an luach iar-phróiseáilte "
"nó nach raibh, nó eisceacht má theip ar iar-phróiseáil."

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` "
"uses this behind the scenes to replace the paths with their hashed "
"counterparts and update the cache appropriately."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an: Class: "
"`~django.contrib.staticFiles.Storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` é seo taobh "
"thiar de na radhairc chun a gcomhghleacaithe hashaithe a chur in ionad na "
"cosáin agus an taisce a nuashonrú go cuí."

msgid "``ManifestStaticFilesStorage``"
msgstr "``Stóráil Comhad ManifestStatic``"

msgid ""
"A subclass of "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage` storage "
"backend which stores the file names it handles by appending the MD5 hash of "
"the file's content to the filename. For example, the file ``css/styles.css`` "
"would also be saved as ``css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css``."
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme den chúltaca stórála:class: "
"`~django.contrib.staticFiles.Storage.staticFilesStorage` a stóráil na "
"hainmneacha comhaid a láimhseálann sé trí hash MD5 d'ábhar an chomhaid a "
"chur leis an ainm comhaid. Mar shampla, sábhálfaí an comhad ``css/"
"styles.css`` mar `css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css`` freisin."

msgid ""
"The purpose of this storage is to keep serving the old files in case some "
"pages still refer to those files, e.g. because they are cached by you or a "
"3rd party proxy server. Additionally, it's very helpful if you want to apply "
"`far future Expires headers`_ to the deployed files to speed up the load "
"time for subsequent page visits."
msgstr ""
"Is é cuspóir an stórála seo freastal ar na sean-chomhaid i gcás go "
"dtagraíonn roinnt leathanaigh fós do na comhaid sin, m.sh. toisc go bhfuil "
"tú féin nó seachfhreastalaí tríú páirtí iad a chosc. Ina theannta sin, tá sé "
"an-chabhrach más mian leat `ceannteidiúirí in éag sa todhchaí' _ a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar na comhaid imscartha chun an t-am ualaigh a bhrostú le haghaidh "
"cuairteanna leathanaigh ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid ""
"The storage backend automatically replaces the paths found in the saved "
"files matching other saved files with the path of the cached copy (using "
"the :meth:`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage.post_process` "
"method). The regular expressions used to find those paths "
"(``django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.HashedFilesMixin.patterns``) cover:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an cúltaca stórála in ionad na cosáin a fhaightear sna comhaid "
"shábháilte a mheaitseálann comhaid shábháilte eile le cosán na cóip taisce "
"(ag baint úsáide as an modh:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.staticfilesStorage.post_process`). "
"Clúdaíonn na nathanna rialta a úsáidtear chun na cosáin sin a aimsiú "
"(``Django.Contrib.StaticFiles.Storage.HashedFilesMixin.Patterns``):"

msgid ""
"The `@import`_ rule and `url()`_ statement of `Cascading Style Sheets`_."
msgstr ""
"An riail `@import `_ agus an ráiteas `url () `_ ar `Bileoga Stíl Cascading`_."

msgid "`Source map`_ comments in CSS and JavaScript files."
msgstr "Tuairimí `léarscáil foinse`_ i gcomhaid CSS agus JavaScript."

msgid ""
"Subclass ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` and set the "
"``support_js_module_import_aggregation`` attribute to ``True``, if you want "
"to use the experimental regular expressions to cover:"
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` agus socraigh an tréith "
"``support_js_module_import_aggregation`` le `True``, más mian leat na "
"nathanna rialta turgnamhacha a úsáid chun clúdach:"

msgid "The `modules import`_ in JavaScript."
msgstr "Iompórtáil na modúil i JavaScript."

msgid "The `modules aggregation`_ in JavaScript."
msgstr "An `comhiomlánú modúl`_ i JavaScript."

msgid "For example, the ``'css/styles.css'`` file with this content:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, an comhad ``css/styles.css'`` leis an ábhar seo:"

msgid ""
"...would be replaced by calling "
"the :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.url` method of the "
"``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` storage backend, ultimately saving a ``'css/"
"styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css'`` file with the following content:"
msgstr ""
"... cuireadh in ionad an modh cúltaca stórála ``ManifeststaticFilesStorage`` "
"`ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` a ghlaoch, `~django.core.files.storage.url`, "
"ag sábháil comhad ```css/styles.55e7cbb9ba48.css'` leis an ábhar seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid "Usage of the ``integrity`` HTML attribute with local files"
msgstr "Úsáid an tréith HTML ``comhláiteacht ``le comhaid áitiúla"

msgid ""
"When using the optional ``integrity`` attribute within tags like "
"``<script>`` or ``<link>``, its value should be calculated based on the "
"files as they are served, not as stored in the filesystem. This is "
"particularly important because depending on how static files are collected, "
"their checksum may have changed (for example when "
"using :djadmin:`collectstatic`). At the moment, there is no out-of-the-box "
"tooling available for this."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear an tréith roghnach ``sláiteacht ``laistigh de chlibeanna "
"mar`` ``nó`` <script>``, ba ch <link>eart a luach a ríomh bunaithe ar na "
"comhaid mar a sheirbheáltar iad, ní mar atá stóráilte sa chóras comhaid. Tá "
"sé seo tábhachtach go háirithe mar, ag brath ar an gcaoi a mbailítear "
"comhaid statacha, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh athrú ar a seicsum (mar shampla "
"nuair a úsáidtear: djadmin: `collectstatic`). I láthair na huaire, níl aon "
"uirlisí lasmuigh den bhosca ar fáil chuige seo."

msgid ""
"You can change the location of the manifest file by using a custom "
"``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` subclass that sets the ``manifest_storage`` "
"argument. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat suíomh an chomhaid léirithe a athrú trí fho-aicme "
"saincheaptha ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` a shocraíonn an argóint "
"``manifest_storage`` a úsáid. Mar shampla::"

msgid "References in comments"
msgstr "Tagairtí i dtuairimí"

msgid ""
"``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` doesn't ignore paths in statements that are "
"commented out. This :ticket:`may crash on the nonexistent paths <21080>`. "
"You should check and eventually strip comments."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` neamhaird de chosáin i ráitis a "
"ndéantar trácht orthu. <21080>Seo:ticéad: `d'fhéadfadh titim ar na cosáin "
"nach bhfuil ann `. Ba chóir duit tuairimí a sheiceáil agus sa deireadh a "
"bhaint"

msgid ""
"This attribute provides a single hash that changes whenever a file in the "
"manifest changes. This can be useful to communicate to SPAs that the assets "
"on the server have changed (due to a new deployment)."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an tréith seo hash amháin a athraíonn aon uair a athraíonn "
"comhad sa léiriú. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith úsáideach chun cur in iúl do "
"SPAanna go bhfuil athrú tagtha ar na sócmhainní ar an bhfreastalaí (mar "
"gheall ar imscaradh nua)."

msgid ""
"Since static files might reference other static files that need to have "
"their paths replaced, multiple passes of replacing paths may be needed until "
"the file hashes converge. To prevent an infinite loop due to hashes not "
"converging (for example, if ``'foo.css'`` references ``'bar.css'`` which "
"references ``'foo.css'``) there is a maximum number of passes before post-"
"processing is abandoned. In cases with a large number of references, a "
"higher number of passes might be needed. Increase the maximum number of "
"passes by subclassing ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` and setting the "
"``max_post_process_passes`` attribute. It defaults to 5."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhféadfadh comhaid statacha tagairt a dhéanamh do chomhaid "
"statacha eile a gcaithfear a gcosáin a athsholáthar, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh "
"gá le pasanna iolracha de chosáin athsholáthair go dtí Chun lúb gan teorainn "
"a chosc mar gheall ar hashes nach bhfuil ag teacht le chéile (mar shampla, "
"má thagann ``'foo.css'`` tagairtí ``'bar.css'`` a thagann tagairt do "
"``'foo.css'``) tá líon uasta pasanna ann sula dtréigtear an iar-phróiseáil. "
"I gcásanna a bhfuil líon mór tagairtí acu, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh líon níos "
"airde pasanna ag teastáil. Méadaigh an líon uasta pasanna trí "
"`ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` a fho-aicmiú agus an tréith "
"``max_post_process_passes`` a shocrú. Tá sé réamhshocraithe go 5."

msgid ""
"To enable the ``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` you have to make sure the "
"following requirements are met:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an `ManifeststaticFilesStorage`` a chumasú caithfidh tú a chinntiú go "
"gcomhlíontar na riachtanais seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"the ``staticfiles`` storage backend in :setting:`STORAGES` setting is set to "
"``'django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage'``"
msgstr ""
"an cúltaca stórála ``staticfiles`` in:setting: socraítear socrú `STORAGES` "
"go ``django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.manifestStaticFilesStorage'``"

msgid "the :setting:`DEBUG` setting is set to ``False``"
msgstr "socraítear an socrú: `DEBUG` go ``False``"

msgid ""
"you've collected all your static files by using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` "
"management command"
msgstr ""
"bhailigh tú do chuid comhad statacha go léir tríd an ordú bainistíochta: "
"djadmin: `collectstatic` a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Since creating the MD5 hash can be a performance burden to your website "
"during runtime, ``staticfiles`` will automatically store the mapping with "
"hashed names for all processed files in a file called ``staticfiles.json``. "
"This happens once when you run the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é gur féidir le cruthú an hash MD5 a bheith ina ualach feidhmíochta "
"ar do shuíomh Gréasáin le linn rith ama, stóráilfidh `staticfiles`` an "
"mapáil go huathoibríoch le hainmneacha hashaithe do gach comhad próiseáilte "
"i gcomhad ar a dtugtar ``staticfiles.json``. Tarlaíonn sé seo uair amháin "
"nuair a ritheann tú an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic`."

msgid ""
"If a file isn't found in the ``staticfiles.json`` manifest at runtime, a "
"``ValueError`` is raised. This behavior can be disabled by subclassing "
"``ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` and setting the ``manifest_strict`` attribute "
"to ``False`` -- nonexistent paths will remain unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfaightear comhad sa léiriú ``staticfiles.json`` ag an am rith, "
"ardaítear ``ValueError``. Is féidir an t-iompar seo a dhíchumasú trí "
"`ManifestStaticFilesStorage`` a fho-aicmiú agus an tréith "
"``manifest_strict`` a shocrú le ``False`` - fanfaidh cosáin nach bhfuil ann "
"gan athrú."

msgid ""
"Due to the requirement of running :djadmin:`collectstatic`, this storage "
"typically shouldn't be used when running tests as ``collectstatic`` isn't "
"run as part of the normal test setup. During testing, ensure that "
"``staticfiles`` storage backend in the :setting:`STORAGES` setting is set to "
"something else like "
"``'django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage'`` (the default)."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an riachtanas a bhaineann le rith: djadmin: `collectstatic`, "
"de ghnáth níor cheart an stóráil seo a úsáid agus tástálacha á reáchtáil mar "
"nach reáchtáiltear ``collectstatic`` mar chuid den ghnáthshocrú tástála. Le "
"linn na tástála, déan cinnte go bhfuil cúltaca stórála ``staticfiles`` sa "
"socrú: `STORAGES` socraithe ar rud éigin eile cosúil le "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.staticfilesStorage`` (an "
"réamhshocraithe)."

msgid ""
"The method that is used when creating the hashed name of a file. Needs to "
"return a hash for the given file name and content. By default it calculates "
"a MD5 hash from the content's chunks as mentioned above. Feel free to "
"override this method to use your own hashing algorithm."
msgstr ""
"An modh a úsáidtear agus ainm hashed comhad á chruthú. Ní mór hash a "
"thabhairt ar ais le haghaidh ainm agus ábhar an chomhaid tugtha. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe ríomhann sé hash MD5 ó phíosaí an ábhair mar a luaitear "
"thuas. Ná bíodh leisce ort an modh seo a shárú chun d'algartam hashing féin "
"a úsáid."

msgid "``ManifestFilesMixin``"
msgstr "``ManifestFilesMixin``"

msgid ""
"Use this mixin with a custom storage to append the MD5 hash of the file's "
"content to the filename as :class:`~storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` does."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an meascán seo le stóráil saincheaptha chun hash MD5 d'ábhar an "
"chomhaid a chur leis an ainm comhaid mar: class: "
"`~Storage.ManifestStaticFilesStorage` a dhéanann."

msgid "Finders Module"
msgstr "Modúl aimsitheoirí"

msgid ""
"``staticfiles`` finders has a ``searched_locations`` attribute which is a "
"list of directory paths in which the finders searched. Example usage::"
msgstr ""
"Tá tréith ``searched_locations`` ag aimsitheoirí ``staticfiles`` ar liosta "
"de na cosáin eolaire inar chuardaigh na faighteoirí. Úsáid sampla::"

msgid "Other Helpers"
msgstr "Cúntóirí Eile"

msgid ""
"There are a few other helpers outside of the :mod:`staticfiles "
"<django.contrib.staticfiles>` app to work with static files:"
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla cúntóir eile lasmuigh den aip: mod: `staticfiles "
"<django.contrib.staticfiles>`chun oibriú le comhaid statacha:"

msgid ""
"The :func:`django.template.context_processors.static` context processor "
"which adds :setting:`STATIC_URL` to every template context rendered "
"with :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` contexts."
msgstr ""
"An próiseálaí comhthéacs: Func: `django.template.context_processors.static` "
"a chuireann: socrú: `STATIC_URL` le gach comhthéacs teimpléad a rinneadh "
"le:class: `~django.template.requestContext` comhthéacsanna."

msgid ""
"The builtin template tag :ttag:`static` which takes a path and urljoins it "
"with the static prefix :setting:`STATIC_URL`. If "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles`` is installed, the tag uses the ``url()`` "
"method of the ``staticfiles`` storage backend from :setting:`STORAGES` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Tag:ttag an teimpléad tógáilte: `static` a thógann cosán agus a cheanglaíonn "
"leis an réamhshocrú statach: socrú: `STATIC_URL`. Má tá "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles`` suiteáilte, úsáideann an chlib an modh ``url "
"() ``den chúlcheann stórála ``staticfiles`` ó:setting: `STORAGES` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"The builtin template tag :ttag:`get_static_prefix` which populates a "
"template variable with the static prefix :setting:`STATIC_URL` to be used as "
"a variable or directly."
msgstr ""
"Tag:ttag: `get_static_prefix` an teimpléad bunaithe a chuireann athróg "
"teimpléad leis an réamhshocrú statach: setting: `STATIC_URL` le húsáid mar "
"athróg nó go díreach."

msgid ""
"The similar template tag :ttag:`get_media_prefix` which works "
"like :ttag:`get_static_prefix` but uses :setting:`MEDIA_URL`."
msgstr ""
"An teimpléad den chineál céanna tag:ttag: `get_media_prefix` a oibríonn "
"cosúil:ttag: `get_static_prefix` ach úsáideann sé: socrú: `MEDIA_URL`."

msgid ""
"The ``staticfiles`` key in :data:`django.core.files.storage.storages` "
"contains a ready-to-use instance of the staticfiles storage backend."
msgstr ""
"Sa eochair `staticfiles`` in:data: `django.core.files.storage.storages` tá "
"sampla réidh le húsáid de chúlcheann stórála staticfiles."

msgid "Static file development view"
msgstr "Amharc forbartha comhad statach"

msgid ""
"The static files tools are mostly designed to help with getting static files "
"successfully deployed into production. This usually means a separate, "
"dedicated static file server, which is a lot of overhead to mess with when "
"developing locally. Thus, the ``staticfiles`` app ships with a **quick and "
"dirty helper view** that you can use to serve files locally in development."
msgstr ""
"Tá na huirlisí comhaid statacha deartha den chuid is mó chun cabhrú le "
"comhaid statacha a imscaradh go rathúil i dtáirgeadh. De ghnáth ciallaíonn "
"sé seo freastalaí comhad statach ar leithligh, tiomnaithe, atá go leor "
"lasbhairde le praiseach leis agus tú ag forbairt go háitiúil. Dá bhrí sin, "
"seoltar an aip `staticfiles`` le radharc cúntóra tapa agus salach** is "
"féidir leat a úsáid chun comhaid a sheirbheáil go háitiúil atá i bhforbairt."

msgid "This view function serves static files in development."
msgstr "Freastalaíonn an fheidhm radhairc seo ar chomhaid statacha atá i bh"

msgid "This view will only work if :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True``."
msgstr "Ní oibreoidh an dearcadh seo ach mura bhfuil: socrú: `DEBUG` ``True``."

msgid ""
"That's because this view is **grossly inefficient** and probably "
"**insecure**. This is only intended for local development, and should "
"**never be used in production**."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé sin toisc go bhfuil an dearcadh seon**an-neamhéifeachtúil** agus is "
"dóchúil** neamhchinnteach**. Níl sé seo beartaithe ach d'fhorbairt áitiúil, "
"agus níor cheart é a úsáid riamh i dtáirgeach**."

msgid ""
"To guess the served files' content types, this view relies on "
"the :py:mod:`mimetypes` module from the Python standard library, which "
"itself relies on the underlying platform's map files. If you find that this "
"view doesn't return proper content types for certain files, it is most "
"likely that the platform's map files are incorrect or need to be updated. "
"This can be achieved, for example, by installing or updating the ``mailcap`` "
"package on a Red Hat distribution, ``mime-support`` on a Debian "
"distribution, or by editing the keys under ``HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT`` in the "
"Windows registry."
msgstr ""
"Chun cineálacha ábhair na gcomhaid a sheirbheáiltear a thuairim, braitheann "
"an dearcadh seo ar an modúl: py:mod: `mimetypes` ó leabharlann caighdeánach "
