msgid "Cross Site Request Forgery protection"
msgstr "Iarratas ar Trasláithreán Cosaint Fholsaíochta"

msgid ""
"The CSRF middleware and template tag provides easy-to-use protection against "
"`Cross Site Request Forgeries`_. This type of attack occurs when a malicious "
"website contains a link, a form button or some JavaScript that is intended "
"to perform some action on your website, using the credentials of a logged-in "
"user who visits the malicious site in their browser. A related type of "
"attack, 'login CSRF', where an attacking site tricks a user's browser into "
"logging into a site with someone else's credentials, is also covered."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an clib meán-earraí agus teimpléad CSRF cosaint atá éasca le "
"húsáid i gcoinne `Forgeasaithe Iarratais Tras-Láithreacha`_. Tarlaíonn an "
"cineál ionsaithe seo nuair a bhíonn nasc, cnaipe foirme nó roinnt JavaScript "
"i láithreán gréasáin mailíseach atá beartaithe chun gníomh éigin a dhéanamh "
"ar do shuíomh Gréasáin, ag úsáid dintiúir úsáideora logáilte isteach a "
"thugann cuairt ar an suíomh mailíseach ina mbrabhsálaí. Clúdaítear cineál "
"ionsaí gaolmhar, 'logáil isteach CSRF', áit a gcuireann suíomh ionsaitheach "
"brabhsálaí úsáideora isteach i suíomh le dintiúir duine eile, clúdaithe "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"The first defense against CSRF attacks is to ensure that GET requests (and "
"other 'safe' methods, as defined by :rfc:`9110#section-9.2.1`) are side "
"effect free. Requests via 'unsafe' methods, such as POST, PUT, and DELETE, "
"can then be protected by the steps outlined in :ref:`using-csrf`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chosaint i gcoinne ionsaithe CSRF ná a chinntiú go bhfuil "
"iarratais GET (agus modhanna 'sábháilte' eile, mar a shainmhínítear ag: rfc: "
"`9110 #section -9.2.1`) saor ó fho-iarsmaí. Is féidir iarratais trí "
"mhodhanna 'neamhshábháilte', mar shampla POST, PUT, agus DELETE, a chosaint "
"leis na céimeanna a leagtar amach in:ref: `using-csrf`."

msgid "The CSRF protection is based on the following things:"
msgstr "Tá cosaint CSRF bunaithe ar na rudaí seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"A CSRF cookie that is a random secret value, which other sites will not have "
"access to."
msgstr ""
"Fianán CSRF atá ina luach rúnda randamach é, nach mbeidh rochtain ag "
"suíomhanna eile air."

msgid ""
"``CsrfViewMiddleware`` sends this cookie with the response whenever "
"``django.middleware.csrf.get_token()`` is called. It can also send it in "
"other cases. For security reasons, the value of the secret is changed each "
"time a user logs in."
msgstr ""
"Seolann ``csrfViewMiddleware`` an fianán seo leis an bhfreagra aon uair a "
"thugtar ``django.middleware.csrf.get_token () ``. Féadfaidh sé é a sheoladh "
"i gcásanna eile freisin. Ar chúiseanna slándála, athraítear luach an rúnda "
"gach uair a logálann úsáideoir isteach."

msgid ""
"A hidden form field with the name 'csrfmiddlewaretoken', present in all "
"outgoing POST forms."
msgstr ""
"Réimse foirme i bhfolach leis an ainm 'csrfmiddlewaretoken', atá i láthair i "
"ngach foirm POST atá ag imeacht."

msgid ""
"In order to protect against `BREACH`_ attacks, the value of this field is "
"not simply the secret. It is scrambled differently with each response using "
"a mask. The mask is generated randomly on every call to ``get_token()``, so "
"the form field value is different each time."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn cosaint a dhéanamh ar ionsaithe `BREACH`_, ní hé luach an réimse seo "
"ach an rún. Déantar é a scrampáil go difriúil le gach freagra ag baint "
"úsáide as masc. Gintear an masc go randamach ar gach glao chuig ``get_token "
"() ``, mar sin tá luach réimse na foirme difriúil gach uair."

msgid "This part is done by the :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag."
msgstr "Déantar an chuid seo ag an gclib teimpléad:ttag: `csrf_token`."

msgid ""
"For all incoming requests that are not using HTTP GET, HEAD, OPTIONS or "
"TRACE, a CSRF cookie must be present, and the 'csrfmiddlewaretoken' field "
"must be present and correct. If it isn't, the user will get a 403 error."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le gach iarratas atá ag teacht isteach nach n-úsáideann HTTP GET, "
"HEAD, OPTIONS nó TRACE, caithfidh fianán CSRF a bheith i láthair, agus "
"caithfidh an réimse 'csrfmiddlewaretoken' a bheith i láthair agus ceart. "
"Mura bhfuil sé, gheobhaidh an t-úsáideoir earráid 403."

msgid ""
"When validating the 'csrfmiddlewaretoken' field value, only the secret, not "
"the full token, is compared with the secret in the cookie value. This allows "
"the use of ever-changing tokens. While each request may use its own token, "
"the secret remains common to all."
msgstr ""
"Agus luach réimse 'csrfmiddlewaretoken' á bhailíochtú, ní dhéantar ach an "
"rún, ní an comhartha iomlán, a chur i gcomparáid leis an rún sa luach "
"fianán. Ligeann sé seo comharthaí atá ag athrú i gcónaí a úsáid. Cé go "
"bhféadfaidh gach iarratas a chomhartha féin a úsáid, fós an rún coitianta do "
"gach duine."

msgid "This check is done by ``CsrfViewMiddleware``."
msgstr "Déanann an seiceáil seo ag ``CSRFViewMiddleware``."

msgid ""
"``CsrfViewMiddleware`` verifies the `Origin header`_, if provided by the "
"browser, against the current host and the :setting:`CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` "
"setting. This provides protection against cross-subdomain attacks."
msgstr ""
"Fíoraíonn ``CSRFViewMiddleware`` an ceannteideal `Origin `_, má "
"sholáthraíonn an brabhsálaí, i gcoinne an óstach reatha agus an "
"socrú:setting: `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`. Soláthraíonn sé seo cosaint i gcoinne "
"ionsaithe trasfho-fearainn."

msgid ""
"In addition, for HTTPS requests, if the ``Origin`` header isn't provided, "
"``CsrfViewMiddleware`` performs strict referer checking. This means that "
"even if a subdomain can set or modify cookies on your domain, it can't force "
"a user to post to your application since that request won't come from your "
"own exact domain."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, maidir le hiarratais HTTPS, mura gcuirtear an ceannteideal "
"``Origin` ar fáil, déanann `CSRFViewMiddleware`` seiceáil docht atreoraithe. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo fiú más féidir le fo-fhearann fianáin a shocrú nó a "
"mhodhnú ar do fhearann, ní féidir leis iallach a chur ar úsáideoir postáil "
"chuig d'iarratas ós rud é nach dtiocfaidh an t-iarratas sin ó do fhearann "
"cruinn féin."

msgid ""
"This also addresses a man-in-the-middle attack that's possible under HTTPS "
"when using a session independent secret, due to the fact that HTTP ``Set-"
"Cookie`` headers are (unfortunately) accepted by clients even when they are "
"talking to a site under HTTPS. (Referer checking is not done for HTTP "
"requests because the presence of the ``Referer`` header isn't reliable "
"enough under HTTP.)"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé seo aghaidh freisin ar ionsaí fear in-the-lár atá indéanta faoi "
"HTTPS agus rún neamhspleách seisiúin á úsáid, toisc go nglacann cliaint (ar "
"an drochuair) ceannteidil HTTP `Set-Cookie` fiú nuair a bhíonn siad ag caint "
"le suíomh faoi HTTPS. (Ní dhéantar seiceáil atreoraithe le haghaidh "
"iarratais HTTP toisc nach bhfuil láithreacht an cheanntásc ``Referer`` "
"iontaofa go leor faoi HTTP.)"

msgid ""
"If the :setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN` setting is set, the referer is compared "
"against it. You can allow cross-subdomain requests by including a leading "
"dot. For example, ``CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN = '.example.com'`` will allow POST "
"requests from ``www.example.com`` and ``api.example.com``. If the setting is "
"not set, then the referer must match the HTTP ``Host`` header."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an socrú: setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN` socraithe, déantar an "
"tagairteoir i gcomparáid ina choinne. Is féidir leat iarratais tras-fho-"
"fhearann a cheadú trí phríomhphointe a áireamh. Mar shampla, ceadóidh "
"``CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN = '.example.com'`` iarratais POST ó `www.example.com`` "
"agus ``api.example.com``. Mura bhfuil an socrú socraithe, ansin caithfidh an "
"tagairteoir an ceannteideal HTTP ``Host`` a mheaitseáil."

msgid ""
"Expanding the accepted referers beyond the current host or cookie domain can "
"be done with the :setting:`CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na tagairteoirí a nglactar leo a leathnú thar an bhfearann óstach "
"nó fianán reatha a dhéanamh leis an socrú: setting: `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`."

msgid ""
"This ensures that only forms that have originated from trusted domains can "
"be used to POST data back."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn sé seo nach féidir ach foirmeacha a tháinig ó fearainn iontaofa a "
"úsáid chun sonraí POST ar ais."

msgid ""
"It deliberately ignores GET requests (and other requests that are defined as "
"'safe' by :rfc:`9110#section-9.2.1`). These requests ought never to have any "
"potentially dangerous side effects, and so a CSRF attack with a GET request "
"ought to be harmless. :rfc:`9110#section-9.2.1` defines POST, PUT, and "
"DELETE as 'unsafe', and all other methods are also assumed to be unsafe, for "
"maximum protection."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé neamhaird d'aon ghnó ar iarratais GET (agus iarratais eile a "
"shainmhínítear mar 'sábháilte' ag: rfc: `9110 #section -9.2.1`). Níor cheart "
"go mbeadh aon fho-iarsmaí a d'fhéadfadh a bheith contúirteach a bheith ag na "
"hiarratais seo riamh, agus mar sin ba chóir go mbeadh ionsaí CSRF le "
"hiarratas GET ne :rfc: Sainmhíníonn `9110 #section -9.2.1` POST, PUT, agus "
"DELETE mar 'neamhshábháilte', agus glactar leis go bhfuil gach modh eile "
"neamhshábháilte, chun an chosaint is mó."

msgid ""
"The CSRF protection cannot protect against man-in-the-middle attacks, so "
"use :ref:`HTTPS <security-recommendation-ssl>` with :ref:`http-strict-"
"transport-security`. It also assumes :ref:`validation of the HOST header "
"<host-headers-virtual-hosting>` and that there aren't any :ref:`cross-site "
"scripting vulnerabilities <cross-site-scripting>` on your site (because XSS "
"vulnerabilities already let an attacker do anything a CSRF vulnerability "
"allows and much worse)."
msgstr ""
"<security-recommendation-ssl>Ní féidir leis an gcosaint CSRF cosaint a "
"dhéanamh i gcoinne ionsaithe an duine sa lár, mar sin bain úsáid as: ref: "
"`HTTPS `le: ref: `http-strict-transport-security`. Glacann sé freisin: ref: "
"`bailíochtú ceanntásc HOST <host-headers-virtual-hosting>`agus nach bhfuil "
"aon leochaileachtaí scrip <cross-site-scripting>teanna tras-láithreáin ann "
"ar do shuíomh (toisc go ligeann leochaileachtaí XSS d'ionsaitheoir aon rud a "
"cheadaíonn leochaileacht CSRF a dhéanamh agus i bhfad níos measa)."

msgid "Removing the ``Referer`` header"
msgstr "An ceanntásc ``Referer`` a bhaint"

msgid ""
"To avoid disclosing the referrer URL to third-party sites, you might want to "
"`disable the referer`_ on your site's ``<a>`` tags. For example, you might "
"use the ``<meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"no-referrer\">`` tag or include "
"the ``Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`` header. Due to the CSRF protection's "
"strict referer checking on HTTPS requests, those techniques cause a CSRF "
"failure on requests with 'unsafe' methods. Instead, use alternatives like "
"``<a rel=\"noreferrer\" ...>\"`` for links to third-party sites."
msgstr ""
"<a>Chun URL an atreoraithe a nochtadh chuig suíomhanna tríú páirtí a "
"sheachaint, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an réiteoir a dhíchumasú ar chlibeanna "
"```do shuíomh. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá an chlib ```a úsáid nó an ceannteideal "
"<meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"no-referrer\">``Refrer-Policy: no-atreor`` "
"a chur san áireamh. Mar gheall ar sheiceáil dhian atreoraithe na cosanta "
"CSRF ar iarratais HTTPS, is cúis le teip CSRF ar iarratais le modhanna "
"'neamhshábháilte' ar na teicnící sin. Ina áit sin, bain úsáid as roghanna "
"eile mar ``<a rel=\"noreferrer\" ...>“`` le haghaidh naisc chuig suíomhanna "
"tríú páirtí."

msgid ""
"Subdomains within a site will be able to set cookies on the client for the "
"whole domain. By setting the cookie and using a corresponding token, "
"subdomains will be able to circumvent the CSRF protection. The only way to "
"avoid this is to ensure that subdomains are controlled by trusted users (or, "
"are at least unable to set cookies). Note that even without CSRF, there are "
"other vulnerabilities, such as session fixation, that make giving subdomains "
"to untrusted parties a bad idea, and these vulnerabilities cannot easily be "
"fixed with current browsers."
msgstr ""
"Beidh fo-fearainn laistigh de shuíomh in ann fianáin a shocrú ar an gcliant "
"don fhearann iomlán. Trí an fianán a shocrú agus comhartha comhfhreagrach a "
"úsáid, beidh fo-fhearann in ann cosaint CSRF a sheachaint. Is é an t-aon "
"bhealach chun é seo a sheachaint ná a chinntiú go bhfuil fo-fhearann á rialú "
"ag úsáideoirí iontaofa (nó, ar a laghad nach bhfuil siad in ann fianáin a "
"shocrú). Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil leochaileachtaí eile ann, mar shampla "
"socrú seisiúin, fiú gan CSRF, a fhágann gur droch-smaoineamh é fo-fhearann a "
"thabhairt do pháirtithe neamhiontaofa, agus ní féidir na leochaileachtaí seo "
"a shocrú go héasca le brabhsálaithe reatha."

msgid "Utilities"
msgstr "fóntais"

msgid ""
"The examples below assume you are using function-based views. If you are "
"working with class-based views, you can refer to :ref:`Decorating class-"
"based views<decorating-class-based-views>`."
msgstr ""
"Glacann na samplaí thíos go bhfuil tuairimí bunaithe ar fheidhm á úsáid agat "
"<decorating-class-based-views>Má tá tú ag obair le tuairimí rang-bhunaithe, "
"is féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh u:ref: `Tuairimí rangbhunaithe a mhaisiú `."

msgid ""
"This decorator marks a view as being exempt from the protection ensured by "
"the middleware. Example::"
msgstr ""
"Marcann an maisitheoir seo go bhfuil dearcadh díolmhaithe ón gcosaint a "
"chinntíonn na meánearraí. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Decorator that provides the protection "
"of :class:`~django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware` to a view."
msgstr ""

msgid "Usage::"
msgstr "Úsáid::"

msgid ""
"Normally the :ttag:`csrf_token` template tag will not work if "
"``CsrfViewMiddleware.process_view`` or an equivalent like ``csrf_protect`` "
"has not run. The view decorator ``requires_csrf_token`` can be used to "
"ensure the template tag does work. This decorator works similarly to "
"``csrf_protect``, but never rejects an incoming request."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth ní oibreoidh an chlib teimpléad:ttag: `csrf_token` mura ritheann "
"``csrfViewMiddleware.process_view`` nó coibhéis cosúil le `csrf_protect``. "
"Is féidir an maisitheoir amharc ``requires_csrf_token`` a úsáid chun a "
"chinntiú go n-oibríonn an chlib teimpléid. Oibríonn an maisitheoir seo ar an "
"gcéanna le `csrf_protect``, ach ní dhiúltaíonn sé iarratas isteach riamh."

msgid "This decorator forces a view to send the CSRF cookie."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an maisitheoir seo iallach ar dhearcadh an fianán CSRF a sheoladh."

msgid "A number of settings can be used to control Django's CSRF behavior:"
msgstr "Is féidir roinnt socruithe a úsáid chun iompar CSRF Django a rialú:"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_AGE`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_AGE`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_NAME`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_NAME`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_PATH`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CSRF_COOKIE_PATH`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_HEADER_NAME`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_HEADER_NAME`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`"

msgid ":setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS`"
msgstr ":setting: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS`"

msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr "Ceisteanna Coitianta"

msgid ""
"Is posting an arbitrary CSRF token pair (cookie and POST data) a "
"vulnerability?"
msgstr ""
"An leochaileacht é péire comhartha treallach CSRF a phostáil (sonraí fianán "
"agus POST)?"

msgid ""
"No, this is by design. Without a man-in-the-middle attack, there is no way "
"for an attacker to send a CSRF token cookie to a victim's browser, so a "
"successful attack would need to obtain the victim's browser's cookie via XSS "
"or similar, in which case an attacker usually doesn't need CSRF attacks."
msgstr ""
"Níl, tá sé seo de réir dearaidh. Gan ionsaí fear sa lár, níl aon bhealach "
"ann d'ionsaitheoir fianán comhartha CSRF a sheoladh chuig brabhsálaí "
"íospartaigh, mar sin bheadh le hionsaí rathúil fianán brabhsálaí an "
"íospartaigh a fháil trí XSS nó dá leithéid, sa chás sin de ghnáth ní "
"theastaíonn ionsaithe CSRF d'ionsaitheoir."

msgid ""
"Some security audit tools flag this as a problem but as mentioned before, an "
"attacker cannot steal a user's browser's CSRF cookie. \"Stealing\" or "
"modifying *your own* token using Firebug, Chrome dev tools, etc. isn't a "
"vulnerability."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann roinnt uirlisí iniúchta slándála mar fhadhb seo ach mar a luadh "
"cheana, ní féidir le hionsaitheoir fianán CSRF brabhsálaí úsáideora a ghoid. "
"Ní leochaileacht é “goid” nó do chomharthaí* féin* a mhodhnú ag baint úsáide "
"as Firebug, uirlisí déanta Chrome, srl."

msgid ""
"Is it a problem that Django's CSRF protection isn't linked to a session by "
"default?"
msgstr ""
"An fadhb í nach bhfuil cosaint CSRF Django nasctha le seisiún de réir "
"réamhshocraithe?"

msgid ""
"No, this is by design. Not linking CSRF protection to a session allows using "
"the protection on sites such as a *pastebin* that allow submissions from "
"anonymous users which don't have a session."
msgstr ""
"Níl, tá sé seo de réir dearaidh. Gan chosaint CSRF a nascadh le seisiún is "
"féidir an chosaint a úsáid ar shuíomhanna cosúil* pastebin* a cheadaíonn "
"aighneachtaí ó úsáideoirí gan ainm nach bhfuil seisiún acu."

msgid ""
"If you wish to store the CSRF token in the user's session, use "
"the :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat an comhartha CSRF a stóráil i seisiún an úsáideora, bain úsáid "
"as an socrú:setting: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS`."

msgid "Why might a user encounter a CSRF validation failure after logging in?"
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth a d'fhéadfadh teip bailíochtaithe CSRF a bheith ag úsáideoir tar "
"éis logáil isteach?"

msgid ""
"For security reasons, CSRF tokens are rotated each time a user logs in. Any "
"page with a form generated before a login will have an old, invalid CSRF "
"token and need to be reloaded. This might happen if a user uses the back "
"button after a login or if they log in a different browser tab."
msgstr ""
"Ar chúiseanna slándála, rothlaítear comharthaí CSRF gach uair a logálann "
"úsáideoir isteach. Beidh sean-chomhartha CSRF neamhbhailí ag aon leathanach "
"le foirm a ghintear roimh logáil isteach agus caithfear é a athluchtú. "
"D'fhéadfadh sé seo tarlú má úsáideann úsáideoir an cnaipe ar ais tar éis "
"logáil isteach nó má logálann siad isteach i gcluaisín brabhsálaí difriúil."

msgid "Databases"
msgstr "Bunachair sonraí"

msgid "Django officially supports the following databases:"
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django go hoifigiúil leis na bunachair sonraí seo"

msgid ":ref:`PostgreSQL <postgresql-notes>`"
msgstr "<postgresql-notes>:ref: `PostgreSQL `"

msgid ":ref:`MariaDB <mariadb-notes>`"
msgstr "<mariadb-notes>:ref: `MariaDB `"

msgid ":ref:`MySQL <mysql-notes>`"
msgstr "<mysql-notes>:ref: `MySQL `"

msgid ":ref:`Oracle <oracle-notes>`"
msgstr "<oracle-notes>:ref: `Oracle `"

msgid ":ref:`SQLite <sqlite-notes>`"
msgstr "<sqlite-notes>:tagairt: `SQLite `"

msgid ""
"There are also a number of :ref:`database backends provided by third parties "
"<third-party-notes>`."
msgstr ""
"<third-party-notes>Tá roinnt cúltaca bunachar sonraí ann freisin: ref: `a "
"sholáthraíonn tríú páirtithe `."

msgid ""
"Django attempts to support as many features as possible on all database "
"backends. However, not all database backends are alike, and we've had to "
"make design decisions on which features to support and which assumptions we "
"can make safely."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django iarracht tacú leis an oiread gnéithe agus is féidir ar gach "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí. Mar sin féin, níl gach cúltaca bunachar sonraí mar "
"an gcéanna, agus bhí orainn cinntí dearaidh a dhéanamh faoi na gnéithe le "
"tacú le tacú leo agus na toimhdeanna is féidir linn a dhéanamh go sábháilte."

msgid ""
"This file describes some of the features that might be relevant to Django "
"usage. It is not intended as a replacement for server-specific documentation "
"or reference manuals."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an comhad seo cur síos ar chuid de na gnéithe a d'fhéadfadh a bheith "
"ábhartha le húsáid Django. Níl sé beartaithe mar athsholáthar do dhoiciméadú "
"nó lámhleabhair tagartha atá sonrach le freastalaí."

msgid "General notes"
msgstr "Nótaí ginearálta"

msgid "Persistent connections"
msgstr "Naisc leanúnacha"

msgid ""
"Persistent connections avoid the overhead of reestablishing a connection to "
"the database in each HTTP request. They're controlled by "
"the :setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE` parameter which defines the maximum lifetime of "
"a connection. It can be set independently for each database."
msgstr ""
"Seachnaíonn naisc leanúnacha an lasbhaird a bhaineann le nasc leis an "
"mbunachar sonraí a athbhunú i ngach iarratas HTTP. Tá siad á rialú ag an "
"bparaiméadar: setting: `CONN_MAX_AGE` a shainmhíníonn saolré uasta nasc. Is "
"féidir é a shocrú go neamhspleách do gach bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The default value is ``0``, preserving the historical behavior of closing "
"the database connection at the end of each request. To enable persistent "
"connections, set :setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE` to a positive integer of seconds. "
"For unlimited persistent connections, set it to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Is é “0” an luach réamhshocraithe, ag caomhnú an t-iompar stairiúil a "
"bhaineann le nasc an bhunachar sonraí a dhúnadh ag deireadh gach iarratais. "
"Chun naisc leanúnacha a chumasú, socraí:setting: `CONN_MAX_AGE` go sláimhir "
"dearfach soicind. Maidir le naisc leanúnacha neamhtheoranta, socraigh é go "
"``None ``."

msgid ""
"When using ASGI, persistent connections should be disabled. Instead, use "
"your database backend's built-in connection pooling if available, or "
"investigate a third-party connection pooling option if required."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connection management"
msgstr "Bainistíocht nasc"

msgid ""
"Django opens a connection to the database when it first makes a database "
"query. It keeps this connection open and reuses it in subsequent requests. "
"Django closes the connection once it exceeds the maximum age defined "
"by :setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE` or when it isn't usable any longer."
msgstr ""
"Osclaíonn Django nasc leis an mbunachar sonraí nuair a dhéanann sé ceist "
"bunachar sonraí ar dtús. Coinníonn sé an nasc seo oscailte agus athúsáideann "
"sé é in iarratais ina dhiaidh sin. Dúnann Django an nasc nuair a sháraíonn "
"sé an t-aois uasta atá sainmhínithe ag: setting: `CONN_MAX_AGE` nó nuair "
"nach bhfuil sé inúsáidte a thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"In detail, Django automatically opens a connection to the database whenever "
"it needs one and doesn't have one already — either because this is the first "
"connection, or because the previous connection was closed."
msgstr ""
"Go mion, osclaíonn Django nasc leis an mbunachar sonraí go huathoibríoch aon "
"uair a theastaíonn ceann uaidh agus níl ceann aige cheana féin - toisc gurb "
"é seo an chéad nasc, nó toisc go raibh an nasc roimhe seo dúnta."

msgid ""
"At the beginning of each request, Django closes the connection if it has "
"reached its maximum age. If your database terminates idle connections after "
"some time, you should set :setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE` to a lower value, so that "
"Django doesn't attempt to use a connection that has been terminated by the "
"database server. (This problem may only affect very low traffic sites.)"
msgstr ""
"Ag tús gach iarratais, dúnann Django an nasc má tá a uasaois bainte amach "
"aige. Má chuireann do bhunachar sonraí deireadh le naisc díomhaoin tar éis "
"roinnt ama, ba chóir duit:setting: `CONN_MAX_AGE` a shocrú go luach níos "
"ísle, ionas nach ndéanfaidh Django iarracht nasc a chuir deireadh leis an "
"bhfreastalaí bunachar sonraí a úsáid. (Ní fhéadfaidh an fhadhb seo dul i "
"bhfeidhm ach ar shuíomhanna tráchta an-íseal.)"

msgid ""
"At the end of each request, Django closes the connection if it has reached "
"its maximum age or if it is in an unrecoverable error state. If any database "
"errors have occurred while processing the requests, Django checks whether "
"the connection still works, and closes it if it doesn't. Thus, database "
"errors affect at most one request per each application's worker thread; if "
"the connection becomes unusable, the next request gets a fresh connection."
msgstr ""
"Ag deireadh gach iarratais, dúnann Django an nasc má tá a uasaois bainte "
"amach aige nó má tá sé i stát earráide neamh-inaisghabháilte. Má tharla aon "
"earráidí bunachar sonraí agus na hiarrataí á bpróiseáil, seiceálann Django "
"an n-oibríonn an nasc fós, agus dúnann sé mura ndéanann sé. Mar sin, bíonn "
"tionchar ag earráidí bunachar sonraí ar iarratas amháin ar a mhéad in "
"aghaidh an snáithe oibrí gach iarratais; má éiríonn an nasc neamhúsáidte, "
"faigheann an chéad iarratas eile nasc úr"

msgid ""
"Setting :setting:`CONN_HEALTH_CHECKS` to ``True`` can be used to improve the "
"robustness of connection reuse and prevent errors when a connection has been "
"closed by the database server which is now ready to accept and serve new "
"connections, e.g. after database server restart. The health check is "
"performed only once per request and only if the database is being accessed "
"during the handling of the request."
msgstr ""
"Socraithe:Socrú: Is féidir `CONN_HEALTH_CHECKS` go ``True`` a úsáid chun "
"láidneacht athúsáide nasc a fheabhsú agus earráidí a chosc nuair a dhúntar "
"nasc ag an bhfreastalaí bunachar sonraí atá réidh anois chun nasc nua a "
"ghlacadh agus a sheirbheáil, m.sh. tar éis freastalaí bunachar sonraí a "
"atosú. Ní dhéantar an seiceáil sláinte ach uair amháin in aghaidh an "
"iarratais agus ach amháin má tá rochtain ar an mbunachar sonraí le linn "
"láimhseáil an iarratais."

msgid "Caveats"
msgstr "Rabhadh"

msgid ""
"Since each thread maintains its own connection, your database must support "
"at least as many simultaneous connections as you have worker threads."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go gcoinníonn gach snáithe a nasc féin, caithfidh do bhunachar "
"sonraí tacú leis an oiread naisc chomhuaineach ar a laghad agus atá "
"snáitheanna oi"

msgid ""
"Sometimes a database won't be accessed by the majority of your views, for "
"example because it's the database of an external system, or thanks to "
"caching. In such cases, you should set :setting:`CONN_MAX_AGE` to a low "
"value or even ``0``, because it doesn't make sense to maintain a connection "
"that's unlikely to be reused. This will help keep the number of simultaneous "
"connections to this database small."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta ní bhfaighidh tromlach do thuairimí rochtain ar bhunachar sonraí, "
"mar shampla toisc gurb é bunachar sonraí córas seachtrach é, nó a bhuíochas "
"le caching. I gcásanna den sórt sin, ba chóir duit:socrú: `CONN_MAX_AGE` go "
"luach íseal nó fiú `0``, toisc nach bhfuil ciall aige nasc a choinneáil nach "
"dócha go n-athúsáidfear. Cuideoidh sé seo líon na naisc chomhuaineach leis "
"an mbunachar sonraí seo a choinneáil beag."

msgid ""
"The development server creates a new thread for each request it handles, "
"negating the effect of persistent connections. Don't enable them during "
"development."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn an freastalaí forbartha snáithe nua do gach iarratas a "
"láimhseálann sé, ag diúltú ar éifeacht naisc leanúnacha. Ná cuir ar chumas "
"iad le linn na forbartha."

msgid ""
"When Django establishes a connection to the database, it sets up appropriate "
"parameters, depending on the backend being used. If you enable persistent "
"connections, this setup is no longer repeated every request. If you modify "
"parameters such as the connection's isolation level or time zone, you should "
"either restore Django's defaults at the end of each request, force an "
"appropriate value at the beginning of each request, or disable persistent "
"connections."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhunaíonn Django nasc leis an mbunachar sonraí, bunaíonn sé "
"paraiméadair iomchuí, ag brath ar an gcúltaca atá á úsáid. Má chumasaíonn tú "
"naisc leanúnacha, ní dhéantar an socrú seo a athdhéanamh gach iarratas a "
"thuilleadh. Má mhodhníonn tú paraiméadair mar leibhéal aonrú nó crios ama an "
"nasc, ba cheart duit réamhshocruithe Django a athbhunú ag deireadh gach "
"iarratais, luach cuí a chur i bhfeidhm ag tús gach iarratais, nó naisc "
"leanúnacha a dhíchumasú."

msgid ""
"If a connection is created in a long-running process, outside of Django’s "
"request-response cycle, the connection will remain open until explicitly "
"closed, or timeout occurs. You can use ``django.db.close_old_connections()`` "
"to close all old or unusable connections."
msgstr ""
"Má chruthaítear nasc i bpróiseas fadtéarmach, lasmuigh de thimthriall "
"iarrata-freagartha Django, fanfaidh an nasc oscailte go dtí go ndúnfar go "
"sainráite, nó go dtarlóidh an t-am. Is féidir leat "
"``django.db.close_old_connexions () ``a úsáid chun gach sean-nasc nó "
"neamhúsáidte a dhúnadh."

msgid "Encoding"
msgstr "Ionchódú"

msgid ""
"Django assumes that all databases use UTF-8 encoding. Using other encodings "
"may result in unexpected behavior such as \"value too long\" errors from "
"your database for data that is valid in Django. See the database specific "
"notes below for information on how to set up your database correctly."
msgstr ""
"Glacann Django leis go n-úsáideann gach bunachar sonraí ionchódú UTF-8. "
"D'fhéadfadh iompar gan choinne mar earráidí “luach rófhada” ó do bhunachar "
"sonraí a bheith mar thoradh ar ionchódú eile a úsáid le haghaidh sonraí atá "
"bailí i Django. Féach na nótaí sonracha bunachar sonraí thíos chun faisnéis "
"a fháil ar conas do bhunachar sonraí a chur ar bun i gceart"

msgid "PostgreSQL notes"
msgstr "Nótaí PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"Django supports PostgreSQL 14 and higher. `psycopg`_ 3.1.8+ or `psycopg2`_ "
"2.8.4+ is required, though the latest `psycopg`_ 3.1.8+ is recommended."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support for ``psycopg2`` is likely to be deprecated and removed at some "
"point in the future."
msgstr ""
"Is dóigh go ndéanfar tacaíocht do `psycopg2` a dhíchur agus a bhaint ag "
"pointe éigin sa todhchaí."

msgid "PostgreSQL connection settings"
msgstr "Socruithe nasc PostgreSQL"

msgid "See :setting:`HOST` for details."
msgstr "Féach: socrú: `HOST` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"To connect using a service name from the `connection service file`_ and a "
"password from the `password file`_, you must specify them in "
"the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`:"
msgstr ""
"Chun ceangal ag baint úsáide as ainm seirbhíse ón `comhad seirbhíse nasc`_ "
"agus pasfhocal ón `comhad pasfhocal`_, ní mór duit iad a shonrú sa "
"chuid:setting: `OPTIONS` de do chumraíocht bunachar sonraí in:setting: "
"`DATABASES`:"

msgid "``settings.py``"
msgstr "``settings.py``"

msgid "``.pg_service.conf``"
msgstr "``.pg_service.conf``"

msgid "``.my_pgpass``"
msgstr "``.my_pgpass``"

msgid ""
"The PostgreSQL backend passes the content of :setting:`OPTIONS` as keyword "
"arguments to the connection constructor, allowing for more advanced control "
"of driver behavior. All available `parameters`_ are described in detail in "
"the PostgreSQL documentation."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann cúltaca PostgreSQL ábhar de:setting: `OPTIONS` mar argóintí "
"eochairfhocal chuig an tógálaí nasc, rud a ligeann rialú níos airde ar "
"iompar tiománaí. Déantar cur síos mion ar na paraiméadair go léir atá ar "
"fáil i ndoiciméadú PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"Using a service name for testing purposes is not supported. "
"This :ticket:`may be implemented later <33685>`."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear le húsáid ainm seirbhíse chun críocha tástála. "
"<33685>Seo:ticéad: `féadfar a chur i bhfeidhm níos déanaí `."

msgid "Optimizing PostgreSQL's configuration"
msgstr "Cumraíocht PostgreSQL a bharrfheabhsú"

msgid "Django needs the following parameters for its database connections:"
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn Django na paraiméadair seo a leanas dá naisc bunachar sonraí:"

msgid "``client_encoding``: ``'UTF8'``,"
msgstr "``client_encoding``: ```UTF8'``,"

msgid ""
"``default_transaction_isolation``: ``'read committed'`` by default, or the "
"value set in the connection options (see below),"
msgstr ""
"``default_transaction_isolation``: ``'read committed'`` de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, nó an luach atá leagtha síos sna roghanna nasc (féach "
"thíos),"

msgid "``timezone``:"
msgstr "``crios ama ``:"

msgid ""
"when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, ``'UTC'`` by default, or "
"the :setting:`TIME_ZONE <DATABASE-TIME_ZONE>` value set for the connection,"
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-TIME_ZONE>nuai:setting: is é `USE_TZ` ``True``, ``UTC'`` de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, nó an:setting: `TIME_ZON` luach socraithe don nasc,"

msgid ""
"when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``False``, the value of the "
"global :setting:`TIME_ZONE` setting."
msgstr ""
"nuai:setting: `USE_TZ` ``False``, luach an socrú domhanna:setting: "
"`TIME_ZONE`."

msgid ""
"If these parameters already have the correct values, Django won't set them "
"for every new connection, which improves performance slightly. You can "
"configure them directly in :file:`postgresql.conf` or more conveniently per "
"database user with `ALTER ROLE`_."
msgstr ""
"Má tá na luachanna cearta ag na paraiméadair seo cheana féin, ní shocróidh "
"Django iad do gach nasc nua, rud a fheabhsaíonn feidhmíocht beagán. Is "
"féidir leat iad a chumrú go díreach in:file: `postgresql.conf` nó níos "
"áisiúla in aghaidh an úsáideora bunachar sonraí le `ALTER ROLE`_."

msgid ""
"Django will work just fine without this optimization, but each new "
"connection will do some additional queries to set these parameters."
msgstr ""
"Oibreoidh Django go breá gan an barrfheabhsú seo, ach déanfaidh gach nasc "
"nua roinnt ceisteanna breise chun na paraiméadair seo a shocrú."

msgid "Isolation level"
msgstr "Leibhéal aonrú"

msgid ""
"Like PostgreSQL itself, Django defaults to the ``READ COMMITTED`` `isolation "
"level`_. If you need a higher isolation level such as ``REPEATABLE READ`` or "
"``SERIALIZABLE``, set it in the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database "
"configuration in :setting:`DATABASES`::"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le PostgreSQL féin, déanann Django réamhshocrú ar an leibhéal aonair "
"``READ COMMITTED`_. Má theastaíonn leibhéal aonrúcháin níos airde uait mar "
"``REPEATABLE READ ``nó `SERIALIZABLE``, socraigh é sa chuid:SETTING: "
"`OPTIONS` de chumraíocht do bhunachar sonraí in:setting: `DATABASES`::"

msgid ""
"Under higher isolation levels, your application should be prepared to handle "
"exceptions raised on serialization failures. This option is designed for "
"advanced uses."
msgstr ""
"Faoi leibhéil aonrú níos airde, ba cheart d'iarratas a bheith ullmhaithe "
"chun eisceachtaí a ardaítear ar theipeanna sraitheach Tá an rogha seo "
"deartha le haghaidh ardúsáidí."

msgid "Role"
msgstr "Ról"

msgid ""
"If you need to use a different role for database connections than the role "
"used to establish the connection, set it in the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of "
"your database configuration in :setting:`DATABASES`::"
msgstr ""

msgid "Connection pool"
msgstr "Linn snámha nasc"

msgid ""
"To use a connection pool with `psycopg`_, you can either set ``\"pool\"`` in "
"the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES` to be a dict to be passed "
"to :class:`~psycopg:psycopg_pool.ConnectionPool`, or to ``True`` to use the "
"``ConnectionPool`` defaults::"
msgstr ""
"Chun linn nasc le `psycopg`_ a úsáid, is féidir leat ``\"pool\"`` a shocrú "
"sa chuid:setting: `OPTIONS` de do chumraíocht bunachar sonraí in:setting: "
"`DATABASES` chun a bheith ina dict le rith chuig:class: "
"`~psycopg:psycopg_pool.connectionpool`, nó go ``True`` chun an "
"`Connectionpool`` def` a úsáid buntáistí::"

msgid ""
"This option requires ``psycopg[pool]`` or :pypi:`psycopg-pool` to be "
"installed and is ignored with ``psycopg2``."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn an rogha seo ``psycopg [pool] ``nó:pypi: `psycopg-pool` a shuiteáil "
"agus neamhaird a dhéanamh air le `psycopg2``."

msgid "Server-side parameters binding"
msgstr "Paraiméadair taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"With `psycopg`_ 3.1.8+, Django defaults to the :ref:`client-side binding "
"cursors <psycopg:client-side-binding-cursors>`. If you want to use "
"the :ref:`server-side binding <psycopg:server-side-binding>` set it in "
"the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`::"
msgstr ""
"<psycopg:client-side-binding-cursors>Le `psycopg`_ 3.1.8+, déanann Django "
"réamhshocraithe ar na: ref: `cúrsaí ceangailte taobh an chliaint `. Más mian "
"leat an: ref: `ceangailt taobh freastala <psycopg:server-side-binding>í `a "
"úsáid, socraigh é sa chuid:setting: `OPTIONS` de do chumraíocht bunachar "
"sonraí in:setting: `DATABASES`::"

msgid "This option is ignored with ``psycopg2``."
msgstr "Déantar neamhaird ar an rogha seo le `psycopg2``."

msgid "Indexes for ``varchar`` and ``text`` columns"
msgstr "Innéacsanna do cholúin ``varchar`` agus ``text``"

msgid ""
"When specifying ``db_index=True`` on your model fields, Django typically "
"outputs a single ``CREATE INDEX`` statement.  However, if the database type "
"for the field is either ``varchar`` or ``text`` (e.g., used by "
"``CharField``, ``FileField``, and ``TextField``), then Django will create an "
"additional index that uses an appropriate `PostgreSQL operator class`_ for "
"the column.  The extra index is necessary to correctly perform lookups that "
"use the ``LIKE`` operator in their SQL, as is done with the ``contains`` and "
"``startswith`` lookup types."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shonraítear `DB_index = True`` ar do réimsí samhail, is gnách go n-"
"aschuireann Django ráiteas ``CREATE INDEX`` amháin. Mar sin féin, más é "
"`varchar`` nó `text`` an cineál bunachar sonraí don réimse (m.sh., úsáideann "
"``Charfield``, `Filefield``, agus ``Textfield``), ansin cruthóidh Django "
"innéacs breise a úsáideann `rang oibreora PostgreSQL cuí `_ don cholún. Tá "
"an t-innéacs breise riachtanach chun cuardaigh a dhéanamh i gceart a "
"úsáideann an oibreoir ``LIKE`` ina SQL, mar a dhéantar leis na cineálacha "
"cuardaigh ``contains`` agus ``startswith`."

msgid "Migration operation for adding extensions"
msgstr "Oibríocht imirce chun síntí a chur"

msgid ""
"If you need to add a PostgreSQL extension (like ``hstore``, ``postgis``, "
"etc.) using a migration, use "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.operations.CreateExtension` operation."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit síneadh PostgreSQL a chur leis (cosúil le ``hstore``, "
"`postgis``, srl.) ag baint úsáide as imirce, bain úsáid as an "
"oibríocht: :class: `~django.contrib.postgres.operations.createExtension`."

msgid "Server-side cursors"
msgstr "Cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"When using :meth:`QuerySet.iterator() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.iterator>`, Django opens a :ref:`server-"
"side cursor <psycopg:server-side-cursors>`. By default, PostgreSQL assumes "
"that only the first 10% of the results of cursor queries will be fetched. "
"The query planner spends less time planning the query and starts returning "
"results faster, but this could diminish performance if more than 10% of the "
"results are retrieved. PostgreSQL's assumptions on the number of rows "
"retrieved for a cursor query is controlled with the `cursor_tuple_fraction`_ "
"option."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.iterator><psycopg:server-side-cursors>Nuair "
"a úsáidtear: meth: `QuerySet.iterator () `, osclaíonn Django a:ref: `cúrsóir "
"taobh freastalaí`. De réir réamhshocraithe, glacann PostgreSQL leis nach "
"bhfaighfear ach an chéad 10% de thorthaí na gceisteanna cúrsóra a fháil. "
"Caitheann an pleanálaí fiosrúcháin níos lú ama a phleanáil an cheist agus "
"tosaíonn sé torthaí a thabhairt ar ais níos gasta, ach d'fhéadfadh sé seo "
"feidhmíocht a laghdú má aisghairtear níos mó ná 10% Rialaítear toimhdí "
"PostgreSQL ar líon na sraitheanna a aisghabháiltear le haghaidh ceist "
"cúrsóra leis an rogha `cursor_tuple_fraction`_."

msgid "Transaction pooling and server-side cursors"
msgstr "Comhdhlúthú idirbheart agus cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"Using a connection pooler in transaction pooling mode (e.g. `PgBouncer`_) "
"requires disabling server-side cursors for that connection."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí a dhíchumasú don nasc sin a úsáid i "
"mód comhiontála idirbheart (m.sh. `PGBouncer`_)."

msgid ""
"Server-side cursors are local to a connection and remain open at the end of "
"a transaction when :setting:`AUTOCOMMIT <DATABASE-AUTOCOMMIT>` is ``True``. "
"A subsequent transaction may attempt to fetch more results from a server-"
"side cursor. In transaction pooling mode, there's no guarantee that "
"subsequent transactions will use the same connection. If a different "
"connection is used, an error is raised when the transaction references the "
"server-side cursor, because server-side cursors are only accessible in the "
"connection in which they were created."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-AUTOCOMMIT>Tá cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí áitiúil le nasc agus "
"fanann siad oscailte ag deireadh idirbheart nuai:socrú: `AUTOCOMMIT` "
"``True``. Féadfaidh idirbheart ina dhiaidh sin iarracht a dhéanamh níos mó "
"torthaí a fháil ó chúrsóir taobh an fhreastalaí. I mód comhiontála "
"idirbheart, níl aon ráthaíocht ann go n-úsáidfidh idirbhearta ina dhiaidh "
"sin an nasc céanna. Má úsáidtear nasc difriúil, ardaítear earráid nuair a "
"thagraíonn an t-idirbheart don chúrsóir taobh an fhreastalaí, toisc nach "
"bhfuil cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí inrochtana ach sa nasc inar cruthaíodh "
"iad."

msgid ""
"One solution is to disable server-side cursors for a connection "
"in :setting:`DATABASES` by setting :setting:`DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS "
"<DATABASE-DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS>` to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS>Réiteach amháin is ea cursóirí taobh "
"an fhreastalaí a dhíchumasú le haghaidh nasc in:setting: `DATABASES` trí "
"shocrú: socrú: `DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS `go ``True``."

msgid ""
"To benefit from server-side cursors in transaction pooling mode, you could "
"set up :doc:`another connection to the database </topics/db/multi-db>` in "
"order to perform queries that use server-side cursors. This connection needs "
"to either be directly to the database or to a connection pooler in session "
"pooling mode."
msgstr ""
"Chun leas a bhaint as cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí i mód comhiomlánaithe "
"idirbheart, d'fhéadfá: doc: `nasc eile leis an mbunachar sonraithe' a chur "
"ar bun d'fhonn ceisteanna a dhéanamh a úsáideann cúrsaí taobh an fhreastala</"
"topics/db/multi-db> í. Caithfidh an nasc seo a bheith go díreach chuig an "
"mbunachar sonraí nó le seoltóir nasc i mód comhiomlánaithe seisiúin."

msgid ""
"Another option is to wrap each ``QuerySet`` using server-side cursors in "
"an :func:`~django.db.transaction.atomic` block, because it disables "
"``autocommit`` for the duration of the transaction. This way, the server-"
"side cursor will only live for the duration of the transaction."
msgstr ""
"Rogha eile is ea gach ``QuerySet`` a fhilleadh ag baint úsáide as cúrsaí "
"taobh an fhreastalaí i mbloc:func: `~django.db.transaction.atomic`, toisc go "
"ndéanann sé ``autocommit ``a dhíchumasú ar feadh ré an idirbheart. Ar an "
"mbealach seo, ní bheidh an cúrsóir taobh an fhreastalaí beo ach ar feadh "
"tréimhse an idirbheart."

msgid "Manually-specifying values of auto-incrementing primary keys"
msgstr "Luachanna na n-eochracha bunscoile atá ag méadú uathoibríoch"

msgid ""
"Django uses PostgreSQL's identity columns to store auto-incrementing primary "
"keys. An identity column is populated with values from a `sequence`_ that "
"keeps track of the next available value. Manually assigning a value to an "
"auto-incrementing field doesn't update the field's sequence, which might "
"later cause a conflict. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django colúin aitheantais PostgreSQL chun eochracha bunmhéadaithe "
"uathoibríoch a stóráil. Tá luachanna ó `seicheamh`_ i gcolún aitheantais a "
"choinníonn súil ar an gcéad luach eile atá ar fáil. Ní dhéanann luach a "
"shannadh de láimh do réimse uathoibríoch a nuashonrú seicheamh an réimse, "
"rud a d'fhéadfadh coinbhleacht a bheith ina chúis níos déanaí. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"If you need to specify such values, reset the sequence afterward to avoid "
"reusing a value that's already in the table. The :djadmin:`sqlsequencereset` "
"management command generates the SQL statements to do that."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit luachanna den sórt sin a shonrú, athshocraigh an seicheamh ina "
"dhiaidh sin chun luach atá sa tábla cheana féin a athúsáid a sheachaint. "
"Gineann an t-ordú bainistíochta: Djadmin: `sqlsequencereset` na ráitis SQL "
"chun é sin a dhéanamh."

msgid "Test database templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid bhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"You can use the :setting:`TEST['TEMPLATE'] <TEST_TEMPLATE>` setting to "
"specify a `template`_ (e.g. ``'template0'``) from which to create a test "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an socrú:setting: `TEST ['<TEST_TEMPLATE>TEMPLATE'] `a úsáid "
"chun `teimpléad`_ a shonrú (m.sh. ``'teimpléad0'`) uaidh chun bunachar "
"sonraí tástála a chruthú."

msgid "Speeding up test execution with non-durable settings"
msgstr "Forghníomhú tástála a bhrostú le socruithe neamh-bhuan"

msgid ""
"You can speed up test execution times by `configuring PostgreSQL to be non-"
"durable <https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/non-durability.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"< https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/non-durability.html>Is féidir leat "
"amanna forghníomhaithe tástála a bhrostú trí `PostgreSQL a chumrú le bheith "
"neamh-bhuanaithe`_."

msgid ""
"This is dangerous: it will make your database more susceptible to data loss "
"or corruption in the case of a server crash or power loss. Only use this on "
"a development machine where you can easily restore the entire contents of "
"all databases in the cluster."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo contúirteach: déanfaidh sé do bhunachar sonraí níos so-ghabháilte "
"do chaillteanas sonraí nó éilliú i gcás timpiste freastalaí nó caillteanas "
"cumhachta. Úsáid é seo ach ar mheaisín forbartha inar féidir leat ábhar "
"iomlán na mbunachar sonraí go léir sa bhraisle a athbhunú go héasca."

msgid "MariaDB notes"
msgstr "Nótaí MariaDB"

msgid "Django supports MariaDB 10.5 and higher."
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django le MariaDB 10.5 agus níos airde."

msgid ""
"To use MariaDB, use the MySQL backend, which is shared between the two. See "
"the :ref:`MySQL notes <mysql-notes>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Chun MariaDB a úsáid, bain úsáid as an gcúltaca MySQL, atá roinnte idir an "
"dá cheann. Féach na:ref: `Nótaí MySQL <mysql-notes>`le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "MySQL notes"
msgstr "Nótaí MySQL"

msgid "Version support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht leagan"

msgid "Django supports MySQL 8.0.11 and higher."
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django le MySQL 8.0.11 agus níos airde."

msgid ""
"Django's ``inspectdb`` feature uses the ``information_schema`` database, "
"which contains detailed data on all database schemas."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann gné ``inspectdb ``Django an bunachar sonraí `information_schema``, "
"ina bhfuil sonraí mionsonraithe ar gach scéim bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Django expects the database to support Unicode (UTF-8 encoding) and "
"delegates to it the task of enforcing transactions and referential "
"integrity. It is important to be aware of the fact that the two latter ones "
"aren't actually enforced by MySQL when using the MyISAM storage engine, see "
"the next section."
msgstr ""
"Tá Django ag súil go dtacóidh an bunachar sonraí le Unicode (ionchódú UTF-8) "
"agus a thosclaíonn sé dó idirbhearta agus sláine tagartha a fhorfheidhmiú. "
"Tá sé tábhachtach a bheith ar an eolas faoin bhfíric nach bhforfheidhmíonn "
"MySQL an dá cheann deireanach i ndáiríre agus an t-inneall stórála MyISAM á "
"úsáid agat, féach an chéad chuid eile."

msgid "Storage engines"
msgstr "Innill stórála"

msgid ""
"MySQL has several `storage engines`_. You can change the default storage "
"engine in the server configuration."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt `inneall stórála`_ ag MySQL. Is féidir leat an t-inneall stórála "
"réamhshocraithe a athrú i gcumraíocht na freastala"

msgid ""
"MySQL's default storage engine is InnoDB_. This engine is fully "
"transactional and supports foreign key references. It's the recommended "
"choice. However, the InnoDB autoincrement counter is lost on a MySQL restart "
"because it does not remember the ``AUTO_INCREMENT`` value, instead "
"recreating it as \"max(id)+1\". This may result in an inadvertent reuse "
"of :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` values."
msgstr ""
"Is é InnoDB_ inneall stórála réamhshocraithe MySQL. Tá an t-inneall seo "
"idirbheart go hiomlán agus tacaíonn sé le príomhthagairtí eachtracha. Is é "
"an rogha a mholtar é. Mar sin féin, cailltear cuntar autoincrement InnoDB ar "
"atosú MySQL toisc nach gcuimhneann sé an luach `AUTO_INCREMENT``, ina ionad "
"sin é a athchruthú mar “max (id) +1\". D'fhéadfadh luachanna: class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.AutoField` athúsáid neamhthuigneach mar thoradh air seo."

msgid ""
"The main drawbacks of MyISAM_ are that it doesn't support transactions or "
"enforce foreign-key constraints."
msgstr ""
"Is iad príomh-mhíbhuntáistí MyISAM_ ná nach dtacaíonn sé le hidirbhearta nó "
"nach bhforfheidhmíonn sé srianta eachtracha eachtrach."

msgid "MySQL DB API Drivers"
msgstr "Tiománaithe API MySQL DB"

msgid ""
"MySQL has a couple drivers that implement the Python Database API described "
"in :pep:`249`:"
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla tiománaí ag MySQL a chuireann an API Bunachar Sonraí Python i "
"bhfeidhm a thuairiscítear in:pep: `249`:"

msgid ""
":pypi:`mysqlclient` is a native driver. It's **the recommended choice**."
msgstr ""
":pypi: Is tiománaí dúchasach é `mysqlclient`. Is éine** an rogha a mholta**."

msgid ""
"`MySQL Connector/Python`_ is a pure Python driver from Oracle that does not "
"require the MySQL client library or any Python modules outside the standard "
"library."
msgstr ""
"Is tiománaí íon Python ó Oracle é `MySQL Connector/Python`_ nach dteastaíonn "
"leabharlann cliant MySQL nó aon mhodúil Python lasmuigh den leabharlann "
"chaighdeánach."

msgid ""
"In addition to a DB API driver, Django needs an adapter to access the "
"database drivers from its ORM. Django provides an adapter for mysqlclient "
"while MySQL Connector/Python includes `its own`_."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le tiománaí API DB, teastaíonn oiriúnóir ó Django chun rochtain "
"a fháil ar na tiománaithe bunachar sonraí óna ORM. Soláthraíonn Django "
"cuibheoir do mysqlclient agus cuimsíonn MySQL Connector/Python `a chuid féin "
"`_."

msgid "mysqlclient"
msgstr "mysqlclient"

msgid "Django requires `mysqlclient`_ 1.4.3 or later."
msgstr "Éilíonn Django `mysqlclient`_ 1.4.3 nó níos déanaí."

msgid "MySQL Connector/Python"
msgstr "Ceanglóir MySQL/Python"

msgid ""
"MySQL Connector/Python is available from the `download page`_. The Django "
"adapter is available in versions 1.1.X and later. It may not support the "
"most recent releases of Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá MySQL Connector/Python ar fáil ón leathanach `íoslódálaí`_. Tá an t-"
"oiriúntóir Django ar fáil i leaganacha 1.1.X agus níos déanaí. B'fhéidir "
"nach dtacaíonn sé leis na heisiúintí is déanaí de Django."

msgid "Time zone definitions"
msgstr "Sainmhínithe crios ama"

msgid ""
"If you plan on using Django's :doc:`timezone support </topics/i18n/"
"timezones>`, use `mysql_tzinfo_to_sql`_ to load time zone tables into the "
"MySQL database. This needs to be done just once for your MySQL server, not "
"per database."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé ar intinn agat Django's:doc: `timezone taca` a úsáid, bain úsáid as "
"`mysql_tzinfo_to_sql`_ chun táblaí cri</topics/i18n/timezones> os ama a "
"luchtú isteach sa bhunachar sonraí MySQL. Ní mór é seo a dhéanamh uair "
"amháin do do fhreastalaí MySQL, ní in aghaidh an bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "Creating your database"
msgstr "Cruthú do bhunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"You can `create your database`_ using the command-line tools and this SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat `do bhunachar sonraí a chruthai`_ ag baint úsáide as na "
"huirlisí líne ordaithe agus an SQL seo:"

msgid "This ensures all tables and columns will use UTF-8 by default."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn sé seo go n-úsáidfidh gach tábla agus colún UTF-8 de réir "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Collation settings"
msgstr "Socruithe coláireachta"

msgid ""
"The collation setting for a column controls the order in which data is "
"sorted as well as what strings compare as equal. You can specify the "
"``db_collation`` parameter to set the collation name of the column "
"for :attr:`CharField <django.db.models.CharField.db_collation>` "
"and :attr:`TextField <django.db.models.TextField.db_collation>`."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an socrú comhlánaithe do cholún an t-ord ina ndéantar sonraí a "
"shórtáil chomh maith leis na teaghráin a gcomparáid mar chomhionann. "
"<django.db.models.CharField.db_collation><django.db.models.TextField.db_collation>Is "
"féidir leat an paraiméadar ``db_collation`` a shonrú chun ainm comhlánaithe "
"an cholúin a shocrú le haghaidh: attr: `CharField `agus:attr: `TextField`."

msgid ""
"The collation can also be set on a database-wide level and per-table. This "
"is `documented thoroughly`_ in the MySQL documentation. In such cases, you "
"must set the collation by directly manipulating the database settings or "
"tables. Django doesn't provide an API to change them."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an bailiú a shocrú freisin ar leibhéal ar fud an mbunachar sonraí "
"agus in aghaidh an tábla. Tá sé seo `doiciméadaithe go críochnú`_ sa "
"doiciméadú MySQL. I gcásanna den sórt sin, ní mór duit an comhlánú a shocrú "
"trí na socruithe nó na táblaí bunachar sonraí a ionramháil go díreach. Ní "
"sholáthraíonn Django API chun iad a athrú."

msgid ""
"By default, with a UTF-8 database, MySQL will use the ``utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci`` "
"collation. This results in all string equality comparisons being done in a "
"*case-insensitive* manner. That is, ``\"Fred\"`` and ``\"freD\"`` are "
"considered equal at the database level. If you have a unique constraint on a "
"field, it would be illegal to try to insert both ``\"aa\"`` and ``\"AA\"`` "
"into the same column, since they compare as equal (and, hence, non-unique) "
"with the default collation. If you want case-sensitive comparisons on a "
"particular column or table, change the column or table to use the "
"``utf8mb4_0900_as_cs`` collation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Please note that according to `MySQL Unicode Character Sets`_, comparisons "
"for the ``utf8mb4_general_ci`` collation are faster, but slightly less "
"correct, than comparisons for ``utf8mb4_unicode_ci``. If this is acceptable "
"for your application, you should use ``utf8mb4_general_ci`` because it is "
"faster. If this is not acceptable (for example, if you require German "
"dictionary order), use ``utf8mb4_unicode_ci`` because it is more accurate."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Model formsets validate unique fields in a case-sensitive manner. Thus when "
"using a case-insensitive collation, a formset with unique field values that "
"differ only by case will pass validation, but upon calling ``save()``, an "
"``IntegrityError`` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn foirmeacha samhlacha réimsí uathúla ar bhealach cás-íogair. Mar sin "
"nuair a úsáidtear comhdhlúthú cás-neamh-íogair, rachaidh foirm le luachanna "
"réimse uathúla nach bhfuil difriúil ach de réir cháis bailíochtú, ach nuair "
"a ghlaoch ar `save () ``, ardófar ``IntegrityError``."

msgid "Connecting to the database"
msgstr "Ceangal leis an mbunachar sonraí"

msgid "Refer to the :doc:`settings documentation </ref/settings>`."
msgstr "Féach ar an doiciméadú: `socruithe doiciméadúsaí` </ref/settings>."

msgid "Connection settings are used in this order:"
msgstr "Úsáidtear socruithe nasc san ord seo:"

msgid ":setting:`OPTIONS`."
msgstr ": socrú: `ROGHANNAÍ`."

msgid ":setting:`NAME`, :setting:`USER`, :setting:`PASSWORD`, :setting:`HOST`, :setting:`PORT`"
msgstr ""
":setting: `NAME`, :setting: `USER`, :setting: `PASSWORD`, :setting: "
"`HOST`, :setting: `PORT`"

msgid "MySQL option files."
msgstr "Comhaid rogha MySQL."

msgid ""
"In other words, if you set the name of the database in :setting:`OPTIONS`, "
"this will take precedence over :setting:`NAME`, which would override "
"anything in a `MySQL option file`_."
msgstr ""
"Is é sin le rá, má shocraíonn tú ainm an bhunachar sonraí in:setting: "
"`OPTIONS`, beidh tosaíocht aige seo thair:setting: `NAME`, a chuirfeadh aon "
"rud i gcomhad rogha `MySQL`_ a sháraigh."

msgid "Here's a sample configuration which uses a MySQL option file::"
msgstr "Seo cumraíocht shamplach a úsáideann comhad rogha MySQL::"

msgid ""
"Several other `MySQLdb connection options`_ may be useful, such as ``ssl``, "
"``init_command``, and ``sql_mode``."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh roinnt roghanna ceangail `MySQLDB `_ eile úsáideach, "
"mar shampla ``ssl``, ``init_command ``, agus ``sql_mode``."

msgid "Setting ``sql_mode``"
msgstr "Socrú ``sql_mode``"

msgid ""
"The default value of the ``sql_mode`` option contains "
"``STRICT_TRANS_TABLES``. That option escalates warnings into errors when "
"data are truncated upon insertion, so Django highly recommends activating a "
"`strict mode`_ for MySQL to prevent data loss (either "
"``STRICT_TRANS_TABLES`` or ``STRICT_ALL_TABLES``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``STRICT_TRANS_TABLES`` sa luach réamhshocraithe den rogha ``sql_mode``. "
"Méadaíonn an rogha sin rabhaidh ina earráidí nuair a ghearrtar sonraí nuair "
"a chuirtear isteach orthu, mar sin molann Django go mór `modh dian `_ a "
"ghníomhachtú do MySQL chun caillteanas sonraí a chosc "
"(`STRICT_TRANS_TABLES`` nó ``STRICT_ALL_TABLES``)."

msgid ""
"If you need to customize the SQL mode, you can set the ``sql_mode`` variable "
"like other MySQL options: either in a config file or with the entry "
"``'init_command': \"SET sql_mode='STRICT_TRANS_TABLES'\"`` in "
"the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit an modh SQL a shaincheapadh, is féidir leat an athróg "
"``sql_mode`` a shocrú cosúil le roghanna MySQL eile: i gcomhad cumraithe nó "
"leis an iontráil ``'init_command': “SET SQL_MODE='STRICT_TRANS_TABLES'\"`` "
"san :setting: `OPTIONS` cuid de do chumraíocht bunachar sonraí in:setting: "
"`DATABASES`."

msgid ""
"When running concurrent loads, database transactions from different sessions "
"(say, separate threads handling different requests) may interact with each "
"other. These interactions are affected by each session's `transaction "
"isolation level`_. You can set a connection's isolation level with an "
"``'isolation_level'`` entry in the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database "
"configuration in :setting:`DATABASES`. Valid values for this entry are the "
"four standard isolation levels:"
msgstr ""
"Agus ualaí comharthacha á rith, féadfaidh idirbhearta bunachar sonraí ó "
"sheisiúin éagsúla (abair, snáitheanna ar leithligh a láimhseálann iarrat "
"Bíonn tionchar ag `leibhéal aonrú idirbhearta`_ gach seisiúin ar na "
"hidirghníomhaíochtaí seo. Is féidir leat leibhéal aonrú nasc a shocrú le "
"iontráil ``'isolation_level'`` sa chuid:setting: `OPTIONS` de chumraíocht do "
"bhunachar sonraí in:setting: `DATABASES`. Is iad na ceithre leibhéal aonrú "
"caighdeánacha luachanna bailí don iontráil seo:"

msgid "``'read uncommitted'``"
msgstr "```'léamh neamhchoitianta ``"

msgid "``'read committed'``"
msgstr "```'choiste léitheach'`"

msgid "``'repeatable read'``"
msgstr "```'inléite athsheolacha'`"

msgid "``'serializable'``"
msgstr "````sraitheach``"

msgid ""
"or ``None`` to use the server's configured isolation level. However, Django "
"works best with and defaults to read committed rather than MySQL's default, "
"repeatable read. Data loss is possible with repeatable read. In particular, "
"you may see cases "
"where :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get_or_create` will raise "
"an :exc:`~django.db.IntegrityError` but the object won't appear in a "
"subsequent :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get` call."
msgstr ""
"nó ``None`` chun leibhéal aonrú cumraithe an fhreastalaí a úsáid. Mar sin "
"féin, is fearr a oibríonn Django le léamh tiomanta agus déanann sé "
"réamhshocraithe léamh MySQL seachas léamh réamhshocraithe MySQL. Is féidir "
"caillteanas sonraí a dhéanamh le léamh in-athsheolta. Go háirithe, b'fhéidir "
"go bhfeicfidh tú cásanna ina n-ardóidh: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.get_or_create` an:exc: "
"`~django.db.IntegrityError` ach ní bheidh an réad le feiceáil i nglaoch ina "
"dhiaidh sin: `~django.db.models.queryset.get`."

msgid "Creating your tables"
msgstr "Do tháblaí a chruthú"

msgid ""
"When Django generates the schema, it doesn't specify a storage engine, so "
"tables will be created with whatever default storage engine your database "
"server is configured for. The easiest solution is to set your database "
"server's default storage engine to the desired engine."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a ghineann Django an scéim, ní shonraíonn sé inneall stórála, mar sin "
"cruthófar táblaí le cibé inneall stórála réamhshocraithe a bhfuil do "
"fhreastalaí bunachar sonraí cumraithe dó. Is é an réiteach is éasca inneall "
"stórála réamhshocraithe do fhreastalaí bunachar sonraí a shocrú go dtí an t-"
"inneall"

msgid ""
"If you're using a hosting service and can't change your server's default "
"storage engine, you have a couple of options."
msgstr ""
"Má tá seirbhís óstála á úsáid agat agus mura féidir leat inneall stórála "
"réamhshocraithe do fhreastalaí a athrú, tá cúpla rogha agat."

msgid ""
"After the tables are created, execute an ``ALTER TABLE`` statement to "
"convert a table to a new storage engine (such as InnoDB):"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis na táblaí a chruthú, déan ráiteas ``ALTER TABLE`` a fhorghníomhú "
"chun tábla a thiontú go inneall stórála nua (mar shampla InnoDB):"

msgid "This can be tedious if you have a lot of tables."
msgstr "Is féidir leis seo a bheith deacair má tá a lán táblaí agat."

msgid ""
"Another option is to use the ``init_command`` option for MySQLdb prior to "
"creating your tables::"
msgstr ""
"Rogha eile is ea an rogha ``init_command ``a úsáid le haghaidh MySQLDB sula "
"gcruthóidh tú do tháblaí::"

msgid ""
"This sets the default storage engine upon connecting to the database. After "
"your tables have been created, you should remove this option as it adds a "
"query that is only needed during table creation to each database connection."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé seo an t-inneall stórála réamhshocraithe nuair a cheanglaíonn "
"sé leis an Tar éis do tháblaí a chruthú, ba cheart duit an rogha seo a "
"bhaint toisc go gcuireann sé ceist nach gá ach le linn cruthú tábla le gach "
"nasc bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Table names"
msgstr "Ainmneacha tábla"

msgid ""
"There are `known issues`_ in even the latest versions of MySQL that can "
"cause the case of a table name to be altered when certain SQL statements are "
"executed under certain conditions. It is recommended that you use lowercase "
"table names, if possible, to avoid any problems that might arise from this "
"behavior. Django uses lowercase table names when it auto-generates table "
"names from models, so this is mainly a consideration if you are overriding "
"the table name via the :class:`~django.db.models.Options.db_table` parameter."
msgstr ""
"Tá `saincheisteanna aitheanna`_ ann fiú sna leaganacha is déanaí de MySQL a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith ina chúis le cás ainm tábla a athrú nuair a dhéantar "
"ráitis SQL áirithe a fhorghníomhú faoi choinníollacha áirithe. Moltar duit "
"ainmneacha tábla beaga a úsáid, más féidir, chun aon fhadhbanna a "
"d'fhéadfadh teacht chun cinn ón iompar seo a sheachaint. Úsáideann Django "
"ainmneacha tábla beaga nuair a ghineann sé ainmneacha tábla go huathoibríoch "
"ó mhúnlaí, mar sin is breithniú é seo den chuid is mó má tá tú ag dul i "
"bhfeidhm ar ainm an tábla tríd an bparaiméadar: Class: "
"`~Django.DB.Models.Options.DB_Table`."

msgid "Savepoints"
msgstr "Sábháilteachta"

msgid ""
"Both the Django ORM and MySQL (when using the InnoDB :ref:`storage engine "
"<mysql-storage-engines>`) support database :ref:`savepoints <topics-db-"
"transactions-savepoints>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-transactions-savepoints>Tacaíonn an Django ORM agus MySQL araon "
"(agus an InnoDB: Ref: `inneall stórála `á n-úsáid agat<mysql-storage-"
"engines>) le bunachar sonraí: ref: `savepoints`."

msgid ""
"If you use the MyISAM storage engine please be aware of the fact that you "
"will receive database-generated errors if you try to use the :ref:`savepoint-"
"related methods of the transactions API <topics-db-transactions-"
"savepoints>`. The reason for this is that detecting the storage engine of a "
"MySQL database/table is an expensive operation so it was decided it isn't "
"worth to dynamically convert these methods in no-op's based in the results "
"of such detection."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-transactions-savepoints>Má úsáideann tú inneall stórála MyISAM bí "
"ar an eolas faoi do thoil go bhfaighidh tú earráidí a ghintear bunachar "
"sonraí má dhéanann tú iarracht modhanna: ref: `savepoint a bhaineann leis an "
"API idirbhearta `a úsáid. Is é an chúis atá leis seo ná gur oibríocht daor é "
"inneall stórála bunachar sonraí/tábla MySQL a bhrath mar sin socraíodh nach "
"fiú na modhanna seo a thiontú go dinimiciúil i no-op bunaithe i dtorthaí "
"braite den sórt sin."

msgid "Notes on specific fields"
msgstr "Nótaí ar réimsí ar leith"

msgid "Character fields"
msgstr "Réimsí carachtar"

msgid ""
"Any fields that are stored with ``VARCHAR`` column types may have their "
"``max_length`` restricted to 255 characters if you are using ``unique=True`` "
"for the field. This "
"affects :class:`~django.db.models.CharField`, :class:`~django.db.models.SlugField`. "
"See `the MySQL documentation`_ for more details."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh a “max_length” teoranta do 255 carachtar ar aon réimsí "
"a stóráiltear le cineálacha colún ``VARCHAR`` má tá ``unique=true`` á úsáid "
"agat don réimse. Bíonn tionchar aige seo: aicme: "
"`~django.db.models.charfield`, :class: `~django.db.models.slugfield`. Féach "
"`an doiciméadú MySQL `_ le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``TextField`` limitations"
msgstr "Teorainneacha ``TextField``"

msgid ""
"MySQL can index only the first N chars of a ``BLOB`` or ``TEXT`` column. "
"Since ``TextField`` doesn't have a defined length, you can't mark it as "
"``unique=True``. MySQL will report: \"BLOB/TEXT column '<db_column>' used in "
"key specification without a key length\"."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le MySQL ach an chéad chars N de cholún ``BLOB`` nó `TEXT`` a "
"innéacsú. Ós rud é nach bhfuil fad sainithe ag ``Textfield``, ní féidir leat "
"é a mharcáil mar ``Unique=True``. Tuairiscíonn MySQL: “COLÚN BLOB/TEXT "
"<db_column>'a úsáidtear i bpríomhshonraíocht gan fad eochair”."

msgid "Fractional seconds support for Time and DateTime fields"
msgstr "Tacaíocht soicindí codánach do réimsí Am agus DátaTime"

msgid ""
"MySQL can store fractional seconds, provided that the column definition "
"includes a fractional indication (e.g. ``DATETIME(6)``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le MySQL soicindí codánacha a stóráil, ar choinníoll go gcuimsíonn "
"an sainmhíniú colún tásc codánach (m.sh. ``DATETIME (6)``)."

msgid ""
"Django will not upgrade existing columns to include fractional seconds if "
"the database server supports it. If you want to enable them on an existing "
"database, it's up to you to either manually update the column on the target "
"database, by executing a command like:"
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanfaidh Django na colúin atá ann cheana a uasghrádú chun soicind "
"codánacha a áireamh má thacaíonn an freastala Más mian leat iad a chumasú ar "
"bhunachar sonraí atá ann cheana, is fútsa atá sé an colún ar an "
"spriocbhunachar sonraí a nuashonrú de láimh, trí ordú a fhorghníomhú mar:"

msgid ""
"or using a :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation in "
"a :ref:`data migration <data-migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"<data-migrations>nó ag baint úsáide as: oibríocht a:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.Operations.Runsql` in a:ref: `imirce sonraí `."

msgid "``TIMESTAMP`` columns"
msgstr "Colúin ``TIMESTAMP``"

msgid ""
"If you are using a legacy database that contains ``TIMESTAMP`` columns, you "
"must set :setting:`USE_TZ = False <USE_TZ>` to avoid data "
"corruption. :djadmin:`inspectdb` maps these columns "
"to :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` and if you enable timezone "
"support, both MySQL and Django will attempt to convert the values from UTC "
"to local time."
msgstr ""
"<USE_TZ>Má tá bunachar sonraí oidhreachta á úsáid agat ina bhfuil colúin "
"``TIMESTAMP``, ní mór duit:setting: `USE_TZ = False `a shocrú chun éilliú "
"sonraí a sheachaint. :djadmin: Mapáil `inspectdb` na colúin seo chuig:class: "
"`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` agus má chumasaíonn tú tacaíocht crios "
"ama, déanfaidh MySQL agus Django araon iarracht na luachanna a thiontú ó UTC "
"go am áitiúil."

msgid "Row locking with ``QuerySet.select_for_update()``"
msgstr "Glasáil sraithe le ``QuerySet.Select_for_Update () ``"

msgid ""
"MySQL and MariaDB do not support some options to the ``SELECT ... FOR "
"UPDATE`` statement. If ``select_for_update()`` is used with an unsupported "
"option, then a :exc:`~django.db.NotSupportedError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn MySQL agus MariaDB le roinnt roghanna don ``SELECT... LE "
"HAGHAIDH RÁITEAS NUASHONRÚ. Má úsáidtear ``select_for_update () ``le rogha "
"gan tacaíocht, ansin ardaítear a:exc: `~django.db.notSupportedError`."

msgid "Option"
msgstr "Rogha"

msgid "``SKIP LOCKED``"
msgstr "``SCIPEÁIL GLASÁIL``"

msgid "X (≥10.6)"
msgstr "X (≥10.6)"

msgid "``NOWAIT``"
msgstr "``NOW WAIT``"

msgid "``OF``"
msgstr "`````"

msgid "``NO KEY``"
msgstr "```AON EOCHR``"

msgid ""
"When using ``select_for_update()`` on MySQL, make sure you filter a queryset "
"against at least a set of fields contained in unique constraints or only "
"against fields covered by indexes. Otherwise, an exclusive write lock will "
"be acquired over the full table for the duration of the transaction."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag úsáid ``select_for_update () ``ar MySQL, déan cinnte go scagann "
"tú tacar fiosrúcháin i gcoinne sraith réimsí ar a laghad atá i srianta "
"uathúla nó amháin i gcoinne réimsí atá clúdaithe ag innéacsanna. Seachas "
"sin, faighfear glas scríbhneoireachta eisiach thar an tábla iomlán ar feadh "
"ré an idirbheart."

msgid "Automatic typecasting can cause unexpected results"
msgstr "Is féidir torthaí gan choinne a bheith ina chúis le clóscáil"

msgid ""
"When performing a query on a string type, but with an integer value, MySQL "
"will coerce the types of all values in the table to an integer before "
"performing the comparison. If your table contains the values ``'abc'``, "
"``'def'`` and you query for ``WHERE mycolumn=0``, both rows will match. "
"Similarly, ``WHERE mycolumn=1`` will match the value ``'abc1'``. Therefore, "
"string type fields included in Django will always cast the value to a string "
"before using it in a query."
msgstr ""
"Agus ceist á dhéanamh agat ar chineál sreangán, ach le luach sláimhir, "
"cuirfidh MySQL na cineálacha na luachanna go léir sa tábla a chur i gcomhar "
"sula ndéanfaidh sé an comparáid. Má tá na luachanna ``'abc'``, `def'``` i do "
"thábla agus má chuireann tú ceist ar ``WHERE mycolumn=0``, meaitneoidh an dá "
"shraith. Ar an gcaoi chéanna, meaitseálfaidh ``WHERE mycolumn=1`` an luach "
"``'abc1'`. Dá bhrí sin, caitheoidh réimsí cineál sreangán atá san áireamh i "
"Django an luach chuig teaghrán i gcónaí sula n-úsáidtear é i bhfiosrú"

msgid ""
"If you implement custom model fields that inherit "
"from :class:`~django.db.models.Field` directly, are "
"overriding :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.get_prep_value`, or "
"use :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.RawSQL`, :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.extra`, "
"or :meth:`~django.db.models.Manager.raw`, you should ensure that you perform "
"appropriate typecasting."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú réimsí samhail saincheaptha a chuireann oidhreacht ó:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Field` i bhfeidhm go díreach, tá siad róthéar:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.field.get_prep_value`, nó úsáide:class: "
"`~django.db.Models.Expressions.rawsql`, :meth: "
"`~django.db.db.s.query.queryset.extra`, nó: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.manager.raw`, ba cheart duit a chinntiú go ndéanann tú "
"cineastáil iomchuí."

msgid "SQLite notes"
msgstr "Nótaí SQLite"

msgid "Django supports SQLite 3.31.0 and later."
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django le SQLite 3.31.0 agus níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"SQLite_ provides an excellent development alternative for applications that "
"are predominantly read-only or require a smaller installation footprint. As "
"with all database servers, though, there are some differences that are "
"specific to SQLite that you should be aware of."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn SQLite_ rogha forbartha den scoth d'iarratais nach bhfuil léite "
"amháin den chuid is mó nó a dteastaíonn lorg suiteála níos lú uathu. Mar is "
"amhlaidh le gach freastalaithe bunachar sonraí, áfach, tá roinnt difríochtaí "
"ann atá sonrach do SQLite ar chóir duit a bheith ar an eolas fúthu."

msgid "Substring matching and case sensitivity"
msgstr "Meaitseáil fo-shraith agus íogaireacht"

msgid ""
"For all SQLite versions, there is some slightly counterintuitive behavior "
"when attempting to match some types of strings.  These are triggered when "
"using the :lookup:`iexact` or :lookup:`contains` filters in querysets. The "
"behavior splits into two cases:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"1. For substring matching, all matches are done case-insensitively. That is "
"a filter such as ``filter(name__contains=\"aa\")`` will match a name of "
"``\"Aabb\"``."
msgstr ""
"1. Maidir le meaitseáil fotheagán, déantar gach cluiche go mí-íogair. Is é "
"sin scagaire mar ``filter (name__contains=\"aa”) ``a mheaitseálfaidh ainm "
"``\"Aabb\"``."

msgid ""
"2. For strings containing characters outside the ASCII range, all exact "
"string matches are performed case-sensitively, even when the case-"
"insensitive options are passed into the query. So the :lookup:`iexact` "
"filter will behave exactly the same as the :lookup:`exact` filter in these "
"cases."
msgstr ""
"2. Maidir le teaghráin ina bhfuil carachtair lasmuigh den raon ASCII, "
"déantar gach cluiche sreangán cruinn go cás-íogair, fiú nuair a chuirtear na "
"roghanna cás-neamh-íogair isteach sa cheist. Mar sin iompróidh an "
"scagair:lookup: `iexact` díreach mar an gcéanna leis an scagair:lookup: "
"`exact` sna cásanna seo."

msgid ""
"Some possible workarounds for this are `documented at sqlite.org`_, but they "
"aren't utilized by the default SQLite backend in Django, as incorporating "
"them would be fairly difficult to do robustly. Thus, Django exposes the "
"default SQLite behavior and you should be aware of this when doing case-"
"insensitive or substring filtering."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt réamhshocruithe féideartha chuige seo `doiciméadaithe ag "
"sqlite.org`_, ach ní úsáideann an cúltaca réamhshocraithe SQLite i Django "
"iad, mar bheadh sé deacair measartha iad a ionchorprú go láidir. Dá bhrí "
"sin, nochtann Django an t-iompar réamhshocraithe SQLite agus ba chóir duit a "
"bheith ar an eolas faoi seo agus tú ag déanamh scagadh cás-neamh-íogair nó "
"fo-string."

msgid "Decimal handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil deach"

msgid ""
"SQLite has no real decimal internal type. Decimal values are internally "
"converted to the ``REAL`` data type (8-byte IEEE floating point number), as "
"explained in the `SQLite datatypes documentation`__, so they don't support "
"correctly-rounded decimal floating point arithmetic."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon chineál inmheánach dáiríre deachúil ag SQLite. Déantar luachanna "
"deachúla a thiontú go hinmheánach go dtí an cineál sonraí `REAL`` (uimhir "
"phointe snámh IEEE 8-bheart), mar a mhínítear sa doiciméadú `SQLite "
"datatypees' __, ionas nach dtacaíonn siad le huimhríocht snámphointe "
"deachúil cruinn i gceart."

msgid "\"Database is locked\" errors"
msgstr "Earráidí “Tá bunachar sonraí faoi ghlas”"

msgid ""
"SQLite is meant to be a lightweight database, and thus can't support a high "
"level of concurrency. ``OperationalError: database is locked`` errors "
"indicate that your application is experiencing more concurrency than "
"``sqlite`` can handle in default configuration. This error means that one "
"thread or process has an exclusive lock on the database connection and "
"another thread timed out waiting for the lock the be released."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé i gceist gur bunachar sonraí éadrom é SQLite, agus dá bhrí sin ní "
"féidir leis tacú le leibhéal ard comhréireachta. ``OperationalError: tá "
"bunachar sonraí faoi ghlas ``léiríonn earráidí go bhfuil níos mó "
"comhréireachta ag d'iarratas ná mar is féidir le `sqlite` a láimhseáil i "
"gcumraíocht réamhshocraithe. Ciallaíonn an earráid seo go bhfuil glas "
"eisiach ag snáithe nó próiseas amháin ar nasc an bhunachar sonraí agus "
"snáithe eile amuigh amach ag fanacht go scaoilfear an glas."

msgid ""
"Python's SQLite wrapper has a default timeout value that determines how long "
"the second thread is allowed to wait on the lock before it times out and "
"raises the ``OperationalError: database is locked`` error."
msgstr ""
"Tá luach ama réamhshocraithe ag fillteán SQLite Python a chinneann cé chomh "
"fada agus a cheadaítear don dara snáithe fanacht ar an glas sula n-aimsíonn "
"sé amach agus ardaíonn sé an earráid ``OperationalError: bunachar sonraí "
"faoi ghlas ``."

msgid "If you're getting this error, you can solve it by:"
msgstr "Má tá an earráid seo á fháil agat, is féidir leat é a réiteach trí:"

msgid ""
"Switching to another database backend. At a certain point SQLite becomes too "
"\"lite\" for real-world applications, and these sorts of concurrency errors "
"indicate you've reached that point."
msgstr ""
"Aistriú go cúltaca bunachar sonraí eile. Ag pointe áirithe éiríonn SQLite "
"ró-“ lite” d'fheidhmchláir an domhain fíor, agus léiríonn na cineálacha "
"earráidí comhréireachta seo gur shroich tú an pointe sin."

msgid ""
"Rewriting your code to reduce concurrency and ensure that database "
"transactions are short-lived."
msgstr ""
"Do chód a athscríobh chun comhréireacht a laghdú agus a chinntiú go bhfuil "
"idirbhearta bunachar sonraí gearrré."

msgid ""
"Increase the default timeout value by setting the ``timeout`` database "
"option::"
msgstr ""
"Méadaigh an luach ama réamhshocraithe tríd an rogha bunachar sonraí "
"``timeout` a shocrú::"

msgid ""
"This will make SQLite wait a bit longer before throwing \"database is "
"locked\" errors; it won't really do anything to solve them."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh sé seo ar SQLite fanacht beagán níos faide sula gcaitheann sé "
"earráidí “tá bunachar sonraí faoi ghlas”; ní dhéanfaidh sé aon rud i "
"ndáiríre chun iad a réiteach."

msgid "Transactions behavior"
msgstr "Iompar idirbhearta"

msgid ""
"SQLite supports three transaction modes: ``DEFERRED``, ``IMMEDIATE``, and "
"``EXCLUSIVE``."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn SQLite le trí mhodh idirbheart: ``DIFRÉAD``, `IMMEDIATE``, agus "
"``EXCLUSIVE``."

msgid ""
"The default is ``DEFERRED``. If you need to use a different mode, set it in "
"the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`, for example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an réamhshocraithe ná ``FERRED``. Más gá duit modh difriúil a úsáid, "
"socraigh é sa chuid:SETTING: `OPTIONS` de do chumraíocht bunachar sonraí "
"in:setting: `DATABASES`, mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"To make sure your transactions wait until ``timeout`` before raising "
"\"Database is Locked\", change the transaction mode to ``IMMEDIATE``."
msgstr ""
"Chun a chinntiú go fanann d'idirbhearta go dtí go n-ardóidh tú “Timeout” "
"sula ndéantar “Bunachar Sonraí faoi ghlas”, athraigh an modh idirbheart go "
"``IMREACHTA``."

msgid ""
"For the best performance with ``IMMEDIATE`` and ``EXCLUSIVE``, transactions "
"should be as short as possible. This might be hard to guarantee for all of "
"your views so the usage of :setting:`ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-"
"ATOMIC_REQUESTS>` is discouraged  in this case."
msgstr ""
"Chun an fheidhmíocht is fearr le `IMMEDIATE`` agus ``EXCLUSIVE``, ba chóir "
"go mbeadh idirbhearta chomh gearr agus is féidir. B'fhéidir go mbeadh sé "
"deacair é seo a ráthú do chuid tuairimí go léir mar sin díspreagtar "
"úsáid:setting: `ATOMIC_REQUESTS <DATABASE-ATOMIC_REQUESTS>`sa chás seo."

msgid "For more information see `Transactions in SQLite`_."
msgstr "Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise féach `Idirbhearta i SQLite`_."

msgid "``QuerySet.select_for_update()`` not supported"
msgstr "``QuerySet.Select_for_Update () ``níl tacaíocht"

msgid ""
"SQLite does not support the ``SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`` syntax. Calling it "
"will have no effect."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn SQLite leis an ``SELECT... LE HAGHAIDH COMHRÉIR A NUASHONRÚ. Ní "
"bheidh aon éifeacht ag glaoch air."

msgid "Isolation when using ``QuerySet.iterator()``"
msgstr "Lionadh agus tú ag úsáid ``QuerySet.iterator () ``"

msgid ""
"There are special considerations described in `Isolation In SQLite`_ when "
"modifying a table while iterating over it using :meth:`.QuerySet.iterator`. "
"If a row is added, changed, or deleted within the loop, then that row may or "
"may not appear, or may appear twice, in subsequent results fetched from the "
"iterator. Your code must handle this."
msgstr ""
"Tá breithnithe speisialta ann a thuairiscítear in `Isolation In SQLite`_ "
"agus tábla á mhodhnú agus tú ag athrú air ag baint úsáide as: meth: "
"`.querySet.iterator`. Má chuirtear sraith leis, a athraítear nó a scriosadh "
"laistigh den lúb, ansin d'fhéadfadh nó nach mbeadh an tsraith sin le "
"feiceáil, nó d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith le feiceáil faoi dhó, i dtorthaí ina "
"dhiaidh sin a fhaightear ón iterator. Caithfidh do chód é seo a láimhseáil."

msgid "Enabling JSON1 extension on SQLite"
msgstr "Síneadh JSON1 a chumasú ar SQLite"

msgid ""
"To use :class:`~django.db.models.JSONField` on SQLite, you need to enable "
"the `JSON1 extension`_ on Python's :py:mod:`sqlite3` library. If the "
"extension is not enabled on your installation, a system error "
"(``fields.E180``) will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Chun: class: `~django.db.models.jsonField` a úsáid ar SQLite, ní mór duit an "
"síneadh `JSON1 `_ a chumasú ar leabharlann Python 's:PY:MOD: `sqlite3`. Mura "
"bhfuil an síneadh cumasaithe ar do shuiteáil, ardófar earráid chórais "
"(`Fields.e180`)."

msgid ""
"To enable the JSON1 extension you can follow the instruction on `the wiki "
"page`_."
msgstr ""
"Chun an síneadh JSON1 a chumasú is féidir leat an treoir a leanúint ar `an "
"leathanach wiki`_."

msgid "The JSON1 extension is enabled by default on SQLite 3.38+."
msgstr ""
"Tá an síneadh JSON1 cumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe ar SQLite 3.38+."

msgid "Setting pragma options"
msgstr "Roghanna pragma a shocrú"

msgid ""
"`Pragma options`_ can be set upon connection by using the ``init_command`` "
"in the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your database configuration "
"in :setting:`DATABASES`. The example below shows how to enable extra "
"durability of synchronous writes and change the ``cache_size``::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir `Pragma roghanna `_ a shocrú ar nasc tríd an ``init_command ``a "
"úsáid sa chuid: setting: `OPTIONS` de chumraíocht do bhunachar sonraí "
"in:setting: `DATABASES`. Taispeánann an sampla thíos conas marthanacht "
"bhreise na scríbhneoireachtaí sioncrónach a chumasú agus an `cache_size`` a "
"athrú:"

msgid "Oracle notes"
msgstr "Nótaí Oracle"

msgid ""
"Django supports `Oracle Database Server`_ versions 19c and higher. Version "
"2.3.0 or higher of the `oracledb`_ Python driver is required."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for ``cx_Oracle`` is deprecated."
msgstr "Tá tacaíocht do ``CX_Oracle`` díluaite."

msgid ""
"In order for the ``python manage.py migrate`` command to work, your Oracle "
"database user must have privileges to run the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Ionas go n-oibreoidh an t-ordú `python manage.py migrate``, ní mór "
"pribhléidí a bheith ag d'úsáideoir bunachar sonraí Oracle chun na horduithe "
"seo a leanas a reáchtáil:"

msgid "CREATE TABLE"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH TÁBLA"

msgid "CREATE SEQUENCE"
msgstr "SEICHEAMH A CHRUTHÚ"

msgid "CREATE PROCEDURE"
msgstr "CRUTHÚ NÓS IMEACHTA"

msgid "CREATE TRIGGER"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH TRUICEAR"

msgid ""
"To run a project's test suite, the user usually needs these *additional* "
"privileges:"
msgstr ""
"Chun sraith tástála tionscadail a reáchtáil, de ghnáth teastaíonn na "
"pribhléidí* breiseanna* seo ón úsáideoir"

msgid "CREATE USER"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH ÚSÁIDEOIR"

msgid "ALTER USER"
msgstr "ATHRAIGH ÚSÁIDEOIR"

msgid "DROP USER"
msgstr "SCAOIL ÚSÁIDEOIR"

msgid "CREATE TABLESPACE"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH SPÁS TÁBLA"

msgid "DROP TABLESPACE"
msgstr "SPÁS TÁBLA TITIM"

msgid "CREATE SESSION WITH ADMIN OPTION"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH SEISIÚN LE ROGHA RIARACHÁIN"

msgid "CREATE TABLE WITH ADMIN OPTION"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH TÁBLA LE ROGHA RIARACHÁIN"

msgid "CREATE SEQUENCE WITH ADMIN OPTION"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH SEICHEAMH LE ROGHA RIARACHÁIN"

msgid "CREATE PROCEDURE WITH ADMIN OPTION"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH NÓS IMEACHTA LE ROGHA RIARACHÁIN"

msgid "CREATE TRIGGER WITH ADMIN OPTION"
msgstr "CRUTHAIGH TRUICEAR LE ROGHA RIARACHÁIN"

msgid ""
"While the ``RESOURCE`` role has the required ``CREATE TABLE``, ``CREATE "
"SEQUENCE``, ``CREATE PROCEDURE``, and ``CREATE TRIGGER`` privileges, and a "
"user granted ``RESOURCE WITH ADMIN OPTION`` can grant ``RESOURCE``, such a "
"user cannot grant the individual privileges (e.g. ``CREATE TABLE``), and "
"thus ``RESOURCE WITH ADMIN OPTION`` is not usually sufficient for running "
"tests."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil na pribhléidí riachtanacha ``CREATE TABLE``, `CREATE "
"SEQUENCE``, `CREATE PROCESURE``, agus `CREATE TRIGGER``, agus is féidir le "
"húsáideoir deonaithe `RESOURCE WITH ADMIN OPTION`` a dheonú ``ACMHAIN``, ní "
"féidir le húsáideoir den sórt sin na pribhléidí aonair a dheonú (m.sh. "
"`CREATE TABLE``), agus dá bhrí sin `RESOURCE WITH ADMIN OPTION`` Ní leor "
"``de ghnáth chun tástálacha a reáchtáil."

msgid ""
"Some test suites also create views or materialized views; to run these, the "
"user also needs ``CREATE VIEW WITH ADMIN OPTION`` and ``CREATE MATERIALIZED "
"VIEW WITH ADMIN OPTION`` privileges. In particular, this is needed for "
"Django's own test suite."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn roinnt sraith tástála tuairimí nó tuairimí ábhartha freisin; chun "
"iad seo a reáchtáil, teastaíonn pribhléidí “CREATE VIEW WITH ADMIN ROGHA” "
"agus `CRUTHAIGH AMHARC ÁIRITHE LE ROGHA ADMIN ``ag an úsáideoir freisin. Go "
"háirithe, tá sé seo ag teastáil le haghaidh sraith tástála Django féin."

msgid ""
"All of these privileges are included in the DBA role, which is appropriate "
"for use on a private developer's database."
msgstr ""
"Tá na pribhléidí seo go léir san áireamh sa ról DBA, atá oiriúnach le húsáid "
"ar bhunachar sonraí forbróra príobháideach."

msgid ""
"The Oracle database backend uses the ``SYS.DBMS_LOB`` and "
"``SYS.DBMS_RANDOM`` packages, so your user will require execute permissions "
"on it. It's normally accessible to all users by default, but in case it is "
"not, you'll need to grant permissions like so:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann cúltaca bunachar sonraí Oracle na pacáistí ``SYS.DBMS_LOB`` agus "
"`SYS.DBMS_RANDOM``, mar sin beidh ceadanna forghníomhaithe ag teastáil ó "
"úsáideoir. De ghnáth bíonn sé inrochtana do gach úsáideoir de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, ach i gcás nach bhfuil, beidh ort ceadanna mar sin a dheonú:"

msgid ""
"To connect using the service name of your Oracle database, your "
"``settings.py`` file should look something like this::"
msgstr ""
"Chun nascadh ag baint úsáide as ainm seirbhíse do bhunachar sonraí Oracle, "
