msgstr ""
"Tá athrú mór ag leaganacha Django agus gnéithe ORM a thacaíonn na cúltaca "
"neamhfhoifigiúla seo. Ba cheart ceisteanna maidir le cumais shonracha na "
"gcúltaca neamhoifigiúla seo, mar aon le haon cheisteanna tacaíochta, a "
"threorú chuig na bealaí tacaíochta a sholáthraíonn gach tionscadal tríú"

msgid "``django-admin`` and ``manage.py``"
msgstr "``django-admin`` agus ``manage.py``"

msgid ""
"``django-admin`` is Django's command-line utility for administrative tasks. "
"This document outlines all it can do."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``django-admin ``fóntais líne ordaithe Django le haghaidh tascanna "
"riaracháin. Tugann an doiciméad seo leagan amach ar gach is féidir leis a "
"dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"In addition, ``manage.py`` is automatically created in each Django project. "
"It does the same thing as ``django-admin`` but also sets "
"the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment variable so that it points "
"to your project's ``settings.py`` file."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, cruthaítear `manage.py`` go huathoibríoch i ngach "
"tionscadal Django. Déanann sé an rud céanna le ``django-admin ``ach "
"socraíonn sé an athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` ionas go "
"dtreoraíonn sé comhad ``settings.py`` do thionscadail."

msgid ""
"The ``django-admin`` script should be on your system path if you installed "
"Django via ``pip``. If it's not in your path, ensure you have your virtual "
"environment activated."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an script ``django-admin ``ar do chonair chórais má "
"shuiteáil tú Django trí ``pip``. Mura bhfuil sé i do chosán, cinntigh go "
"bhfuil do thimpeallacht fhíorúil gníomhachtaithe agat."

msgid ""
"Generally, when working on a single Django project, it's easier to use "
"``manage.py`` than ``django-admin``. If you need to switch between multiple "
"Django settings files, use ``django-admin`` "
"with :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` or the :option:`--settings` command "
"line option."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, agus tú ag obair ar thionscadal amháin Django, tá sé níos "
"éasca ``manage.py`` a úsáid ná ``django-admin ``. Más gá duit aistriú idir "
"iolracha comhaid socruithe Django, bain úsáid as ``django-admin ``le: "
"envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` nó an rogha líne ordaithe: `--settings`."

msgid ""
"The command-line examples throughout this document use ``django-admin`` to "
"be consistent, but any example can use ``manage.py`` or ``python -m django`` "
"just as well."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann na samplaí líne ordaithe ar fud an doiciméad seo ``django-admin "
"``le bheith comhsheasmhach, ach is féidir le haon sampla `manage.py`` nó "
"`python -m django`` a úsáid chomh maith."

msgid ""
"``command`` should be one of the commands listed in this document. "
"``options``, which is optional, should be zero or more of the options "
"available for the given command."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh ``ord`` ar cheann de na horduithe atá liostaithe sa "
"doiciméad seo. Ba chóir go mbeadh “roghanna”, atá roghnach, nialas nó níos "
"mó de na roghanna atá ar fáil don ordú tugtha."

msgid "Getting runtime help"
msgstr "Cúnamh rith a fháil"

msgid ""
"Run ``django-admin help`` to display usage information and a list of the "
"commands provided by each application."
msgstr ""
"Rith ``cabhair django-admin ``chun faisnéis úsáide agus liosta de na "
"horduithe a sholáthraíonn gach feidhmchlár a thaispeáint."

msgid ""
"Run ``django-admin help --commands`` to display a list of all available "
"commands."
msgstr ""
"Rith ``django-admin help --commands`` chun liosta de na horduithe go léir "
"atá ar fáil a thaispeáint."

msgid ""
"Run ``django-admin help <command>`` to display a description of the given "
"command and a list of its available options."
msgstr ""
"Rith ``django-admin cabhair <command>``chun cur síos ar an ordú tugtha agus "
"liosta de na roghanna atá ar fáil a thaispeáint."

msgid "App names"
msgstr "Ainmneacha aipeanna"

msgid ""
"Many commands take a list of \"app names.\" An \"app name\" is the basename "
"of the package containing your models. For example, if "
"your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains the string ``'mysite.blog'``, the "
"app name is ``blog``."
msgstr ""
"Tógann go leor orduithe liosta de “ainmneacha aipeanna.” Is é “ainm aip” "
"bunainm an phacáiste ina bhfuil do mhúnlaí. Mar shampla, má tá an teaghrán "
"``'mysite.blog'`` i dta:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, is é `blog`` ainm an aip."

msgid "Determining the version"
msgstr "An leagan a chinneadh"

msgid "Run ``django-admin version`` to display the current Django version."
msgstr ""
"Rith ``leagan django-admin ``chun an leagan reatha Django a thaispeáint."

msgid "The output follows the schema described in :pep:`440`:"
msgstr "Leanann an t-aschur an scéim a thuairiscítear in:pep: `440`:"

msgid "Displaying debug output"
msgstr "Aschur dífhabhtaithe á th"

msgid ""
"Use :option:`--verbosity`, where it is supported, to specify the amount of "
"notification and debug information that ``django-admin`` prints to the "
"console."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: rogha: `--verbosity`, nuair a thacaítear leis, chun an méid fógra a "
"shonrú agus an fhaisnéis a dhífhabhtú a phriontáil ``django-admin ``chuig an "
"gconsól."

msgid "Available commands"
msgstr "Orduithe atá ar fáil"

msgid "``check``"
msgstr "``Seiceáil ``"

msgid ""
"Uses the :doc:`system check framework </ref/checks>` to inspect the entire "
"Django project for common problems."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé an: doc: `creat seiceála córas` chun an tionscadal iomlán "
"Django a ini</ref/checks> úchadh le haghaidh fadhbanna coitianta."

msgid ""
"By default, all apps will be checked. You can check a subset of apps by "
"providing a list of app labels as arguments:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, seiceálfar gach aip. Is féidir leat fo-thacar "
"aipeanna a sheiceáil trí liosta lipéid aipeanna a sholáthar mar argóintí:"

msgid ""
"The system check framework performs many different types of checks that "
"are :ref:`categorized with tags <system-check-builtin-tags>`. You can use "
"these tags to restrict the checks performed to just those in a particular "
"category. For example, to perform only models and compatibility checks, run:"
msgstr ""
"<system-check-builtin-tags>Déanann creat seiceála an chórais go leor "
"cineálacha éagsúla seiceálacha ara:ref: `catagóirithe le clibeanna `. Is "
"féidir leat na clibeanna seo a úsáid chun na seiceálacha a dhéantar a "
"shrianadh chuig iad siúd i gcatagóir áirithe. Mar shampla, chun samhlacha "
"agus seiceálacha comhoiriúnachta a dhéanamh amháin, reáchtáil:"

msgid "Specifies the database to run checks requiring database access:"
msgstr "Sonraíonn an bunachar sonraí chun seiceálacha a reáchtáil a éilíonn"

msgid "By default, these checks will not be run."
msgstr "De réir réamhshocraithe, ní reáchtálfar na seiceálacha seo."

msgid "Lists all available tags."
msgstr "Liostaíonn gach clib atá ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Activates some additional checks that are only relevant in a deployment "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhachtaíonn sé roinnt seiceálacha breise nach bhfuil ábhartha ach i "
"suíomh imscartha."

msgid ""
"You can use this option in your local development environment, but since "
"your local development settings module may not have many of your production "
"settings, you will probably want to point the ``check`` command at a "
"different settings module, either by setting "
"the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment variable, or by passing the "
"``--settings`` option:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an rogha seo a úsáid i do thimpeallacht forbartha áitiúil, "
"ach ós rud é go mb'fhéidir nach bhfuil go leor de do shocruithe táirgeachta "
"ag do mhodúl socruithe forbartha áitiúil, is dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh "
"an t-ordú ``check`` a chur ar mhodúl socruithe difriúil, tríd an athróg "
"timpeallachta:"

msgid ""
"Or you could run it directly on a production or staging deployment to verify "
"that the correct settings are in use (omitting ``--settings``). You could "
"even make it part of your integration test suite."
msgstr ""
"Nó d'fhéadfá é a reáchtáil go díreach ar imscaradh léiriúcháin nó stáitse "
"chun a fhíorú go bhfuil na socruithe cearta in úsáid (``--socruithe ``a "
"fhágáil). D'fhéadfá é a dhéanamh mar chuid de do tsraith tástála "
"comhtháthaithe fiú."

msgid ""
"Specifies the message level that will cause the command to exit with a non-"
"zero status. Default is ``ERROR``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an leibhéal teachtaireachta a chuirfidh ar an ordú imeacht le "
"stádas neamh-nialas. Is é “ERROR” réamhshocraithe."

msgid "``compilemessages``"
msgstr "``teachtaireachtaí tiomsaitheach``"

msgid ""
"Compiles ``.po`` files created by :djadmin:`makemessages` to ``.mo`` files "
"for use with the built-in gettext support. See :doc:`/topics/i18n/index`."
msgstr ""
"Tiomsaíonn sé comhaid ``.po`` a chruthaí:djadmin: `makemessages` chuig "
"comhaid `.mo`` le húsáid leis an tacaíocht gettext ionsuite. Féach: doc: `/"
"topics/i18n/index`."

msgid ""
"Specifies the locale(s) to process. If not provided, all locales are "
"processed."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na háiteanna atá le próiseáil. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, déantar "
"gach ceann áitiúil a phróiseáil."

msgid ""
"Specifies the locale(s) to exclude from processing. If not provided, no "
"locales are excluded."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na háiteanna atá le eisiamh ó phróiseáil. Mura gcuirtear ar "
"fáil, níl aon áiteanna áitiúla eisiata."

msgid "Includes `fuzzy translations`_ into compiled files."
msgstr "Cuimsíonn sé `aistriúcháin doiléirí`_ i gcomhaid thiomsaithe."

msgid ""
"Ignores directories matching the given :mod:`glob`-style pattern. Use "
"multiple times to ignore more."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé neamhaird ar eolairí a mheaitseálann leis an bpatrún given:mod: "
"`glob`-style. Úsáid arís agus arís eile chun neamhaird a dhéanamh de"

msgid "``createcachetable``"
msgstr "``cruthaitheachtabhaí``"

msgid ""
"Creates the cache tables for use with the database cache backend using the "
"information from your settings file. See :doc:`/topics/cache` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé na táblaí taisce le húsáid le cúltaca taisce an bhunachar "
"sonraí agus an fhaisnéis ó do chomhad socruithe á úsáid. Féach: doc: `/"
"topics/cache` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"Specifies the database in which the cache table(s) will be created. Defaults "
"to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí ina gcruthófar an tábla/na taisce. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Prints the SQL that would be run without actually running it, so you can "
"customize it or use the migrations framework."
msgstr ""
"Priontáil an SQL a bheidh á reáchtáil gan é a reáchtáil i ndáiríre, ionas "
"gur féidir leat é a shaincheapadh nó an creat imirce a úsáid."

msgid "``dbshell``"
msgstr "``dbshell``"

msgid ""
"Runs the command-line client for the database engine specified in "
"your :setting:`ENGINE <DATABASE-ENGINE>` setting, with the connection "
"parameters specified in your :setting:`USER`, :setting:`PASSWORD`, etc., "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé an cliant líne ordaithe don inneall bunachar sonraí a "
"shonraítear i do shuíomh: socrú: `ENGIN <DATABASE-ENGINE>`, leis na "
"paraiméadair nasc a shonraítear i do: setting: `USER`, :setting: `PASSWORD`, "
"srl., socruithe."

msgid "For PostgreSQL, this runs the ``psql`` command-line client."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le PostgreSQL, ritheann sé seo an cliant líne ordaithe ``psql ``."

msgid "For MySQL, this runs the ``mysql`` command-line client."
msgstr "Maidir le MySQL, ritheann sé seo an cliant líne ordaithe ``mysql`."

msgid "For SQLite, this runs the ``sqlite3`` command-line client."
msgstr "Maidir le SQLite, ritheann sé seo an cliant líne ordaithe ``sqlite3`."

msgid "For Oracle, this runs the ``sqlplus`` command-line client."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le Oracle, ritheann sé seo an cliant líne ordaithe ``sqlplus ``."

msgid ""
"This command assumes the programs are on your ``PATH`` so that a call to the "
"program name (``psql``, ``mysql``, ``sqlite3``, ``sqlplus``) will find the "
"program in the right place. There's no way to specify the location of the "
"program manually."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an t-ordú seo leis go bhfuil na cláir ar do `PATH`` ionas go "
"bhfaighidh glao chuig ainm an chláir (``psql``, `mysql``, `sqlite3``, "
"`sqlplus``) an clár san áit cheart. Níl aon bhealach ann suíomh an chláir a "
"shonrú de láimh."

msgid ""
"Specifies the database onto which to open a shell. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí chun blaosc a oscailt air. Réamhshocraithe "
"go ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Any arguments following a ``--`` divider will be passed on to the underlying "
"command-line client. For example, with PostgreSQL you can use the ``psql`` "
"command's ``-c`` flag to execute a raw SQL query directly:"
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear aon argóintí tar éis roinnteora ``-- `ar aghaidh chuig an gcliant "
"líne ordaithe bunúsach. Mar shampla, le PostgreSQL is féidir leat bratach ``-"
"c`` an ordaithe ``psql`` a úsáid chun fiosrúchán SQL amh a fhorghníomhú go "
"díreach:"

msgid ""
"On MySQL/MariaDB, you can do this with the ``mysql`` command's ``-e`` flag:"
msgstr ""
"Ar MySQL/MariaDB, is féidir leat é seo a dhéanamh le bratach ``-e`` an "
"ordaithe ``mysql``:"

msgid ""
"Be aware that not all options set in the :setting:`OPTIONS` part of your "
"database configuration in :setting:`DATABASES` are passed to the command-"
"line client, e.g. ``'isolation_level'``."
msgstr ""
"Bí ar an eolas nach gcuirtear gach rogha atá leagtha síos sa chuid:setting: "
"`OPTIONS` de chumraíocht do bhunachar sonraí in:setting: `DATABASES` chuig "
"an gcliant líne ordaithe, m.sh. ``isolation_level'``."

msgid "``diffsettings``"
msgstr "``difríochtaí ``"

msgid ""
"Displays differences between the current settings file and Django's default "
"settings (or another settings file specified by :option:`--default`)."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé difríochtaí idir an comhad socruithe reatha agus socruithe "
"réamhshocraithe Django (nó comhad socruithe eile a shonraítear ar:option: `--"
"default`)."

msgid ""
"Settings that don't appear in the defaults are followed by ``\"###\"``. For "
"example, the default settings don't define :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF`, "
"so :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF` is followed by ``\"###\"`` in the output of "
"``diffsettings``."
msgstr ""
"Leanann ``\"###\"`` socruithe nach bhfuil le feiceáil sna réamhshocruithe. "
"Mar shampla, ní shainmhíníonn na socruithe réamhshocraithe:setting: "
"`ROOT_URLCONF`, mar sin: `ROOT_URLCONF` tar éis ``\"###\"`` i aschur "
"``diffsettings``."

msgid ""
"Displays all settings, even if they have Django's default value. Such "
"settings are prefixed by ``\"###\"``."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé na socruithe go léir, fiú má tá luach réamhshocraithe Django "
"acu. Tá socruithe den sórt sin réamhshocraithe le ``\"###\"``."

msgid ""
"The settings module to compare the current settings against. Leave empty to "
"compare against Django's default settings."
msgstr ""
"An modúl socruithe chun comparáid a dhéanamh idir na socruithe reatha ina "
"choinne. Fág folamh le comparáid i gcoinne socruithe réamhshocraithe Django."

msgid ""
"Specifies the output format. Available values are ``hash`` and ``unified``. "
"``hash`` is the default mode that displays the output that's described "
"above. ``unified`` displays the output similar to ``diff -u``. Default "
"settings are prefixed with a minus sign, followed by the changed setting "
"prefixed with a plus sign."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an fhormáid aschuir. Is iad na luachanna atá ar fáil ná `hash`` "
"agus ``aontaithe ``. Is é ``hash ``an modh réamhshocraithe a thaispeánann an "
"t-aschur atá cur síos thuas. Taispeánann ``unified`` an t-aschur cosúil le "
"``diff -u``. Déantar socruithe réamhshocraithe a réamhshocrú le comhartha "
"lúide, agus ina dhiaidh sin tá an suíomh athraithe réamhshocraithe le "
"comhartha móide."

msgid "``dumpdata``"
msgstr "``Dumpdata``"

msgid ""
"Outputs to standard output all data in the database associated with the "
"named application(s)."
msgstr ""
"Aschuir chuig aschur caighdeánach gach sonraí sa bhunachar sonraí a "
"bhaineann leis an bhfeidhmchlár (í) ainmnithe."

msgid ""
"If no application name is provided, all installed applications will be "
"dumped."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcuirtear aon ainm iarratais ar fáil, déanfar gach feidhmchlár "
"suiteáilte a dumpáil."

msgid ""
"The output of ``dumpdata`` can be used as input for :djadmin:`loaddata`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir aschur ``dumpdata ``a úsáid mar ionchur le haghaidh: djadmin: "
"`loaddata`."

msgid ""
"When result of ``dumpdata`` is saved as a file, it can serve as "
"a :ref:`fixture <fixtures-explanation>` for :ref:`tests <topics-testing-"
"fixtures>` or as an :ref:`initial data <initial-data-via-fixtures>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-testing-fixtures><initial-data-via-fixtures>Nuair a shábháiltear "
"toradh ``dumpdata`` mar chomhad, féadfaidh sé feidhmiú mar a:ref: `daingneán "
"`le haghaidh: ref: `tástálacha` nó mar an <fixtures-explanation>:ref: "
"`sonraí tosaigh `."

msgid ""
"Note that ``dumpdata`` uses the default manager on the model for selecting "
"the records to dump. If you're using a :ref:`custom manager <custom-"
"managers>` as the default manager and it filters some of the available "
"records, not all of the objects will be dumped."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go n-úsáideann `dumpdata ``an bainisteoir réamhshocraithe "
"ar an tsamhail chun na taifid a roghnú le dumpáil. Má tá a: ref: "
"`bainisteoir saincheaptha <custom-managers>`á úsáid agat mar an bhainisteoir "
"réamhshocraithe agus scagann sé cuid de na taifid atá ar fáil, ní dhéanfar "
"na rudaí go léir a dumpáil."

msgid ""
"Uses Django's base manager, dumping records which might otherwise be "
"filtered or modified by a custom manager."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann bainisteoir bonn Django, taifid dumpála a d'fhéadfadh bainisteoir "
"saincheaptha a scagadh nó a mhodhnú ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"Specifies the serialization format of the output. Defaults to JSON. "
"Supported formats are listed in :ref:`serialization-formats`."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé formáid sraitheach an aschuir. Réamhshocraithe go JSON. Tá "
"formáidí tacaithe liostaithe in:ref: `serialization-formats`."

msgid ""
"Specifies the number of indentation spaces to use in the output. Defaults to "
"``None`` which displays all data on single line."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé líon na spásanna ionbhrúite le húsáid san aschur. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``None ``a thaispeánann na sonraí go léir ar líne amháin."

msgid ""
"Prevents specific applications or models (specified in the form of "
"``app_label.ModelName``) from being dumped. If you specify a model name, "
"then only that model will be excluded, rather than the entire application. "
"You can also mix application names and model names."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar iarratais nó samhlacha sonracha (sonraithe i bhfoirm "
"``App_Label.ModelName``) a dumpáil. Má shonraíonn tú ainm samhail, ansin ní "
"bheidh ach an tsamhail sin eisiata, seachas an feidhmchlár iomlán. Is féidir "
"leat ainmneacha feidhmchláir agus ainmneacha samhail a mheascadh"

msgid ""
"If you want to exclude multiple applications, pass ``--exclude`` more than "
"once:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iarratais iolracha a eisiamh, pas ``--eisiam`` níos mó ná uair "
"amháin:"

msgid ""
"Specifies the database from which data will be dumped. Defaults to "
"``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí as a ndéanfar sonraí a dumpáil. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Uses the ``natural_key()`` model method to serialize any foreign key and "
"many-to-many relationship to objects of the type that defines the method. If "
"you're dumping ``contrib.auth`` ``Permission`` objects or "
"``contrib.contenttypes`` ``ContentType`` objects, you should probably use "
"this flag. See the :ref:`natural keys <topics-serialization-natural-keys>` "
"documentation for more details on this and the next option."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé an modh samhail ``natural_key () ``chun aon eochair eachtrach "
"agus gaol go leor a shraitheadh le rudaí den chineál a shainmhíníonn an "
"modh. Má tá tú ag dumpáil rudaí ``contrib.auth`` ``Ceadúna`` nó rudaí "
"``contrib.contenttypes`` ``contentType``, is dócha gur chóir duit an bratach "
"seo a úsáid. Féach an doiciméad:ref: `eochracha nádúrtha <topics-"
"serialization-natural-keys>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoin gcéad rogha "
"seo agus an chéad rogha eile."

msgid ""
"Omits the primary key in the serialized data of this object since it can be "
"calculated during deserialization."
msgstr ""
"Fágann sé an príomh-eochair i sonraí sraitheacha an réada seo ós rud é gur "
"féidir é a ríomh le linn díshealaithe."

msgid ""
"Outputs only the objects specified by a comma separated list of primary "
"keys. This is only available when dumping one model. By default, all the "
"records of the model are output."
msgstr ""
"Ní aschuireann ach na rudaí a shonraítear le liosta scoite camóg d'eochracha "
"bunscoile. Níl sé seo ar fáil ach amháin nuair a dhumpáiltear samhail "
"amháin. De réir réamhshocraithe, tá gach taifid den tsamhail aschur."

msgid ""
"Specifies a file to write the serialized data to. By default, the data goes "
"to standard output."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé comhad chun na sonraí sraitheacha a scríobh chuig. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, téann na sonraí chuig aschur caighdeánach."

msgid ""
"When this option is set and ``--verbosity`` is greater than 0 (the default), "
"a progress bar is shown in the terminal."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraítear an rogha seo agus go bhfuil `- verbosity`` níos mó ná 0 "
"(an réamhshocraithe), taispeántar barra dul chun cinn sa chríochfort."

msgid "Fixtures compression"
msgstr "Daingneáin comhbhrú"

msgid ""
"The output file can be compressed with one of the ``bz2``, ``gz``, ``lzma``, "
"or ``xz`` formats by ending the filename with the corresponding extension. "
"For example, to output the data as a compressed JSON file:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an comhad aschuir a chomhbhrú le ceann de na formáidí ``bz2``, "
"`gz``, `lzma`, nó ``xz`` tríd an ainm comhaid a chríochnú leis an síneadh "
"comhfhreagrach. Mar shampla, chun na sonraí a aschur mar chomhad JSON "
"comhbhrúite:"

msgid "``flush``"
msgstr "```Flush``"

msgid ""
"Removes all data from the database and re-executes any post-synchronization "
"handlers. The table of which migrations have been applied is not cleared."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé na sonraí go léir ón mbunachar sonraí agus déanann sé aon "
"láimhseálaithe iar-sioncrónaithe Ní ghlantar an tábla ar cuireadh imirce i "
"bhfeidhm air."

msgid ""
"If you would rather start from an empty database and rerun all migrations, "
"you should drop and recreate the database and then run :djadmin:`migrate` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Más fearr leat tosú ó bhunachar sonraí folamh agus gach imirce a "
"athreáchtáil, ba cheart duit an bunachar sonraí a scaoileadh agus a "
"athchruthú agus ansin rith: djadmin: `migrate` ina ionad."

msgid "Suppresses all user prompts."
msgstr "Cuireann sé cosc ar gach leideanna úsáideora."

msgid "Specifies the database to flush. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí le sruthú. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Introspects the database tables in the database pointed-to by "
"the :setting:`NAME` setting and outputs a Django model module (a "
"``models.py`` file) to standard output."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé iniúchadh ar na táblaí bunachar sonraí sa bhunachar sonraí a "
"shonraítear trí:setting: `NAME` agus aschur modúl samhail Django (comhad "
"``models.py`) chuig aschur caighdeánach."

msgid ""
"You may choose what tables or views to inspect by passing their names as "
"arguments. If no arguments are provided, models are created for views only "
"if the :option:`--include-views` option is used. Models for partition tables "
"are created on PostgreSQL if the :option:`--include-partitions` option is "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú na táblaí nó na tuairimí atá le iniúchadh a roghnú trí a n-"
"ainmneacha a chur ar aghaidh Mura gcuirtear aon argóintí ar fáil, "
"cruthaítear samhlacha le haghaidh tuairimí ach amháin má úsáidtear an "
"roghna:option: `--include-views`. Cruthaítear samhlacha do tháblaí deighilte "
"ar PostgreSQL má úsáidtear an rogha: rogha: `--include-parttions`."

msgid ""
"Use this if you have a legacy database with which you'd like to use Django. "
"The script will inspect the database and create a model for each table "
"within it."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid é seo má tá bunachar sonraí oidhreachta agat ar mhaith leat Django a "
"úsáid leis. Déanfaidh an script iniúchadh ar an mbunachar sonraí agus "
"cruthóidh sé samhail do gach tábla laistigh de."

msgid ""
"As you might expect, the created models will have an attribute for every "
"field in the table. Note that ``inspectdb`` has a few special cases in its "
"field-name output:"
msgstr ""
"Mar a d'fhéadfá a bheith ag súil leis, beidh tréith ag na samhlacha "
"cruthaithe do gach réimse sa tábla. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil cúpla cás "
"speisialta ag ``inspectdb`` ina aschur ainm réimse:"

msgid ""
"If ``inspectdb`` cannot map a column's type to a model field type, it'll use "
"``TextField`` and will insert the Python comment ``'This field type is a "
"guess.'`` next to the field in the generated model. The recognized fields "
"may depend on apps listed in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. For "
"example, :mod:`django.contrib.postgres` adds recognition for several "
"PostgreSQL-specific field types."
msgstr ""
"Mura féidir le ``inspectdb`` cineál colún a mhapáil go cineál réimse "
"samhail, úsáidfidh sé ``Textfield`` agus cuirfidh sé an trácht Python "
"isteach ```Is tuairim é an cineál réimse seo.``` in aice leis an réimse sa "
"tsamhail ghintear. Féadfaidh na réimsí aitheanta ag brath ar aipeanna atá "
"liostaithe in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`. Mar shampla, cuireann :mod: "
"`django.contrib.postgres` aitheantas do roinnt cineálacha réimse atá sonrach "
"le PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"If the database column name is a Python reserved word (such as ``'pass'``, "
"``'class'`` or ``'for'``), ``inspectdb`` will append ``'_field'`` to the "
"attribute name. For example, if a table has a column ``'for'``, the "
"generated model will have a field ``'for_field'``, with the ``db_column`` "
"attribute set to ``'for'``. ``inspectdb`` will insert the Python comment "
"``'Field renamed because it was a Python reserved word.'`` next to the field."
msgstr ""
"Más focal curtha in áirithe Python é ainm an cholún bunachar sonraí (mar "
"shampla ```'pass'``, ``class'`` nó ```for'``), cuirfidh ``inspectdb`` "
"```_field'`` leis an ainm tréithe. Mar shampla, má tá colún ``'for'`` i "
"dtábla, beidh réimse ``'for_field'`` ag an tsamhail ghintear, agus an tréith "
"``db_column`` socraithe go ```for'``. Cuirfidh ``inspectdb`` an trácht "
"Python isteach ```Athainmníodh réimse toisc gur focal forchoimeádaithe "
"Python a bhí aige. '``in aice leis an réimse."

msgid ""
"This feature is meant as a shortcut, not as definitive model generation. "
"After you run it, you'll want to look over the generated models yourself to "
"make customizations. In particular, you'll need to rearrange models' order, "
"so that models that refer to other models are ordered properly."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ghné seo i gceist mar aicearra, ní mar ghiniúint samhail "
"chinntitheach. Tar éis duit é a reáchtáil, beidh tú ag iarraidh breathnú ar "
"na samhlacha ginte tú féin chun saincheaptha a dhéanamh. Go háirithe, beidh "
"ort ord samhlacha a athshocrú, ionas go n-ordófar samhlacha a thagraíonn do "
"mhúnlaí eile i gceart."

msgid ""
"Django doesn't create database defaults when "
"a :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default` is specified on a model field. "
"Similarly, database defaults aren't translated to model field defaults or "
"detected in any fashion by ``inspectdb``."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn Django réamhshocraithe bunachar sonraí nuair a shonraítear "
"a:attr: `~django.db.models.field.default` ar réimse samhail. Ar an gcaoi "
"chéanna, ní aistrítear réamhshocruithe bunachar sonraí go réimse samhail ná "
"ní bhraithnítear ar bhealach ar bith ag `inspectdb`."

msgid ""
"By default, ``inspectdb`` creates unmanaged models. That is, ``managed = "
"False`` in the model's ``Meta`` class tells Django not to manage each "
"table's creation, modification, and deletion. If you do want to allow Django "
"to manage the table's lifecycle, you'll need to change "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.managed` option to ``True`` (or remove "
"it because ``True`` is its default value)."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cruthaíonn ``inspectdb ``samhlacha neamh-"
"bhainistithe. Is é sin, deir ``bhainistithe = False`` i rang ``Meta`` an "
"tsamhail le Django gan cruthú, modhnú agus scriosadh gach tábla a "
"bhainistiú. Más mian leat ligean a thabhairt do Django saolré an tábla a "
"bhainistiú, beidh ort an rogha: attr: `~django.db.models.options.managed` a "
"athrú go `True`` (nó é a bhaint toisc gurb é `True`` a luach "
"réamhshocraithe)."

msgid "Database-specific notes"
msgstr "Nótaí sonracha bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Models are created for materialized views if :option:`--include-views` is "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaítear samhlacha le haghaidh tuairimí ábhartha má úsáidtear: rogha: `--"
"include-views`."

msgid "Models are created for foreign tables."
msgstr "Cruthaítear samhlacha le haghaidh táblaí eachtracha."

msgid ""
"Models are created for partition tables if :option:`--include-partitions` is "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaítear samhlacha le haghaidh táblaí deighilte má úsáidtear: rogha: `--"
"include-parttions`."

msgid "Specifies the database to introspect. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí chun iontráil a dhéanamh. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "If this option is provided, models are also created for partitions."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear an rogha seo ar fáil, cruthaítear samhlacha le haghaidh "
"deighiltí freisin."

msgid "Only support for PostgreSQL is implemented."
msgstr "Ní chuirtear ach tacaíocht do PostgreSQL i bhfeidhm."

msgid "If this option is provided, models are also created for database views."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear an rogha seo ar fáil, cruthaítear samhlacha freisin le haghaidh "
"tuairimí bunachar sonraí."

msgid "``loaddata``"
msgstr "``Loaddata``"

msgid ""
"Searches for and loads the contents of the named :ref:`fixture <fixtures-"
"explanation>` into the database."
msgstr ""
"<fixtures-explanation>Cuardaigh agus luchtú ábhar an ainmne:ref: `daingneáin "
"`isteach sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Specifies the database into which the data will be loaded. Defaults to "
"``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí ina luchtálfar na sonraí. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Ignores fields and models that may have been removed since the fixture was "
"originally generated."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé neamhaird ar réimsí agus samhlacha a d'fhéadfadh a bheith bainte "
"ó ghintear an daingneán ar dtús."

msgid ""
"Specifies a single app to look for fixtures in rather than looking in all "
"apps."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé aip amháin chun daingneáin a lorg seachas breathnú i ngach aip."

msgid ""
"Specifies the :ref:`serialization format <serialization-formats>` (e.g., "
"``json`` or ``xml``) for fixtures :ref:`read from stdin <loading-fixtures-"
"stdin>`."
msgstr ""
"<loading-fixtures-stdin>Sonraíonn sé an fhormáid: ref: `sraitheoireacht "
"<serialization-formats>`(m.sh., ``json`` nó ``xml``) le haghaidh daingneáin: "
"ref: `léamh ó stdin`."

msgid ""
"Excludes loading the fixtures from the given applications and/or models (in "
"the form of ``app_label`` or ``app_label.ModelName``). Use the option "
"multiple times to exclude more than one app or model."
msgstr ""
"Ní áirítear na daingneáin a luchtú ó na feidhmchláir agus/nó na samhlacha ar "
"leith (i bhfoirm ``app_label`` nó ``App_Label.ModelNam``). Úsáid an rogha "
"arís agus arís eile chun níos mó ná aip nó samhail amháin a eisiamh."

msgid "Loading fixtures from ``stdin``"
msgstr "Daingneáin á luchtú ó ``stdin``"

msgid ""
"You can use a dash as the fixture name to load input from ``sys.stdin``. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat doic a úsáid mar ainm an daingneáin chun ionchur a luchtú ó "
"`sys.stdin`. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"When reading from ``stdin``, the :option:`--format <loaddata --format>` "
"option is required to specify the :ref:`serialization format <serialization-"
"formats>` of the input (e.g., ``json`` or ``xml``)."
msgstr ""
"<serialization-formats>Agus tú ag léamh ó `stdin``, <loaddata --format>is gá "
"ar an roghna:rogha: `--format `chun an: ref: `formáid sraitheach` den "
"ionchur a shonrú (m.sh., ``json`` nó ``xml``)."

msgid ""
"Loading from ``stdin`` is useful with standard input and output "
"redirections. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tá luchtú ó `stdin ``úsáideach le hathreoruithe ionchuir agus aschuir "
"caighdeánacha. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`dumpdata` command can be used to generate input for "
"``loaddata``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an t-ordú: DJadmin: `dumpdata` a úsáid chun ionchur a ghiniúint do "
"`loaddata`."

msgid ""
"For more detail about fixtures see the :ref:`fixtures-explanation` topic."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoi daingneáin féach an t-ábhar: ref: "
"`fixtures-explication`."

msgid "``makemessages``"
msgstr "``déanmhachtaireachtaí ``"

msgid ""
"Runs over the entire source tree of the current directory and pulls out all "
"strings marked for translation. It creates (or updates) a message file in "
"the conf/locale (in the Django tree) or locale (for project and application) "
"directory. After making changes to the messages files you need to compile "
"them with :djadmin:`compilemessages` for use with the builtin gettext "
"support. See the :ref:`i18n documentation <how-to-create-language-files>` "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé thar chrann foinse iomlán an eolaire reatha agus tarraingíonn sé "
"amach gach teaghráin atá marcáilte le haistriúchán. Cruthaíonn sé (nó "
"nuashonraíonn sé) comhad teachtaireachta san eolaire conf/locale (sa chrann "
"Django) nó áitiúil (le haghaidh tionscadail agus feidhmchláir). Tar éis "
"athruithe a dhéanamh ar na comhaid teachtaireachtaí ní mór duit iad a "
"thiomsú le: djadmin: `compilemessages` le húsáid leis an tacaíocht gettext "
"bunaithe. <how-to-create-language-files>Féach an doiciméadú: ref: `i18n `le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"This command doesn't require configured settings. However, when settings "
"aren't configured, the command can't ignore the :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` "
"and :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` directories or include :setting:`LOCALE_PATHS`."
msgstr ""
"Ní theastaíonn socruithe cumraithe ag an ordú seo. Mar sin féin, nuair nach "
"bhfuil socruithe cumraithe, ní féidir leis an ordú neamhaird a dhéanamh ar "
"eolairí: socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT` agus:setting: `STATIC_ROOT` nó lena n-áirítear: "
"socrú: `LOCALE_PATHS`."

msgid "Updates the message files for all available languages."
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíonn sé na comhaid teachtaireachta do gach teanga atá ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Specifies a list of file extensions to examine (default: ``html``, ``txt``, "
"``py`` or ``js`` if :option:`--domain` is ``djangojs``)."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé liosta síntí comhaid le scrúdú (réamhshocraithe: ``html``, "
"`txt``, `py`` nó ``js ``ife:option: `--domain` is ``djangojs``)."

msgid ""
"Separate multiple extensions with commas or use ``-e`` or ``--extension`` "
"multiple times:"
msgstr ""
"Déan síntí iolracha a scaradh le camóga nó bain úsáid as ``-e`` nó ``-- "
"síneadh ``arís agus arís eile:"

msgid "Specifies the locale(s) to process."
msgstr "Sonraíonn sé na háiteanna atá le próiseáil."

msgid "Specifies the domain of the messages files. Supported options are:"
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn fearann na gcomhaid teachtaireachtaí. Is iad na roghanna tacaithe:"

msgid "``django`` for all ``*.py``, ``*.html`` and ``*.txt`` files (default)"
msgstr ""
"``django`` do gach comhad ``*.py``, `*.html`` agus ``*.txt "
"``(réamhshocraithe)"

msgid "``djangojs`` for ``*.js`` files"
msgstr "``djangojs`` do chomhaid ``*.js ``"

msgid ""
"Follows symlinks to directories when looking for new translation strings."
msgstr ""
"Leanann sé naisc shiombailí chuig eolairí agus tú ag lorg teaghráin aistriú"

msgid ""
"Ignores files or directories matching the given :mod:`glob`-style pattern. "
"Use multiple times to ignore more."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé neamhaird ar chomhaid nó eolairí a mheaitseálann leis an bpatrún "
"given:mod: `global `style. Úsáid arís agus arís eile chun neamhaird a "
"dhéanamh de"

msgid ""
"These patterns are used by default: ``'CVS'``, ``'.*'``, ``'*~'``, "
"``'*.pyc'``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear na patrúin seo de réir réamhshocraithe: ``'CVS'``, ```.*'``, "
"```*~'``, ``'*.pyc'``."

msgid "Disables the default values of ``--ignore``."
msgstr "Díchumasaíonn luachanna réamhshocraithe ``- ignore``."

msgid ""
"Disables breaking long message lines into several lines in language files."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasaíonn sé línte teachtaireachta fada a bhriseadh i roinnt línte i "
"gcomhaid"

msgid ""
"Suppresses writing '``#: filename:line``’ comment lines in language files. "
"Using this option makes it harder for technically skilled translators to "
"understand each message's context."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar scríbhneoireacht '``#: fileainm:line``' línte tráchta i "
"gcomhaid teanga. Má úsáidtear an rogha seo, bíonn sé níos deacra "
"d'aistritheoirí oilte go teicniúil comhthéacs gach teachtaireachta"

msgid ""
"Controls ``#: filename:line`` comment lines in language files. If the option "
"is:"
msgstr ""
"Rialuithe ``#: ainm comhad:line`` línte tráchta i gcomhaid teanga. Más é an "
"rogha:"

msgid ""
"``full`` (the default if not given): the lines include both file name and "
"line number."
msgstr ""
"``iomlána`` (an réamhshocrú mura dtugtar): tá ainm comhaid agus uimhir líne "
"san áireamh sna línte."

msgid "``file``: the line number is omitted."
msgstr "``comhad ``: fágtar an uimhir líne."

msgid "``never``: the lines are suppressed (same as :option:`--no-location`)."
msgstr ""
"``riamh ``: cuirtear na línte faoi chois (mar an gcéanna le: rogha: `--no-"
"location`)."

msgid "Requires ``gettext`` 0.19 or newer."
msgstr "Éilíonn ``gettext`` 0.19 nó níos nuaí."

msgid "Removes obsolete message strings from the ``.po`` files."
msgstr ""
"Baineann teaghráin teachtaireachta atá as feidhm as na comhaid ``.po``."

msgid ""
"Prevents deleting the temporary ``.pot`` files generated before creating the "
"``.po`` file. This is useful for debugging errors which may prevent the "
"final language files from being created."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar na comhaid shealadacha ``.pot`` a ghintear a scriosadh "
"sula gcruthaítear an comhad ``.po``. Tá sé seo úsáideach le haghaidh "
"earráidí dífhabhtaithe a d'fhéadfadh cosc a chur ar na comhaid teanga "
"deiridh a chruthú."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`customizing-makemessages` for instructions on how to customize the "
"keywords that :djadmin:`makemessages` passes to ``xgettext``."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: `customizing-makemessages` le haghaidh treoracha maidir le conas "
"na heochairfhocail a shaincheapadh: djadmin: `makemessages` chuig "
"``xgettext``."

msgid "``makemigrations``"
msgstr "``déanaimirceach``"

msgid ""
"Creates new migrations based on the changes detected to your models. "
"Migrations, their relationship with apps and more are covered in depth "
"in :doc:`the migrations documentation</topics/migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn imirce nua bunaithe ar na hathruithe a bhraitear ar do mhúnlaí. "
"Tá imirce, a gcaidreamh le feidhmchláir agus go leor eile clúdaithe go "
"domhain in:doc: `an doicimé@@</topics/migrations> adú imirceacha'."

msgid ""
"Providing one or more app names as arguments will limit the migrations "
"created to the app(s) specified and any dependencies needed (the table at "
"the other end of a ``ForeignKey``, for example)."
msgstr ""
"Ag soláthar ainm aipeanna amháin nó níos mó mar argóintí, cuirfear teorainn "
"leis na himirce a cruthaíodh chuig an aip (í) a shonraítear agus aon "
"spleáchais atá ag teastáil (an tábla ag an gceann eile de `ForeignKey`, mar "
"shampla)."

msgid ""
"To add migrations to an app that doesn't have a ``migrations`` directory, "
"run ``makemigrations`` with the app's ``app_label``."
msgstr ""
"Chun imirce a chur le aip nach bhfuil eolaire ``migrations` aige, reáchtáil "
"``makemigrations`` le `app_label`` an aip."

msgid ""
"Suppresses all user prompts. If a suppressed prompt cannot be resolved "
"automatically, the command will exit with error code 3."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar gach leideanna úsáideora. Mura féidir pras faoi chois a "
"réiteach go huathoibríoch, imeoidh an t-ordú le cód earráide 3."

msgid ""
"Outputs an empty migration for the specified apps, for manual editing. This "
"is for advanced users and should not be used unless you are familiar with "
"the migration format, migration operations, and the dependencies between "
"your migrations."
msgstr ""
"Aisíonn imirce folamh do na feidhmchláir sonraithe, le haghaidh "
"eagarthóireachta láimhe. Tá sé seo le haghaidh ardúsáideoirí agus níor "
"cheart é a úsáid mura bhfuil tú eolach ar an bhformáid imirce, ar "
"oibríochtaí imirce, agus na spleáchais idir d'imirce."

msgid ""
"Shows what migrations would be made without actually writing any migrations "
"files to disk. Using this option along with ``--verbosity 3`` will also show "
"the complete migrations files that would be written."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé cad iad na himirce a dhéanfaí gan aon chomhaid imirce a "
"scríobh chuig diosca. Ag baint úsáide as an rogha seo in éineacht le ``--"
"verbosity 3`` taispeánfar na comhaid imirce iomlána a scríobhadh freisin."

msgid "Enables fixing of migration conflicts."
msgstr "Cumasaíonn sé coinbhleachtaí imirce a shocrú"

msgid ""
"Allows naming the generated migration(s) instead of using a generated name. "
"The name must be a valid Python :ref:`identifier <python:identifiers>`."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé an imirce ginte a ainmniú in ionad ainm ginte a úsáid. "
"<python:identifiers>Caithfidh an t-ainm a bheith ina Python bailí:ref: "
"`aitheantóir `."

msgid "Generate migration files without Django version and timestamp header."
msgstr "Ginigh comhaid imirce gan leagan Django agus ceannteideal stampa ama."

msgid ""
"Makes ``makemigrations`` exit with a non-zero status when model changes "
"without migrations are detected. Implies ``--dry-run``."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé imeacht `makemigrations` le stádas neamh-nialasach nuair a "
"bhraitear athruithe samhail gan imirce. Tugann le tuiscint ```--dry-run ``."

msgid ""
"Diverts log output and input prompts to ``stderr``, writing only paths of "
"generated migration files to ``stdout``."
msgstr ""
"Atreoraíonn sé aschur log agus leideanna ionchuir chuig ``stderr``, agus ní "
"scríobhann ach cosáin de chomhaid imirce ginte chuig ``stdout``."

msgid ""
"Merges model changes into the latest migration and optimize the resulting "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"Comhcheanglaíonn sé athruithe samhail san imirce is déanaí agus na "
"hoibríochtaí atá mar thoradh air a"

msgid ""
"The updated migration will have a generated name. In order to preserve the "
"previous name, set it using ``--name``."
msgstr ""
"Beidh ainm ginte ag an imirce nuashonraithe. D'fhonn an t-ainm roimhe seo a "
"chaomhnú, socraigh é ag baint úsáide as ``--ainm ``."

msgid "``migrate``"
msgstr "```imirce``"

msgid ""
"Synchronizes the database state with the current set of models and "
"migrations. Migrations, their relationship with apps and more are covered in "
"depth in :doc:`the migrations documentation</topics/migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé an staid bunachar sonraí a shioncronú leis an tacar reatha "
"samhlacha agus imirce. Tá imirce, a gcaidreamh le feidhmchláir agus go leor "
"eile clúdaithe go domhain in:doc: `an doicimé@@</topics/migrations> adú "
"imirceacha'."

msgid ""
"The behavior of this command changes depending on the arguments provided:"
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn iompar an ordaithe seo ag brath ar na hargóintí a chuirtear ar "
"fáil:"

msgid "No arguments: All apps have all of their migrations run."
msgstr "Gan aon argóintí: Tá a n-imirce go léir á reáchtáil ag gach aip."

msgid ""
"``<app_label>``: The specified app has its migrations run, up to the most "
"recent migration. This may involve running other apps' migrations too, due "
"to dependencies."
msgstr ""
"<app_label>```: Tá a imirce ag an aip sonraithe a reáchtáil, suas go dtí an "
"imirce is déanaí. D'fhéadfadh imirce aipeanna eile a reáchtáil i gceist leis "
"seo freisin, mar gheall ar spleáchas."

msgid ""
"``<app_label> <migrationname>``: Brings the database schema to a state where "
"the named migration is applied, but no later migrations in the same app are "
"applied. This may involve unapplying migrations if you have previously "
"migrated past the named migration. You can use a prefix of the migration "
"name, e.g. ``0001``, as long as it's unique for the given app name. Use the "
"name ``zero`` to migrate all the way back i.e. to revert all applied "
"migrations for an app."
msgstr ""
"<app_label><migrationname>```: Tugann sé scéim an bhunachar sonraí go stát "
"ina gcuirtear an imirce ainmnithe i bhfeidhm, ach ní chuirtear imirce níos "
"déanaí san aip céanna i bhfeidhm. D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh imirce gan cur i "
"bhfeidhm i gceist leis seo má rinne tú imirce thar an imirce ainmnithe Is "
"féidir leat réimír den ainm imirce a úsáid, m.sh. `0001``, fad is atá sé "
"uathúil d'ainm an aip ar leith. Úsáid an t-ainm ``nialó` chun imirce ar fad "
"ar ais ie chun gach imirce a chur ar ais d'aip."

msgid ""
"When unapplying migrations, all dependent migrations will also be unapplied, "
"regardless of ``<app_label>``. You can use ``--plan`` to check which "
"migrations will be unapplied."
msgstr ""
"<app_label>Nuair a dhéantar imirce a chur i bhfeidhm, ní chuirfear gach "
"imirce spleách i bhfeidhm freisin, beag beann ar ```. Is féidir leat ``--"
"plan ``a úsáid chun a sheiceáil cé na himirce nach gcuirfear i bhfeidhm."

msgid "Specifies the database to migrate. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí le himirce. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Marks the migrations up to the target one (following the rules above) as "
"applied, but without actually running the SQL to change your database schema."
msgstr ""
"Marcann na himirce suas go dtí an sprioccheann (ag leanúint na rialacha "
"thuas) mar a chuirtear i bhfeidhm, ach gan an SQL a reáchtáil i ndáiríre "
"chun do scéim bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"This is intended for advanced users to manipulate the current migration "
"state directly if they're manually applying changes; be warned that using "
"``--fake`` runs the risk of putting the migration state table into a state "
"where manual recovery will be needed to make migrations run correctly."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo beartaithe d'ardúsáideoirí an stát imirce reatha a ionramháil go "
"díreach má tá athruithe á chur i bhfeidhm de láimh; tabhair rabhadh go "
"mbíonn an baol ag baint úsáide as ``--fake`` tábla an stáit imirce a chur i "
"stát ina mbeidh gá le téarnamh láimhe chun imirce a rith i gceart."

msgid ""
"Allows Django to skip an app's initial migration if all database tables with "
"the names of all models created by "
"all :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.CreateModel` operations in that "
"migration already exist. This option is intended for use when first running "
"migrations against a database that preexisted the use of migrations. This "
"option does not, however, check for matching database schema beyond matching "
"table names and so is only safe to use if you are confident that your "
"existing schema matches what is recorded in your initial migration."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé do Django imirce tosaigh aip a scipeáil má tá gach tábla bunachar "
"sonraí le hainmneacha na samhlacha go léir a chruthaigh uach:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.createModel` oibríochtaí san imirce sin "
"cheana féin. Tá an rogha seo beartaithe le húsáid nuair a bhíonn imirce á "
"reáchtáil ar dtús i gcoinne bunachar sonraí a raibh úsáid imirce ann roimh "
"ré. Ní sheiceálann an rogha seo, áfach, an scéim bunachar sonraí a "
"mheaitseáil níos faide ná ainmneacha táblaí a mheaitseáil agus mar sin níl "
"sé sábháilte le húsáid ach má tá tú muiníneach go bhfuil an scéim atá ann "
"cheana comhoiriúnach leis an"

msgid ""
"Shows the migration operations that will be performed for the given "
"``migrate`` command."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé na hoibríochtaí imirce a dhéanfar don ordú ``imirce`` a "
"thugtar."

msgid ""
"Allows creating tables for apps without migrations. While this isn't "
"recommended, the migrations framework is sometimes too slow on large "
"projects with hundreds of models."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé táblaí a chruthú d'aipeanna gan imirce. Cé nach mholtar é seo, "
"bíonn an creat imirce ró-mhall uaireanta ar thionscadail mhóra le céadta "
"samhail."

msgid ""
"Suppresses all user prompts. An example prompt is asking about removing "
"stale content types."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar gach leideanna úsáideora. Is sampla pras is ea fiafraí "
"faoi chineálacha ábhair seasta a bhaint."

msgid ""
"Makes ``migrate`` exit with a non-zero status when unapplied migrations are "
"detected."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé imeacht ``imirce`` le stádas neamh-nialasach nuair a bhraitear "
"imirce neamhfheidhmeacha."

msgid ""
"Deletes nonexistent migrations from the ``django_migrations`` table. This is "
"useful when migration files replaced by a squashed migration have been "
"removed. See :ref:`migration-squashing` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé imirce nach bhfuil ann ón tábla ``django_migrations``. Tá sé "
"seo úsáideach nuair a baineadh comhaid imirce ina ionad imirce scáilte. "
"Féach:ref: `migration-squashing` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``optimizemigration``"
msgstr "``Eimirce barrfheabhsaithe``"

msgid ""
"Optimizes the operations for the named migration and overrides the existing "
"file. If the migration contains functions that must be manually copied, the "
"command creates a new migration file suffixed with ``_optimized`` that is "
"meant to replace the named migration."
msgstr ""
"Uasmhéadaíonn sé na hoibríochtaí don imirce ainmnithe agus sáraíonn sé an "
"comhad atá ann cheana. Má tá feidhmeanna san imirce nach mór a chóipeáil de "
"láimh, cruthaíonn an t-ordú comhad imirce nua ar iarmhairc le ``_optimed`` "
"atá i gceist chun an imirce ainmnithe a athsholáthar."

msgid ""
"Makes ``optimizemigration`` exit with a non-zero status when a migration can "
"be optimized."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé “barrfheabhsú inimirce” imeacht le stádas neamh-nialasach nuair "
"is féidir imirce a bharrfheabhsú."

msgid ""
"Starts a lightweight development web server on the local machine. By "
"default, the server runs on port 8000 on the IP address ``127.0.0.1``. You "
"can pass in an IP address and port number explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn freastalaí gréasáin forbartha éadrom ar an meaisín áitiúil. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, ritheann an freastalaí ar chalafort 8000 ar an seoladh IP "
"``127.0.0.1 ``. Is féidir leat seoladh IP agus uimhir chalafoirt a chur "
"isteach go sainráite."

msgid ""
"If you run this script as a user with normal privileges (recommended), you "
"might not have access to start a port on a low port number. Low port numbers "
"are reserved for the superuser (root)."
msgstr ""
"Má ritheann tú an script seo mar úsáideoir le gnáthphribhléidí (moltar), "
"b'fhéidir nach mbeidh rochtain agat calafort a thosú ar uimhir íseal "
"calafort. Tá uimhreacha calafoirt íseal in áirithe don superuser (fréamh)."

msgid ""
"This server uses the WSGI application object specified by "
"the :setting:`WSGI_APPLICATION` setting."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an freastalaí seo réad feidhmchláir WSGI a shonraítear leis an "
"socrú: setting: `WSGI_APPLICATION`."

msgid "DO NOT USE THIS SERVER IN A PRODUCTION SETTING."
msgstr "NÁ HÚSÁID AN FREASTALAÍ SEO I SUÍOMH TÁIRGEACHTA."

msgid ""
"This lightweight development server has not gone through security audits or "
"performance tests, hence is unsuitable for production. Making this server "
"able to handle a production environment is outside the scope of Django."
msgstr ""
"Níor chuaigh an freastalaí forbartha éadrom seo trí iniúchtaí slándála nó "
"tástálacha feidhmíochta, mar sin tá sé míoiriúnach Tá an freastalaí seo in "
"ann timpeallacht táirgeachta a láimhseáil lasmuigh de raon feidhme Django."

msgid ""
"The development server automatically reloads Python code for each request, "
"as needed. You don't need to restart the server for code changes to take "
"effect. However, some actions like adding files don't trigger a restart, so "
"you'll have to restart the server in these cases."
msgstr ""
"Athluchtaíonn an freastalaí forbartha cód Python go huathoibríoch do gach "
"iarratas, de réir mar is Ní gá duit an freastalaí a atosú chun athruithe cód "
"a bheith i bhfeidhm. Mar sin féin, ní spreagann roinnt gníomhartha cosúil le "
"comhaid a chur leis atosú, mar sin beidh ort an freastalaí a atosú sna "
"cásanna seo."

msgid ""
"If you're using Linux or MacOS and install both :pypi:`pywatchman` and the "
"`Watchman`_ service, kernel signals will be used to autoreload the server "
"(rather than polling file modification timestamps each second). This offers "
"better performance on large projects, reduced response time after code "
"changes, more robust change detection, and a reduction in power usage. "
"Django supports ``pywatchman`` 1.2.0 and higher."
msgstr ""
"Má tá Linux nó macOS á úsáid agat agus má shuiteálann tú araon: pypi: "
"`pywatchman` agus an tseirbhís `Watchman`_, úsáidfear comharthaí eithne chun "
"an freastalaí a athluchtú uathoibríoch (seachas stampaí ama modhnú comhad a "
"vótáil gach soicind). Tugann sé seo feidhmíocht níos fearr ar thionscadail "
"mhóra, am freagartha laghdaithe tar éis athruithe cód, braite athruithe níos "
"láidre, agus laghdú ar úsáid cumhachta. Tacaíonn Django le ``pywatchman`` "
"1.2.0 agus níos airde."

msgid "Large directories with many files may cause performance issues"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh fadhbanna feidhmíochta a bheith mar thoradh ar eolairí"

msgid ""
"When using Watchman with a project that includes large non-Python "
"directories like ``node_modules``, it's advisable to ignore this directory "
"for optimal performance. See the `watchman documentation`_ for information "
"on how to do this."
msgstr ""
"Agus Watchman á úsáid agat le tionscadal a chuimsíonn eolairí móra neamh-"
"Python mar `node_modules``, moltar neamhaird a dhéanamh ar an eolaire seo "
"chun feidhmíocht is fearr a fháil. Féach an “doiciméadú faire” _ le haghaidh "
"faisnéise maidir le conas é seo a dhéanamh."

msgid "Watchman timeout"
msgstr "Amach Watchman"

msgid ""
"The default timeout of ``Watchman`` client is 5 seconds. You can change it "
"by setting the :envvar:`DJANGO_WATCHMAN_TIMEOUT` environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Is é 5 soicind an t-am réamhshocraithe de chliant `Watchman`. Is féidir leat "
"é a athrú tríd an athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_WATCHMAN_TIMEOUT` a "
"shocrú."

msgid ""
"When you start the server, and each time you change Python code while the "
"server is running, the system check framework will check your entire Django "
"project for some common errors (see the :djadmin:`check` command). If any "
"errors are found, they will be printed to standard output. You can use the "
"``--skip-checks`` option to skip running system checks."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thosaíonn tú an freastalaí, agus gach uair a athraíonn tú cód Python "
"agus an freastalaí ag rith, seiceálfaidh creat seiceála an chórais do "
"thionscadal iomlán Django le haghaidh roinnt earráidí coitianta (féach an t-"
"ordú:djadmin: `check`). Má aimsítear aon earráidí, clófar iad chuig aschur "
"caighdeánach. Is féidir leat an rogha ``--skip-checks`` a úsáid chun "
"seiceálacha córais reatha a scipeáil."

msgid ""
"You can run as many concurrent servers as you want, as long as they're on "
"separate ports by executing ``django-admin runserver`` more than once."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an oiread freastalaithe comhthráthacha a reáchtáil agus is "
"mian leat, chomh fada agus a bhíonn siad ar chalafoirt ar leithligh trí "
"“django-admin runserver” a fhorghníomhú níos mó ná uair amháin."

msgid ""
"Note that the default IP address, ``127.0.0.1``, is not accessible from "
"other machines on your network. To make your development server viewable to "
"other machines on the network, use its own IP address (e.g. "
"``192.168.2.1``), ``0`` (shortcut for ``0.0.0.0``), ``0.0.0.0``, or ``::`` "
"(with IPv6 enabled)."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil an seoladh IP réamhshocraithe, ``127.0.0.1 "
"``, inrochtana ó mheaisíní eile ar do líonra. Chun do fhreastalaí forbartha "
"a dhéanamh infheicthe do mheaisíní eile ar an líonra, bain úsáid as a "
"sheoladh IP féin (m.sh. `192.168.2.1 ``), `0`` (aicearra le haghaidh "
"``0.0.0.0``), ``0.0.0.0``, nó``: ``(le IPv6 cumasaithe)."

msgid ""
"You can provide an IPv6 address surrounded by brackets (e.g. "
"``[200a::1]:8000``). This will automatically enable IPv6 support."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat seoladh IPv6 a sholáthar timpeallaithe ag lúibíní (m.sh. "
"``[200a: :1]: 8000``). Cumasóidh sé seo tacaíocht IPv6 go huathoibríoch."

msgid "A hostname containing ASCII-only characters can also be used."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ainm óstach ina bhfuil carachtair ASCII amháin a úsáid freisin."

msgid ""
"If the :doc:`staticfiles</ref/contrib/staticfiles>` contrib app is enabled "
"(default in new projects) the :djadmin:`runserver` command will be "
"overridden with its own :ref:`runserver<staticfiles-runserver>` command."
msgstr ""
"</ref/contrib/staticfiles> <staticfiles-runserver>Má tá an aip contrib: doc: "
"`staticfiles` cumasaithe (réamhshocraithe i dtionscadail nua) cuirfear an t-"
"ordú:djadmin: `runserver` ar a ordú féin: ref: `runserver`."

msgid ""
"Logging of each request and response of the server is sent to "
"the :ref:`django-server-logger` logger."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar logáil ar gach iarratas agus freagra an fhreastalaí chuig an "
"logger:ref: `django-server-logger`."

msgid ""
"Disables the auto-reloader. This means any Python code changes you make "
"while the server is running will *not* take effect if the particular Python "
"modules have already been loaded into memory."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasann sé an t-athluchtaitheoir uathoibr Ciallaíonn sé seo go mbeidh "
"aon athruithe cód Python a dhéanann tú agus an freastalaí ag rith * ní "
"thiocfaidh éifeacht má tá na modúil Python áirithe luchtaithe i gcuimhne "
"cheana féin."

msgid ""
"Disables use of threading in the development server. The server is "
"multithreaded by default."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasaíonn sé úsáid snáithe sa fhreastalaí forbartha. Tá an freastalaí "
"ilshreathaithe de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Uses IPv6 for the development server. This changes the default IP address "
"from ``127.0.0.1`` to ``::1``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann IPv6 don fhreastalaí forbartha. Athraíonn sé seo an seoladh IP "
"réamhshocraithe ó ``127.0.0.1`` go ``: :1``."

msgid ""
"By default, a warning is printed to the console that ``runserver`` is not "
"suitable for production:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set this environment variable to ``\"true\"`` to hide this warning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Examples of using different ports and addresses"
msgstr "Samplaí de úsáid calafoirt agus seoltaí éagsúla"

msgid "Port 8000 on IP address ``127.0.0.1``:"
msgstr "Port 8000 ar sheoladh IP ``127.0.0.1 ``:"

msgid "Port 8000 on IP address ``1.2.3.4``:"
msgstr "Port 8000 ar sheoladh IP ``1.2.3.4`:"

msgid "Port 7000 on IP address ``127.0.0.1``:"
msgstr "Port 7000 ar sheoladh IP ``127.0.0.1 ``:"

msgid "Port 7000 on IP address ``1.2.3.4``:"
msgstr "Port 7000 ar sheoladh IP ``1.2.3.4``:"

msgid "Port 8000 on IPv6 address ``::1``:"
msgstr "Port 8000 ar sheoladh IPv6 ``:: 1``:"

msgid "Port 7000 on IPv6 address ``::1``:"
msgstr "Port 7000 ar sheoladh IPv6 ``: :1``:"

msgid "Port 7000 on IPv6 address ``2001:0db8:1234:5678::9``:"
msgstr "Port 7000 ar sheoladh IPv6 ``2001:0 db 8:1234:5678: :9``:"

msgid "Port 8000 on IPv4 address of host ``localhost``:"
msgstr "Port 8000 ar sheoladh IPv4 an óstach ``localhost``:"

msgid "Port 8000 on IPv6 address of host ``localhost``:"
msgstr "Port 8000 ar sheoladh IPv6 an óstach ``localhost``:"

msgid "Serving static files with the development server"
msgstr "Comhaid statacha a sheirbheáil leis an bhfreastalaí"

msgid ""
"By default, the development server doesn't serve any static files for your "
"site (such as CSS files, images, things under :setting:`MEDIA_URL` and so "
"forth). If you want to configure Django to serve static media, read :doc:`/"
"howto/static-files/index`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní fhreastalaíonn an freastalaí forbartha aon "
"chomhaid statacha do do shuíomh (mar shampla comhaid CSS, íomhánna, rudaí "
"faoi: socrú: `MEDIA_URL` agus mar sin de). Más mian leat Django a chumrú "
"chun freastal ar na meáin statacha, léigh: doc: `/howto/static-files/index `."

msgid "Serving with ASGI in development"
msgstr "Ag freastal le ASGI i bhforbairt"

msgid ""
"Django's ``runserver`` command provides a WSGI server. In order to run under "
"ASGI you will need to use an :doc:`ASGI server </howto/deployment/asgi/"
"index>`. The Django Daphne project provides :ref:`daphne-runserver` that you "
"can use."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn ordú ``runserver`` Django freastalaí WSGI. D'fhonn rith faoi "
"ASGI beidh ort an:doc: `ASGI freastala` a </howto/deployment/asgi/index> "
"úsáid. Soláthraíonn tionscadal Django Daphne:ref: `daphne-runserver` is "
"féidir leat a úsáid."

msgid "``sendtestemail``"
msgstr "``sendtestemail``"

msgid ""
"Sends a test email (to confirm email sending through Django is working) to "
"the recipient(s) specified. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Seolann sé ríomhphost tástála (chun a dhearbhú go bhfuil ríomhphost a "
"sheoladh trí Django ag obair) chuig an bhfaighteoir (í) a sh Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"There are a couple of options, and you may use any combination of them "
"together:"
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla rogha ann, agus féadfaidh tú aon teaglaim díobh a úsáid le chéile:"

msgid ""
"Mails the email addresses specified in :setting:`MANAGERS` "
"using :func:`~django.core.mail.mail_managers`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mails the email addresses specified in :setting:`ADMINS` "
"using :func:`~django.core.mail.mail_admins`."
msgstr ""

msgid "``shell``"
msgstr "``sliog``"

msgid "Starts the Python interactive interpreter."
msgstr "Tosaíonn an ateangaire idirghníomhach Python."

msgid ""
"All models from installed apps are automatically imported into the shell "
"environment. Models from apps listed earlier in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"take precedence. For a ``--verbosity`` of 2 or higher, the automatically "
"imported objects will be listed. To disable automatic importing entirely, "
"use the ``--no-imports`` flag."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See the guide on :ref:`customizing this behaviour <customizing-shell-auto-"
"imports>` to add or remove automatic imports."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic models import was added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specifies the shell to use. By default, Django will use IPython_ or bpython_ "
"if either is installed. If both are installed, specify which one you want "
"like so:"
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bhlaosc atá le húsáid. De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáidfidh "
"Django iPython_ nó bpython_ má tá ceachtar acu suiteáilte. Má tá an dá "
"cheann suiteáilte, sonraigh cén ceann is mian leat mar sin:"

msgid "IPython:"
msgstr "IPython:"

msgid "bpython:"
msgstr "bpython:"

msgid ""
"If you have a \"rich\" shell installed but want to force use of the "
"\"plain\" Python interpreter, use ``python`` as the interface name, like so:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá blaosc “saibhir” suiteáilte agat ach má theastaíonn uait an ateangaire "
"Python “simplí” a úsáid, bain úsáid as `python`` mar ainm an chomhéadain, "
"mar sin:"

msgid ""
"Disables reading the startup script for the \"plain\" Python interpreter. By "
"default, the script pointed to by the :envvar:`PYTHONSTARTUP` environment "
"variable or the ``~/.pythonrc.py`` script is read."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasaíonn sé an script tosaithe a léamh don ateangairí Python “simplí”. "
"De réir réamhshocraithe, léitear an script chuig an athróg comhshaoil: "
"envvar: `PYTHONSTARTUP` nó an script ``~/.pythonrc.py``."

msgid "Disables the automatic import of models from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lets you pass a command as a string to execute it as Django, like so:"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann duit ordú a rith mar shreang chun é a fhorghníomhú mar Django, mar "
"sin:"

msgid "You can also pass code in on standard input to execute it. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cód a chur isteach ar ionchur caighdeánach chun é a "
"fhorghníomhú. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"On Windows, the REPL is output due to implementation limits "
"of :func:`select.select` on that platform."
msgstr ""
"Ar Windows, tá an REPL aschur mar gheall ar theorainneacha cur chun feidhme "
"de:func: `select.select` ar an ardán sin."

msgid "``showmigrations``"
msgstr "``imirce taispeánaithe``"

msgid ""
"Shows all migrations in a project. You can choose from one of two formats:"
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an imirce go léir i dtionscadal. Is féidir leat a roghnú ó "
"cheann de dhá fhormáid:"

msgid ""
"Lists all of the apps Django knows about, the migrations available for each "
"app, and whether or not each migration is applied (marked by an ``[X]`` next "
"to the migration name). For a ``--verbosity`` of 2 and above, the applied "
"datetimes are also shown."
msgstr ""
"Liostaíonn gach ceann de na feidhmchláir atá ar eolas ag Django fúthu, na "
"himirce atá ar fáil do gach aip, agus cibé an gcuirtear gach imirce i "
"bhfeidhm nó nach bhfuil (marcáilte le ``[X]`` in aice leis an ainm imirce). "
"Maidir le ``- verbosity`` de 2 agus os a chionn, taispeántar na dáta a "
"chuirtear i bhfeidhm freisin."

msgid ""
"Apps without migrations are also listed, but have ``(no migrations)`` "
"printed under them."
msgstr ""
"Liostaítear aipeanna gan imirce freisin, ach tá ``(gan imirce)`` clóite "
"fúthu."

msgid "This is the default output format."
msgstr "Is é seo an formáid aschuir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Shows the migration plan Django will follow to apply migrations. Like ``--"
"list``, applied migrations are marked by an ``[X]``. For a ``--verbosity`` "
"of 2 and above, all dependencies of a migration will also be shown."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an plean imirce a leanfaidh Django chun imirce a chur i "
"bhfeidhm. Cosúil le ``--liosta`, tá imirce feidhmithe marcáilte le ``[X]``. "
"Maidir le ``--fhógraíocht ``de 2 agus os a chionn, taispeánfar gach "
"spleáchas imirce freisin."

msgid ""
"``app_label``\\s arguments limit the output, however, dependencies of "
"provided apps may also be included."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann argóintí `app_label`` teorainn leis an aschur, áfach, féadfar "
"spleáchais na n-aipeanna curtha ar fáil a áireamh freisin."

msgid "Specifies the database to examine. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí le scrúdú. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "``sqlflush``"
msgstr "``sqlflush ``"

msgid ""
"Prints the SQL statements that would be executed for the :djadmin:`flush` "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Priontáil na ráitis SQL a chuirfeadh i bhfeidhm don ordú:djadmin: `flush`."

msgid ""
"Specifies the database for which to print the SQL. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí chun an SQL a phriontáil. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "``sqlmigrate``"
msgstr "``sqlmigrate``"

msgid ""
"Prints the SQL for the named migration. This requires an active database "
"connection, which it will use to resolve constraint names; this means you "
"must generate the SQL against a copy of the database you wish to later apply "
"it on."
msgstr ""
"Priontáil an SQL don imirce ainmnithe. Éilíonn sé seo nasc gníomhach "
"bunachar sonraí, a úsáidfidh sé chun ainmneacha srianta a réiteach; "
"ciallaíonn sé seo go gcaithfidh tú an SQL a ghiniúint i gcoinne cóip den "
"bhunachar sonraí is mian leat é a chur i bhfeidhm níos déanaí."

msgid "Note that ``sqlmigrate`` doesn't colorize its output."
msgstr "Tabhair faoi deara nach ndéanann `sqlmigrate`` dathú a aschur."

msgid ""
"Generates the SQL for unapplying the migration. By default, the SQL created "
"is for running the migration in the forwards direction."
msgstr ""
"Gineann sé an SQL chun an imirce a dhíchur i bhfeidhm. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, is é an SQL a cruthaíodh chun an imirce a reáchtáil sa treo "
"ar aghaidh."

msgid ""
"Specifies the database for which to generate the SQL. Defaults to "
"``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí chun an SQL a ghiniúint. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "``sqlsequencereset``"
msgstr "``sqlsequencereset ``"

msgid ""
"Prints the SQL statements for resetting sequences for the given app name(s)."
msgstr ""
"Priontáil na ráitis SQL chun seicheamh a athshocrú d'ainmne/ainmneacha an "
"aip ar leith."

msgid ""
"Sequences are indexes used by some database engines to track the next "
"available number for automatically incremented fields."
msgstr ""
"Is innéacsanna iad seicheamh a úsáideann roinnt innill bunachar sonraí chun "
"an chéad uimhir eile atá ar fáil a rianú do réimsí a fhásann"

msgid ""
"Use this command to generate SQL which will fix cases where a sequence is "
"out of sync with its automatically incremented field data."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an t-ordú seo chun SQL a ghiniúint a shocróidh cásanna ina bhfuil "
"seicheamh as sioncronú lena sonraí réimse atá ag méadú go huathoibríoch."

msgid "``squashmigrations``"
msgstr "```Scuashimirce``"

msgid ""
"Squashes the migrations for ``app_label`` up to and including "
"``migration_name`` down into fewer migrations, if possible. The resulting "
"squashed migrations can live alongside the unsquashed ones safely. For more "
"information, please read :ref:`migration-squashing`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an imirce le haghaidh `app_label`` suas go dtí ``migration_name`` "
"san áireamh síos ina níos lú imirce, más féidir. Is féidir leis na himirce "
"scáilte a eascraíonn as maireachtáil in éineacht leis na cinn neamh-scáilte "
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, léigh: ref: `migration-squashing`."

msgid ""
"When ``start_migration_name`` is given, Django will only include migrations "
"starting from and including this migration. This helps to mitigate the "
"squashing limitation of :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunPython` "
"and :class:`django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` migration operations."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thugtar ``start_migration_name``, ní chuimseoidh Django ach imirce "
"ag tosú ón imirce seo agus lena n-áirítear. Cuidíonn sé seo leis an teorannú "
"squasing de:class: `~django.db.migrations.operations.runpython` agus:class: "
"`django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` oibríochtaí imirce a mhaolú."

msgid ""
"Disables the optimizer when generating a squashed migration. By default, "
"Django will try to optimize the operations in your migrations to reduce the "
"size of the resulting file. Use this option if this process is failing or "
"creating incorrect migrations, though please also file a Django bug report "
"about the behavior, as optimization is meant to be safe."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasann sé an barrfheabhsaitheoir agus imirce scáite á ghiniúint. De "
"réir réamhshocraithe, déanfaidh Django iarracht na hoibríochtaí i d'imirce a "
"bharrfheabhsú chun méid an chomhaid mar thoradh air a laghdú. Úsáid an rogha "
"seo má tá an próiseas seo ag teip nó ag cruthú imirce mícheart, cé go "
"gcomhdaigh tuarascáil fabht Django faoin iompar le do thoil, mar tá sé i "
"gceist go mbeadh optamú sábháilte."

msgid ""
"Sets the name of the squashed migration. When omitted, the name is based on "
"the first and last migration, with ``_squashed_`` in between."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé ainm na himirce squashed. Nuair a fhágtar amach, tá an t-ainm "
"bunaithe ar an gcéad imirce agus an imirce deireanach, agus ``_squashed_`` "
"eatarthu."

msgid ""
"Generate squashed migration file without Django version and timestamp header."
msgstr ""
"Ginigh comhad imirce squashed gan leagan Django agus ceannteideal stampa ama."

msgid "``startapp``"
msgstr "``Startapp``"

msgid ""
"Creates a Django app directory structure for the given app name in the "
"current directory or the given destination."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn struchtúr eolaire aip Django don ainm aip ar leith san eolaire "
"reatha nó sa cheann scríbe ar leith."

msgid ""
"By default, :source:`the new directory <django/conf/app_template>` contains "
"a ``models.py`` file and other app template files. If only the app name is "
"given, the app directory will be created in the current working directory."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, :source: tá comhad `<django/conf/app_template> "
"`models.py` agus comhaid teimpléad aip eile sa stiúrthóir nua'. Mura dtugtar "
"ach ainm an aip, cruthófar eolaire an aip san eolaire oibre reatha."

msgid ""
"If the optional destination is provided, Django will use that existing "
"directory rather than creating a new one. You can use '.' to denote the "
"current working directory."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear an ceann scríbe roghnach ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django an eolaire "
"atá ann cheana sin seachas ceann nua a chruthú. Is féidir leat '.' a úsáid "
"chun an eolaire oibre reatha a léiriú."

msgid ""
"Provides the path to a directory with a custom app template file, or a path "
"to an uncompressed archive (``.tar``) or a compressed archive (``.tar.gz``, "
"``.tar.bz2``, ``.tar.xz``, ``.tar.lzma``, ``.tgz``, ``.tbz2``, ``.txz``, "
"``.tlz``, ``.zip``) containing the app template files."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn sé an cosán chuig eolaire le comhad teimpléad aip saincheaptha, "
"nó cosán chuig cartlann neamhbhrúite (`.tar``) nó cartlann comhbhrúite "
"(`.tar.gz``, `.tar.bz2``, `.tar.xz``, `.tar.lzma`, `.tgz``, `.tbz`tx`, "
"`.tbz`` z``, `.tlz``, `.zip``) ina bhfuil na comhaid teimpléad aip."

msgid ""
"For example, this would look for an app template in the given directory when "
"creating the ``myapp`` app:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cuardódh sé seo teimpléad aip san eolaire tugtha agus an aip "
"`myapp`` á chruthú:"

msgid ""
"Django will also accept URLs (``http``, ``https``, ``ftp``) to compressed "
"archives with the app template files, downloading and extracting them on the "
"fly."
msgstr ""
"Glacfaidh Django le URLanna freisin (``http``, `https``, `ftp``) chuig "
"cartlanna comhbhrúite leis na comhaid teimpléad aip, agus iad a íoslódáil "
"agus a bhaint ar an eitilt."

msgid ""
"For example, taking advantage of GitHub's feature to expose repositories as "
"zip files, you can use a URL like:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ag baint leasa as ghné GitHub chun stórais a nochtadh mar "
"chomhaid zip, is féidir leat URL a úsáid mar:"

msgid ""
"Templates provided via ``--template`` are used as is. Malicious or poorly "
"constructed templates may introduce security weaknesses or unintended "
"behavior. Compressed archives may also consume excessive resources during "
"extraction, potentially causing crashes or hangs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contents of templates should be carefully inspected before use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specifies which file extensions in the app template should be rendered with "
"the template engine. Defaults to ``py``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na síntí comhaid sa teimpléad aip ba chóir a léiriú leis an "
"inneall teimpléid. Réamhshocraithe go ``py``."

msgid ""
"Specifies which files in the app template (in addition to those matching ``--"
"extension``) should be rendered with the template engine. Defaults to an "
"empty list."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé cé na comhaid i dteimpléad an aip (i dteannta na comhaid sin a "
"mheaitseálann “- síneadh”) ba chóir a léiriú leis an inneall teimpléid. "
"Réamhshocraithe ar liosta folamh."

msgid ""
"Specifies which directories in the app template should be excluded, in "
"addition to ``.git`` and ``__pycache__``. If this option is not provided, "
"directories named ``__pycache__`` or starting with ``.`` will be excluded."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé cé na heolairí sa teimpléad aip ba chóir a eisiamh, i dteannta "
"le ``.git`` agus ``__pycache__``. Mura gcuirtear an rogha seo ar fáil, "
"cuirfear eolairí darb ainm ``__pycache__`` nó ag tosú le ``.`` eisiata."

msgid ""
"The :class:`template context <django.template.Context>` used for all "
"matching files is:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an: aicme: `comhthéacs teimpléad <django.template.Context>`a úsáidtear "
"le haghaidh gach comhad meaitseála:"

msgid ""
"Any option passed to the ``startapp`` command (among the command's supported "
"options)"
msgstr ""
"Aon rogha a chuirtear chuig an ordú ``startapp`` (i measc roghanna tacaithe "
"ón ordú)"

msgid "``app_name`` -- the app name as passed to the command"
msgstr "``app_name`` - ainm an aip mar a chuirtear chuig an ordú"

msgid "``app_directory`` -- the full path of the newly created app"
msgstr "``app_directory`` - cosán iomlán an aip nua-chruthaithe"

msgid "``camel_case_app_name`` -- the app name in camel case format"
msgstr "``camel_case_app_name`` - ainm an aip i bhformáid cáis camel"

msgid ""
"``docs_version`` -- the version of the documentation: ``'dev'`` or ``'1.x'``"
msgstr "``docs_version`` - leagan na doiciméadaithe: ``'dev'`` nó ```1.x'``"

msgid "``django_version`` -- the version of Django, e.g. ``'2.0.3'``"
msgstr "``django_version`` - leagan de Django, m.sh. ```'2.0.3'``"

msgid ""
"When the app template files are rendered with the Django template engine (by "
"default all ``*.py`` files), Django will also replace all stray template "
"variables contained. For example, if one of the Python files contains a "
"docstring explaining a particular feature related to template rendering, it "
"might result in an incorrect example."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéantar comhaid teimpléad an aip a léiriú le hinneall teimpléad "
"Django (de réir réamhshocraithe gach comhad ``*.py``), cuirfidh Django in "
"ionad gach athróg teimpléad craiceáilte atá ann freisin. Mar shampla, má tá "
"docstring i gceann de na comhaid Python a mhíníonn gné áirithe a bhaineann "
"le rindreáil teimpléid, d'fhéadfadh sampla mícheart a bheith mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"To work around this problem, you can use the :ttag:`templatetag` template "
"tag to \"escape\" the various parts of the template syntax."
msgstr ""
"Chun oibriú timpeall ar an bhfadhb seo, is féidir leat an chlib "
"teimpléad:ttag: `templatetag` a úsáid chun na codanna éagsúla den chomhréir "
"teimpléid a éalú."

msgid ""
"In addition, to allow Python template files that contain Django template "
"language syntax while also preventing packaging systems from trying to byte-"
"compile invalid ``*.py`` files, template files ending with ``.py-tpl`` will "
"be renamed to ``.py``."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, chun comhaid teimpléad Python ina bhfuil comhréir teanga "
"teanga Django a cheadú agus cosc a chur ar chórais phacáistithe iarracht a "
"dhéanamh comhaid `*.py` neamhbhailí a thiomsú, athainmnítear comhaid "
"teimpléad a chríochnaíonn le `.py` go `.py``."

msgid ""
"The contents of custom app (or project) templates should always be audited "
"before use: Such templates define code that will become part of your "
"project, and this means that such code will be trusted as much as any app "
"you install, or code you write yourself. Further, even rendering the "
"templates is, effectively, executing code that was provided as input to the "
"management command. The Django template language may provide wide access "
"into the system, so make sure any custom template you use is worthy of your "
"trust."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir ábhar teimpléid aip saincheaptha (nó tionscadail) a iniúchadh i "
"gcónaí sula n-úsáidtear iad: Sainmhíníonn teimpléid den sórt sin cód a "
"bheidh mar chuid de do thionscadal, agus ciallaíonn sé seo go mbeidh muinín "
"ag cód den sórt sin an oiread agus aon aip a shuiteálann tú, nó cód a "
"scríobhann tú féin Ina theannta sin, is é fiú na teimpléid a rindreáil, go "
"héifeachtach, cód a cuireadh ar fáil mar ionchur don ordú bainistíochta a "
"fhor Féadfaidh teanga teanga teimpléid Django rochtain leathan a sholáthar "
"isteach sa chóras, mar sin déan cinnte go bhfuil aon teimpléad saincheaptha "
"a úsáideann tú fiú do mhuinín"

msgid "``startproject``"
msgstr "``tionscadal tosaithe``"

msgid ""
"Creates a Django project directory structure for the given project name in "
"the current directory or the given destination."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn struchtúr eolaire tionscadail Django don ainm tionscadail ar "
"leith san eolaire reatha nó sa cheann scríbe ar leith."

msgid ""
"By default, :source:`the new directory <django/conf/project_template>` "
"contains ``manage.py`` and a project package (containing a ``settings.py`` "
"and other files)."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, :source: tá `<django/conf/project_template> "
"manage.py`` agus pacáiste tionscadail (ina bhfuil `settings.py`` agus "
"comhaid eile) sa stiúrthóir nua."

msgid ""
"If only the project name is given, both the project directory and project "
"package will be named ``<projectname>`` and the project directory will be "
"created in the current working directory."
msgstr ""
"Mura dtugtar ach ainm an tionscadail, ainmneofar <projectname>```eolaire an "
"tionscadail agus an pacáiste tionscadail araon agus cruthófar eolaire an "
"tionscadail san eolaire oibre reatha."

msgid ""
"If the optional destination is provided, Django will use that existing "
"directory as the project directory, and create ``manage.py`` and the project "
"package within it. Use '.' to denote the current working directory."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear an ceann scríbe roghnach ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django an t-eolaire "
"atá ann cheana sin mar eolaire an tionscadail, agus cruthóidh sé `manage.py` "
"agus an pacáiste tionscadail laistigh de. Úsáid '.' chun an eolaire oibre "
"reatha a léiriú."

msgid ""
"Specifies a directory, file path, or URL of a custom project template. See "
"the :option:`startapp --template` documentation for examples and usage. The "
"same **security considerations** described for ``startapp`` templates apply "
"here: malicious or poorly constructed templates may introduce weaknesses or "
"consume excessive resources, and templates should be carefully inspected "
"before use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specifies which file extensions in the project template should be rendered "
"with the template engine. Defaults to ``py``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na síntí comhaid i dteimpléad an tionscadail ba chóir a léiriú "
"leis an inneall teimplé Réamhshocraithe go ``py``."

msgid ""
"Specifies which files in the project template (in addition to those matching "
"``--extension``) should be rendered with the template engine. Defaults to an "
"empty list."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na comhaid i dteimpléad an tionscadail (i dteannta na comhaid "
"sin a mheaitseálann ``--extension``) ba chóir a léiriú leis an inneall "
"teimpléid. Réamhshocraithe ar liosta folamh."

msgid ""
"Specifies which directories in the project template should be excluded, in "
"addition to ``.git`` and ``__pycache__``. If this option is not provided, "
"directories named ``__pycache__`` or starting with ``.`` will be excluded."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé na heolairí sa teimpléad tionscadail ba chóir a eisiamh, chomh "
"maith le ``.git`` agus ``__pycache__``. Mura gcuirtear an rogha seo ar fáil, "
"cuirfear eolairí darb ainm ``__pycache__`` nó ag tosú le ``.`` eisiata."

msgid "The :class:`template context <django.template.Context>` used is:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an: aicme: `comhthéacs teimpléad <django.template.Context>`a úsáidtear:"

msgid ""
"Any option passed to the ``startproject`` command (among the command's "
"supported options)"
msgstr ""
"Aon rogha a chuirtear chuig an ordú ``startproject`` (i measc roghanna "
"tacaithe ag an ordú)"

msgid "``project_name`` -- the project name as passed to the command"
msgstr "``project_name`` - ainm an tionscadail mar a chuirtear chuig an ordú"

msgid "``project_directory`` -- the full path of the newly created project"
msgstr "``project_directory`` -- cosán iomlán an tionscadail nua-chruthaithe"

msgid "``secret_key`` -- a random key for the :setting:`SECRET_KEY` setting"
msgstr "``secret_key`` - eochair randamach don socrú: setting: `SECRET_KEY`"

msgid ""
"Please also see the :ref:`rendering warning <render_warning>` "
"and :ref:`trusted code warning <trusted_code_warning>` as mentioned "
"for :djadmin:`startapp`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freisin: ref: `rabhadh rindreála `agus:ref: `rabhadh c "
"<render_warning>ód iontaofa` mar a luaitear le haghaidh: djadmin: `startapp "
"<trusted_code_warning>`."

msgid "``test``"
msgstr "``tástála``"

msgid ""
"Runs tests for all installed apps. See :doc:`/topics/testing/index` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé tástálacha do gach aip suiteáilte. Féach: doc: `/topics/tástáil/"
"innéacs `le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"Stops running tests and reports the failure immediately after a test fails."
msgstr ""
"Stopann tástálacha a reáchtáil agus tuairiscíonn sé an teip díreach tar éis "
"teip"

msgid ""
"Controls the test runner class that is used to execute tests. This value "
"overrides the value provided by the :setting:`TEST_RUNNER` setting."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn sé an rang rith tástála a úsáidtear chun tástálacha a fhorghníomhú "
"Sáraíonn an luach seo an luach a sholáthraíonn an socrú: setting: "
"`TEST_RUNNER`."

msgid ""
"Suppresses all user prompts. A typical prompt is a warning about deleting an "
"existing test database."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar gach leideanna úsáideora. Is é pras tipiciúil rabhadh "
"faoi bhunachar sonraí tástála atá ann cheana a scriosadh."

msgid "Test runner options"
msgstr "Tástáil roghanna rudaí"

msgid ""
"The ``test`` command receives options on behalf of the specified :option:`--"
"testrunner`. These are the options of the default test "
"runner: :class:`~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner`."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann an t-ordú `tástála` roghanna thar ceann an rogha sonraithe:rogha: "
"`--testrunner`. Seo iad na roghanna an rádálaí tástála "
"réamhshocraithe: :class: `~django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner`."

msgid ""
"Preserves the test database between test runs. This has the advantage of "
"skipping both the create and destroy actions which can greatly decrease the "
"time to run tests, especially those in a large test suite. If the test "
"database does not exist, it will be created on the first run and then "
"preserved for each subsequent run. Unless the :setting:`MIGRATE "
"<TEST_MIGRATE>` test setting is ``False``, any unapplied migrations will "
"also be applied to the test database before running the test suite."
msgstr ""
"Caomhníonn sé bunachar sonraí tástála idir rith tástála. Tá an buntáiste "
"aige seo na gníomhartha a chruthú agus a scriosadh a scipeáil ar féidir leo "
"an t-am chun tástálacha a reáchtáil a laghdú go mór, go háirithe iad siúd i "
"sraith tástála mór Mura bhfuil an bunachar sonraí tástála ann, cruthófar é "
"ar an gcéad rith agus ansin caomhnófar é do gach rith ina dhiaidh sin. Mura "
"bhfuil an socrú tástála: `MIGRATE <TEST_MIGRATE>``False``, cuirfear aon "
"imirce neamhfheidhmeacha i bhfeidhm ar bhunachar sonraí na tástála freisin "
"sula rith an tsraith tástála."

msgid ""
"Randomizes the order of tests before running them. This can help detect "
"tests that aren't properly isolated. The test order generated by this option "
"is a deterministic function of the integer seed given. When no seed is "
"passed, a seed is chosen randomly and printed to the console. To repeat a "
"particular test order, pass a seed. The test orders generated by this option "
"preserve Django's :ref:`guarantees on test order <order-of-tests>`. They "
"also keep tests grouped by test case class."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé ord na dtástálacha a randamach sula ndéantar iad a rith. Is "
"féidir leis seo cabhrú le tástálacha nach bhfuil scoite i gceart a bhrath. "
"Is feidhm chinnitheach den síol sláireach a thugtar an t-ordú tástála a "
"ghineann an rogha seo. Nuair nach ndéantar aon síol a rith, roghnaítear síol "
"go randamach agus é a phriontáil chuig an gconsól. Chun ordú tástála áirithe "
"a athdhéanamh, pas síol. <order-of-tests>Coinníonn na horduithe tástála a "
"ghineann an rogha seo Django's:ref: `ráthaíochtaí ar ordú tástála `. "
"Coinníonn siad tástálacha grúpáilte de réir aicme cásanna tástála freisin"

msgid ""
"The shuffled orderings also have a special consistency property useful when "
"narrowing down isolation issues. Namely, for a given seed and when running a "
"subset of tests, the new order will be the original shuffling restricted to "
"the smaller set. Similarly, when adding tests while keeping the seed the "
"same, the order of the original tests will be the same in the new order."
msgstr ""
"Tá maoin comhsheasmhachta speisialta ag na horduithe cumhdaithe atá "
"úsáideach agus saincheisteanna aonair a chúngú. Eadhon, i gcás síol ar leith "
"agus nuair a bhíonn fo-thacar tástálacha á reáchtáil, is é an t-ordú nua an "
"t-ordú bunaidh atá teoranta don tacar níos lú. Ar an gcaoi chéanna, agus "
"tástálacha á chur leis agus an síol á choinneáil mar an gcéanna, beidh ord "
"na dtástálacha bunaidh mar an gcéanna san ord nua."

msgid ""
"Sorts test cases in the opposite execution order. This may help in debugging "
"the side effects of tests that aren't properly isolated. :ref:`Grouping by "
"test class <order-of-tests>` is preserved when using this option. This can "
"be used in conjunction with ``--shuffle`` to reverse the order for a "
"particular seed."
msgstr ""
"Déanann cásanna tástála a shórtáil san ord forghníomhaithe D'fhéadfadh sé "
"seo cabhrú le fo-iarsmaí tástálacha nach bhfuil scoite i gceart a "
"dhífhabhtú. :ref: Caomhnaítear `Grúpáil de réir aicme tástá <order-of-"
"tests>la` nuair a úsáidtear an rogha seo. Is féidir é seo a úsáid i gcomhar "
"le ``--shuffle`` chun an t-ordú do shíol áirithe a aisiompú."

msgid ""
"Sets the :setting:`DEBUG` setting to ``True`` prior to running tests. This "
"may help troubleshoot test failures."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an socrú: socrú: `DEBUG` go ``True`` sula ndéantar tástálacha a "
"reáchtáil. D'fhéadfadh sé seo cabhrú le teipeanna tástála a réiteach"

msgid ""
"Enables :ref:`SQL logging <django-db-logger>` for failing tests. If ``--"
"verbosity`` is ``2``, then queries in passing tests are also output."
msgstr ""
"<django-db-logger>Cumasaí:ref: `Logáil SQL `le haghaidh tástálacha a theip. "
"Más é ```--verbosity`` ``2``, ansin aschur ceisteanna i dtástálacha pas "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"Runs tests in separate parallel processes. Since modern processors have "
"multiple cores, this allows running tests significantly faster."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé tástálacha i bpróisis chomhthreomhara Ós rud é go bhfuil croí "
"iomadúla ag próiseálaithe nua-aimseartha, ceadaíonn sé seo tástálacha"

msgid ""
"Using ``--parallel`` without a value, or with the value ``auto``, runs one "
"test process per core according to :func:`multiprocessing.cpu_count()`. You "
"can override this by passing the desired number of processes, e.g. ``--"
"parallel 4``, or by setting the :envvar:`DJANGO_TEST_PROCESSES` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as ``--parallel`` gan luach, nó leis an luach ``auto``, "
"reáchtáiltear próiseas tástála amháin in aghaidh an chroí de réir: func: "
"`multiprocessing.cpu_count () `. Is féidir leat é seo a shárú tríd an líon "
"próisis atá ag teastáil a rith, m.sh. ``--comhthreomhar 4``, nó tríd an "
"athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_TEST_PROCESSES` a shocrú."

msgid ""
"Django distributes test cases — :class:`unittest.TestCase` subclasses — to "
"subprocesses. If there are fewer test case classes than configured "
"processes, Django will reduce the number of processes accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Dáileann Django cásanna tástála -: class: `UnitTest.TestCase` fo-aicmí - "
"chuig fo-phróisis. Má tá níos lú ranganna cásanna tástála ann ná próisis "
"chumraithe, laghdóidh Django líon na bpróisis dá réir."

msgid ""
"Each process gets its own database. You must ensure that different test case "
"classes don't access the same resources. For instance, test case classes "
"that touch the filesystem should create a temporary directory for their own "
"use."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann gach próiseas a bhunachar sonraí féin. Ní mór duit a chinntiú nach "
"bhfuil rochtain ag ranganna cásanna tástála éagsúla ar na hacmhainní céanna "
"Mar shampla, ba cheart d'aicmí cásanna tástála a théann i dteagmháil leis an "
"gcóras comhaid eolaire sealadach a chruthú lena n-úsáid féin."

msgid ""
"If you have test classes that cannot be run in parallel, you can use "
"``SerializeMixin`` to run them sequentially. See :ref:`Enforce running test "
"classes sequentially <topics-testing-enforce-run-sequentially>`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ranganna tástála agat nach féidir a reáchtáil go comhthreomhar, is "
"féidir leat ``SerializeMixin`` a úsáid chun iad a reáchtáil go seicheamhach. "
"<topics-testing-enforce-run-sequentially>Féach:tagairt: `Ranganna tástála "
"reatha a fhorfheidhmiú go seicheamh`."

msgid ""
"This option requires the third-party ``tblib`` package to display tracebacks "
"correctly:"
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn an rogha seo an pacáiste ``tblib`` tríú páirtí chun rianais a "
"thaispeáint i gceart:"

msgid ""
"This feature isn't available on Windows. It doesn't work with the Oracle "
"database backend either."
msgstr ""
"Níl an ghné seo ar fáil ar Windows. Ní oibríonn sé le cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí Oracle ach an oiread."

msgid ""
"If you want to use :mod:`pdb` while debugging tests, you must disable "
"parallel execution (``--parallel=1``). You'll see something like "
"``bdb.BdbQuit`` if you don't."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat: mod: `pdb` a úsáid agus tú ag dífhabhtú tástálacha, ní mór "
"duit forghníomhú comhthreomhar a dhíchumasú (``--parallel=1``). Feicfidh tú "
"rud éigin cosúil le ``bdb.bdbQuit ``mura ndéanann tú."

msgid ""
"When test parallelization is enabled and a test fails, Django may be unable "
"to display the exception traceback. This can make debugging difficult. If "
"you encounter this problem, run the affected test without parallelization to "
"see the traceback of the failure."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéantar comhthreomhar tástála a chumasú agus nuair a theipeann ar "
"thástáil, b'fhéidir nach mbeidh Django in ann an rianú eisceachta a thaispe "
"Féadann sé seo dífhabhtú a dhéanamh deacair. Má thagann tú ar an bhfadhb "
"seo, reáchtáil an tástáil atá buailte gan comhthreomhar chun rianú an teip a "
"fheiceáil."

msgid ""
"This is a known limitation. It arises from the need to serialize objects in "
"order to exchange them between processes. See :ref:`python:pickle-picklable` "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Is teorannú aitheanta é seo. Eascraíonn sé as an ngá le rudaí a shraitheadh "
"d'fhonn iad a mhalartú idir próisis. Féach:ref: `python:pickle-picklable` le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"Runs only tests :ref:`marked with the specified tags <topics-tagging-"
"tests>`. May be specified multiple times and combined with :option:`test --"
"exclude-tag`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-tagging-tests>Ní ritheann sé ach tástálacha: ref: `marcáilte leis na "
"clibeanna sonraithe `. Is féidir é a shonrú arís agus arís eile agus é a "
"chomhcheangal le: rogha: `test --exclude-tag`."

msgid "Tests that fail to load are always considered matching."
msgstr ""
"Meastar go bhfuil tástálacha nach dteipfidh orthu a luchtú a mheaitseáil"

msgid ""
"Excludes tests :ref:`marked with the specified tags <topics-tagging-tests>`. "
"May be specified multiple times and combined with :option:`test --tag`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-tagging-tests>Ní áirítear tástálacha: ref: `marcáilte leis na "
"clibeanna sonraithe `. Is féidir é a shonrú arís agus arís eile agus é a "
"chomhcheangal le: rogha: `test --tag`."

msgid ""
"Runs test methods and classes matching test name patterns, in the same way "
"as :option:`unittest's -k option<unittest.-k>`. Can be specified multiple "
"times."
msgstr ""
"<unittest.-k>Ritheann sé modhanna tástála agus ranganna a mheaitseálann "
"patrúin ainmneacha tástála, ar an mbealach céanna le: rogha: `rogha -k "
"unittest `. Is féidir é a shonrú arís agus arís eile."

msgid ""
"Spawns a ``pdb`` debugger at each test error or failure. If you have it "
"installed, ``ipdb`` is used instead."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn dífhabhtaitheoir `pdb`` ag gach earráid tástála nó teip. Má tá sé "
"suiteáilte agat, úsáidtear ``ipdb`` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Discards output (``stdout`` and ``stderr``) for passing tests, in the same "
"way as :option:`unittest's --buffer option<unittest.-b>`."
msgstr ""
"<unittest.-b>Scaoileann sé aschur (``stdout`` agus ``stderr``) chun "
"tástálacha a rith, ar an mbealach céanna se:option: `unittest's --buffer "
"rogha `."

msgid ""
"Django automatically calls :func:`faulthandler.enable()` when starting the "
"tests, which allows it to print a traceback if the interpreter crashes. Pass "
"``--no-faulthandler`` to disable this behavior."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn Django go huathoibríoch:func: `faulthandler.enable () `nuair a "
"thosaíonn na tástálacha, rud a ligeann dó rianú a phriontáil má thimpíonn an "
"t-ateangaire. Pas ``--no-faulthandler`` chun an t-iompar seo a dhíchumasú."

msgid "Outputs timings, including database setup and total run time."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta aschuir, lena n-áirítear socrú bunachar sonraí agus am reatha "
"iomlán."

msgid "Shows the N slowest test cases (N=0 for all)."
msgstr "Taispeánann sé na cásanna tástála N is moille (N = 0 do gach duine)."

msgid "Python 3.12 and later"
msgstr "Python 3.12 agus níos déanaí"

msgid "This feature is only available for Python 3.12 and later."
msgstr "Níl an ghné seo ar fáil ach le haghaidh Python 3.12 agus níos déanaí."

msgid "``testserver``"
msgstr "``freastalaí tástála``"

msgid ""
"Runs a Django development server (as in :djadmin:`runserver`) using data "
"from the given fixture(s)."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé freastalaí forbartha Django (mar atá in:djadmin: `runserver`) ag "
"baint úsáide as sonraí ón daingneán (í) ar leith."

msgid "For example, this command:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, an t-ordú seo:"

msgid "...would perform the following steps:"
msgstr "... déanfadh na céimeanna seo a leanas:"

msgid "Create a test database, as described in :ref:`the-test-database`."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh bunachar sonraí tástála, mar a thuairiscítear in:ref: `the-test-"
"database`."

msgid ""
"Populate the test database with fixture data from the given fixtures. (For "
"more on fixtures, see the documentation for :djadmin:`loaddata` above.)"
msgstr ""
"Déan an bunachar sonraí tástála a líonadh le sonraí daingneáin ó na "
"daingneáin ar leith. (Le haghaidh tuilleadh faoi daingneáin, féach an "
"doiciméadú le haghaidh: djadmin: `loaddata` thuas.)"

msgid ""
"Runs the Django development server (as in :djadmin:`runserver`), pointed at "
"this newly created test database instead of your production database."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé an freastalaí forbartha Django (mar atá in:djadmin: "
"`runserver`), dírithe ar an mbunachar sonraí tástála nua-chruthaithe seo in "
"ionad do bhunachar sonraí táirgeachta."

msgid "This is useful in a number of ways:"
msgstr "Tá sé seo úsáideach ar roinnt bealaí:"

msgid ""
"When you're writing :doc:`unit tests </topics/testing/overview>` of how your "
"views act with certain fixture data, you can use ``testserver`` to interact "
"with the views in a web browser, manually."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn tú ag scríobh: doc: `tástálacha aonaid` ar an gcaoi a "
"ngníomhaíonn do thuairimí le sonraí daing</topics/testing/overview> neáin "
"áirithe, is féidir leat ``testserver`` a úsáid chun idirghníomhú leis na "
"tuairimí i mbrabhsálaí gréasáin, de láimh."

msgid ""
"Let's say you're developing your Django application and have a \"pristine\" "
"copy of a database that you'd like to interact with. You can dump your "
"database to a :ref:`fixture <fixtures-explanation>` (using "
"the :djadmin:`dumpdata` command, explained above), then use ``testserver`` "
"to run your web application with that data.  With this arrangement, you have "
"the flexibility of messing up your data in any way, knowing that whatever "
"data changes you're making are only being made to a test database."
msgstr ""
"Abair go bhfuil do fheidhmchlár Django á fhorbairt agat agus go bhfuil cóip "
"“pristine” de bhunachar sonraí ar mhaith leat idirghníomhú leis. Is féidir "
"leat do bhunachar sonraí a dhoir <fixtures-explanation>teadh chuig a:ref: "
"`fixture `(ag baint úsáide as an ordú:djadmin: `dumpdata`, a mhínítear "
"thuas), ansin bain úsáid as ``testserver`` chun d'fheidhmchlár gréasáin a "
"reáchtáil leis na sonraí sin. Leis an socrú seo, tá an solúbthacht agat do "
"chuid sonraí a chur suas ar bhealach ar bith, agus a fhios agat nach bhfuil "
"cibé athruithe sonraí atá á déanamh agat ach ar bhunachar sonraí tástála."

msgid ""
"Note that this server does *not* automatically detect changes to your Python "
"source code (as :djadmin:`runserver` does). It does, however, detect changes "
"to templates."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhraitheann an freastalaí seo* athruithe ar do chód "
"foinse Python go huathoibríoch (mar: djadmin: déanann `runserver`). "
"Braitheann sé athruithe ar theimpléid, áfach."

msgid ""
"Specifies a different port, or IP address and port, from the default of "
"``127.0.0.1:8000``. This value follows exactly the same format and serves "
"exactly the same function as the argument to the :djadmin:`runserver` "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn calafort difriúil, nó seoladh IP agus calafort, ó réamhshocrú "
"``127.0.0. 1:8000 ``. Leanann an luach seo an fhormáid chéanna go díreach "
"agus freastalaíonn sé go díreach an fheidhm chéanna leis an argóint leis an "
"ordú:djadmin: `runserver`."

msgid "To run the test server on port 7000 with ``fixture1`` and ``fixture2``:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an freastalaí tástála a reáchtáil ar chalafort 7000 le ``fixture1`` "
"agus `fixture2``:"

msgid ""
"(The above statements are equivalent. We include both of them to demonstrate "
"that it doesn't matter whether the options come before or after the fixture "
"arguments.)"
msgstr ""
"(Tá na ráitis thuas coibhéiseach. Cuirimid an dá cheann acu san áireamh chun "
"a thaispeáint nach bhfuil sé cuma an dtagann na roghanna roimh nó tar éis na "
"hargóintí daingneáin.)"

msgid "To run on 1.2.3.4:7000 with a ``test`` fixture:"
msgstr "Chun rith ar 1.2.3. 4:7000 le daingneán ``tástála`:"

msgid "Commands provided by applications"
msgstr "Orduithe a sholáthraíonn iarratais"

msgid ""
"Some commands are only available when the ``django.contrib`` application "
"that :doc:`implements </howto/custom-management-commands>` them has "
"been :setting:`enabled <INSTALLED_APPS>`. This section describes them "
"grouped by their application."
msgstr ""
"</howto/custom-management-commands> <INSTALLED_APPS>Níl roinnt orduithe ar "
"fáil ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an feidhmchlár ``django.contrib`` ara:doc: "
"`cur i bhfeidhm 'iad: socrú: `cumasaithe `. Déanann an chuid seo cur síos "
"orthu atá grúpáilte de réir a bhfeidh"

msgid "``changepassword``"
msgstr "``athraitheaspassword``"

msgid ""
"This command is only available if Django's :doc:`authentication system </"
"topics/auth/index>` (``django.contrib.auth``) is installed."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-ordú seo ar fáil ach amháin má tá Django's:doc: `córas "
"fíordheimhniúcháin` (``django.contrib.auth``) suiteáilte. </topics/auth/"
"index>"

msgid ""
"Allows changing a user's password. It prompts you to enter a new password "
"twice for the given user. If the entries are identical, this immediately "
"becomes the new password. If you do not supply a user, the command will "
"attempt to change the password whose username matches the current user."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn sé pasfhocal úsáideora a athrú. Spreagann sé duit pasfhocal nua a "
"iontráil faoi dhó don úsáideoir ar leith. Má tá na hiontrálacha comhionann, "
"is é seo an pasfhocal nua láithreach. Mura soláthraíonn tú úsáideoir, "
"déanfaidh an t-ordú iarracht an pasfhocal a mheaitseálann a n-ainm úsáideora "
"leis an úsáideoir reatha a athrú."

msgid "Specifies the database to query for the user. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí le fiosrú don úsáideoir. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "``createsuperuser``"
msgstr "``createsuperuser``"

msgid ""
"Creates a superuser account (a user who has all permissions). This is useful "
"if you need to create an initial superuser account or if you need to "
"programmatically generate superuser accounts for your site(s)."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé cuntas superuser (úsáideoir a bhfuil gach cead aige). Tá sé "
"seo úsáideach más gá duit cuntas sárúsáideora tosaigh a chruthú nó más gá "
"duit cuntais sárúsáideora a ghiniúint go cláraitheach do do shuíomh (í)."

msgid ""
"When run interactively, this command will prompt for a password for the new "
"superuser account. When run non-interactively, you can provide a password by "
"setting the :envvar:`DJANGO_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` environment variable. "
"Otherwise, no password will be set, and the superuser account will not be "
"able to log in until a password has been manually set for it."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh sé á reáchtáil go hidirghníomhach, spreagfaidh an t-ordú seo "
"pasfhocal don chuntas sárúsáideora nua. Nuair a reáchtáiltear go neamh-"
"idirghníomhach, is féidir leat pasfhocal a sholáthar tríd an athróg "
"comhshaoil: envvar: `DJANGO_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` a shocrú. Seachas sin, ní "
"shocrófar aon phasfhocal, agus ní bheidh an cuntas superuser in ann logáil "
"isteach go dtí go socraítear pasfhocal de láimh dó."

msgid ""
"In non-interactive mode, "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.CustomUser.USERNAME_FIELD` and "
"required fields (listed "
"in :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.CustomUser.REQUIRED_FIELDS`) fall back "
"to ``DJANGO_SUPERUSER_<uppercase_field_name>`` environment variables, unless "
"they are overridden by a command line argument. For example, to provide an "
"``email`` field, you can use ``DJANGO_SUPERUSER_EMAIL`` environment variable."
msgstr ""
"<uppercase_field_name>I mód neamh-idirghníomhach, tagann na:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.customUser.username_field` agus réimsí "
"riachtanacha (liostaithe in:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.customUser.required_fields`) ar ais chuig "
"athróga comhshaoil `DJANGO_SUPERUSER_ ``, mura gcuirtear athróg ordaithe "
"orthu. Mar shampla, chun réimse ``ríomhphost`` a sholáthar, is féidir leat "
"athróg comhshaoil ``DJANGO_SUPERUSER_EMAIL`` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Suppresses all user prompts. If a suppressed prompt cannot be resolved "
"automatically, the command will exit with error code 1."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé cosc ar gach leideanna úsáideora. Mura féidir pras faoi chois a "
"réiteach go huathoibríoch, imeoidh an t-ordú le cód earráide 1."

msgid ""
"The username and email address for the new account can be supplied by using "
"the ``--username`` and ``--email`` arguments on the command line. If either "
"of those is not supplied, ``createsuperuser`` will prompt for it when "
"running interactively."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an t-ainm úsáideora agus an seoladh ríomhphoist don chuntas nua a "
"sholáthar trí na hargóintí ``--username`` agus ``--email ``a úsáid ar an "
"líne ordaithe. Mura gcuirtear ceachtar acu sin ar fáil, spreagfaidh "
"``createsuperuser`` dó agus é ag rith idirghníomhach."

msgid "Specifies the database into which the superuser object will be saved."
msgstr "Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí ina sábhálfar an réad superuser."

msgid ""
"You can subclass the management command and override ``get_input_data()`` if "
"you want to customize data input and validation. Consult the source code for "
"details on the existing implementation and the method's parameters. For "
"example, it could be useful if you have a ``ForeignKey`` "
"in :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.CustomUser.REQUIRED_FIELDS` and want "
"to allow creating an instance instead of entering the primary key of an "
"existing instance."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an t-ordú bainistíochta a fho-aicmiú agus ``get_input_data () "
"`a shárú más mian leat ionchur agus bailíochtú sonraí a shaincheapadh. Téigh "
"i gcomhairle leis an gcód foinse le haghaidh sonraí ar an gcur chun feidhme "
"atá ann cheana agus paraiméadair Mar shampla, d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith "
"úsáideach má tá ``ForeignKey`` agat in:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.customUser.required_fields` agus gur mhaith "
"leat sampla a chruthú in ionad eochair phríomh-eochair an chás atá ann "
"cheana a iontráil."

msgid "``django.contrib.contenttypes``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.contenttypes``"

msgid "``remove_stale_contenttypes``"
msgstr "````cineálacha ábhar a bhaint ``"

msgid ""
"This command is only available if Django's :doc:`contenttypes app </ref/"
"contrib/contenttypes>` (:mod:`django.contrib.contenttypes`) is installed."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-ordú seo ar fáil ach amháin má tá django's:doc: `contenttypes app` "
"(:mod: `django.contrib.contenttypes` </ref/contrib/contenttypes>) suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"Deletes stale content types (from deleted models) in your database. Any "
"objects that depend on the deleted content types will also be deleted. A "
"list of deleted objects will be displayed before you confirm it's okay to "
"proceed with the deletion."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé cineálacha ábhair bhasa (ó mhúnlaí scriosta) i do bhunachar "
"sonraí. Scriosfar aon rudaí atá ag brath ar na cineálacha ábhair scriosta "
"freisin. Taispeánfar liosta de na rudaí scriosta sula ndeimhníonn tú go "
"bhfuil sé ceart go leor dul ar aghaidh leis an scriosadh."

msgid "Specifies the database to use. Defaults to ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an bunachar sonraí atá le húsáid. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid ""
"Deletes stale content types including ones from previously installed apps "
"that have been removed from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé cineálacha ábhar seasta lena n-áirítear cinn ó aipeanna atá "
"suiteáilte roimhe seo a baineadh ó:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid "``django.contrib.gis``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.gis``"

msgid ""
"This command is only available if :doc:`GeoDjango </ref/contrib/gis/index>` "
"(``django.contrib.gis``) is installed."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-ordú seo ar fáil ach amháin má tá: doc: `GeodJango` "
"(``django.contrib.gis`` </ref/contrib/gis/index>) suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"Please refer to its :djadmin:`description <ogrinspect>` in the GeoDjango "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Féach le do thoil dá: djadmin: `cur síos <ogrinspect>`sa doiciméadú "
"GeodJango."

msgid "``django.contrib.sessions``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.sesions``"

msgid "``clearsessions``"
msgstr "``seisiúin ghlanadh ``"

msgid "Can be run as a cron job or directly to clean out expired sessions."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir é a reáchtáil mar phost cron nó go díreach chun seisiúin atá in "
"éag a ghlanadh."

msgid "``django.contrib.staticfiles``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.staticfiles ``"

msgid ""
"This command is only available if the :doc:`static files application </howto/"
"static-files/index>` (``django.contrib.staticfiles``) is installed."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-ordú seo ar fáil ach amháin má tá an: doc: `feidhmchlár comhaid "
"stataich` (``django.contrib.staticfiles``) suiteáil</howto/static-files/"
"index> te."

msgid ""
"Please refer to its :djadmin:`description <collectstatic>` in "
"the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Féach dá: djadmin: `cur síos `sa doiciméad:doc: `staticfiles</ref/contrib/"
"staticfiles><collectstatic>` le do thoil."

msgid ""
"Please refer to its :djadmin:`description <findstatic>` in "
"the :doc:`staticfiles </ref/contrib/staticfiles>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Féach dá: djadmin: `cur síos `sa doiciméad:doc: `staticfiles</ref/contrib/"
"staticfiles><findstatic>` le do thoil."

msgid "Default options"
msgstr "Roghanna réamhshocrai"

msgid ""
"Although some commands may allow their own custom options, every command "
"allows for the following options by default:"
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhféadfadh roinnt orduithe a roghanna saincheaptha féin a cheadú, "
"ceadaíonn gach ordú na roghanna seo a leanas de réir réamh"

msgid ""
"Adds the given filesystem path to the Python :py:data:`sys.path` module "
"attribute. If this isn't provided, ``django-admin`` will use "
"the :envvar:`PYTHONPATH` environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an cosán córas comhaid tugtha leis an tréith modúl Python: py:data: "
"`sys.path`. Mura gcuirtear é seo ar fáil, úsáidfidh ``django-admin`` an "
"athróg comhshaoil: envvar: `PYTHONPATH`."

msgid ""
"This option is unnecessary in ``manage.py``, because it takes care of "
"setting the Python path for you."
msgstr ""
"Níl an rogha seo gan ghá i `manage.py``, toisc go dtugann sé aire do chonair "
"Python a shocrú duit."

msgid ""
"Specifies the settings module to use. The settings module should be in "
"Python package syntax, e.g. ``mysite.settings``. If this isn't provided, "
"``django-admin`` will use the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé an modúl socruithe le húsáid. Ba chóir go mbeadh an modúl "
"socruithe i gcomhréir pacáiste Python, m.sh. ``mysite.settings``. Mura "
"gcuirtear é seo ar fáil, úsáidfidh ``django-admin`` an athróg comhshaoil: "
"envvar: `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`."

msgid ""
"This option is unnecessary in ``manage.py``, because it uses ``settings.py`` "
"from the current project by default."
msgstr ""
"Níl an rogha seo gan ghá i `manage.py``, toisc go n-úsáideann sé "
"``settings.py`` ón tionscadal reatha de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Displays a full stack trace when "
"a :exc:`~django.core.management.CommandError` is raised. By default, "
"``django-admin`` will show an error message when a ``CommandError`` occurs "
"and a full stack trace for any other exception."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé rian iomlán cruach nuair a ardaítear a:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Management.CommandError`. De réir réamhshocraithe, "
"taispeánfaidh ``django-admin`` teachtaireacht earráide nuair a tharlaíonn "
"``CommandError`` agus rian iomlán cruach d'aon eisceacht eile."

msgid "This option is ignored by :djadmin:`runserver`."
msgstr "Déanann neamhaird ar an rogha seo ag: djadmin: `runserver`."

msgid ""
"Specifies the amount of notification and debug information that a command "
"should print to the console."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé méid na faisnéise fógra agus dífhabhtaithe ba chóir d'ordú a "
"phriontáil chuig an gconsól."

msgid "``0`` means no output."
msgstr "Ciallaíonn ``0`` gan aon aschur."

msgid "``1`` means normal output (default)."
msgstr "Ciallaíonn ``1`` gnáthaschur (réamhshocraithe)."

msgid "``2`` means verbose output."
msgstr "Ciallaíonn ``2`` aschur fhearbhóiseach."

msgid "``3`` means *very* verbose output."
msgstr "Ciallaíonn ```3`` aschur fíor* mór*."

msgid ""
"Disables colorized command output.  Some commands format their output to be "
"colorized. For example, errors will be printed to the console in red and SQL "
"statements will be syntax highlighted."
msgstr ""
"Díchumasann sé aschur ordaithe daite. Formálaíonn roinnt orduithe a n-aschur "
"le dathú. Mar shampla, clófar earráidí chuig an gconsól i ndearg agus "
"cuirfear béim ar chomhréireacht ráitis SQL."

msgid ""
"Forces colorization of the command output if it would otherwise be disabled "
"as discussed in :ref:`syntax-coloring`. For example, you may want to pipe "
"colored output to another command."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé dathú an aschur ordaithe dá ndéanfaí é a dhíchumasú ar shlí eile "
"mar a pléadh in:ref: `syntax-coloring`. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith "
"leat aschur daite a phíobáil chuig ordú eile."

msgid ""
"Skips running system checks prior to running the command. This option is "
"only available if "
"the :attr:`~django.core.management.BaseCommand.requires_system_checks` "
"command attribute is not an empty list or tuple."
msgstr ""
"Scaipeann sé seiceálacha córais a reáchtáil sula rith an t-ordú. Níl an "
"rogha seo ar fáil ach mura bhfuil an tréith ordaithe: attr: "
"`~django.core.management.baseCommand.requires_System_Checks` ina liosta "
"folamh nó tuple."

msgid "Extra niceties"
msgstr "Naiseachtaí breise"

msgid "Syntax coloring"
msgstr "Dathú comhréireachta"

msgid ""
"The ``django-admin`` / ``manage.py`` commands will use pretty color-coded "
"output if your terminal supports ANSI-colored output. It won't use the color "
"codes if you're piping the command's output to another program unless "
"the :option:`--force-color` option is used."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfidh na horduithe ``django-admin``/`manage.py`` aschur dathchódaithe "
"deas má thacaíonn do chríochfort le aschur daite ANSI. Ní úsáidfidh sé na "
"cóid datha má tá tú ag píobáil aschur an ordaithe chuig clár eile mura n-"
"úsáidtear an rogha: `--force-color`."

msgid "Windows support"
msgstr "Tacaíocht Windows"

msgid ""
"On Windows 10, the `Windows Terminal`_ application, `VS Code`_, and "
"PowerShell (where virtual terminal processing is enabled) allow colored "
"output, and are supported by default."
msgstr ""
"Ar Windows 10, ceadaíonn feidhmchlár `Windows Terminal`_, `VS Code `_, agus "
"PowerShell (áit a bhfuil próiseáil críochfoirt fíorúil cumasaithe) aschur "
"daite, agus tacaíonn siad de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Under Windows, the legacy ``cmd.exe`` native console doesn't support ANSI "
"escape sequences so by default there is no color output. In this case either "
"of two third-party libraries are needed:"
msgstr ""
"Faoi Windows, ní thacaíonn an consól dúchasach oidhreachta `cmd.exe`` le "
"seicheamh éalaithe ANSI mar sin de réir réamhshocraithe níl aon aschur datha "
"ann. Sa chás seo tá gá le ceachtar de dhá leabharlann tríú páirtí:"

msgid ""
"Install :pypi:`colorama`, a Python package that translates ANSI color codes "
"into Windows API calls. Django commands will detect its presence and will "
"make use of its services to color output just like on Unix-based platforms. "
"``colorama`` can be installed via pip:"
msgstr ""
"Install: pypi: `colorama`, pacáiste Python a aistríonn cóid dathanna ANSI go "
"glaonna API Windows. Braithfidh orduithe Django a láithreacht agus bainfidh "
"siad úsáid as a sheirbhísí chun aschur a dhathú díreach mar atá ar ardáin "
"bunaithe ar Unix-bhunaithe. Is féidir ``colorama ``a shuiteáil trí phíopa:"

msgid ""
"Install `ANSICON`_, a third-party tool that allows ``cmd.exe`` to process "
"ANSI color codes. Django commands will detect its presence and will make use "
"of its services to color output just like on Unix-based platforms."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil `ANSICON`_, uirlis tríú páirtí a ligeann ``cmd.exe`` cóid dathanna "
"ANSI a phróiseáil. Braithfidh orduithe Django a láithreacht agus bainfidh "
"siad úsáid as a sheirbhísí chun aschur a dhathú díreach mar atá ar ardáin "
"bunaithe ar Unix-bhunaithe."

msgid ""
"Other modern terminal environments on Windows, that support terminal colors, "
"but which are not automatically detected as supported by Django, may "
"\"fake\" the installation of ``ANSICON`` by setting the appropriate "
"environmental variable, ``ANSICON=\"on\"``."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh timpeallachtaí críochfoirt nua-aimseartha eile ar Windows, a "
"thacaíonn le dathanna teirminéil, ach nach bhraitear go huathoibríoch mar a "
"thacaíonn Django, suiteáil ``ANSICON`` a “bréagadh” tríd an athróg "
"comhshaoil iomchuí a shocrú, `ANSICON=\"on\"``."

msgid "Custom colors"
msgstr "Dathanna saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"The colors used for syntax highlighting can be customized. Django ships with "
"three color palettes:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir na dathanna a úsáidtear le haghaidh aibhsiú comhréireachta a shain "
"Longa Django le trí phailéid dathanna:"

msgid ""
"``dark``, suited to terminals that show white text on a black background. "
"This is the default palette."
msgstr ""
"``dorch``, oiriúnach do theirminéil a thaispeánann téacs bán ar chúlra dubh. "
"Is é seo an pailéad réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"``light``, suited to terminals that show black text on a white background."
msgstr ""
"``solas`, oiriúnach do theirminéil a thaispeánann téacs dubh ar chúlra bán."

msgid "``nocolor``, which disables syntax highlighting."
msgstr "``nocolor``, a dhíchumasaíonn aibhsiú comhréireachta."

msgid ""
"You select a palette by setting a :envvar:`DJANGO_COLORS` environment "
"variable to specify the palette you want to use. For example, to specify the "
"``light`` palette under a Unix or OS/X BASH shell, you would run the "
"following at a command prompt:"
msgstr ""
"Roghnaíonn tú pailéad trí athróg comhshaoil a: envvar: `DJANGO_COLORS` a "
"shocrú chun an pailéad is mian leat a úsáid a shonrú. Mar shampla, chun an "
"pailéad ``sola` a shonrú faoi bhlaosc Unix nó OS/X BASH, rith tú an méid seo "
"a leanas ag pras ordaithe:"

msgid ""
"You can also customize the colors that are used. Django specifies a number "
"of roles in which color is used:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat na dathanna a úsáidtear a shaincheapadh freisin. Sonraíonn "
"Django roinnt róil ina n-úsáidtear dath:"

msgid "``error`` - A major error."
msgstr "``earráid ``- Earráid mhór."

msgid "``notice`` - A minor error."
msgstr "``fógra`` - Earráid bheag."

msgid "``success`` - A success."
msgstr "``rath ``- Rath."

msgid "``warning`` - A warning."
msgstr "``rabhadh ``- Rabhadh."

msgid "``sql_field`` - The name of a model field in SQL."
msgstr "``sql_field`` - Ainm réimse samhail i SQL."

msgid "``sql_coltype`` - The type of a model field in SQL."
msgstr "``sql_coltype`` - An cineál réimse samhail i SQL."

msgid "``sql_keyword`` - An SQL keyword."
msgstr "``sql_keywords ``- Eochairfhocal SQL."

msgid "``sql_table`` - The name of a model in SQL."
msgstr "``sql_table`` - Ainm samhail i SQL."

msgid "``http_info`` - A 1XX HTTP Informational server response."
msgstr "``http_info`` - Freagra freastalaí faisnéise 1XX HTTP."

msgid "``http_success`` - A 2XX HTTP Success server response."
msgstr "``http_success`` - Freagra freastalaí rathúlachta 2XX HTTP."

msgid "``http_not_modified`` - A 304 HTTP Not Modified server response."
msgstr "``http_not_modified`` - Freagra freastalaí 304 HTTP Gan Athraithe."

msgid "``http_redirect`` - A 3XX HTTP Redirect server response other than 304."
msgstr ""
"``http_redirect`` - Freagra freastalaí atreoraithe HTTP 3XX seachas 304."

msgid "``http_not_found`` - A 404 HTTP Not Found server response."
msgstr "``http_not_found`` - Freagra freastalaí 404 HTTP Gan aimsiú."

msgid ""
"``http_bad_request`` - A 4XX HTTP Bad Request server response other than 404."
msgstr ""
"``http_bad_request`` - Freagra freastalaí Droch-Iarratas HTTP 4XX seachas "
"404."

msgid "``http_server_error`` - A 5XX HTTP Server Error response."
msgstr "``http_server_error`` - Freagra Earráid Freastalaí HTTP 5XX."

msgid "``migrate_heading`` - A heading in a migrations management command."
msgstr "``migrate_heading`` - Ceannteideal i ordú bainistíochta imirce."

msgid "``migrate_label`` - A migration name."
msgstr "``migrate_label`` - Ainm imirce."

msgid ""
"Each of these roles can be assigned a specific foreground and background "
"color, from the following list:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir tosaigh agus dath cúlra ar leith a shannadh do gach ceann de na "
"róil seo, ón liosta seo a leanas:"

msgid "``black``"
msgstr "``Dub``"

msgid "``red``"
msgstr "``dearg ``"

msgid "``green``"
msgstr "``glas ``"

msgid "``yellow``"
msgstr "```buí``"

msgid "``blue``"
msgstr "``gorm``"

msgid "``magenta``"
msgstr "``magenta``"

msgid "``cyan``"
msgstr "``cyan``"

msgid "``white``"
msgstr "```bán``"

msgid ""
"Each of these colors can then be modified by using the following display "
"options:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir gach ceann de na dathanna seo a athrú ansin trí na roghanna "
"taispeána seo a leanas a úsáid:"

msgid "``bold``"
msgstr "```bold``"

msgid "``underscore``"
msgstr "``Unscór``"

msgid "``blink``"
msgstr "``blink``"

msgid "``reverse``"
msgstr "```aisiom``"

msgid "``conceal``"
msgstr "``ceilitheach``"

msgid "A color specification follows one of the following patterns:"
msgstr "Leanann sonraíocht datha ceann de na patrúin seo a leanas:"

msgid "``role=fg``"
msgstr "``ról = fg``"

msgid "``role=fg/bg``"
msgstr "``ról = fg/bg``"

msgid "``role=fg,option,option``"
msgstr "``role = fg, rogha, rogha ``"

msgid "``role=fg/bg,option,option``"
msgstr "``role = fg/bg, rogha, rogha ``"

msgid ""
"where ``role`` is the name of a valid color role, ``fg`` is the foreground "
"color, ``bg`` is the background color and each ``option`` is one of the "
"color modifying options. Multiple color specifications are then separated by "
"a semicolon. For example:"
msgstr ""
"áit is é `ról bailí datha ```, 'ról', is é `fg`` an dath tosaigh, ``bg`` an "
"dath cúlra agus tá gach ``rogha ``ar cheann de na roghanna modhnaithe "
"dathanna. Déantar sonraíochtaí dathanna iolracha scartha ansin le leath-"
"icolón. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"would specify that errors be displayed using blinking yellow on blue, and "
"notices displayed using magenta. All other color roles would be left "
"uncolored."
msgstr ""
"sonródh sé go dtaispeánfaí earráidí ag baint úsáide as buí bliantach ar "
"gorm, agus fógraí a thaispeántar ag úsáid magenta D'fhágfaí gach ról datha "
"eile gan daite."

msgid ""
"Colors can also be specified by extending a base palette. If you put a "
"palette name in a color specification, all the colors implied by that "
"palette will be loaded. So:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir dathanna a shonrú freisin trí phailéad bonn a leathnú. Má "
"chuireann tú ainm pailéad i sonraíocht dathanna, luchtálfar na dathanna go "
"léir a thugann an pailéad sin. Mar sin:"

msgid ""
"would specify the use of all the colors in the light color palette, *except* "
"for the colors for errors and notices which would be overridden as specified."
msgstr ""
"sonródh sé úsáid na dathanna go léir sa phailéad dathanna éadrom, * seachas "
"na dathanna le haghaidh earráidí agus fógraí a shárófaí mar a shonraítear."

msgid "Bash completion"
msgstr "Críochnú Bash"

msgid ""
"If you use the Bash shell, consider installing the Django bash completion "
"script, which lives in :source:`extras/django_bash_completion` in the Django "
"source distribution. It enables tab-completion of ``django-admin`` and "
"``manage.py`` commands, so you can, for instance..."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú an bhlaosc Bash, smaoinigh ar script críochnaithe Django "
"bash a shuiteáil, a chónaíonn in:source: `extras/django_bash_completion` sa "
"dáileadh foinse Django. Cumasaíonn sé orduithe ``django-admin ``agus "
"`manage.py`` a chríochnú cluaisíní, ionas gur féidir leat, mar shampla..."

msgid "Type ``django-admin``."
msgstr "Cineál ``django-admin ``."

msgid "Press [TAB] to see all available options."
msgstr "Brúigh [TAB] chun gach rogha atá ar fáil a fheiceáil."

msgid ""
"Type ``sql``, then [TAB], to see all available options whose names start "
"with ``sql``."
msgstr ""
"Clóscríobh ``sql``, ansin [TAB], chun na roghanna go léir atá ar fáil a "
"dtosaíonn a n-ainmneacha le `sql`` a fheiceáil."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`/howto/custom-management-commands` for how to add customized "
"actions."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/conas/saincheapach-bhainistí-orduithe `maidir le conas "
"gníomhartha saincheaptha a chur leis."

msgid "Black formatting"
msgstr "Formáidiú dubh"

msgid ""
"The Python files created "
"by :djadmin:`startproject`, :djadmin:`startapp`, :djadmin:`optimizemigration`, :djadmin:`makemigrations`, "
"and :djadmin:`squashmigrations` are formatted using the ``black`` command if "
"it is present on your ``PATH``."
msgstr ""
"Déantar na comhaid Python a chruthaí:djadmin: `startproject`, :djadmin: "
"`startapp`, :djadmin: `optimemigration`, :djadmin: `makemigrations`, "
"agus:djadmin: `squashmigrations` a fhormáidiú ag baint úsáide as an ordú "
"``black`` má tá sé i láthair ar do `PATH``."

msgid ""
"If you have ``black`` globally installed, but do not wish it used for the "
"current project, you can set the ``PATH`` explicitly:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``dub`` suiteáilte go domhanda agat, ach mura dteastaíonn uait go n-"
"úsáidtear é don tionscadal reatha, is féidir leat an `PATH`` a shocrú go "
"sainráite:"

msgid ""
"For commands using ``stdout`` you can pipe the output to ``black`` if needed:"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh orduithe a úsáideann ``stdout`` is féidir leat an t-aschur a "
"phíobáil chuig ``dub`` más gá:"

msgid "Running management commands from your code"
msgstr "Orduithe bainistíochta a rith ó do chód"

msgid "To call a management command from code use ``call_command()``."
msgstr ""
"Chun ordú bainistíochta a ghlaoch ón gcód bain úsáid as ``call_command () ``."

msgid ""
"the name of the command to call or a command object. Passing the name is "
"preferred unless the object is required for testing."
msgstr ""
"ainm an ordaithe le glaoch nó réad ordaithe. Is fearr an t-ainm a rith mura "
"bhfuil an réad ag teastáil le haghaidh tástála."

msgid "``*args``"
msgstr "``*args``"

msgid ""
"a list of arguments accepted by the command. Arguments are passed to the "
"argument parser, so you can use the same style as you would on the command "
"line. For example, ``call_command('flush', '--verbosity=0')``."
msgstr ""
"liosta de na hargóintí a nglacann an t-ordú leo. Cuirtear argóintí chuig an "
"parser argóint, ionas gur féidir leat an stíl chéanna a úsáid agus a dhéanfá "
"ar an líne ordaithe. Mar shampla, ``call_command ('flush', '--verbosity=0') "
"``."

msgid "``**options``"
msgstr "``**roghanna ``"

msgid ""
"named options accepted on the command-line. Options are passed to the "
"command without triggering the argument parser, which means you'll need to "
"pass the correct type. For example, ``call_command('flush', verbosity=0)`` "
"(zero must be an integer rather than a string)."
msgstr ""
"roghanna ainmnithe a nglactar leo ar an líne ordaithe. Cuirtear roghanna "
"chuig an ordú gan an parser argóint a spreagadh, rud a chiallaíonn go mbeidh "
"ort an cineál ceart a rith. Mar shampla, ``call_command ('flush', "
"verbosity=0) ``(caithfidh nialas a bheith ina shláimhir seachas sreang)."

msgid ""
"Note that command options that take no arguments are passed as keywords with "
"``True`` or ``False``, as you can see with the ``interactive`` option above."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go ndéantar roghanna ordaithe nach nglacann aon argóintí "
"a rith mar eochairfhocail le ``True`` nó ``False``, mar a fheiceann tú leis "
"an rogha ``idirghníomhach` thuas."

msgid ""
"Named arguments can be passed by using either one of the following syntaxes::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir argóintí ainmnithe a rith trí cheann de na sintáisí seo a leanas a "
"úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Some command options have different names when using ``call_command()`` "
"instead of ``django-admin`` or ``manage.py``. For example, ``django-admin "
"createsuperuser --no-input`` translates to ``call_command('createsuperuser', "
"interactive=False)``. To find what keyword argument name to use for "
"``call_command()``, check the command's source code for the ``dest`` "
"argument passed to ``parser.add_argument()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá ainmneacha difriúla ag roinnt roghanna ordaithe nuair a úsáidtear "
"``call_command () ``in ionad ``django-admin`` nó ``manage.py``. Mar shampla, "
"aistríonn ``django-admin createsuperuser --no-input`` go ``call_command "
"('createsuperuser', interactive=false) ``. Chun a fháil amach cén t-ainm "
"argóint eochairfhocal atá le húsáid le haghaidh ``call_command () ``, "
"seiceáil cód foinse an ordaithe don argóint ``dest`` a chuirtear chuig "
"`parser.add_argument ()``."

msgid "Command options which take multiple options are passed a list::"
msgstr "Cuirtear liosta ar roghanna ordaithe a thógann roghanna éagsúla:"

msgid ""
"The return value of the ``call_command()`` function is the same as the "
"return value of the ``handle()`` method of the command."
msgstr ""
"Tá luach tuairisceáin na feidhme ``call_command () ``mar an gcéanna le luach "
"tuairisceáin modh ``handle ()`` den ordaithe."

msgid "Output redirection"
msgstr "Atreorú aschuir"

msgid ""
"Note that you can redirect standard output and error streams as all commands "
"support the ``stdout`` and ``stderr`` options. For example, you could write::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur féidir leat sruthanna caighdeánacha aschuir agus "
"earráide a atreorú toisc go dtacaíonn gach ordú leis na roghanna ``stdout`` "
"agus ``stderr``. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá scríobh:"

msgid "Django Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí Django"

msgid ""
"Django raises some of its own exceptions as well as standard Python "
"exceptions."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn Django cuid dá eisceachtaí féin chomh maith le heisceachtaí "
"caighdeánacha Python."

msgid "Django Core Exceptions"
msgstr "Croíeisceachtaí Django"

msgid ""
"Django core exception classes are defined in ``django.core.exceptions``."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear croí-aicmí eisceachta Django in ``django.core.exceptions``."

msgid "``AppRegistryNotReady``"
msgstr "``AppregistryNotready``"

msgid ""
"This exception is raised when attempting to use models before the :ref:`app "
"loading process <app-loading-process>`, which initializes the ORM, is "
"complete."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht seo agus tú ag iarraidh samhlacha a úsáid sula mbeidh "
"an próiseas luchtaithe aipe:ref: `<app-loading-process>`, a thosaíonn an "
"ORM, críochnaithe."

msgid "``ObjectDoesNotExist``"
msgstr "``ObjectDoesNotExist``"

msgid ""
"The base class for :exc:`Model.DoesNotExist "
"<django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist>` exceptions. A ``try/except`` for "
"``ObjectDoesNotExist`` will "
"catch :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist` exceptions for all models."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist>An bunaicme le haghaidh: exc: "
"`Model.doesNotExist `eisceachtaí. Tabharfaidh eisceachtaí ``triach/"
"eisceacht' do `ObjectDoesNotExist``: exc: "
"`~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` eisceachtaí do gach samhail."

msgid "See :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.get()`."
msgstr "Féach: Meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.get () `."

msgid "``EmptyResultSet``"
msgstr "``EmptyResultSet``"

msgid ""
"``EmptyResultSet`` may be raised during query generation if a query won't "
"return any results. Most Django projects won't encounter this exception, but "
"it might be useful for implementing custom lookups and expressions."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar ``EmptyResultSet ``a ardú le linn giniúint ceisteanna mura "
"dtabharfaidh ceist aon torthaí ar ais. Ní thiocfaidh an t-eisceacht seo ar "
"an gcuid is mó de thionscadal Django, ach d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith úsáideach "
"chun cuardaigh agus nathanna saincheaptha a chur"

msgid "``FullResultSet``"
msgstr "``Full-ResultSet``"

msgid ""
"``FullResultSet`` may be raised during query generation if a query will "
"match everything. Most Django projects won't encounter this exception, but "
"it might be useful for implementing custom lookups and expressions."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar ``FullResultSet ``a ardú le linn giniúint ceisteanna má mheaitseoidh "
"ceist gach rud. Ní thiocfaidh an t-eisceacht seo ar an gcuid is mó de "
"thionscadal Django, ach d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith úsáideach chun cuardaigh "
"agus nathanna saincheaptha a chur"

msgid "``FieldDoesNotExist``"
msgstr "``Fielddoesnotexist``"

msgid ""
"The ``FieldDoesNotExist`` exception is raised by a model's "
"``_meta.get_field()`` method when the requested field does not exist on the "
"model or on the model's parents."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht ``FieldDoesNotExist`` trí mhodh ``_meta.get_field () "
"``samhail nuair nach bhfuil an réimse iarrtha ann ar an tsamhail nó ar "
"thuismitheoirí an tsamhail."

msgid "``MultipleObjectsReturned``"
msgstr "``Iolrrudaíreachtaí ar ais ``"

msgid ""
"The base class for :exc:`Model.MultipleObjectsReturned "
"<django.db.models.Model.MultipleObjectsReturned>` exceptions. A ``try/"
"except`` for ``MultipleObjectsReturned`` will "
"catch :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.MultipleObjectsReturned` exceptions for "
"all models."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.MultipleObjectsReturned>An bunaicme le haghaidh: "
"exc: `Model.MultipleObjectsReturned `eisceachtaí. Tabharfaidh eisceachtaí "
"``trial/except`` le haghaidh ``MultipleObjectsReturned``: exc: "
"`~django.db.models.model.multipleObjectsReturned` eisceachtaí do gach "
"samhail."

msgid "``SuspiciousOperation``"
msgstr "``Oibríocht amhrasacha``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`SuspiciousOperation` exception is raised when a user has performed "
"an operation that should be considered suspicious from a security "
"perspective, such as tampering with a session cookie. Subclasses of "
"``SuspiciousOperation`` include:"
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht:EXC: `AspiciousOperation` nuair a bhíonn oibríocht "
"déanta ag úsáideoir ar chóir a mheas amhrasach ó thaobh slándála, mar "
"shampla cur isteach ar fhianán seisiúin. I measc na bhfo-aicmí de "
"``AspiciousOperation`` tá:"

msgid "``DisallowedHost``"
msgstr "``Óstach Disallowed``"

msgid "``DisallowedModelAdminLookup``"
msgstr "``DisallowedModelAdminlookup``"

msgid "``DisallowedModelAdminToField``"
msgstr "``DisallowedModelAdmintoField``"

msgid "``DisallowedRedirect``"
msgstr "``DisallowedRedirect ``"

msgid "``InvalidSessionKey``"
msgstr "``InvalidSessionKey``"

msgid "``RequestDataTooBig``"
msgstr "``RequestDataToobig``"

msgid "``SuspiciousFileOperation``"
msgstr "``Oibríocht comhaid amhrasacha``"

msgid "``SuspiciousMultipartForm``"
msgstr "``AmhrasachaFoirm Ilpháirt``"

msgid "``SuspiciousSession``"
msgstr "``Seisiún amhrasacha``"

msgid "``TooManyFieldsSent``"
msgstr "``ToomanyFieldssent``"

msgid "``TooManyFilesSent``"
msgstr "``ToomanyFilessent``"

msgid ""
"If a ``SuspiciousOperation`` exception reaches the ASGI/WSGI handler level "
"it is logged at the ``Error`` level and results in "
"a :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseBadRequest`. See the :doc:`logging "
"documentation </topics/logging/>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Má shroicheann eisceacht ``SusciousOperation`` leibhéal láimhseála ASGI/WSGI "
"logáiltear é ag an leibhéal ``Error ``agus bíonn a: class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponseBadRequest` mar thoradh air. Féach na:doc: "
"`doiciméadú logála `le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais. </topics/logging/>"

msgid "``PermissionDenied``"
msgstr "``Ceadú diúlt``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`PermissionDenied` exception is raised when a user does not have "
"permission to perform the action requested."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht: EXC: `PermissionDenied` nuair nach bhfuil cead ag "
"úsáideoir an gníomh a iarrtar a dhéanamh."

msgid "``ViewDoesNotExist``"
msgstr "``ViewdoesNotExist``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`ViewDoesNotExist` exception is raised by :mod:`django.urls` when a "
"requested view does not exist."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn an eisceacht:exc: `ViewDoesNotExist` ag: mod: `django.urls` nuair "
"nach bhfuil amharc iarrtha ann."

msgid "``MiddlewareNotUsed``"
msgstr "``MiddlewareNotused``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`MiddlewareNotUsed` exception is raised when a middleware is not "
"used in the server configuration."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear eisceacht: EXC: `MiddlewareNotUsed` nuair nach n-úsáidtear "
"middleware i gcumraíocht an fhreastalaí."

msgid "``ImproperlyConfigured``"
msgstr "``Neamhchumrú go cuiriún``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`ImproperlyConfigured` exception is raised when Django is somehow "
"improperly configured -- for example, if a value in ``settings.py`` is "
"incorrect or unparseable."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear eisceacht: EXC: `ImproperlyConfigured` nuair a dhéantar Django a "
"chumrú go míchuí ar bhealach éigin -- mar shampla, má tá luach in "
"`settings.py`` mícheart nó neamh-inpháirteach."

msgid "``FieldError``"
msgstr "``Fielderror``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`FieldError` exception is raised when there is a problem with a "
"model field. This can happen for several reasons:"
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear eisceacht: EXC: `Fielderror` nuair a bhíonn fadhb ann le réimse "
"samhail. Is féidir leis seo tarlú ar chúiseanna éagsúla:"

msgid ""
"A field in a model clashes with a field of the same name from an abstract "
"base class"
msgstr ""
"Bíonn réimse i samhail ag teacht le réimse den ainm céanna ó rang bonn teibí"

msgid "An infinite loop is caused by ordering"
msgstr "Tá lúb gan teorainn mar thoradh ar ordú"

msgid "A keyword cannot be parsed from the filter parameters"
msgstr "Ní féidir eochairfhocal a pháirseáil ó na paraiméadair scagaire"

msgid "A field cannot be determined from a keyword in the query parameters"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir réimse a chinneadh ó eochairfhocal sna paraiméadair fiosrúcháin"

msgid "A join is not permitted on the specified field"
msgstr "Ní cheadaítear páirt a ghlacadh ar an réimse sonraithe"

msgid "A field name is invalid"
msgstr "Tá ainm réimse neamhbhailí"

msgid "A query contains invalid order_by arguments"
msgstr "Tá argóintí neamhbhailí ord_by sa cheist"

msgid "``ValidationError``"
msgstr "``Earráid Bailíochtaithe``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`ValidationError` exception is raised when data fails form or model "
"field validation. For more information about validation, see :doc:`Form and "
"Field Validation </ref/forms/validation>`, :ref:`Model Field Validation "
"<validating-objects>` and the :doc:`Validator Reference </ref/validators>`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear eisceacht: EXC: `ValidationError` nuair a theipeann ar shonraí "
"bailíochtú réimse foirme nó samhail. </ref/forms/validation> </ref/"
"validators> <validating-objects>Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi "
"bhailíochtú, féach:doc: `Bailíochtú Foirm agus Réimse`, :ref: `Bailíochtú "
"Réimse Samhail `agus an:doc: `Tagairt Bailíochtaitheoir`."

msgid "``NON_FIELD_ERRORS``"
msgstr "``EARRÁID_NEAMH_RÉIMSE``"

msgid ""
"``ValidationError``\\s that don't belong to a particular field in a form or "
"model are classified as ``NON_FIELD_ERRORS``. This constant is used as a key "
"in dictionaries that otherwise map fields to their respective list of errors."
msgstr ""
"Aicmítear ``ValidationError`` nach mbaineann le réimse áirithe i bhfoirm nó "
"i msamhail mar ``NON_FIELD_ERRORS``. Úsáidtear an tairiseach seo mar eochair "
"i bhfoclóirí a dhéanann réimsí a mharpáil ar a liosta earráidí faoi seach."

msgid "``BadRequest``"
msgstr "``Iarratas ar Bád``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`BadRequest` exception is raised when the request cannot be "
"processed due to a client error. If a ``BadRequest`` exception reaches the "
"ASGI/WSGI handler level it results in "
"a :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseBadRequest`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht: EXC: `BadRequest` nuair nach féidir an t-iarratas a "
"phróiseáil mar gheall ar earráid cliant. Má shroicheann eisceacht "
"``BadRequest`` leibhéal láimhseála ASGI/WSGI mar thoradh air: a:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponseBadRequest`."

msgid "``RequestAborted``"
msgstr "``Iarrtha``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`RequestAborted` exception is raised when an HTTP body being read "
"in by the handler is cut off midstream and the client connection closes, or "
"when the client does not send data and hits a timeout where the server "
"closes the connection."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an eisceacht: EXC: `Requestaborted` nuair a ghearrtar comhlacht "
"HTTP atá á léamh ag an láimhseálaí isteach i lár an sruth agus nuair a "
"dhúnann an nasc cliant, nó nuair nach seolann an cliant sonraí agus nuair a "
"bhuaileann an t-am nuair a dhúnann an freastalaí an nasc."

msgid ""
"It is internal to the HTTP handler modules and you are unlikely to see it "
"elsewhere. If you are modifying HTTP handling code, you should raise this "
"when you encounter an aborted request to make sure the socket is closed "
"cleanly."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé inmheánach leis na modúil láimhseála HTTP agus ní dócha go bhfeicfidh "
"tú é in áiteanna eile. Má tá cód láimhseála HTTP á mhodhnú agat, ba cheart "
"duit é seo a ardú nuair a thagann tú ar iarratas a ghearradh chun a chinntiú "
"go bhfuil an soicéad dúnta go glan."

msgid "``SynchronousOnlyOperation``"
msgstr "``Oibríocht sioncrónaitheach``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`SynchronousOnlyOperation` exception is raised when code that is "
"only allowed in synchronous Python code is called from an asynchronous "
"context (a thread with a running asynchronous event loop). These parts of "
"Django are generally heavily reliant on thread-safety to function and don't "
"work correctly under coroutines sharing the same thread."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear eisceacht: EXC: `SynchronousOnlyOperation` nuair a thugtar cód "
"nach gceadaítear ach i gcód Python sioncrónach ó chomhthéacs asincrónach "
"(snáithe le lúb imeachta asincrónach reatha). De ghnáth bíonn na codanna seo "
"de Django ag brath go mór ar shábháilteacht snáithe chun feidhmiú agus ní "
"oibríonn siad i gceart faoi choroutines a roinneann an snáithe céanna."

msgid ""
"If you are trying to call code that is synchronous-only from an asynchronous "
"thread, then create a synchronous thread and call it in that. You can "
"accomplish this is with :func:`asgiref.sync.sync_to_async`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag iarraidh cód a ghlaoch atá sioncrónach amháin ó snáithe "
"asincrónach, ansin cruthaigh snáithe sioncrónach agus glaoigh air sin. Is "
"féidir leat é seo a chur i gcrích le: func: `asgiref.sync.sync_to_async`."

msgid "URL Resolver exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí réiteach URL"

msgid "URL Resolver exceptions are defined in ``django.urls``."
msgstr "Sainmhínítear eisceachtaí Resolver URL in ``django.url ``."

msgid "``Resolver404``"
msgstr "``Resolver404``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`Resolver404` exception is raised by :func:`~django.urls.resolve()` "
"if the path passed to ``resolve()`` doesn't map to a view. It's a subclass "
"of :class:`django.http.Http404`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn an eisceacht:EXC: `Resolver404` arraí:func: `~django.urls.solve () "
"`mura ndéanann an cosán a chuirtear chuig `resolution () ``léarscáil go "
"radharc. Is fo-aicme é de:class: `Django.http.http404`."

msgid "``NoReverseMatch``"
msgstr "``NoReversematch``"

msgid ""
"The :exc:`NoReverseMatch` exception is raised by :mod:`django.urls` when a "
"matching URL in your URLconf cannot be identified based on the parameters "
"supplied."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn an eisceacht: EXC: `NoReverseMatch` trí:mod: `django.urls` nuair "
"nach féidir URL meaitseála i do URLConf a aithint bunaithe ar na "
"paraiméadair a sholáthraítear."

msgid "Database Exceptions"
msgstr "Eiceachtaí Bunachar Sonraí"

msgid "Database exceptions may be imported from ``django.db``."
msgstr "Is féidir eisceachtaí bunachar sonraí a allmhairiú ó ``django.db``."

msgid ""
"Django wraps the standard database exceptions so that your Django code has a "
"guaranteed common implementation of these classes."
msgstr ""
"Fillteann Django na heisceachtaí caighdeánacha bunachar sonraí ionas go "
"mbeidh cur i bhfeidhm coiteann ráthaithe ag do chód Django na ranganna seo."

msgid ""
"The Django wrappers for database exceptions behave exactly the same as the "
"underlying database exceptions. See :pep:`249`, the Python Database API "
"Specification v2.0, for further information."
msgstr ""
"Iompraíonn fillteáin Django le haghaidh eisceachtaí bunachar sonraí díreach "
"mar an gcéanna leis na heisceachtaí bunúsacha bunachar Féach: PEP: `249`, "
"Sonraíocht API Bunachar Sonraí Python v2.0, le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"As per :pep:`3134`, a ``__cause__`` attribute is set with the original "
"(underlying) database exception, allowing access to any additional "
"information provided."
msgstr ""
"Mar: pep: `3134`, socraítear tréith ``__cause__`` leis an eisceacht bunaidh "
"(bunúsach) bunachar sonraí, rud a cheadaíonn rochtain ar aon fhaisnéis "
"bhreise a chuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Raised to prevent deletion of referenced objects when "
"using :attr:`django.db.models.PROTECT`. :exc:`models.ProtectedError` is a "
"subclass of :exc:`IntegrityError`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe chun rudaí tagartha a scriosadh a chosc agus iad ag úsáid: attr: "
"`Django.db.Models.Protect`. :exc: Is fo-aicme é `Models.ProtectedError` "
"de:exc: `IntegrityError`."

msgid ""
"Raised to prevent deletion of referenced objects when "
"using :attr:`django.db.models.RESTRICT`. :exc:`models.RestrictedError` is a "
"subclass of :exc:`IntegrityError`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe chun rudaí tagartha a scriosadh a chosc agus iad ag úsáid: attr: "
"`Django.db.Models.restrict`. :exc: Is fo-aicme é `Models.RestrictedError` "
"de:exc: `IntegrityError`."

msgid "HTTP Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí HTTP"

msgid "HTTP exceptions may be imported from ``django.http``."
msgstr "Is féidir eisceachtaí HTTP a allmhairiú ó ``django.http``."

msgid "``UnreadablePostError``"
msgstr "``UnreadablePostError``"

msgid ":exc:`UnreadablePostError` is raised when a user cancels an upload."
msgstr ""
":exc: Ardaítear `UnreadablePostError` nuair a chuireann úsáideoir uaslódáil "
"ar ceal."

msgid "Sessions Exceptions"
msgstr "Seisiúin eisceachtaí"

msgid ""
"Sessions exceptions are defined in ``django.contrib.sessions.exceptions``."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear eisceachtaí seisiúin in ``django.contrib.sessions.exceptions``."

msgid "``SessionInterrupted``"
msgstr "``Seisiún curtha isteach ``"

msgid ""
":exc:`SessionInterrupted` is raised when a session is destroyed in a "
"concurrent request. It's a subclass "
"of :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.BadRequest`."
msgstr ""
":exc: Ardaítear `sessionInterrupted` nuair a dhéantar seisiún a scriosadh in "
"iarratas comhuaineach. Is fo-aicme é de:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.badRequest`."

msgid "Transaction Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí Idirbheart"

msgid "Transaction exceptions are defined in ``django.db.transaction``."
msgstr "Sainmhínítear eisceachtaí idirbheart in ``django.db.transaction``."

msgid "``TransactionManagementError``"
msgstr "``Earráid Bainistíochta Idirbhearta``"

msgid ""
":exc:`TransactionManagementError` is raised for any and all problems related "
"to database transactions."
msgstr ""
":exc: Ardaítear `TransactionManagementError` le haghaidh aon fhadhb agus "
"gach fadhb a bhaineann le hidirbhearta bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Testing Framework Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí Creata Tástála"

msgid "Exceptions provided by the ``django.test`` package."
msgstr "Eisceachtaí a sholáthraíonn an pacáiste ``django.test``."

msgid "``RedirectCycleError``"
msgstr "``RedirectCycleError``"

msgid ""
":exc:`~client.RedirectCycleError` is raised when the test client detects a "
"loop or an overly long chain of redirects."
msgstr ""
": exc: Ardaítear `~Client.RedirectCycleError` nuair a bhraitheann an cliant "
"tástála lúb nó slabhra athreoruithe ró-fhada."

msgid "Python Exceptions"
msgstr "Eisceachtaí Python"

msgid ""
"Django raises built-in Python exceptions when appropriate as well. See the "
"Python documentation for further information on the :ref:`bltin-exceptions`."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn Django eisceachtaí Python ionsuite nuair is cuí freisin. Féach "
"doiciméadú Python le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise fao:ref: `bltin-"
"exceptions`."

msgid "The ``File`` object"
msgstr "An réad ``Comhad ``"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.core.files` module and its submodules contain built-in "
"classes for basic file handling in Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá ranganna ionsuite sa mhodúl:MOD: `django.core.files` agus a fho-mhodúil "
"le haghaidh láimhseáil comhaid bunúsach i Django."

msgid "The ``File`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``Comhad ````"

msgid ""
"The :class:`File` class is a thin wrapper around a Python :py:term:`file "
"object` with some Django-specific additions. Internally, Django uses this "
"class when it needs to represent a file."
msgstr ""
"Is fillteán tanaí é an rang:class: `File` timpeall Python: Py:term: `réad "
"comhad` le roinnt breiseanna sonracha Django. Go hinmheánach, úsáideann "
"Django an rang seo nuair is gá dó comhad a léiriú."

msgid ":class:`File` objects have the following attributes and methods:"
msgstr ":class: Tá na tréithe agus na modhanna seo a leanas ag rudaí `Comhad`:"

msgid ""
"The name of the file including the relative path from :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an chomhaid lena n-áirítear an cosán coibhneasta ó:setting: "
"`MEDIA_ROOT`."

msgid "The size of the file in bytes."
msgstr "Méid an chomhaid i mbetaí."

msgid "The underlying :py:term:`file object` that this class wraps."
msgstr "An bunús:py:term: `réad comhad` a fhilleann an rang seo."

msgid "Be careful with this attribute in subclasses."
msgstr "Bí cúramach leis an tréith seo i bhfo-aicmí."

msgid ""
"Some subclasses of :class:`File`, "
"including :class:`~django.core.files.base.ContentFile` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.fields.files.FieldFile`, may replace this "
"attribute with an object other than a Python :py:term:`file object`. In "
"these cases, this attribute may itself be a :class:`File` subclass (and not "
"necessarily the same subclass). Whenever possible, use the attributes and "
"methods of the subclass itself rather than the those of the subclass's "
"``file`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh roinnt fo-aicmí de:class: `File`, lena n-áir:class: "
"`~django.core.files.base.contentfile` agus:class: "
"`~django.db.models.fields.files.fieldfile`, réad seachas réad "
"Python:py:term: `file 'in ionad an tréith seo. Sna cásanna seo, féadfaidh an "
"tréith seo a: fo-aicme: “Comhad” a bheith ina bhfo-aicme (agus ní gá gurb é "
"an fo-aicme céanna). Nuair is féidir, bain úsáid as tréithe agus modhanna an "
"fho-aicme féin seachas tréithe tréithe “comhad” an fho-aicme."

msgid "The read/write mode for the file."
msgstr "An modh léithe/scríbhneoireachta don chomhad."

msgid ""
"Open or reopen the file (which also does ``File.seek(0)``). The ``mode`` "
"argument allows the same values as Python's built-in :func:`python:open()`. "
"``*args`` and ``**kwargs`` are passed after ``mode`` to Python's built-"
"in :func:`python:open`."
msgstr ""
"Oscail nó athoscail an comhad (a dhéanann freisin ``File.seek (0) ``). "
"Ceadaíonn an argóint ``mod`` na luachanna céanna le Python ion:func: "
"`python:open () `. Cuirtear ``*args`` agus ``**kwargs`` tar éis ``mode`` "
"chuig Python ionsuite: func: `python:open`."

msgid ""
"When reopening a file, ``mode`` will override whatever mode the file was "
"originally opened with; ``None`` means to reopen with the original mode."
msgstr ""
"Agus comhad á athoscailt, déanfaidh `mod`` athoscailt cibé modh a osclaíodh "
"an comhad leis ar dtús; ciallaíonn ``None ``athoscailt leis an modh bunaidh."

msgid "It can be used as a context manager, e.g. ``with file.open() as f:``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir é a úsáid mar bhainisteoir comhthéacs, m.sh. `with file.open () "
"mar f: ``."

msgid "Iterate over the file yielding one line at a time."
msgstr "Athraigh thar an gcomhad ag tabhairt líne amháin ag an am."

msgid ""
"Iterate over the file yielding \"chunks\" of a given size. ``chunk_size`` "
"defaults to 64 KB."
msgstr ""
"Athraigh thar an gcomhad ag tabhairt “píosaí” de mhéid ar leith. Tá "
"``chunk_size`` réamhshocraithe go 64 KB."

msgid ""
"This is especially useful with very large files since it allows them to be "
"streamed off disk and avoids storing the whole file in memory."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe le comhaid an-mhóra ós rud é go gceadaíonn "
"sé iad a shruthú as diosca agus seachnaíonn sé an comhad iomlán a stóráil i "
"gcuimhne."

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the file is large enough to require multiple chunks to "
"access all of its content give some ``chunk_size``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann tuairisceáin ``True`` má tá an comhad mór go leor chun go dteastaíonn "
"go leor píosaí chun rochtain a fháil ar a ábhar go léir, tugann roinnt "
"``chunk_size``."

msgid "Close the file."
msgstr "Dún an comhad."

msgid ""
"In addition to the listed methods, :class:`~django.core.files.File` exposes "
"the following attributes and methods of its ``file`` object: ``encoding``, "
"``fileno``, ``flush``, ``isatty``, ``newlines``, ``read``, ``readinto``, "
"``readline``, ``readlines``, ``seek``, ``tell``, ``truncate``, ``write``, "
"``writelines``, ``readable()``, ``writable()``, and ``seekable()``."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na modhanna liostaithe, nochtann :class: "
"`~django.core.files.file` na tréithe agus na modhanna seo a leanas dá réad "
"``comhad ``: `encoding``, `fileno``, ``flush``, `isatty``, `newlines``, "
"`readin``, `read `line`` `, `línte léite``, `cuarda``, `insint``, "
"`truncate``, `scríbhneoireach``, `scríbhneoireannaithe``, `inléite () ``, "
"`inscríofa ()``, agus ``cuardaitheach () ``."

msgid "The ``ContentFile`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``Contentfile``"

msgid ""
"The ``ContentFile`` class inherits from :class:`~django.core.files.File`, "
"but unlike :class:`~django.core.files.File` it operates on string content "
"(bytes also supported), rather than an actual file. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá an rang ``ContentFile`` oidhreacht ó:class: `~django.core.files.file`, "
"ach ní cosúil:class: `~django.core.files.file` oibríonn sé ar ábhar teaghrán "
"(tacaíonn béite freisin), seachas comhad iarbhír. Mar shampla::"

msgid "The ``ImageFile`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``Imagefile``"

msgid ""
"Django provides a built-in class specifically for "
"images. :class:`django.core.files.images.ImageFile` inherits all the "
"attributes and methods of :class:`~django.core.files.File`, and additionally "
"provides the following:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django rang ionsuite go sonrach le haghaidh íomhánna. :class: "
"`Django.Core.Files.Images.ImageFile` oidhreacht na tréithe agus na modhanna "
"uile de:class: `~django.core.files.file`, agus soláthraíonn sé an méid seo a "
"leanas freisin:"

msgid "Width of the image in pixels."
msgstr "Leithead na híomhá i bpicteilíní."

msgid "Height of the image in pixels."
msgstr "Airde na híomhá i bpicteilíní."

msgid "Additional methods on files attached to objects"
msgstr "Modhanna breise ar chomhaid atá ceangailte le rudaí"

msgid ""
"Any :class:`File` that is associated with an object (as with ``Car.photo``, "
"below) will also have a couple of extra methods:"
msgstr ""
"Aon: Class: Beidh cúpla modh breise ag `Comhad` a bhaineann le réad (mar atá "
"le ``Car.photo``, thíos) freisin:"

msgid ""
"Saves a new file with the file name and contents provided. This will not "
"replace the existing file, but will create a new file and update the object "
"to point to it. If ``save`` is ``True``, the model's ``save()`` method will "
"be called once the file is saved. That is, these two lines:"
msgstr ""
"Sábhálann comhad nua leis an ainm comhaid agus an t-ábhar a chuirtear ar "
"fáil. Ní chuirfidh sé seo in ionad an comhad atá ann cheana, ach cruthóidh "
"sé comhad nua agus nuashonróidh sé an réad chun cur in iúl dó. Más é "
"```Save`` `True``, glaofar modh ``save () ```` an tsamhail nuair a "
"shábháiltear an comhad. Is é sin, an dá líne seo:"

msgid "are equivalent to:"
msgstr "atá coibhéiseach le:"

msgid ""
"Note that the ``content`` argument must be an instance of "
"either :class:`File` or of a subclass of :class:`File`, such "
"as :class:`~django.core.files.base.ContentFile`."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcaithfidh an argóint ``content`` a bheith ina shampla "
"de: :class: `File` nó de fho-aicme de:class: `File`, mar shampla:class: "
"`~django.core.files.base.contentfile`."

msgid ""
"Removes the file from the model instance and deletes the underlying file. If "
"``save`` is ``True``, the model's ``save()`` method will be called once the "
"file is deleted."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé an comhad ón samhail samhail agus scriosann sé an comhad "
"bunúsach. Más é ```Save`` `True``, glaofar modh ``save () ```` an tsamhail "
"nuair a scriosfar an comhad."

msgid "File handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil comhad"

msgid "File storage API"
msgstr "API stórála comhad"

msgid "Getting the default storage class"
msgstr "An rang stórála réamhshocraithe a fháil"

msgid "Django provides convenient ways to access the default storage class:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django bealaí áisiúla chun teacht ar an rang stórála "
"réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"A dictionary-like object that allows retrieving a storage instance using its "
"alias as defined by :setting:`STORAGES`."
msgstr ""
"Rud cosúil le foclóir a cheadaíonn cás stórála a aisghabháil ag baint úsáide "
"as a ainm mar a shainmhínítear ar:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"``storages`` has an attribute ``backends``, which defaults to the raw value "
"provided in :setting:`STORAGES`."
msgstr ""
"Tá tréith ``backends`` ag `stórálaí ``, a réamhshocraíonn an luach amh a "
"chuirtear ar fáil in:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"Additionally, ``storages`` provides a ``create_storage()`` method that "
"accepts the dictionary used in :setting:`STORAGES` for a backend, and "
"returns a storage instance based on that backend definition. This may be "
"useful for third-party packages needing to instantiate storages in tests:"
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, soláthraíonn ``storages`` modh ``create_storage () ``a "
"ghlacann leis an bhfoclóir a úsáidtear in:setting: `STORAGES` le haghaidh "
"cúltaca, agus a thugann sé sampla stórála bunaithe ar an sainmhíniú cúltaca "
"sin. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith úsáideach do phacáistí tríú páirtí a "
"theastaíonn uathu stórálaí a thabhairt isteach i d"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.core.files.storage.DefaultStorage` provides lazy access to "
"the default storage system as defined by ``default`` key "
"in :setting:`STORAGES`. :class:`DefaultStorage` "
"uses :data:`~django.core.files.storage.storages` internally."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.core.files.storage.defaultStorage` soláthraíonn rochtain "
"leisciúil ar an gcóras stórála réamhshocraithe mar a shainmhínítear ag "
"`default`` eochair in:setting: `STORAGES`. :class: `DefaultStorage` "
"úsáideann: sonraí: `~django.core.files.storage.storages` go hinmheánach."

msgid ""
":data:`~django.core.files.storage.default_storage` is an instance of "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.storage.DefaultStorage`."
msgstr ""
":data: `~django.core.files.storage.default_storage` is sampla den :class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.defaultStorage`."

msgid "The ``FileSystemStorage`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``FilesystemStorage``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage` class implements "
"basic file storage on a local filesystem. It inherits "
"from :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` and provides "
"implementations for all the public methods thereof."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann rang:class: `~django.core.files.storage.filesystemStorage` stóráil "
"bunúsach comhaid i bhfeidhm ar chóras comhaid áitiúil. Oidhreacht aige "
"ó:class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage` agus soláthraíonn sé cur i "
"bhfeidhm do na modhanna poiblí uile dá leithéid."

msgid ""
"The ``FileSystemStorage.delete()`` method will not raise an exception if the "
"given file name does not exist."
msgstr ""
"Ní ardóidh an modh ``FilesystemStorage.delete () ``eisceacht mura bhfuil "
"ainm an chomhaid tugtha ann."

msgid ""
"Absolute path to the directory that will hold the files. Defaults to the "
"value of your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` setting."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán chuig an eolaire a shealbhóidh na comhaid. Réamhshocraithe ar "
"luach do shuíomh: socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"URL that serves the files stored at this location. Defaults to the value of "
"your :setting:`MEDIA_URL` setting."
msgstr ""
"URL a fhreastalaíonn ar na comhaid atá stóráilte ag an áit seo. "
"Réamhshocraithe ar luach do shuíomh: socrú: `MEDIA_URL`."

msgid ""
"The file system permissions that the file will receive when it is saved. "
"Defaults to :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS`."
msgstr ""
"Ceadanna an chórais chomhaid a gheobhaidh an comhad nuair a shábháiltear é. "
"Réamhshocraithe chuig: socrú: `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS`."

msgid ""
"The file system permissions that the directory will receive when it is "
"saved. Defaults to :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`."
msgstr ""
"Ceadanna an chórais chomhaid a gheobhaidh an eolaire nuair a shábháiltear é. "
"Réamhshocraithe chuig: socrú: `FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`."

msgid ""
"Flag to control allowing saving a new file over an existing one. Defaults to "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
"Bratach chun rialú a ligeann comhad nua a shábháil thar ceann atá ann "
"cheana. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`~datetime.datetime` of the system's ctime, "
"i.e. :func:`os.path.getctime`. On some systems (like Unix), this is the time "
"of the last metadata change, and on others (like Windows), it's the creation "
"time of the file."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceann a:class: `~datetime.datetime` de ctime an chórais, i.e.:func: "
"`os.path.getctime`. Ar roinnt córais (cosúil le Unix), is é seo an t-athrú "
"meiteashonraí deireanach, agus ar chórais eile (cosúil le Windows), is é am "
"cruthaithe an chomhaid é."

msgid "The ``InMemoryStorage`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``InmemoryStorage``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.core.files.storage.InMemoryStorage` class implements a "
"memory-based file storage. It has no persistence, but can be useful for "
"speeding up tests by avoiding disk access."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann rang:class: `~django.core.files.storage.inMemoryStorage` stóráil "
"comhaid bunaithe ar chuimhne i bhfeidhm. Níl aon mharthanacht aige, ach "
"féadann sé a bheith úsáideach chun tástálacha a bhrostú trí rochtain ar "
"dhiosca a sheachaint."

msgid ""
"Absolute path to the directory name assigned to files. Defaults to the value "
"of your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` setting."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán chuig ainm an eolaire a shanntar do chomhaid. Réamhshocraithe "
"ar luach do shuíomh: socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"The file system permissions assigned to files, provided for compatibility "
"with ``FileSystemStorage``. Defaults to :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS`."
msgstr ""
"Na ceadanna córais chomhaid a shanntar do chomhaid, a sholáthraítear le "
"haghaidh comhoiriúnacht le ``FilesystemStorage``. Réamhshocraithe chuig: "
"socrú: `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS`."

msgid ""
"The file system permissions assigned to directories, provided for "
"compatibility with ``FileSystemStorage``. Defaults "
"to :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`."
msgstr ""
"Na ceadanna córais chomhaid a shanntar d'eolairí, a sholáthraítear le "
"haghaidh comhoiriúnacht le ``FilesystemStorage``. Réamhshocraithe chuig: "
"socrú: `FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS`."

msgid "The ``Storage`` class"
msgstr "An rang ``Stórála``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` class provides a "
"standardized API for storing files, along with a set of default behaviors "
"that all other storage systems can inherit or override as necessary."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an rang:Class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage` API "
"caighdeánaithe chun comhaid a stóráil, mar aon le sraith iompraíochtaí "
"réamhshocraithe ar féidir le gach córas stórála eile a oidhreacht nó a shárú "
"de réir mar is gá."

msgid ""
"When methods return naive ``datetime`` objects, the effective timezone used "
"will be the current value of ``os.environ['TZ']``; note that this is usually "
"set from Django's :setting:`TIME_ZONE`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a fhilleann modhanna rudaí ``datetime`` naif, is é an crios ama "
"éifeachtach a úsáidtear ná luach reatha ``os.environ ['TZ'] `; tabhair faoi "
"deara go socraítear é seo de ghnáth ó Django's:SETTING: `TIME_ZONE`."

msgid ""
"Deletes the file referenced by ``name``. If deletion is not supported on the "
"target storage system this will raise ``NotImplementedError`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé an comhad dá dtagraítear ``ainm ``. Mura dtacaítear le "
"scriosadh ar an spriocchóras stórála ardóidh sé seo ``NotImplementederror`` "
"ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if a file referenced by the given name already exists in "
"the storage system."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá comhad dá dtagraítear leis an ainm tugtha "
"cheana sa chóras stórála."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`~datetime.datetime` of the last accessed time of the file. "
"For storage systems unable to return the last accessed time this will "
"raise :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceann a:class: `~datetime.datetime` an t-am deireanach a rochtain ar "
"an gcomhad. Maidir le córais stórála nach féidir leis an am dheireanach a "
"rochtain a thabhairt ar ais, ardóidh sé seo: exc: `NotImplementeDerror`."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, returns an aware ``datetime``, otherwise "
"returns a naive ``datetime`` in the local timezone."
msgstr ""
"Má tá: Setting: ```True`` `USE_TZ`, filleann ``datetime`` ar an eolas, ar "
"shlí eile filleann ``datetime`` naif sa chrios ama áitiúil."

msgid ""
"Returns an alternative filename based on the ``file_root`` and ``file_ext`` "
"parameters, an underscore plus a random 7 character alphanumeric string is "
"appended to the filename before the extension."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ainm comhaid malartach ar ais bunaithe ar na paraiméadair "
"`file_root`` agus `file_ext``, cuirtear béim móide sreang alfauméireach "
"randamach 7 charachtar leis an ainm comhaid roimh an síneadh."

msgid ""
"Returns a filename based on the ``name`` parameter that's free and available "
"for new content to be written to on the target storage system."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ainm comhaid ar ais bunaithe ar an bparaiméadar ``ainm ``atá saor in "
"aisce agus atá ar fáil le haghaidh ábhar nua le scríobh chuige ar an "
"spriocchóras stórála."

msgid ""
"The length of the filename will not exceed ``max_length``, if provided. If a "
"free unique filename cannot be found, a :exc:`SuspiciousFileOperation "
"<django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation>` exception will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Ní rachaidh fad an ainm comhaid thar ``max_length ``, má chuirtear ar fáil. "
"<django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation>Mura féidir ainm comhaid uathúil "
"saor in aisce a fháil, ardófar eisceacht a: exc: `SuspiciousFileOperation`."

msgid ""
"If a file with ``name`` already exists, :meth:`get_alternative_name` is "
"called to obtain an alternative name."
msgstr ""
"Má tá comhad le ``ainm ``ann cheana féin, glaoirtear ar :meth: "
"`get_alternative_name` chun ainm malartach a fháil."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`~datetime.datetime` of the creation time of the file. For "
"storage systems unable to return the creation time this will "
"raise :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceann a:class: `~datetime.datetime` am cruthaithe an chomhaid. Maidir "
"le córais stórála nach féidir leis an am cruthaithe a thabhairt ar ais, "
"ardóidh sé seo: exc: `NotImplementeDerror`."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`~datetime.datetime` of the last modified time of the file. "
"For storage systems unable to return the last modified time this will "
"raise :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Tugann a:class: `~datetime.datetime` an t-am modhnaithe deireanach den "
"chomhad. Maidir le córais stórála nach féidir leis an am deireanach "
"modhnaithe a thabhairt ar ais, ardóidh sé seo: exc: `NotImplementeDerror`."

msgid ""
"Returns a filename based on the ``name`` parameter that's suitable for use "
"on the target storage system."
msgstr ""
"Tugann ainm comhaid ar ais bunaithe ar an bparaiméadar ``ainm ``atá "
"oiriúnach le húsáid ar an spriocchóras stórála."

msgid ""
"Validates the ``filename`` by calling :attr:`get_valid_name()` and returns a "
"filename to be passed to the :meth:`save` method."
msgstr ""
"Bailíonn sé an ``ainm comhaid ``trí ghlaoch: attr: `get_valid_name () `agus "
"cuireann sé ainm comhaid ar ais chuig an modh:meth: `save`."

msgid ""
"The ``filename`` argument may include a path as returned "
"by :attr:`FileField.upload_to <django.db.models.FileField.upload_to>`. In "
"that case, the path won't be passed to :attr:`get_valid_name()` but will be "
"prepended back to the resulting name."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.FileField.upload_to>D'fhéadfadh cosán a bheith san argóint "
"``ainm comhad ``mar a thug ar ais ar:attr: `filefield.upload_to `. Sa chás "
"sin, ní rachfar an cosán chuig: attr: `get_valid_name () `ach cuirfear ar "
"ais chuig an ainm mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"The default implementation uses :mod:`os.path` operations. Override this "
"method if that's not appropriate for your storage."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe oibríochtaí: mod: `os.path`. "
"Athraigh an modh seo mura bhfuil sé sin oiriúnach do do stóráil."

msgid ""
"Lists the contents of the specified path, returning a 2-tuple of lists; the "
"first item being directories, the second item being files. For storage "
"systems that aren't able to provide such a listing, this will raise a "
"``NotImplementedError`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Liostaíonn sé ábhar an chosáin shonraithe, ag tabhairt ar ais dhá liostaí; "
"is eolairí an chéad mhír, agus is comhaid an dara mír. Maidir le córais "
"stórála nach bhfuil in ann liostú den sórt sin a sholáthar, ardóidh sé seo "
"“NotImplementederror” ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Opens the file given by ``name``. Note that although the returned file is "
"guaranteed to be a ``File`` object, it might actually be some subclass. In "
"the case of remote file storage this means that reading/writing could be "
"quite slow, so be warned."
msgstr ""
"Osclaíonn sé an comhad a thugtar ag ``ainm ``. Tabhair faoi deara cé go "
"ráthaítear gurb é an comhad a chuirtear ar ais ina réad ``Comhad ``, "
"d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith i ndáiríre fo-aicme éigin. I gcás stórála comhaid "
"iargúlta ciallaíonn sé seo go bhféadfadh léitheoir/scríbhneoireacht a bheith "
"mall go leor, mar sin tabhair rabhadh."

msgid ""
"The local filesystem path where the file can be opened using Python's "
"standard ``open()``. For storage systems that aren't accessible from the "
"local filesystem, this will raise ``NotImplementedError`` instead."
msgstr ""
"An cosán córais chomhaid áitiúil inar féidir an comhad a oscailt ag baint "
"úsáide as caighdeánach Python `open () `. Maidir le córais stórála nach "
"bhfuil inrochtana ón gcóras comhaid áitiúil, ardóidh sé seo "
"`NotImplementederror`` ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Saves a new file using the storage system, preferably with the name "
"specified. If there already exists a file with this name ``name``, the "
"storage system may modify the filename as necessary to get a unique name. "
"The actual name of the stored file will be returned."
msgstr ""
"Sábhálann sé comhad nua ag baint úsáide as an gcóras stórála, b'fhearr leis "
"an ainm a sh Má tá comhad ann cheana féin leis an ainm seo ``ainm ``, "
"féadfaidh an córas stórála an t-ainm comhaid a mhodhnú de réir mar is gá "
"chun ainm uathúil a fháil. Cuirfear ainm iarbhír an chomhaid stóráilte ar "
"ais."

msgid ""
"The ``max_length`` argument is passed along to :meth:`get_available_name`."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear an argóint `max_length ``ar aghaidh chuig: meth: "
"`get_available_name`."

msgid ""
"The ``content`` argument must be an instance "
"of :class:`django.core.files.File` or a file-like object that can be wrapped "
"in ``File``."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an argóint ``content`` a bheith ina shampla de:class: "
"`django.core.files.file` nó réad cosúil le comhad is féidir a fhilleadh i "
"`Comhad ``."

msgid ""
"Returns the total size, in bytes, of the file referenced by ``name``. For "
"storage systems that aren't able to return the file size this will raise "
"``NotImplementedError`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais méid iomlán, i mbeátaí, an chomhaid dá dtagraítear ``ainm "
"``. Maidir le córais stórála nach bhfuil in ann méid an chomhaid a thabhairt "
"ar ais, ardóidh sé seo `NotImplementederror`` ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"Returns the URL where the contents of the file referenced by ``name`` can be "
"accessed. For storage systems that don't support access by URL this will "
"raise ``NotImplementedError`` instead."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an URL ar ais inar féidir teacht ar ábhar an chomhaid dá "
"dtagraítear ``ainm ``. Maidir le córais stórála nach dtacaíonn le rochtain "
"trí URL ardóidh sé seo ``NotImplementederror`` ina ionad sin."

msgid "Uploaded Files and Upload Handlers"
msgstr "Comhaid Uaslódála agus Láimhseálaithe"

msgid "Uploaded files"
msgstr "comhaid uaslódáil"

msgid ""
"During file uploads, the actual file data is stored in :attr:`request.FILES "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.FILES>`. Each entry in this dictionary is an "
"``UploadedFile`` object (or a subclass) -- a wrapper around an uploaded "
"file. You'll usually use one of these methods to access the uploaded content:"
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.FILES>Le linn uaslódála comhaid, stóráiltear na "
"sonraí comhaid iarbhír in:attr: `request.files `. Is réad ``Uploadedfile`` "
"(nó fo-aicme) é gach iontráil sa fhoclóir seo - fillteán timpeall comhad "
"uaslódáilte. De ghnáth úsáidfidh tú ceann de na modhanna seo chun rochtain a "
"fháil ar an ábhar uaslódáil"

msgid ""
"Read the entire uploaded data from the file. Be careful with this method: if "
"the uploaded file is huge it can overwhelm your system if you try to read it "
"into memory. You'll probably want to use ``chunks()`` instead; see below."
msgstr ""
"Léigh na sonraí uaslódáilte iomlána ón gcomhad. Bí cúramach leis an modh "
"seo: má tá an comhad uaslódáilte ollmhór féadfaidh sé do chóras a shárú má "
"dhéanann tú iarracht é a léamh isteach i gcuimhne. Is dócha go mbeidh tú ag "
"iarraidh ``chunks () ``a úsáid ina ionad; féach thíos."

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the uploaded file is big enough to require reading in "
"multiple chunks. By default this will be any file larger than 2.5 megabytes, "
"but that's configurable; see below."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá an comhad uaslódáilte mór go leor chun go "
"mbeidh léamh ag teastáil i gcodanna iolracha. De réir réamhshocraithe beidh "
"sé seo aon chomhad níos mó ná 2.5 meigabyte, ach tá sé sin inchumraithe; "
"féach thíos."

msgid ""
"A generator returning chunks of the file. If ``multiple_chunks()`` is "
"``True``, you should use this method in a loop instead of ``read()``."
msgstr ""
"Gineadóir ag filleadh codanna den chomhad. Más é ```multiple_chunks () "
"```True``, ba chóir duit an modh seo a úsáid i lúb in ionad ``read ()``."

msgid ""
"In practice, it's often easiest to use ``chunks()`` all the time. Looping "
"over ``chunks()`` instead of using ``read()`` ensures that large files don't "
"overwhelm your system's memory."
msgstr ""
"Go praiticiúil, is minic a bhíonn sé níos éasca ```chunks () ``a úsáid an t-"
"am ar fad. Cinntíonn lupáil thar ``chunks () ``in ionad ``read ()`` a úsáid "
"nach gcuireann comhaid mhóra cuimhne do chórais a shárú."

msgid "Here are some useful attributes of ``UploadedFile``:"
msgstr "Seo roinnt tréithe úsáideacha de ``uploadedfile``:"

msgid "The name of the uploaded file (e.g. ``my_file.txt``)."
msgstr "Ainm an chomhaid uaslódáilte (m.sh. ``my_file.txt``)."

msgid "The size, in bytes, of the uploaded file."
msgstr "Méid, i mbeátaí, an chomhaid uaslódáilte."

msgid ""
"The content-type header uploaded with the file (e.g. :mimetype:`text/plain` "
"or :mimetype:`application/pdf`). Like any data supplied by the user, you "
"shouldn't trust that the uploaded file is actually this type. You'll still "
"need to validate that the file contains the content that the content-type "
"header claims -- \"trust but verify.\""
msgstr ""
"An ceannteideal cineál ábhair a uaslódáil leis an gcomhad (m.sh.: mimetype: "
"`text/plain` nó: mimetype: `application/pdf`). Cosúil le haon sonraí a "
"sholáthraíonn an t-úsáideoir, níor chóir duit muinín a bheith agat gurb é an "
"comhad uaslódáilte an cineál seo Beidh ort fós a bhailíochtú go bhfuil an t-"
"ábhar a éilíonn an ceannteideal de chineál ábhair sa chomhad - “muinín a "
"bheith agat ach fíoraigh.”"

msgid ""
"A dictionary containing extra parameters passed to the ``content-type`` "
"header. This is typically provided by services, such as Google App Engine, "
"that intercept and handle file uploads on your behalf. As a result your "
"handler may not receive the uploaded file content, but instead a URL or "
"other pointer to the file (see :rfc:`RFC 2388 <2388#section-5.3>`)."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil paraiméadair bhreise curtha ar aghaidh chuig an "
"gceannteideal ``cineál-ábhair ``. Is gnách go soláthraíonn seirbhísí seo, "
"mar shampla Google App Engine, a chuireann uaslódálacha comhad a thar do "
"cheann a idirghabháil agus a láimhseáil. <2388 #section -5.3>Mar thoradh air "
"sin b'fhéidir nach bhfaighidh do láimhseálaí an t-ábhar comhad uaslódáilte, "
"ach ina ionad sin URL nó pointeoir eile chuig an gcomhad (féach: rfc: `RFC "
"2388`)."

msgid ""
"For :mimetype:`text/*` content-types, the character set (i.e. ``utf8``) "
"supplied by the browser. Again, \"trust but verify\" is the best policy here."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le: mimetype: `téacs/*` cineálacha ábhair, an tacar carachtair (ie "
"``utf8``) a sholáthraíonn an brabhsálaí. Arís, is é “muinín ach fíorú” an "
"beartas is fearr anseo."

msgid ""
"Like regular Python files, you can read the file line-by-line by iterating "
"over the uploaded file::"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le comhaid rialta Python, is féidir leat an comhad a léamh líne ar "
"líne trí athrú thar an gcomhad uaslódáilte::"

msgid ""
"Lines are split using :pep:`universal newlines <278>`. The following are "
"recognized as ending a line: the Unix end-of-line convention ``'\\n'``, the "
"Windows convention ``'\\r\\n'``, and the old Macintosh convention ``'\\r'``."
msgstr ""
"<278>Roinntear línte ag baint úsáide as: pep: `línte nua uilíoch `. "
"Aithnítear na nithe seo a leanas mar chríochnú líne: coinbhinsiún deireadh "
"líne Unix ```\\\\ n '`, coinbhinsiún Windows ``'\\ r\\ n '``, agus an sean-"
"choinbhinsiún Macintosh``'\\ r'``."

msgid "Subclasses of ``UploadedFile`` include:"
msgstr "I measc na bhfo-aicmí de `Uploadedfile`` tá:"

msgid ""
"A file uploaded to a temporary location (i.e. stream-to-disk). This class is "
"used by "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.uploadhandler.TemporaryFileUploadHandler`. In "
"addition to the methods from :class:`UploadedFile`, it has one additional "
"method:"
msgstr ""
"Comhad a uaslódáil chuig suíomh sealadach (ie sruth-go-diosca). Úsáideann an "
"rang seo ag an: class: "
"`~django.core.files.uploadHandler.TemporaryFileUploadHandler`. Chomh maith "
"leis na modhanna ó:class: `uploadedFile`, tá modh breise amháin aige:"

msgid "Returns the full path to the temporary uploaded file."
msgstr "Tugann sé an cosán iomlán ar ais chuig an gcomhad uaslódáilte"

msgid ""
"A file uploaded into memory (i.e. stream-to-memory). This class is used by "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.uploadhandler.MemoryFileUploadHandler`."
msgstr ""
"Comhad a uaslódáiltear i gcuimhne (ie sruth-chuimhne). Úsáideann an rang seo "
"ag an: class: `~django.core.files.uploadHandler.MemoryFileUploadHandler`."

msgid "Built-in upload handlers"
msgstr "Láimhseálaithe uaslódála"

msgid ""
"Together the :class:`MemoryFileUploadHandler` "
"and :class:`TemporaryFileUploadHandler` provide Django's default file upload "
"behavior of reading small files into memory and large ones onto disk. They "
"are located in ``django.core.files.uploadhandler``."
msgstr ""
"Le chéile soláthraíonn an:class: `MemoryFileUploadHandler` agus:class: "
"`TemporaryFileUploadHandler` iompar uaslódála comhaid réamhshocraithe Django "
"maidir le comhaid bheaga a léamh isteach i gcuimhne agus cinn mhóra ar an "
"diosca. Tá siad suite i ``django.core.files.uploadhandler``."

msgid ""
"File upload handler to stream uploads into memory (used for small files)."
msgstr ""
"Láimhseálaí uaslódála comhad chun uaslódálacha a shruthú isteach i gcuimhne "
"(úsáidtear le haghaidh comh"

msgid ""
"Upload handler that streams data into a temporary file "
"using :class:`~django.core.files.uploadedfile.TemporaryUploadedFile`."
msgstr ""
"Uaslódáil láimhseálaí a sruthaíonn sonraí isteach i gcomhad sealadach ag "
"baint úsáid:class: `~django.core.files.uploadedfile.temporaryUploadedFile`."

msgid "Writing custom upload handlers"
msgstr "Láimhseálaithe uaslódáil saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"All file upload handlers should be subclasses of "
"``django.core.files.uploadhandler.FileUploadHandler``. You can define upload "
"handlers wherever you wish."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh fo-aicmí de "
"``Django.Core.Files.uploadHandler.FileUploadHandler`` i ngach láimhseálaí "
"uaslódála comhad. Féadfaidh tú láimhseálaithe uaslódála a shainiú cibé áit"

msgid "Required methods"
msgstr "Modhanna riachtanacha"

msgid "Custom file upload handlers **must** define the following methods:"
msgstr ""
"Ní mór do láimhseálaithe uaslódála comhad saincheaptaí** na modhanna seo a "
"leanas a"

msgid "Receives a \"chunk\" of data from the file upload."
msgstr "Faigheann sé “píosa” sonraí ón uaslódáil comhad."

msgid "``raw_data`` is a bytestring containing the uploaded data."
msgstr "Is bytestring é ``raw_data`` ina bhfuil na sonraí uaslódáilte."

msgid ""
"``start`` is the position in the file where this ``raw_data`` chunk begins."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``start`` an suíomh sa chomhad ina dtosaíonn an chuid ``raw_data`` seo."

msgid ""
"The data you return will get fed into the subsequent upload handlers' "
"``receive_data_chunk`` methods. In this way, one handler can be a \"filter\" "
"for other handlers."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear na sonraí a chuireann tú ar ais isteach sna modhanna "
"``receive_data_chunk ``láimhseálaithe uaslódála ina dhiaidh sin. Ar an "
"mbealach seo, is féidir le láimhseálaí amháin a bheith ina “scagaire” do "
"láimhseálaithe eile."

msgid ""
"Return ``None`` from ``receive_data_chunk`` to short-circuit remaining "
"upload handlers from getting this chunk. This is useful if you're storing "
"the uploaded data yourself and don't want future handlers to store a copy of "
"the data."
msgstr ""
"Fill ``None`` ó `receive_data_chunk`` chuig láimhseálaithe uaslódála "
"gearrchiorcad atá fágtha ó an píosa seo a fháil. Tá sé seo úsáideach má tá "
"na sonraí uaslódáilte á stóráil agat féin agus mura dteastaíonn uait go "
"ndéanfaidh láimhseálaithe sa todhchaí cóip de na sonraí a"

msgid ""
"If you raise a ``StopUpload`` or a ``SkipFile`` exception, the upload will "
"abort or the file will be completely skipped."
msgstr ""
"Má ardaíonn tú eisceacht ``StopUpload`` nó `Skipfile``, cuirfear deireadh "
"leis an uaslódáil nó scipeánfar an comhad go hiomlán."

msgid "Called when a file has finished uploading."
msgstr "Glaoigh nuair a bheidh comhad críochnaithe ag uaslódáil."

msgid ""
"The handler should return an ``UploadedFile`` object that will be stored in "
"``request.FILES``. Handlers may also return ``None`` to indicate that the "
"``UploadedFile`` object should come from subsequent upload handlers."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir don láimhseálaí réad ``uploadedFile`` a chur ar ais a stóráilfear "
"in ``Request.Files``. Féadfaidh láimhseálaithe ``None ``a thabhairt ar ais "
"freisin chun a léiriú gur chóir go dtiocfadh an réad ``Uploadedfile`` ó "
"láimhseálaithe uaslódála ina dhiaidh sin."

msgid "Optional methods"
msgstr "Modhanna roghnacha"

msgid ""
"Custom upload handlers may also define any of the following optional methods "
"or attributes:"
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh láimhseálaithe uaslódála saincheaptha aon cheann de na modhanna nó "
"tréithe roghnacha seo a leanas"

msgid ""
"Size, in bytes, of the \"chunks\" Django should store into memory and feed "
"into the handler. That is, this attribute controls the size of chunks fed "
"into ``FileUploadHandler.receive_data_chunk``."
msgstr ""
"Méid, i mbeátaí, de na “píosaí” ba chóir do Django a stóráil i gcuimhne agus "
"a bheathú isteach sa láimhseálaí. Is é sin, rialaíonn an tréith seo méid na "
"gcodanna a chuirtear isteach i ``FileUploadHandler.Receive_Data_Chunk``."

msgid ""
"For maximum performance the chunk sizes should be divisible by ``4`` and "
"should not exceed 2 GB (2\\ :sup:`31` bytes) in size. When there are "
"multiple chunk sizes provided by multiple handlers, Django will use the "
"smallest chunk size defined by any handler."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh an fheidhmíochta is mó ba chóir go mbeadh méideanna na píosa "
"inroinnte le ``4`` agus níor cheart go mbeadh méid níos mó ná 2 GB "
"(2\\ :sup: `31` bytes). Nuair a bhíonn ilmhéideanna píosa ar fáil ag "
"láimhseálaithe iolracha, úsáidfidh Django an méid píosa is lú a "
"shainmhíníonn aon láimhseálaí."

msgid "The default is 64*2\\ :sup:`10` bytes, or 64 KB."
msgstr "Is é an réamhshocrú 64* 2\\ :sup: `10` bytes, nó 64 KB."

msgid ""
"Callback signaling that a new file upload is starting. This is called before "
"any data has been fed to any upload handlers."
msgstr ""
"Aisghlaonna ag comharthaíocht go bhfuil uaslódáil comhaid nua ag tosú. "
"Tugtar air seo sula gcuirtear aon sonraí a bheathú d'aon láimhseálaithe "
"uaslódála."

msgid "``field_name`` is a string name of the file ``<input>`` field."
msgstr "<input>Is ainm teaghrán é ``field_name`` réimse an chomhaid ```."

msgid "``file_name`` is the filename provided by the browser."
msgstr "Is é ``file_name`` an t-ainm comhaid a sholáthraíonn an brabhsálaí."

msgid ""
"``content_type`` is the MIME type provided by the browser -- E.g. ``'image/"
"jpeg'``."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``content_type`` an cineál MIME a sholáthraíonn an brabhsálaí -- m.sh. "
"````íomha/jpeg'``."

msgid ""
"``content_length`` is the length of the image given by the browser. "
"Sometimes this won't be provided and will be ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Is é `content_length ``fad na híomhá a thugann an brabhsálaí. Uaireanta ní "
"chuirfear é seo ar fáil agus beidh sé “None”."

msgid ""
"``charset`` is the character set (i.e. ``utf8``) given by the browser. Like "
"``content_length``, this sometimes won't be provided."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``charset`` an tacar carachtair (ie ``utf8``) a thugann an brabhsálaí. "
"Cosúil le `content_length ``, ní chuirfear é seo ar fáil uaireanta."

msgid ""
"``content_type_extra`` is extra information about the file from the "
"``content-type`` header. See :attr:`UploadedFile.content_type_extra "
"<django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile.content_type_extra>`."
msgstr ""
"Is faisnéis bhreise é ``content_type_extra`` faoin gcomhad ón gceannteideal "
"``content-type``. "
"<django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile.content_type_extra>Féach: attr: "
"`Uploadedfile.content_type_extra `."

msgid ""
"This method may raise a ``StopFutureHandlers`` exception to prevent future "
"handlers from handling this file."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh an modh seo eisceacht ``StopFutureHandlers `a ardú chun cosc a "
"chur ar láimhseálaithe sa todhchaí an comhad seo a láimhseáil."

msgid "Callback signaling that the entire upload (all files) has completed."
msgstr ""
"Comharthaíonn glaoch ar ais go bhfuil an t-uaslódáil iomlán (gach comhad) "
"críochnaithe."

msgid ""
"Callback signaling that the upload was interrupted, e.g. when the user "
"closed their browser during file upload."
msgstr ""
"Aisghlaonna a chomharthaíonn gur cuireadh isteach ar an uaslódáil, m.sh. "
"nuair a dhún an t-úsáideoir a bhrabhsálaí"

msgid ""
"Allows the handler to completely override the parsing of the raw HTTP input."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé don láimhseálaí parsáil an ionchuir amh HTTP a shárú go hiomlán."

msgid "``input_data`` is a file-like object that supports ``read()``-ing."
msgstr ""
"Is réad cosúil le comhad é ``input_data`` a thacaíonn le ``read () ````-ing."

msgid "``META`` is the same object as ``request.META``."
msgstr "Is é ``META`` an réad céanna le ``request.meta``."

msgid ""
"``content_length`` is the length of the data in ``input_data``. Don't read "
"more than ``content_length`` bytes from ``input_data``."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``content_length ``fad na sonraí in ``input_data``. Ná léigh níos mó ná "
"baite ``content_length ``ó ``input_data``."

msgid "``boundary`` is the MIME boundary for this request."
msgstr "Is é ``teorainne`` an teorainn MIME don iarratas seo."

msgid "``encoding`` is the encoding of the request."
msgstr "Is é “ionchódú” ionchódú an iarratais."

msgid ""
"Return ``None`` if you want upload handling to continue, or a tuple of "
"``(POST, FILES)`` if you want to return the new data structures suitable for "
"the request directly."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair ar ais ``None`` más mian leat leanúint ar aghaidh le láimhseáil "
"uaslódála, nó tuple ``(POST, FILES)`` más mian leat na struchtúir sonraí nua "
"atá oiriúnach don iarraidh a thabhairt ar ais go díreach."

msgid "The Forms API"
msgstr "Na Foirmeacha API"

msgid "About this document"
msgstr "Maidir leis an doiciméad seo"

msgid ""
"This document covers the gritty details of Django's forms API. You should "
"read the :doc:`introduction to working with forms </topics/forms/index>` "
"first."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn an doiciméad seo sonraí crua API foirmeacha Django. Ba chóir "
"duit:doc: `réamhrá ar obair le foirmeacha 'a léamh ar dtús </topics/forms/"
"index>."

msgid "Bound and unbound forms"
msgstr "Foirmeacha ceangailte agus gan cheangal"

msgid ""
"A :class:`Form` instance is either **bound** to a set of data, or "
"**unbound**."
msgstr ""
"A: Aicme: Is é an sampla `Foirme` **teorann** le tacar sonraí, nó **gan "
"teorann**."

msgid ""
"If it's **bound** to a set of data, it's capable of validating that data and "
"rendering the form as HTML with the data displayed in the HTML."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé **teorann** le tacar sonraí, tá sé in ann na sonraí sin a "
"bhailíochtú agus an fhoirm a léiriú mar HTML leis na sonraí a thaispeántar "
"sa HTML."

msgid ""
"If it's **unbound**, it cannot do validation (because there's no data to "
"validate!), but it can still render the blank form as HTML."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé**gan teorann**, ní féidir leis bailíochtú a dhéanamh (toisc nach "
"bhfuil aon sonraí le bailíochtú!) , ach is féidir leis an bhfoirm bán a "
"rinneadh mar HTML fós."

msgid "To create an unbound :class:`Form` instance, instantiate the class:"
msgstr ""
"Chun sampla untheor:class: `Form` a chruthú, déan an rang a chur isteach:"

msgid ""
"To bind data to a form, pass the data as a dictionary as the first parameter "
"to your :class:`Form` class constructor:"
msgstr ""
"Chun sonraí a cheangal le foirm, cuir na sonraí mar fhoclóir mar an chéad "
"pharaiméadar chuig do thógálaí aicme:class: `Form`:"

msgid ""
"In this dictionary, the keys are the field names, which correspond to the "
"attributes in your :class:`Form` class. The values are the data you're "
"trying to validate. These will usually be strings, but there's no "
"requirement that they be strings; the type of data you pass depends on "
"the :class:`Field`, as we'll see in a moment."
msgstr ""
"Sa bhfoclóir seo, is iad na heochracha na hainmneacha réimse, a fhreagraíonn "
"do na tréithe i d'aicme:class: `Form`. Is iad na luachanna na sonraí atá tú "
"ag iarraidh a bhailíochtú. Is teaghráin iad seo de ghnáth, ach níl aon "
"cheanglas ann gur teaghráin iad; braitheann an cineál sonraí a chuireann tú "
"ar: aicme: `Field`, mar a fheicfimid i gceann nóiméad."

msgid ""
"If you need to distinguish between bound and unbound form instances at "
"runtime, check the value of the form's :attr:`~Form.is_bound` attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir cásanna foirme ceangailte agus "
"neamhcheangailte ag an am rith, seiceáil luach na tréithe foirme's:attr: "
"`~form.is_bound`:"

msgid ""
"Note that passing an empty dictionary creates a *bound* form with empty data:"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcruthaíonn foirm*teorann* le sonraí folamh a rith le "
"foclóir folamh:"

msgid ""
"If you have a bound :class:`Form` instance and want to change the data "
"somehow, or if you want to bind an unbound :class:`Form` instance to some "
"data, create another :class:`Form` instance. There is no way to change data "
"in a :class:`Form` instance. Once a :class:`Form` instance has been created, "
"you should consider its data immutable, whether it has data or not."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sampla teorain:class: `Form` agat agus má theastaíonn uait na sonraí a "
"athrú ar bhealach éigin, nó más mian leat sampla untheor:class: `Form` a "
"cheangal le roinnt sonraí, cruthaigh sampla eile: class: `Form`. Níl aon "
"bhealach ann chun sonraí a athrú i gcás a:class: `Form`. Nuair a cruthaíodh "
"a: aicme: `Form` sampla, ba cheart duit a shonraí a mheas gan athrú, cibé "
"acu tá sonraí aige nó nach bhfuil."

msgid "Using forms to validate data"
msgstr "Foirmeacha a úsáid chun sonraí a bhailíochtú"

msgid ""
"Implement a ``clean()`` method on your ``Form`` when you must add custom "
"validation for fields that are interdependent. See :ref:`validating-fields-"
"with-clean` for example usage."
msgstr ""
"Cuir modh ``glan () `i bhfeidhm ar do ``Foirm ``nuair a chaithfidh tú "
"bailíochtú saincheaptha a chur le haghaidh réimsí atá idirspleáchach. Féach: "
"ref: `validating-fields-with-glan `mar shampla úsáid."

msgid ""
"The primary task of a :class:`Form` object is to validate data. With a "
"bound :class:`Form` instance, call the :meth:`~Form.is_valid` method to run "
"validation and return a boolean designating whether the data was valid:"
msgstr ""
"Is é príomhthasc a: aicme: `Form` ná sonraí a bhailíochtú. Le sampla "
"teorain:class: `Form`, glaoigh ar an modh:meth: `~form.is_valid` chun "
"bailíochtú a reáchtáil agus boolean a thabhairt ar ais ag ainmniú an raibh "
"na sonraí bailí:"

msgid ""
"Let's try with some invalid data. In this case, ``subject`` is blank (an "
"error, because all fields are required by default) and ``sender`` is not a "
"valid email address:"
msgstr ""
"Déanaimis iarracht le roinnt sonraí neamhbhailí. Sa chás seo, tá ``ábhar "
"``bán (earráid, toisc go bhfuil gach réimse riachtanach de réir "
"réamhshocraithe) agus ní seoladh ríomhphoist bailí é ``seoltó`:"

msgid ""
"Access the :attr:`~Form.errors` attribute to get a dictionary of error "
"messages:"
msgstr ""
"Rochtain ar thréith :attr: `~form.errors` chun foclóir teachtaireachtaí "
"earráide a fháil:"

msgid ""
"In this dictionary, the keys are the field names, and the values are lists "
"of strings representing the error messages. The error messages are stored in "
"lists because a field can have multiple error messages."
msgstr ""
"Sa fhoclóir seo, is iad na heochracha na hainmneacha réimse, agus is liostaí "
"teaghráin iad na luachanna a léiríonn na teachtaireachtaí earráide. "
"Stóráiltear na teachtaireachtaí earráide i liostaí toisc go bhféadfadh "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide iliomad a bheith"

msgid ""
"You can access :attr:`~Form.errors` without having to "
"call :meth:`~Form.is_valid` first. The form's data will be validated the "
"first time either you call :meth:`~Form.is_valid` or "
"access :attr:`~Form.errors`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar: attr: `~form.errors` gan glaoch ar: "
"meth: `~form.is_valid` ar dtús. Déanfar sonraí na foirme a bhailíochtú an "
"chéad uair a ghlaonn tú ar: meth: `~form.is_valid` nó access:attr: "
"`~form.errors`."

msgid ""
"The validation routines will only get called once, regardless of how many "
"times you access :attr:`~Form.errors` or call :meth:`~Form.is_valid`. This "
"means that if validation has side effects, those side effects will only be "
"triggered once."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlaofar ar na gnáthaimh bailíochtaithe ach uair amháin, is cuma cé mhéad "
"uair a rochtain agat ar: attr: `~form.errors` nó glao:meth: "
"`~form.is_valid`. Ciallaíonn sé seo má tá fo-iarsmaí ag bailíochtú, ní "
"spreagfar na fo-iarsmaí sin ach uair amháin."

msgid ""
"Returns a ``dict`` that maps fields to their original ``ValidationError`` "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann ``dict`` ar ais a léarscáil réimsí chuig a gcásanna bunaidh "
"``ValidationError``."

msgid ""
"Use this method anytime you need to identify an error by its ``code``. This "
"enables things like rewriting the error's message or writing custom logic in "
"a view when a given error is present. It can also be used to serialize the "
"errors in a custom format (e.g. XML); for "
"instance, :meth:`~Form.errors.as_json()` relies on ``as_data()``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an modh seo am ar bith is gá duit earráid a aithint trína ``cód ``. "
"Cuireann sé seo ar chumas rudaí cosúil le teachtaireacht an earráide a "
"athscríobh nó loighic saincheaptha a scríobh i radharc nuair a bhíonn "
"earráid Is féidir é a úsáid freisin chun na hearráidí a shraitheadh i "
"bhformáid saincheaptha (m.sh. XML); mar shampla,:: meth: "
"`~form.errors.as_json () `ag brath ar ``as_data () ``."

msgid ""
"The need for the ``as_data()`` method is due to backwards compatibility. "
"Previously ``ValidationError`` instances were lost as soon as their "
"**rendered** error messages were added to the ``Form.errors`` dictionary. "
"Ideally ``Form.errors`` would have stored ``ValidationError`` instances and "
"methods with an ``as_`` prefix could render them, but it had to be done the "
"other way around in order not to break code that expects rendered error "
"messages in ``Form.errors``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an gá atá le modh ``as_data () ``mar gheall ar chomhoiriúnacht ar ais. "
"Cailleadh cásanna ``ValidationError`` roimhe seo chomh luath agus a gcuid "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide **a rinneadh leis an bhfoclóir ``Form.errors``. Go "
"hidéalach bheadh `Form.errors`` stóráilte cásanna agus modhanna "
"``ValidationError`` le réimír ``as_`` iad a dhéanamh, ach b'éigean é a "
"dhéanamh ar an mbealach eile d'fhonn gan cód a bhriseadh a bhfuil súil le "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide a rinneadh i `Form.errors``."

msgid "Returns the errors serialized as JSON."
msgstr "Filleann sé na hearráidí a shraitheadh mar JSON."

msgid ""
"By default, ``as_json()`` does not escape its output. If you are using it "
"for something like AJAX requests to a form view where the client interprets "
"the response and inserts errors into the page, you'll want to be sure to "
"escape the results on the client-side to avoid the possibility of a cross-"
"site scripting attack. You can do this in JavaScript with "
"``element.textContent = errorText`` or with jQuery's ``$"
"(el).text(errorText)`` (rather than its ``.html()`` function)."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní éalaíonn ``as_json () ``a aschur. Má tá tú á "
"úsáid le haghaidh rud éigin cosúil le hiarratais AJAX chuig amharc foirme "
"ina ndéanann an cliant an freagra a léirmhíniú agus earráidí isteach sa "
"leathanach, beidh tú ag iarraidh a bheith cinnte go n-éalóidh tú na torthaí "
"ar thaobh an chliaint chun an fhéidearthacht ionsaí scripteála tras-"
"láithreáin a sheachaint. Is féidir leat é seo a dhéanamh i JavaScript le "
"``Element.textContent = ErrorText`` nó le ``$ (el) .text (ErrorText) "
"``jQuery (seachas a fheidhm ``.html ()``)."

msgid ""
"If for some reason you don't want to use client-side escaping, you can also "
"set ``escape_html=True`` and error messages will be escaped so you can use "
"them directly in HTML."
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait éalú taobh an chliaint a úsáid ar chúis éigin, is "
"féidir leat ``escape_html = true`` a shocrú freisin agus éalófar "
"teachtaireachtaí earráide ionas gur féidir leat iad a úsáid go díreach i "
"HTML."

msgid ""
"Returns the errors as a dictionary suitable for serializing to "
"JSON. :meth:`Form.errors.as_json()` returns serialized JSON, while this "
"returns the error data before it's serialized."
msgstr ""
"Tugann na hearráidí ar ais mar fhoclóir atá oiriúnach le sraitheadh chuig "
"JSON. :meth: `Form.errors.as_json () `filleann JSON sraitheach, agus "
"filleann sé seo na sonraí earráide ar ais sula ndéantar iad a shraitheadh."

msgid ""
"The ``escape_html`` parameter behaves as described "
"in :meth:`Form.errors.as_json()`."
msgstr ""
"Iompraíonn an paraiméadar ``escape_html`` mar a thuairiscítear in:meth: "
"`Form.errors.as_json () `."

msgid ""
"This method allows adding errors to specific fields from within the "
"``Form.clean()`` method, or from outside the form altogether; for instance "
"from a view."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an modh seo earráidí a chur le réimsí ar leith ón modh ``Form.clean "
"() `, nó ón taobh amuigh den fhoirm ar fad; mar shampla ó radharc."

msgid ""
"The ``field`` argument is the name of the field to which the errors should "
"be added. If its value is ``None`` the error will be treated as a non-field "
"error as returned by :meth:`Form.non_field_errors() "
"<django.forms.Form.non_field_errors>`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an argóint ``réimse`` ainm an réimse ar chóir na hearráidí a chur leis. "
"<django.forms.Form.non_field_errors>Más é a luach ``None``, déileálfar leis "
"an earráid mar earráid neamh-réimse mar a d'fhaigh:meth: "
"`form.non_field_errors () `."

msgid ""
"The ``error`` argument can be a string, or preferably an instance of "
"``ValidationError``. See :ref:`raising-validation-error` for best practices "
"when defining form errors."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an argóint ``earráid`` a bheith ina shreang, nó b'fhéidir mar "
"shampla de ``ValidationError``. Féach:ref: `earrá-bhailíochtai-earráid` le "
"haghaidh dea-chleachtais agus earráidí foirme á sainmhíniú."

msgid ""
"Note that ``Form.add_error()`` automatically removes the relevant field from "
"``cleaned_data``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go mbaineann ``form.add_error () ``an réimse ábhartha go "
"huathoibríoch ó ``cleaned_data``."

msgid ""
"This method returns a boolean designating whether a field has an error with "
"a specific error ``code``. If ``code`` is ``None``, it will return ``True`` "
"if the field contains any errors at all."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh seo boolean ar ais ag ainmniú an bhfuil earráid i réimse le "
"earráid sonrach ``cód ``. Más é ```Cód ```None``, fillfidh sé ``True`` má tá "
"aon earráidí sa réimse ar chor ar bith."

msgid ""
"To check for non-field errors "
"use :data:`~django.core.exceptions.NON_FIELD_ERRORS` as the ``field`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Chun seiceáil le haghaidh earráidí neamh-réimse bain úsáid as: data: "
"`~django.core.EXCEPTIONS.NON_FIELD_ERRORS` mar an paraiméadar ``field``."

msgid ""
"This method returns the list of errors from :attr:`Form.errors "
"<django.forms.Form.errors>`  that aren't associated with a particular field. "
"This includes ``ValidationError``\\s that are raised in :meth:`Form.clean() "
"<django.forms.Form.clean>` and errors added "
"using :meth:`Form.add_error(None, \"...\") <django.forms.Form.add_error>`."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an modh seo an liosta earráidí ó:attr: `Form.errors "
"<django.forms.Form.errors>`nach bhfuil baint acu le réimse áirithe. Áirítear "
"leis seo ``ValidationError``\\ s a ardaítear in:meth: `Form.clean () `agus "
"earráidí curtha leis ag baint úsáid:meth: `Form.add_error (None, "
"<django.forms.Form.clean>“...”) <django.forms.Form.add_error>`."

msgid "Behavior of unbound forms"
msgstr "Iompar foirmeacha neamhcheangailte"

msgid ""
"It's meaningless to validate a form with no data, but, for the record, "
"here's what happens with unbound forms:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé gan chiall foirm a bhailíochtú gan aon sonraí, ach, chun an taifead, "
"seo cad a tharlaíonn le foirmeacha neamhcheangailte:"

msgid "Initial form values"
msgstr "Luachanna foirme tosaigh"

msgid ""
"Use :attr:`~Form.initial` to declare the initial value of form fields at "
"runtime. For example, you might want to fill in a ``username`` field with "
"the username of the current session."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid: Attr: `~Form.Initial` chun luach tosaigh réimsí foirme a dhearbhú ag "
"an am rith. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat réimse ``ainm úsáideora "
"``a líonadh isteach le hainm úsáideora an tseisiúin reatha."

msgid ""
"To accomplish this, use the :attr:`~Form.initial` argument to "
"a :class:`Form`. This argument, if given, should be a dictionary mapping "
"field names to initial values. Only include the fields for which you're "
"specifying an initial value; it's not necessary to include every field in "
"your form. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a chur i gcrích, bain úsáid as an argóint:attr: `~form.initial` "
"chuig a:class: `Form`. Ba chóir go mbeadh an argóint seo, má thugtar, ina "
"fhoclóir a mhapáil ainmneacha réimse go luachanna Cuir san áireamh ach na "
"réimsí a bhfuil luach tosaigh á shonrú agat dóibh; ní gá gach réimse a "
"áireamh i d'fhoirm. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"These values are only displayed for unbound forms, and they're not used as "
"fallback values if a particular value isn't provided."
msgstr ""
"Ní thaispeántar na luachanna seo ach le haghaidh foirmeacha "
"neamhcheangailte, agus ní úsáidtear iad mar luachanna cúltaca mura gcuirtear "
"luach ar leith ar fáil."

msgid ""
"If a :class:`~django.forms.Field` defines :attr:`~Field.initial` *and* you "
"include :attr:`~Form.initial` when instantiating the ``Form``, then the "
"latter ``initial`` will have precedence. In this example, ``initial`` is "
"provided both at the field level and at the form instance level, and the "
"latter gets precedence:"
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhíníonn a:class: `~django.forms.field`: attr: `~Field.Initial` "
"*agus* san áireamh tuat:attr: `~form.initial` agus an `Form`` á gcur isteach "
"agat, ansin beidh tosaíocht ag an deireanach ``initial``. Sa sampla seo, "
"soláthraítear ``tosaithe`` ag leibhéal an réimse agus ag leibhéal na foirme "
"araon, agus faigheann an dara ceann tosaíocht:"

msgid ""
"Returns the initial data for a form field. It retrieves the data "
"from :attr:`Form.initial` if present, otherwise "
"trying :attr:`Field.initial`. Callable values are evaluated."
msgstr ""
"Tugann na sonraí tosaigh ar ais do réimse foirme. Aisghabhann sé na sonraí "
"ó:attr: `Form.initial` má tá sé i láthair, ar shlí eile iarracht: attr: "
"`Field.initial`. Déantar luachanna inghlaonta a mheas."

msgid ""
"It is recommended to use :attr:`BoundField.initial` "
"over :meth:`~Form.get_initial_for_field()` because ``BoundField.initial`` "
"has a simpler interface. Also, "
"unlike :meth:`~Form.get_initial_for_field()`, :attr:`BoundField.initial` "
"caches its values. This is useful especially when dealing with callables "
"whose return values can change (e.g. ``datetime.now`` or ``uuid.uuid4``):"
msgstr ""
"Moltar úsáid: attr: `BoundField.Initial` thar: meth: "
"`~form.get_initial_for_field () `toisc go bhfuil comhéadan níos simplí ag "
"``BoundField.initial``. Chomh maith leis sin, dícheanglaíonn: meth: "
"`~form.get_initial_for_field () `, :attr: `BoundField.Initial` a luachanna a "
"choscáin. Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe agus tú ag déileáil le glaonna a "
"bhféadann a luachanna tuairisceáin athrú (m.sh. `datetime.now`` nó "
"``uuid.uuid4``):"

msgid "Checking which form data has changed"
msgstr "Seiceáil cén fhoirm sonraí atá athraithe"

msgid ""
"Use the ``has_changed()`` method on your ``Form`` when you need to check if "
"the form data has been changed from the initial data."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an modh ``has_changed () ``ar do `Foirm`` nuair is gá duit a sheiceáil "
"an bhfuil sonraí na foirme athraithe ó na sonraí tosaigh."

msgid ""
"When the form is submitted, we reconstruct it and provide the original data "
"so that the comparison can be done:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuirtear an fhoirm isteach, déanaimid í a athchógáil agus "
"soláthraímid na sonraí bunaidh ionas gur féidir an comparáid a dhéanamh:"

msgid ""
"``has_changed()`` will be ``True`` if the data from ``request.POST`` differs "
"from what was provided in :attr:`~Form.initial` or ``False`` otherwise. The "
"result is computed by calling :meth:`Field.has_changed` for each field in "
"the form."
msgstr ""
"Beidh ``has_modified () ``True`` má tá na sonraí ó `Request.post`` difriúil "
"ón méid a cuireadh ar fáil in:attr: `~form.initial` nó ``False`` ar shlí "
"eile. Déantar an toradh a ríomh trí ghlaoch: meth: `field.has_changed` do "
"gach réimse san fhoirm."

msgid ""
"The ``changed_data`` attribute returns a list of the names of the fields "
"whose values in the form's bound data (usually ``request.POST``) differ from "
"what was provided in :attr:`~Form.initial`. It returns an empty list if no "
"data differs."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an tréith ``changed_data`` liosta d'ainmneacha na réimsí a bhfuil a "
"luachanna i sonraí ceangailte na foirme (`request.post`` de ghnáth) difriúil "
"ón méid a cuireadh ar fáil in:attr: `~form.initial`. Tugann sé liosta folamh "
"ar ais mura bhfuil aon sonraí difriúil."

msgid "Accessing the fields from the form"
msgstr "Rochtain a fháil ar na réimsí ón bhfoirm"

msgid ""
"You can access the fields of :class:`Form` instance from its ``fields`` "
"attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar na réimsí de:class: `Form` ón tréith "
"``fields``:"

msgid ""
"You can alter the field and :class:`.BoundField` of :class:`Form` instance "
"to change the way it is presented in the form:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an réimse agus:class: `.BoundField` den sampla: Class: `Form` "
"a athrú chun an bealach a chuirtear i láthair sa fhoirm a athrú:"

msgid ""
"Beware not to alter the ``base_fields`` attribute because this modification "
"will influence all subsequent ``ContactForm`` instances within the same "
"Python process:"
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach gan an tréith ``base_fields`` a athrú toisc go mbeidh tionchar "
"ag an modhnú seo ar gach cás ``ContactForm ``ina dhiaidh sin laistigh den "
"phróiseas Python céanna:"

msgid "Accessing \"clean\" data"
msgstr "Rochtain a fháil ar shonraí “glan”"

msgid ""
"Each field in a :class:`Form` class is responsible not only for validating "
"data, but also for \"cleaning\" it -- normalizing it to a consistent format. "
"This is a nice feature, because it allows data for a particular field to be "
"input in a variety of ways, always resulting in consistent output."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach réimse i rang a: “Foirm” freagrach ní amháin as sonraí a "
"bhailíochtú, ach freisin as iad a “ghlanadh” - iad a normalú go formáid "
"chomhsheasmhach. Is gné deas í seo, toisc go gceadaíonn sé sonraí do réimse "
"áirithe a ionchur ar bhealaí éagsúla, agus aschur comhsheasmhach mar thoradh "
"air i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"For example, :class:`~django.forms.DateField` normalizes input into a Python "
"``datetime.date`` object. Regardless of whether you pass it a string in the "
"format ``'1994-07-15'``, a ``datetime.date`` object, or a number of other "
"formats, ``DateField`` will always normalize it to a ``datetime.date`` "
"object as long as it's valid."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, normalaíonn :class: `~django.forms.dateField` ionchur isteach i "
"réad Python ``datetime.date``. Is cuma má chuireann tú sreang air san "
"fhormáid ``'1994-07-15'`, réad ``datetime.date ``, nó roinnt formáidí eile, "
"normalóidh ``DateField`` é i gcónaí go réad ``datetime.`date` fad is atá sé "
"bailí."

msgid ""
"Once you've created a :class:`~Form` instance with a set of data and "
"validated it, you can access the clean data via its ``cleaned_data`` "
"attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh sampla a:class: `~Form cruthaithe agat le sraith sonraí agus "
"é a bhailíochtú, is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar na sonraí glan trína "
"tréith ``cleaned_data``:"

msgid ""
"Note that any text-based field -- such as ``CharField`` or ``EmailField`` -- "
"always cleans the input into a string. We'll cover the encoding implications "
"later in this document."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go nglanann aon réimse téacs-bhunaithe - mar "
"``Charfield`` nó ``Emailfield`` - an t-ionchur i sreang i gcónaí. Clúdóimid "
"na himpleachtaí ionchódú níos déanaí sa doiciméad seo."

msgid ""
"If your data does *not* validate, the ``cleaned_data`` dictionary contains "
"only the valid fields:"
msgstr ""
"Mura ndéantar do chuid sonraí a bhailíochtú, níl ach na réimsí bailí sa "
"fhoclóir ``cleaned_data ``:"

msgid ""
"``cleaned_data`` will always *only* contain a key for fields defined in the "
"``Form``, even if you pass extra data when you define the ``Form``. In this "
"example, we pass a bunch of extra fields to the ``ContactForm`` constructor, "
"but ``cleaned_data`` contains only the form's fields:"
msgstr ""
"Beidh eochair le haghaidh réimsí a shainmhínítear sa ``Foirm`` i gcónaí* sa "
"`cleaned_data``, fiú má chuireann tú sonraí breise nuair a shainmhíníonn tú "
"an ``Foirm``. Sa sampla seo, cuirimid dornán réimsí breise chuig an tógálaí "
"`ContactForm ``, ach níl ach réimsí na foirme sa `cleaned_data``:"

msgid ""
"When the ``Form`` is valid, ``cleaned_data`` will include a key and value "
"for *all* its fields, even if the data didn't include a value for some "
"optional fields. In this example, the data dictionary doesn't include a "
"value for the ``nick_name`` field, but ``cleaned_data`` includes it, with an "
"empty value:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh an `Foirm`` bailí, cuimsíonn ``cleaned_data`` eochair agus "
"luach d'*all* a réimsí, fiú mura raibh luach san áireamh sna sonraí do "
"roinnt réimsí roghnacha. Sa sampla seo, ní chuimsíonn an foclóir sonraí "
"luach don réimse ``nick_name``, ach cuimsíonn ``cleaned_data ``é, le luach "
"folamh:"

msgid ""
"In this above example, the ``cleaned_data`` value for ``nick_name`` is set "
"to an empty string, because ``nick_name`` is ``CharField``, and "
"``CharField``\\s treat empty values as an empty string. Each field type "
"knows what its \"blank\" value is -- e.g., for ``DateField``, it's ``None`` "
"instead of the empty string. For full details on each field's behavior in "
"this case, see the \"Empty value\" note for each field in the :ref:`built-in-"
"fields` section below."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can write code to perform validation for particular form fields (based "
"on their name) or for the form as a whole (considering combinations of "
"various fields). More information about this is in :doc:`/ref/forms/"
"validation`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cód a scríobh chun bailíochtú a dhéanamh do réimsí foirme "
"áirithe (bunaithe ar a n-ainm) nó don fhoirm ina iomláine (ag smaoineamh ar "
"theaglaim de réimsí éagsúla). Tá tuilleadh faisnéise faoi seo in:doc: `/ref/"
"forms/validation`."

msgid "Outputting forms as HTML"
msgstr "Foirmeacha a chur amach mar HTML"

msgid ""
"The second task of a ``Form`` object is to render itself as HTML. To do so, "
"``print`` it:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara tasc atá ag réad ``Foirm`` é féin a rinneadh mar HTML. Chun é "
"sin a dhéanamh, ``print`` é:"

msgid ""
"If the form is bound to data, the HTML output will include that data "
"appropriately. For example, if a field is represented by an ``<input "
"type=\"text\">``, the data will be in the ``value`` attribute. If a field is "
"represented by an ``<input type=\"checkbox\">``, then that HTML will include "
"``checked`` if appropriate:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an fhoirm ceangailte le sonraí, cuirfear na sonraí sin san áireamh go "
"cuí san aschur HTML. Mar shampla, má léirítear réimse le ``<input "
"type=\"text\">``, beidh na sonraí sa tréith ``luach``. Má léirítear réimse "
"le ```, ansin cuir <input type=\"checkbox\">fidh an HTML sin ``seiceáil`` "
"más cuí:"

msgid ""
"This default output wraps each field with a ``<div>``. Notice the following:"
msgstr ""
"<div>Cumhdaíonn an t-aschur réamhshocraithe seo gach réimse le ```. Tabhair "
"faoi deara a leanas:"

msgid ""
"For flexibility, the output does *not* include the ``<form>`` and ``</"
"form>`` tags or an ``<input type=\"submit\">`` tag. It's your job to do that."
msgstr ""
"<input type=\"submit\">Maidir le solúbthacht, ní chuimsíonn an aschuir* na "
"clibeanna ```` <form>agus ```` ``nó clib</form>`` ``. Is é do phost é sin a "
"dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"Each field type has a default HTML representation. ``CharField`` is "
"represented by an ``<input type=\"text\">`` and ``EmailField`` by an "
"``<input type=\"email\">``. ``BooleanField(null=False)`` is represented by "
"an ``<input type=\"checkbox\">``. Note these are merely sensible defaults; "
"you can specify which HTML to use for a given field by using widgets, which "
"we'll explain shortly."
msgstr ""
"Tá ionadaíocht HTML réamhshocraithe ag gach cineál réimse. <input "
"type=\"email\">Léirítear ``charfield`` le ```` ``agus ``Ríomhphost`` le`` "
"```` ```` ```` ```` ````` ```` ```` <input type=\"text\">```` <input "
"type=\"checkbox\">Léirítear ```BooleanField (Null=bréagach) ``le`` ``. "
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil siad seo ach réamhshocruithe ciallmhara; is "
"féidir leat a shonrú cén HTML atá le húsáid do réimse ar leith trí "
"ghuirléidí a úsáid, a mhíneoimid go luath."

msgid ""
"The HTML ``name`` for each tag is taken directly from its attribute name in "
"the ``ContactForm`` class."
msgstr ""
"Tógtar an ``ainm ``HTML do gach clib go díreach óna ainm tréithe sa rang "
"``Contactform``."

msgid ""
"The text label for each field -- e.g. ``'Subject:'``, ``'Message:'`` and "
"``'Cc myself:'`` is generated from the field name by converting all "
"underscores to spaces and upper-casing the first letter. Again, note these "
"are merely sensible defaults; you can also specify labels manually."
msgstr ""
"Gintear an lipéad téacs do gach réimse - m.sh. ```'Ábhar: '``, "
"``'Teachtaireacht:'`` agus ```Cc mé féin:`` ``, Gintear ó ainm an réimse trí "
"gach béim a thiontú go spásanna agus an chéad litir a chosú uachtarach. "
"Arís, tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil siad seo ach réamhshocruithe ciallmhar; "
"is féidir leat lipéid a shonrú de láimh freisin."

msgid ""
"Each text label is surrounded in an HTML ``<label>`` tag, which points to "
"the appropriate form field via its ``id``. Its ``id``, in turn, is generated "
"by prepending ``'id_'`` to the field name. The ``id`` attributes and "
"``<label>`` tags are included in the output by default, to follow best "
"practices, but you can change that behavior."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach lipéad téacs timpeallaithe i gclib HTML ``<label>``, a chuireann in "
"iúl don réimse foirme iomchuí trína `id ``. Gintear a `id``, ina dhiaidh "
"sin, trí ``id_'`` a réamhfheidhmiú chuig ainm an réimse. Cuirtear na tréithe "
"`id`` agus na clibeanna ``<label>`` san áireamh san aschur de réir "
"réamhshocraithe, chun dea-chleachtais a leanúint, ach is féidir leat an t-"
"iompar sin a athrú."

msgid ""
"The output uses HTML5 syntax, targeting ``<!DOCTYPE html>``. For example, it "
"uses boolean attributes such as ``checked`` rather than the XHTML style of "
"``checked='checked'``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an t-aschur comhréir HTML5, ag díriú ar ``<DOCTYPE html>``. Mar "
"shampla, úsáideann sé tréithe boolean mar ``checked`` seachas an stíl XHTML "
"de ``checked='checked'`."

msgid ""
"Although ``<div>`` output is the default output style when you ``print`` a "
"form you can customize the output by using your own form template which can "
"be set site-wide, per-form, or per-instance. See :ref:`reusable-form-"
"templates`."
msgstr ""
"Cé gurb é as <div>chur ```an stíl aschuir réamhshocraithe nuair a dhéanann "
"tú foirm`` a phriontáil ``is féidir leat an t-aschur a shaincheapadh trí do "
"theimpléad foirme féin a úsáid ar féidir a shocrú ar fud an láithreáin, in "
"aghaidh foirme, nó in aghaidh na sampla. Féach:ref: `teimpléid foirm-"
"athúsáid'."

msgid "Default rendering"
msgstr "Rindreáil réamhshocrai"

msgid ""
"The default rendering when you ``print`` a form uses the following methods "
"and attributes."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an rindreáil réamhshocraithe nuair a dhéanann tú foirm “priontáil” "
"na modhanna agus na tréithe seo a leanas."

msgid "``template_name``"
msgstr "``ainmne_teimpléad``"

msgid ""
"The name of the template rendered if the form is cast into a string, e.g. "
"via ``print(form)`` or in a template via ``{{ form }}``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid a rinneadh má theilgtear an fhoirm isteach i sreang, m.sh. "
"trí ``priontáil (foirm) ``nó i dteimpléad trí`` {{form}} ``."

msgid ""
"By default, a property returning the value of the "
"renderer's :attr:`~django.forms.renderers.BaseRenderer.form_template_name`. "
"You may set it as a string template name in order to override that for a "
"particular form class."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, maoin ag filleadh luach an renderer's:attr: "
"`~django.forms.renderers.baserenderer.form_template_name`. Féadfaidh tú é a "
"shocrú mar ainm teimpléad teaghrán d'fhonn é sin a shárú d'aicme foirme "
"áirithe."

msgid "``render()``"
msgstr "``render () ``"

msgid ""
"The render method is called by ``__str__`` as well as "
"the :meth:`.Form.as_div`, :meth:`.Form.as_table`, :meth:`.Form.as_p`, "
"and :meth:`.Form.as_ul` methods. All arguments are optional and default to:"
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ``__str__`` ar an modh rindreála chomh maith leis na:meth: "
"`.form.as_div`, :meth: `.form.as_table`, :meth: `.form.as_p`, agus:meth: "
"`.form.as_ul` modhanna. Tá gach argóint roghnach agus réamhshocraithe:"

msgid "``template_name``: :attr:`.Form.template_name`"
