"glaóidh sé, ina dhiaidh sin, na modhanna saincheaptha ``to_python () ``agus "
"``validate ()``."

msgid "Cleaning a specific field attribute"
msgstr "Glanadh tréith réimse ar leith"

msgid ""
"Continuing on from the previous example, suppose that in our "
"``ContactForm``, we want to make sure that the ``recipients`` field always "
"contains the address ``\"fred@example.com\"``. This is validation that is "
"specific to our form, so we don't want to put it into the general "
"``MultiEmailField`` class. Instead, we write a cleaning method that operates "
"on the ``recipients`` field, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Ag leanúint ar aghaidh ón sampla roimhe seo, cuir i gcás gur mhaith linn a "
"chinntiú go bhfuil an seoladh ``” fred@example.com “`` sa réimse "
"``faighteoirí ``i gcónaí. Is bailíochtú é seo atá sonrach dár bhfoirm, mar "
"sin níl muid ag iarraidh é a chur isteach sa rang ginearálta "
"``Multiemailfield`. Ina áit sin, scríobhaimid modh glantacháin a oibríonn ar "
"an réimse ``faighteoirí ``, mar sin:"

msgid "Cleaning and validating fields that depend on each other"
msgstr "Réimsí a ghlanadh agus a bhailíochtú atá ag brath ar a chéile"

msgid ""
"Suppose we add another requirement to our contact form: if the ``cc_myself`` "
"field is ``True``, the ``subject`` must contain the word ``\"help\"``. We "
"are performing validation on more than one field at a time, so the "
"form's :meth:`~Form.clean()` method is a good spot to do this. Notice that "
"we are talking about the ``clean()`` method on the form here, whereas "
"earlier we were writing a ``clean()`` method on a field. It's important to "
"keep the field and form difference clear when working out where to validate "
"things. Fields are single data points, forms are a collection of fields."
msgstr ""
"Cuirimid riachtanas eile lenár bhfoirm teagmhála: más é “Fíor” sa réimse "
"`cc_myself``, ní mór go mbeadh an focal ``\"cabhrach\"` sa `ábhar ``. Táimid "
"ag déanamh bailíochtaithe ar níos mó ná réimse amháin ag an am, mar sin is "
"áit mhaith é an modh foirm: meth: `~form.clean () `chun é seo a dhéanamh. "
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuilimid ag caint faoin modh ``clean () ``ar an "
"bhfoirm anseo, ach níos luaithe bhí modh ``clean ()`` á scríobh againn ar "
"réimse. Tá sé tábhachtach an réimse agus an difríocht foirme a choinneáil "
"soiléir agus tú ag obair amach cá háit le rudaí a bhail Is pointí sonraí "
"aonair iad réimsí, is bailiúchán réimsí iad foirmeacha."

msgid ""
"By the time the form's ``clean()`` method is called, all the individual "
"field clean methods will have been run (the previous two sections), so "
"``self.cleaned_data`` will be populated with any data that has survived so "
"far. So you also need to remember to allow for the fact that the fields you "
"are wanting to validate might not have survived the initial individual field "
"checks."
msgstr ""
"Faoin am a dtugtar modh ``clean () ``ar an bhfoirm, beidh na modhanna glan "
"réimse aonair go léir á reáchtáil (an dá chuid roimhe seo), mar sin déanfar "
"``self.cleaned_data`` daonra le haon sonraí a tháinig maireachtáil go dtí "
"seo. Mar sin ní mór duit cuimhneamh freisin a cheadú go mb'fhéidir nár mhair "
"na réimsí atá tú ag iarraidh a bhailíochtú sna seiceálacha réimse aonair "
"tosaigh."

msgid ""
"There are two ways to report any errors from this step. Probably the most "
"common method is to display the error at the top of the form. To create such "
"an error, you can raise a ``ValidationError`` from the ``clean()`` method. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá bhealach ann chun aon earráidí ón gcéim seo a thuairisciú. Is dócha "
"gurb é an modh is coitianta an earráid a thaispeáint ag barr na foirme. Chun "
"earráid den sórt sin a chruthú, is féidir leat ``ValidationError`` a ardú ón "
"modh ``clean () ``. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"In this code, if the validation error is raised, the form will display an "
"error message at the top of the form (normally) describing the problem. Such "
"errors are non-field errors, which are displayed in the template with "
"``{{ form.non_field_errors }}``."
msgstr ""
"Sa chód seo, má ardaítear an earráid bailíochtaithe, taispeánfaidh an fhoirm "
"teachtaireacht earráide ag barr na foirme (de ghnáth) ag cur síos ar an "
"bhfadhb. Is earráidí neamh-réimse iad earráidí den sórt sin, a thaispeántar "
"sa teimpléad le ``{{form.non_field_errors}}``."

msgid ""
"The call to ``super().clean()`` in the example code ensures that any "
"validation logic in parent classes is maintained. If your form inherits "
"another that doesn't return a ``cleaned_data`` dictionary in its ``clean()`` "
"method (doing so is optional), then don't assign ``cleaned_data`` to the "
"result of the ``super()`` call and use ``self.cleaned_data`` instead::"
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn an glao chuig ``super () .clean () ``sa chód samplaí go "
"gcoinnítear aon loighic bailíochtaithe i ranganna tuismitheoirí. Má tá foirm "
"eile ag d'oidhreacht nach gcuireann foclóir ``cleaned_data ``ar ais ina modh "
"``clean ()`` (is roghnach é sin a dhéanamh), ansin ná sannadh "
"``cleaned_data`` do thoradh an ghlaonna ``super () ``agus bain úsáid as "
"``self.cleaned_data`` ina ionad:"

msgid ""
"The second approach for reporting validation errors might involve assigning "
"the error message to one of the fields. In this case, let's assign an error "
"message to both the \"subject\" and \"cc_myself\" rows in the form display. "
"Be careful when doing this in practice, since it can lead to confusing form "
"output. We're showing what is possible here and leaving it up to you and "
"your designers to work out what works effectively in your particular "
"situation. Our new code (replacing the previous sample) looks like this::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh sé go mbeadh an teachtaireacht earráide a shannadh chuig ceann "
"de na réimsí leis an dara cur chuige chun earráidí bailíochtaithe Sa chás "
"seo, déanaimis teachtaireacht earráide a shannadh do na sraitheanna “ábhar” "
"agus “cc_myself” araon sa taispeáint foirme. Bí cúramach agus é seo á "
"dhéanamh go praiticiúil, ós rud é go bhféadfadh aschur foirme mearbhall a "
"bheith mar thoradh Táimid ag taispeáint cad is féidir anseo agus táimid ag "
"fágáil ort féin agus do dhearthóirí é a oibriú amach cad a oibríonn go "
"héifeachtach i do chás áirithe. Tá cuma seo ar ár gcód nua (in ionad an "
"tsampla roimhe seo):"

msgid ""
"The second argument of ``add_error()`` can be a string, or preferably an "
"instance of ``ValidationError``. See :ref:`raising-validation-error` for "
"more details. Note that ``add_error()`` automatically removes the field from "
"``cleaned_data``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an dara argóint de ``add_error () ``a bheith ina shreang, nó "
"b'fhéidir mar shampla de ``ValidationError``. Féach:ref: `raising-validation-"
"error` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí. Tabhair faoi deara go mbaineann "
"``add_error () ``an réimse go huathoibríoch ó ``cleaned_data``."

msgid ""
"A widget is Django's representation of an HTML input element. The widget "
"handles the rendering of the HTML, and the extraction of data from a GET/"
"POST dictionary that corresponds to the widget."
msgstr ""
"Is é giuirléid léiriú Django ar eilimint ionchuir HTML. Láimhseálann an "
"giuirléid rindreáil an HTML, agus eastóscadh sonraí ó fhoclóir GET/POST a "
"fhreagraíonn don ghuirléid."

msgid ""
"The HTML generated by the built-in widgets uses HTML5 syntax, targeting ``<!"
"DOCTYPE html>``. For example, it uses boolean attributes such as ``checked`` "
"rather than the XHTML style of ``checked='checked'``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an HTML a ghineann na giuirléidí ionsuite comhréir HTML5, ag díriú "
"ar ``<DOCTYPE html>``. Mar shampla, úsáideann sé tréithe boolean mar "
"``checked`` seachas an stíl XHTML de ``checked='checked'`."

msgid ""
"Widgets should not be confused with the :doc:`form fields </ref/forms/"
"fields>`. Form fields deal with the logic of input validation and are used "
"directly in templates. Widgets deal with rendering of HTML form input "
"elements on the web page and extraction of raw submitted data. However, "
"widgets do need to be :ref:`assigned <widget-to-field>` to form fields."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir giuirléidí a mheascadh leis na:doc: `réimsí foirmeacha `</ref/"
"forms/fields>. Déileálann réimsí foirme le loighic na bailíochtaithe "
"ionchuir agus úsáidtear iad go díreach i dteimpl Déileálann giuirléidí le "
"rindreáil eilimintí ionchuir foirme HTML ar an leathanach gréasáin agus "
"eastóscadh sonraí amha curtha isteach. Mar sin féin, ní mór go mbeadh "
"giuirléidí: ref: `sannta <widget-to-field>`chun réimsí a fhoirmiú."

