msgid "Special Operations"
msgstr "Oibríochtaí Speisialta"

msgid "``RunSQL``"
msgstr "``Runsql``"

msgid ""
"Allows running of arbitrary SQL on the database - useful for more advanced "
"features of database backends that Django doesn't support directly."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn sé SQL treallach a reáchtáil ar an mbunachar sonraí - úsáideach le "
"haghaidh gnéithe níos airde de chúltaca bunachar sonraí nach dtacaíonn "
"Django go díreach."

msgid ""
"``sql``, and ``reverse_sql`` if provided, should be strings of SQL to run on "
"the database. On most database backends (all but PostgreSQL), Django will "
"split the SQL into individual statements prior to executing them."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh `sql``, agus `reverse_sql`` má sholáthraítear iad, "
"teaghráin SQL le rith ar an mbunachar sonraí. Ar fhormhór na gcúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí (gach ceann ach PostgreSQL), roinnfidh Django an SQL ina "
"ráitis aonair sula ndéanfaidh sé iad a fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"On PostgreSQL and SQLite, only use ``BEGIN`` or ``COMMIT`` in your SQL "
"in :ref:`non-atomic migrations <non-atomic-migrations>`, to avoid breaking "
"Django's transaction state."
msgstr ""
"<non-atomic-migrations>Ar PostgreSQL agus SQLite, ní húsáid ach ``BEGIN`` nó "
"`COMMIT`` i do SQL in:ref: `imirce neamh-adamhacha `, chun staid idirbheart "
"Django a bhriseadh a sheachaint."

msgid ""
"You can also pass a list of strings or 2-tuples. The latter is used for "
"passing queries and parameters in the same way as :ref:`cursor.execute() "
"<executing-custom-sql>`. These three operations are equivalent::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat liosta teaghráin nó 2-tuples a rith freisin. <executing-"
"custom-sql>Úsáidtear an dara ceann chun ceisteanna agus paraiméadair a rith "
"ar an mbealach céanna amha:ref: `cursor.execute () `. Tá na trí oibríocht "
"seo coibhéiseach:"

msgid ""
"If you want to include literal percent signs in the query, you have to "
"double them if you are passing parameters."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat comharthaí faoin gcéad liteartha a áireamh sa cheist, "
"caithfidh tú iad a dhúbailt má tá tú ag dul ar pharaiméadair."

msgid ""
"The ``reverse_sql`` queries are executed when the migration is unapplied. "
"They should undo what is done by the ``sql`` queries. For example, to undo "
"the above insertion with a deletion::"
msgstr ""
"Déantar na ceisteanna `reverse_sql`` a fhorghníomhú nuair nach ndéantar an "
"imirce a chur i bhfeidhm. Ba chóir dóibh an méid a dhéanann na ceisteanna "
"`sql` a chealú. Mar shampla, chun an t-ionchur thuas a chealú le scriosadh:"

msgid ""
"If ``reverse_sql`` is ``None`` (the default), the ``RunSQL`` operation is "
"irreversible."
msgstr ""
"Más é ``reverse_sql`` ``None`` (an réamhshocraithe), tá an oibríocht "
"``Runsql`` dochúlghabháilte."

msgid ""
"The ``state_operations`` argument allows you to supply operations that are "
"equivalent to the SQL in terms of project state. For example, if you are "
"manually creating a column, you should pass in a list containing an "
"``AddField`` operation here so that the autodetector still has an up-to-date "
"state of the model. If you don't, when you next run ``makemigrations``, it "
"won't see any operation that adds that field and so will try to run it "
"again. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an argóint `state_operations`` duit oibríochtaí atá comhionann leis "
"an SQL a sholáthar i dtéarmaí staid an tionscadail. Mar shampla, má tá colún "
"á chruthú agat de láimh, ba chóir duit dul isteach i liosta ina bhfuil "
"oibríocht `Addfield` anseo ionas go mbeidh staid cothrom le dáta den "
"tsamhail fós ag an uathbhreithnitheoir. Mura ndéanann tú, nuair a "
"reáchtálann tú `makemigrations` eile, ní fheicfidh sé aon oibríocht a "
"chuireann an réimse sin leis agus mar sin déanfaidh sé iarracht é a "
"reáchtáil arís. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The optional ``hints`` argument will be passed as ``**hints`` to "
"the :meth:`allow_migrate` method of database routers to assist them in "
"making routing decisions. See :ref:`topics-db-multi-db-hints` for more "
"details on database hints."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear an argóint roghnach ``leideanna ``ar aghaidh mar `**hints`` chuig "
"an modh:meth: `allow_migrate` de ródairí bunachar sonraí chun cabhrú leo "
"cinntí ródaithe a dhéanamh. Féach:ref: `topics-db-multi-db-hints` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí ar leideanna bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The optional ``elidable`` argument determines whether or not the operation "
"will be removed (elided) when :ref:`squashing migrations <migration-"
"squashing>`."
msgstr ""
"<migration-squashing>Cinneann an argóint roghnach ``elidable`` cibé an "
"mbainfear an oibríocht nó nach ndéanfar an oibríocht nuai:ref: `imirce "
"squashing `."

msgid ""
"Pass the ``RunSQL.noop`` attribute to ``sql`` or ``reverse_sql`` when you "
"want the operation not to do anything in the given direction. This is "
"especially useful in making the operation reversible."
msgstr ""
"Pas an tréith ``Runsql.noop`` go `sql`` nó ``reverse_sql`` nuair a "
"theastaíonn uait gan an oibríocht aon rud a dhéanamh sa treo ar leith. Tá sé "
"seo úsáideach go háirithe chun an oibríocht a dhéanamh inchúlaithe."

msgid "``RunPython``"
msgstr "``Runpython``"

msgid ""
"Runs custom Python code in a historical context. ``code`` (and "
"``reverse_code`` if supplied) should be callable objects that accept two "
"arguments; the first is an instance of ``django.apps.registry.Apps`` "
"containing historical models that match the operation's place in the project "
"history, and the second is an instance of :class:`SchemaEditor "
"<django.db.backends.base.schema.BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor>`."
msgstr ""
"Ritheann sé cód saincheaptha Python i gcomhthéacs stairiúil. "
"<django.db.backends.base.schema.BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor>Ba chóir go mbeadh "
"“code” (agus `reverse_code`` má sholáthraítear) a ghlacann le dhá argóint; "
"is sampla de `Django.Apps.Registry.apps`` é an chéad cheann ina bhfuil "
"samhlacha stairiúla a mheaitseálann áit na hoibríochta i stair an "
"tionscadail, agus is é an dara ceann de: class: `SchemaEditor`."

msgid ""
"The ``reverse_code`` argument is called when unapplying migrations. This "
"callable should undo what is done in the ``code`` callable so that the "
"migration is reversible. If ``reverse_code`` is ``None`` (the default), the "
"``RunPython`` operation is irreversible."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ar an argóint `reverse_code`` nuair a dhéantar imirce a chur i "
"bhfeidhm. Ba chóir don ghlaoiteoir seo an méid a dhéantar sa ``cód "
"``inghlaochta a chealú ionas go mbeidh an imirce inchúlaithe. Más é "
"``reverse_code`` ``None`` (an réamhshocraithe), ní féidir an oibríocht "
"``RunPython`` dochúlghabháilte."

msgid ""
"The optional ``hints`` argument will be passed as ``**hints`` to "
"the :meth:`allow_migrate` method of database routers to assist them in "
"making a routing decision. See :ref:`topics-db-multi-db-hints` for more "
"details on database hints."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear an argóint roghnach ``leideanna ``ar aghaidh mar `**hints`` chuig "
"an modh:meth: `allow_migrate` de ródairí bunachar sonraí chun cabhrú leo "
"cinneadh ródaithe a dhéanamh. Féach:ref: `topics-db-multi-db-hints` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí ar leideanna bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"You are advised to write the code as a separate function above the "
"``Migration`` class in the migration file, and pass it to ``RunPython``. "
"Here's an example of using ``RunPython`` to create some initial objects on a "
"``Country`` model::"
msgstr ""
"Moltar duit an cód a scríobh mar fheidhm ar leithligh os cionn an aicme "
"``Imigration`` sa chomhad imirce, agus é a chur chuig `Runpython``. Seo "
"sampla de ``Runpython`` a úsáid chun roinnt rudaí tosaigh a chruthú ar "
"mhúnla ``Tír ``:"

msgid ""
"This is generally the operation you would use to create :ref:`data "
"migrations <data-migrations>`, run custom data updates and alterations, and "
"anything else you need access to an ORM and/or Python code for."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth is é seo <data-migrations>an oibríocht a úsáideann tú chun: ref: "
"`imirce sonraí `a chruthú, nuashonruithe agus athruithe sonraí saincheaptha "
"a reáchtáil, agus aon rud eile a theastaíonn uait rochtain ar chód ORM agus/"
"nó Python dó."

msgid ""
"Much like :class:`RunSQL`, ensure that if you change schema inside here "
"you're either doing it outside the scope of the Django model system (e.g. "
"triggers) or that you use :class:`SeparateDatabaseAndState` to add in "
"operations that will reflect your changes to the model state - otherwise, "
"the versioned ORM and the autodetector will stop working correctly."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: class: `Runsql`, cinntigh má athraíonn tú scéim taobh istigh "
"anseo go bhfuil tú ag déanamh taobh amuigh de scóip chórais samhail Django "
"(m.sh. spreagthóirí) nó go n-úsáideann tú: class: `SeparateDatabaseandState` "
"chun oibríochtaí a chur isteach a léireoidh do chuid athruithe ar an stát "
"samhail - ar shlí eile, stopfaidh an ORM leaganaithe agus an autodetector ag "
"obair i gceart."

msgid ""
"By default, ``RunPython`` will run its contents inside a transaction on "
"databases that do not support DDL transactions (for example, MySQL and "
"Oracle). This should be safe, but may cause a crash if you attempt to use "
"the ``schema_editor`` provided on these backends; in this case, pass "
"``atomic=False`` to the ``RunPython`` operation."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, reáchtálfaidh ``RunPython`` a ábhar taobh istigh "
"d'idirbheart ar bhunachair sonraí nach dtacaíonn le hidirbhearta DDL (mar "
"shampla, MySQL agus Oracle). Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo sábháilte, ach "
"féadfaidh sé timpiste a bheith ina chúis má dhéanann tú iarracht an "
"`schema_editor`` a chuirtear ar fáil ar na cúltaca seo a úsáid; sa chás seo, "
"cuir ``Atomic=False`` chuig an oibríocht ``RunPython``."

msgid ""
"On databases that do support DDL transactions (SQLite and PostgreSQL), "
"``RunPython`` operations do not have any transactions automatically added "
"besides the transactions created for each migration. Thus, on PostgreSQL, "
"for example, you should avoid combining schema changes and ``RunPython`` "
"operations in the same migration or you may hit errors like "
"``OperationalError: cannot ALTER TABLE \"mytable\" because it has pending "
"trigger events``."
msgstr ""
"Ar bhunachair sonraí a thacaíonn le hidirbhearta DDL (SQLite agus "
"PostgreSQL), níl aon idirbhearta curtha leis go huathoibríoch ar oibríochtaí "
"`Runpython` seachas na hidirbhearta a cruthaíodh do gach imirce. Dá bhrí "
"sin, ar PostgreSQL, mar shampla, ba cheart duit athruithe scéime agus "
"oibríochtaí ``RunPython`` a chomhcheangal san imirce céanna nó féadfaidh tú "
"earráidí mar `OperationalError: can't ALTER TABLE “mytable” toisc go bhfuil "
"imeachtaí truiceacha ar feitheamh aige ``."

msgid ""
"If you have a different database and aren't sure if it supports DDL "
"transactions, check the ``django.db.connection.features.can_rollback_ddl`` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"Má tá bunachar sonraí difriúil agat agus mura bhfuil tú cinnte an dtacaíonn "
"sé le hidirbhearta DDL, seiceáil an tréith "
"``django.db.connection.features.can_rollback_ddl``."

msgid ""
"If the ``RunPython`` operation is part of a :ref:`non-atomic migration <non-"
"atomic-migrations>`, the operation will only be executed in a transaction if "
"``atomic=True`` is passed to the ``RunPython`` operation."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an oibríocht ``RunPython`` mar chuid de a:ref: `imirce neamh-"
"adamh`<non-atomic-migrations>, ní fhorghníomhfar an oibríocht ach in "
"idirbheart má chuirtear ``Atomic=True`` chuig an oibríocht ``RunPython``."

msgid ""
"``RunPython`` does not magically alter the connection of the models for you; "
"any model methods you call will go to the default database unless you give "
"them the current database alias (available from "
"``schema_editor.connection.alias``, where ``schema_editor`` is the second "
"argument to your function)."
msgstr ""
"Ní athraíonn ``RunPython`` nasc na samhlacha duit go draíochta; rachaidh aon "
"mhodhanna samhail a ghlaonn tú chuig an mbunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe "
"mura dtugann tú an alias bunachar sonraí reatha dóibh (ar fáil ó "
"`schema_editor.connection.alias``, áit is é `schema_editor ``an dara argóint "
"le do fheidhm)."

msgid ""
"Pass the ``RunPython.noop`` method to ``code`` or ``reverse_code`` when you "
"want the operation not to do anything in the given direction. This is "
"especially useful in making the operation reversible."
msgstr ""
"Pas an modh ``Runpython.noop`` go `code`` nó ``reverse_code`` nuair is mian "
"leat gan an oibríocht aon rud a dhéanamh sa treo ar leith. Tá sé seo "
"úsáideach go háirithe chun an oibríocht a dhéanamh inchúlaithe."

msgid "``SeparateDatabaseAndState``"
msgstr "``ScaoilteDatabaseandstát ``"

msgid ""
"A highly specialized operation that lets you mix and match the database "
"(schema-changing) and state (autodetector-powering) aspects of operations."
msgstr ""
"Oibríocht an-speisialaithe a ligeann duit gnéithe na hoibríochtaí bunachar "
"sonraí (ag athrú scéime) agus stáit (cumhacht uathbhreithadóir) a mheascadh "
"agus a mheaitseáil."

msgid ""
"It accepts two lists of operations. When asked to apply state, it will use "
"the ``state_operations`` list (this is a generalized version "
"of :class:`RunSQL`'s ``state_operations`` argument). When asked to apply "
"changes to the database, it will use the ``database_operations`` list."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé le dhá liosta oibríochtaí. Nuair a iarrtar sé stát a chur i "
"bhfeidhm, úsáidfidh sé an liosta ``state_operations`` (is leagan ginearálta "
"é seo d'argóint ``state_operations`` `class: `RunSQL`). Nuair a iarrtar ar "
"athruithe a chur i bhfeidhm ar an mbunachar sonraí, úsáidfidh sé an liosta "
"``database_operations`."

msgid ""
"If the actual state of the database and Django's view of the state get out "
"of sync, this can break the migration framework, even leading to data loss. "
"It's worth exercising caution and checking your database and state "
"operations carefully. You can use :djadmin:`sqlmigrate` "
"and :djadmin:`dbshell` to check your database operations. You can "
"use :djadmin:`makemigrations`, especially with :option:`--dry-"
"run<makemigrations --dry-run>`, to check your state operations."
msgstr ""
"Má éiríonn staid iarbhír an bhunachar sonraí agus dearcadh Django ar an stát "
"as sioncrónú, féadfaidh sé seo an creat imirce a bhriseadh, fiú caillteanas "
"sonraí a bheith mar thoradh air. Is fiú cúramach a bheith agat agus "
"d'oibríochtaí bunachar sonraí agus stáit a sheiceáil go cúramach. Is féidir "
"leat: djadmin: `sqlmigrate` agus:djadmin: `dbshell` a úsáid chun "
"d'oibríochtaí bunachar sonraí a sheiceáil. <makemigrations --dry-run>Is "
"féidir leat: djadmin: `makemigrations` a úsáid, go háirithe le:option: `--"
"dry-run `, chun d'oibríochtaí stáit a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"For an example using ``SeparateDatabaseAndState``, see :ref:`changing-a-"
"manytomanyfield-to-use-a-through-model`."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla ag baint úsáide as ``SeparatedAtabaseandState``, féach:ref: "
"`changing-a-manytomanyfield-to-use-a-through-model`."

msgid "Operation category"
msgstr "Catagóir oibríochta"

msgid ""
"Categories of migration operation used by the :djadmin:`makemigrations` "
"command to display meaningful symbols."
msgstr ""
"Catagóirí oibríochta imirce a úsáidtear ag an ordú:djadmin: `makemigrations` "
"chun siombailí bríocha a thaispeáint."

msgid "*Symbol*: ``+``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``+``"

msgid "*Symbol*: ``-``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``-``"

msgid "*Symbol*: ``~``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``~``"

msgid "*Symbol*: ``p``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``p``"

msgid "*Symbol*: ``s``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``s``"

msgid "*Symbol*: ``?``"
msgstr "*Siombail*: ``? ``"

msgid "Writing your own"
msgstr "Do chuid féin a scríobh"

msgid ""
"Operations have a relatively simple API, and they're designed so that you "
"can easily write your own to supplement the built-in Django ones. The basic "
"structure of an ``Operation`` looks like this::"
msgstr ""
"Tá API réasúnta simplí ag oibríochtaí, agus tá siad deartha ionas gur féidir "
"leat do chuid féin a scríobh go héasca chun na cinn Django ionsuite a "
"fhorlíonadh. Breathnaíonn struchtúr bunúsach ``Oibríocht' mar seo:"

msgid ""
"You can take this template and work from it, though we suggest looking at "
"the built-in Django operations in ``django.db.migrations.operations`` - they "
"cover a lot of the example usage of semi-internal aspects of the migration "
"framework like ``ProjectState`` and the patterns used to get historical "
"models, as well as ``ModelState`` and the patterns used to mutate historical "
"models in ``state_forwards()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an teimpléad seo a thógáil agus oibriú uaidh, cé go molaimid "
"féachaint ar na hoibríochtaí ionsuite Django i "
"`django.db.migrations.operations`` - clúdaíonn siad go leor den úsáid "
"shamplach gnéithe leath-inmheánacha den chreat imirce cosúil le "
"`Project`state `agus na patrúin a úsáidtear chun samhlacha stairiúla a "
"fháil, chomh maith le `ModelState` agus na patrúin a úsáidtear chun "
"samhlacha stairiúla a athrú ar aghaidh () ``."

msgid "Some things to note:"
msgstr "Roinnt rudaí le tabhairt faoi deara:"

msgid ""
"You don't need to learn too much about ``ProjectState`` to write migrations; "
"just know that it has an ``apps`` property that gives access to an app "
"registry (which you can then call ``get_model`` on)."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá duit an iomarca a fhoghlaim faoi `ProjectState`` chun imirce a "
"scríobh; níl a fhios agat ach go bhfuil maoin `apps ``aipeanna aige a "
"thugann rochtain ar chlárlann aipeanna (ar féidir leat ``get_model`` a "
"ghlaoch ansin air)."

msgid ""
"``database_forwards`` and ``database_backwards`` both get two states passed "
"to them; these represent the difference the ``state_forwards`` method would "
"have applied, but are given to you for convenience and speed reasons."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann ``database_forwards`` agus `database_backwards`` dhá stát ar "
"aghaidh chucu; léiríonn siad seo an difríocht a bheadh i bhfeidhm ag an modh "
"``state_forward ``, ach tugtar duit ar chúiseanna áisiúlachta agus luais."

msgid ""
"If you want to work with model classes or model instances from the "
"``from_state`` argument in ``database_forwards()`` or "
"``database_backwards()``, you must render model states using the "
"``clear_delayed_apps_cache()`` method to make related models available::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat oibriú le ranganna samhail nó cásanna samhail ón argóint "
"``from_state ``i `database_forwards ()`` nó `database_backwards () ``, ní "
"mór duit stáit samhail a thabhairt ag baint úsáide as an modh "
"``clear_delayed_apps_cache ()`` chun samhlacha gaolmhara a chur ar fáil:"

msgid ""
"``to_state`` in the database_backwards method is the *older* state; that is, "
"the one that will be the current state once the migration has finished "
"reversing."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``to_state ``sa mhodh database_backwards an stát*níos sine; is é sin, "
"an ceann a bheidh mar an staid reatha nuair a bheidh an imirce críochnaithe "
"ag aisiompú."

msgid ""
"You might see implementations of ``references_model`` on the built-in "
"operations; this is part of the autodetection code and does not matter for "
"custom operations."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go bhfeicfeá cur i bhfeidhm ``references_model`` ar na "
"hoibríochtaí ionsuite; is cuid den chód uathbhreithnithe é seo agus níl sé "
"tábhacht le haghaidh oibríochtaí saincheaptha."

msgid ""
"For performance reasons, the :class:`~django.db.models.Field` instances in "
"``ModelState.fields`` are reused across migrations. You must never change "
"the attributes on these instances. If you need to mutate a field in "
"``state_forwards()``, you must remove the old instance from "
"``ModelState.fields`` and add a new instance in its place. The same is true "
"for the :class:`~django.db.models.Manager` instances in "
"``ModelState.managers``."
msgstr ""
"Ar chúiseanna feidhmíochta, athúsáidtear na cásanna: class: "
"`~django.db.models.field` i `ModelState.Field` trasna imirce. Ní mór duit na "
"tréithe ar na cásanna seo a athrú riamh. Más gá duit réimse a athrú in "
"`state_forwards () ``, ní mór duit an seanshampla a bhaint as "
"`ModelState.fields`` agus cás nua a chur ina áit. Tá an rud céanna fíor "
"maidir leis na cásanna: class: `~Django.db.Models.Manager` i "
"`ModelState.Manager`."

msgid ""
"As an example, let's make an operation that loads PostgreSQL extensions "
"(which contain some of PostgreSQL's more exciting features). Since there's "
"no model state changes, all it does is run one command::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, déanaimis oibríocht a luchtaíonn síntí PostgreSQL (ina bhfuil "
"cuid de na gnéithe níos spreagúla PostgreSQL). Ós rud é nach bhfuil aon "
"athruithe stáit samhail ann, níl le déanamh aige ach ordú amháin a "
"reáchtáil::"

msgid "Model class reference"
msgstr "Tagairt aicme múnla"

msgid ""
"This document covers features of the :class:`~django.db.models.Model` class. "
"For more information about models, see :doc:`the complete list of Model "
"reference guides </ref/models/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn an doiciméad seo gnéithe den range:class: "
