"A class attribute, as a format string, that describes the SQL that is "
"generated for this aggregate. Defaults to ``'%(function)s(%(distinct)s%"
"(expressions)s)'``."
msgstr ""
"Tréith aicme, mar shreang formáide, a chuireann síos ar an SQL a ghintear "
"don chomhiomlán seo. Réamhshocraithe go ``'% (function) s (% (difriúil) s% "
"(abairtí) s) '`."

msgid ""
"A class attribute describing the aggregate function that will be generated. "
"Specifically, the ``function`` will be interpolated as the ``function`` "
"placeholder within :attr:`template`. Defaults to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Tréith aicme a dhéanann cur síos ar an bhfeidhm chomhiomlán a ghinteofar. Go "
"sonrach, déanfar an `feidhm ``idirphóilte mar shealbhóir an ``feidhmi`` "
"laistigh de: attr: `teimpléad`. Réamhshocraithe go ``None``."

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``True`` since most aggregate functions can be used as the "
"source expression in :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.Window`."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True`` ós rud é gur féidir an chuid is mó de na "
"feidhmeanna comhiomlána a úsáid mar an abairt foinse in:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Expressions.Window`."

msgid ""
"A class attribute determining whether or not this aggregate function allows "
"passing a ``distinct`` keyword argument. If set to ``False`` (default), "
"``TypeError`` is raised if ``distinct=True`` is passed."
msgstr ""
"Tréith aicme a chinneann cibé an gceadaíonn an fheidhm chomhiomlán seo "
"argóint eochairfhocal “difriúil” a rith nó nach bhfuil. Má tá sé socraithe "
"go ``False`` (réamhshocraithe), ardaítear ``TypeError`` má chuirtear "
"``Distinct=True``."

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``None`` since most aggregate functions result in ``NULL`` when "
"applied to an empty result set."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``None`` ós rud é go mbíonn `NULL`` mar thoradh ar an "
"gcuid is mó de na feidhmeanna comhiomlána nuair a chuirtear i bhfeidhm ar "
"shraith torthaí folamh."

msgid ""
"The ``expressions`` positional arguments can include expressions, transforms "
"of the model field, or the names of model fields. They will be converted to "
"a string and used as the ``expressions`` placeholder within the ``template``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis na hargóintí seasaimh ``léiritheach`` abairtí, claochruithe "
"an réimse samhail, nó ainmneacha réimsí samhail a bheith san áireamh. "
"Déanfar iad a thiontú go sreang agus úsáidfear iad mar shealbhóir áit "
"``léiritheoir` laistigh den `teimpléad`."

msgid ""
"The ``distinct`` argument determines whether or not the aggregate function "
"should be invoked for each distinct value of ``expressions`` (or set of "
"values, for multiple ``expressions``). The argument is only supported on "
"aggregates that have :attr:`~Aggregate.allow_distinct` set to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann an argóint ``difriúil ``cibé an gcaithfear an fheidhm chomhiomlán a "
"ghairm nó nach bhfuil i gcás gach luach ar leith ``léiritheach`` (nó tacar "
"luachanna, le haghaidh iolracha ``léiritheach``). Ní thacaítear leis an "
"argóint ach ar chomhiomláin a bhfuil: attr: `~Aggregate.allow_Distinct` "
"socraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"The ``filter`` argument takes a :class:`Q object <django.db.models.Q>` "
"that's used to filter the rows that are aggregated. See :ref:`conditional-"
"aggregation` and :ref:`filtering-on-annotations` for example usage."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an argóint ``scagair`` a:class: `Q rud `a úsáidtear chun na sraithe "
"<django.db.models.Q>anna atá comhiomlánaithe a scagadh. Féach: ref: "
"`comhiomlánú coinníollach` agus:ref: `filtering-on-annotations` mar shampla "
"úsáid."

msgid ""
"The ``default`` argument takes a value that will be passed along with the "
"aggregate to :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Coalesce`. This is useful "
"for specifying a value to be returned other than ``None`` when the queryset "
"(or grouping) contains no entries."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an argóint `default`` luach a chuirfear in éineacht leis an "
"comhiomlán chuig:class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Coalesce`. Tá sé seo "
"úsáideach chun luach atá le tabhairt ar ais seachas ``None`` a shonrú nuair "
"nach bhfuil aon iontrálacha sa tacar fiosrúcháin (nó an ghrúpáil)."

msgid ""
"The ``**extra`` kwargs are ``key=value`` pairs that can be interpolated into "
"the ``template`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na kwargs ``**extra`` péirí ``eochair=luach`` is féidir iad a "
"ionghabháil isteach sa tréith ``teimpléad ``."

msgid "Creating your own Aggregate Functions"
msgstr "Do Feidhmeanna Comhiomlánacha féin a"

msgid ""
"You can create your own aggregate functions, too. At a minimum, you need to "
"define ``function``, but you can also completely customize the SQL that is "
"generated. Here's a brief example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat do fheidhmeanna comhiomlána féin a chruthú freisin. Ar a "
"laghad, ní mór duit ``feidhm ``a shainiú, ach is féidir leat an SQL a "
"ghintear a shaincheapadh go hiomlán freisin. Seo sampla gairid::"

msgid "``Value()`` expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna ``Luach () ``"

msgid ""
"A ``Value()`` object represents the smallest possible component of an "
"expression: a simple value. When you need to represent the value of an "
"integer, boolean, or string within an expression, you can wrap that value "
"within a ``Value()``."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn réad ``Luach () ``an chomhpháirt is lú is féidir de abairt: luach "
"simplí. Nuair is gá duit luach sláimhir, boolean nó sreang a léiriú laistigh "
"de abairt, is féidir leat an luach sin a fhilleadh laistigh de ``Luach () ``."

msgid ""
"You will rarely need to use ``Value()`` directly. When you write the "
"expression ``F('field') + 1``, Django implicitly wraps the ``1`` in a "
"``Value()``, allowing simple values to be used in more complex expressions. "
"You will need to use ``Value()`` when you want to pass a string to an "
"expression. Most expressions interpret a string argument as the name of a "
"field, like ``Lower('name')``."
msgstr ""
"Is annamh a bheidh ort ``Luach () ``a úsáid go díreach. Nuair a scríobhann "
"tú an abairt ``F ('field') + 1``, fillteann Django an ``1`` go hinneach i "
"``Luach () ``, ag ligean luachanna simplí a úsáid i nathanna níos casta. "
"Beidh ort ``Luach () ``a úsáid nuair is mian leat teaghrán a chur chuig "
"abairt. Léirmhíníonn an chuid is mó de na nathanna argóint teaghrán mar ainm "
"réimse, cosúil le ``Lower ('ainm') `."

msgid ""
"The ``value`` argument describes the value to be included in the expression, "
"such as ``1``, ``True``, or ``None``. Django knows how to convert these "
"Python values into their corresponding database type."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an argóint ``luach`` cur síos ar an luach atá le cur san áireamh sa "
"abairt, mar shampla ```1``, `True``, nó ``None``. Tá a fhios ag Django conas "
"na luachanna Python seo a thiontú ina gcineál bunachar sonraí comhfhreag"

msgid ""
"If no :ref:`output_field<output-field>` is specified, it will be inferred "
"from the type of the provided ``value`` for many common types. For example, "
"passing an instance of :py:class:`datetime.datetime` as ``value`` defaults "
"``output_field`` to :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`."
msgstr ""
"Má shonraítear no:ref: `output_field <output-field>`, déanfar é a thabhairt "
"chun cinn ó chineál an `luach`` a chuirtear ar fáil do go leor cineálacha "
"coitianta. Mar shampla, ag rith sampla de:py:class: `datetime.datetime` mar "
"`value`` réamhshocraithe ``output_field`` chuig:class: "
"`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`."

msgid "``ExpressionWrapper()`` expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna ``ExpressionWrapper () ``"

msgid ""
"``ExpressionWrapper`` surrounds another expression and provides access to "
"properties, such as :ref:`output_field<output-field>`, that may not be "
"available on other expressions. ``ExpressionWrapper`` is necessary when "
"using arithmetic on ``F()`` expressions with different types as described "
"in :ref:`using-f-with-annotations`."
msgstr ""
"<output-field>Tá ``ExpressionWrapper`` timpeall ar abairt eile agus "
"soláthraíonn sé rochtain ar airíonna, mar shampla:ref: `output_field `, nach "
"mbeadh ar fáil ar abairtí eile. Tá ``ExpressionWrapper`` riachtanach nuair a "
"úsáidtear uimhríocht ar abairtí ``F () ``le cineálacha éagsúla mar a "
"thuairiscítear in:ref: `using-f-with-annotations`."

msgid "Conditional expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna coinníollach"

msgid ""
"Conditional expressions allow you to "
"use :keyword:`if` ... :keyword:`elif` ... :keyword:`else` logic in queries. "
"Django natively supports SQL ``CASE`` expressions. For more details "
"see :doc:`conditional-expressions`."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann nathanna coinníollach duit úsáid:keyword: `if `... :keyword: "
"`elif`... :keyword: loighic `else` i gceisteanna. Tacaíonn Django le "
"nathanna SQL ``CASE`` go dúchasach. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí féach:doc: "
"`conditional-expressions`."

msgid "``Subquery()`` expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna ``Subquest () ``"

msgid ""
"You can add an explicit subquery to a ``QuerySet`` using the ``Subquery`` "
"expression."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat fo-cheist sainráite a chur le ``QuerySet`` ag baint úsáide as "
"an abairt ``SubQuery``."

msgid ""
"For example, to annotate each post with the email address of the author of "
"the newest comment on that post:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun gach post a anótáil le seoladh ríomhphoist údar an trácht "
"is nua ar an bpost sin:"

msgid "On PostgreSQL, the SQL looks like:"
msgstr "Ar PostgreSQL, tá cuma ar an SQL:"

msgid ""
"The examples in this section are designed to show how to force Django to "
"execute a subquery. In some cases it may be possible to write an equivalent "
"queryset that performs the same task more clearly or efficiently."
msgstr ""
"Tá na samplaí sa chuid seo deartha chun a thaispeáint conas iallach a chur "
"ar Django focheist a fhorghníomhú. I gcásanna áirithe d'fhéadfadh sé a "
"bheith indéanta tacar ceisteanna coibhéiseach a scríobh a dhéanann an tasc "
"céanna níos soiléire nó níos éifeachtaí."

msgid "Referencing columns from the outer queryset"
msgstr "Tagairt do cholúin ón tacar ceisteanna seachtrach"

msgid ""
"Use ``OuterRef`` when a queryset in a ``Subquery`` needs to refer to a field "
"from the outer query or its transform. It acts like an :class:`F` expression "
"except that the check to see if it refers to a valid field isn't made until "
"the outer queryset is resolved."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``OuterRef`` nuair is gá le tacar ceisteanna i ``Focheiste`` tagairt a "
"dhéanamh do réimse ón bhfiosrú seachtrach nó a chlaochlú. Feidhmíonn sé "
"cosúil le léiriú: aicme: `F` ach amháin nach ndéantar an seiceáil chun a "
"fheiceáil an dtagraíonn sé do réimse bailí go dtí go réitear an tacar "
"ceisteanna seachtrach."

msgid ""
"Instances of ``OuterRef`` may be used in conjunction with nested instances "
"of ``Subquery`` to refer to a containing queryset that isn't the immediate "
"parent. For example, this queryset would need to be within a nested pair of "
"``Subquery`` instances to resolve correctly:"
msgstr ""
"Féadfar cásanna ``OuterRef`` a úsáid i gcomhar le cásanna neadaithe de "
"``Subcheiste`` chun tagairt a dhéanamh do thacar fiosrúcháin ina bhfuil nach "
"é an tuismitheoir láithreach. Mar shampla, caithfeadh an tacar ceisteanna "
"seo a bheith laistigh de phéire neadaithe cásanna ``Subcheiste`` chun "
"réiteach i gceart:"

msgid "Limiting a subquery to a single column"
msgstr "Focheisteanna a theorannú go colún amháin"

msgid ""
"There are times when a single column must be returned from a ``Subquery``, "
"for instance, to use a ``Subquery`` as the target of an ``__in`` lookup. To "
"return all comments for posts published within the last day:"
msgstr ""
"Tá amanna ann nuair a chaithfear colún amháin a thabhairt ar ais ó "
"``Subcheiste``, mar shampla, chun ``Subcheiste`` a úsáid mar sprioc "
"chuardaigh ``__in``. Chun gach trácht ar phoist a fhoilsíodh laistigh den lá "
"deireanach a thabhairt ar ais:"

msgid ""
"In this case, the subquery must use :meth:`~.QuerySet.values` to return only "
"a single column: the primary key of the post."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, ní mór don fho-cheist a úsáid: meth: `~.queryset.values` chun "
"colún amháin a thabhairt ar ais: príomh-eochair an phoist."

msgid "Limiting the subquery to a single row"
msgstr "An fho-cheist a theorannú go sraith amháin"

msgid ""
"To prevent a subquery from returning multiple rows, a slice (``[:1]``) of "
"the queryset is used:"
msgstr ""
"Chun fo-cheist a chosc ó iliomad sraitheanna a thabhairt ar ais, úsáidtear "
"slisnas (``[:1]``) den tacar fiosrúcháin:"

msgid ""
"In this case, the subquery must only return a single column *and* a single "
"row: the email address of the most recently created comment."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, ní mór don fho-cheist ach colún aon* agus* sraith amháin a "
"thabhairt ar ais: seoladh ríomhphoist an trácht is déanaí a cruthaíodh."

msgid ""
"(Using :meth:`~.QuerySet.get` instead of a slice would fail because the "
"``OuterRef`` cannot be resolved until the queryset is used within a "
"``Subquery``.)"
msgstr ""
"(Teipfeadh ag baint úsáid:Meth: `~.querySet.get` in ionad slisnas toisc nach "
"féidir an ``OuterRef`` a réiteach go dtí go n-úsáidfear an tacar fiosrúcháin "
"laistigh de ``Subcheiste``.)"

msgid "``Exists()`` subqueries"
msgstr "Focheisteanna ``Tá ann () ``"

msgid ""
"``Exists`` is a ``Subquery`` subclass that uses an SQL ``EXISTS`` statement. "
"In many cases it will perform better than a subquery since the database is "
"able to stop evaluation of the subquery when a first matching row is found."
msgstr ""
"Is fo-aicme ```Subcheiste`` é `Exists`` a úsáideann ráiteas SQL ``EXISTS``. "
"I go leor cásanna feidhmeoidh sé níos fearr ná fo-cheist ós rud é go bhfuil "
"an bunachar sonraí in ann stop a chur le meastóireacht ar an bhfo-cheist "
"nuair a aimsítear an chéad tsraith meaitseála."

msgid ""
"For example, to annotate each post with whether or not it has a comment from "
"within the last day:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun gach post a anótáil le cibé an bhfuil trácht aige laistigh "
"den lá deireanach nó nach bhfuil:"

msgid ""
"It's unnecessary to force ``Exists`` to refer to a single column, since the "
"columns are discarded and a boolean result is returned. Similarly, since "
"ordering is unimportant within an SQL ``EXISTS`` subquery and would only "
"degrade performance, it's automatically removed."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá iallach ar ``Exists`` tagairt a dhéanamh do cholún amháin, ós rud é go "
"ndéantar na colúin a chaitheamh agus cuirtear toradh boolean ar ais. Ar an "
"gcaoi chéanna, ós rud é nach bhfuil ordú tábhachtach laistigh de fhocheistiú "
"SQL `EXISTS` agus nach ndéanfadh sé ach feidhmíocht a laghdú, baintear é go "
"huathoibríoch."

msgid "You can query using ``NOT EXISTS`` with ``~Exists()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ceist a dhéanamh ag baint úsáide as ``NOT EXISTS`` le "
"``~Exists () ``."

msgid "Filtering on a ``Subquery()`` or ``Exists()`` expressions"
msgstr "Scagadh ar nathanna ``Focheist ()`` nó ``Existents ()`` `"

msgid ""
"``Subquery()`` that returns a boolean value and ``Exists()`` may be used as "
"a ``condition`` in :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.When` expressions, "
"or to directly filter a queryset:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ``Subquery () ``a thugann luach boolean agus ``Existents ()`` a "
"úsáid mar ``coinníoll`` in:class: `~django.db.Models.Expressions.When "
"`abairtí, nó chun tacar fiosrúcháin a scagadh go díreach:"

msgid ""
"This will ensure that the subquery will not be added to the ``SELECT`` "
"columns, which may result in a better performance."
msgstr ""
"Cinnteoidh sé seo nach gcuirfear an fo-cheist leis na colúin ``SELECT``, rud "
"a d'fhéadfadh feidhmíocht níos fearr a bheith mar thoradh air."

msgid "Using aggregates within a ``Subquery`` expression"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as comhiomlánaithe laistigh de abairt ```Focheisteanna ``"

msgid ""
"Aggregates may be used within a ``Subquery``, but they require a specific "
"combination of :meth:`~.QuerySet.filter`, :meth:`~.QuerySet.values`, "
"and :meth:`~.QuerySet.annotate` to get the subquery grouping correct."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir comhiomláin a úsáid laistigh de ``SubQuery``, ach teastaíonn "
"teaglaim shonrach uathu de:meth: `~.queryset.filter`, :meth: "
"`~.queryset.values`, agus:meth: `~.queryset.annotate` chun an grúpáil fo-"
"cheisteanna a chur i gceart."

msgid ""
"Assuming both models have a ``length`` field, to find posts where the post "
"length is greater than the total length of all combined comments:"
msgstr ""
"Ag glacadh leis go bhfuil réimse ``fad ``ag an dá mhúnla, chun poist a "
"aimsiú ina bhfuil fad an phoist níos mó ná fad iomlán na dtuairimí "
"comhcheangailte go léir:"

msgid ""
"The initial ``filter(...)`` limits the subquery to the relevant parameters. "
"``order_by()`` removes the "
"default :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.ordering` (if any) on the "
"``Comment`` model. ``values('post')`` aggregates comments by ``Post``. "
"Finally, ``annotate(...)`` performs the aggregation. The order in which "
"these queryset methods are applied is important. In this case, since the "
"subquery must be limited to a single column, ``values('total')`` is required."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an “scagaire (...)” tosaigh teorainn leis an bhfocheistiú go dtí na "
"paraiméadair ábhartha. Baineann ``order_by () ``an réamhshocraithe:attr: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Options.Ordering` (más ann) ar an tsamhail ``Comment``. "
"Comhiomlánann ``luachanna ('post') ``tuairimí le ``Post``. Faoi dheireadh, "
"déanann ``annotate (...) ``an comhiomlánú. Tá an t-ord ina gcuirtear na "
"modhanna ceisteanna seo i bhfeidhm tábhachtach. Sa chás seo, ós rud é go "
"gcaithfear an fo-cheist a bheith teoranta do cholún amháin, tá gá le "
"`luachanna ('iomlán') ``."

msgid ""
"This is the only way to perform an aggregation within a ``Subquery``, as "
"using :meth:`~.QuerySet.aggregate` attempts to evaluate the queryset (and if "
"there is an ``OuterRef``, this will not be possible to resolve)."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an t-aon bhealach chun comhiomlánú a dhéanamh laistigh de "
"``SubQuery``, mar a úsáideann: meth: `~.queryset.aggregate` iarracht an "
"tacar ceisteanna a mheas (agus má tá ``OuterRef`` ann, ní féidir é seo a "
"réiteach)."

msgid "Raw SQL expressions"
msgstr "Nathanna amh SQL"

msgid ""
"Sometimes database expressions can't easily express a complex ``WHERE`` "
"clause. In these edge cases, use the ``RawSQL`` expression. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta ní féidir le nathanna bunachar sonraí clásal casta ``WHERE`` a "
"chur in iúl go héasca. Sna cásanna imeall seo, bain úsáid as an abairt "
"``Rawsql`. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"These extra lookups may not be portable to different database engines "
"(because you're explicitly writing SQL code) and violate the DRY principle, "
"so you should avoid them if possible."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir nach mbeidh na cuardaigh breise seo iniompartha d'innill bhunachar "
"sonraí éagsúla (toisc go bhfuil cód SQL á scríobh go sainráite agat) agus "
"sáraíonn tú prionsabal DRY, mar sin ba cheart duit iad a sheachaint más "
"féidir."

msgid ""
"``RawSQL`` expressions can also be used as the target of ``__in`` filters:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir nathanna ``Rawsql`` a úsáid freisin mar sprioc scagairí ``__in``:"

msgid ""
"To protect against `SQL injection attacks <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"SQL_injection>`_, you must escape any parameters that the user can control "
"by using ``params``. ``params`` is a required argument to force you to "
"acknowledge that you're not interpolating your SQL with user-provided data."
msgstr ""
"Chun cosaint a dhéanamh ar `ionsaithe insteallta SQL `_ < https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SQL_injection>, ní mór duit éalú aon pharaiméadair is "
"féidir leis an úsáideoir a rialú trí `params' a úsáid. Is argóint "
"riachtanach é `params' chun iallach ort a admháil nach bhfuil tú ag "
"idirphóiriú do SQL le sonraí a sholáthraíonn an úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"You also must not quote placeholders in the SQL string. This example is "
"vulnerable to SQL injection because of the quotes around ``%s``::"
msgstr ""
"Ní mór duit sealbhóirí áiteanna a lua sa teaghrán SQL freisin. Tá an sampla "
"seo leochaileach do instealladh SQL mar gheall ar na luachana timpeall "
"``%s``:"

msgid ""
"You can read more about how Django's :ref:`SQL injection protection <sql-"
"injection-protection>` works."
msgstr ""
"<sql-injection-protection>Is féidir leat tuilleadh a léamh faoin gcaoi a n-"
"oibríonn Django's:ref: `Cosaint insteallta SQL `."

msgid ""
"Window functions provide a way to apply functions on partitions. Unlike a "
"normal aggregation function which computes a final result for each set "
"defined by the group by, window functions operate on :ref:`frames <window-"
"frames>` and partitions, and compute the result for each row."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn feidhmeanna fuinneoige bealach chun feidhmeanna a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar Murab ionann agus gnáthfheidhm chomhiomlánaithe a ríomhaíonn "
"toradh deiridh do gach tacar a shainmhíníonn an grúpa ag, oibríonn "
"feidhmeanna fuinneoige ar:ref: `frámaí <window-frames>`agus deighiltí, agus "
"ríomhaíonn siad an toradh do gach sraith."

msgid ""
"You can specify multiple windows in the same query which in Django ORM would "
"be equivalent to including multiple expressions in "
"a :doc:`QuerySet.annotate() </topics/db/aggregation>` call. The ORM doesn't "
"make use of named windows, instead they are part of the selected columns."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat fuinneoga iolracha a shonrú san fhiosrúchán céanna a bheadh i "
"Django ORM comhionann le nathanna iolracha a áireamh in a:doc: `Query</"
"topics/db/aggregation> Set.annotate () `glao. Ní úsáideann an ORM fuinneoga "
"ainmnithe, ina ionad sin tá siad mar chuid de na colúin roghnaithe."

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``%(expression)s OVER (%(window)s)``. If only the ``expression`` "
"argument is provided, the window clause will be blank."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``% (abairt) s OVER (% (window) s) `. Mura gcuirtear ach "
"an argóint ``léirithe`` ar fáil, beidh clásal na fuinneoige bán."

msgid "The ``Window`` class is the main expression for an ``OVER`` clause."
msgstr "Is é an rang ``Windows ``an príomh-abairt do chlásal ``OVER``."

msgid ""
"The ``expression`` argument is either a :ref:`window function <window-"
"functions>`, an :ref:`aggregate function <aggregation-functions>`, or an "
"expression that's compatible in a window clause."
msgstr ""
"Is é an argóint ``léirithe`` a: ref: `feidhm fuinneog `<window-functions>, "
"an:ref: `feidhm chomhiomlán`, nó abairt atá comhoiriúnach i gclá "
"<aggregation-functions>sal fuinneoige."

msgid ""
"The ``partition_by`` argument accepts an expression or a sequence of "
"expressions (column names should be wrapped in an ``F``-object) that control "
"the partitioning of the rows.  Partitioning narrows which rows are used to "
"compute the result set."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an argóint `partition_by`` le abairt nó le seicheamh abairtí (ba "
"chóir ainmneacha colún a fhilleadh i réad ``F``) a rialaíonn deighilt na "
"sraitheanna. Déanann deighilt a chúngú cé na sraitheanna a úsáidtear chun an "
"tacar torthaí a ríomh."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`output_field<output-field>` is specified either as an argument or "
"by the expression."
msgstr ""
"Sonraítear an:ref: `output_field <output-field>`mar argóint nó leis an "
"abairt."

msgid ""
"The ``order_by`` argument accepts an expression on which you can "
"call :meth:`~django.db.models.Expression.asc` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.Expression.desc`, a string of a field name "
"(with an optional ``\"-\"`` prefix which indicates descending order), or a "
"tuple or list of strings and/or expressions. The ordering controls the order "
"in which the expression is applied. For example, if you sum over the rows in "
"a partition, the first result is the value of the first row, the second is "
"the sum of first and second row."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an argóint `order_by`` le abairt ar féidir leat glao:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.expression.asc` agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.expression.desc`, teaghrán ainm réimse (le réimír "
"roghnach ``” -\"`` a léiríonn ord íslitheach), nó liosta teaghráin agus/nó "
"nathanna. Rialaíonn an t-ordú an t-ord ina gcuirtear an abairt i bhfeidhm. "
"Mar shampla, má chuireann tú suim thar na sraitheanna i ndeighilt, is é an "
"chéad toradh luach an chéad shraith, is é an dara ceann suim den chéad agus "
"an dara sraith."

msgid ""
"The ``frame`` parameter specifies which other rows that should be used in "
"the computation. See :ref:`window-frames` for details."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn an paraiméadar ``fráma ``na sraitheanna eile ba chóir a úsáid sa "
"ríomh. Féach: Ref: `fhrámaí fuinneog` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"For example, to annotate each movie with the average rating for the movies "
"by the same studio in the same genre and release year:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun anótáil a dhéanamh ar gach scannán leis an meánrátáil do "
"na scannáin ag an stiúideo céanna sa seánra agus sa bhliain scaoilte céanna:"

msgid ""
"This allows you to check if a movie is rated better or worse than its peers."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé seo duit seiceáil an bhfuil scannán a rátáil níos fearr nó níos "
"measa ná a phiaraí."

msgid ""
"You may want to apply multiple expressions over the same window, i.e., the "
"same partition and frame. For example, you could modify the previous example "
"to also include the best and worst rating in each movie's group (same "
"studio, genre, and release year) by using three window functions in the same "
"query. The partition and ordering from the previous example is extracted "
"into a dictionary to reduce repetition:"
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat nathanna iolracha a chur i bhfeidhm thar an "
"bhfuinneog chéanna, ie, an deighilt agus an fráma céanna. Mar shampla, "
"d'fhéadfá an sampla roimhe seo a mhodhnú chun an rátáil is fearr agus is "
"measa a áireamh i ngrúpa gach scannáin (an stiúideo céanna, an seánra agus "
"an bhliain scaoilte céanna) trí fheidhm fuinneoige a úsáid san fhiosrú "
"céanna. Baintear an deighilt agus an t-ordú ón sampla roimhe seo isteach i "
"bhfoclóir chun athrá a laghdú:"

msgid ""
"Filtering against window functions is supported as long as lookups are not "
"disjunctive (not using ``OR`` or ``XOR`` as a connector) and against a "
"queryset performing aggregation."
msgstr ""
"Tacaítear le scagadh i gcoinne feidhmeanna fuinneoige chomh fada agus nach "
"bhfuil cuardaigh díghníomhach (gan úsáid `OR`` nó ``XOR`` mar chónascaire) "
"agus i gcoinne tacar cheisteanna a dhéanann comhiomlánú."

msgid ""
"For example, a query that relies on aggregation and has an ``OR``-ed filter "
"against a window function and a field is not supported. Applying combined "
"predicates post-aggregation could cause rows that would normally be excluded "
"from groups to be included:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ní thacaítear le ceist a bhraitheann ar chomhiomlánú agus a "
"bhfuil scagaire ``Or`` -ED aige i gcoinne feidhm fuinneoige agus réimse. "
"D'fhéadfadh go gcuirfí sraitheanna a eisiamh ó ghrúpaí de ghnáth a chur san "
"áireamh iar-chomhiomlánú réamhchóga comhcheang"

msgid ""
"Among Django's built-in database backends, MySQL, PostgreSQL, and Oracle "
"support window expressions. Support for different window expression features "
"varies among the different databases. For example, the options "
"in :meth:`~django.db.models.Expression.asc` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.Expression.desc` may not be supported. Consult "
"the documentation for your database as needed."
msgstr ""
"I measc cúltaca bunachar sonraí ionsuite Django, tacaíonn MySQL, PostgreSQL, "
"agus Oracle nathanna fuinneoige. Athraíonn tacaíocht do ghnéithe éagsúla "
"léirithe fuinneoige i measc na mbun Mar shampla, ní fhéadfar tacú leis na "
"roghanna in:meth: `~Django.db.Models.Expression.asc` agus:meth: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Expression.desc`. Téigh i gcomhairle leis na cáipéisíocht "
"do do bhunachar sonraí"

msgid "Frames"
msgstr "Frámaí"

msgid ""
"For a window frame, you can choose either a range-based sequence of rows or "
"an ordinary sequence of rows."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le fráma fuinneoige, is féidir leat seicheamh sraitheanna bunaithe ar "
"raon nó gnáthseicheamh sraitheanna a roghnú."

msgid "This attribute is set to ``'RANGE'``."
msgstr "Tá an tréith seo socraithe go ``'RANGE``."

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL has limited support for ``ValueRange`` and only supports use of "
"the standard start and end points, such as ``CURRENT ROW`` and ``UNBOUNDED "
"FOLLOWING``."
msgstr ""
"Tá tacaíocht theoranta ag PostgreSQL do `ValueRange`` agus ní thacaíonn sé "
"ach le húsáid na bpointí tosaigh agus deiridh caighdeánacha, mar shampla "
"``CURRENT ROW`` agus ``UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING``."

msgid "The ``exclusion`` argument was added."
msgstr "Cuireadh an argóint ``eisiaim`` leis."

msgid "This attribute is set to ``'ROWS'``."
msgstr "Tá an tréith seo socraithe go ``'ROWS'``."

msgid "Both classes return SQL with the template:"
msgstr "Tugann an dá rang SQL ar ais leis an teimpléad:"

msgid ""
"The ``exclusion`` argument allows excluding rows "
"(:attr:`~WindowFrameExclusion.CURRENT_ROW`), groups "
"(:attr:`~WindowFrameExclusion.GROUP`), and ties "
"(:attr:`~WindowFrameExclusion.TIES`) from the window frames on supported "
"databases:"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an argóint ``eisiamh ``sraitheanna (:attr: "
"`~WindowFrameExclusion.current_row`), grúpaí (:attr: "
"`~WindowFrameExclusion.group`), agus ceangail (:attr: "
"`~WindowFrameExclusion.ties`) a eisiamh ó na frámaí fuinneoige ar bhunachar "
"sonraí tacaithe:"

msgid ""
"Frames narrow the rows that are used for computing the result. They shift "
"from some start point to some specified end point. Frames can be used with "
"and without partitions, but it's often a good idea to specify an ordering of "
"the window to ensure a deterministic result. In a frame, a peer in a frame "
"is a row with an equivalent value, or all rows if an ordering clause isn't "
"present."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn frámaí na sraitheanna a úsáidtear chun an toradh a ríomh. "
"Aistríonn siad ó phointe tosaigh éigin go pointe deiridh sonraithe éigin. Is "
"féidir frámaí a úsáid le deighiltí agus gan deighiltí, ach is minic gur "
"smaoineamh maith é ordú na fuinneoige a shonrú chun toradh cinntitheach a "
"chinntiú. I bhfráma, is é piaraí i bhfráma ina chéile le luach coibhéiseach, "
"nó gach sraitheanna mura bhfuil clásal ordaithe i láthair."

msgid ""
"The default starting point for a frame is ``UNBOUNDED PRECEDING`` which is "
"the first row of the partition. The end point is always explicitly included "
"in the SQL generated by the ORM and is by default ``UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING``. "
"The default frame includes all rows from the partition to the last row in "
"the set."
msgstr ""
"Is é an pointe tosaigh réamhshocraithe le haghaidh fráma ná ``UNBOUNDED "
"PRESEING`` arb é an chéad tsraith den dheighilt. Cuirtear an pointe deiridh "
"san áireamh go sainráite i gcónaí sa SQL a ghineann an ORM agus de réir "
"réamhshocraithe é “FOLLOWING UNBOUNDED”. Cuimsíonn an fráma réamhshocraithe "
"gach sraitheanna ón deighilt go dtí an tsraith deireanach sa tacar."

msgid ""
"The accepted values for the ``start`` and ``end`` arguments are ``None``, an "
"integer, or zero. A negative integer for ``start`` results in ``N "
"PRECEDING``, while ``None`` yields ``UNBOUNDED PRECEDING``. In ``ROWS`` "
"mode, a positive integer can be used for ``start`` resulting in ``N "
"FOLLOWING``. Positive integers are accepted for ``end`` and results in ``N "
"FOLLOWING``. In ``ROWS`` mode, a negative integer can be used for ``end`` "
"resulting in ``N PRECEDING``. For both ``start`` and ``end``, zero will "
"return ``CURRENT ROW``."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na luachanna a nglactar leis do na hargóintí ``tús ``agus "
"``deireadh`` ná ``None``, sláimhir, nó nialas. Mar thoradh ar shláimhir "
"dhiúltach do ``tosaithe`` bíonn ``N ROIMH ROIMH`` mar thoradh ar ````None`` "
"`ROIMH `ROIMH NEAMHTHEANNA``. I mód ``ROWS`, is féidir sláimhir dhearfach a "
"úsáid le haghaidh ``tús ``mar thoradh ar ``N FOLLOWING``. Glactar le "
"sláimhreacha dearfacha le haghaidh ``deireadh ``agus bíonn `N FOLLOWING`` "
"mar thoradh air. I mód ``ROWS`, is féidir sláimhir dhiúltach a úsáid le "
"haghaidh ``deireadh ``mar thoradh air sin ``N ROIMH``. Maidir le ``tosa`` "
"agus ``deireadh ``araon, fillfidh nialas ``CURRENT ROW``."

