"Cuireadh tacaíocht do shláimhir dearfach ```tús ``agus sláimhir dhiúltach "
"``deireadh`` le haghaidh `Rowrange``."

msgid "Technical Information"
msgstr "Eolas Teicniúil"

msgid ""
"Below you'll find technical implementation details that may be useful to "
"library authors. The technical API and examples below will help with "
"creating generic query expressions that can extend the built-in "
"functionality that Django provides."
msgstr ""
"Anseo thíos gheobhaidh tú sonraí feidhme teicniúla a d'fhéadfadh a bheith "
"úsáideach d'údair leabharlainne Cuideoidh an API teicniúil agus na samplaí "
"thíos le nathanna ceisteanna cineálacha a chruthú ar féidir leo an "
"fheidhmiúlacht ionsuite a sholáthraíonn Django"

msgid "Expression API"
msgstr "API léiriú"

msgid ""
"Query expressions implement the :ref:`query expression API <query-"
"expression>`, but also expose a number of extra methods and attributes "
"listed below. All query expressions must inherit from ``Expression()`` or a "
"relevant subclass."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann nathanna fiosrúcháin an: ref: `abairt fiosraithe API <query-"
"expression>`i bhfeidhm, ach nochtann roinnt modhanna agus tréithe breise atá "
"liostaithe thíos freisin. Caithfidh gach abairt fiosrúcháin a oidhreacht ó "
"``Expression () ``nó ó fho-aicme ábhartha."

msgid ""
"When a query expression wraps another expression, it is responsible for "
"calling the appropriate methods on the wrapped expression."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a fhilleann abairt fiosrúcháin abairt eile, tá sé freagrach as na "
"modhanna cuí a ghlaoch ar an abairt fillte."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression can be used in :attr:`Field.db_default`. "
"Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django gur féidir an abairt seo a úsáid in:attr: "
"`Field.db_default`. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression can be used during a constraint "
"validation. Expressions with ``constraint_validation_compatible`` set to "
"``False`` must have only one source expression. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django gur féidir an abairt seo a úsáid le linn bailíochtú "
"srianta. Ní mór ach abairt foinse amháin a bheith ag abhairtí le "
"``restricint_validation_compatible`` atá socraithe go ``False``. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression contains an aggregate and that a ``GROUP "
"BY`` clause needs to be added to the query."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django go bhfuil comhiomlán sa abairt seo agus gur gá clásal "
"`GROUP BY ``a chur leis an gceist."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression contains "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.Window` expression. It's used, for "
"example, to disallow window function expressions in queries that modify data."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django go bhfuil a: aicme: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Expressions.Window` léiriú sa abairt seo. Úsáidtear é, "
"mar shampla, chun nathanna feidhme fuinneoige a dhícheadú i gceisteanna a "
"mhodhnóidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression can be referenced "
"in :meth:`.QuerySet.filter`. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django gur féidir tagairt a thabhairt don abairt seo in:meth: "
"`.querySet.filter`. Réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression can be used as the source expression "
"in :class:`~django.db.models.expressions.Window`. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django gur féidir an abairt seo a úsáid mar an abairt foinse "
"in:class: `~Django.db.Models.Expressions.Window`. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``False``."

msgid ""
"Tells Django which value should be returned when the expression is used to "
"apply a function over an empty result set. Defaults "
"to :py:data:`NotImplemented` which forces the expression to be computed on "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé le Django cén luach ba chóir a thabhairt ar ais nuair a úsáidtear "
"an abairt chun feidhm a chur i bhfeidhm thar shraith torthaí folamh. "
"Réamhshocraithe to:py:data: `NotImplemented` a chuireann iallach ar an "
"abairt a ríomh ar an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression contains a set-returning function, "
"enforcing subquery evaluation. It's used, for example, to allow some "
"Postgres set-returning functions (e.g. ``JSONB_PATH_QUERY``, ``UNNEST``, "
"etc.) to skip optimization and be properly evaluated when annotations spawn "
"rows themselves. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tells Django that this expression allows composite expressions, for example, "
"to support :ref:`composite primary keys <cpk-and-database-functions>`. "
"Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Provides the chance to do any preprocessing or validation of the expression "
"before it's added to the query. ``resolve_expression()`` must also be called "
"on any nested expressions. A ``copy()`` of ``self`` should be returned with "
"any necessary transformations."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn sé deis aon réamhphróiseáil nó bailíochtú an abairt a dhéanamh "
"sula gcuirtear é leis an bhfiosrú. Ní mór ``resolve_expression () ``a "
"ghlaoch freisin ar aon nathanna neadaithe. Ba chóir ``cóip () ``de ``féin`` "
"a thabhairt ar ais le haon claochlú riachtanach."

msgid "``query`` is the backend query implementation."
msgstr "Is é ``fiosraithe`` cur i bhfeidhm na ceisteanna cúltaca."

msgid ""
"``allow_joins`` is a boolean that allows or denies the use of joins in the "
"query."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é `allow_joins`` a cheadaíonn nó a dhiúltaíonn úsáid "
"comhpháirteanna sa cheist."

msgid "``reuse`` is a set of reusable joins for multi-join scenarios."
msgstr ""
"Is sraith de chomhpháirteanna in-athúsáidte é ``athúsáid` le haghaidh "
"cásanna ilcheangailte."

msgid ""
"``summarize`` is a boolean that, when ``True``, signals that the query being "
"computed is a terminal aggregate query."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é ``achoimre ``a thugann comharthaíocht, nuair a dhéanann "
"``True``, gur ceist chomhiomlán críochfoirt é an cheist atá á ríomh."

msgid ""
"``for_save`` is a boolean that, when ``True``, signals that the query being "
"executed is performing a create or update."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é ``for_save`` a thugann comharthaíocht, nuair a dhéanann "
"``True``, go bhfuil an ceist atá á fhorghníomhú ag déanamh cruthú nó "
"nuashonrú."

msgid "Returns an ordered list of inner expressions. For example:"
msgstr "Tugann liosta ordaithe de nathanna istigh ar ais. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Takes a list of expressions and stores them such that "
"``get_source_expressions()`` can return them."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé liosta nathanna agus stóráilíonn sé iad ionas gur féidir le "
"``get_source_expressions () ``iad a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"Returns a clone (copy) of ``self``, with any column aliases relabeled. "
"Column aliases are renamed when subqueries are created. "
"``relabeled_clone()`` should also be called on any nested expressions and "
"assigned to the clone."
msgstr ""
"Tugann clón (cóip) de ``féin`` ar ais, le haon ainmneacha colún "
"athlipéadaithe. Athainmnítear ainmneacha colún nuair a chruthaítear fo-"
"cheisteanna. Ba chóir ``relabeled_clone () ``a ghlaoch freisin ar aon "
"nathanna neadaithe agus a shannadh don chlón."

msgid "``change_map`` is a dictionary mapping old aliases to new aliases."
msgstr ""
"Is foclóir é ``change_map`` a mhapáil sean-ainmneacha chuig ainmneacha nua."

msgid ""
"A hook allowing the expression to coerce ``value`` into a more appropriate "
"type."
msgstr "Crúca a ligeann don abairt “luach” a chur i gcrích níos oiriúnaí."

msgid "``expression`` is the same as ``self``."
msgstr "Tá ``léirithe`` mar an gcéanna le ``féin``."

msgid ""
"Responsible for returning the list of columns references by this expression. "
"``get_group_by_cols()`` should be called on any nested expressions. ``F()`` "
"objects, in particular, hold a reference to a column."
msgstr ""
"Freagrach as liosta na dtagairtí colúin a thabhairt ar ais leis an abairt "
"seo. Ba chóir ``get_group_by_cols () ``a ghlaoch ar aon abairtí neadaithe. "
"Tá tagairt do cholún go háirithe ag rudaí ``F () `."

msgid "Returns the expression ready to be sorted in ascending order."
msgstr "Filleann sé an abairt atá réidh le sórtáil in ord ardaitheach."

msgid ""
"``nulls_first`` and ``nulls_last`` define how null values are sorted. "
"See :ref:`using-f-to-sort-null-values` for example usage."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn ``nulls_first`` agus ``nulls_last`` conas a shórtáiltear "
"luachanna null. Féach:ref: `using-f-to-sort-null-values` mar shampla úsáid."

msgid "Returns the expression ready to be sorted in descending order."
msgstr "Filleann sé an abairt atá réidh le sórtáil in ord íslitheach."

msgid ""
"Returns ``self`` with any modifications required to reverse the sort order "
"within an ``order_by`` call. As an example, an expression implementing "
"``NULLS LAST`` would change its value to be ``NULLS FIRST``. Modifications "
"are only required for expressions that implement sort order like "
"``OrderBy``. This method is called "
"when :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.reverse()` is called on a "
"queryset."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé “féin” ar ais le haon mhodhnuithe a theastaíonn chun an t-ordú "
"sórtála a aisiompú laistigh de ghlao ``order_by``. Mar shampla, athródh "
"abairt a chur i bhfeidhm ``NULLS LAST`` a luach go `NULLS FIRST``. Ní "
"theastaíonn modhnuithe ach le haghaidh nathanna a chuireann ord sórtála i "
"bhfeidhm mar `Orderby``. Tugtar an modh seo nuair a ghlaítear: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.reverse () `ar fhiosraith."

msgid "Writing your own Query Expressions"
msgstr "Scríobh do chuid Nathanna Fiosrúcháin"

msgid ""
"You can write your own query expression classes that use, and can integrate "
"with, other query expressions. Let's step through an example by writing an "
"implementation of the ``COALESCE`` SQL function, without using the built-"
"in :ref:`Func() expressions <func-expressions>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat d'aicmí léirithe fiosrúcháin féin a scríobh a úsáideann "
"nathanna fiosrúcháin eile agus is féidir leo comhtháthú leo. <func-"
"expressions>Déanaimis céim trí shampla trí chur i bhfeidhm an fheidhm "
"``COALESCE`` SQL a scríobh, gan na nathanna ionsuite: ref: `Func () `a úsáid."

msgid ""
"The ``COALESCE`` SQL function is defined as taking a list of columns or "
"values. It will return the first column or value that isn't ``NULL``."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear an fheidhm SQL `COALESCE`` mar liosta de cholúin nó luachanna "
"a ghlacadh. Cuirfidh sé an chéad cholún nó an luach ar ais nach ``NULL``."

msgid ""
"We'll start by defining the template to be used for SQL generation and an "
"``__init__()`` method to set some attributes::"
msgstr ""
"Tosóimid tríd an teimpléad atá le húsáid le haghaidh giniúint SQL agus modh "
"``__init__ () ``a shainiú chun roinnt tréithe a shocrú:"

msgid ""
"We do some basic validation on the parameters, including requiring at least "
"2 columns or values, and ensuring they are expressions. We are "
"requiring :ref:`output_field<output-field>` here so that Django knows what "
"kind of model field to assign the eventual result to."
msgstr ""
"Déanaimid roinnt bailíochtú bunúsach ar na paraiméadair, lena n-áirítear 2 "
"cholún nó luach ar a laghad a éileamh, agus a chinntiú gur nathanna iad "
"Táimid ag iarraidh:ref: `output_field <output-field>`anseo ionas go mbeidh a "
"fhios ag Django cén cineál réimse samhail chun an toradh deiridh a shannadh "
"dó."

msgid ""
"Now we implement the preprocessing and validation. Since we do not have any "
"of our own validation at this point, we delegate to the nested expressions::"
msgstr ""
"Anois cuirimid an réamhphróiseáil agus bailíochtú i bhfeidhm. Ós rud é nach "
"bhfuil aon cheann dár mbailíochtú féin againn ag an bpointe seo, tarmligimid "
"chuig na nathanna neadaithe:"

msgid "Next, we write the method responsible for generating the SQL::"
msgstr "Ansin, scríobhaimid an modh atá freagrach as an SQL a ghiniúint::"

msgid ""
"``as_sql()`` methods can support custom keyword arguments, allowing "
"``as_vendorname()`` methods to override data used to generate the SQL "
"string. Using ``as_sql()`` keyword arguments for customization is preferable "
"to mutating ``self`` within ``as_vendorname()`` methods as the latter can "
"lead to errors when running on different database backends. If your class "
"relies on class attributes to define data, consider allowing overrides in "
"your ``as_sql()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le modhanna ``as_sql () ``tacú le hargóintí saincheaptha "
"eochairfhocal, rud a ligeann do mhodhanna ``as_vendorname ()`` sonraí a "
"úsáidtear chun an teaghrán SQL a ghiniúint a shárú. Is fearr argóintí "
"eochairfhocal ``as_sql () ``a úsáid le haghaidh saincheaptha ná ``self`` a "
"athrú laistigh de mhodhanna `as_vendorname ()`` mar is féidir earráidí a "
"bheith mar thoradh ar an dara ceann agus iad ag rith ar chúlpháirteanna "
"éagsúla bunachar sonraí. Má bhíonn do rang ag brath ar thréithe ranga chun "
"sonraí a shainiú, smaoinigh ar sháraitheanna a cheadú i do mhodh `as_sql () "
"``."

msgid ""
"We generate the SQL for each of the ``expressions`` by using the "
"``compiler.compile()`` method, and join the result together with commas. "
"Then the template is filled out with our data and the SQL and parameters are "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Gineann muid an SQL do gach ceann de na “léirithe” tríd an modh "
"``compiler.compiler.compiler () ``a úsáid, agus cuirimid an toradh in "
"éineacht le camóga. Ansin líontar an teimpléad lenár sonraí agus cuirtear an "
"SQL agus na paraiméadair ar ais."

msgid ""
"We've also defined a custom implementation that is specific to the Oracle "
"backend. The ``as_oracle()`` function will be called instead of ``as_sql()`` "
"if the Oracle backend is in use."
msgstr ""
"Tá cur i bhfeidhm saincheaptha sainmhínithe againn freisin atá sonrach don "
"chúlcheann Oracle. Glaofar an fheidhm ``as_oracle () ``in ionad ``as_sql "
"()`` má tá cúltaca Oracle in úsáid."

msgid ""
"Finally, we implement the rest of the methods that allow our query "
"expression to play nice with other query expressions::"
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, cuirimid an chuid eile de na modhanna i bhfeidhm a ligeann "
"dár léiriú ceisteanna imirt go deas le nathanna ceisteanna eile::"

msgid "Let's see how it works:"
msgstr "Feicfimid conas a oibríonn sé:"

msgid "Avoiding SQL injection"
msgstr "Instealladh SQL a sheachaint"

msgid ""
"Since a ``Func``'s keyword arguments for ``__init__()``  (``**extra``) and "
"``as_sql()`` (``**extra_context``) are interpolated into the SQL string "
"rather than passed as query parameters (where the database driver would "
"escape them), they must not contain untrusted user input."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go ndéantar argóintí eochairfhocal ``Func`` do `__init__ () "
"``(``**extra_context``)`` (``**extra_context``) idirphóilte isteach sa "
"teaghrán SQL seachas a rith mar pharaiméadair cheistiúcháin (áit a n-éalfadh "
"an tiománaí bunachar sonraí iad), ní mór ionchur úsáideora neamhiontaofa "
"iontu."

msgid ""
"For example, if ``substring`` is user-provided, this function is vulnerable "
"to SQL injection::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má sholáthraítear ``foshraithe`` ón úsáideoir, tá an fheidhm "
"seo leochaileach do instealladh SQL:"

msgid ""
"This function generates an SQL string without any parameters. Since "
"``substring`` is passed to ``super().__init__()`` as a keyword argument, "
"it's interpolated into the SQL string before the query is sent to the "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Gineann an fheidhm seo teaghrán SQL gan aon pharaiméadair. Ós rud é go "
"gcuirtear ``foshraithe`` ar aghaidh chuig ``super (). __init__ () ``mar "
"argóint eochairfhocal, déantar é a idirphóladh isteach sa teaghrán SQL sula "
"seoltar an cheist chuig an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid "Here's a corrected rewrite::"
msgstr "Seo athscríobh ceartaithe::"

msgid ""
"With ``substring`` instead passed as a positional argument, it'll be passed "
"as a parameter in the database query."
msgstr ""
"Le “foshraitheacht” a rith mar argóint seasaimh ina ionad sin, cuirfear ar "
"aghaidh mar pharaiméadar san fhiosrúchán bunachar sonraí."

msgid "Adding support in third-party database backends"
msgstr "Tacaíocht a chur i gcúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú"

msgid ""
"If you're using a database backend that uses a different SQL syntax for a "
"certain function, you can add support for it by monkey patching a new method "
"onto the function's class."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cúltaca bunachar sonraí á úsáid agat a úsáideann comhréir SQL difriúil "
"le haghaidh feidhm áirithe, is féidir leat tacaíocht a chur leis trí mhoncaí "
"modh nua a phaiteáil ar rang na feidhme."

msgid ""
"Let's say we're writing a backend for Microsoft's SQL Server which uses the "
"SQL ``LEN`` instead of ``LENGTH`` for the :class:`~functions.Length` "
"function. We'll monkey patch a new method called ``as_sqlserver()`` onto the "
"``Length`` class::"
msgstr ""
"Abair go bhfuilimid ag scríobh cúltaca do Freastalaí SQL Microsoft a "
"úsáideann an SQL ``LEN`` in ionad ``LENGTH`` don fheidhme:class: "
"`~functions.LENGTH`. Déanfaimid moncaí modh nua ar a dtugtar ``as_sqlserver "
"() ``a phaisteáil ar an rang ``Length``:"

msgid ""
"You can also customize the SQL using the ``template`` parameter of "
"``as_sql()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an SQL a shaincheapadh freisin ag baint úsáide as an "
"paraiméadar ``teimpléad`` de `as_sql () ``."

msgid ""
"We use ``as_sqlserver()`` because ``django.db.connection.vendor`` returns "
"``sqlserver`` for the backend."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidimid ``as_sqlserver () ``toisc go bhfilleann "
"``django.db.connection.vendor`` ``sqlserver`` don chúltaca."

msgid ""
"Third-party backends can register their functions in the top level "
"``__init__.py`` file of the backend package or in a top level "
"``expressions.py`` file (or package) that is imported from the top level "
"``__init__.py``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le cúltaca tríú páirtí a gcuid feidhmeanna a chlárú i gcomhad "
"``__init__.py`` barr leibhéal an phacáiste cúltaca nó i gcomhad "
"``expressions.py`` barr leibhéal (nó pacáiste) a allmhairítear ón leibhéal "
"barr ``__init__.py``."

msgid ""
"For user projects wishing to patch the backend that they're using, this code "
"should live in an :meth:`AppConfig.ready()<django.apps.AppConfig.ready>` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"<django.apps.AppConfig.ready>Maidir le tionscadail úsáideora atá ag iarraidh "
"an cúltaca atá á úsáid acu a phaiseáil, ba chóir go mbeadh an cód seo i "
"modh: meth: `AppConfig.ready () `."

msgid "Model field reference"
msgstr "Tagairt réimse múnla"

msgid ""
"This document contains all the API references of :class:`Field` including "
"the `field options`_ and `field types`_ Django offers."
msgstr ""
"Tá na tagairtí API go léir sa doiciméad seo de:class: `Field` lena n-"
"áirítear na `roghanna réimse`_ agus `cineálacha réimse`_ a thairgeann Django."

msgid ""
"If the built-in fields don't do the trick, you can try :pypi:`django-"
"localflavor` (`documentation <https://django-localflavor.readthedocs.io/"
">`_), which contains assorted pieces of code that are useful for particular "
"countries and cultures."
msgstr ""
"Mura ndéanann na réimsí ionsuite an cleas, is féidir leat triail a bhaint "
"aith:pypi: `django-localflavor` (`documentation`_ < https://django-"
"localflavor.readthedocs.io/>), ina bhfuil píosaí éagsúla cód atá úsáideach "
"do thíortha agus cultúir áirithe."

msgid ""
"Also, you can easily :doc:`write your own custom model fields </howto/custom-"
"model-fields>`."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, is féidir leat go héasca: doc: `scríobh do réimsí "
"samhail saincheaptha féin`. </howto/custom-model-fields>"

msgid ""
"Fields are defined in :mod:`django.db.models.fields`, but for convenience "
"they're imported into :mod:`django.db.models`. The standard convention is to "
"use ``from django.db import models`` and refer to fields as ``models."
"<Foo>Field``."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear réimsí in:mod: `django.db.models.fields`, ach ar mhaithe le "
"háisiúlacht déantar iad a allmhairiú chuig: mod: `django.db.models`. Is é an "
"coinbhinsiún caighdeánach ná ``ó samhlacha allmhairiúcháin django.db ``a "
"úsáid agus tagairt a dhéanamh do réimsí mar `samhlacha. <Foo>Réimse ``."

msgid "Field options"
msgstr "Roghanna réimse"

msgid ""
"The following arguments are available to all field types. All are optional."
msgstr ""
"Tá na hargóintí seo a leanas ar fáil do gach cineál réimse. Tá gach ceann "
"roghnach."

msgid "``null``"
msgstr "``Null``"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, Django will store empty values as ``NULL`` in the database. "
"Default is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, stóráilfidh Django luachanna folmha mar ``NULL`` sa "
"bhunachar sonraí. Is é “False” réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Avoid using :attr:`~Field.null` on string-based fields such "
"as :class:`CharField` and :class:`TextField`. The Django convention is to "
"use an empty string, not ``NULL``, as the \"no data\" state for string-based "
"fields. If a string-based field has ``null=False``, empty strings can still "
"be saved for \"no data\". If a string-based field has ``null=True``, that "
"means it has two possible values for \"no data\": ``NULL``, and the empty "
"string. In most cases, it's redundant to have two possible values for \"no "
"data\". One exception is when a :class:`CharField` has both ``unique=True`` "
"and ``blank=True`` set. In this situation, ``null=True`` is required to "
"avoid unique constraint violations when saving multiple objects with blank "
"values."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For both string-based and non-string-based fields, you will also need to set "
"``blank=True`` if you wish to permit empty values in forms, as "
"the :attr:`~Field.null` parameter only affects database storage "
"(see :attr:`~Field.blank`)."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí sreanga-bhunaithe agus neamh-shreanga-bhunaithe araon, "
"beidh ort ``Blank = True`` a shocrú más mian leat luachanna folmha a cheadú "
"i bhfoirmeacha, mar ní théann an paraiméadar: attr: `~field.null` ach ar "
"stóráil bunachar sonraí (féach: attr: `~field.blank`)."

msgid ""
"When using the Oracle database backend, the value ``NULL`` will be stored to "
"denote the empty string regardless of this attribute."
msgstr ""
"Agus cúltaca bunachar sonraí Oracle á úsáid agat, stóráilfear an luach "
"``NULL`` chun an teaghrán folamh a léiriú beag beann ar an tréith seo."

msgid "``blank``"
msgstr "``blank``"

msgid "If ``True``, the field is allowed to be blank. Default is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá “Fíor”, ceadaítear don réimse a bheith bán. Is é “False” "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Note that this is different than :attr:`~Field.null`. :attr:`~Field.null` is "
"purely database-related, whereas :attr:`~Field.blank` is validation-related. "
"If a field has ``blank=True``, form validation will allow entry of an empty "
"value. If a field has ``blank=False``, the field will be required."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil sé seo difriúil ná: attr: `~Field.null`. :attr: "
"`~Field.null` a bhaineann le bunachar sonraí amháin, áit a bhaineann le "
"bailíochtú: attr: `~Field.blank`. Má tá ``Blank=True`` i réimse, ligfidh "
"bailíochtú foirm luach folamh a iontráil. Má tá ``blank=false ``i réimse, "
"beidh an réimse ag teastáil."

msgid "Supplying missing values"
msgstr "Luachanna atá in easnamh a"

msgid ""
"``blank=True`` can be used with fields having ``null=False``, but this will "
"require implementing :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.clean` on the model in "
"order to programmatically supply any missing values."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ``Blank=True`` a úsáid le réimsí a bhfuil `Null=False``, ach beidh "
"gá aige seo: meth: `~django.db.models.model.clean` a chur i bhfeidhm ar an "
"tsamhail d'fhonn aon luachanna atá in easnamh a sholáthar go clárach."

msgid "``choices``"
msgstr "``roghnaí``"

msgid ""
"A mapping or iterable in the format described below to use as choices for "
"this field. If choices are given, they're enforced by :ref:`model validation "
"<validating-objects>` and the default form widget will be a select box with "
"these choices instead of the standard text field."
msgstr ""
"Mapáil nó athraitheach san fhormáid a thuairiscítear thíos le húsáid mar "
"roghanna don réimse seo. Má thugtar roghanna, déantar iad a fhorfhe "
"<validating-objects>idhmiú trí:ref: `bailíochtú samhail `agus is bosca "
"roghnaithe is é an giuirléid fhoirme réamhshocraithe leis na roghanna seo in "
"ionad an réimse téacs caighdeánach."

msgid ""
"If a mapping is given, the key element is the actual value to be set on the "
"model, and the second element is the human readable name. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má thugtar mapáil, is é an príomhghné an luach iarbhír atá le socrú ar an "
"tsamhail, agus is é an dara gné an t-ainm inléite don duine. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"You can also pass a :term:`sequence` consisting itself of iterables of "
"exactly two items (e.g. ``[(A1, B1), (A2, B2), …]``). The first element in "
"each tuple is the actual value to be set on the model, and the second "
"element is the human-readable name. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat: téarma a rith freisin: `seicheamh` ina bhfuil athrá de dhá "
"mhír díreach (m.sh. ``[(A1, B1), (A2, B2),...]``). Is é an chéad eilimint i "
"ngach tuple an luach iarbhír atá le socrú ar an tsamhail, agus is é an dara "
"gné an t-ainm inléite le duine. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"``choices`` can also be defined as a callable that expects no arguments and "
"returns any of the formats described above. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir “roghanna” a shainiú freisin mar ghlaoiteoir nach bhfuil ag súil "
"le haon argóintí agus nach bhfilleann aon cheann de na formáidí a "
"thuairiscítear thuas. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Passing a callable for ``choices`` can be particularly handy when, for "
"example, the choices are:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir go mbeadh sé áisiúil go háirithe le haghaidh “roghanna” a rith "
"nuair is iad, mar shampla, na roghanna seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"the result of I/O-bound operations (which could potentially be cached), such "
"as querying a table in the same or an external database, or accessing the "
"choices from a static file."
msgstr ""
"toradh oibríochtaí I/O-cheangailte (a d'fhéadfaí a choscáil), mar shampla "
"tábla a cheistiú sa bhunachar sonraí céanna nó sa bhunachar sonraí "
"seachtrach, nó rochtain a fháil ar na roghanna ó chomhad statach."

msgid ""
"a list that is mostly stable but could vary from time to time or from "
"project to project. Examples in this category are using third-party apps "
"that provide a well-known inventory of values, such as currencies, "
"countries, languages, time zones, etc."
msgstr ""
"liosta atá cobhsaí den chuid is mó ach a d'fhéadfadh athrú ó am go ham nó ó "
"thionscadal go tionscadal. Is iad samplaí sa chatagóir seo aipeanna tríú "
"páirtí a úsáid a sholáthraíonn fardal aitheanta luachanna, mar shampla "
"airgeadraí, tíortha, teangacha, criosanna ama, srl."

msgid ""
"Generally, it's best to define choices inside a model class, and to define a "
"suitably-named constant for each value::"
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, is fearr roghanna a shainiú taobh istigh de rang samhail, "
"agus tairiseach ainmnithe go cuí a shainiú do gach luach:"

msgid ""
"Though you can define a choices list outside of a model class and then refer "
"to it, defining the choices and names for each choice inside the model class "
"keeps all of that information with the class that uses it, and helps "
"reference the choices (e.g, ``Student.SOPHOMORE`` will work anywhere that "
"the ``Student`` model has been imported)."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir leat liosta roghanna a shainiú lasmuigh de rang samhail agus "
"tagairt a dhéanamh dó, coinníonn na roghanna agus ainmneacha do gach rogha "
"laistigh den rang samhail an fhaisnéis sin go léir leis an rang a úsáideann "
"í, agus cabhraíonn sé leis na roghanna a thagairt (m.sh., oibreoidh "
"``Student.sophomore`` áit ar bith a allmhairigh an tsamhail ``Student``)."

msgid ""
"You can also collect your available choices into named groups that can be "
"used for organizational purposes::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat na roghanna atá ar fáil a bhailiú i ngrúpaí ainmnithe is "
"féidir iad a úsáid chun críocha eagraíochtúla:"

msgid ""
"The key of the mapping is the name to apply to the group and the value is "
"the choices inside that group, consisting of the field value and a human-"
"readable name for an option. Grouped options may be combined with ungrouped "
"options within a single mapping (such as the ``\"unknown\"`` option in this "
"example)."
msgstr ""
"Is é eochair na mapála an t-ainm atá le cur i bhfeidhm ar an ngrúpa agus is "
"é an luach na roghanna taobh istigh den ghrúpa sin, comhdhéanta de luach an "
"réimse agus ainm inléite don duine le haghaidh rogha. Is féidir roghanna "
"grúpáilte a chomhcheangal le roghanna neamhghrúpáilte laistigh de mhapáil "
"amháin (mar shampla an rogha ``\"neamhfhiosna\"` sa sampla seo)."

msgid "You can also use a sequence, e.g. a list of 2-tuples::"
msgstr "Is féidir leat seicheamh a úsáid freisin, m.sh. liosta de 2-tuples::"

msgid ""
"Note that choices can be any sequence object -- not necessarily a list or "
"tuple. This lets you construct choices dynamically. But if you find yourself "
"hacking :attr:`~Field.choices` to be dynamic, you're probably better off "
"using a proper database table with "
"a :class:`ForeignKey`. :attr:`~Field.choices` is meant for static data that "
"doesn't change much, if ever."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur féidir le roghanna a bheith ina réad seicheamh ar "
"bith - ní gá gur liosta nó tuple. Ligeann sé seo duit roghanna a thógáil go "
"dinim Ach má aimsíonn tú féin ag hacáil: attr: `~field.choices` a bheith "
"dinimiciúil, is dócha go mbeidh tú níos fearr tábla bunachar sonraí ceart a "
"úsáid le a:class: `ForeignKey`. :attr: Tá `~Field.choices` i gceist le "
"haghaidh sonraí statacha nach n-athraíonn mórán, más riamh."

msgid "A new migration is created each time the order of ``choices`` changes."
msgstr "Cruthaítear imirce nua gach uair a athraíonn ord na “roghanna”."

msgid ""
"For each model field that has :attr:`~Field.choices` set, Django will "
"normalize the choices to a list of 2-tuples and add a method to retrieve the "
"human-readable name for the field's current value. "
"See :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.get_FOO_display` in the database API "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"I gcás gach réimse samhail a bhfuil: attr: `~ field.choices` tacar aige, "
"normalóidh Django na roghanna le liosta de 2-tuples agus cuirfidh sé modh "
"chun an t-ainm inléite don duine a aisghabháil do luach reatha an réimse. "
"Féach: Meth: `~django.db.models.model.get_foo_display` sa cháipéisíocht API "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Unless :attr:`blank=False<Field.blank>` is set on the field along with "
"a :attr:`~Field.default` then a label containing ``\"---------\"`` will be "
"rendered with the select box. To override this behavior, add a tuple to "
"``choices`` containing ``None``; e.g. ``(None, 'Your String For Display')``. "
"Alternatively, you can use an empty string instead of ``None`` where this "
"makes sense - such as on a :class:`~django.db.models.CharField`."
msgstr ""
"Unless:attr: `Blank = Fal <Field.blank>se `socraítear ar an réimse in "
"éineacht le a:attr: `~field.default` ansin déanfar lipéad ina bhfuil ``” "
"---------\"`` a rinneadh leis an mbosca roghnaithe. Chun an t-iompar seo a "
"shárú, cuir tuple le ``roghnaí`` ina bhfuil ``None``; m.sh. ``(Níl aon, 'Do "
"String Le Taispeán')``. De rogha air sin, is féidir leat teaghrán folamh a "
"úsáid in ionad ``None`` nuair a bhíonn ciall leis seo - mar shampla ar "
"a:class: `~django.db.models.charfield`."

msgid "Enumeration types"
msgstr "Cineálacha áireamh"

msgid ""
"In addition, Django provides enumeration types that you can subclass to "
"define choices in a concise way::"
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, soláthraíonn Django cineálacha áireamh ar féidir leat a "
"fho-aicmiú chun roghanna a shainiú ar bhealach gonta:"

msgid ""
"These work similar to :mod:`enum` from Python's standard library, but with "
"some modifications:"
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn siad seo cosúil le:mod: `enum` ó leabharlann caighdeánach Python, "
"ach le roinnt modhnuithe:"

msgid ""
"Enum member values are a tuple of arguments to use when constructing the "
"concrete data type. Django supports adding an extra string value to the end "
"of this tuple to be used as the human-readable name, or ``label``. The "
"``label`` can be a lazy translatable string. Thus, in most cases, the member "
"value will be a ``(value, label)`` 2-tuple. See below for :ref:`an example "
"of subclassing choices <field-choices-enum-subclassing>` using a more "
"complex data type. If a tuple is not provided, or the last item is not a "
"(lazy) string, the ``label`` is :ref:`automatically generated <field-choices-"
"enum-auto-label>` from the member name."
msgstr ""
"Is cúpla argóintí iad luachanna ball Enum le húsáid agus an cineál sonraí "
"coincréite á thógáil. Tacaíonn Django le luach sreangán breise a chur le "
"deireadh an tuple seo le húsáid mar an t-ainm inléite don duine, nó "
"“lipéad”. Is féidir leis an `lipéad`` a bheith ina shreang leisciúil "
"inaistrithe. Dá bhrí sin, i bhformhór na gcásanna, is é an luach ball ná "
"``(luach, lipéad)`` 2-tuple. Féach thíos le haghaidh: ref: `sampla de "
"roghanna fo-aicmiúcháin <field-choices-enum-subclassing>`ag baint úsáide as "
"cineál sonraí níos casta. <field-choices-enum-auto-label>Mura gcuirtear "
"tuple ar fáil, nó mura bhfuil teaghrán (leisciúil) an mír deireanach, is é "
"an `lipéad``: ref: `ghintear go huathoibríoch `ó ainm an chomhalta."

msgid ""
"A ``.label`` property is added on values, to return the human-readable name."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear maoin `.label`` leis na luachanna, chun an t-ainm inléite don duine "
"a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"A number of custom properties are added to the enumeration classes -- "
"``.choices``, ``.labels``, ``.values``, and ``.names`` -- to make it easier "
"to access lists of those separate parts of the enumeration."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear roinnt airíonna saincheaptha leis na haicmí áireamh -- `.choices``, "
"`.labels``, `.values``, agus `.ainmne`` - chun go mbeidh sé níos éasca "
"rochtain a fháil ar liostaí de na codanna ar leithligh sin den áireamh."

msgid ""
"These property names cannot be used as member names as they would conflict."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir na hainmneacha maoine seo a úsáid mar ainmneacha ball mar go "
"mbeadh siad ag coinbhleacht."

msgid ""
"The use of :func:`enum.unique()` is enforced to ensure that values cannot be "
"defined multiple times. This is unlikely to be expected in choices for a "
"field."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear úsáid de:func: `enum.unique () `i bhfeidhm chun a chinntiú nach "
"féidir luachanna a shainiú arís agus arís eile. Ní dócha go mbeadh súil leis "
"seo i roghanna do réimse."

msgid ""
"Note that using ``YearInSchool.SENIOR``, ``YearInSchool['SENIOR']``, or "
"``YearInSchool('SR')`` to access or lookup enum members work as expected, as "
"do the ``.name`` and ``.value`` properties on the members."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go n-oibríonn úsáid ``YearinSchool.Senior``, "
"`YearinSchool ['SENIOR'] `, nó ``YearinSchool ('SR') ``chun rochtain a fháil "
"nó cuardach ar na baill mar a bhíothas ag súil leis, mar a dhéanann na "
"hairíonna `.name`` agus ``.value`` ar na baill."

msgid ""
"If you don't need to have the human-readable names translated, you can have "
"them inferred from the member name (replacing underscores with spaces and "
"using title-case):"
msgstr ""
"Mura gá duit na hainmneacha inléite don duine a aistriú, is féidir leat iad "
"a thabhairt chun cinn ó ainm an chomhalta (spásanna a chur in ionad béim "
"agus cás teidil a úsáid):"

msgid ""
"Since the case where the enum values need to be integers is extremely "
"common, Django provides an ``IntegerChoices`` class. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhfuil an cás ina gcaithfidh na luachanna enum a bheith ina "
"shláimhreacha thar a bheith coitianta, soláthraíonn Django aicme "
"``IntegerChoices`. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"It is also possible to make use of the `Enum Functional API <https://"
"docs.python.org/3/howto/enum.html#functional-api>`_ with the caveat that "
"labels are automatically generated as highlighted above:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir freisin úsáid a bhaint as an `Enum Functional API`_ leis an "
"rabhadh go ngintear lipéid go huathoibr< https://docs.python.org/3/howto/"
"enum.html#functional-api> íoch mar a leagtar béim thuas:"

msgid ""
"If you require support for a concrete data type other than ``int`` or "
"``str``, you can subclass ``Choices`` and the required concrete data type, "
"e.g. :class:`~datetime.date` for use "
"with :class:`~django.db.models.DateField`::"
msgstr ""
"Má theastaíonn tacaíocht uait do chineál sonraí coincréite seachas ``int`` "
"nó ``str``, is féidir leat fo-aicme ``Roghanna ``agus an cineál sonraí "
"coincréite riachtanach, e.g.:class: `~datetime.date` le húsáid le:class: "
"`~django.db.models.datefield`:"

msgid "There are some additional caveats to be aware of:"
msgstr "Tá roinnt rabhaidh breise le bheith ar an eolas faoi:"

msgid ""
"Enumeration types do not support :ref:`named groups <field-choices-named-"
"groups>`."
msgstr ""
"<field-choices-named-groups>Ní thacaíonn cineálacha áirim:ref: `grúpaí "
"ainmnithe `."

msgid ""
"Because an enumeration with a concrete data type requires all values to "
"match the type, overriding the :ref:`blank label <field-choices-blank-"
"label>` cannot be achieved by creating a member with a value of ``None``. "
"Instead, set the ``__empty__`` attribute on the class::"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go n-éilíonn áireamh le cineál sonraí coincréite go léir an cineál a "
"mheaitseáil, ní féidir an lipéad: ref: `blank <field-choices-blank-label>`a "
"bhaint amach trí bhall a chruthú le luach ``None``. Ina áit sin, socraigh an "
"tréith ``__empty__`` ar an rang:"

msgid "``db_column``"
msgstr "``db_column``"

msgid ""
"The name of the database column to use for this field. If this isn't given, "
"Django will use the field's name."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an cholún bunachar sonraí le húsáid don réimse seo. Mura dtugtar é seo, "
"úsáidfidh Django ainm an réimse."

msgid ""
"If your database column name is an SQL reserved word, or contains characters "
"that aren't allowed in Python variable names -- notably, the hyphen -- "
"that's OK. Django quotes column and table names behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Más focal fhorchoimeádaithe SQL é ainm do cholún bunachar sonraí, nó má tá "
"carachtair nach gceadaítear in ainmneacha athróg Python - go háirithe, an "
"bhreith - tá sin ceart go leor. Luann Django ainmneacha colún agus tábla "
"taobh thiar de na radhairc."

msgid "``db_comment``"
msgstr "``db_comment ``"

msgid ""
"The comment on the database column to use for this field. It is useful for "
"documenting fields for individuals with direct database access who may not "
"be looking at your Django code. For example::"
msgstr ""
"An trácht ar an gcolún bunachar sonraí le húsáid don réimse seo. Tá sé "
"úsáideach chun réimsí a dhoiciméadú do dhaoine aonair a bhfuil rochtain "
"dhíreach acu ar bhunachar sonraí nach bhfuil ag féachaint ar do chód Django. "
"Mar shampla::"

msgid "``db_default``"
msgstr "``db_default``"

msgid ""
"The database-computed default value for this field. This can be a literal "
"value or a database function, such "
"as :class:`~django.db.models.functions.Now`::"
msgstr ""
"An luach réamhshocraithe ríofa bunachar sonraí don réimse seo. Is féidir "
"leis seo a bheith ina luach litriúil nó ina fheidhm bunachar sonraí, mar "
"shampla:class: `~Django.db.Models.Functions.Now`:"

msgid ""
"More complex expressions can be used, as long as they are made from literals "
"and database functions::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir nathanna níos casta a úsáid, chomh fada agus a dhéantar iad ó "
"litríochtaí agus feidhmeanna bunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"Database defaults cannot reference other fields or models. For example, this "
"is invalid::"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le réamhshocraithe bunachar sonraí réimsí nó samhlacha eile "
"tagairt a dhéanamh. Mar shampla, tá sé seo neamhbhailí::"

msgid ""
"If both ``db_default`` and :attr:`Field.default` are set, ``default`` will "
"take precedence when creating instances in Python code. ``db_default`` will "
"still be set at the database level and will be used when inserting rows "
"outside of the ORM or when adding a new field in a migration."
msgstr ""
"Má tá `db_default`` agus:attr: `Field.default` araon socraithe, tabharfaidh "
"``default`` tosaíocht agus cásanna á chruthú i gcód Python. Socrófar "
"``db_default`` fós ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí agus úsáidfear é agus "
"sraitheanna á chur isteach lasmuigh den ORM nó nuair a chuirtear réimse nua "
"i imirce."

msgid ""
"If a field has a ``db_default`` without a ``default`` set and no value is "
"assigned to the field, a ``DatabaseDefault`` object is returned as the field "
"value on unsaved model instances. The actual value for the field is "
"determined by the database when the model instance is saved."
msgstr ""
"Má tá `db_default`` i réimse gan tacar ``default`` agus nach sanntar aon "
"luach don réimse, cuirtear réad ``databasedefault`` ar ais mar luach an "
"réimse ar chásanna samhail neamhshábháilte. Is é an bunachar sonraí a "
"chinneann an luach iarbhír don réimse nuair a shábháiltear an tsamhail "
"samhail."

msgid "``db_index``"
msgstr "``db_index``"

msgid "If ``True``, a database index will be created for this field."
msgstr "Má tá ``True``, cruthófar innéacs bunachar sonraí don réimse seo."

msgid "Use the :attr:`~Options.indexes` option instead."
msgstr "Úsáid an rogha: attr: `~Options.indexes` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Where possible, use the :attr:`Meta.indexes <Options.indexes>` option "
"instead. In nearly all cases, :attr:`~Options.indexes` provides more "
"functionality than ``db_index``. ``db_index`` may be deprecated in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"<Options.indexes>Nuair is féidir, bain úsáid as an roghna:attr: "
"`Meta.Indexes `ina ionad. I mbeagnach gach cás, soláthraíonn :attr: "
"`~Options.indexes` níos mó feidhmiúlachta ná `db_index ``. D'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh `db_index ``a dhíchur sa todhchaí."

msgid "``db_tablespace``"
msgstr "``db_tablespace``"

msgid ""
"The name of the :doc:`database tablespace </topics/db/tablespaces>` to use "
"for this field's index, if this field is indexed. The default is the "
"project's :setting:`DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE` setting, if set, or "
"the :attr:`~Options.db_tablespace` of the model, if any. If the backend "
"doesn't support tablespaces for indexes, this option is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an:doc: `database tablespace` le húsáid le haghaidh innéacs an réimse "
"seo </topics/db/tablespaces>, má tá an réimse seo innéacsaithe. Is é an "
"réamhshocrú an socrú tionscadla:setting: `DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE`, má tá "
"sé socraithe, nó an:attr: `~OPTIONS.DB_TABLESPACE` den tsamhail, más ann. "
"Mura dtacaíonn an cúltaca le spásanna tábla le haghaidh innéacsanna, déantar "
"neamhaird ar an rogha seo."

msgid "``default``"
msgstr "``réamhshocraithe``"

msgid ""
"The default value for the field. This can be a value or a callable object. "
"If callable it will be called every time a new object is created."
msgstr ""
"An luach réamhshocraithe don réimse. Is féidir leis seo a bheith ina luach "
"nó ina réad inghlaonta. Má tá sé inghlaoch, glaofar air gach uair a "
"chruthaítear réad nua."

msgid ""
"The default can't be a mutable object (model instance, ``list``, ``set``, "
"etc.), as a reference to the same instance of that object would be used as "
"the default value in all new model instances. Instead, wrap the desired "
"default in a callable. For example, if you want to specify a default "
"``dict`` for :class:`~django.db.models.JSONField`, use a function::"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leis an réamhshocrú a bheith ina réad inathraithe (sampla samhail, "
"``liost``, `set``, srl.), Mar a úsáidfeadh tagairt don sampla céanna den "
"réad sin mar an luach réamhshocraithe i ngach cás samhail nua. Ina áit sin, "
"fillte an réamhshocrú atá ag teastáil i nglaoch inghlaonta Mar shampla, más "
"mian leat réamhshocraithe ``dict`` a shonrú fao:class: "
"`~django.db.models.jsonField`, bain úsáid as feidhm:"

msgid ""
"``lambda``\\s can't be used for field options like ``default`` because they "
"can't be :ref:`serialized by migrations <migration-serializing>`. See that "
"documentation for other caveats."
msgstr ""
"<migration-serializing>Ní féidir ``lambda``\\ s a úsáid le haghaidh roghanna "
"réimse cosúil le ``default`` toisc nach féidir leo a bheith: ref: `sraith ag "
"imirce `. Féach an doiciméadú sin le haghaidh rabhaidh eile."

msgid ""
"For fields like :class:`ForeignKey` that map to model instances, defaults "
"should be the value of the field they reference (``pk`` "
"unless :attr:`~ForeignKey.to_field` is set) instead of model instances."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí cosúil:class: `ForeignKey` a léarscáil chuig cásanna "
"samhail, ba chóir go mbeadh réamhshocraithe mar luach an réimse a thagraíonn "
"siad (``pk`` unless:attr: `~ForeignKey.to_field` socraítear) in ionad "
"cásanna samhail."

msgid ""
"The default value is used when new model instances are created and a value "
"isn't provided for the field. When the field is a primary key, the default "
"is also used when the field is set to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an luach réamhshocraithe nuair a chruthaítear cásanna samhail nua "
"agus nach gcuirtear luach ar fáil don réimse. Nuair is príomh-eochair é an "
"réimse, úsáidtear an réamhshocrú freisin nuair a shocraítear an réimse go "
"``None``."

msgid ""
"The default value can also be set at the database level "
"with :attr:`Field.db_default`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an luach réamhshocraithe a shocrú freisin ag leibhéal an bhunachar "
"sonraí le: attr: `Field.db_default`."

msgid "``editable``"
msgstr "``Eagarthóireach``"

msgid ""
"If ``False``, the field will not be displayed in the admin or any "
"other :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`. It will also be skipped "
"during :ref:`model validation <validating-objects>`. Default is ``True``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ``error_messages`` argument lets you override the default messages that "
"the field will raise. Pass in a dictionary with keys matching the error "
"messages you want to override."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an argóint ``error_messages`` duit na teachtaireachtaí "
"réamhshocraithe a ardóidh an réimse a shárú. Pas isteach i bhfoclóir le "
"heochracha a mheaitseálann leis na teachtaireachtaí earráide is mian leat a "
"shárú."

msgid ""
"Error message keys include ``null``, ``blank``, ``invalid``, "
"``invalid_choice``, ``unique``, and ``unique_for_date``. Additional error "
"message keys are specified for each field in the `Field types`_ section "
"below."
msgstr ""
"I measc na heochracha teachtaireachta earráide tá ``null``, `blank``, "
"`invalid``, `invalid_choice``, ``unique``, agus ``unique_for_date``. "
"Sonraítear eochracha teachtaireachta earráide breise do gach réimse sa chuid "
"`Cineálacha réimsea`_ thíos."

msgid ""
"These error messages often don't propagate to forms. "
"See :ref:`considerations-regarding-model-errormessages`."
msgstr ""
"Is minic nach n-iomadaíonn na teachtaireachtaí earráide seo chuig "
"foirmeacha. Féach:ref: `breithnitheachtaireachtaí maidir le samhail-earráidí "
"teachtaireachtaí `."

msgid ""
"Extra \"help\" text to be displayed with the form widget. It's useful for "
"documentation even if your field isn't used on a form."
msgstr ""
"Téacs breise “cabhrach” le taispeáint leis an ngiuirléid fhoirme. Tá sé "
"úsáideach le haghaidh doiciméadú fiú mura n-úsáidtear do réimse ar fhoirm."

msgid ""
"Note that this value is *not* HTML-escaped in automatically-generated forms. "
"This lets you include HTML in :attr:`~Field.help_text` if you so desire. For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil an luach seo* ag éalú HTML i bhfoirmeacha a "
"ghintear go huathoibríoch. Ligeann sé seo duit HTML a áireamh in:attr: "
"`~field.help_text` más mian leat. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Alternatively you can use plain text and :func:`django.utils.html.escape` to "
"escape any HTML special characters. Ensure that you escape any help text "
"that may come from untrusted users to avoid a cross-site scripting attack."
msgstr ""
"Nó is féidir leat gnáthtéacs agus: func: `django.utils.html.escape` a úsáid "
"chun éalú aon charachtair speisialta HTML. Cinntigh go n-éalaíonn tú aon "
"téacs cabhrach a d'fhéadfadh teacht ó úsáideoirí neamhiontaofa chun ionsaí "
"scripteála tras-láithreáin a sheachaint."

msgid "``primary_key``"
msgstr "``eochair_phríomh``"

msgid "If ``True``, this field is the primary key for the model."
msgstr "Má tá ``True``, is é an réimse seo an príomh-eochair don tsamhail."

msgid ""
"If you don't specify ``primary_key=True`` for any field in your model and "
"have not defined a composite primary key, Django will automatically add a "
"field to hold the primary key. So, you don't need to set "
"``primary_key=True`` on any of your fields unless you want to override the "
"default primary-key behavior. The type of auto-created primary key fields "
"can be specified per app in :attr:`AppConfig.default_auto_field "
"<django.apps.AppConfig.default_auto_field>` or globally in "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD` setting. For more, see :ref:`automatic-"
"primary-key-fields`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``primary_key=True`` implies :attr:`null=False <Field.null>` "
"and :attr:`unique=True <Field.unique>`. Only one field per model can set "
"``primary_key=True``. Composite primary keys must be defined "
"using :class:`CompositePrimaryKey` instead of setting this flag to ``True`` "
"for all fields to maintain this invariant."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The primary key field is read-only. If you change the value of the primary "
"key on an existing object and then save it, a new object will be created "
"alongside the old one."
msgstr ""
"Tá an príomhréimse léite amháin. Má athraíonn tú luach an phríomh-eochair ar "
"réad atá ann cheana agus ansin é a shábháil, cruthófar réad nua in éineacht "
"leis an seancheann."

msgid ""
"The primary key field is set to ``None`` when :meth:`deleting "
"<django.db.models.Model.delete>` an object."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.delete>Socraítear an príomhréimse go ``None`` "
"nuai:meth: ``scriosadh `réad."

msgid "The ``CompositePrimaryKey`` field was added."
msgstr ""

msgid "If ``True``, this field must be unique throughout the table."
msgstr ""
"Má tá “Fíor”, caithfidh an réimse seo a bheith uathúil ar fud an tábla."

msgid ""
"This is enforced at the database level and by model validation. If you try "
"to save a model with a duplicate value in a :attr:`~Field.unique` field, "
"a :exc:`django.db.IntegrityError` will be raised by the "
"model's :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` method."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear é seo i bhfeidhm ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí agus trí "
"bhailíochtú samhail Má dhéanann tú iarracht samhail a shábháil le luach "
"dúbailte i réimse a:attr: `~Field.Unique`, ardófar a:exc: "
"`Django.db.IntegrityError` ag an modh samhail 's:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.save`."

msgid ""
"This option is valid on all field types except :class:`ManyToManyField` "
"and :class:`OneToOneField`."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rogha seo bailí ar gach cineál réimse seachas: class: "
"`ManyTomanyField` agus:class: `OneToOneField`."

msgid ""
"Note that when ``unique`` is ``True``, you don't need to "
"specify :attr:`~Field.db_index`, because ``unique`` implies the creation of "
"an index."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil ``unique`` ``True``, ní gá duit:attr: "
"`~field.db_index` a shonrú, mar tugann ``unique`` le tuiscint go gcruthófar "
"innéacs."

msgid "``unique_for_date``"
msgstr "``uath_dáta`"

msgid ""
"Set this to the name of a :class:`DateField` or :class:`DateTimeField` to "
"require that this field be unique for the value of the date field."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é seo ar ainm a: class: `DateField` nó:class: `DateTimeField` chun "
"a cheangal go mbeidh an réimse seo uathúil do luach an réimse dáta."

msgid ""
"For example, if you have a field ``title`` that has "
"``unique_for_date=\"pub_date\"``, then Django wouldn't allow the entry of "
"two records with the same ``title`` and ``pub_date``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá réimse ``title`` agat a bhfuil "
"``unique_for_date=\"pub_date” ``, ansin ní cheadódh Django dhá thaifead a "
"iontráil leis an ``title`` agus ``pub_date`` céanna."

msgid ""
"Note that if you set this to point to a :class:`DateTimeField`, only the "
"date portion of the field will be considered. Besides, "
"when :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, the check will be performed in "
"the :ref:`current time zone <default-current-time-zone>` at the time the "
"object gets saved."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara má shocraíonn tú é seo chun díriú ar a: class: "
"`DateTimeField`, ní dhéanfar ach an chuid dáta den réimse a mheas. <default-"
"current-time-zone>Thairis sin, nuair a bhíonn: socrú: `USE_TZ` ``True``, "
"déanfar an seiceáil san: ref: `crios ama reatha `ag an am a shábháiltear an "
"réad."

msgid ""
"This is enforced by :meth:`Model.validate_unique()` during model validation "
"but not at the database level. If any :attr:`~Field.unique_for_date` "
"constraint involves fields that are not part of "
"a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` (for example, if one of the fields is "
"listed in ``exclude`` or "
"has :attr:`editable=False<Field.editable>`), :meth:`Model.validate_unique()` "
"will skip validation for that particular constraint."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear é seo i bhfeidhm ag: meth: `model.validate_unique () `le linn "
"bailíochtú samhail ach ní ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí. "
"<Field.editable>Más réimsí nach cuid de a:class: `~django.forms.modelForm: "
"`~django.forms.modelForm` (mar shampla, má tá ceann de na réimsí liostaithe "
"i ``exclude`` nó má aith:attr: `editable=false `), scipeánfaidh :meth: "
"`Model.validate_unique ()` bailíochtú don srian áirithe sin a ghearradh."

msgid "``unique_for_month``"
msgstr "``uach_ar feadh míosa``"

msgid ""
"Like :attr:`~Field.unique_for_date`, but requires the field to be unique "
"with respect to the month."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: attr: `~field.unique_for_date`, ach éilíonn sé go mbeadh an "
"réimse uathúil maidir leis an mí."

msgid "``unique_for_year``"
msgstr "``Unique_doir_bliana``"

msgid ""
"Like :attr:`~Field.unique_for_date` and :attr:`~Field.unique_for_month`."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: attr: `~Field.Unique_for_Date` agus:attr: "
"`~Field.Unique_for_Month`."

msgid "``verbose_name``"
msgstr "``ainm_verbose``"

msgid ""
"A human-readable name for the field. If the verbose name isn't given, Django "
"will automatically create it using the field's attribute name, converting "
"underscores to spaces. See :ref:`Verbose field names <verbose-field-names>`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm inléite don duine don réimse. Mura dtugtar an t-ainm fhíorúil, "
"cruthóidh Django é go huathoibríoch ag baint úsáide as ainm tréith an "
"réimse, ag athrú béim go spásanna. <verbose-field-names>Féach:ref: "
"`Ainmneacha réimse verbose `."

msgid ""
"A list of validators to run for this field. See the :doc:`validators "
"documentation </ref/validators>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na bailíochtóirí le reáchtáil don réimse seo. Féach na:doc: "
"doiciméadú `bailíochtóir` le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais. </ref/validators>"

msgid "Field types"
msgstr "Cineálacha réimse"

msgid "``AutoField``"
msgstr "``Autofield``"

msgid ""
"An :class:`IntegerField` that automatically increments according to "
"available IDs. You usually won't need to use this directly; a primary key "
"field will automatically be added to your model if you don't specify "
"otherwise. See :ref:`automatic-primary-key-fields`."
msgstr ""
"An:class: `Integerfield` a mhéadaíonn go huathoibríoch de réir ID atá ar "
"fáil. De ghnáth ní bheidh ort é seo a úsáid go díreach; cuirfear "
"príomhréimse go huathoibríoch le do mhúnla mura sonraíonn tú a mhalairt. "
"Féach: tagairt: `uathoibrí-phríomh-eochair-réimsí `."

msgid "``BigAutoField``"
msgstr "``BigAutofield``"

msgid ""
"A 64-bit integer, much like an :class:`AutoField` except that it is "
"guaranteed to fit numbers from ``1`` to ``9223372036854775807``."
msgstr ""
"Sláimhir 64-giotán, cosúil leis an:class: `Autofield` ach amháin go bhfuil "
"sé ráthaithe go n-oirfidh sé uimhreacha ó ``1`` go `9223372036854775807``."

msgid "``BigIntegerField``"
msgstr "``BigIntegerfield``"

msgid ""
"A 64-bit integer, much like an :class:`IntegerField` except that it is "
"guaranteed to fit numbers from ``-9223372036854775808`` to "
"``9223372036854775807``. The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.NumberInput`."
msgstr ""
"Sláimhir 64-giotán, cosúil leis an:class: `IntegerField` ach amháin go "
"bhfuil sé ráthaithe go n-oirfidh sé uimhreacha ó ``-9223372036854775808` go "
"``9223372036854775807``. Is é a: class: `~django.forms.numberInput` an "
"giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo."

msgid "``BinaryField``"
msgstr "``Binaryfield``"

msgid ""
"A field to store raw binary data. It can be "
"assigned :class:`bytes`, :class:`bytearray`, or :class:`memoryview`."
msgstr ""
"Réimse chun sonraí dénártha amh a stóráil. Is féidir é a shannt:class: "
"`bytes`, :class: `bytearray`, nó:class: `memoryview`."

msgid ""
"By default, ``BinaryField`` sets :attr:`~Field.editable` to ``False``, in "
"which case it can't be included in a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, socraíonn ``BinaryField``: attr: `~Field.editable` "
"go ``False``, sa chás sin ní féidir é a áireamh in a:class: "
"`~Django.Forms.ModelForm`."

msgid ""
"Optional. The maximum length (in bytes) of the field. The maximum length is "
"enforced in Django's validation "
"using :class:`~django.core.validators.MaxLengthValidator`."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. An fad uasta (i mbeátaí) an réimse. Cuirtear an fad uasta i "
"bhailíochtú Django i bhfeidhm ag baint úsáidea:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.maxLengthValidator`."

msgid "Abusing ``BinaryField``"
msgstr "Mí-úsáid ``Binaryfield``"

msgid ""
"Although you might think about storing files in the database, consider that "
"it is bad design in 99% of the cases. This field is *not* a replacement for "
"proper :doc:`static files </howto/static-files/index>` handling."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhféadfá smaoineamh ar chomhaid a stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí, "
"smaoinigh gur droch-dhearadh é i 99% de na cásanna. Ní h* é an réimse seo "
"ina athsholáthar do láimhseáil proper:doc: </howto/static-files/index> "
"`comhaid stataithe'."

msgid "A true/false field."
msgstr "Réimse fíor-bhréagach."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field "
"is :class:`~django.forms.CheckboxInput`, "
"or :class:`~django.forms.NullBooleanSelect` if :attr:`null=True "
"<Field.null>`."
msgstr ""
"<Field.null>Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo ná: "
"class: `~django.forms.checkboxInput`, nó:class: "
"`~django.forms.nullBooleanSelect` if: attr: `Null=True `."

msgid ""
"The default value of ``BooleanField`` is ``None`` when :attr:`Field.default` "
"isn't defined."
msgstr ""
"Is é luach réamhshocraithe ``BooleanField`` ``None`` nuair nach "
"sainmhínítear: attr: `Field.default`."

msgid "``CompositePrimaryKey``"
msgstr ""

msgid "A virtual field used for defining a composite primary key."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This field must be defined as the model's ``pk`` attribute. If present, "
"Django will create the underlying model table with a composite primary key."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ``*field_names`` argument is a list of positional field names that "
"compose the primary key."
msgstr ""

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/composite-primary-key` for more details."
msgstr ""

msgid "A string field, for small- to large-sized strings."
msgstr "Réimse teaghráin, le haghaidh teaghráin beag go mórmhéide."

msgid "For large amounts of text, use :class:`~django.db.models.TextField`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh méideanna móra téacs, bain úsáid as: class: "
"`~django.db.models.textfield`."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is a :class:`~django.forms.TextInput`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a:class: "
"`~django.forms.textInput`."

msgid ":class:`CharField` has the following extra arguments:"
msgstr ":class: Tá na hargóintí breise seo a leanas ag `Charfield`:"

msgid ""
"The maximum length (in characters) of the field. The ``max_length`` is "
"enforced at the database level and in Django's validation "
"using :class:`~django.core.validators.MaxLengthValidator`. It's required for "
"all database backends included with Django except PostgreSQL and SQLite, "
"which supports unlimited ``VARCHAR`` columns."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are writing an application that must be portable to multiple database "
"backends, you should be aware that there are restrictions on ``max_length`` "
"for some backends. Refer to the :doc:`database backend notes </ref/"
"databases>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Má tá iarratas á scríobh agat a chaithfidh a bheith iniompartha chuig "
"cúltaca iolracha bunachar sonraí, ba chóir duit a bheith ar an eolas go "
"bhfuil srianta ar `max_length ``do roinnt cúltaca. Féach go dt:doc: `nótaí "
"cúltaca bunachar sonraí` le haghaidh sonraí </ref/databases>."

msgid "Support for unlimited ``VARCHAR`` columns was added on SQLite."
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional. The database collation name of the field."
msgstr "Roghnach. Ainm bailithe bunachar sonraí an réimse."

msgid ""
"Collation names are not standardized. As such, this will not be portable "
"across multiple database backends."
msgstr ""
"Níl ainmneacha coláireachta caighdeánaithe. Dá bhrí sin, ní bheidh sé seo "
"iniompartha ar fud iomadúla cúltaca bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Oracle supports collations only when the ``MAX_STRING_SIZE`` database "
"initialization parameter is set to ``EXTENDED``."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn Oracle le comparáidí ach amháin nuair a dhéantar an paraiméadar "
"tionscnaimh bunachar sonraí ``MAX_STRING_SIZE`` socraithe go ``EXTENDED`."

msgid ""
"A date, represented in Python by a ``datetime.date`` instance. Has a few "
"extra, optional arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Dáta, a léirítear i Python le sampla ``datetime.date``. Tá cúpla argóint "
"roghnach breise aige:"

msgid ""
"Automatically set the field to now every time the object is saved. Useful "
"for \"last-modified\" timestamps. Note that the current date is *always* "
"used; it's not just a default value that you can override."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an réimse go huathoibríoch anois gach uair a shábháiltear an réad. "
"Úsáideach le haghaidh stampaí ama “modhnaithe deireanach”. Tabhair faoi "
"deara go n-úsáidtear an dáta reatha i gcónaí*; ní luach réamhshocraithe é "
"amháin ar féidir leat a shárú."

msgid ""
"The field is only automatically updated when calling :meth:`Model.save() "
"<django.db.models.Model.save>`. The field isn't updated when making updates "
"to other fields in other ways such as :meth:`QuerySet.update() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>`, though you can specify a custom "
"value for the field in an update like that."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Model.save>Ní dhéantar an réimse a nuashonrú go "
"huathoibríoch ach nuair a ghlaoitear: meth: `Model.save () `. Ní "
"nuashonraítear an réim <django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>se agus "
"nuashonruithe á dhéanamh ar réimsí eile ar bhealaí eile mar: meth: "
"`QuerySet.update () `, cé gur féidir leat luach saincheaptha don réimse a "
"shonrú i nuashonrú mar sin."

msgid ""
"Automatically set the field to now when the object is first created. Useful "
"for creation of timestamps. Note that the current date is *always* used; "
"it's not just a default value that you can override. So even if you set a "
"value for this field when creating the object, it will be ignored. If you "
"want to be able to modify this field, set the following instead of "
"``auto_now_add=True``:"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh an réimse go huathoibríoch go dtí anois nuair a chruthaítear an "
"réad Úsáideach chun stampaí ama a chruthú. Tabhair faoi deara go n-úsáidtear "
"an dáta reatha i gcónaí*; ní luach réamhshocraithe é amháin ar féidir leat a "
"shárú. Mar sin fiú má shocraíonn tú luach don réimse seo agus an réad á "
"chruthú agat, déanfar neamhaird air. Más mian leat a bheith in ann an réimse "
"seo a mhodhnú, socraigh an méid seo a leanas in ionad ``auto_now_add=true``:"

msgid ""
"For :class:`DateField`: ``default=date.today`` - "
"from :meth:`datetime.date.today`"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh: aicme: `dátefield`: ``default=date.today`` - ó:meth: "
"`datetime.date.today`"

msgid ""
"For :class:`DateTimeField`: ``default=timezone.now`` - "
"from :func:`django.utils.timezone.now`"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh: aicme: `DateTimeField`: ``default=timezone.now`` - ó:func: "
"`django.utils.timezone.now`"

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.DateInput`. The admin adds a JavaScript calendar, "
"and a shortcut for \"Today\". Includes an additional ``invalid_date`` error "
"message key."
msgstr ""
"Is é a: class: `~django.forms.DateInput` an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe "
"don réimse seo. Cuireann an riarachán féilire JavaScript leis, agus aicearra "
"do “Inniu”. Cuimsíonn sé eochair teachtaireachta earráide breise "
"``invalid_date``."

msgid ""
"The options ``auto_now_add``, ``auto_now``, and ``default`` are mutually "
"exclusive. Any combination of these options will result in an error."
msgstr ""
"Tá na roghanna ``auto_now_add``, `auto_now``, agus ``default`` go "
"comhpháirteach. Beidh earráid mar thoradh ar aon teaglaim de na roghanna seo."

msgid ""
"As currently implemented, setting ``auto_now`` or ``auto_now_add`` to "
"``True`` will cause the field to have ``editable=False`` and ``blank=True`` "
"set."
msgstr ""
"Mar a chuirtear i bhfeidhm faoi láthair, beidh ``auto_now`` nó "
"`auto_now_add`` nó ``auto_now_add`` a shocrú go ``True`` beidh "
"``Editable=False`` agus ``blank=True`` socraithe sa réimse."

msgid ""
"The ``auto_now`` and ``auto_now_add`` options will always use the date in "
"the :ref:`default timezone <default-current-time-zone>` at the moment of "
"creation or update. If you need something different, you may want to "
"consider using your own callable default or overriding ``save()`` instead of "
"using ``auto_now`` or ``auto_now_add``; or using a ``DateTimeField`` instead "
"of a ``DateField`` and deciding how to handle the conversion from datetime "
"to date at display time."
msgstr ""
"<default-current-time-zone>Úsáidfidh na roghanna ``auto_now`` agus "
"``auto_now_add`` an dáta i gcónaí sa :ref: `crios ama réamhshocraitheo` ag "
"nóiméad an chruthaithe nó nuashonraithe. Má theastaíonn rud éigin difriúil "
"uait, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat smaoineamh ar do réamhshocrú inghlaonta féin "
"nó `save () ``a shárú in ionad ``auto_now`` nó `auto_now_add`` a úsáid; nó "
"``DateTimefield`` a úsáid in ionad `Date`field`` agus cinneadh conas an "
"tiontú a láimhseáil ó dáta go dtí seo ag am taispeána."

msgid "Always use :class:`DateField` with a ``datetime.date`` instance."
msgstr "Úsáid i gcónaí:class: `DateField` le sampla ``datetime.date``."

msgid ""
"If you have a ``datetime.datetime`` instance, it's recommended to convert it "
"to a ``datetime.date`` first. If you don't, :class:`DateField` will localize "
"the ``datetime.datetime`` to the :ref:`default timezone <default-current-"
"time-zone>` and convert it to a ``datetime.date`` instance, removing its "
"time component. This is true for both storage and comparison."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sampla ``datetime.datetime`` agat, moltar é a thiontú go "
"`datetime.date`` ar dtús. <default-current-time-zone>Mura ndéanann tú, "
"logálfaidh :class: `DateField` an `datetime.datetime`` go dtí an:ref: "
"`réamhshocraithe ama 'agus é a thiontú go sampla ``datetime.date``, ag baint "
"a chomhpháirt ama. Tá sé seo fíor maidir le stóráil agus comparáid araon."

msgid ""
"A date and time, represented in Python by a ``datetime.datetime`` instance. "
"Takes the same extra arguments as :class:`DateField`."
msgstr ""
"Dáta agus am, a léirítear i Python le sampla ``datetime.datetime``. Glacann "
"sé na hargóintí breise céanna amha:class: `DateField`."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is a "
"single :class:`~django.forms.DateTimeInput`. The admin uses two "
"separate :class:`~django.forms.TextInput` widgets with JavaScript shortcuts."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo ná aonair: class: "
"`~django.forms.DateTimeInput`. Úsáideann an riarachán dhá ghuirléidí "
"leithligh: class: `~django.forms.textInput` le aicearraí JavaScript."

msgid ""
"Always use :class:`DateTimeField` with a ``datetime.datetime`` instance."
msgstr "Úsáid i gcónaí:class: `DateTimeField` le sampla ``datetime.datetime``."

msgid ""
"If you have a ``datetime.date`` instance, it's recommended to convert it to "
"a ``datetime.datetime`` first. If you don't, :class:`DateTimeField` will use "
"midnight in the :ref:`default timezone <default-current-time-zone>` for the "
"time component. This is true for both storage and comparison. To compare the "
"date portion of a :class:`DateTimeField` with a ``datetime.date`` instance, "
"use the :lookup:`date` lookup."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sampla ``datetime.date`` agat, moltar é a thiontú go "
"`datetime.datetime`` ar dtús. <default-current-time-zone>Mura ndéanann tú, "
"úsáidfidh :class: `DateTimeField` meán oíche san :ref: `crios ama "
"réamhshocraithe `don chomhpháirt ama. Tá sé seo fíor maidir le stóráil agus "
"comparáid araon. Chun comparáid a dhéanamh idir an chuid dáta de a:class: "
"`DateTimeField` le sampla ``datetime.date``, bain úsáid as an cuardach: "
"`lookup: `dáta`."

msgid ""
"A fixed-precision decimal number, represented in Python by "
"a :class:`~decimal.Decimal` instance. It validates the input "
"using :class:`~django.core.validators.DecimalValidator`."
msgstr ""
"Uimhir deachúil cruinneas seasta, arna léiriú i Python ag a: class: "
"`~decimal.decimal` sampla. Bailíonn sé an t-ionchur ag baint úsáid:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.decimalValidator`."

msgid "Has the following **required** arguments:"
msgstr "An bhfuil na hargóintí** riachtana** seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The maximum number of digits allowed in the number. Note that this number "
"must be greater than or equal to ``decimal_places``."
msgstr ""
"An líon uasta na ndigit a cheadaítear san uimhir. Tabhair faoi deara go "
"gcaithfidh an uimhir seo a bheith níos mó ná nó cothrom le ``deach_places``."

msgid "The number of decimal places to store with the number."
msgstr "Líon na n-áiteanna deachúil le stóráil leis an uimhir."

msgid ""
"For example, to store numbers up to ``999.99`` with a resolution of 2 "
"decimal places, you'd use::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun uimhreacha a stóráil suas go dtí ``999.99`` le réiteach de "
"2 áit deachúil, bheadh úsáid agat:"

msgid ""
"And to store numbers up to approximately one billion with a resolution of 10 "
"decimal places::"
msgstr ""
"Agus uimhreacha a stóráil suas le thart ar aon billiún le réiteach de 10 n-"
"áit deachúil:"

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.NumberInput` "
"when :attr:`~django.forms.Field.localize` is ``False`` "
"or :class:`~django.forms.TextInput` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a:class: "
"`~django.forms.numberInput` nuai:attr: `~django.forms.field.localize` "
"``False`` nó:class: `~django.forms.textInput` ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"For more information about the differences between the :class:`FloatField` "
"and :class:`DecimalField` classes, please see :ref:`FloatField vs. "
"DecimalField <floatfield_vs_decimalfield>`. You should also be aware "
"of :ref:`SQLite limitations <sqlite-decimal-handling>` of decimal fields."
msgstr ""
"<floatfield_vs_decimalfield>Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoi na "
"difríochtaí idir na haicm:class: `FloatField` agus:class: `DecimalField`, "
"féach le do thoil: `FloatField vs DecimalField`. Ba chóir duit a bheith ar "
"an eolas freisin fao:ref: `Teorainneacha SQLite <sqlite-decimal-handling>`na "
"réimsí deachúil."

msgid ""
"A field for storing periods of time - modeled in Python "
"by :class:`~python:datetime.timedelta`. When used on PostgreSQL, the data "
"type used is an ``interval`` and on Oracle the data type is ``INTERVAL "
"DAY(9) TO SECOND(6)``. Otherwise a ``bigint`` of microseconds is used."
msgstr ""
"Réimse chun tréimhsí ama a stóráil - múnlaithe i Python ag: class: "
"`~python:datetime.timedelta`. Nuair a úsáidtear é ar PostgreSQL, is é "
"“interval” an cineál sonraí a úsáidtear agus ar Oracle is é an cineál sonraí "
"``INTERVAL DAY (9) GO SECOND (6) ``. Seachas sin úsáidtear “bigint” de "
"mhicreasoicind."

msgid ""
"Arithmetic with ``DurationField`` works in most cases. However on all "
"databases other than PostgreSQL, comparing the value of a ``DurationField`` "
"to arithmetic on ``DateTimeField`` instances will not work as expected."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn uimhríocht le ``DurationField`` i bhformhór na gcásanna. Mar sin "
"féin, ar gach bunachar sonraí seachas PostgreSQL, ní oibreoidh comparáid "
"idir luach ``DurationField` agus uimhrithíocht ar chásanna ``DateTimeField`` "
"mar a bhíothas ag súil leis."

msgid ""
"A :class:`CharField` that checks that the value is a valid email address "
"using :class:`~django.core.validators.EmailValidator`."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: `Charfield` a sheiceálann gur seoladh ríomhphoist bailí é an luach "
"ag baint úsáid:class: `~django.core.validators.emailValidator`."

msgid "A file-upload field."
msgstr "Réimse uaslódála comhad."

msgid ""
"The ``primary_key`` argument isn't supported and will raise an error if used."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear leis an argóint `primary_key`` agus ardóidh sé earráid má "
"úsáidtear é."

msgid "Has the following optional arguments:"
msgstr "Tá na hargóintí roghnacha seo a leanas ann"

msgid ""
"This attribute provides a way of setting the upload directory and file name, "
"and can be set in two ways. In both cases, the value is passed to "
"the :meth:`Storage.save() <django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>` method."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an tréith seo bealach chun an eolaire uaslódála agus ainm an "
"chomhaid a shocrú, agus is féidir é a shocrú ar dhá bhealach. "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.save>Sa dá chás, cuirtear an luach ar "
"aghaidh chuig an modh:: `Storage.save () `."

msgid ""
"If you specify a string value or a :class:`~pathlib.Path`, it may "
"contain :func:`~time.strftime` formatting, which will be replaced by the "
"date/time of the file upload (so that uploaded files don't fill up the given "
"directory). For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má shonraíonn tú luach teaghrán nó a:class: `~pathlib.path`, féadfaidh "
"formáidiú: func: `~time.strftime` a bheith ann, a chuirfear dát/am an "
"uaslódála comhad in ionad (ionas nach líonfaidh comhaid uaslódáilte an "
"eolaire tugtha suas). Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"If you are using the "
"default :class:`~django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage`, the string "
"value will be appended to your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` path to form the "
"location on the local filesystem where uploaded files will be stored. If you "
"are using a different storage, check that storage's documentation to see how "
"it handles ``upload_to``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an réamhshocraithe:class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.filesystemStorage` á úsáid agat, cuirfear an "
"luach teaghrán i gceangal le do chonair:: `MEDIA_ROOT` chun an suíomh a "
"fhoirmiú ar an gcóras comhaid áitiúil ina stóráilfear comhaid uaslódáilte. "
"Má tá stóráil dhifriúil á úsáid agat, seiceáil doiciméadú an stórála sin "
"chun a fheiceáil conas a láimhseálann sé ``upload_`."

msgid ""
"``upload_to`` may also be a callable, such as a function. This will be "
"called to obtain the upload path, including the filename. This callable must "
"accept two arguments and return a Unix-style path (with forward slashes) to "
"be passed along to the storage system. The two arguments are:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh ``upload_to`` inghlaonta freisin, mar shampla feidhm. "
"Glaofar air seo chun an cosán uaslódála a fháil, lena n-áirítear ainm an "
"chomhaid. Caithfidh an glaoch seo glacadh le dhá argóint agus cosán i stíl "
"Unix a thabhairt ar ais (le slashes ar aghaidh) le dul chuig an gcóras "
"stórála. Is iad an dá argóint:"

msgid "``instance``"
msgstr "``Instance``"

msgid ""
"An instance of the model where the ``FileField`` is defined. More "
"specifically, this is the particular instance where the current file is "
"being attached."
msgstr ""
"Sampla den tsamhail ina bhfuil an `FileField`` sainmhínithe. Níos sonrach, "
"is é seo an cás áirithe ina bhfuil an comhad reatha á gceangal."

msgid ""
"In most cases, this object will not have been saved to the database yet, so "
"if it uses the default ``AutoField``, *it might not yet have a value for its "
"primary key field*."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, ní shábháiltear an réad seo ar an mbunachar sonraí "
"go fóill, mar sin má úsáideann sé an réamhshocraithe ``Autofield`, "
"*b'fhéidir nach mbeidh luach aige fós dá phríomhréimse*."

msgid "``filename``"
msgstr "``ainm comhad ``"

msgid ""
"The filename that was originally given to the file. This may or may not be "
"taken into account when determining the final destination path."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm comhaid a tugadh don chomhad ar dtús. Féadfar nó nach féidir é seo "
"a chur san áireamh agus an cosán ceann scríbe deiridh á chinneadh."

msgid ""
"A storage object, or a callable which returns a storage object. This handles "
"the storage and retrieval of your files. See :doc:`/topics/files` for "
"details on how to provide this object."
msgstr ""
"Rud stórála, nó inghlaoch a thugann réad stórála ar ais. Láimhseálann sé seo "
"stóráil agus aisghabháil do chuid comhad. Féach: doc: `/topics/files` le "
"haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas an réad seo a sholáthar."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.ClearableFileInput`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a:class: "
"`~django.forms.clearaableFileInput`."

msgid ""
"Using a :class:`FileField` or an :class:`ImageField` (see below) in a model "
"takes a few steps:"
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé cúpla céim ag baint úsáide as a: class: `FileField` nó an:class: "
"`ImageField` (féach thíos) i samhail:"

msgid ""
"In your settings file, you'll need to define :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` as the "
"full path to a directory where you'd like Django to store uploaded files. "
"(For performance, these files are not stored in the database.) "
"Define :setting:`MEDIA_URL` as the base public URL of that directory. Make "
"sure that this directory is writable by the web server's user account."
msgstr ""
"I do chomhad socruithe, beidh ort :setting:'MEDIA_ROOT' a shainmhíniú mar an "
"cosán iomlán chuig eolaire inar mhaith leat Django chun comhaid uaslódáilte "
"a stóráil. (Le haghaidh feidhmíochta, ní stóráiltear na comhaid seo sa "
"bhunachar sonraí.) Sainmhínigh :setting:'MEDIA_URL' mar bhun-URL poiblí an "
"eolaire sin. Cinntigh go bhfuil an chomhadlann seo inscríofa ag cuntas "
"úsáideora an fhreastalaí gréasáin."

msgid ""
"Add the :class:`FileField` or :class:`ImageField` to your model, defining "
"the :attr:`~FileField.upload_to` option to specify a subdirectory "
"of :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` to use for uploaded files."
msgstr ""
"Cuir an:class: `FileField` nó:class: `ImageField` le do mhúnla, ag "
"sainmhíniú an roghna:attr: `~filefield.upload_to` chun fo-eolaire "
"de:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` a shonrú le húsáid le haghaidh comhaid uaslódáilte."

msgid ""
"All that will be stored in your database is a path to the file (relative "
"to :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`). You'll most likely want to use the "
"convenience :attr:`~django.db.models.fields.files.FieldFile.url` attribute "
"provided by Django. For example, if your :class:`ImageField` is called "
"``mug_shot``, you can get the absolute path to your image in a template with "
"``{{ object.mug_shot.url }}``."
msgstr ""
"Is é gach rud a stóráilfear i do bhunachar sonraí ná cosán chuig an gcomhad "
"(i gcoibhneas le:socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT`). Is dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh an "
"tréith áisiúlach:attr: `~django.db.models.fields.files.fieldfile.url` a "
"sholáthraíonn Django a úsáid. Mar shampla, má thugtar ``mug_shot`` ar do: "
"class: `ImageField`, is féidir leat an cosán iomlán chuig d'íomhá a fháil i "
"dteimpléad le ``{{object.mug_shot.url}}``."

msgid ""
"For example, say your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` is set to ``'/home/media'``, "
"and :attr:`~FileField.upload_to` is set to ``'photos/%Y/%m/%d'``. The ``'%Y/"
"%m/%d'`` part of :attr:`~FileField.upload_to` is :func:`~time.strftime` "
"formatting; ``'%Y'`` is the four-digit year, ``'%m'`` is the two-digit month "
"and ``'%d'`` is the two-digit day. If you upload a file on Jan. 15, 2007, it "
"will be saved in the directory ``/home/media/photos/2007/01/15``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, abair go bhfuil do: setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` socraithe go ``'/home/"
"media'``, agus:attr: `~filefield.upload_to` socraithe go ``'Photos/%y/%M/"
"%D'``. Is é an ``'%Y/%M/%D'`` cuid de:attr: `~filefield.upload_to` í:func: "
"`~time.strftime` formáidiú; ``'%Y'`` an bhliain ceithre dhigit, ``%m'`` an "
"mhí dhá dhigit agus ``'%d'`` an lá dhá dhigit. Má uaslódálann tú comhad ar "
"15 Eanáir, 2007, sábhálfar é san eolaire ``/home/media/photos/2007/01/15``."

msgid ""
"If you wanted to retrieve the uploaded file's on-disk filename, or the "
"file's size, you could use the :attr:`~django.core.files.File.name` "
"and :attr:`~django.core.files.File.size` attributes respectively; for more "
"information on the available attributes and methods, see "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.File` class reference and the :doc:`/topics/"
"files` topic guide."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ainm comhaid ar dhiosca an chomhaid uaslódáilte, nó méid an "
"chomhaid a aisghabháil, d'fhéadfá na tréithe: attr: "
"`~django.core.files.name` agus:attr: `~django.core.file.size` a úsáid faoi "
"seach; le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise ar na tréithe agus na modhanna atá ar "
"fáil, féach rang:class: `~django.core.files.file` agus an treoir ábhair: "
"doc: `/topics/files`."

msgid ""
"The file is saved as part of saving the model in the database, so the actual "
"file name used on disk cannot be relied on until after the model has been "
"saved."
msgstr ""
"Sábháiltear an comhad mar chuid den tsamhail a shábháil sa bhunachar sonraí, "
"mar sin ní féidir brath ar an ainm comhaid iarbhír a úsáidtear ar dhiosca go "
"dtí go ndéanfar an tsamhail a shábháil."

msgid ""
"The uploaded file's relative URL can be obtained using "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.fields.files.FieldFile.url` attribute. "
"Internally, this calls the :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.url` "
"method of the underlying :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` class."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir URL coibhneasta an chomhaid uaslódáilte a fháil trí thréith: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.fields.files.fieldfile.url`. Go hinmheánach, glaonn sé "
"seo modh:meth: `~django.core.files.storage.url` an aicme bunlying:class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage.storage`."

msgid ""
"Note that whenever you deal with uploaded files, you should pay close "
"attention to where you're uploading them and what type of files they are, to "
"avoid security holes. *Validate all uploaded files* so that you're sure the "
"files are what you think they are. For example, if you blindly let somebody "
"upload files, without validation, to a directory that's within your web "
"server's document root, then somebody could upload a CGI or PHP script and "
"execute that script by visiting its URL on your site. Don't allow that."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, gach uair a dhéileálann tú le comhaid uaslódáilte, ba "
"chóir duit aird mhór a thabhairt ar an áit a bhfuil tú ag uaslódáil iad agus "
"cén cineál comhaid iad, chun poill slándála a sheachaint * Bailíochnaigh "
"gach comhad uaslódáil* ionas go mbeidh tú cinnte gurb iad na comhaid mar a "
"cheapann tú go bhfuil siad. Mar shampla, má ligeann tú do dall do dhuine "
"comhaid a uaslódáil, gan bailíochtú, chuig eolaire atá laistigh de fhréamh "
"doiciméad do fhreastalaí gréasáin, ansin d'fhéadfadh duine éigin script CGI "
"nó PHP a uaslódáil agus an script sin a fhorghníomhú trí chuairt a thabhairt "
"ar a URL ar do shuíomh. Ná lig sin."

msgid ""
"Also note that even an uploaded HTML file, since it can be executed by the "
"browser (though not by the server), can pose security threats that are "
"equivalent to XSS or CSRF attacks."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin gur féidir le fiú comhad HTML uaslódáilte, ós rud "
"é gur féidir leis an mbrabhsálaí é a fhorghníomhú (cé nach leis an "
"bhfreastalaí), bagairtí slándála a bheith comhionann le hionsaithe XSS nó "
"CSRF."

msgid ""
":class:`FileField` instances are created in your database as ``varchar`` "
"columns with a default max length of 100 characters. As with other fields, "
"you can change the maximum length using the :attr:`~CharField.max_length` "
"argument."
msgstr ""
":class: Cruthaítear cásanna `FileField` i do bhunachar sonraí mar cholúin "
"``varchar`` le fad uasta réamhshocraithe de 100 carachtar. Mar is amhlaidh "
"le réimsí eile, is féidir leat an fad uasta a athrú ag baint úsáide as an "
"argóint: attr: `~charfield.MAX_LENGTH`."

msgid "``FileField`` and ``FieldFile``"
msgstr "``FileField`` agus ``Fieldfile``"

msgid ""
"When you access a :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` on a model, you are "
"given an instance of :class:`FieldFile` as a proxy for accessing the "
"underlying file."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn rochtain agat ar a:class: `~django.db.models.filefield` ar "
"mhúnla, tugtar sampla duit:class: `FieldFile` mar sheachfhreastalaí chun "
"rochtain a fháil ar an gcomhad bunúsach."

msgid ""
"The API of :class:`FieldFile` mirrors that "
"of :class:`~django.core.files.File`, with one key difference: *The object "
"wrapped by the class is not necessarily a wrapper around Python's built-in "
"file object.* Instead, it is a wrapper around the result of "
"the :attr:`Storage.open()<django.core.files.storage.Storage.open>` method, "
"which may be a :class:`~django.core.files.File` object, or it may be a "
"custom storage's implementation of the :class:`~django.core.files.File` API."
msgstr ""
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.open>Scáthaíonn API de:class: `Fieldfile` "
"an réad atá f:class: `~django.core.files.file`, le príomhdhifríocht amháin: "
"*Ní gá go bhfuil an réad atá fillte ag an rang timpeall réad comhaid "
"ionsuite Python.* Ina áit sin, is fillteán é timpeall toradh an modh:attr: "
"`Storage.open () `, a d'fhéadfadh a bheith a:class: "
"`Djan.~Djan.Go.Core.Files.File` réad, nó d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith ina chur i "
"bhfeidhm stórála saincheaptha ar an API: class: `~django.core.files.file`."

msgid ""
"In addition to the API inherited from :class:`~django.core.files.File` such "
"as ``read()`` and ``write()``, :class:`FieldFile` includes several methods "
"that can be used to interact with the underlying file:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis an API a oidhreacht ó:class: `~django.core.files.file` mar "
"``read () ``agus ``write ()``, `, :class: `FieldFile` tá roinnt modhanna is "
"féidir a úsáid chun idirghníomhú leis an gcomhad bunúsach:"

msgid ""
"Two methods of this class, :meth:`~FieldFile.save` "
"and :meth:`~FieldFile.delete`, default to saving the model object of the "
"associated ``FieldFile`` in the database."
msgstr ""
"Dhá mhodh den rang seo, :meth: `~Fieldfile.save` agus:meth: "
"`~Fieldfile.delete`, réamhshocraithe chun réad samhail an ``FieldFile`` "
"gaolmhar a shábháil sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The name of the file including the relative path from the root of "
"the :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` of the "
"associated :class:`~django.db.models.FileField`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an chomhaid lena n-áirítear an cosán coibhneasta ó fhréamh na:class: "
"`~django.core.files.storage` den chomhcheangail:class: "
"`~django.db.models.filefield`."

msgid ""
"A read-only property to access the file's local filesystem path by calling "
"the :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.path` method of the "
"underlying :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` class."
msgstr ""
"Maoin léite amháin chun rochtain a fháil ar chonair chóras comhaid áitiúil "
"an chomhaid trí ghlaoch ar an modh: :meth: `~django.core.files.storage.path` "
"den aicme bunlying:class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage`."

msgid ""
"The result of the underlying :attr:`Storage.size() "
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.size>` method."
msgstr ""
"<django.core.files.storage.Storage.size>Toradh an mhodh bunús:attr: "
"`Storage.size () `."

msgid ""
"A read-only property to access the file's relative URL by calling "
"the :meth:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage.url` method of the "
"underlying :class:`~django.core.files.storage.Storage` class."
msgstr ""
"Maoin léite amháin chun rochtain a fháil ar URL choibhneasta an chomhaid trí "
"ghlaoch ar an modh: :meth: `~django.core.files.storage.url` den aicme "
"bunlying:class: `~django.core.files.storage.storage`."

msgid ""
"Opens or reopens the file associated with this instance in the specified "
"``mode``. Unlike the standard Python ``open()`` method, it doesn't return a "
"file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"Osclaíonn nó athosclaíonn sé an comhad a bhaineann leis an gcás seo sa "
"`mod`` sonraithe. Murab ionann agus an modh caighdeánach Python `open () `, "
"ní thugann sé tuairiscóir comhad ar ais."

msgid ""
"Since the underlying file is opened implicitly when accessing it, it may be "
"unnecessary to call this method except to reset the pointer to the "
"underlying file or to change the ``mode``."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go n-osclaítear an comhad bunúsach intuigthe agus é ag teacht air, "
"b'fhéidir nach mbeadh sé gan ghá an modh seo a ghlaoch ach amháin an pointí "
"a athshocrú chuig an gcomhad bunúsach nó an `mod` a athrú."

msgid ""
"Behaves like the standard Python ``file.close()`` method and closes the file "
"associated with this instance."
msgstr ""
"Iompraíonn sé cosúil leis an modh caighdeánach Python `file.close () ``agus "
"dúnann sé an comhad a bhaineann leis an gcás seo."

msgid ""
"This method takes a filename and file contents and passes them to the "
"storage class for the field, then associates the stored file with the model "
"field. If you want to manually associate file data "
"with :class:`~django.db.models.FileField` instances on your model, the "
"``save()`` method is used to persist that file data."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an modh seo ainm comhaid agus ábhar comhaid agus cuireann sé iad "
"chuig an rang stórála don réimse, ansin comhcheanglaíonn sé an comhad "
"stóráilte leis an réimse samhail. Más mian leat sonraí comhaid a cheangal de "
"láimh le:class: `~django.db.models.filefield` cásanna ar do mhúnla, "
"úsáidtear an modh `save () ``chun na sonraí comhaid sin a leanúint."

msgid ""
"Takes two required arguments: ``name`` which is the name of the file, and "
"``content`` which is an object containing the file's contents.  The optional "
"``save`` argument controls whether or not the model instance is saved after "
"the file associated with this field has been altered. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé dhá argóint riachtanach: ``ainm ``arb é ainm an chomhaid, agus`` "
"ábhar ``is réad é ina bhfuil ábhar an chomhaid. Rialaíonn an argóint "
"roghnach ``sábháil' cibé an sábhálfar an tsamhail nó nach bhfuil an tsamhail "
"tar éis an comhad a bhaineann leis an réimse seo a athrú. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``True``."

msgid ""
"Note that the ``content`` argument should be an instance "
"of :class:`django.core.files.File`, not Python's built-in file object. You "
"can construct a :class:`~django.core.files.File` from an existing Python "
"file object like this::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur chóir go mbeadh an argóint ``content`` mar shampla "
"de:class: `django.core.files.file`, ní réad comhad ionsuite Python. Is "
"féidir leat a:class: `~django.core.files.file` a thógáil ó réad comhaid "
"Python atá ann cheana mar seo::"

msgid "Or you can construct one from a Python string like this::"
msgstr "Nó is féidir leat ceann a thógáil ó shreang Python mar seo::"

msgid "For more information, see :doc:`/topics/files`."
msgstr "Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, féach:doc: `/topics/files`."

msgid ""
"Deletes the file associated with this instance and clears all attributes on "
"the field. Note: This method will close the file if it happens to be open "
"when ``delete()`` is called."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé an comhad a bhaineann leis an gcás seo agus glanann sé gach "
"tréith ar an réimse. Nóta: Dúnfaidh an modh seo an comhad má tharlaíonn sé a "
"bheith oscailte nuair a ghlaofar ``delete () ``."

msgid ""
"The optional ``save`` argument controls whether or not the model instance is "
"saved after the file associated with this field has been deleted. Defaults "
"to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an argóint roghnach ``sábháil`` cibé an sábhálfar an tsamhail nó "
"nach bhfuil an tsamhail tar éis an comhad a bhaineann leis an réimse seo a "
"scriosadh. Réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid ""
"Note that when a model is deleted, related files are not deleted. If you "
"need to cleanup orphaned files, you'll need to handle it yourself (for "
"instance, with a custom management command that can be run manually or "
"scheduled to run periodically via e.g. cron)."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach scriostar comhaid ghaolmhara nuair a scriostar "
"samhail. Más gá duit comhaid dílleachta a ghlanadh, beidh ort é a láimhseáil "
"tú féin (mar shampla, le ordú bainistíochta saincheaptha is féidir a "
"reáchtáil de láimh nó a sceidealú le rith go tréimhsiúil trí e.g. cron)."

msgid ""
"A :class:`CharField` whose choices are limited to the filenames in a certain "
"directory on the filesystem. Has some special arguments, of which the first "
"is **required**:"
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: `Charfield` a bhfuil a roghanna teoranta do na hainmneacha comhaid "
"in eolaire áirithe ar an gcóras comhaid. Tá roinnt argóintí speisialta aige, "
"agus is gá an chéad cheann díú**:"

msgid ""
"Required. The absolute filesystem path to a directory from which "
"this :class:`FilePathField` should get its choices. Example: ``\"/home/"
"images\"``."
msgstr ""
"Riachtanach. An cosán iomlán chórais chomhaid chuig eolaire as ba chóir go "
"bhfaighidh seo:class: `FilePathfield` a roghanna. Sampla: ``” /home/"
"images\"``."

msgid ""
"``path`` may also be a callable, such as a function to dynamically set the "
"path at runtime. Example::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh ``path`` inghlaonta freisin, mar shampla feidhm chun "
"an cosán a shocrú go dinimiciúil ag an am rith. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Optional. A regular expression, as a string, that :class:`FilePathField` "
"will use to filter filenames. Note that the regex will be applied to the "
"base filename, not the full path. Example: ``\"foo.*\\.txt$\"``, which will "
"match a file called ``foo23.txt`` but not ``bar.txt`` or ``foo23.png``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Léiriú rialta, mar shreang, a úsáidfidh: class: `FilePathfield` "
"chun ainmneacha comhaid a scagadh. Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirfear an regex "
"i bhfeidhm ar an mbunainm comhaid, ní ar an gcosán iomlán. Sampla: "
"``\"foo.*\\ .txt$\"``, a mheaitseálfaidh comhad ar a dtugtar ``foo23.txt`` "
"ach ní ``bar.txt`` nó ``foo23.png``."

msgid ""
"Optional. Either ``True`` or ``False``. Default is ``False``. Specifies "
"whether all subdirectories of :attr:`~FilePathField.path` should be included"
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Ceachtar ``Fíor`` nó ``Bréag``. Is é “False” réamhshocraithe. "
"Sonraíonn sé an gcaithfear gach fo-eolaire de:attr: `~FilePathfield.path` a "
"chur san áireamh"

msgid ""
"Optional.  Either ``True`` or ``False``.  Default is ``True``.  Specifies "
"whether files in the specified location should be included.  Either this "
"or :attr:`~FilePathField.allow_folders` must be ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Ceachtar ``Fíor`` nó ``Bréag``. Is é réamhshocraithe ``True``. "
"Sonraíonn sé an gcaithfear comhaid sa suíomh sonraithe a áireamh. Caithfidh "
"ceachtar seo nó: attr: `~FilePathfield.allow_Folders` a bheith ``True``."

msgid ""
"Optional.  Either ``True`` or ``False``.  Default is ``False``.  Specifies "
"whether folders in the specified location should be included.  Either this "
"or :attr:`~FilePathField.allow_files` must be ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Ceachtar ``Fíor`` nó ``Bréag``. Is é “False” réamhshocraithe. "
"Sonraíonn sé an gcaithfear fillteáin sa suíomh sonraithe a áireamh. "
"Caithfidh ceachtar seo nó: attr: `~FilePathfield.allow_files` a bheith "
"``True``."

msgid ""
"The one potential gotcha is that :attr:`~FilePathField.match` applies to the "
"base filename, not the full path. So, this example::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an gotcha féideartha amháin go mbaineann: attr: `~FilePathfield.match` "
"leis an mbunainm comhaid, ní leis an gcosán iomlán. Mar sin, an sampla seo::"

msgid ""
"...will match ``/home/images/foo.png`` but not ``/home/images/foo/bar.png`` "
"because the :attr:`~FilePathField.match` applies to the base filename "
"(``foo.png`` and ``bar.png``)."
msgstr ""
"... meaitseálfaidh sé ``/home/images/foo.png`` ach ní ``/home/images/foo/"
"bar.png`` toisc go mbaineann an:attr: `~FilePathfield.match` leis an "
"mbunainm comhaid (``foo.png`` agus ``bar.png``)."

msgid ""
":class:`FilePathField` instances are created in your database as ``varchar`` "
"columns with a default max length of 100 characters. As with other fields, "
"you can change the maximum length using the :attr:`~CharField.max_length` "
"argument."
msgstr ""
":class: Cruthaítear cásanna `FilePathfield` i do bhunachar sonraí mar "
"cholúin ``varchar`` le fad uasta réamhshocraithe de 100 carachtar. Mar is "
"amhlaidh le réimsí eile, is féidir leat an fad uasta a athrú ag baint úsáide "
"as an argóint: attr: `~charfield.MAX_LENGTH`."

msgid "A floating-point number represented in Python by a ``float`` instance."
msgstr "Uimhir phointe snámh a léirítear i Python le sampla ``snám`."

msgid "``FloatField`` vs. ``DecimalField``"
msgstr "``Floatfield`` vs ``Decimalfield``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`FloatField` class is sometimes mixed up with "
"the :class:`DecimalField` class. Although they both represent real numbers, "
"they represent those numbers differently. ``FloatField`` uses Python's "
"``float`` type internally, while ``DecimalField`` uses Python's ``Decimal`` "
"type. For information on the difference between the two, see Python's "
"documentation for the :mod:`decimal` module."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta déantar an rang: class: `Floatfield` a mheascadh suas leis an "
"aicme:class: `Decimalfield`. Cé go léiríonn siad beirt fíor-uimhreacha, "
"léiríonn siad na huimhreacha sin ar bheal Úsáideann ``Floatfield`` cineál "
"``float`` Python go hinmheánach, agus úsáideann ``Decimalfield`` cineál "
"``Decimal`` Python. Le haghaidh faisnéise faoin difríocht idir an dá cheann, "
"féach doiciméadú Python don mhodúl:mod: `decimal`."

msgid "``GeneratedField``"
msgstr "``Réimse Ginithe ``"

msgid ""
"A field that is always computed based on other fields in the model. This "
"field is managed and updated by the database itself. Uses the ``GENERATED "
"ALWAYS`` SQL syntax."
msgstr ""
"Réimse a ríomhtar i gcónaí bunaithe ar réimsí eile sa tsamhail. Déanann an "
"bunachar sonraí féin an réimse seo a bhainistiú agus a nuashonrú. Úsáideann "
"sé an comhréir SQL ``GENERATED ALWAYS``."

msgid ""
"There are two kinds of generated columns: stored and virtual. A stored "
"generated column is computed when it is written (inserted or updated) and "
"occupies storage as if it were a regular column. A virtual generated column "
"occupies no storage and is computed when it is read. Thus, a virtual "
"generated column is similar to a view and a stored generated column is "
"similar to a materialized view."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chineál colún ginte ann: stóráilte agus fíorúil. Déantar colún a "
"ghintear stóráilte a ríomh nuair a dhéantar é a scríobh (cuireadh isteach nó "
"nuashonraithe) agus tá sé á stóráil amhail is dá mba cholún rialta é. Níl "
"aon stóráil ag colún fíorúil a ghintear agus ríomhtar é nuair a léitear é. "
"Dá bhrí sin, tá colún ginte fíorúil cosúil le radharc agus tá colún ginte "
"stóráilte cosúil le radharc ábhartha."

msgid ""
"An :class:`Expression` used by the database to automatically set the field "
"value each time the model is changed."
msgstr ""
"An: aicme: `Expression` a úsáideann an bunachar sonraí chun luach an réimse "
"a shocrú go huathoibríoch gach uair a athraítear an tsamhail."

msgid ""
"The expressions should be deterministic and only reference fields within the "
"model (in the same database table). Generated fields cannot reference other "
"generated fields. Database backends can impose further restrictions."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh na nathanna cinntiúcháin agus gan ach réimsí tagartha "
"laistigh den tsamhail (sa tábla bunachar sonraí céanna). Ní féidir le réimsí "
"ginte tagairt a dhéanamh do réimsí ginte eile Is féidir le cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí srianta breise a fhorchur."

msgid "A model field instance to define the field's data type."
msgstr "Sampla réimse samhail chun cineál sonraí an réimse a shainiú."

msgid ""
"Determines if the database column should occupy storage as if it were a real "
"column. If ``False``, the column acts as a virtual column and does not "
"occupy database storage space."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann sé an chóir go n-áitigh an cholún bunachar sonraí stóráil amhail is "
"dá mba cholún fíor é. Má tá “False”, feidhmíonn an colún mar cholún fíorúil "
"agus ní áitigh sé spás stórála bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL only supports persisted columns. Oracle only supports virtual "
"columns."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn PostgreSQL ach le colúin leanúnacha. Ní thacaíonn Oracle ach "
"colúin fíorúla"

msgid "Refresh the data"
msgstr "Athnuachan na sonraí"

msgid ""
"Since the database computes the value, the object must be reloaded to access "
"the new value after :meth:`~Model.save()`, for example, by "
"using :meth:`~Model.refresh_from_db()`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Database limitations"
msgstr "Teoranta bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"There are many database-specific restrictions on generated fields that "
"Django doesn't validate and the database may raise an error e.g. PostgreSQL "
"requires functions and operators referenced in a generated column to be "
"marked as ``IMMUTABLE``."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor srianta sonrach le bunachar sonraí ar réimsí ginte nach ndéanann "
"Django bailíochtú agus féadfaidh an bunachar sonraí earráid a ardú m.sh. "
"Éilíonn PostgreSQL feidhmeanna agus oibreoirí dá dtagraítear i gcolún ginte "
"a mharcáil mar “IMMUTABLE”."

msgid ""
"You should always check that ``expression`` is supported on your database. "
"Check out `MariaDB`_, `MySQL`_, `Oracle`_, `PostgreSQL`_, or `SQLite`_ docs."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit seiceáil i gcónaí go dtacaítear le ``expression`` ar do "
"bhunachar sonraí. Amharc ar `MariaDB`_, `MySQL`_, `Oracle`_, `PostgreSQL`_, "
"nó `SQLite`_ docs."

msgid ""
"An IPv4 or IPv6 address, in string format (e.g. ``192.0.2.30`` or "
"``2a02:42fe::4``). The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.TextInput`."
msgstr ""
"Seoladh IPv4 nó IPv6, i bhformáid teaghrán (m.sh. ``192.0.2.30`` nó ``2a "
"02:42 fe: :4``). Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a: "
"class: `~django.forms.textInput`."

msgid ""
"Limits valid inputs to the specified protocol. Accepted values are "
"``'both'`` (default), ``'IPv4'`` or ``'IPv6'``. Matching is case insensitive."
msgstr ""
"Teoraíonn sé ionchuir bailí don phrótacal sonraithe. Is iad na luachanna a "
"nglactar leo ná ``'beach'`` (réamhshocraithe), ``'IPv4'`` nó ```IPv6'``. Tá "
"an meaitseáil neamh-íogair."

msgid ""
"If you allow for blank values, you have to allow for null values since blank "
"values are stored as null."
msgstr ""
"Má cheadaíonn tú luachanna bána, caithfidh tú luachanna neall a cheadú ós "
"rud é go ndéantar luachanna bána a stóráil mar null."

msgid ""
"Inherits all attributes and methods from :class:`FileField`, but also "
"validates that the uploaded object is a valid image."
msgstr ""
"Oidhreann sé gach tréith agus modh ó:class: `FileField`, ach bailíonn sé "
"freisin gur íomhá bailí é an réad uaslódáilte."

msgid ""
"In addition to the special attributes that are available "
"for :class:`FileField`, an :class:`ImageField` also has ``height`` and "
"``width`` attributes."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis na tréithe speisialta atá ar fáil dó:class: `FileField`, tá "
"tréithe ```airde`` agus ``leithead`` ag: `Class: `ImageField` freisin."

msgid ""
"To facilitate querying on those attributes, :class:`ImageField` has the "
"following optional arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Chun fiosrú ar na tréithe sin a éascú, tá na hargóintí roghnacha seo a "
"leanas ag :class: `ImageField`:"

msgid ""
"Name of a model field which is auto-populated with the height of the image "
"each time an image object is set."
msgstr ""
"Ainm réimse samhail a dhéantar go huathoibríoch le airde na híomhá gach uair "
"a shocraítear réad íomhá."

msgid ""
"Name of a model field which is auto-populated with the width of the image "
"each time an image object is set."
msgstr ""
"Ainm réimse samhail a dhéantar go huathoibríoch le leithead na híomhá gach "
"uair a shocraítear réad íomhá."

msgid "Requires the :pypi:`pillow` library."
msgstr "Éilíonn an leabharlanna:pypi: `pillow`."

msgid ""
":class:`ImageField` instances are created in your database as ``varchar`` "
"columns with a default max length of 100 characters. As with other fields, "
"you can change the maximum length using the :attr:`~CharField.max_length` "
"argument."
msgstr ""
":class: Cruthaítear cásanna `ImageField` i do bhunachar sonraí mar cholúin "
"``varchar`` le fad uasta réamhshocraithe de 100 carachtar. Mar is amhlaidh "
"le réimsí eile, is féidir leat an fad uasta a athrú ag baint úsáide as an "
"argóint: attr: `~charfield.MAX_LENGTH`."

msgid ""
"An integer. Values are only allowed between certain (database-dependent) "
"points. Values from ``-2147483648`` to ``2147483647`` are compatible in all "
"databases supported by Django."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It uses :class:`~django.core.validators.MinValueValidator` "
"and :class:`~django.core.validators.MaxValueValidator` to validate the input "
"based on the values that the default database supports."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé: aicme: `~django.core.validators.minvalueValidator` agus:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.maxvalueValidator` chun an t-ionchur a bhailíochtú "
"bunaithe ar na luachanna a thacaíonn an bunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"A field for storing JSON encoded data. In Python the data is represented in "
"its Python native format: dictionaries, lists, strings, numbers, booleans "
"and ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Réimse chun sonraí ionchódaithe JSON a stóráil. I Python léirítear na sonraí "
"ina bhformáid dúchasach Python: foclóirí, liostaí, teaghráin, uimhreacha, "
"booleans agus ``None ``."

msgid ""
"``JSONField`` is supported on MariaDB, MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL, and SQLite "
"(with the :ref:`JSON1 extension enabled <sqlite-json1>`)."
msgstr ""
"<sqlite-json1>Tacaítear le ``JSONField`` ar MariaDB, MySQL, Oracle, "
"PostgreSQL, agus SQLite (leis an síneadh: ref: `JSON1 cumasaithe `)."

msgid ""
"An optional :py:class:`json.JSONEncoder` subclass to serialize data types "
"not supported by the standard JSON serializer (e.g. ``datetime.datetime`` "
"or :class:`~python:uuid.UUID`). For example, you can use "
"the :class:`~django.core.serializers.json.DjangoJSONEncoder` class."
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme roghnaí:py:class: `JSON.JSONEncoder` chun cineálacha sonraí nach "
"dtacaíonn an sraitheoir caighdeánach JSON a shraitheadh (m.sh. "
"`datetime.datetime`` nó:class: `~python:uuid.uuid`). Mar shampla, is féidir "
"leat an rang:class: `~django.core.serializers.json.djangojsonEncoder` a "
"úsáid."

msgid ""
"An optional :py:class:`json.JSONDecoder` subclass to deserialize the value "
"retrieved from the database. The value will be in the format chosen by the "
"custom encoder (most often a string). Your deserialization may need to "
"account for the fact that you can't be certain of the input type. For "
"example, you run the risk of returning a ``datetime`` that was actually a "
"string that just happened to be in the same format chosen for "
"``datetime``\\s."
msgstr ""
"Fo-aicme roghnaí:py:class: `JSON.JSONDecoder` chun an luach a "
"aisghabháiltear ón mbunachar sonraí a dhíshealú. Beidh an luach san fhormáid "
"a roghnaíonn an t-ionchódóir saincheaptha (sreang is minic). B'fhéidir go "
"gcaithfidh do dhístiriú cuntas a thabhairt ar an bhfíric nach féidir leat a "
"bheith cinnte faoin gcineál ionchuir. Mar shampla, tá an baol agat go "
"bhfaighidh tú ``datetime`` a thabhairt ar ais a bhí i ndáiríre ina teaghrán "
"a bhí díreach sa fhormáid chéanna a roghnaíodh do `datetime``\\ s."

msgid "To query ``JSONField`` in the database, see :ref:`querying-jsonfield`."
msgstr ""
"Chun ``Jsonfield`` a cheistiú sa bhunachar sonraí, féach:ref: `querying-"
"jsonfield`."

msgid "Default value"
msgstr "Luach réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"If you give the field a :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default`, ensure it's "
"a callable such as the :py:class:`dict` class or a function that returns a "
"fresh object each time. Incorrectly using a mutable object like ``default={}"
"`` or ``default=[]`` creates a mutable default that is shared between all "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"Má thugann tú an réimse a:attr: `~django.db.models.field.default`, déan "
"cinnte go bhfuil sé inghlaonta mar an aicme:py:class: `dict` nó feidhm a "
"thugann réad úr ar ais gach uair. Cruthaíonn réad inathraithe mar `default= "
"{} ``nó ``default= []`` go mícheart réamhshocraithe inathraithe a roinntear "
"idir gach cás."

msgid "Indexing"
msgstr "Innéacsú"

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.Index` and :attr:`.Field.db_index` both create a B-"
"tree index, which isn't particularly helpful when querying ``JSONField``. On "
"PostgreSQL only, you can "
"use :class:`~django.contrib.postgres.indexes.GinIndex` that is better suited."
msgstr ""
":class: `~django.db.Models.index` agus:attr: `.field.db_index` cruthaíonn "
"innéacs B-tree araon, rud nach bhfuil cabhrach go háirithe nuair a "
"fhiosraítear ``JSONField``. Ar PostgreSQL amháin, is féidir leat úsáid a "
"úsáid:class: `~django.contrib.postgres.indexes.ginIndex` atá níos oiriúnaí."

msgid "PostgreSQL users"
msgstr "Úsáideoirí PostgreSQL"

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL has two native JSON based data types: ``json`` and ``jsonb``. The "
"main difference between them is how they are stored and how they can be "
"queried. PostgreSQL's ``json`` field is stored as the original string "
"representation of the JSON and must be decoded on the fly when queried based "
"on keys. The ``jsonb`` field is stored based on the actual structure of the "
"JSON which allows indexing. The trade-off is a small additional cost on "
"writing to the ``jsonb`` field. ``JSONField`` uses ``jsonb``."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chineál sonraí bunaithe ar JSON dúchasacha ag PostgreSQL: ``json`` "
"agus ``jsonb``. Is é an difríocht is mó eatarthu ná conas a stóráiltear iad "
"agus conas is féidir iad a fhiosrú. Stóráiltear réimse `json`` PostgreSQL "
"mar léiriú teaghrán bunaidh an JSON agus caithfear é a dhíchódú ar an eitilt "
"nuair a fhiosraítear é bunaithe ar eochracha. Stóráiltear an réimse `jsonb`` "
"bunaithe ar struchtúr iarbhír an JSON a cheadaíonn innéacsú. Is costas beag "
"breise é an trádáil ar scríobh chuig an réimse ``jsonb``. Úsáideann "
"``jsonfield`` ``jsonb``."

msgid "Oracle users"
msgstr "Úsáideoirí Oracle"

msgid ""
"Oracle Database does not support storing JSON scalar values. Only JSON "
"objects and arrays (represented in Python using :py:class:`dict` "
"and :py:class:`list`) are supported."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn Bunachar Sonraí Oracle le luachanna scalar JSON a stóráil. Ní "
"thacaítear ach le rudaí agus eagair JSON (a léirítear i Python ag baint "
"úsáide as: py:class: `dict` agus:py:class: `list`)."

msgid "``PositiveBigIntegerField``"
msgstr "``PositiveBigIntegerField``"

msgid ""
"Like a :class:`PositiveIntegerField`, but only allows values under a certain "
"(database-dependent) point. Values from ``0`` to ``9223372036854775807`` are "
"compatible in all databases supported by Django."
msgstr ""

msgid "``PositiveIntegerField``"
msgstr "``Réimse Dearfach Iomlán ``"

msgid ""
"Like an :class:`IntegerField`, but must be either positive or zero (``0``). "
"Values are only allowed under a certain (database-dependent) point. Values "
"from ``0`` to ``2147483647`` are compatible in all databases supported by "
"Django. The value ``0`` is accepted for backward compatibility reasons."
msgstr ""

msgid "``PositiveSmallIntegerField``"
msgstr "``PositivesmallIntéarréimh``"

msgid ""
"Like a :class:`PositiveIntegerField`, but only allows values under a certain "
"(database-dependent) point. Values from ``0`` to ``32767`` are compatible in "
"all databases supported by Django."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":term:`Slug <slug>` is a newspaper term. A slug is a short label for "
"something, containing only letters, numbers, underscores or hyphens. They're "
"generally used in URLs."
msgstr ""
":term: Is téarma nuachtáin é `Slug <slug>`. Is lipéad gairid é slug le "
"haghaidh rud éigin, nach bhfuil ach litreacha, uimhreacha, béim nó hiphens "
"ann. Úsáidtear iad go ginearálta i URLanna."

msgid ""
"Like a CharField, you can specify :attr:`~CharField.max_length` (read the "
"note about database portability and :attr:`~CharField.max_length` in that "
"section, too). If :attr:`~CharField.max_length` is not specified, Django "
"will use a default length of 50."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le CharField, is féidir leat: attr: `~charfield.MAX_LENGTH` a shonrú "
"(léigh an nóta faoi iniomparthacht bunachar sonraí agus:attr: "
"`~charfield.MAX_LENGTH` sa chuid sin freisin). Más: Attr: "
"`~Charfield.max_Length` nach sonraítear, úsáidfidh Django fad "
"réamhshocraithe de 50."

msgid "Implies setting :attr:`Field.db_index` to ``True``."
msgstr "Tugann sé le tuiscint socrú: attr: `Field.db_index` go ``True``."

msgid ""
"It is often useful to automatically prepopulate a SlugField based on the "
"value of some other value.  You can do this automatically in the admin "
"using :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.prepopulated_fields`."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a bhíonn sé úsáideach SlugField a réamhdhíonrú go huathoibríoch "
"bunaithe ar luach luach éigin eile. Is féidir leat é seo a dhéanamh go "
"huathoibríoch sa riarachán ag baint úsáidea:attr: "
"`~django.contrib.admin.modeladmin.prePopulated_fields`."

msgid ""
"It uses :class:`~django.core.validators.validate_slug` "
"or :class:`~django.core.validators.validate_unicode_slug` for validation."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé: aicme: `~django.core.validators.validate_slug` nó:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.validate_unicode_slug` le haghaidh bailíochtaithe."

msgid ""
"If ``True``, the field accepts Unicode letters in addition to ASCII letters. "
"Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, glacann an réimse litreacha Unicode i dteannta litreacha "
"ASCII. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid "``SmallAutoField``"
msgstr "``SmallAutofield``"

msgid ""
"Like an :class:`AutoField`, but only allows values under a certain (database-"
"dependent) limit. Values from ``1`` to ``32767`` are compatible in all "
"databases supported by Django."
msgstr ""

msgid "``SmallIntegerField``"
msgstr "``SmallIntegerField``"

msgid ""
"Like an :class:`IntegerField`, but only allows values under a certain "
"(database-dependent) point. Values from ``-32768`` to ``32767`` are "
"compatible in all databases supported by Django."
msgstr ""

msgid "``TextField``"
msgstr "``Réimse téacs``"

msgid ""
"A large text field. The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.Textarea`."
msgstr ""
"Réimse mór téacs. Is é a: class: `~django.forms.textarea` an giuirléid "
"foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo."

msgid ""
"If you specify a ``max_length`` attribute, it will be reflected in "
"the :class:`~django.forms.Textarea` widget of the auto-generated form field. "
"However it is not enforced at the model or database level. Use "
"a :class:`CharField` for that."
msgstr ""
"Má shonraíonn tú tréith ``max_length ``, léireofar é sa ghuirléid: class: "
"`~django.forms.textarea` den réimse foirme uathghinithe. Ní chuirtear i "
"bhfeidhm é, áfach, ag leibhéal an tsamhail nó bunachar sonraí. Úsáid "
"a:class: `Charfield` chuige sin."

msgid "Oracle does not support collations for a ``TextField``."
msgstr "Ní thacaíonn Oracle le comparáidí do ``Textfield``."

msgid ""
"A time, represented in Python by a ``datetime.time`` instance. Accepts the "
"same auto-population options as :class:`DateField`."
msgstr ""
"Am, a léirítear i Python le sampla ``datetime.time``. Glacann sé leis na "
"roghanna uathoibríoch céanna mar: class: `DateField`."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is "
"a :class:`~django.forms.TimeInput`. The admin adds some JavaScript shortcuts."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a: class: "
"`~django.forms.timeinput`. Cuireann an riarachán roinnt aicearraí JavaScript "
"leis."

msgid ""
"A :class:`CharField` for a URL, validated "
"by :class:`~django.core.validators.URLValidator`."
msgstr ""
"A: Class: `Charfield` le haghaidh URL, bailíochtaithe ar:class: "
"`~django.core.validators.urlValidator`."

msgid ""
"The default form widget for this field is a :class:`~django.forms.URLInput`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an giuirléid foirme réamhshocraithe don réimse seo a: class: "
"`~django.forms.urlinput`."

msgid ""
"Like all :class:`CharField` subclasses, :class:`URLField` takes the "
"optional :attr:`~CharField.max_length` argument. If you don't "
"specify :attr:`~CharField.max_length`, a default of 200 is used."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le gach fo-aicm:class: `Charfield`, glacann: class: `URLField` an "
"argóint roghnaí:attr: `~charfield.MAX_LENGTH`. Mura sonraíonn tú: attr: "
"`~charfield.max_Length`, úsáidtear réamhshocrú 200."

msgid ""
"A field for storing universally unique identifiers. Uses "
"Python's :class:`~python:uuid.UUID` class. When used on PostgreSQL and "
"MariaDB 10.7+, this stores in a ``uuid`` datatype, otherwise in a "
"``char(32)``."
msgstr ""
"Réimse chun aitheantóirí uathúla a stóráil. Úsáideann Python's:class: "
"`~Python: uuid.uuid` aicme. Nuair a úsáidtear é ar PostgreSQL agus MariaDB "
"10.7+, stóráilíonn sé seo i gcineál sonraí ``uuid``, ar shlí eile i ``char "
"(32) ``."

msgid ""
"Universally unique identifiers are a good alternative to :class:`AutoField` "
"for :attr:`~Field.primary_key`. The database will not generate the UUID for "
"you, so it is recommended to use :attr:`~Field.default`::"
msgstr ""
"Is rogha eile maith iad aitheantóirí uathúla go huilíoch seach:class: "
"`Autofield` for:attr: `~field.primary_key`. Ní ghinfidh an bunachar sonraí "
"an UUID duit, mar sin moltar a úsáid:attr: `~field.default`::"

msgid ""
"Note that a callable (with the parentheses omitted) is passed to "
"``default``, not an instance of ``UUID``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirtear glaoch inghlaonta (agus na lúibíní fágtha) "
"chuig ``default``, ní sampla de ``UUID ``."

msgid "Lookups on PostgreSQL and MariaDB 10.7+"
msgstr "Cuardaigh ar PostgreSQL agus MariaDB 10.7+"

msgid ""
"Using :lookup:`iexact`, :lookup:`contains`, :lookup:`icontains`, :lookup:`startswith`, :lookup:`istartswith`, :lookup:`endswith`, "
"or :lookup:`iendswith` lookups on PostgreSQL don't work for values without "
"hyphens, because PostgreSQL and MariaDB 10.7+ store them in a hyphenated "
"uuid datatype type."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid:lookup: `iexact`, :lookup: `contains`, :lookup: `icontains`, :lookup: "
"`startswith`, :lookup: `istartswith`, :lookup: `endswith`, nó:lookup: "
"`iendswith` ní oibríonn cuardaigh `iendswith` ar PostgreSQL le haghaidh "
"luachanna gan bhreithíní, mar gheall ar PostgreSQL Stóráilíonn L agus "
"MariaDB 10.7+ iad i gcineál sonraí uuid frithphéadaithe."

msgid "Relationship fields"
msgstr "Réimsí caidrimh"

msgid "Django also defines a set of fields that represent relations."
msgstr "Sainmhíníonn Django sraith réimsí freisin a léiríonn caidreamh."

msgid "``ForeignKey``"
msgstr "``ForeignKey``"

msgid ""
"A many-to-one relationship. Requires two positional arguments: the class to "
"which the model is related and the :attr:`~ForeignKey.on_delete` option::"
msgstr ""
"Caidreamh go leor le duine. Éilíonn dhá argóint seasaimh: an rang lena "
"mbaineann an tsamhail agus an rogha: attr: `~ForeignKey.on_delete`::"

msgid ""
"The first positional argument can be either a concrete model class or "
"a :ref:`lazy reference <lazy-relationships>` to a model "
"class. :ref:`Recursive relationships <recursive-relationships>`, where a "
"model has a relationship with itself, are also supported."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an gcéad argóint seasaimh a bheith ina aicme samhail nithiúil "
"nó a:ref: `tagairt leisciúil <lazy-relationships>`d'aicme samhail. :ref: "
"Tacaítear le `caidrimh ath <recursive-relationships>shlánacha `, áit a "
"bhfuil caidreamh ag samhail leis féin, freisin."

msgid ""
"See :attr:`ForeignKey.on_delete` for details on the second positional "
"argument."
msgstr ""
"Féach: attr: `ForeignKey.on_delete` le haghaidh sonraí faoin dara argóint "
"seasmhach."

msgid ""
"A database index is automatically created on the ``ForeignKey``. You can "
"disable this by setting :attr:`~Field.db_index` to ``False``.  You may want "
"to avoid the overhead of an index if you are creating a foreign key for "
"consistency rather than joins, or if you will be creating an alternative "
"index like a partial or multiple column index."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaítear innéacs bunachar sonraí go huathoibríoch ar an `ForeignKey``. Is "
"féidir leat é seo a dhíchumasú trí shocrú: attr: `~field.db_index` go "
"``False``. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat lasbhreas innéacs a sheachaint má tá "
"eochair eachtrach á chruthú agat le haghaidh comhsheasmhachta seachas dul "
"isteach, nó má bheidh tú ag cruthú innéacs malartach cosúil le hinnéacs "
"colún páirteach nó iolrach."

msgid "Database Representation"
msgstr "Ionadaíocht Bunachar Sonraí"

msgid ""
"Behind the scenes, Django appends ``\"_id\"`` to the field name to create "
"its database column name. In the above example, the database table for the "
"``Car`` model will have a ``manufacturer_id`` column. You can change this "
"explicitly by specifying :attr:`~Field.db_column`, however, your code should "
"never have to deal with the database column name (unless you write custom "
"SQL). You'll always deal with the field names of your model object."
msgstr ""
"Taobh thiar de na radhairc, cuireann Django ``\"_id\"`` leis an ainm réimse "
"chun a ainm colún bunachar sonraí a chruthú. Sa sampla thuas, beidh colún "
"``manufacturer_id`` sa tábla bunachar sonraí don tsamhail ``Car``. Is féidir "
"leat é seo a athrú go sainráite trí:attr: `~field.db_column` a shonrú, "
"áfach, níor cheart go mbeadh ar do chód déileáil le hainm an cholúin "
"bunachar sonraí riamh (mura scríobhann tú SQL saincheaptha). Déileálfaidh tú "
"i gcónaí le hainmneacha réimse do réad samhail."

msgid "Arguments"
msgstr "Argóintí"

msgid ""
":class:`ForeignKey` accepts other arguments that define the details of how "
"the relation works."
msgstr ""
":class: Glacann `ForeignKey` le hargóintí eile a shainmhíníonn na sonraí "
"faoin gcaoi a n-oibríonn an gaol."

msgid ""
"When an object referenced by a :class:`ForeignKey` is deleted, Django will "
"emulate the behavior of the SQL constraint specified by "
"the :attr:`on_delete` argument. For example, if you have a "
"nullable :class:`ForeignKey` and you want it to be set null when the "
"referenced object is deleted::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a scriostar réad dá dtagraíonn a:class: `ForeignKey`, déanfaidh Django "
"aithris ar iompar an srianta SQL a shonraítear leis an argóint: attr: "
"`on_delete`. Mar shampla, má tá nullable:class: `ForeignKey` agat agus má "
"theastaíonn uait go mbeadh sé a shocrú null nuair a scriostar an réad "
"tagartha::"

msgid ""
"``on_delete`` doesn't create an SQL constraint in the database. Support for "
"database-level cascade options :ticket:`may be implemented later <21961>`."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn ``on_delete`` srian SQL sa bhunachar sonraí. <21961>Tacaíocht "
"do roghanna cascadh ar leibhéal bunachar sonraí: ticéad: `féadfar a chur i "
"bhfeidhm níos déanaí `."

msgid ""
"The possible values for :attr:`~ForeignKey.on_delete` are found "
"in :mod:`django.db.models`:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na luachanna féideartha le haghaidh: attr: `~ForeignKey.on_delete` le "
"fáil in:mod: `django.db.models`:"

msgid ""
"Cascade deletes. Django emulates the behavior of the SQL constraint ``ON "
"DELETE CASCADE`` and also deletes the object containing "
"the :class:`ForeignKey`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":meth:`.Model.delete` isn't called on related models, but "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_delete` "
"and :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_delete` signals are sent for all "
"deleted objects."
msgstr ""
":meth: Ní ghlaítear `.model.delete` ar mhúnlaí gaolmhara, ach seoltar na "
"comharthaí: data: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_delete` agus:data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_delete` do gach rud scriosta."

msgid ""
"Prevent deletion of the referenced object by "
"raising :exc:`~django.db.models.ProtectedError`, a subclass "
"of :exc:`django.db.IntegrityError`."
msgstr ""
"Cosc a chur ar scriosadh an réad tagartha trí:exc: "
"`~django.db.models.protectedError`, fo-aicme de:exc: "
"`Django.db.IntegrityError` a ardú."

msgid ""
"Prevent deletion of the referenced object by "
"raising :exc:`~django.db.models.RestrictedError` (a subclass "
"of :exc:`django.db.IntegrityError`). Unlike :attr:`PROTECT`, deletion of the "
"referenced object is allowed if it also references a different object that "
"is being deleted in the same operation, but via a :attr:`CASCADE` "
"relationship."
msgstr ""
"Cosc a chur ar an réad tagartha a scriosadh trí:exc: "
