msgstr "Cuir modh leis ar bhainisteoir saincheaptha (is fearr de ghnáth):"

msgid "Customizing model loading"
msgstr "Luchtú samhail a shaincheapadh"

msgid ""
"The ``from_db()`` method can be used to customize model instance creation "
"when loading from the database."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an modh ``from_db () ``a úsáid chun cruthú sampla samhail a "
"shaincheapadh agus tú ag luchtú ón mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``db`` argument contains the database alias for the database the model "
"is loaded from, ``field_names`` contains the names of all loaded fields, and "
"``values`` contains the loaded values for each field in ``field_names``. The "
"``field_names`` are in the same order as the ``values``. If all of the "
"model's fields are present, then ``values`` are guaranteed to be in the "
"order ``__init__()`` expects them. That is, the instance can be created by "
"``cls(*values)``. If any fields are deferred, they won't appear in "
"``field_names``. In that case, assign a value of "
"``django.db.models.DEFERRED`` to each of the missing fields."
msgstr ""
"Tá an ailias bunachar sonraí don bhunachar sonraí ón argóint `db`` a "
"luchtaítear an tsamhail uaidh, tá `field_names`` ainmneacha na réimsí "
"luchtaithe go léir, agus tá `luacha`` na luachanna luchtaithe do gach réimse "
"in `field_names``. Tá na ``field_names`` san ord céanna leis na `luacha``. "
"Má tá réimsí uile an tsamhail i láthair, ansin ráthaítear go mbeidh "
"``luacha`` san ord a bhfuil `__init__ () `ag súil leo. Is é sin, is féidir "
"an sampla a chruthú le ``cls (*luachanna) ``. Má chuirtear aon réimsí ar "
"iarchur, ní bheidh siad le feiceáil in `field_names``. Sa chás sin, sannadh "
"luach ``Django.db.Models.Deferred`` do gach ceann de na réimsí atá in "
"easnamh."

msgid ""
"In addition to creating the new model, the ``from_db()`` method must set the "
"``adding`` and ``db`` flags in the new instance's :attr:`~Model._state` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis an tsamhail nua a chruthú, ní mór don modh ``from_db () "
"``na bratacha ```adding`` agus ``db`` a shocrú sa instanse nua 's:attr: "
"`~Model. tréith _state."

msgid ""
"Below is an example showing how to record the initial values of fields that "
"are loaded from the database::"
msgstr ""
"Seo thíos sampla a thaispeánann conas luachanna tosaigh réimsí a luchtaítear "
"ón mbunachar sonraí a thaifeadadh:"

msgid ""
"The example above shows a full ``from_db()`` implementation to clarify how "
"that is done. In this case it would be possible to use a ``super()`` call in "
"the ``from_db()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann an sampla thuas cur chun feidhme iomlán ``from_db () `chun "
"soiléiriú a dhéanamh ar an gcaoi a ndéantar é sin. Sa chás seo bheadh sé in "
"ann glao ``super () ``a úsáid sa mhodh ``from_db ()``."

msgid "Refreshing objects from database"
msgstr "Rudaí athnuachana ón mbunachar"

msgid ""
"If you delete a field from a model instance, accessing it again reloads the "
"value from the database:"
msgstr ""
"Má scriosann tú réimse ó shampla samhail, déanann rochtain a fháil air an "
"luach ón mbunachar sonraí a athluchtú arís:"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``arefresh_from_db()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``arefresh_from_db () ``"

msgid ""
"If you need to reload a model's values from the database, you can use the "
"``refresh_from_db()`` method. When this method is called without arguments "
"the following is done:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit luachanna samhail a athluchtú ón mbunachar sonraí, is féidir "
"leat an modh `fresh_from_db () `a úsáid. Nuair a ghlaofar an modh seo gan "
"argóintí déantar an méid seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"All non-deferred fields of the model are updated to the values currently "
"present in the database."
msgstr ""
"Déantar gach réimse neamh-iarchurtha den tsamhail a nuashonrú go dtí na "
"luachanna atá i láthair sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid "Any cached relations are cleared from the reloaded instance."
msgstr "Déantar aon chaidreamh taisceáilte a ghlanadh ón gcás athluchtaithe."

msgid ""
"Only fields of the model are reloaded from the database. Other database-"
"dependent values such as annotations aren't reloaded. "
"Any :func:`@cached_property <django.utils.functional.cached_property>` "
"attributes aren't cleared either."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéantar ach réimsí den tsamhail a athluchtú ón mbunachar sonraí. Ní "
"dhéantar luachanna eile atá ag brath ar bhunachar sonraí mar anótaí a "
"athluchtú. Any:func: "
"`@cached_property<django.utils.functional.cached_property>` ní ghlantar "
"tréithe ach an oiread."

msgid ""
"The reloading happens from the database the instance was loaded from, or "
"from the default database if the instance wasn't loaded from the database. "
"The ``using`` argument can be used to force the database used for reloading."
msgstr ""
"Tarlaíonn an t-athluchtú ón mbunachar sonraí ar luchtadh an cás uaidh, nó ón "
"mbunachar sonraí réamhshocraithe mura luchtaíodh an cás ón mbunachar sonraí. "
"Is féidir an argóint ``úsáid ``a úsáid chun an bunachar sonraí a úsáidtear "
"le haghaidh athluchtaithe a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"It is possible to force the set of fields to be loaded by using the "
"``fields`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir iallach a chur ar an tacar réimsí a luchtú tríd an argóint "
"``réimsí ``a úsáid."

msgid ""
"For example, to test that an ``update()`` call resulted in the expected "
"update, you could write a test similar to this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun tástáil a dhéanamh go raibh an nuashonrú ag súil leis mar "
"thoradh ar ghlao ``update () ``, d'fhéadfá tástáil cosúil leis seo a scríobh:"

msgid ""
"Note that when deferred fields are accessed, the loading of the deferred "
"field's value happens through this method. Thus it is possible to customize "
"the way deferred loading happens. The example below shows how one can reload "
"all of the instance's fields when a deferred field is reloaded::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, nuair a bhíonn rochtain ar réimsí iarchurtha, go "
"dtarlaíonn luach an réimse iarchurtha tríd an modh seo. Dá bhrí sin is "
"féidir an bealach a tharlaíonn luchtú iarchurtha a shaincheapadh. "
"Taispeánann an sampla thíos conas is féidir le réimsí uile an cháis a "
"athluchtú nuair a dhéantar réimse iarchurtha a athluchtú:"

msgid ""
"The ``from_queryset`` argument allows using a different queryset than the "
"one created from :attr:`~django.db.models.Model._base_manager`. It gives you "
"more control over how the model is reloaded. For example, when your model "
"uses soft deletion you can make ``refresh_from_db()`` to take this into "
"account::"
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn an argóint ``from_queryset`` tacar ceisteanna difriúil a úsáid ná "
"an ceann a cruthaíodh ó: attr: `~django.db.models.model. _bainisteoir "
"bunaisteoir'. Tugann sé níos mó smachta duit ar an gcaoi a n-athluchtaítear "
"an tsamhail. Mar shampla, nuair a úsáideann do mhúnla scriosadh bog is "
"féidir leat ``fresh_from_db () ``a dhéanamh chun é seo a chur san áireamh:"

msgid ""
"You can cache related objects that otherwise would be cleared from the "
"reloaded instance::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rudaí a bhaineann le taisce a ghlanfaí ar shlí eile ón gcás "
"athluchtaithe:"

msgid ""
"You can lock the row until the end of transaction before reloading a model's "
"values::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an tsraith a ghlasáil go dtí deireadh an idirbheart sula "
"ndéanfaidh tú luachanna samhail a athlódáil:"

msgid "The ``from_queryset`` argument was added."
msgstr "Cuireadh an argóint ``from_queryset`` leis."

msgid ""
"A helper method that returns a set containing the attribute names of all "
"those fields that are currently deferred for this model."
msgstr ""
"Modh cúntóra a thugann tacar ina bhfuil ainmneacha tréithe na réimsí sin go "
"léir atá iarchurtha faoi láthair don tsamhail seo."

msgid "Validating objects"
msgstr "Rudaí a bhailíochtú"

msgid "There are four steps involved in validating a model:"
msgstr "Tá ceithre chéim i gceist le samhail a bhailíochtú:"

msgid "Validate the model fields - :meth:`Model.clean_fields()`"
msgstr "Bailíochtú na réimsí samhail -:meth: `Model.clean_fields () `"

msgid "Validate the model as a whole - :meth:`Model.clean()`"
msgstr "Bailíochtú an tsamhail ina iomláine -:meth: `Model.clean () `"

msgid "Validate the field uniqueness - :meth:`Model.validate_unique()`"
msgstr "Bailíochtú uathúlacht an réimse -:meth: `Model.validate_unique () `"

msgid "Validate the constraints - :meth:`Model.validate_constraints`"
msgstr "Bailíochtú na srianta -:meth: `Model.validate_restricints`"

msgid ""
"All four steps are performed when you call a "
"model's :meth:`~Model.full_clean` method."
msgstr ""
"Déantar na ceithre chéim go léir nuair a ghlaonn tú ar mhodh samhail "
"'s:meth: `~model.full_clean`."

msgid ""
"When you use a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`, the call "
"to :meth:`~django.forms.Form.is_valid()` will perform these validation steps "
"for all the fields that are included on the form. See the :doc:`ModelForm "
"documentation </topics/forms/modelforms>` for more information. You should "
"only need to call a model's :meth:`~Model.full_clean()` method if you plan "
"to handle validation errors yourself, or if you have excluded fields from "
"the :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` that require validation."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáideann tú a:class: `~django.forms.modelform`, déanfaidh an glao "
"chuig:meth: `~django.forms.form.is_valid () `na céimeanna bailíochtaithe seo "
"do na réimsí uile atá san áireamh ar an bhfoirm. Féach na:doc: `Modelform "
"doiciméadach` le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais. </topics/forms/modelforms> Níor "
"chóir duit glaoch ar mhodh samhail's:meth: `~model.full_clean () `má tá sé "
"ar intinn agat earráidí bailíochtaithe a láimhseáil tú féin, nó má tá réimsí "
"eisiata agat ó:class: `~django.forms.ModelForm` a dteastaíonn bailíochtú "
"uathu."

msgid ""
"This method "
"calls :meth:`Model.clean_fields()`, :meth:`Model.clean()`, :meth:`Model.validate_unique()` "
"(if ``validate_unique`` is ``True``),  "
"and :meth:`Model.validate_constraints()` (if ``validate_constraints`` is "
"``True``) in that order and raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` that has a ``message_dict`` "
"attribute containing errors from all four stages."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn an modh seo: meth: `Model.clean_fields () `, :meth: `Model.clean "
"()`, :meth: `Model.validate_unique () `(má tá ``validate_unique`` `True``), "
"agus:meth: `Model.validate_restrictions ()` (más rud é "
"``validate_restricints`` True`` E``) san ord sin agus ardaíonn a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` a bhfuil tréith ``message_dict`` "
"ina bhfuil earráidí ó na ceithre chéim."

msgid ""
"The optional ``exclude`` argument can be used to provide a ``set`` of field "
"names that can be excluded from validation and "
"cleaning. :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm` uses this argument to exclude "
"fields that aren't present on your form from being validated since any "
"errors raised could not be corrected by the user."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an argóint roghnach ``eisiam`` a úsáid chun `taca`` d'ainmneacha "
"réimse a sholáthar is féidir iad a eisiamh ó bhailíochtú agus "
"glantachán. :class: `~django.forms.ModelForm` úsáideann an argóint seo chun "
"réimsí nach bhfuil i láthair ar d'fhoirm a eisiamh ó bheith bailíochtaithe "
"ós rud é nach bhféadfadh an t-úsáideoir aon earráidí a ardaíodh a cheartú."

msgid ""
"Note that ``full_clean()`` will *not* be called automatically when you call "
"your model's :meth:`~Model.save()` method. You'll need to call it manually "
"when you want to run one-step model validation for your own manually created "
"models. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go nglaofar ``full_clean () ``*ní* go huathoibríoch nuair "
"a ghlaonn tú ar do mhúnla 's:meth: `~model.save () `modh. Beidh ort glaoch "
"air de láimh nuair is mian leat bailíochtú samhail aon-chéim a reáchtáil do "
"do mhúnlaí féin a cruthaíodh de láimh. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The first step ``full_clean()`` performs is to clean each individual field."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chéim a dhéanann ``full_clean () ``gach réimse aonair a "
"ghlanadh."

msgid ""
"This method will validate all fields on your model. The optional ``exclude`` "
"argument lets you provide a ``set`` of field names to exclude from "
"validation. It will raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` "
"if any fields fail validation."
msgstr ""
"Bailíochnóidh an modh seo gach réimse ar do mhúnla. Ligeann an argóint "
"roghnach ``eisiam`` duit `taca`` d'ainmneacha réimse a sholáthar chun "
"eisiamh ó bhailíochtú. Ardóidh sé a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar aon réimsí "
"bailíochtú."

msgid ""
"The second step ``full_clean()`` performs is to call :meth:`Model.clean()`. "
"This method should be overridden to perform custom validation on your model."
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara céim a dhéanann ``full_clean () ``glaoch ar: meth: `Model.clean "
"() `. Ba chóir an modh seo a athsholáthar chun bailíochtú saincheaptha a "
"dhéanamh ar do mhúnla."

msgid ""
"This method should be used to provide custom model validation, and to modify "
"attributes on your model if desired. For instance, you could use it to "
"automatically provide a value for a field, or to do validation that requires "
"access to more than a single field::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir an modh seo a úsáid chun bailíochtú samhail saincheaptha a "
"sholáthar, agus tréithe ar do mhúnla a mhodhnú más mian. Mar shampla, "
"d'fhéadfá é a úsáid chun luach a sholáthar go huathoibríoch do réimse, nó "
"chun bailíochtú a dhéanamh a éilíonn rochtain ar níos mó ná réimse amháin:"

msgid ""
"Note, however, that like :meth:`Model.full_clean()`, a model's ``clean()`` "
"method is not invoked when you call your model's :meth:`~Model.save()` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, áfach, cosúil:meth: `Model.full_clean () `, ní "
"ghairmtear modh ``clean () ``samhail nuair a ghlaonn tú ar do mhúnla "
"'s:meth: `~Model.save ()` modh."

msgid ""
"In the above example, the :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` "
"exception raised by ``Model.clean()`` was instantiated with a string, so it "
"will be stored in a special error dictionary "
"key, :data:`~django.core.exceptions.NON_FIELD_ERRORS`. This key is used for "
"errors that are tied to the entire model instead of to a specific field::"
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, rinneadh an eisceacht: exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ValidationError` arna ardú ag ``Model.clean () ``le "
"sreang, mar sin stóráilfear é in eochair foclóir earráide speisialta, :data: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.non_field_errors`. Úsáidtear an eochair seo le "
"haghaidh earráidí atá ceangailte leis an tsamhail iomlán in ionad le réimse "
"ar leith:"

msgid ""
"To assign exceptions to a specific field, instantiate "
"the :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a dictionary, where "
"the keys are the field names. We could update the previous example to assign "
"the error to the ``pub_date`` field::"
msgstr ""
"Chun eisceachtaí a shannadh do réimse ar leith, cuir ainmne:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le foclóir, áit a bhfuil na "
"heochracha ainmneacha réimse. D'fhéadfaimis an sampla roimhe seo a nuashonrú "
"chun an earráid a shannadh don réimse ``pub_date``:"

msgid ""
"If you detect errors in multiple fields during ``Model.clean()``, you can "
"also pass a dictionary mapping field names to errors::"
msgstr ""
"Má bhraitheann tú earráidí i réimsí iolracha le linn ``Model.clean () ``, is "
"féidir leat ainmneacha réimse mapála foclóra a chur ar earráidí freisin:"

msgid "Then, ``full_clean()`` will check unique constraints on your model."
msgstr "Ansin, seiceálfaidh ``full_clean () ``srianta uathúla ar do mhúnla."

msgid ""
"How to raise field-specific validation errors if those fields don't appear "
"in a ``ModelForm``"
msgstr ""
"Conas earráidí bailíochtaithe réimsiúnta a ardú mura bhfuil na réimsí sin le "
"feiceáil i ``Modelfhoirme``"

msgid ""
"You can't raise validation errors in ``Model.clean()`` for fields that don't "
"appear in a model form (a form may limit its fields using ``Meta.fields`` or "
"``Meta.exclude``). Doing so will raise a ``ValueError`` because the "
"validation error won't be able to be associated with the excluded field."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leat earráidí bailíochtaithe a ardú in `Model.clean () ``do réimsí "
"nach bhfuil le feiceáil i bhfoirm mhúnla (féadfaidh foirm a réimsí a "
"theorannú ag baint úsáide as `Meta.Fields`` nó `Meta.Exclude``). Ag déanamh "
"amhlaidh, ardófar ``Error lua`` toisc nach mbeidh an earráid bailíochtaithe "
"in ann a bheith bainteach leis an réimse eisiata."

msgid ""
"To work around this dilemma, instead override :meth:`Model.clean_fields() "
"<django.db.models.Model.clean_fields>` as it receives the list of fields "
"that are excluded from validation. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun oibriú timpeall ar an aincheist seo, ina ionad sin déan iarrthó:meth: "
"`model.clean_fields () <django.db.models.Model.clean_fields>`mar a "
"fhaigheann sé liosta na réimsí atá eisiata ó bhailíochtú. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"This method is similar to :meth:`~Model.clean_fields`, but validates "
"uniqueness constraints defined "
"via :attr:`.Field.unique`, :attr:`.Field.unique_for_date`, :attr:`.Field.unique_for_month`, :attr:`.Field.unique_for_year`, "
"or :attr:`Meta.unique_together <django.db.models.Options.unique_together>` "
"on your model instead of individual field values. The optional ``exclude`` "
"argument allows you to provide a ``set`` of field names to exclude from "
"validation. It will raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` "
"if any fields fail validation."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.unique_together>Tá an modh seo cosúil le:meth: "
"`~Model.Clean_Fields`, ach bailíochnaíonn sé srianta uathúlachta atá "
"sainmhínithe trí:attr: `.field.unique`, :attr: "
"`.field.unique_for_date`, :attr: `.field.unique_for_year`, nó r: "
"`Meta.unique_Together `ar do mhúnla in ionad luachanna réimse aonair. "
"Ligeann an argóint roghnach ``eisiam`` duit `taca`` d'ainmneacha réimse a "
"sholáthar chun eisiamh ó bhailíochtú. Ardóidh sé a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar aon réimsí "
"bailíochtú."

msgid ""
":class:`~django.db.models.UniqueConstraint`\\s defined in "
"the :attr:`Meta.constraints <django.db.models.Options.constraints>` are "
"validated by :meth:`Model.validate_constraints`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.constraints>:class: "
"`~Django.db.Models.UniqueConstraint`\\ na sainmhínithe in:attr: "
"`Meta.Constraint` bailíochtaí:meth: `Model.validate_restricints`."

msgid ""
"Note that if you provide an ``exclude`` argument to ``validate_unique()``, "
"any :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.unique_together` constraint involving "
"one of the fields you provided will not be checked."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara má sholáthraíonn tú argóint ``exclude`` do "
"`validate_unique () ``, ní sheiceálfar srian aon cheann:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.unique_together` a bhaineann le ceann de na "
"réimsí a chuir tú ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Finally, ``full_clean()`` will check any other constraints on your model."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, seiceálfaidh ``full_clean () ``aon srianta eile ar do mhúnla."

msgid ""
"This method validates all constraints defined in :attr:`Meta.constraints "
"<django.db.models.Options.constraints>`. The optional ``exclude`` argument "
"allows you to provide a ``set`` of field names to exclude from validation. "
"It will raise a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if any "
"constraints fail validation."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Options.constraints>Bailíonn an modh seo na srianta go "
"léir a shainmhínítear in:attr: `Meta.Constraints `. Ligeann an argóint "
"roghnach ``eisiam`` duit `taca`` d'ainmneacha réimse a sholáthar chun "
"eisiamh ó bhailíochtú. Ardóidh sé a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar aon srianta ar "
"bhailíochtú."

msgid "Saving objects"
msgstr "Rudaí a shábháil"

msgid "To save an object back to the database, call ``save()``:"
msgstr ""
"Chun réad a shábháil ar ais chuig an mbunachar sonraí, glaoigh ar `save () "
"``:"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``asave()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``asave () ``"

msgid ""
"For details on using the ``force_insert`` and ``force_update`` arguments, "
"see :ref:`ref-models-force-insert`. Details about the ``update_fields`` "
"argument can be found in the :ref:`ref-models-update-fields` section."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sonraí maidir le húsáid na hargóintí ``force_insert`` agus "
"``force_update``, féach:ref: `ref-models-force-insert`. Is féidir sonraí "
"faoin argóint ``update_fields`` a fháil sa ranna:ref: `ref-models-update-"
"fields`."

msgid ""
"If you want customized saving behavior, you can override this ``save()`` "
"method. See :ref:`overriding-model-methods` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iompar sábhála saincheaptha, is féidir leat an modh “save ()” "
"seo a shárú. Féach: Ref: `overriding-model-methods` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"The model save process also has some subtleties; see the sections below."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt caoilteachtaí ag an bpróiseas sábhála samhail freisin; féach na "
"codanna thíos."

msgid "Support for positional arguments is deprecated."
msgstr "Tá tacaíocht d'argóintí seasaimh míchuige."

msgid "Auto-incrementing primary keys"
msgstr "Eochracha bunscoile uathoibríoch"

msgid ""
"If a model has an :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` — an auto-"
"incrementing primary key — then that auto-incremented value will be "
"calculated and saved as an attribute on your object the first time you call "
"``save()``:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá samhail ag: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` - eochair phríomh-"
"mhéadaithe uathoibríoch - ansin ríomhfar agus sábhálfar an luach "
"uathoibríoch sin mar thréith ar do réad an chéad uair a ghlaonn tú ar `save "
"() ``:"

msgid ""
"There's no way to tell what the value of an ID will be before you call "
"``save()``, because that value is calculated by your database, not by Django."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon bhealach ann a insint cad é luach aitheantais sula nglaonn tú ar "
"``save () ``, toisc go ríomh do bhunachar sonraí an luach sin, ní ag Django."

msgid ""
"For convenience, each model has an :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` "
"named ``id`` by default unless you explicitly specify ``primary_key=True`` "
"on a field in your model. See the documentation "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le áisiúlacht, tá: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` ag gach "
"samhail darb ainm `id`` de réir réamhshocraithe mura sonraíonn tú go "
"sainráite ``primary_key=true`` ar réimse i do mhúnla. Féach an doiciméadú le "
"haghaidh: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "The ``pk`` property"
msgstr "An mhaoin ``pk``"

msgid ""
"Regardless of whether you define a primary key field yourself, or let Django "
"supply one for you, each model will have a property called ``pk``. It "
"behaves like a normal attribute on the model, but is actually an alias for "
"whichever field or fields compose the primary key for the model. You can "
"read and set this value, just as you would for any other attribute, and it "
"will update the correct fields in the model."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support for the primary key to be composed of multiple fields was added via "
"``CompositePrimaryKey``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Explicitly specifying auto-primary-key values"
msgstr "Luachanna eochair uathoibríoch-phríomhúil"

msgid ""
"If a model has an :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` but you want to "
"define a new object's ID explicitly when saving, define it explicitly before "
"saving, rather than relying on the auto-assignment of the ID:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` ag samhail ach ba mhaith leat "
"aitheantas réad nua a shainiú go sainráite agus tú ag sábháil, sainmhínigh é "
"go sainráite sula ndéantar é a shábháil, seachas brath ar shannadh "
"uathoibríoch an ID:"

msgid ""
"If you assign auto-primary-key values manually, make sure not to use an "
"already-existing primary-key value! If you create a new object with an "
"explicit primary-key value that already exists in the database, Django will "
"assume you're changing the existing record rather than creating a new one."
msgstr ""
"Má shannann tú luachanna eochair uathoibríoch de láimh, déan cinnte nach n-"
"úsáideann tú luach príomh-eochair atá ann cheana féin! Má chruthaíonn tú "
"réad nua le luach príomh-eochair follasach atá ann cheana féin sa bhunachar "
"sonraí, glacfaidh Django leis go bhfuil tú ag athrú an taifead atá ann "
"cheana seachas ceann nua a chruthú."

msgid ""
"Given the above ``'Cheddar Talk'`` blog example, this example would override "
"the previous record in the database::"
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an sampla bhlag ``Cheddar Talk`` thuas, chuirfeadh an sampla "
"seo an taifead roimhe seo sa bhunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"See `How Django knows to UPDATE vs. INSERT`_, below, for the reason this "
"happens."
msgstr ""
"Féach `Conas a bhfuil a fhios ag Django nuashonrú vs INSERT`_, thíos, ar an "
"gcúis a tharlaíonn sé seo."

msgid ""
"Explicitly specifying auto-primary-key values is mostly useful for bulk-"
"saving objects, when you're confident you won't have primary-key collision."
msgstr ""
"Tá luachanna eochair uathoibríoch a shonrú go sainráite úsáideach den chuid "
"is mó le haghaidh rudaí sábhála móra, nuair a bhíonn tú muiníneach nach "
"mbeidh imbhuailt eochair"

msgid ""
"If you're using PostgreSQL, the sequence associated with the primary key "
"might need to be updated; see :ref:`manually-specified-autoincrement-pk`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá PostgreSQL á úsáid agat, b'fhéidir go mbeadh gá an seicheamh a "
"bhaineann leis an bpríomh-eochair a nuashonrú; féach:ref: `manually-specied-"
"autoincrement-pk`."

msgid "What happens when you save?"
msgstr "Cad a tharlaíonn nuair a shábháil tú?"

msgid "When you save an object, Django performs the following steps:"
msgstr "Nuair a shábhálann tú réad, déanann Django na céimeanna seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"**Emit a pre-save signal.** The :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` "
"signal is sent, allowing any functions listening for that signal to do "
"something."
msgstr ""
"**Easaigh comhartha réamh-shábháil.** Seoltar an comhartha: Data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save`, rud a ligeann d'aon fheidhmeanna a "
"éisteann don chomhartha sin rud éigin a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"**Preprocess the data.** Each "
"field's :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.pre_save` method is called to perform "
"any automated data modification that's needed. For example, the date/time "
"fields override ``pre_save()`` to "
"implement :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now_add` "
"and :attr:`~django.db.models.DateField.auto_now`."
msgstr ""
"**Réamhphróiseáil na sonraí.** Glaítear ar gach réimse:: "
"`~django.db.models.field.pre_save` modh chun aon mhodhnú uathoibrithe sonraí "
"a theastaíonn a dhéanamh. Mar shampla, athraíonn na réimsí dáta/ama "
"``pre_save () ``chun cur i bhfeidhmiú:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.datefield.auto_now_add` agus:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.datefield.auto_now`."

msgid ""
"**Prepare the data for the database.** Each "
"field's :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.get_db_prep_save` method is asked to "
"provide its current value in a data type that can be written to the database."
msgstr ""
"**Ullmhaigh na sonraí don bhunachar sonraí.** Iarrtar ar gach réimse:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.field.get_db_prep_save` modh a luach reatha a sholáthar i "
"gcineál sonraí is féidir a scríobh chuig an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Most fields don't require data preparation. Simple data types, such as "
"integers and strings, are 'ready to write' as a Python object. However, more "
"complex data types often require some modification."
msgstr ""
"Ní theastaíonn ullmhú sonraí ó chuid is mó de na réimsí. Tá cineálacha "
"sonraí simplí, mar shampla sláimhreacha agus teaghráin, 'réidh le scríobh' "
"mar réad Python. Mar sin féin, is minic a éilíonn roinnt modhnú ó "
"chineálacha sonraí níos cast"

msgid ""
"For example, :class:`~django.db.models.DateField` fields use a Python "
"``datetime`` object to store data. Databases don't store ``datetime`` "
"objects, so the field value must be converted into an ISO-compliant date "
"string for insertion into the database."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, úsáideann réimsí: :class: `~django.db.Models.DateField` réad "
"Python ``datetime`` chun sonraí a stóráil. Ní stóráilíonn bunachair sonraí "
"rudaí ``datetime``, mar sin caithfear an luach réimse a thiontú ina teaghrán "
"dáta comhlíontach ISO lena chur isteach sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"**Insert the data into the database.** The preprocessed, prepared data is "
"composed into an SQL statement for insertion into the database."
msgstr ""
"**Cuir na sonraí isteach sa bhunachar sonraí.** Tá na sonraí "
"réamhphróiseáilte, ullmhaithe comhdhéanta i ráiteas SQL lena chur isteach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"**Emit a post-save signal.** The :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` "
"signal is sent, allowing any functions listening for that signal to do "
"something."
msgstr ""
"**Easaigh comhartha iar-shábháil.** Seoltar an comhartha: Data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_save`, rud a ligeann d'aon fheidhmeanna a "
"éisteann don chomhartha sin rud éigin a dhéanamh."

msgid "How Django knows to UPDATE vs. INSERT"
msgstr "Conas a bhfuil a fhios ag Django UPDATE vs INSERT"

msgid ""
"You may have noticed Django database objects use the same ``save()`` method "
"for creating and changing objects. Django abstracts the need to use "
"``INSERT`` or ``UPDATE`` SQL statements. Specifically, when you call "
"``save()`` and the object's primary key attribute does **not** define "
"a :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_default`, Django follows this algorithm:"
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur thug tú faoi deara go n-úsáideann rudaí bunachar sonraí Django "
"an modh céanna ``save () `chun rudaí a chruthú agus a athrú. Déanann Django "
"achoimrí ar an ngá chun ráitis SQL ``INSERT`` nó ``UPDATE`` a úsáid. Go "
"sonrach, nuair a ghlaonn tú ar `save () ``agus nuair a shainmhíníonn príomh-"
"thréith an réad** a:attr: `~django.db.models.field.default` nó: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.db_default`, leanann Django an algartam seo:"

msgid ""
"If the object's primary key attribute is set to anything except ``None``, "
"Django executes an ``UPDATE``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the object's primary key attribute is *not* set or if the ``UPDATE`` "
"didn't update anything (e.g. if primary key is set to a value that doesn't "
"exist in the database), Django executes an ``INSERT``."
msgstr ""
"Más rud é príomh-thréith eochair an réad* socraithe nó mura ndearna an "
"`UPDATE`` rud ar bith a nuashonrú (m.sh. má tá eochair phríomhúil socraithe "
"ar luach nach bhfuil sa bhunachar sonraí ann), déanann Django ``INSERT`` a "
"fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"If the object's primary key attribute defines "
"a :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_default` then Django executes an "
"``UPDATE`` if it is an existing model instance and primary key is set to a "
"value that exists in the database. Otherwise, Django executes an ``INSERT``."
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhíníonn príomhthréith an réada a:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.default` nó: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.db_default` ansin déanann Django ``UPDATE`` a "
"fhorghníomhú más samhail samhail atá ann agus socraítear eochair phríomhúil "
"ar luach atá ann sa bhunachar sonraí. Seachas sin, déanann Django ``INSERT`` "
"a fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"The one gotcha here is that you should be careful not to specify a primary-"
"key value explicitly when saving new objects, if you cannot guarantee the "
"primary-key value is unused. For more on this nuance, see `Explicitly "
"specifying auto-primary-key values`_ above and `Forcing an INSERT or "
"UPDATE`_ below."
msgstr ""
"Is é an ceann a thugann anseo ná gur chóir duit a bheith cúramach gan luach "
"príomh-eochair a shonrú go sainráite agus rudaí nua á shábháil, mura féidir "
"leat a ráthú nach bhfuil an luach príomh-eochair neamhúsáidte. Le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais faoin nuans seo, féach `Luachanna uathoibríoch-phríomhúil a "
"shonrú go sainráite `_ thuas agus `INSERT nó UPDATE`a chur i bhfeidhm `_ "
"thíos."

msgid ""
"In Django 1.5 and earlier, Django did a ``SELECT`` when the primary key "
"attribute was set. If the ``SELECT`` found a row, then Django did an "
"``UPDATE``, otherwise it did an ``INSERT``. The old algorithm results in one "
"more query in the ``UPDATE`` case. There are some rare cases where the "
"database doesn't report that a row was updated even if the database contains "
"a row for the object's primary key value. An example is the PostgreSQL ``ON "
"UPDATE`` trigger which returns ``NULL``. In such cases it is possible to "
"revert to the old algorithm by setting "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.select_on_save` option to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"I Django 1.5 agus níos luaithe, rinne Django ``SELECT`` nuair a shocraíodh "
"an príomh-thréith eochair. Má aimsigh an ``SELECT`` sraith, ansin rinne "
"Django ``UPDATE``, ar shlí eile rinne sé ``INSERT``. Mar thoradh ar an sean-"
"algartam bíonn ceist amháin eile sa chás ``UPDATE``. Tá roinnt cásanna "
"annamh ann nach dtuairiscíonn an bunachar sonraí gur nuashonraíodh sraith "
"fiú má tá sraith sa bhunachar sonraí do phríomhluach an réada. Sampla is ea "
"an truicear PostgreSQL ``ON UPDATE`` a fhilleann ``NULL``. I gcásanna den "
"sórt sin is féidir filleadh ar an sean-algartam tríd an rogha: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.select_on_save` a shocrú go ``True``."

msgid "Forcing an INSERT or UPDATE"
msgstr "INSERT nó UPDATE a chur i bhfeidhm"

msgid ""
"In some rare circumstances, it's necessary to be able to force "
"the :meth:`~Model.save()` method to perform an SQL ``INSERT`` and not fall "
"back to doing an ``UPDATE``. Or vice-versa: update, if possible, but not "
"insert a new row. In these cases you can pass the ``force_insert=True`` or "
"``force_update=True`` parameters to the :meth:`~Model.save()` method. "
"Passing both parameters is an error: you cannot both insert *and* update at "
"the same time!"
msgstr ""
"I roinnt imthosca annamh, is gá a bheith in ann an modh: meth: `~Model.save "
"() `a chur i bhfeidhm chun SQL ``INSERT`` a dhéanamh agus gan titim siar "
"chun ``UPDATE`` a dhéanamh. Nó a mhalairt: nuashonraigh, más féidir, ach ná "
"cuir isteach sraith nua. Sna cásanna seo is féidir leat na paraiméadair "
"``Force_insert=True`` nó ``Force_Update=True`` a chur chuig an modh:meth: "
"`~Model.save () `. Is earráid é an dá pharaiméadar a rith: ní féidir leat "
"nuashonraithe* agus* a chur isteach ag an am céanna!"

msgid ""
"When using :ref:`multi-table inheritance <multi-table-inheritance>`, it's "
"also possible to provide a tuple of parent classes to ``force_insert`` in "
"order to force ``INSERT`` statements for each base. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear: ref: `oidhreacht il-tábla <multi-table-inheritance>`, is "
"féidir freisin tuipéil de na tuismitheoirí a sholáthar do ``force_insert`` "
"d'fhonn ráitis ``INSERT`` a chur i bhfeidhm do gach bonn. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"You can pass ``force_insert=(models.Model,)`` to force an ``INSERT`` "
"statement for all parents. By default, ``force_insert=True`` only forces the "
"insertion of a new row for the current model."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``force_insert= (Models.model,) ``a rith chun ráiteas "
"``INSERT`` a chur i bhfeidhm do gach tuismitheoir. De réir réamhshocraithe, "
"ní chuireann ``force_insert=True`` ach sraith nua a chur isteach don "
"tsamhail reatha."

msgid ""
"It should be very rare that you'll need to use these parameters. Django will "
"almost always do the right thing and trying to override that will lead to "
"errors that are difficult to track down. This feature is for advanced use "
"only."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh sé an-annamh go mbeidh ort na paraiméadair seo a úsáid. "
"Déanfaidh Django an rud ceart beagnach i gcónaí agus déanfaidh sé iarracht a "
"shárú a bheidh mar thoradh ar earráidí atá deacair a rianú. Tá an ghné seo "
"le haghaidh ardúsáide amháin."

msgid ""
"Using ``update_fields`` will force an update similarly to ``force_update``."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as ``update_fields``, cuirfear iallach ar nuashonrú ar an "
"gcéanna le ``force_update``."

msgid "Updating attributes based on existing fields"
msgstr "tréithe a nuashonrú bunaithe ar réimsí atá ann"

msgid ""
"Sometimes you'll need to perform a simple arithmetic task on a field, such "
"as incrementing or decrementing the current value. One way of achieving this "
"is doing the arithmetic in Python like:"
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta beidh ort tasc uimhrithíochta simplí a dhéanamh ar réimse, mar "
"shampla an luach reatha a mhéadú nó a laghdú. Bealach amháin chun é seo a "
"bhaint amach is ea an uimhríocht a dhéanamh i Python mar:"

msgid ""
"If the old ``number_sold`` value retrieved from the database was 10, then "
"the value of 11 will be written back to the database."
msgstr ""
"Más é 10 an seanluach ``number_sold`` a aisghabhadh ón mbunachar sonraí, "
"ansin scríobhfar luach 11 ar ais chuig an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The process can be made robust, :ref:`avoiding a race condition <avoiding-"
"race-conditions-using-f>`, as well as slightly faster by expressing the "
"update relative to the original field value, rather than as an explicit "
"assignment of a new value. Django provides :class:`F expressions "
"<django.db.models.F>` for performing this kind of relative update. "
"Using :class:`F expressions <django.db.models.F>`, the previous example is "
"expressed as:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an próiseas a dhéanamh láidir, :ref: `<avoiding-race-conditions-"
"using-f>riocht rása a sheachaint`, chomh maith le beagán níos gasta tríd an "
"nuashonrú a chur in iúl i gcoibhneas leis an luach réimse bunaidh, seachas "
"mar shannadh follasach de luach nua. Soláthraíonn Django: class: `Abairtí F "
"<django.db.models.F>`chun nuashonrú coibhneasta den chineál seo a dhéanamh. "
"Ag baint úsáide as: aicme: `Abairtí F <django.db.models.F>`, cuirtear an "
"sampla roimhe seo in iúl mar:"

msgid ""
"For more details, see the documentation on :class:`F expressions "
"<django.db.models.F>` and their :ref:`use in update queries <topics-db-"
"queries-update>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-queries-update>Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, féach an doiciméadú "
"ar:class: `F abairtí <django.db.models.F>`agus a n:ref: `úsáid i gceisteanna "
"nuashonraithe`."

msgid "Specifying which fields to save"
msgstr "Sonraítear na réimsí atá le sábháil"

msgid ""
"If ``save()`` is passed a list of field names in keyword argument "
"``update_fields``, only the fields named in that list will be updated. This "
"may be desirable if you want to update just one or a few fields on an "
"object. There will be a slight performance benefit from preventing all of "
"the model fields from being updated in the database. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear ``save () ``ar liosta ainmneacha réimse in argóint "
"eochairfhocal ``update_fields``, ní dhéanfar ach na réimsí ainmnithe ar an "
"liosta sin a nuashonrú. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith inmhianaithe más mian "
"leat ach réimse amháin nó cúpla réimse a nuashonrú ar réad. Beidh leas beag "
"feidhmíochta ann as cosc a chur ar na réimsí samhlacha go léir a nuashonrú "
"sa bhunachar sonraí. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The ``update_fields`` argument can be any iterable containing strings. An "
"empty ``update_fields`` iterable will skip the save. A value of ``None`` "
"will perform an update on all fields."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an argóint `update_fields`` a bheith ina aon athraitheacha "
"ina bhfuil teaghráin. Sceapfaidh athraitheach folamh ``update_fields`` an "
"sábháil. Déanfaidh luach ``None ``nuashonrú ar gach réimse."

msgid "Specifying ``update_fields`` will force an update."
msgstr "Má shonrófar ``update_fields``, cuirfear iallach ar nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"When saving a model fetched through deferred model loading "
"(:meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.only()` "
"or :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.defer()`) only the fields loaded "
"from the DB will get updated. In effect there is an automatic "
"``update_fields`` in this case. If you assign or change any deferred field "
"value, the field will be added to the updated fields."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shábháil samhail a fuarthas trí luchtú samhail iarchurtha (:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.only () `nó: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.defer ()`) ní dhéanfar ach na réimsí "
"luchtaithe ón DB a nuashonrú. I ndáiríre tá ``update_fields`` uathoibríoch "
"sa chás seo. Má shannann tú nó má athraíonn tú aon luach réimse iarchurtha, "
"cuirfear an réimse leis na réimsí nuashonraithe."

msgid "``Field.pre_save()`` and ``update_fields``"
msgstr "``Field.pre_save () ``agus ``update_fields``"

msgid ""
"If ``update_fields`` is passed in, only "
"the :meth:`~django.db.models.Field.pre_save` methods of the "
"``update_fields`` are called. For example, this means that date/time fields "
"with ``auto_now=True`` will not be updated unless they are included in the "
"``update_fields``."
msgstr ""
"Má chuirtear ``update_fields`` isteach, ní thugtar ach modhanna: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.field.pre_save` de na modhanna ``update_fields``. Mar "
"shampla, ciallaíonn sé seo nach ndéanfar réimsí dáta/ama le `auto_now=true`` "
"a nuashonrú mura gcuirtear iad san áireamh sna ``update_fields``."

msgid "Deleting objects"
msgstr "Rudaí a scriosadh"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``adelete()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``adelete () ``"

msgid ""
"Issues an SQL ``DELETE`` for the object. This only deletes the object in the "
"database; the Python instance will still exist and will still have data in "
"its fields, except for the primary key set to ``None``. This method returns "
"the number of objects deleted and a dictionary with the number of deletions "
"per object type."
msgstr ""
"Eisíonn SQL ``DELETE`` don réad. Ní scriosann sé seo ach an réad sa "
"bhunachar sonraí; beidh an cás Python ann fós agus beidh sonraí ann ina "
"réimsí fós, ach amháin an príomh-eochair atá socraithe go ``None``. Tugann "
"an modh seo líon na rudaí scriosta agus foclóir le líon na scriosadh in "
"aghaidh an chineál réada ar ais."

msgid ""
"For more details, including how to delete objects in bulk, see :ref:`topics-"
"db-queries-delete`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí, lena n-áirítear conas rudaí a scriosadh ar an "
"mórchóir, féach:ref: `topics-db-queries-delete`."

msgid ""
"If you want customized deletion behavior, you can override the ``delete()`` "
"method. See :ref:`overriding-model-methods` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat iompar scriosta saincheaptha, is féidir leat an modh ``delete "
"() ``a shárú. Féach: Ref: `overriding-model-methods` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid ""
"Sometimes with :ref:`multi-table inheritance <multi-table-inheritance>` you "
"may want to delete only a child model's data. Specifying "
"``keep_parents=True`` will keep the parent model's data."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta <multi-table-inheritance>le: ref: `oidhreacht il-tábla` b'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat ach sonraí samhail linbh a scriosadh. Coinneoidh sonraí an "
"tsamhail tuismitheora a shonrú ``keep_parents=True``."

msgid "Pickling objects"
msgstr "Rudaí piceála"

msgid ""
"When you :mod:`pickle` a model, its current state is pickled. When you "
"unpickle it, it'll contain the model instance at the moment it was pickled, "
"rather than the data that's currently in the database."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéanann tú: mod: `pickle` samhail, piciltear a staid reatha. Nuair "
"a dhíphicfidh tú é, beidh an samhail samhail ann i láthair na huaire a "
"piceáladh é, seachas na sonraí atá sa bhunachar sonraí faoi láthair."

msgid "You can't share pickles between versions"
msgstr "Ní féidir leat picíní a roinnt idir leaganacha"

msgid ""
"Pickles of models are only valid for the version of Django that was used to "
"generate them. If you generate a pickle using Django version N, there is no "
"guarantee that pickle will be readable with Django version N+1. Pickles "
"should not be used as part of a long-term archival strategy."
msgstr ""
"Níl picilí samhlacha bailí ach don leagan de Django a úsáideadh chun iad a "
"ghiniúint. Má ghineann tú picle ag baint úsáide as leagan Django N, níl aon "
"ráthaíocht ann go mbeidh picle inléite le leagan Django N+1. Níor chóir "
"picilí a úsáid mar chuid de straitéis cartlainne fadtéarmach."

msgid ""
"Since pickle compatibility errors can be difficult to diagnose, such as "
"silently corrupted objects, a ``RuntimeWarning`` is raised when you try to "
"unpickle a model in a Django version that is different than the one in which "
"it was pickled."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhféadfadh sé a bheith deacair earráidí comhoiriúnachta picéil a "
"dhiagnóisiú, mar shampla rudaí truaillithe go ciúin, ardaítear "
"``RuntimeWarning`` nuair a dhéanann tú iarracht samhail a dhíphiocadh i "
"leagan Django atá difriúil ná an ceann inar piceáladh é."

msgid "Other model instance methods"
msgstr "Modhanna samhail eile"

msgid "A few object methods have special purposes."
msgstr "Tá cuspóirí speisialta ag cúpla modh réad."

msgid "``__str__()``"
msgstr "```__str__ () ``"

msgid ""
"The ``__str__()`` method is called whenever you call ``str()`` on an object. "
"Django uses ``str(obj)`` in a number of places. Most notably, to display an "
"object in the Django admin site and as the value inserted into a template "
"when it displays an object. Thus, you should always return a nice, human-"
"readable representation of the model from the ``__str__()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Glaítear ar an modh ``__str__ () ``aon uair a ghlaonn tú ``str ()`` ar réad. "
"Úsáideann Django ``str (obj) ``i roinnt áiteanna. Go háirithe, rud a "
"thaispeáint ar shuíomh riaracháin Django agus mar an luach a cuireadh "
"isteach i dteimpléad nuair a thaispeánann sé réad. Dá bhrí sin, ba cheart "
"duit léiriú deas, inléite don duine ar an tsamhail a thabhairt ar ais i "
"gcónaí ón modh ``__str__ () ``."

msgid "``__eq__()``"
msgstr "```__eq__ () ``"

msgid ""
"The equality method is defined such that instances with the same primary key "
"value and the same concrete class are considered equal, except that "
"instances with a primary key value of ``None`` aren't equal to anything "
"except themselves. For proxy models, concrete class is defined as the "
"model's first non-proxy parent; for all other models it's simply the model's "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínítear an modh comhionannais ionas go measfar cásanna a bhfuil an "
"príomh-luach céanna agus an aicme coincréite céanna cothrom acu, ach amháin "
"nach bhfuil cásanna a bhfuil príomh-phríomhluach “None” comhionann le haon "
"rud seachas iad féin. Maidir le samhlacha seachfhreastalaí, sainmhínítear "
"rang coincréite mar an chéad thuismitheoir neamh-seachfhreastalaí an "
"tsamhail; i gcás gach samhail eile níl ann ach aicme"

msgid "``__hash__()``"
msgstr "``__hash__ () ``"

msgid ""
"The ``__hash__()`` method is based on the instance's primary key value. It "
"is effectively ``hash(obj.pk)``. If the instance doesn't have a primary key "
"value then a ``TypeError`` will be raised (otherwise the ``__hash__()`` "
"method would return different values before and after the instance is saved, "
"but changing the :meth:`~object.__hash__` value of an instance is forbidden "
"in Python."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh ``__hash__ () ``bunaithe ar phríomhluach an cháis. Tá sé go "
"héifeachtach ``hash (obj.pk) ``. Mura bhfuil príomhluach ag an gcás ansin "
"ardófar ``TypeError`` (ar shlí eile chuirfeadh an modh ``__hash__ () "
"``luachanna difriúla ar ais roimh agus tar éis an cás a shábháil, ach "
"athródh an: meth: `~ réad. Tá toirmiscthe ar luach __hash__` de shampla i "
"Python."

msgid "``get_absolute_url()``"
msgstr "```get_absolute_url () ``"

msgid ""
"Define a ``get_absolute_url()`` method to tell Django how to calculate the "
"canonical URL for an object. To callers, this method should appear to return "
"a string that can be used to refer to the object over HTTP."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhínigh modh ``get_absolute_url () ``chun a insint do Django conas an "
"URL canónach do réad a ríomh. Maidir le glaonna, ba cheart go bhfeicfeadh an "
"modh seo sreang ar ais is féidir a úsáid chun tagairt a dhéanamh don réad "
"thar HTTP."

msgid ""
"While this code is correct and simple, it may not be the most portable way "
"to to write this kind of method. The :func:`~django.urls.reverse` function "
"is usually the best approach."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil an cód seo ceart agus simplí, b'fhéidir nach é an bealach is "
"iniompartha chun modh den chineál seo a scríobh. Is gnách gurb é an fheidhm: "
"Func: `~django.urls.reverse` an cur chuige is fearr."

msgid ""
"One place Django uses ``get_absolute_url()`` is in the admin app. If an "
"object defines this method, the object-editing page will have a \"View on "
"site\" link that will jump you directly to the object's public view, as "
"given by ``get_absolute_url()``."
msgstr ""
"Tá áit amháin a úsáideann Django ``get_absolute_url () ``san aip riaracháin. "
"Má shainmhíníonn réad an modh seo, beidh nasc “Amharc ar an láithreán” ag an "
"leathanach eagarthóireachta réada a léimfidh tú go díreach chuig dearcadh "
"poiblí an réada, mar a thugann ``get_absolute_url () ``."

msgid ""
"Similarly, a couple of other bits of Django, such as the :doc:`syndication "
"feed framework </ref/contrib/syndication>`, use ``get_absolute_url()`` when "
"it is defined. If it makes sense for your model's instances to each have a "
"unique URL, you should define ``get_absolute_url()``."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, úsáideann cúpla giotán eile de Django, mar shampla an: "
"doc: `creat beatha syndication` ``get_absolute_url () ``nuair </ref/contrib/"
"syndication> a shainmhínítear é. Má tá sé ciallmhar do chásanna do mhúnla go "
"bhfuil URL uathúil ag gach ceann acu, ba cheart duit ``get_absolute_url () "
"`a shainiú."

msgid ""
"You should avoid building the URL from unvalidated user input, in order to "
"reduce possibilities of link or redirect poisoning::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit an URL a thógáil ó ionchur úsáideora neamhbhailíochtaithe a "
"sheachaint, d'fhonn féidearthachtaí nasc nó nimhiú a atreorú a laghdú"

msgid ""
"If ``self.name`` is ``'/example.com'`` this returns ``'//example.com/'`` "
"which, in turn, is a valid schema relative URL but not the expected ``'/"
"%2Fexample.com/'``."
msgstr ""
"Más é ``self.name`` ```/example.com'`` filleann sé ```'//example.com/'`` ar "
"URL bailí scéime coibhneasta é ach ní an ``'/%2Fexample.com/'` a bhfuil súil "
"leis."

msgid ""
"It's good practice to use ``get_absolute_url()`` in templates, instead of "
"hard-coding your objects' URLs. For example, this template code is bad:"
msgstr ""
"Is dea-chleachtas é ``get_absolute_url () ``a úsáid i dteimpléid, in ionad "
"URLanna do chuid rudaí a chódú go crua. Mar shampla, tá an cód teimpléid seo "
"dona:"

msgid "This template code is much better:"
msgstr "Tá an cód teimpléad seo i bhfad níos fearr:"

msgid ""
"The logic here is that if you change the URL structure of your objects, even "
"for something small like correcting a spelling error, you don't want to have "
"to track down every place that the URL might be created. Specify it once, in "
"``get_absolute_url()`` and have all your other code call that one place."
msgstr ""
"Is é an loighic anseo ná má athraíonn tú struchtúr URL do chuid rudaí, fiú "
"le haghaidh rud beag cosúil le earráid litrithe a cheartú, nach dteastaíonn "
"uait gach áit a d'fhéadfaí an URL a chruthú a rianú. Sonraigh é uair amháin, "
"i `get_absolute_url () ``agus glaoigh do chód eile go léir ar an áit amháin "
"sin."

msgid ""
"The string you return from ``get_absolute_url()`` **must** contain only "
"ASCII characters (required by the URI specification, :rfc:`3986#section-2`) "
"and be URL-encoded, if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór ach carachtair ASCII a bheith san teaghrán a fhilleann tú ó "
"`get_absolute_url () ``**** (a theastaíonn ag an sonraíocht URI, :rfc: `3986 "
"#section -2`) agus ionchódaithe URL, más gá."

msgid ""
"Code and templates calling ``get_absolute_url()`` should be able to use the "
"result directly without any further processing. You may wish to use the "
"``django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri()`` function to help with this if you are "
"using strings containing characters outside the ASCII range."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh cód agus teimpléid ag glaoch ar ``get_absolute_url () "
"``in ann an toradh a úsáid go díreach gan aon phróiseáil bhreise. B'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat an fheidhm ``django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri () `a úsáid "
"chun cabhrú leis seo má tá teaghráin á úsáid agat ina bhfuil carachtair "
"lasmuigh den raon ASCII."

msgid "Extra instance methods"
msgstr "Modhanna sampla breise"

msgid ""
"In addition to :meth:`~Model.save()`, :meth:`~Model.delete()`, a model "
"object might have some of the following methods:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le:meth: `~Model.save () `, :meth: `~Model.delete ()`, "
"d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cuid de na modhanna seo a leanas ag réad samhail:"

msgid ""
"For every field that has :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.choices` set, the "
"object will have a ``get_FOO_display()`` method, where ``FOO`` is the name "
"of the field. This method returns the \"human-readable\" value of the field."
msgstr ""
"I gcás gach réimse a bhfuil: attr: `~django.db.models.field.choices` tacar "
"aige, beidh modh ``get_foo_display () ``ag an réad, áit a bhfuil `FOO`` ainm "
"an réimse. Tugann an modh seo luach “inléite don duine” an réimse ar ais."

msgid ""
"For every :class:`~django.db.models.DateField` "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` that does not "
"have :attr:`null=True <django.db.models.Field.null>`, the object will have "
"``get_next_by_FOO()`` and ``get_previous_by_FOO()`` methods, where ``FOO`` "
"is the name of the field. This returns the next and previous object with "
"respect to the date field, raising "
"a :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist` exception when appropriate."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Field.null>I gcás gach duine: "
"`~Django.db.Models.DateField` agus:class: `~Django.db.Models.DateTimeField` "
"nach bhfuil aith:attr: `Null=True `, beidh modhanna ``Get_NEXT_BY_FOO () "
"``agus ``GET_PREVIOUS_BY_FOO ()`` Is é ``ainm an réimse. Tugann sé seo an "
"chéad rud eile agus roimhe seo ar ais maidir leis an réimse dáta, ag ardú:: "
"exc: `~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` eisceacht nuair is cuí."

msgid ""
"Both of these methods will perform their queries using the default manager "
"for the model. If you need to emulate filtering used by a custom manager, or "
"want to perform one-off custom filtering, both methods also accept optional "
"keyword arguments, which should be in the format described in :ref:`Field "
"lookups <field-lookups>`."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh an dá mhodh seo a gceisteanna ag baint úsáide as an mbainisteoir "
"réamhshocraithe don tsamhail. <field-lookups>Más gá duit aithris a dhéanamh "
"ar scagadh a úsáideann bainisteoir saincheaptha, nó más mian leat scagadh "
"saincheaptha aonuaire a dhéanamh, glacann an dá mhodh le hargóintí "
"eochairfhocal roghnacha freisin, ar chóir go mbeadh san fhormáid a "
"thuairiscítear in:ref: `Lookups allamui`."

msgid ""
"Note that in the case of identical date values, these methods will use the "
"primary key as a tie-breaker. This guarantees that no records are skipped or "
"duplicated. That also means you cannot use those methods on unsaved objects."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, i gcás luachanna dáta comhionanna, úsáidfidh na modhanna "
"seo an príomh-eochair mar bhriseadh ceangail. Ráthaíonn sé seo nach ndéantar "
"aon taifid a scipeáil nó a dhúbailt. Ciallaíonn sé sin freisin nach féidir "
"leat na modhanna sin a úsáid ar rudaí neamhshábháilte."

msgid "Overriding extra instance methods"
msgstr "Modhanna sampla breise a shárú"

msgid ""
"In most cases overriding or inheriting ``get_FOO_display()``, "
"``get_next_by_FOO()``, and ``get_previous_by_FOO()`` should work as "
"expected. Since they are added by the metaclass however, it is not practical "
"to account for all possible inheritance structures. In more complex cases "
"you should override ``Field.contribute_to_class()`` to set the methods you "
"need."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna ba chóir go n-oibreodh ``get_foo_display () ``, "
"`get_next_by_foo ()``, agus ``get_previous_by_foo () ``, agus "
"``get_previous_by_foo () `` `` `` Get_Previous_by_foo ()``. Ós rud é go "
"gcuireann an metaclass iad leis, áfach, níl sé praiticiúil cuntas a "
"thabhairt ar gach struchtúr oidhreachta féideartha. I gcásanna níos casta ba "
"chóir duit ``Field.contribute_to_class () ``a shárú chun na modhanna a "
"theastaíonn uait a shocrú."

msgid "Other attributes"
msgstr "Tréithe eile"

msgid "``_state``"
msgstr "``_stáit``"

msgid ""
"The ``_state`` attribute refers to a ``ModelState`` object that tracks the "
"lifecycle of the model instance."
msgstr ""
"Tagraíonn an tréith ``_state ``do réad ``ModelState`` a rianaíonn saolré an "
"tsamhail shampla."

msgid ""
"The ``ModelState`` object has two attributes: ``adding``, a flag which is "
"``True`` if the model has not been saved to the database yet, and ``db``, a "
"string referring to the database alias the instance was loaded from or saved "
"to."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá thréith ag an réad ``ModelState``: ``Adding``, bratach atá ``True`` "
"mura sábháladh an tsamhail chuig an mbunachar sonraí go fóill, agus `db``, "
"teaghrán a thagraíonn don ainm bunachar sonraí a luchtadh uaidh nó a "
"shábháiltear leis."

msgid ""
"Newly instantiated instances have ``adding=True`` and ``db=None``, since "
"they are yet to be saved. Instances fetched from a ``QuerySet`` will have "
"``adding=False`` and ``db`` set to the alias of the associated database."
msgstr ""
"Tá `Adding=true`` agus ``db=none`` ag cásanna nua-ionchasacha, ós rud é nach "
"bhfuil siad fós le sábháil. Beidh `Adding=False`` agus ``db`` socraithe ar "
"ainm an bhunachar sonraí gaolmhar ar chásanna a gheobhaidh ó ``QuerySet``."

msgid "``_is_pk_set()``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ``_is_pk_set()`` method returns whether the model instance's ``pk`` is "
"set. It abstracts the model's primary key definition, ensuring consistent "
"behavior regardless of the specific ``pk`` configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lookup API reference"
msgstr "Tagairt API cuardaigh"

msgid ""
"This document has the API references of lookups, the Django API for building "
"the ``WHERE`` clause of a database query. To learn how to *use* lookups, "
"see :doc:`/topics/db/queries`; to learn how to *create* new lookups, "
"see :doc:`/howto/custom-lookups`."
msgstr ""
"Tá tagairtí API na cuardaigh sa doiciméad seo, an API Django chun clásal "
"``WHERE`` d'fhiosrúchán bunachar sonraí a thógáil. Chun foghlaim conas* "
"cuardaithe* a úsáid, féach: doc: `/topics/db/queries`; chun foghlaim "
"conas*cuardaigh nua* a chruthú, féach: doc: `/howto/custom-lookups`."

msgid ""
"The lookup API has two components: a :class:`~lookups.RegisterLookupMixin` "
"class that registers lookups, and the :ref:`Query Expression API <query-"
"expression>`, a set of methods that a class has to implement to be "
"registrable as a lookup."
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá chomhpháirt ag an API cuardaigh: a:class: "
"`~Lookups.RegisterLookUpMixin` aicme a chláraíonn cuardaigh, agus an:ref: "
"`Query Expression API <query-expression>`, sraith modhanna a chaithfidh rang "
"a chur i bhfeidhm chun a bheith inchláraithe mar chuardach."

msgid ""
"Django has two base classes that follow the query expression API and from "
"where all Django builtin lookups are derived:"
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá rang bonn ag Django a leanann an API abairt fiosrúcháin agus ón áit a "
"ndíorthaítear gach cuardach tógtha Django:"

msgid ""
":class:`Lookup`: to lookup a field (e.g. the ``exact`` of "
"``field_name__exact``)"
msgstr ""
":class: `Lookup`: chun réimse a chuardach (m.sh. an ``cruth`` de "
"`field_name__exact``)"

msgid ":class:`Transform`: to transform a field"
msgstr ":class: `Transform`: chun réimse a athrú"

msgid "A lookup expression consists of three parts:"
msgstr "Is éard atá i léiriú cuardaigh trí chuid:"

msgid ""
"Fields part (e.g. "
"``Book.objects.filter(author__best_friends__first_name...``);"
msgstr ""
"Cuid réimsí (m.sh. `Book.Objects.Filter (author__best_friends__first_name... "
"``);"

msgid ""
"Transforms part (may be omitted) (e.g. ``__lower__first3chars__reversed``);"
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn sé cuid (féadfar é a fhágáil) (m.sh. "
"``__lower__first3chars__reversed``);"

msgid ""
"A lookup (e.g. ``__icontains``) that, if omitted, defaults to ``__exact``."
msgstr ""
"Cuardach (m.sh. ``__icontains``) a thagann réamhshocraithe go ``__exact`` má "
"fhágtar amach."

msgid "Registration API"
msgstr "API Clárúcháin"

msgid ""
"Django uses :class:`~lookups.RegisterLookupMixin` to give a class the "
"interface to register lookups on itself or its instances. The two prominent "
"examples are :class:`~django.db.models.Field`, the base class of all model "
"fields, and :class:`Transform`, the base class of all Django transforms."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django: class: `~Lookups.RegisterLookUpMixin` chun an comhéadan a "
"thabhairt do rang chun cuardaigh a chlárú air féin nó ar a chásanna. Is iad "
"an dá shampla suntasach ná: aicme: `~django.db.models.field`, bunaicme gach "
"réimse samhail, agus:class: `Transform`, bunaicme gach Django a athraíonn."

msgid "A mixin that implements the lookup API on a class."
msgstr "Mixin a chuireann an API cuardaigh i bhfeidhm ar rang."

msgid "Registers a new lookup in the class or class instance. For example::"
msgstr "Cláraíonn sé cuardach nua sa rang nó sa rang. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"will register ``YearExact`` lookup on ``DateField`` and ``MonthExact`` "
"lookup on the ``User.date_joined`` (you can use :ref:`Field Access API "
"<model-meta-field-api>` to retrieve a single field instance). It overrides a "
"lookup that already exists with the same name. Lookups registered on field "
"instances take precedence over the lookups registered on classes. "
"``lookup_name`` will be used for this lookup if provided, otherwise "
"``lookup.lookup_name`` will be used."
msgstr ""
"<model-meta-field-api>cláróidh sé cuardach ``YearExact ``ar `DateField`` "
"agus ``MonthExact`` cuardach ar ``User.Date_Joined`` (is féidir leat:ref: "
"`Field Access API `a úsáid chun sampla réimse amháin a aisghabháil). "
"Sáraíonn sé cuardach atá ann cheana leis an ainm céanna. Tá tosaíocht ag "
"cuardaigh atá cláraithe ar chásanna allamuigh seachas na cuardaigh atá "
"cláraithe ar ranganna. Úsáidfear ``lookup_name`` don chuardach seo má "
"chuirtear ar fáil, ar shlí eile úsáidfear ``lookup.lookup_name``."

msgid ""
"Returns the :class:`Lookup` named ``lookup_name`` registered in the class or "
"class instance depending on what calls it. The default implementation looks "
"recursively on all parent classes and checks if any has a registered lookup "
"named ``lookup_name``, returning the first match. Instance lookups would "
"override any class lookups with the same ``lookup_name``."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an:class: `Lookup` darb ainm ``lookup_name`` atá cláraithe sa "
"rang nó sa rang ag brath ar an méid a ghlaonn air. Breathnaíonn an cur i "
"bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe go athshlánach ar gach rang tuismitheora agus "
"seiceálann sé an bhfuil cuardach cláraithe ag duine ar bith darb ainm "
"`lookup_name``, agus an chéad chluiche ar ais. Déanfadh cuardach samplaí a "
"shárú ar aon chuardach ranga leis an ``lookup_name`` céanna."

msgid ""
"Returns a dictionary of each lookup name registered in the class or class "
"instance mapped to the :class:`Lookup` class."
msgstr ""
"Tugann foclóir ar ais de gach ainm cuardaigh atá cláraithe sa rang nó sa "
"rang atá mapáilte chuig rang:class: `Lookup`."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`Transform` named ``transform_name`` registered in the "
"class or class instance. The default implementation looks recursively on all "
"parent classes to check if any has the registered transform named "
"``transform_name``, returning the first match."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceáin a:class: `Transform` darb ainm ``transform_name`` cláraithe sa "
"rang nó i gcás ranga. Breathnaíonn an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe go "
"athshlánach ar gach rang tuismitheora chun a sheiceáil an bhfuil an claochlú "
"cláraithe darb ainm `transform_name`` ag aon duine, ag tabhairt ar ais an "
"gcéad"

msgid ""
"For a class to be a lookup, it must follow the :ref:`Query Expression API "
"<query-expression>`. :class:`~Lookup` and :class:`~Transform` naturally "
"follow this API."
msgstr ""
"<query-expression>Chun rang a bheith ina chuardach, caithfidh sé an: ref: "
"`Query Expression API `a leanúint. Leanann: class: `~Lookup` agus:class: "
"`~Transform` an API seo go nádúrtha."

msgid "The Query Expression API"
msgstr "An API Léiriú Fiosrúcháin"

msgid ""
"The query expression API is a common set of methods that classes define to "
"be usable in query expressions to translate themselves into SQL expressions. "
"Direct field references, aggregates, and ``Transform`` are examples that "
"follow this API. A class is said to follow the query expression API when it "
"implements the following methods:"
msgstr ""
"Is sraith coitianta modhanna é an API abairt fiosrúcháin a shainmhíníonn "
"ranganna le bheith inúsáidte in abairtí fiosrúcháin chun iad féin a aistriú "
"go nathanna SQL. Is samplaí iad tagairtí díreacha réimse, comhiomláin, agus "
"`Transform` `` `` `` `` `` ```` ``` Deirtear go leanann rang an API abairt "
"fiosrúcháin nuair a chuireann sé na modhanna seo a leanas i bhfeidhm:"

msgid ""
"Generates the SQL fragment for the expression. Returns a tuple ``(sql, "
"params)``, where ``sql`` is the SQL string, and ``params`` is the list or "
"tuple of query parameters. The ``compiler`` is an ``SQLCompiler`` object, "
"which has a ``compile()`` method that can be used to compile other "
"expressions. The ``connection`` is the connection used to execute the query."
msgstr ""
"Gineann sé an blúire SQL don abairt. Filleann sé tuple ``(sql, params)``, "
"áit gurb é `sql`` an teaghrán SQL, agus `params`` an liosta nó an tiúpla de "
"pharaiméadair fiosrúcháin. Is réad ``SQLcompiler`` é an `compiler``, a "
"bhfuil modh ``compileáil () ``aige is féidir a úsáid chun nathanna eile a "
"thiomsú. Is é an `nasc`` an nasc a úsáidtear chun an ceist a fhorghníomhú."

msgid ""
"Calling ``expression.as_sql()`` is usually incorrect - instead "
"``compiler.compile(expression)`` should be used. The ``compiler.compile()`` "
"method will take care of calling vendor-specific methods of the expression."
msgstr ""
"Is gnách go mbíonn glaoch ar ``expression.as_sql () ``mícheart - ina ionad "
"sin ba chóir ``compiler.compiler.compilation (focal)`` a úsáid. Tabharfaidh "
"an modh `compiler.compiler.compilation () ``aire do mhodhanna an abairt a "
"ghlaoch ar mhodhanna sonracha don dhíoltóir."

msgid ""
"Custom keyword arguments may be defined on this method if it's likely that "
"``as_vendorname()`` methods or subclasses will need to supply data to "
"override the generation of the SQL string. See :meth:`Func.as_sql` for "
"example usage."
msgstr ""
"Féadfar argóintí eochairfhocal saincheaptha a shainiú ar an modh seo más "
"dóichí go mbeidh ar mhodhanna nó fo-aicmí `as_vendorname () `sonraí a "
"sholáthar chun giniúint an teaghrán SQL a shárú. Féach: Meth: `Func.as_sql` "
"mar shampla úsáid."

msgid ""
"Works like ``as_sql()`` method. When an expression is compiled by "
"``compiler.compile()``, Django will first try to call ``as_vendorname()``, "
"where ``vendorname`` is the vendor name of the backend used for executing "
"the query. The ``vendorname`` is one of ``postgresql``, ``oracle``, "
"``sqlite``, or ``mysql`` for Django's built-in backends."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sé cosúil le modh `as_sql () ``. Nuair a thiomsaíonn abairt ag "
"``compiler.compiler () ``, déanfaidh Django iarracht glaoch ar "
"``as_vendorname ()`` ar dtús, áit a bhfuil `vendorname`` ainm díoltóra an "
"chúltaca a úsáidtear chun an cheist a fhorghníomhú. Tá an ``vendorname`` ar "
"cheann de ``postgresql``, ``oracle``, `sqlite``, nó ``mysql`` le haghaidh "
"cúltaca ionsuite Django."

msgid ""
"Must return the lookup named ``lookup_name``. For instance, by returning "
"``self.output_field.get_lookup(lookup_name)``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór an cuardach darb ainm ``lookup_name`` a thabhairt ar ais. Mar "
"shampla, trí ``self.output_field.get_lookup (lookup_name) ``a thabhairt ar "
"ais."

msgid ""
"Must return the lookup named ``transform_name``. For instance, by returning "
"``self.output_field.get_transform(transform_name)``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór an cuardach darb ainm ``transform_name`` a thabhairt ar ais. Mar "
"shampla, trí ``self.output_field.get_transformer (transform_name) ``a "
"thabhairt ar ais."

msgid ""
"Defines the type of class returned by the ``get_lookup()`` method. It must "
"be a :class:`~django.db.models.Field` instance."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an cineál ranga a chuirtear ar ais leis an modh ``get_lookup () "
"``. Caithfidh sé a: class: `~django.db.models.field` sampla."

msgid "``Transform`` reference"
msgstr "Tagairt ``Transform``"

msgid ""
"A ``Transform`` is a generic class to implement field transformations. A "
"prominent example is ``__year`` that transforms a ``DateField`` into a "
"``IntegerField``."
msgstr ""
"Is aicme cineálach é ``Transform`` chun claochlú allamuigh a chur i "
"bhfeidhm. Sampla suntasach is ea ``__year`` a athraíonn ``DataField`` go "
"``ComhlánField``."

msgid ""
"The notation to use a ``Transform`` in a lookup expression is "
"``<expression>__<transformation>`` (e.g. ``date__year``)."
msgstr ""
"<expression><transformation>Is é ``__`` `` Transform ``a úsáid i léiriú "
"cuardaigh (m.sh. `dáta__bliain``)."

msgid ""
"This class follows the :ref:`Query Expression API <query-expression>`, which "
"implies that you can use ``<expression>__<transform1>__<transform2>``. It's "
"a specialized :ref:`Func() expression <func-expressions>` that only accepts "
"one argument.  It can also be used on the right hand side of a filter or "
"directly as an annotation."
msgstr ""
"<expression><transform1><transform2>Leanann an rang seo an:ref: `Query "
"Expression API <query-expression>`, rud a thugann le tuiscint gur féidir "
"leat ``__ __`` a úsáid. Is léiriú speisialaithe é: ref: `Func () <func-"
"expressions>`nach nglacann ach argóint amháin. Is féidir é a úsáid freisin "
"ar thaobh na láimhe deise de scagaire nó go díreach mar anótáil."

msgid ""
"A boolean indicating whether this transformation should apply to both "
"``lhs`` and ``rhs``. Bilateral transformations will be applied to ``rhs`` in "
"the same order as they appear in the lookup expression. By default it is set "
"to ``False``. For example usage, see :doc:`/howto/custom-lookups`."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a léiríonn an chóir go mbeadh feidhm ag an gclaochlú seo maidir le "
"`lhs`` agus `rhs`` araon. Cuirfear claochlú déthaobhacha i bhfeidhm ar "
"``rhs`` san ord céanna agus atá le feiceáil sa léiriú cuardaigh. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe tá sé socraithe go ``False``. Mar shampla úsáid, féach: doc: "
"`/howto/custom-lookups`."

msgid ""
"The left-hand side - what is being transformed. It must follow "
"the :ref:`Query Expression API <query-expression>`."
msgstr ""
"An taobh clé - cad atá á athrú. <query-expression>Caithfidh sé an: ref: "
"`Fiosraithe Expression API `a leanúint."

msgid ""
"The name of the lookup, used for identifying it on parsing query "
"expressions. It cannot contain the string ``\"__\"``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an chuardaigh, a úsáidtear chun é a aithint ar nathanna fiosrúcháin a "
"pháirseáil. Ní féidir leis an sreang ``\"__\"`` a bheith ann."

msgid ""
"Defines the class this transformation outputs. It must be "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.Field` instance. By default is the same as its "
"``lhs.output_field``."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an rang a aschuireann an claochlú seo Caithfidh sé a: class: "
"`~django.db.models.field` sampla. De réir réamhshocraithe tá sé mar an "
"gcéanna lena `lhs.output_field``."

msgid "``Lookup`` reference"
msgstr "Tagairt ```Lookup``"

msgid ""
"A ``Lookup`` is a generic class to implement lookups. A lookup is a query "
"expression with a left-hand side, :attr:`lhs`; a right-hand "
"side, :attr:`rhs`; and a ``lookup_name`` that is used to produce a boolean "
"comparison between ``lhs`` and ``rhs`` such as ``lhs in rhs`` or ``lhs > "
"rhs``."
msgstr ""
"Is aicme cineálach é ``Lookup`` chun cuardaigh a chur i bhfeidhm. Is léiriú "
"fiosrúcháin é cuardach le taobh clé, :attr: `lhs`; taobh ar dheis, :attr: "
"`rhs`; agus ``lookup_name`` a úsáidtear chun comparáid boolean a tháirgeadh "
"idir `lhs`` agus `rhs`` mar ``lhs i rhs`` nó ``lhs > rhs``."

msgid ""
"The primary notation to use a lookup in an expression is "
"``<lhs>__<lookup_name>=<rhs>``. Lookups can also be used directly in "
"``QuerySet`` filters::"
msgstr ""
"<lookup_name><rhs>Is é ``<lhs>__ =`` an príomh-nótaí chun cuardach a úsáid i "
"abairt. Is féidir cuardaigh a úsáid go díreach i scagairí ``QuerySet`:"

msgid "…or annotations::"
msgstr "... nó anótaí::"

msgid ""
"The left-hand side - what is being looked up. The object typically follows "
"the :ref:`Query Expression API <query-expression>`. It may also be a plain "
"value."
msgstr ""
"An taobh clé - cad atá á breathnú suas. <query-expression>De ghnáth leanann "
"an réad an:ref: `Fiosraithe Expression API `. D'fhéadfadh sé a bheith ina "
"luach simplí freisin."

msgid ""
"The right-hand side - what ``lhs`` is being compared against. It can be a "
"plain value, or something that compiles into SQL, typically an ``F()`` "
"object or a ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"An taobh na láimhe deise - cad atá `lhs`` á chur i gcomparáid ina choinne. "
"Is féidir é a bheith ina luach simplí, nó rud éigin a thiomsaíonn isteach i "
"SQL, de ghnáth rud ``F () ``nó ``QuerySet``."

msgid ""
"The name of this lookup, used to identify it on parsing query expressions. "
"It cannot contain the string ``\"__\"``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an chuardaigh seo, a úsáidtear chun é a aithint ar nathanna fiosrúcháin "
"a pháirseáil. Ní féidir leis an sreang ``\"__\"`` a bheith ann."

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``True``. When :attr:`rhs` is a plain value, :attr:`prepare_rhs` "
"determines whether it should be prepared for use as a parameter in a query. "
"In order to do so, ``lhs.output_field.get_prep_value()`` is called if "
"defined, or ``rhs`` is wrapped in :class:`Value() <django.db.models.Value>` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True``. Nuair: attr: Is luach simplí é `rhs`, :attr: "
"`prepare_rhs` cinneann an chóir é a ullmhú le húsáid mar pharaiméadar i "
"bhfiosrúchán. <django.db.models.Value>D'fhonn é sin a dhéanamh, tugtar "
"``lhs.output_field.get_prep_value () ``má shainmhínítear, nó tá `rhs`` "
"fillte in:class: `Value () `ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"Returns a tuple ``(lhs_string, lhs_params)``, as returned by "
"``compiler.compile(lhs)``. This method can be overridden to tune how the "
"``lhs`` is processed."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé tuple ``(lhs_string, lhs_params)`` ar ais ag "
"``compiler.compiler.compiler (lhs) ``. Is féidir an modh seo a shárú chun an "
"chaoi a ndéantar an `lhs`` a phróiseáil a thiúnadh."

msgid ""
"``compiler`` is an ``SQLCompiler`` object, to be used like "
"``compiler.compile(lhs)`` for compiling ``lhs``. The ``connection`` can be "
"used for compiling vendor specific SQL. If ``lhs`` is not ``None``, use it "
"as the processed ``lhs`` instead of ``self.lhs``."
msgstr ""
"Is réad ``sqlcompiler`` é `compiler``, le húsáid cosúil le "
"``compiler.compiler.compiler (lhs) ``chun `lhs`` a thiomsú. Is féidir an "
"``nasc`` a úsáid chun SQL sonrach don díoltóir a thiomsú. Mura bhfuil "
"``lhs`` ``None``, bain úsáid as mar an `lhs`` próiseáilte in ionad "
"``self.lhs``."

msgid "Behaves the same way as :meth:`process_lhs`, for the right-hand side."
msgstr ""
"Iompraíonn sé ar an mbealach céanna le: meth: `process_lhs`, don taobh na "
"láimhe deise."

msgid "Model ``_meta`` API"
msgstr "Mionsamhail ``_meta`` API"

msgid ""
"The model ``_meta`` API is at the core of the Django ORM. It enables other "
"parts of the system such as lookups, queries, forms, and the admin to "
"understand the capabilities of each model. The API is accessible through the "
"``_meta`` attribute of each model class, which is an instance of an "
"``django.db.models.options.Options`` object."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tsamhail ``_meta`` API ag croílár an ORM Django. Cuireann sé ar chumas "
"codanna eile den chóras mar chuardaigh, ceisteanna, foirmeacha agus an "
"riarachán cumais gach samhail a thuiscint. Tá an API inrochtana trí thréith "
"``_meta`` gach aicme samhail, ar shampla é de réad "
"``Django.db.Models.Options.Options``."

msgid "Methods and attributes that it provides can be used to:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Retrieve all field instances of a model"
msgstr "Aisghabháil gach cás réimse de mhúnla"

msgid "Retrieve a single field instance of a model by name"
msgstr "Aisghabháil sampla réimse amháin de mhúnla de réir ainm"

msgid "Retrieve all fields that compose the primary key of a model"
msgstr ""

msgid "Field access API"
msgstr "API rochtana allamuigh"

msgid "Retrieving a single field instance of a model by name"
msgstr "Sampla réimse amháin de mhúnla a aisghabháil de réir ainm"

msgid "Returns the field instance given a name of a field."
msgstr "Tugann ainm réimse ar ais."

msgid ""
"``field_name`` can be the name of a field on the model, a field on an "
"abstract or inherited model, or a field defined on another model that points "
"to the model. In the latter case, the ``field_name`` will be (in order of "
"preference) the :attr:`~.ForeignKey.related_query_name` set by the user, "
"the :attr:`~.ForeignKey.related_name` set by the user, or the name "
"automatically generated by Django."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le `field_name`` a bheith ina ainm réimse ar an tsamhail, réimse "
"ar mhúnla teibí nó oidhreachta, nó réimse atá sainmhínithe ar mhúnla eile a "
"thugann in iúl don tsamhail. Sa chás deireanach sin, is é an `field_name`` "
"(in ord rogha) an:attr: `~.foreignkey.related_query_name` a shocraíonn an t-"
"úsáideoir, an:attr: `~.foreignKey.related_name` atá leagtha amach ag an "
"úsáideoir, nó an t-ainm a ghineann Django go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
":attr:`Hidden fields <django.db.models.Field.hidden>` cannot be retrieved by "
"name."
msgstr ""
":attr: Ní féidir `réimsí i bhfolach <django.db.models.Field.hidden>`a "
"aisghabháil de réir ainm."

msgid ""
"If a field with the given name is not found "
"a :class:`~django.core.exceptions.FieldDoesNotExist` exception will be "
"raised."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfaightear réimse leis an ainm a thugtar a:class: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.fieldDoesNotExist` ardófar eisceacht."

msgid "Retrieving all field instances of a model"
msgstr "Aisghabháil gach cás allamuigh de mhúnla"

msgid ""
"Returns a tuple of fields associated with a model. ``get_fields()`` accepts "
"two parameters that can be used to control which fields are returned:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé cúpla réimsí a bhaineann le samhail ar ais. Glacann ``get_fields "
"() ``le dhá pharaiméadar is féidir a úsáid chun na réimsí a chuirtear ar ais "
"a rialú:"

msgid "``include_parents``"
msgstr "``include_tuismitheoirí ``"

msgid ""
"``True`` by default. Recursively includes fields defined on parent classes. "
"If set to ``False``, ``get_fields()`` will only search for fields declared "
"directly on the current model. Fields from models that directly inherit from "
"abstract models or proxy classes are considered to be local, not on the "
"parent."
msgstr ""
"``True`` de réir réamhshocraithe. Cuimsíonn sé go réimsí atá sainithe ar "
"ranganna tuismitheoirí Má tá sé socraithe ar ``False``, ní chuardóidh "
"``get_fields () ``ach réimsí a dearbhaíodh go díreach ar an tsamhail reatha. "
"Meastar go bhfuil réimsí ó mhúnlaí a dhéanann oidhreacht go díreach ó "
"mhúnlaí teibí nó ó ranganna seachfhreastalaí áitiúla, ní ar an"

msgid "``include_hidden``"
msgstr "``include_hidden``"

msgid ""
"``False`` by default. If set to ``True``, ``get_fields()`` will "
"include :attr:`hidden fields <django.db.models.Field.hidden>`."
msgstr ""
"``False`` de réir réamhshocraithe. <django.db.models.Field.hidden>Má tá sé "
"socraithe go ``True``, beidh `get_fields () ``san áireamh: attr: `réimsí i "
"bhfolach `."

msgid "Retrieving fields composing the primary key of a model"
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns a list of the fields composing the primary key of a model."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a :class:`composite primary key <django.db.models.CompositePrimaryKey>` "
"is defined on a model it will contain all the :class:`fields "
"<django.db.models.Field>` referenced by it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Otherwise it will contain the single field declared as the :attr:`primary "
"key <django.db.models.Field.primary_key>` of the model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model ``Meta`` options"
msgstr "Roghanna múnla ``Meta``"

msgid ""
"This document explains all the possible :ref:`metadata options <meta-"
"options>` that you can give your model in its internal ``class Meta``."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo na roghanna meiteashonraí go léir:ref: féadfaidh "
"<meta-options>tú do mhúnla a thabhairt ina ``aicme Meta`` inmheánach."

msgid "Available ``Meta`` options"
msgstr "Roghanna ``Meta`` ar fáil"

msgid "``abstract``"
msgstr "``teochair``"

msgid ""
"If ``abstract = True``, this model will be an :ref:`abstract base class "
"<abstract-base-classes>`."
msgstr ""
"<abstract-base-classes>Má tá ``abstract = True``, beidh an tsamhail seo "
"an:ref: `aicme bonn teibí `."

msgid ""
"If a model is defined outside of an application "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, it must declare which app it belongs to::"
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhínítear samhail lasmuigh d'iarratas in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, "
"ní mór dó a dhearbhú cén aip leis a bhaineann sé:"

msgid ""
"If you want to represent a model with the format ``app_label.object_name`` "
"or ``app_label.model_name`` you can use ``model._meta.label`` or "
"``model._meta.label_lower`` respectively."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat samhail a léiriú leis an bhformáid ``app_label.object_name`` "
"nó ``app_label.model_name`` is féidir leat ``model a úsáid. _meta.label`` nó "
"``samhail. _meta.label_lower`` faoi seach."

msgid "``base_manager_name``"
msgstr "```ainm_bainisteoir base``"

msgid ""
"The attribute name of the manager, for example, ``'objects'``, to use for "
"the model's :attr:`~django.db.models.Model._base_manager`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm tréithe an bhainisteora, mar shampla, ``'objects``, le húsáid do na "
"samhlach's:attr: `~Django.db.Models.Model. _bainisteoir bunaisteoir'."

msgid "``db_table``"
msgstr "``db_table``"

msgid "The name of the database table to use for the model::"
msgstr "Ainm an tábla bunachar sonraí le húsáid don tsamhail::"

msgid ""
"To save you time, Django automatically derives the name of the database "
"table from the name of your model class and the app that contains it. A "
"model's database table name is constructed by joining the model's \"app "
"label\" -- the name you used in :djadmin:`manage.py startapp <startapp>` -- "
"to the model's class name, with an underscore between them."
msgstr ""
"Chun am a shábháil duit, faigheann Django ainm an tábla bunachar sonraí go "
"huathoibríoch ó ainm d'aicme samhail agus ón aip ina bhfuil sé. Tógtar ainm "
"tábla bunachar sonraí samhail trí “lipéad aip” an tsamhail - an t-ainm a "
"d'úsáid tú in:djadmin: `manage.py startapp <startapp>`- a cheangal le hainm "
"ranga an tsamhail, le béim eatarthu."

msgid ""
"For example, if you have an app ``bookstore`` (as created by ``manage.py "
"startapp bookstore``), a model defined as ``class Book`` will have a "
"database table named ``bookstore_book``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá aip agat `bookstore`` (mar a chruthaigh ``manage.py "
"startapp bookstore``), beidh tábla bunachar sonraí darb ainm "
"``bookstore_book`` ag samhail a shainmhínítear mar ``class Book``."

msgid ""
"To override the database table name, use the ``db_table`` parameter in "
"``class Meta``."
msgstr ""
"Chun ainm an tábla bunachar sonraí a shárú, bain úsáid as an paraiméadar "
"``db_table`` i `aicme Meta``."

msgid ""
"If your database table name is an SQL reserved word, or contains characters "
"that aren't allowed in Python variable names -- notably, the hyphen -- "
"that's OK. Django quotes column and table names behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Más focal fhorchoimeádaithe SQL é d'ainm tábla bunachar sonraí, nó má tá "
"carachtair nach gceadaítear in ainmneacha athróg Python - go háirithe, an "
"giphen - tá sin ceart go leor. Luann Django ainmneacha colún agus tábla "
"taobh thiar de na radhairc."

msgid "Use lowercase table names for MariaDB and MySQL"
msgstr "Úsáid ainmneacha tábla beaga do MariaDB agus MySQL"

msgid ""
"It is strongly advised that you use lowercase table names when you override "
"the table name via ``db_table``, particularly if you are using the MySQL "
"backend. See the :ref:`MySQL notes <mysql-notes>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Moltar go láidir duit ainmneacha tábla beaga a úsáid nuair a dhéanann tú "
"ainm an tábla a shárú trí `db_table``, go háirithe má tá cúltaca MySQL á "
"úsáid agat. Féach na:ref: `Nótaí MySQL <mysql-notes>`le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "Table name quoting for Oracle"
msgstr "Luachan ainm tábla do Oracle"

msgid ""
"In order to meet the 30-char limitation Oracle has on table names, and match "
"the usual conventions for Oracle databases, Django may shorten table names "
"and turn them all-uppercase. To prevent such transformations, use a quoted "
"name as the value for ``db_table``::"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn an teorannú 30-char atá ag Oracle ar ainmneacha tábla a "
"chomhlíonadh, agus na gnáthchoinbhinsiúin do bhunachair sonraí Oracle a "
"mheaitseáil, féadfaidh Django ainmneacha táblaí a ghiorrú agus iad Chun "
"claochlú den sórt sin a chosc, bain úsáid as ainm luaite mar an luach do "
"`db_table``:"

msgid ""
"Such quoted names can also be used with Django's other supported database "
"backends; except for Oracle, however, the quotes have no effect. See "
"the :ref:`Oracle notes <oracle-notes>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ainmneacha luaite den sórt sin a úsáid freisin le cúltaca bunachar "
"sonraí tacaithe eile Django; seachas Oracle, áfach, níl aon éifeacht ag na "
"luachana. Féach in:ref: `Nótaí Oracle <oracle-notes>`le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "``db_table_comment``"
msgstr "``db_table_comment ``"

msgid ""
"The comment on the database table to use for this model. It is useful for "
"documenting database tables for individuals with direct database access who "
"may not be looking at your Django code. For example::"
msgstr ""
"An trácht ar an tábla bunachar sonraí le húsáid don tsamhail seo. Tá sé "
"úsáideach chun táblaí bunachar sonraí a dhoiciméadú do dhaoine aonair a "
"bhfuil rochtain dhíreach acu ar bhunachar sonraí nach bhfuil ag féachaint ar "
"do chód Django. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The name of the :doc:`database tablespace </topics/db/tablespaces>` to use "
"for this model. The default is the project's :setting:`DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` "
"setting, if set. If the backend doesn't support tablespaces, this option is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an:doc: `spás tábla bunachar sonraí` le húsáid don tsamhail seo. </"
"topics/db/tablespaces> Is é an réamhshocrú an tionscadal: setting: "
"`DEFAULT_TABLESPACE` socrú, má tá sé socraithe. Mura dtacaíonn an cúltaca le "
"spásanna tábla, déantar neamhaird ar an rogha seo."

msgid "``default_manager_name``"
msgstr "``ainm_bhainisteoir réamhshocraithe``"

msgid ""
"The name of the manager to use for the "
"model's :attr:`~django.db.models.Model._default_manager`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an bhainisteora le húsáid do na samhail's:attr: "
"`~django.db.Models.Model. _bainisteoir réamhshocraithe'."

msgid "``default_related_name``"
msgstr "``ainm_bhainteach_réamhshocraithe``"

msgid ""
"The name that will be used by default for the relation from a related object "
"back to this one. The default is ``<model_name>_set``."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm a úsáidfear de réir réamhshocraithe don ghaol ó réad gaolmhar ar "
"ais leis an gceann seo. Is é an réamhshocrú ``<model_name>_set``."

msgid "This option also sets :attr:`~ForeignKey.related_query_name`."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an rogha seo freisin: attr: `~ForeignKey.related_query_name`."

msgid ""
"As the reverse name for a field should be unique, be careful if you intend "
"to subclass your model. To work around name collisions, part of the name "
"should contain ``'%(app_label)s'`` and ``'%(model_name)s'``, which are "
"replaced respectively by the name of the application the model is in, and "
"the name of the model, both lowercased. See the paragraph on :ref:`related "
"names for abstract models <abstract-related-name>`."
msgstr ""
"Toisc gur chóir go mbeadh an t-ainm droim ar réimse uathúil, bí cúramach má "
"tá sé ar intinn agat do mhúnla a fho-aicmiú. Chun oibriú timpeall ar "
"imbhuailtí ainmneacha, ba chóir go mbeadh ``'% (app_label) s'`` agus ```% "
"(model_name) s'``, a chuirtear ainm an fheidhmchláir ann an tsamhail in "
"ionad faoi seach, agus ainm an tsamhail, araon níos ísle. <abstract-related-"
"name>Féach an mhír ar:ref: `ainmneacha gaolmhara do mhúnlaí teibí `."

msgid "``get_latest_by``"
msgstr "``faigh_is déanaí_b``"

msgid ""
"The name of a field or a list of field names in the model, "
"typically :class:`DateField`, :class:`DateTimeField`, "
"or :class:`IntegerField`. This specifies the default field(s) to use in your "
"model :class:`Manager`’s :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.latest` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.earliest` methods."
msgstr ""
"Ainm réimse nó liosta d'ainmneacha réimse sa tsamhail, de ghnáthach:class: "
"`DateField`, :class: `DateTimeField`, nó:class: `Integerfield`. Sonraíonn sé "
"seo an réimsí réamhshocraithe atá le húsáid i do mhúnla:class: "
"`Manager`'s:Meth: `~django.db.models.queryset.latest` agus:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.earliest` modhanna."

msgid "See the :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.latest` docs for more."
msgstr ""
"Féach na docs: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.latest` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "``managed``"
msgstr "``bainistithe ``"

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``True``, meaning Django will create the appropriate database "
"tables in :djadmin:`migrate` or as part of migrations and remove them as "
"part of a :djadmin:`flush` management command. That is, Django *manages* the "
"database tables' lifecycles."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``True``, rud a chiallaíonn go gcruthóidh Django na "
"táblaí bunachar sonraí iomchuí in:djadmin: `migrate` nó mar chuid d'imirce "
"agus bainfidh sé iad mar chuid d'ordú bainistíochta a:djadmin: `flush`. Is é "
"sin, bainistíonn Django* saolré na dtáblaí bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"If ``False``, no database table creation, modification, or deletion "
"operations will be performed for this model. This is useful if the model "
"represents an existing table or a database view that has been created by "
"some other means. This is the *only* difference when ``managed=False``. All "
"other aspects of model handling are exactly the same as normal. This includes"
msgstr ""
"Má tá “False”, ní dhéanfar aon oibríochtaí cruthaithe, modhnú nó scriosadh "
"tábla bunachar sonraí don tsamhail seo. Tá sé seo úsáideach má léiríonn an "
"tsamhail tábla atá ann cheana nó dearcadh bunachar sonraí a cruthaíodh ar "
"bhealach éigin eile. Is é seo an difríocht* ionly* nuair a bhíonn "
"`bainistithe = bréag``. Tá gach gné eile de láimhseáil samhail díreach mar "
"an gcéanna leis an ngnách. Áirítear leis seo"

msgid ""
"Adding an automatic primary key field to the model if you don't declare it.  "
"To avoid confusion for later code readers, it's recommended to specify all "
"the columns from the database table you are modeling when using unmanaged "
"models."
msgstr ""
"Réimse eochair phríomhúil uathoibríoch a chur leis an tsamhail mura "
"ndearbhaíonn tú é. Chun mearbhall a sheachaint do léitheoirí cód níos "
"déanaí, moltar na colúin go léir ón tábla bunachar sonraí atá tú ag samhaltú "
"a shonrú agus samhlacha neamhbhainistithe á úsáid agat."

msgid ""
"If a model with ``managed=False`` contains "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` that points to another "
"unmanaged model, then the intermediate table for the many-to-many join will "
"also not be created. However, the intermediary table between one managed and "
"one unmanaged model *will* be created."
msgstr ""
"Má tá a: class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` i samhail le "
"`Managed=False`` a thugann in iúl ar mhúnla neamh-bhainistithe eile, ansin "
"ní chruthófar an tábla idirmheánach don chomhcheangal go leor freisin. Mar "
"sin féin, cruthófar an tábla idirghabhálaí idir samhail amháin bainistithe "
"agus samhail neamh-bhainistithe amháin **."

msgid ""
"If you need to change this default behavior, create the intermediary table "
"as an explicit model (with ``managed`` set as needed) and use "
"the :attr:`ManyToManyField.through` attribute to make the relation use your "
"custom model."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit an t-iompar réamhshocraithe seo a athrú, cruthaigh an tábla "
"idirghabhálaí mar mhúnla follasach (le `bhainistithe ``socraithe de réir mar "
"is gá) agus bain úsáid as an tréith: attr: `ManyTomanyField.through` chun an "
"gaol a úsáid do mhúnla saincheaptha."

msgid ""
"For tests involving models with ``managed=False``, it's up to you to ensure "
"the correct tables are created as part of the test setup."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tástálacha a bhaineann le samhlacha le `Managed = False``, is "
"fútsa atá sé a chinntiú go gcruthaítear na táblaí cearta mar chuid den socrú "
"tástála."

msgid ""
"If you're interested in changing the Python-level behavior of a model class, "
"you *could* use ``managed=False`` and create a copy of an existing model. "
"However, there's a better approach for that situation: :ref:`proxy-models`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá suim agat iompar rang samhail ar leibhéal Python a athrú, d'fhéad* "
"d'fhéad* ``Managed = False`` a úsáid agus cóip de mhúnla atá ann cheana a "
"chruthú. Mar sin féin, tá cur chuige níos fearr ann don chás sin: :ref: "
"`proxy-models`."

msgid "``order_with_respect_to``"
msgstr "```ordó_le_urchúis_to`"

msgid ""
"Makes this object orderable with respect to the given field, usually a "
"``ForeignKey``. This can be used to make related objects orderable with "
"respect to a parent object. For example, if an ``Answer`` relates to a "
"``Question`` object, and a question has more than one answer, and the order "
"of answers matters, you'd do this::"
msgstr ""
"Déanann an réad seo inordaithe maidir leis an réimse ar leith, de ghnáth is "
"“ForeignKey'”. Is féidir é seo a úsáid chun rudaí gaolmhara a dhéanamh "
"inordaithe maidir le réad tuismitheora. Mar shampla, má bhaineann "
"``Freagra`` le réad ``Ceiste``, agus má tá níos mó ná freagra amháin ag "
"ceist, agus má tá ord na bhfreagraí tábhachtach, déanfá seo:"

msgid ""
"When ``order_with_respect_to`` is set, two additional methods are provided "
"to retrieve and to set the order of the related objects: "
"``get_RELATED_order()`` and ``set_RELATED_order()``, where ``RELATED`` is "
"the lowercased model name. For example, assuming that a ``Question`` object "
"has multiple related ``Answer`` objects, the list returned contains the "
"primary keys of the related ``Answer`` objects:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraítear ``order_with_respect_to``, cuirtear dhá mhodh breise ar "
"fáil chun ord na rudaí gaolmhara a aisghabháil agus a shocrú: "
"``get_related_order () ``agus ``set_related_order ()``, áit a bhfuil "
"`RELATED`` ainm an tsamhail ísle. Mar shampla, ag glacadh leis go bhfuil "
"rudaí iolracha ``Freagra`` gaolmhara ag réad ``Ceiste``, tá príomh-eochracha "
"na rudaí ``Freagra`` gaolmhara sa liosta a thugtar ar ais:"

msgid ""
"The order of a ``Question`` object's related ``Answer`` objects can be set "
"by passing in a list of ``Answer`` primary keys:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ord rudaí ``Cheiste`` a bhaineann le ``Freagra`` a shocrú trí "
"liosta de phríomhheochracha ```Freagra`` a chur isteach:"

msgid ""
"The related objects also get two methods, ``get_next_in_order()`` and "
"``get_previous_in_order()``, which can be used to access those objects in "
"their proper order. Assuming the ``Answer`` objects are ordered by ``id``:"
msgstr ""
"Faigheann na rudaí gaolmhara dhá mhodh freisin, ``get_next_in_order () "
"``agus ``get_previous_in_order ()``, ar féidir a úsáid chun rochtain a fháil "
"ar na rudaí sin ina n-ord ceart. Ag glacadh leis go bhfuil na rudaí "
"``Freagra`` ordaithe ag `id``:"

msgid "``order_with_respect_to`` implicitly sets the ``ordering`` option"
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn ``order_with_respect_to`` an rogha ``ordú ```ordúna`` go implíoch"

msgid ""
"Internally, ``order_with_respect_to`` adds an additional field/database "
"column named ``_order`` and sets the model's :attr:`~Options.ordering` "
"option to this field. Consequently, ``order_with_respect_to`` and "
"``ordering`` cannot be used together, and the ordering added by "
"``order_with_respect_to`` will apply whenever you obtain a list of objects "
"of this model."
msgstr ""
"Go hinmheánach, cuireann ``order_with_respect_to`` colún réimse/bunachar "
"sonraí breise darb ainm ``_order`` agus leagann sé an rogha samhail's:attr: "
"`~Options.Ordering` leis an réimse seo. Dá bhrí sin, ní féidir "
"``order_with_respect_to`` agus ``ording`` a úsáid le chéile, agus beidh "
"feidhm ag an ordú a chuirtear leis ``order_with_respect_to`` aon uair a "
"gheobhaidh tú liosta rudaí den tsamhail seo."

msgid "Changing ``order_with_respect_to``"
msgstr "Athrú ``ord_with_respect_to``"

msgid ""
"Because ``order_with_respect_to`` adds a new database column, be sure to "
"make and apply the appropriate migrations if you add or change "
"``order_with_respect_to`` after your initial :djadmin:`migrate`."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go gcuireann ``order_with_respect_to`` colún nua bunachar sonraí leis, "
"bí cinnte na himirce cuí a dhéanamh agus a chur i bhfeidhm má chuireann tú "
"``order_with_respect_to`` nó má athraíonn tú ``order_with_respect_to`` tar "
"éis do thosaithe:djadmin: `migrate`."

msgid "``ordering``"
msgstr "``ordú ``"

msgid ""
"The default ordering for the object, for use when obtaining lists of "
"objects::"
msgstr ""
"An t-ordú réamhshocraithe don réad, le húsáid agus liostaí rudaí á fháil::"

