"This is a tuple or list of strings and/or query expressions. Each string is "
"a field name with an optional \"-\" prefix, which indicates descending "
"order. Fields without a leading \"-\" will be ordered ascending. Use the "
"string \"?\" to order randomly."
msgstr ""
"Is tuple nó liosta teaghráin agus/nó nathanna fiosrúcháin é seo. Is ainm "
"réimse é gach sreang le réimír roghnach “-”, a léiríonn ord íslitheach. "
"Ordófar páirceanna gan tosaigh “-” ag ardú. Úsáid an teaghrán “?” chun ordú "
"go randamach."

msgid "For example, to order by a ``pub_date`` field ascending, use this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun ordú de réir réimse ``pub_date`` ag ardú, bain úsáid as "
"seo:"

msgid "To order by ``pub_date`` descending, use this::"
msgstr "Chun ordú trí `pub_date`` síos, bain úsáid as seo:"

msgid ""
"To order by ``pub_date`` descending, then by ``author`` ascending, use this::"
msgstr ""
"Chun ordú trí `pub_date ``ag dul síos, ansin trí ``author`` ag ardú, bain "
"úsáid as seo:"

msgid ""
"You can also use :doc:`query expressions </ref/models/expressions>`. To "
"order by ``author`` ascending and make null values sort last, use this::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat úsáid freisin: doc: `léirithe fiosraithe' </ref/models/"
"expressions>. Chun ordú trí ``údar`` ag ardú agus luachanna null a shórtáil "
"go deireanach, bain úsáid as seo:"

msgid ""
"Ordering is not a free operation. Each field you add to the ordering incurs "
"a cost to your database. Each foreign key you add will implicitly include "
"all of its default orderings as well."
msgstr ""
"Ní oibríocht saor in aisce é ordú. Tá costas ar do bhunachar sonraí ag gach "
"réimse a chuireann tú leis an ordú. Cuimsíonn gach eochair eachtrach a "
"chuireann tú leis go hiontach a ordú réamhshocraithe go léir freisin."

msgid ""
"If a query doesn't have an ordering specified, results are returned from the "
"database in an unspecified order. A particular ordering is guaranteed only "
"when ordering by a set of fields that uniquely identify each object in the "
"results. For example, if a ``name`` field isn't unique, ordering by it won't "
"guarantee objects with the same name always appear in the same order."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ordú sonraithe i gceist, cuirtear torthaí ar ais ón mbunachar "
"sonraí in ord neamhshonraithe. Ní ráthaítear ordú áirithe ach amháin nuair a "
"ordaítear é ag sraith réimsí a shainaithníonn gach rud sna torthaí go "
"uathúil. Mar shampla, mura bhfuil réimse ``ainm ``uathúil, ní ráthóidh ordú "
"leis go mbeidh rudaí leis an ainm céanna le feiceáil san ord céanna i gcónaí."

msgid "``permissions``"
msgstr "``ceadúnaí``"

msgid ""
"Extra permissions to enter into the permissions table when creating this "
"object. Add, change, delete, and view permissions are automatically created "
"for each model. This example specifies an extra permission, "
"``can_deliver_pizzas``::"
msgstr ""
"Ceadanna breise le dul isteach sa tábla ceadanna agus an réad seo á chruthú. "
"Cruthaítear ceadanna a chur leis, a athrú, a scriosadh agus féachaint go "
"huathoibríoch do gach samhail. Sonraíonn an sampla seo cead breise, "
"``can_deliver_pizzas``:"

msgid ""
"This is a list or tuple of 2-tuples in the format ``(permission_code, "
"human_readable_permission_name)``."
msgstr ""
"Seo liosta nó tiúpla de dhá thúpla san fhormáid ``(ceadúna_cód, "
"human_readable_ceadúna_ainm)``."

msgid "``default_permissions``"
msgstr "``ceadúna_réamhshocraithe``"

msgid ""
"Defaults to ``('add', 'change', 'delete', 'view')``. You may customize this "
"list, for example, by setting this to an empty list if your app doesn't "
"require any of the default permissions. It must be specified on the model "
"before the model is created by :djadmin:`migrate` in order to prevent any "
"omitted permissions from being created."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe go ``('cuir', 'athraigh', 'scrios', 'view')``. Féadfaidh tú "
"an liosta seo a shaincheapadh, mar shampla, tríd é seo a shocrú ar liosta "
"folamh mura dteastaíonn aon chead de na ceadanna réamhshocraithe ag teastáil "
"ó aip. Caithfear é a shonrú ar an tsamhail sula gcruthófar an tsamhail "
"ó:djadmin: `migrate` d'fhonn cosc a chur ar aon cheadanna fágtha a chruthú."

msgid "``proxy``"
msgstr "``proxy``"

msgid ""
"If ``proxy = True``, a model which subclasses another model will be treated "
"as a :ref:`proxy model <proxy-models>`."
msgstr ""
"<proxy-models>Má tá ``proxy = True``, déileálfar le samhail a fho-aicmíonn "
"samhail eile mar a:ref: `seachmhúnla `."

msgid "``required_db_features``"
msgstr "``riachtanach_db_gnéatach``"

msgid ""
"List of database features that the current connection should have so that "
"the model is considered during the migration phase. For example, if you set "
"this list to ``['gis_enabled']``, the model will only be synchronized on GIS-"
"enabled databases. It's also useful to skip some models when testing with "
"several database backends. Avoid relations between models that may or may "
"not be created as the ORM doesn't handle this."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na gnéithe bunachar sonraí ba chóir a bheith ag an nasc reatha "
"ionas go mbreithnítear an tsamhail le linn na céime imirce. Mar shampla, má "
"shocraíonn tú an liosta seo go ``['gis_enabled']``, ní dhéanfar an tsamhail "
"a shioncronú ach ar bhunachar sonraí atá cumasaithe GIS. Tá sé úsáideach "
"freisin roinnt samhlacha a scipeáil agus tú ag tástáil le roinnt cúltaca "
"bunachar sonraí. Seachain caidreamh idir samhlacha a d'fhéadfaí nó nach "
"féidir a chruthú toisc nach láimhseálann an ORM é seo."

msgid "``required_db_vendor``"
msgstr "``riachtanach_db_vendor``"

msgid ""
"Name of a supported database vendor that this model is specific to. Current "
"built-in vendor names are: ``sqlite``, ``postgresql``, ``mysql``, "
"``oracle``. If this attribute is not empty and the current connection vendor "
"doesn't match it, the model will not be synchronized."
msgstr ""
"Ainm díoltóra bunachar sonraí tacaithe a bhfuil an tsamhail seo sonrach air. "
"Is iad na hainmneacha díoltóra ionsuite reatha: ``sqlite``, `postgresql``, "
"``mysql``, ``oracle``. Mura bhfuil an tréith seo folamh agus mura n-oireann "
"an díoltóir nasc reatha leis, ní dhéanfar an tsamhail a shioncronú."

msgid "``select_on_save``"
msgstr "``roghnaithe_on_shábháil``"

msgid ""
"Determines if Django will use the "
"pre-1.6 :meth:`django.db.models.Model.save()` algorithm. The old algorithm "
"uses ``SELECT`` to determine if there is an existing row to be updated. The "
"new algorithm tries an ``UPDATE`` directly. In some rare cases the "
"``UPDATE`` of an existing row isn't visible to Django. An example is the "
"PostgreSQL ``ON UPDATE`` trigger which returns ``NULL``. In such cases the "
"new algorithm will end up doing an ``INSERT`` even when a row exists in the "
"database."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann sé an n-úsáidfidh Django an algartam réamh-1.6: meth: "
"`Django.db.Models.Model.save () `. Úsáideann an sean-algartam ``SELECT`` "
"chun a chinneadh an bhfuil sraith ann atá le nuashonrú. Déanann an algartam "
"nua iarracht ``UPDATE`` go díreach. I roinnt cásanna neamhchoitianta ní "
"fheiceann Django an ``UPDATE`` de shraith atá ann cheana. Sampla is ea an "
"truicear PostgreSQL ``ON UPDATE`` a fhilleann ``NULL``. I gcásanna den sórt "
"sin beidh an algartam nua ag déanamh ``INSERT`` fiú nuair a bhíonn sraith "
"ann sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Usually there is no need to set this attribute. The default is ``False``."
msgstr "De ghnáth ní gá an tréith seo a shocrú. Is é an réamhshocrú ``False``."

msgid ""
"See :meth:`django.db.models.Model.save()` for more about the old and new "
"saving algorithm."
msgstr ""
"Féach: Meth: `django.db.models.model.save () `le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais "
"faoin algartam sábhála sean agus nua."

msgid "``indexes``"
msgstr "``Innéacsanna ``"

msgid ""
"A list of :doc:`indexes </ref/models/indexes>` that you want to define on "
"the model::"
msgstr ""
"Liosta de:doc: `indexes` </ref/models/indexes> ar mhaith leat a shainiú ar "
"an tsamhail::"

msgid "``unique_together``"
msgstr "``uathach_le chéime``"

msgid ""
"Use :class:`.UniqueConstraint` with the :attr:`~Options.constraints` option "
