"``'polls.Question'``."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn an réad, filleann ``app_label.object_name``, m.sh. "
"```Polls.question'``."

msgid "``label_lower``"
msgstr "``label_lower``"

msgid ""
"Representation of the model, returns ``app_label.model_name``, e.g. "
"``'polls.question'``."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn léiriú an tsamhail, filleann ``app_label.model_name``, m.sh. "
"```polls.question'``."

msgid "``QuerySet`` API reference"
msgstr "Tagairt API ``QuerySet ``"

msgid ""
"This document describes the details of the ``QuerySet`` API. It builds on "
"the material presented in the :doc:`model </topics/db/models>` "
"and :doc:`database query </topics/db/queries>` guides, so you'll probably "
"want to read and understand those documents before reading this one."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an doiciméad seo cur síos ar shonraí an API ``QuerySet``. Tógann sé "
"ar an ábhar a chuirtear i láthair sna treoracha: doc: `model` agus:doc: "
"`ceisteanna bunachar sonraí` </topics/db/models>, mar sin is dócha go mbeidh "
"tú ag iarraidh na do</topics/db/queries> iciméid sin a léamh agus a "
"thuiscint sula léann tú an ceann seo."

msgid "When ``QuerySet``\\s are evaluated"
msgstr "Nuair a dhéantar meastóireacht a dhéanamh ar ``QuerySet`"

msgid ""
"Internally, a ``QuerySet`` can be constructed, filtered, sliced, and "
"generally passed around without actually hitting the database. No database "
"activity actually occurs until you do something to evaluate the queryset."
msgstr ""
"Go hinmheánach, is féidir ``QuerySet` a thógáil, a scagadh, a sliseadh, agus "
"a rith timpeall go ginearálta gan an bunachar sonraí a bhualadh i ndáiríre. "
"Ní tharlaíonn aon ghníomhaíocht bunachar sonraí i ndáiríre go dtí go "
"ndéanann tú rud éigin chun an tac"

msgid "You can evaluate a ``QuerySet`` in the following ways:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat ``QuerySet`` a mheas ar na bealaí seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"**Iteration.** A ``QuerySet`` is iterable, and it executes its database "
"query the first time you iterate over it. For example, this will print the "
"headline of all entries in the database::"
msgstr ""
"**Aiter.** Tá ``QuerySet`` in-athraithe, agus déanann sé a cheist bunachar "
"sonraí a fhorghníomhú an chéad uair a dhéanann tú athrá air. Mar shampla, "
"priontóidh sé seo ceannlíne na n-iontrálacha go léir sa bhunachar sonraí::"

msgid ""
"Note: Don't use this if all you want to do is determine if at least one "
"result exists. It's more efficient to use :meth:`~QuerySet.exists`."
msgstr ""
"Nóta: Ná húsáid é seo más mian leat a dhéanamh ach a chinneadh an bhfuil "
"toradh amháin ar a laghad ann. Tá sé níos éifeachtaí úsáid: meth: "
"`~QuerySet.exists`."

msgid ""
"**Asynchronous iteration.** A ``QuerySet`` can also be iterated over using "
"``async for``::"
msgstr ""
"**Athrú asincrónaí.** Is féidir ``QuerySet`` a athrú freisin trí ``async "
"for``:"

msgid ""
"Both synchronous and asynchronous iterators of QuerySets share the same "
"underlying cache."
msgstr ""
"Tá an taisce bunúsach céanna ag athraitheoirí sioncrónach agus asincrónach "
"de QuerySets."

msgid ""
"**Slicing.** As explained in :ref:`limiting-querysets`, a ``QuerySet`` can "
"be sliced, using Python's array-slicing syntax. Slicing an unevaluated "
"``QuerySet`` usually returns another unevaluated ``QuerySet``, but Django "
"will execute the database query if you use the \"step\" parameter of slice "
"syntax, and will return a list. Slicing a ``QuerySet`` that has been "
"evaluated also returns a list."
msgstr ""
"**Sliseach.** Mar a mhínítear in:ref: `limiting-querysets`, is féidir "
"``QuerySet`` a sliseadh, ag baint úsáide as comhréiteach slisnú eagair "
"Python. Is gnách go bhfillfidh ``QuerySet`` neamh-mheasúnaithe ```QuerySet "
"``eile gan mheasúnú, ach déanfaidh Django ceist an bhunachar sonraí a "
"fhorghníomhú má úsáideann tú an paraiméadar “céim” de chomhréir sliseanna, "
"agus cuirfidh sé liosta ar ais. Tugann sé liosta freisin ag sliseadh "
"``QuerySet`` a rinneadh meastóireacht air."

msgid ""
"Also note that even though slicing an unevaluated ``QuerySet`` returns "
"another unevaluated ``QuerySet``, modifying it further (e.g., adding more "
"filters, or modifying ordering) is not allowed, since that does not "
"translate well into SQL and it would not have a clear meaning either."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin cé go bhfilleann ``QuerySet` neamh-mheasúnaithe "
"```QuerySet ``eile neamh-mheasúnaithe, ní cheadaítear é a mhodhnú tuilleadh "
"(m.sh., níos mó scagairí a chur leis, nó ordú a mhodhnú), ós rud é nach "
"aistríonn sé go maith go SQL agus ní bheadh brí soiléir aige ach an oiread."

msgid ""
"**Pickling/Caching.** See the following section for details of what is "
"involved when `pickling QuerySets`_. The important thing for the purposes of "
"this section is that the results are read from the database."
msgstr ""
"**Piccling/Caching.** Féach an chuid seo a leanas le haghaidh sonraí faoin "
"méid a bhfuil i gceist le linn `Picling QuerySets`_. Is é an rud tábhachtach "
"chun críocha an chuid seo ná go léitear na torthaí ón mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"**repr().** A ``QuerySet`` is evaluated when you call ``repr()`` on it. This "
"is for convenience in the Python interactive interpreter, so you can "
"immediately see your results when using the API interactively."
msgstr ""
"**repr () .** Déantar meastóireacht ar ``QuerySet`` nuair a ghlaonn tú "
"``repr () ``air. Tá sé seo ar mhaithe le háisiúlacht san ateangaire "
"idirghníomhach Python, ionas gur féidir leat do thorthaí a fheiceáil "
"láithreach agus an API á úsáid idirghníomhach."

msgid ""
"**len().** A ``QuerySet`` is evaluated when you call ``len()`` on it. This, "
"as you might expect, returns the length of the result list."
msgstr ""
"**len () .** Déantar meastóireacht ar ``QuerySet`` nuair a ghlaonn tú `len "
"() ``air. Tugann sé seo, mar a d'fhéadfá a bheith ag súil leis, fad an "
"liosta torthaí ar ais."

msgid ""
"Note: If you only need to determine the number of records in the set (and "
"don't need the actual objects), it's much more efficient to handle a count "
"at the database level using SQL's ``SELECT COUNT(*)``. Django provides "
"a :meth:`~QuerySet.count` method for precisely this reason."
msgstr ""
"Nóta: Mura gá duit ach líon na dtaifid sa tacar a chinneadh (agus mura "
"dteastaíonn na rudaí iarbhír uait), tá sé i bhfad níos éifeachtaí "
"comhaireamh a láimhseáil ag leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí ag baint úsáide as "
"``SELECT COUNT (*) `SQL. Soláthraíonn Django modh a: meth: `~QuerySet.count` "
"ar an gcúis seo go beacht."

msgid ""
"**list().** Force evaluation of a ``QuerySet`` by calling ``list()`` on it. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"**liosta () .** Meastóireacht a chur i bhfeidhm ar ``QuerySet`` trí `liosta "
"() ``a ghlaoch air. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"**bool().** Testing a ``QuerySet`` in a boolean context, such as using "
"``bool()``, ``or``, ``and`` or an ``if`` statement, will cause the query to "
"be executed. If there is at least one result, the ``QuerySet`` is ``True``, "
"otherwise ``False``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"**bool () .** Trí thástáil a dhéanamh ar ``QuerySet`` i gcomhthéacs boolean, "
"mar shampla ``bool () ``, `nó``, `nó ``, `and`` nó ráiteas ``if``, ``a "
"úsáid, is cúis leis an bhfiosrú a fhorghníomhú. Má tá toradh amháin ar a "
"laghad ann, is é an ``QuerySet`` `True``, `True``, ar shlí eile ``False``. "
"Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Note: If you only want to determine if at least one result exists (and don't "
"need the actual objects), it's more efficient to "
"use :meth:`~QuerySet.exists`."
msgstr ""
"Nóta: Mura dteastaíonn uait ach a chinneadh an bhfuil toradh amháin ar a "
"laghad ann (agus nach dteastaíonn na rudaí iarbhír uait), tá sé níos "
"éifeachtaí úsáid: meth: `~QuerySet.exists`."

msgid "Pickling ``QuerySet``\\s"
msgstr "Picling ```QuerySet``\\ s"

msgid ""
"If you :mod:`pickle` a ``QuerySet``, this will force all the results to be "
"loaded into memory prior to pickling. Pickling is usually used as a "
"precursor to caching and when the cached queryset is reloaded, you want the "
"results to already be present and ready for use (reading from the database "
"can take some time, defeating the purpose of caching). This means that when "
"you unpickle a ``QuerySet``, it contains the results at the moment it was "
"pickled, rather than the results that are currently in the database."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú: mod: `pickle` agus ``QuerySet ``, cuirfidh sé seo iallach ar na "
"torthaí go léir a luchtú isteach i gcuimhne sula ndéantar piceáil. De ghnáth "
"úsáidtear picling mar réamhtheoir do chaching agus nuair a dhéantar an tacar "
"fiosrúcháin a athluchtú, ba mhaith leat go mbeadh na torthaí i láthair "
"cheana féin agus réidh le húsáid (is féidir le léamh ón mbunachar sonraí "
"roinnt ama a thógáil, ag ruaigeadh cuspóir na caching). Ciallaíonn sé seo "
"nuair a dhíphicfidh tú ``QuerySet`, go bhfuil na torthaí ann i láthair na "
"huaire gur piceáladh é, seachas na torthaí atá sa bhunachar sonraí faoi "
"láthair."

msgid ""
"If you only want to pickle the necessary information to recreate the "
"``QuerySet`` from the database at a later time, pickle the ``query`` "
"attribute of the ``QuerySet``. You can then recreate the original "
"``QuerySet`` (without any results loaded) using some code like this:"
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait ach an fhaisnéis riachtanach a phiocadh chun an "
"``QuerySet`` a athchruthú ón mbunachar sonraí níos déanaí, piceáil tréith "
"```QuerySet`` den `QuerySet``. Ansin is féidir leat an `QuerySet` bunaidh a "
"athchruthú (gan aon torthaí luchtaithe) ag baint úsáide as cód éigin mar seo:"

msgid ""
"The ``query`` attribute is an opaque object. It represents the internals of "
"the query construction and is not part of the public API. However, it is "
"safe (and fully supported) to pickle and unpickle the attribute's contents "
"as described here."
msgstr ""
"Is réad trédhearcach é an tréith ``fiosraithe``. Léiríonn sé inmheánacha "
"tógála na fiosrúcháin agus níl sé mar chuid den API poiblí. Mar sin féin, tá "
"sé sábháilte (agus tacaítear go hiomlán) ábhar na tréithe a phiocadh agus a "
"dhíphiocadh mar a thuairiscítear anseo."

msgid "Restrictions on ``QuerySet.values_list()``"
msgstr "Srianta ar ``QuerySet.values_List () ``"

msgid ""
"If you recreate :meth:`QuerySet.values_list` using the pickled ``query`` "
"attribute, it will be converted to :meth:`QuerySet.values`:"
msgstr ""
"Má athchruthaíonn tú: meth: `QuerySet.values_list` ag baint úsáide as an "
"tréith picilte ```Query``, déanfar é a thiontú u:meth: `QuerySet.values`:"

msgid ""
"Pickles of ``QuerySet`` objects are only valid for the version of Django "
"that was used to generate them. If you generate a pickle using Django "
"version N, there is no guarantee that pickle will be readable with Django "
"version N+1. Pickles should not be used as part of a long-term archival "
"strategy."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Since pickle compatibility errors can be difficult to diagnose, such as "
"silently corrupted objects, a ``RuntimeWarning`` is raised when you try to "
"unpickle a queryset in a Django version that is different than the one in "
"which it was pickled."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhféadfadh sé a bheith deacair earráidí comhoiriúnachta picéil a "
"dhiagnóisiú, mar shampla rudaí truaillithe go ciúin, ardaítear "
