"calling ``reverse()``, and will remain undefined afterward)."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, tabhair faoi deara nach gcaithfear `reverse () ``a "
"ghlaoch de ghnáth ach ar ``QuerySet`` a bhfuil ordú sainmhínithe aige "
"(m.sh., agus tú ag fiosrú i gcoinne samhail a shainmhíníonn ordú "
"réamhshocraithe, nó nuair a úsáidtear: meth: `order_by () `). Mura "
"sainmhínítear aon ordú den sórt sin le haghaidh ``QuerySet` ar leith, níl "
"aon éifeacht fhíor ag glaoch ar ``reverse () ``air (ní raibh an t-ordú "
"neamhshainithe sula nglaoigh ar ``reverse ()``, agus fanfaidh sé gan "
"sainmhíniú ina dhiaidh sin)."

msgid "``distinct()``"
msgstr "``difriúil () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns a new ``QuerySet`` that uses ``SELECT DISTINCT`` in its SQL query. "
"This eliminates duplicate rows from the query results."
msgstr ""
"Filleann ``QuerySet`` nua a úsáideann ``SELECT DISTINCT`` ina cheist SQL. "
"Cuireann sé seo deireadh le sraitheanna dúblacha ó thorthaí na gce"

msgid ""
"By default, a ``QuerySet`` will not eliminate duplicate rows. In practice, "
"this is rarely a problem, because simple queries such as "
"``Blog.objects.all()`` don't introduce the possibility of duplicate result "
"rows. However, if your query spans multiple tables, it's possible to get "
"duplicate results when a ``QuerySet`` is evaluated. That's when you'd use "
"``distinct()``."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní chuirfidh `QuerySet ``deireadh le sraitheanna "
"dúblacha. Go praiticiúil, is annamh a bhíonn sé seo ina fhadhb, toisc nach "
"dtugann ceisteanna simplí mar `Blog.Objects.all () `isteach an "
"fhéidearthacht sraitheanna torthaí dúblacha. Mar sin féin, má chuimsíonn "
"d'fhiosrúchán iolrthaí táblaí, is féidir torthaí dúblacha a fháil nuair a "
"dhéantar “QuerySet” a mheas. Sin nuair a úsáideann tú ``difriúil () ``."

msgid ""
"Any fields used in an :meth:`order_by` call are included in the SQL "
"``SELECT`` columns. This can sometimes lead to unexpected results when used "
"in conjunction with ``distinct()``. If you order by fields from a related "
"model, those fields will be added to the selected columns and they may make "
"otherwise duplicate rows appear to be distinct. Since the extra columns "
"don't appear in the returned results (they are only there to support "
"ordering), it sometimes looks like non-distinct results are being returned."
msgstr ""
"Tá aon réimsí a úsáidtear i nglao an:meth: `order_by` san áireamh sna colúin "
"SQL ``SELECT``. Uaireanta d'fhéadfadh torthaí gan choinne a bheith mar "
"thoradh air seo nuair a úsáidtear iad i gcomhar le ``difriúil () ``. Má "
"ordaíonn tú de réir réimsí ó mhúnla gaolmhar, cuirfear na réimsí sin leis na "
"colúin roghnaithe agus féadfaidh siad a bheith cosúil go bhfuil sraitheanna "
"dúblacha ar leith ar shlí eile. Ós rud é nach bhfuil na colúin bhreise le "
"feiceáil sna torthaí ar ais (níl siad ann ach chun tacú le hordú), is cosúil "
"go bhfuil torthaí neamh-shainiúla á thabhairt ar ais uaireanta."

msgid ""
"Similarly, if you use a :meth:`values()` query to restrict the columns "
"selected, the columns used in any :meth:`order_by()` (or default model "
"ordering) will still be involved and may affect uniqueness of the results."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, má úsáideann tú fiosrúchán a:meth: `values () `chun "
"srian a chur ar na colúin a roghnaíodh, beidh baint fós ag na colúin a "
"úsáidtear in aon: meth: `order_by ()` (nó ordú samhail réamhshocraithe) agus "
"féadfaidh siad dul i bhfeidhm ar uathúlacht na dtorthaí."

msgid ""
"The moral here is that if you are using ``distinct()`` be careful about "
"ordering by related models. Similarly, when using ``distinct()`` "
"and :meth:`values()` together, be careful when ordering by fields not in "
"the :meth:`values()` call."
msgstr ""
"Is é an moráltacht anseo má tá tú ag úsáid ``()`` bí cúramach faoi ordú de "
"réir samhlacha gaolmhara. Ar an gcaoi chéanna, agus tú ag úsáid ``()`` "
"agus:meth: `luachanna () `le chéile, bí cúramach agus tú ag ordú de réir "
"réimsí nach bhfuil sa ghlao:meth: `values ()`."

msgid ""
"On PostgreSQL only, you can pass positional arguments (``*fields``) in order "
"to specify the names of fields to which the ``DISTINCT`` should apply. This "
"translates to a ``SELECT DISTINCT ON`` SQL query. Here's the difference. For "
"a normal ``distinct()`` call, the database compares *each* field in each row "
"when determining which rows are distinct. For a ``distinct()`` call with "
"specified field names, the database will only compare the specified field "
"names."
msgstr ""
"Ar PostgreSQL amháin, is féidir leat argóintí seasaimh (`*réimsí ``) a rith "
"d'fhonn ainmneacha na réimsí ar chóir go mbeadh feidhm ag an ``DISTINCT`` a "
"shonrú. Aistríonn sé seo go fiosrúchán SQL ``SELECT DISTINCT ON``. Seo an "
"difríocht. Maidir le gnáthghlao ``difriúil () ``, déanann an bunachar sonraí "
"comparáid idir *gach réimse* i ngach sraith agus iad ag cinneadh cé na "
"sraitheanna atá ar leith. Maidir le glao ``difriúil () ``le hainmneacha "
"réimse sonraithe, ní dhéanfaidh an bunachar sonraí ach comparáid idir na "
"hainmneacha réimse sonraithe."

msgid ""
"When you specify field names, you *must* provide an ``order_by()`` in the "
"``QuerySet``, and the fields in ``order_by()`` must start with the fields in "
"``distinct()``, in the same order."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shonraíonn tú ainmneacha réimse, ní mór duit* ``order_by () ``a "
"sholáthar sa ``QuerySet``, agus ní mór do na réimsí i `order_by ()`` tosú "
"leis na réimsí i ``()``, san ord céanna."

msgid ""
"For example, ``SELECT DISTINCT ON (a)`` gives you the first row for each "
"value in column ``a``. If you don't specify an order, you'll get some "
"arbitrary row."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, tugann ``SELECT DISTINCT ON (a) ``an chéad tsraith duit do gach "
"luach i gcolún ``a``. Mura ndéanann tú ordú a shonrú, gheobhaidh tú sraith "
"treallach éigin."

msgid "Examples (those after the first will only work on PostgreSQL):"
msgstr ""
"Samplaí (ní oibreoidh iad siúd tar éis an chéad cheann ach ar PostgreSQL):"

msgid ""
"Keep in mind that :meth:`order_by` uses any default related model ordering "
"that has been defined. You might have to explicitly order by the relation "
"``_id`` or referenced field to make sure the ``DISTINCT ON`` expressions "
"match those at the beginning of the ``ORDER BY`` clause. For example, if the "
"``Blog`` model defined an :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.ordering` by "
"``name``::"
msgstr ""
"Coinnigh i gcuimhne go n-úsáideann: meth: `order_by` aon ordú samhail "
"ghaolmhara réamhshocraithe atá sainmhínithe. B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort ordú go "
"sainráite de réir an ghaol ``_id`` nó réimse tagartha chun a chinntiú go n-"
"oireann na nathanna ``DISTINCT ON`` iad siúd ag tús an chlásal ``ORDER BY "
"``. Mar shampla, má shainmhíníodh an tsamhail ``Blog`` an:attr: "
"`~Django.db.Models.Options.Ordering` le ``ainm ``:"

msgid ""
"...wouldn't work because the query would be ordered by ``blog__name`` thus "
"mismatching the ``DISTINCT ON`` expression. You'd have to explicitly order "
"by the relation ``_id`` field (``blog_id`` in this case) or the referenced "
"one (``blog__pk``) to make sure both expressions match."
msgstr ""
"... ní oibreodh toisc go ndéanfaí an cheist a ordú ag ``blog__name`` agus ar "
"an gcaoi sin mímheaitseáil an abairt ``DISTINCT ON``. Bheadh ort ordú go "
"sainráite de réir réimse gaolmhar ``_id`` (``blog_id`` sa chás seo) nó an "
"ceann tagartha (``blog__pk``) chun a chinntiú go n-oireann an dá abairt."

msgid "``values()``"
msgstr "``luachanna () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``QuerySet`` that returns dictionaries, rather than model "
"instances, when used as an iterable."
msgstr ""
"Tugann “QuerySet” ar ais foclóirí, seachas cásanna samhlacha, nuair a "
"úsáidtear é mar athrá."

msgid ""
"Each of those dictionaries represents an object, with the keys corresponding "
"to the attribute names of model objects."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn gach ceann de na foclóirí sin réad, agus na heochracha a "
"fhreagraíonn d'ainmneacha tréithe rudaí samhail."

msgid ""
"This example compares the dictionaries of ``values()`` with the normal model "
"objects:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann an sampla seo comparáid idir foclóirí ``luachanna () ``leis na gnáth-"
"rudaí samhail:"

msgid ""
"The ``values()`` method takes optional positional arguments, ``*fields``, "
"which specify field names to which the ``SELECT`` should be limited. If you "
"specify the fields, each dictionary will contain only the field keys/values "
"for the fields you specify. If you don't specify the fields, each dictionary "
"will contain a key and value for every field in the database table."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh ``luachanna () ``argóintí suíomhanna roghnacha, ``*réimsí``, "
"a shonraíonn ainmneacha réimse ar chóir an ``SELECT`` a theorannú dóibh. Má "
"shonraíonn tú na réimsí, ní bheidh i ngach foclóir ach na heochair/luachanna "
"réimse do na réimsí a shonraíonn tú. Mura sonraíonn tú na réimsí, beidh "
"eochair agus luach i ngach foclóir do gach réimse sa tábla bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The ``values()`` method also takes optional keyword arguments, "
"``**expressions``, which are passed through to :meth:`annotate`:"
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh ``luachanna () ``argóintí eochairfhocal roghnacha freisin, "
"``**léiritheach``, a chuirtear trí:meth: `annotate`:"

msgid ""
"You can use built-in and :doc:`custom lookups </howto/custom-lookups>` in "
"ordering. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat úsáid a bhaint as ionsuite agus: doc: `cuardach "
"saincheapaithe' ag ordú </howto/custom-lookups>. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"An aggregate within a ``values()`` clause is applied before other arguments "
"within the same ``values()`` clause. If you need to group by another value, "
"add it to an earlier ``values()`` clause instead. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear comhiomlán laistigh de chlásal ``luachanna () ``i bhfeidhm roimh "
"argóintí eile laistigh den chlásal ``luachanna () `céanna. Más gá duit "
"grúpáil de réir luach eile, cuir é le clásal “luachanna ()” níos luaithe ina "
"ionad. Mar shampla:"

msgid "A few subtleties that are worth mentioning:"
msgstr "Cúpla caolchúrsaíocht is fiú a lua:"

msgid ""
"If you have a field called ``foo`` that is "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`, the default ``values()`` call will "
"return a dictionary key called ``foo_id``, since this is the name of the "
"hidden model attribute that stores the actual value (the ``foo`` attribute "
"refers to the related model). When you are calling ``values()`` and passing "
"in field names, you can pass in either ``foo`` or ``foo_id`` and you will "
"get back the same thing (the dictionary key will match the field name you "
"passed in)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá réimse agat darb ainm `foo`` is é sin a:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey`, cuirfidh an glao réamhshocraithe ``values () "
"``ar ais eochair foclóra ar a dtugtar ``foo_id``, ós rud é seo ainm an "
"tréith samhail i bhfolach a stóráil an luach iarbhír (tagraíonn an tréith "
"`foo' don tsamhail ghaolmhar). Nuair a bhíonn tú ag glaoch ar `luachanna () "
"``agus ag dul isteach ainmneacha réimse, is féidir leat dul isteach ``foo`` "
"nó ``foo_id`` agus gheobhaidh tú an rud céanna ar ais (meaitneoidh an "
"eochair foclóra leis an ainm réimse a chuaigh tú isteach)."

msgid ""
"When using ``values()`` together with :meth:`distinct()`, be aware that "
"ordering can affect the results. See the note in :meth:`distinct` for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Agus `luachanna () `á n-úsáid agat in éineacht le:meth: `different ()`, bí "
"ar an eolas go bhféadfadh ordú dul i bhfeidhm ar na torthaí. Féach an nóta "
"in:meth: `distint` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"If you use a ``values()`` clause after an :meth:`extra()` call, any fields "
"defined by a ``select`` argument in the :meth:`extra()` must be explicitly "
"included in the ``values()`` call. Any :meth:`extra()` call made after a "
"``values()`` call will have its extra selected fields ignored."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú clásal ``luachanna () ``tar éis glao:meth: `extra () `, ní "
"mór aon réimsí a shainmhínítear le argóint ``roghnaithe`` sa :meth: `extra "
"()` a chur san áireamh go sainráite sa ghlao ``luachanna ()``. Déanfar "
"neamhaird ar a réimsí breise roghnaithe aon: Meth: `extra () `a dhéantar tar "
"éis glao ``values () ``."

msgid ""
"Calling :meth:`only()` and :meth:`defer()` after ``values()`` doesn't make "
"sense, so doing so will raise a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""
"Níl ciall ag glaoch: Meth: `only () `agus:meth: `diafer ()` tar éis "
"``luachanna () ``, agus mar sin déanfar amhlaidh ardóidh ``typeError``."

msgid ""
"Combining transforms and aggregates requires the use of two :meth:`annotate` "
"calls, either explicitly or as keyword arguments to :meth:`values`. As "
"above, if the transform has been registered on the relevant field type the "
"first :meth:`annotate` can be omitted, thus the following examples are "
"equivalent:"
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn claochruithe agus comhiomlánaithe a chur le chéile dhá ghlaonna: "
"meth: `annotate` a úsáid, go sainráite nó mar argóintí eochairfhocal "
"chuig:meth: `luacha`. Mar atá thuas, má tá an claochlú cláraithe ar an "
"gcineál réimse ábhartha is féidir an chéad:meth: `annotate` a fhágáil, dá "
"bhrí sin tá na samplaí seo a leanas coibhéiseach:"

msgid ""
"It is useful when you know you're only going to need values from a small "
"number of the available fields and you won't need the functionality of a "
"model instance object. It's more efficient to select only the fields you "
"need to use."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé úsáideach nuair a fhios agat nach mbeidh luachanna ag teastáil uait "
"ach ó líon beag de na réimsí atá ar fáil agus ní bheidh feidhmiúlacht réad "
"samhail de dhíth ort. Tá sé níos éifeachtaí ach na réimsí a theastaíonn uait "
"a úsáid a roghnú."

msgid ""
"Finally, note that you can call ``filter()``, ``order_by()``, etc. after the "
"``values()`` call, that means that these two calls are identical::"
msgstr ""
"Mar fhocal scoir, tabhair faoi deara gur féidir leat glaoch ar ``filter () "
"``, `order_by ()``, srl. Tar éis an ghlao ``values () ``, ciallaíonn sin go "
"bhfuil an dá ghlao seo comhionann::"

msgid ""
"The people who made Django prefer to put all the SQL-affecting methods "
"first, followed (optionally) by any output-affecting methods (such as "
"``values()``), but it doesn't really matter. This is your chance to really "
"flaunt your individualism."
msgstr ""
"Is fearr leis na daoine a rinne Django na modhanna go léir a théann i "
"bhfeidhm ag SQL a chur ar dtús, agus aon mhodhanna a théann i bhfeidhm ag "
"aschur (mar shampla `luachanna () `) ina dhiaidh sin (roghnach), ach níl sé "
"tábhachtach i ndáiríre. Is é seo do sheans do dhaoine aonair a thaispeáint i "
"ndáiríre."

msgid ""
"You can also refer to fields on related models with reverse relations "
"through ``OneToOneField``, ``ForeignKey`` and ``ManyToManyField`` attributes:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh freisin do réimsí ar mhúnlaí gaolmhara le "
"caidreamh droim trí thréithe ``OneTooneField``, `ForeignKey`` agus "
"``ManyTomanyField``:"

msgid ""
"Because :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` attributes and reverse "
"relations can have multiple related rows, including these can have a "
"multiplier effect on the size of your result set. This will be especially "
"pronounced if you include multiple such fields in your ``values()`` query, "
"in which case all possible combinations will be returned."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go bhféadfadh sraitheanna gaolmhara iolracha a bheith ag tréithe agus "
"caidrimh droim: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` agus caidrimh droim, "
"lena n-áirítear is féidir leo seo éifeacht iolraitheach a bheith acu ar "
"mhéid do thraith torthaí. Cuirfear é seo a fhuaimniú go háirithe má "
"chuireann tú réimsí den sórt sin san áireamh i d'fhiosrúchán ``luachanna () "
"``, agus sa chás sin cuirfear gach teaglaim féideartha ar ais."

msgid "Special values for ``JSONField`` on SQLite"
msgstr "Luachanna speisialta do ``JSONField`` ar SQLite"

msgid ""
"Due to the way the ``JSON_EXTRACT`` and ``JSON_TYPE`` SQL functions are "
"implemented on SQLite, and lack of the ``BOOLEAN`` data type, ``values()`` "
"will return ``True``, ``False``, and ``None`` instead of ``\"true\"``, "
"``\"false\"``, and ``\"null\"`` strings "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.JSONField` key transforms."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a chuirtear feidhmeanna SQL `JSON_EXTRACT`` agus "
"``JSON_TYPE`` i bhfeidhm ar SQLite, agus easpa an chineál sonraí `BOOLEAN``, "
"cuirfidh `luachanna () ``ar ais `True``, `False``, agus ``None`` in ionad "
"``true\"``, agus Athraíonn eochair teaghráin ``\"null\"`` d'aicme: "
"`~django.db.models.jsonField`."

msgid ""
"The ``SELECT`` clause generated when using ``values()`` was updated to "
"respect the order of the specified ``*fields`` and ``**expressions``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``values_list()``"
msgstr "``liosta_luachanna () ``"

msgid ""
"This is similar to ``values()`` except that instead of returning "
"dictionaries, it returns tuples when iterated over. Each tuple contains the "
"value from the respective field or expression passed into the "
"``values_list()`` call — so the first item is the first field, etc. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo cosúil le ``luachanna () ``ach amháin go bhfilleann sé foclóirí ar "
"ais, seachas foclóirí a thabhairt ar ais, nuair a dhéantar iad a athrá. "
"Cuimsíonn gach tuple an luach ón réimse nó an abairt faoi seach a chuirtear "
"isteach sa ghlao `values_list () `- mar sin is é an chéad mhír an chéad "
"réimse, srl. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"If you only pass in a single field, you can also pass in the ``flat`` "
"parameter. If ``True``, this will mean the returned results are single "
"values, rather than 1-tuples. An example should make the difference clearer:"
msgstr ""
"Mura dtéann tú ach i réimse amháin, is féidir leat dul isteach sa "
"pharaiméadar ``flat`` freisin. Má tá “Fíor”, ciallaíonn sé seo gur luachanna "
"aonair iad na torthaí ar ais, seachas 1-tuples. Ba chóir go ndéanfadh sampla "
"an difríocht níos soiléire:"

msgid "It is an error to pass in ``flat`` when there is more than one field."
msgstr ""
"Is earráid é dul isteach i ``flat`` nuair a bhíonn níos mó ná réimse amháin "
"ann."

msgid ""
"You can pass ``named=True`` to get results as "
"a :func:`~python:collections.namedtuple`:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``named=true`` a rith chun torthaí a fháil mar a:func: "
"`~python:collections.namedtuple`:"

msgid ""
"Using a named tuple may make use of the results more readable, at the "
"expense of a small performance penalty for transforming the results into a "
"named tuple."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáidtear tuple ainmnithe, d'fhéadfadh úsáid a bhaint as na torthaí níos "
"inléite, ar chostas pionós feidhmíochta beag as na torthaí a athrú go tuple "
"ainmnithe."

msgid ""
"If you don't pass any values to ``values_list()``, it will return all the "
"fields in the model, in the order they were declared."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcuireann tú aon luachanna ar aghaidh chuig `values_list () ``, "
"cuirfidh sé na réimsí go léir sa tsamhail ar ais, san ord a dearbhíodh iad."

msgid ""
"A common need is to get a specific field value of a certain model instance. "
"To achieve that, use ``values_list()`` followed by a ``get()`` call:"
msgstr ""
"Is é riachtanas coitianta luach réimse sonrach a fháil de shampla samhail "
"áirithe. Chun é sin a bhaint amach, bain úsáid as `values_list () ``agus "
"glao ``get ()`` ina dhiaidh sin:"

msgid ""
"``values()`` and ``values_list()`` are both intended as optimizations for a "
"specific use case: retrieving a subset of data without the overhead of "
"creating a model instance. This metaphor falls apart when dealing with many-"
"to-many and other multivalued relations (such as the one-to-many relation of "
"a reverse foreign key) because the \"one row, one object\" assumption "
"doesn't hold."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``luachanna () ``agus `values_list ()`` beartaithe araon mar "
"bharrfheabhsú do chás úsáide ar leith: fo-thacar sonraí a aisghabháil gan an "
"lascaire a bhaineann le samhail samhail a chruthú. Titeann an meafar seo óna "
"chéile agus tú ag déileáil le caidrimh illuachmhar agus caidrimh illuachmhar "
"eile (mar shampla gaol duine le go leor eochair eachtrach droim) toisc nach "
"bhfuil an toimhde “aon tsraith, rud amháin”."

msgid ""
"For example, notice the behavior when querying across "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, tabhair faoi deara an t-iompar agus tú ag fiosrú ar fud "
"a:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`:"

msgid ""
"Authors with multiple entries appear multiple times and authors without any "
"entries have ``None`` for the entry headline."
msgstr ""
"Tá údair le hiontrálacha iolracha le feiceáil arís agus uaireanta agus tá "
"``None ``ag údair gan aon iontrálacha don cheannlíne iontrála."

msgid ""
"Similarly, when querying a reverse foreign key, ``None`` appears for entries "
"not having any author:"
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, nuair a fhiosraítear eochair eachtrach droim, tá ``None "
"``le feiceáil le haghaidh iontrálacha nach bhfuil aon údar acu:"

msgid ""
"Due to the way the ``JSON_EXTRACT`` and ``JSON_TYPE`` SQL functions are "
"implemented on SQLite, and lack of the ``BOOLEAN`` data type, "
"``values_list()`` will return ``True``, ``False``, and ``None`` instead of "
"``\"true\"``, ``\"false\"``, and ``\"null\"`` strings "
"for :class:`~django.db.models.JSONField` key transforms."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a chuirtear feidhmeanna SQL ``JSON_EXTRACT`` agus "
"``JSON_TYPE`` i bhfeidhm ar SQLite, agus easpa an chineál sonraí "
