"`Django.Core.Exceptions.ObjectDoesNotExist` a úsáid chun láimhseáil: exc: "
"`~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` eisceachtaí ó iolracha samhlacha::"

msgid "``create()``"
msgstr "``cruthaigh () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``acreate()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``acreate () ``"

msgid ""
"A convenience method for creating an object and saving it all in one step.  "
"Thus::"
msgstr ""
"Modh áisiúlachta chun réad a chruthú agus é go léir a shábháil i gcéim "
"amháin. Dá bhrí sin::"

msgid "are equivalent."
msgstr "iad coibhéiseach."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`force_insert <ref-models-force-insert>` parameter is documented "
"elsewhere, but all it means is that a new object will always be created. "
"Normally you won't need to worry about this. However, if your model contains "
"a manual primary key value that you set and if that value already exists in "
"the database, a call to ``create()`` will fail with "
"an :exc:`~django.db.IntegrityError` since primary keys must be unique. Be "
"prepared to handle the exception if you are using manual primary keys."
msgstr ""
"Tá an paraim <ref-models-force-insert>éadair: ref: `force_insert "
"`doiciméadaithe in áiteanna eile, ach ní chiallaíonn sé ach go gcruthófar "
"réad nua i gcónaí. De ghnáth ní bheidh ort a bheith buartha faoi seo. Mar "
"sin féin, má tá príomh-luach láimhe i do mhúnla a shocraíonn tú agus má tá "
"an luach sin ann cheana sa bhunachar sonraí, teipeann ar ghlao ar `create () "
"``le an:exc: `~django.db.IntegrityError` ós rud é go gcaithfidh eochracha "
"bunscoile a bheith uathúil. Bí réidh chun an eisceacht a láimhseáil má tá "
"eochracha bunscoile láimhe á úsáid agat."

msgid "``get_or_create()``"
msgstr "```get_or_create () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aget_or_create()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aget_or_create () ``"

msgid ""
"A convenience method for looking up an object with the given ``kwargs`` (may "
"be empty if your model has defaults for all fields), creating one if "
"necessary."
msgstr ""
"Modh áisiúlachta chun réad a chuardach leis an `kwargs ``tugtha (féadfaidh "
"sé a bheith folamh má tá réamhshocruithe ag do mhúnla do gach réimse), ag "
"cruthú ceann más gá."

msgid ""
"Returns a tuple of ``(object, created)``, where ``object`` is the retrieved "
"or created object and ``created`` is a boolean specifying whether a new "
"object was created."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé tuple de ``(réad, cruthaithe)``, áit gurb é ``réad ``an réad "
"aisghabháilte nó cruthaithe agus is boolean é ``cruthaithe`` a shonraíonn an "
"cruthaíodh réad nua."

msgid ""
"This is meant to prevent duplicate objects from being created when requests "
"are made in parallel, and as a shortcut to boilerplatish code. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo i gceist chun rudaí dúblacha a chruthú nuair a dhéantar iarratais "
"go comhthreomhar, agus mar aicearra chuig cód boilerplatish. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Here, with concurrent requests, multiple attempts to save a ``Person`` with "
"the same parameters may be made. To avoid this race condition, the above "
"example can be rewritten using ``get_or_create()`` like so::"
msgstr ""
"Anseo, le hiarratais chomhthráthacha, féadfar iarrachtaí iolracha chun "
"``Duine ``a shábháil leis na paraiméadair chéanna. Chun an coinníoll rása "
"seo a sheachaint, is féidir an sampla thuas a athscríobh ag baint úsáide as "
"``get_or_create () ``mar sin:"

msgid ""
"Any keyword arguments passed to ``get_or_create()`` — *except* an optional "
"one called ``defaults`` — will be used in a :meth:`get()` call. If an object "
"is found, ``get_or_create()`` returns a tuple of that object and ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear aon argóintí eochairfhocal a chuirtear chuig ``get_or_create () "
"``- *seachas ceann roghnach ar a dtugtar ``defaults`` - i nglao a:meth: `get "
"() `. Má aimsítear réad, filleann ``get_or_create () ``tuple den réad sin "
"agus ``False``."

msgid ""
"This method is atomic assuming that the database enforces uniqueness of the "
"keyword arguments (see :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.unique` "
"or :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.unique_together`). If the fields used in "
"the keyword arguments do not have a uniqueness constraint, concurrent calls "
"to this method may result in multiple rows with the same parameters being "
"inserted."
msgstr ""
"Tá an modh seo adamach ag glacadh leis go gcuireann an bunachar sonraí "
