"<django.db.models.Q>Is féidir leat coinníollacha níos casta a shonrú don "
"réad aisghabháilte trí ``get_or_create () ``a shlánú le ``filter ()`` agus "
"ag baint úsáid:class: `Q rudaí `. Mar shampla, chun Robert nó Bob Marley a "
"aisghabháil má tá ceachtar acu ann, agus an dara ceann a chruthú ar shlí "
"eile:"

msgid ""
"If multiple objects are found, ``get_or_create()`` "
"raises :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.MultipleObjectsReturned`. If an object "
"is *not* found, ``get_or_create()`` will instantiate and save a new object, "
"returning a tuple of the new object and ``True``. The new object will be "
"created roughly according to this algorithm::"
msgstr ""
"Má aimsítear rudaí iolracha, ardaíonn ``get_or_create () `:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.multipleObjectsReturned`. Má aimsítear réad *ní "
"fhaightear, déanfaidh `get_or_create () ``réad nua a thabhairt isteach agus "
"a shábháil, ag tabhairt tuple den réad nua agus ``True`` ar ais. Cruthófar "
"an réad nua go garbh de réir an algartam seo:"

msgid ""
"In English, that means start with any non-``'defaults'`` keyword argument "
"that doesn't contain a double underscore (which would indicate a non-exact "
"lookup). Then add the contents of ``defaults``, overriding any keys if "
"necessary, and use the result as the keyword arguments to the model class. "
"If there are any callables in ``defaults``, evaluate them. As hinted at "
"above, this is a simplification of the algorithm that is used, but it "
"contains all the pertinent details. The internal implementation has some "
"more error-checking than this and handles some extra edge-conditions; if "
"you're interested, read the code."
msgstr ""
"I mBéarla, ciallaíonn sé sin tosú le haon argóint eochairfhocal neamh-"
"``defaults`` nach bhfuil béim dhúbailte ann (a chuirfeadh le fios cuardach "
"neamhchruinn). Ansin cuir ábhar `defaults``, ag cur aon eochracha a shárú "
"más gá, agus bain úsáid as an toradh mar na hargóintí eochairfhocal chuig an "
"rang samhail. Má tá aon ghlaonna in ``defaults``, déan meastóireacht orthu. "
"Mar a thuairiscítear thuas, is simplíocht é seo ar an algartam a úsáidtear, "
"ach tá na sonraí ábhartha go léir ann. Tá níos mó seiceála earráidí ag an "
"gcur i bhfeidhm inmheánach ná seo agus láimhseálann sé roinnt coinníollacha "
"imeall breise; má tá suim agat, léigh an cód."

msgid ""
"If you have a field named ``defaults`` and want to use it as an exact lookup "
"in ``get_or_create()``, use ``'defaults__exact'``, like so::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá réimse agat darb ainm ``defaults`` agus má theastaíonn uait é a úsáid "
"mar chuardach cruinn i ``get_or_create () ``, bain úsáid as "
"``'defaults__exact'``, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"The ``get_or_create()`` method has similar error behavior "
"to :meth:`create()` when you're using manually specified primary keys. If an "
"object needs to be created and the key already exists in the database, "
"an :exc:`~django.db.IntegrityError` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Tá iompar earráide comhchosúil ag an modh ``get_or_create () ``leas:meth: "
"`create () `nuair a bhíonn eochracha bunscoile sonraithe de láimh á úsáid "
"agat. Más gá réad a chruthú agus má tá an eochair ann cheana sa bhunachar "
"sonraí, ardófar an:exc: `~django.db.IntegrityError`."

msgid ""
"Finally, a word on using ``get_or_create()`` in Django views. Please make "
"sure to use it only in ``POST`` requests unless you have a good reason not "
"to. ``GET`` requests shouldn't have any effect on data. Instead, use "
"``POST`` whenever a request to a page has a side effect on your data. For "
"more, see :rfc:`Safe methods <9110#section-9.2.1>` in the HTTP spec."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, focal maidir le ``get_or_create () ``a úsáid i dtuairimí "
"Django. Déan cinnte go n-úsáidfidh tú é ach amháin in iarratais ``POST "
"``mura bhfuil cúis mhaith agat gan a dhéanamh. Níor cheart go mbeadh aon "
"éifeacht ag iarratais ``GET`` ar shonraí. Ina áit sin, bain úsáid as `POST "
"``aon uair a bhíonn fo-éifeacht ag iarraidh ar leathanach ar do chuid "
"sonraí. <9110 #section -9.2.1>Le haghaidh tuilleadh, féach: rfc: `Modhanna "
"sábháilte' sa shonraíocht HTTP."

msgid ""
"You can use ``get_or_create()`` "
"through :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` attributes and reverse "
"relations. In that case you will restrict the queries inside the context of "
"that relation. That could lead you to some integrity problems if you don't "
"use it consistently."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat tréithe ``get_or_create () ``a úsáid trí:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField` agus caidreamh aisiompthe. Sa chás sin "
"cuirfidh tú srian ar na ceisteanna taobh istigh de chomhthéacs an chaidrimh "
"sin. D'fhéadfadh sé sin roinnt fadhbanna sláine a bheith mar thoradh ort "
"mura n-úsáideann tú é go comhsheasmhach."

msgid "Being the following models::"
msgstr "Mar na samhlacha seo a leanas::"

