"You can use ``get_or_create()`` through Book's chapters field, but it only "
"fetches inside the context of that book:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``get_or_create () ``a úsáid trí réimse caibidlí an Leabhair, "
"ach ní fhaigheann sé ach taobh istigh de chomhthéacs an leabhair sin:"

msgid ""
"This is happening because it's trying to get or create \"Chapter 1\" through "
"the book \"Ulysses\", but it can't do either: the relation can't fetch that "
"chapter because it isn't related to that book, but it can't create it either "
"because ``title`` field should be unique."
msgstr ""

msgid "``update_or_create()``"
msgstr "``Update_or_create () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aupdate_or_create()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aupdate_or_create () ``"

msgid ""
"A convenience method for updating an object with the given ``kwargs``, "
"creating a new one if necessary. Both ``create_defaults`` and ``defaults`` "
"are dictionaries of (field, value) pairs. The values in both "
"``create_defaults`` and ``defaults`` can be callables. ``defaults`` is used "
"to update the object while ``create_defaults`` are used for the create "
"operation. If ``create_defaults`` is not supplied, ``defaults`` will be used "
"for the create operation."
msgstr ""
"Modh áisiúlachta chun réad a nuashonrú leis an `kwargs ``tugtha, ceann nua a "
"chruthú más gá. Is foclóirí de phéirí (réimse, luach) iad `create_defaults`` "
"agus `defaults`` araon. Is féidir na luachanna i `create_defaults`` agus "
"`defaults`` araon a bheith inghlaonta. Úsáidtear ``defaults`` chun an réad a "
"nuashonrú agus úsáidtear ``create_defaults`` don oibríocht chruthaigh. Mura "
"gcuirtear `create_defaults`` ar fáil, úsáidfear ``defaults`` don oibríocht "
"chruthaithe."

msgid ""
"Returns a tuple of ``(object, created)``, where ``object`` is the created or "
"updated object and ``created`` is a boolean specifying whether a new object "
"was created."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé tuple de ``(réad, cruthaithe)``, ina bhfuil ``réad ``an rud "
"cruthaithe nó nuashonraithe agus is boolean é ``cruthaithe`` a shonraíonn an "
"cruthaíodh réad nua."

msgid ""
"The ``update_or_create`` method tries to fetch an object from database based "
"on the given ``kwargs``. If a match is found, it updates the fields passed "
"in the ``defaults`` dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an modh `update_or_create`` iarracht réad a fháil ón mbunachar "
"sonraí bunaithe ar an `kwargs ``tugtha. Má aimsítear meaitseáil, "
"nuashonraíonn sé na réimsí a rith sa fhoclóir ``defaults`."

msgid "This is meant as a shortcut to boilerplatish code. For example::"
msgstr "Tá sé seo i gceist mar aicearra chuig cód boilerplatish. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"This pattern gets quite unwieldy as the number of fields in a model goes up. "
"The above example can be rewritten using ``update_or_create()`` like so::"
msgstr ""
"Éiríonn an patrún seo go leor de réir mar a théann líon na réimsí i samhail "
"suas. Is féidir an sampla thuas a athscríobh ag baint úsáide as "
"``update_or_create () ``mar sin:"

msgid ""
"For a detailed description of how names passed in ``kwargs`` are resolved, "
"see :meth:`get_or_create`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuairisc mhionsonraithe ar an gcaoi a réitear ainmneacha a rith "
"in `kwargs``, féach:meth: `get_or_create`."

msgid ""
"As described above in :meth:`get_or_create`, this method is prone to a race-"
"condition which can result in multiple rows being inserted simultaneously if "
"uniqueness is not enforced at the database level."
msgstr ""
"Mar a thuairiscítear thuas in:meth: `get_or_create`, tá seans go mbeidh "
"coinníoll rásaíochta ag an modh seo a d'fhéadfadh sraitheanna iolracha a "
"chur isteach ag an am céanna mura gcuirtear uathúlacht i bhfeidhm ag "
"leibhéal an bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`get_or_create` and :meth:`create`, if you're using manually "
"specified primary keys and an object needs to be created but the key already "
"exists in the database, an :exc:`~django.db.IntegrityError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `get_or_create` agus:meth: `create`, má tá eochracha "
"bunscoile sonraithe de láimh á úsáid agat agus má chaithfear réad a chruthú "
"ach tá an eochair ann cheana sa bhunachar sonraí, an:exc: "
"`~django.db.IntegrityError` ardaítear."

msgid "``bulk_create()``"
msgstr "``bulk_create () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``abulk_create()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``abulk_create () ``"

msgid ""
"This method inserts the provided list of objects into the database in an "
"efficient manner (generally only 1 query, no matter how many objects there "
"are), and returns created objects as a list, in the same order as provided:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an modh seo an liosta rudaí a chuirtear ar fáil isteach sa "
"bhunachar sonraí ar bhealach éifeachtach (de ghnáth ní amháin ceist amháin, "
"is cuma cé mhéad rudaí atá ann), agus tugann sé rudaí cruthaithe ar ais mar "
"liosta, san ord céanna mar a chuirtear ar fáil:"

msgid "This has a number of caveats though:"
msgstr "Tá roinnt rabhaidh aige seo áfach:"

msgid ""
"The model's ``save()`` method will not be called, and the ``pre_save`` and "
"``post_save`` signals will not be sent."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlaofar modh ``save () ``an tsamhail, agus ní sheolfar na comharthaí "
"``pre_save`` agus ``post_save``."

msgid ""
"It does not work with child models in a multi-table inheritance scenario."
msgstr "Ní oibríonn sé le samhlacha leanaí i gcás oidhreachta il-tábla."

msgid ""
"If the model's primary key is an :class:`~django.db.models.AutoField` and "
"``ignore_conflicts`` is False, the primary key attribute can only be "
"retrieved on certain databases (currently PostgreSQL, MariaDB, and SQLite "
"3.35+). On other databases, it will not be set."
msgstr ""
"Más é príomh-eochair an tsamhail ná: class: `~django.db.models.autofield` "
"agus ``ignore_conflicts`` False, ní féidir an príomh-thréith a aisghabháil "
"ach ar bhunachair sonraí áirithe (PostgreSQL, MariaDB, agus SQLite 3.35+ "
"faoi láthair). Ar bhunachair sonraí eile, ní shocrófar é."

msgid "It does not work with many-to-many relationships."
msgstr "Ní oibríonn sé le caidrimh go leor."

msgid ""
"It casts ``objs`` to a list, which fully evaluates ``objs`` if it's a "
"generator. The cast allows inspecting all objects so that any objects with a "
"manually set primary key can be inserted first. If you want to insert "
"objects in batches without evaluating the entire generator at once, you can "
"use this technique as long as the objects don't have any manually set "
"primary keys::"
msgstr ""
"Caitheann sé ``objs`` chuig liosta, a dhéanann meastóireacht iomlán ar "
"``objs`` más gineadóir é. Ligeann an teilgthe gach rud a iniúchadh ionas gur "
"féidir aon rudaí a bhfuil eochair phríomhúil socraithe de láimh acu a chur "
"isteach ar dtús. Más mian leat rudaí a chur isteach i mbaisceanna gan an "
"gineadóir iomlán a mheas ag an am céanna, is féidir leat an teicníc seo a "
"úsáid chomh fada agus nach bhfuil aon eochracha bunscoile socraithe de láimh "
"ag na rudaí::"

msgid ""
"The ``batch_size`` parameter controls how many objects are created in a "
"single query. The default is to create as many objects in one batch as the "
"database will allow. (SQLite and Oracle limit the number of parameters in a "
"query.)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On databases that support it (all but Oracle), setting the "
"``ignore_conflicts`` parameter to ``True`` tells the database to ignore "
"failure to insert any rows that fail constraints such as duplicate unique "
"values."
msgstr ""
"Ar bhunachair sonraí a thacaíonn leis (uile ach Oracle), deir an paraiméadar "
"`ignore_conflicts`` a shocrú go ``True`` don bhunachar sonraí neamhaird a "
"dhéanamh ar theip ar aon sraitheanna a chur isteach ina theipeann srianta "
"mar luachanna uathúla dúbailte."

msgid ""
"On databases that support it (all except Oracle), setting the "
"``update_conflicts`` parameter to ``True``, tells the database to update "
"``update_fields`` when a row insertion fails on conflicts. On PostgreSQL and "
"SQLite, in addition to ``update_fields``, a list of ``unique_fields`` that "
"may be in conflict must be provided."
msgstr ""
"Ar bhunachair sonraí a thacaíonn leis (uile seachas Oracle), ag socrú an "
"paraiméadar ``update_conflicts`` go `True``, insíonn don bhunachar sonraí "
"``update_fields`` a nuashonrú nuair a theipeann ar ionchur sraith ar "
"choimhlintí. Ar PostgreSQL agus SQLite, i dteannta le `update_fields``, ní "
"mór liosta de ``unique_fields`` a d'fhéadfadh a bheith i gcoinbhleacht a "
"sholáthar."

msgid ""
"Enabling the ``ignore_conflicts`` parameter disables setting the primary key "
"on each model instance (if the database normally supports it)."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an paraiméadar `ignore_conflicts`` a chumasú ar an bpríomh-eochair a "
"shocrú ar gach samhail (má thacaíonn an bunachar sonraí leis de ghnáth)."

msgid ""
"On MySQL and MariaDB, setting the ``ignore_conflicts`` parameter to ``True`` "
"turns certain types of errors, other than duplicate key, into warnings. Even "
"with Strict Mode. For example: invalid values or non-nullable violations. "
"See the `MySQL documentation`_ and `MariaDB documentation`_ for more details."
msgstr ""
"Ar MySQL agus MariaDB, déanann an paraiméadar `ignore_conflicts`` a shocrú "
"go ``True``, iompaíonn cineálacha áirithe earráidí, seachas eochair "
"dúbailte, ina rabhaidh. Fiú amháin le Mód Dian. Mar shampla: luachanna "
"neamhbhailí nó sáruithe neamh-inneamhnaithe. Féach an `doiciméadú MySQL `_ "
"agus `doiciméadú MariaDB `_ le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``bulk_update()``"
msgstr "``bulk_update () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``abulk_update()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``abulk_update () ``"

msgid ""
"This method efficiently updates the given fields on the provided model "
"instances, generally with one query, and returns the number of objects "
"updated:"
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraíonn an modh seo na réimsí tugtha go héifeachtúil ar na cásanna "
"samhail a chuirtear ar fáil, go ginearálta le ceist amháin, agus filleann sé "
"líon na ruda"

msgid ""
":meth:`.QuerySet.update` is used to save the changes, so this is more "
"efficient than iterating through the list of models and calling ``save()`` "
"on each of them, but it has a few caveats:"
msgstr ""
": meth: Úsáidtear `.querySet.Update` chun na hathruithe a shábháil, mar sin "
"tá sé seo níos éifeachtaí ná athrú tríd an liosta samhlacha agus glaoch ar "
"`save () `ar gach ceann acu, ach tá cúpla rabhadh aige:"

msgid "You cannot update the model's primary key."
msgstr "Ní féidir leat príomh-eochair an tsamhail a nuashonrú."

msgid ""
"Each model's ``save()`` method isn't called, and "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` "
"and :attr:`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` signals aren't sent."
msgstr ""
"Ní thugtar ar mhodh `save () ``gach samhail, agus ní sheoltar na comharthaí: "
"attr: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` agus:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.post_save`."

msgid ""
"If updating a large number of columns in a large number of rows, the SQL "
"generated can be very large. Avoid this by specifying a suitable "
"``batch_size``."
msgstr ""
"Má nuashonraítear líon mór colúin i líon mór sraitheanna, is féidir leis an "
"SQL a ghintear a bheith an-mhór. Seachain é seo trí `batch_size`` oiriúnach "
"a shonrú."

msgid ""
"When updating a large number of objects, be aware that ``bulk_update()`` "
"prepares all of the ``WHEN`` clauses for every object across all batches "
"before executing any queries. This can require more memory than expected. To "
"reduce memory usage, you can use an approach like this::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Updating fields defined on multi-table inheritance ancestors will incur an "
"extra query per ancestor."
msgstr ""
"Beidh ceist bhreise in aghaidh an sinsear ag nuashonrú réimsí a "
"shainmhínítear ar sinsear oidhreachta"

msgid ""
"When an individual batch contains duplicates, only the first instance in "
"that batch will result in an update."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn dúbailtí i mbaisc aonair, ní bheidh nuashonrú mar thoradh ar "
"an gcéad chás sa bhaisc sin."

msgid ""
"The number of objects updated returned by the function may be fewer than the "
"number of objects passed in. This can be due to duplicate objects passed in "
"which are updated in the same batch or race conditions such that objects are "
"no longer present in the database."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh líon na rudaí a nuashonraíonn an fheidhm ar ais níos "
"lú ná líon na rudaí a chuirtear isteach. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith mar "
"gheall ar rudaí dúblacha a rith ina ndéantar nuashonrú sna dálaí baisc nó "
"cine céanna ionas nach bhfuil rudaí i láthair sa bhunachar sonraí a "
"thuilleadh."

msgid ""
"The ``batch_size`` parameter controls how many objects are saved in a single "
"query. The default is to update all objects in one batch, except for SQLite "
"and Oracle which have restrictions on the number of variables used in a "
"query."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an paraiméadar ``batch_size`` cé mhéad rudaí a shábháiltear in aon "
"cheist amháin. Is é an réamhshocrú ná gach rud a nuashonrú i mbaisc amháin, "
"ach amháin SQLite agus Oracle a bhfuil srianta acu ar líon na n-athróg a "
"úsáidtear i gceist."

msgid "``count()``"
msgstr "``comhaireamh () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``acount()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``acount () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns an integer representing the number of objects in the database "
"matching the ``QuerySet``."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé sláimhir a léiríonn líon na rudaí sa bhunachar sonraí a "
"mheaitseann leis an ``QuerySet``."

msgid ""
"A ``count()`` call performs a ``SELECT COUNT(*)`` behind the scenes, so you "
"should always use ``count()`` rather than loading all of the record into "
"Python objects and calling ``len()`` on the result (unless you need to load "
"the objects into memory anyway, in which case ``len()`` will be faster)."
msgstr ""
"Déanann glao ``count () ```SELECT COUNT (*)`` taobh thiar de na radhairc, "
"mar sin ba chóir duit ``count () ``a úsáid i gcónaí seachas an taifead go "
"léir a luchtú isteach i rudaí Python agus glaoch ar `len ()`` ar an toradh "
"(mura gcaithfidh tú na rudaí a luchtú i gcuimhne ar aon nós, sa chás sin "
"beidh `len () ``níos gasta)."

msgid ""
"Note that if you want the number of items in a ``QuerySet`` and are also "
"retrieving model instances from it (for example, by iterating over it), it's "
"probably more efficient to use ``len(queryset)`` which won't cause an extra "
"database query like ``count()`` would."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara más mian leat líon na míreanna i ``QuerySet`` agus má tá "
"tú ag aisghabháil cásanna samhail uaidh freisin (mar shampla, trí athrú "
"air), is dócha go mbeidh sé níos éifeachtaí ``len (queryset) ``a úsáid nach "
"gcuirfidh ceist bunachar sonraí breise mar ``count ()``."

msgid ""
"If the queryset has already been fully retrieved, ``count()`` will use that "
"length rather than perform an extra database query."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an tacar ceisteanna aisghabháilte go hiomlán cheana féin, úsáidfidh "
"``count () ``an fad sin seachas ceist breise bunachar sonraí a dhéanamh."

msgid "``in_bulk()``"
msgstr "``in_bulk () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``ain_bulk()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``ain_bulk () ``"

msgid ""
"Takes a list of field values (``id_list``) and the ``field_name`` for those "
"values, and returns a dictionary mapping each value to an instance of the "
"object with the given field value. "
"No :exc:`django.core.exceptions.ObjectDoesNotExist` exceptions will ever be "
"raised by ``in_bulk``; that is, any ``id_list`` value not matching any "
"instance will simply be ignored. If ``id_list`` isn't provided, all objects "
"in the queryset are returned. ``field_name`` must be a unique field or a "
"distinct field (if there's only one field specified in :meth:`distinct`). "
"``field_name`` defaults to the primary key."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé liosta de luachanna réimse (``id_list``) agus an ``field_name`` "
"do na luachanna sin, agus filleann sé foclóir a mhapáil gach luach go sampla "
"den réad leis an luach réimse a thugtar. No:exc: Ardóidh eisceachtaí "
"`django.core.exceptions.objectDoesNotExist` riamh le ``in_bulk``; is é sin, "
"ní dhéanfar neamhaird ar aon luach ``id_list`` nach bhfuil meaitseáil le "
"haon chás. Mura gcuirtear ``id_list`` ar fáil, cuirtear gach rud sa tacar "
"fiosrúcháin ar ais. Caithfidh `field_name`` a bheith ina réimse uathúil nó "
"ina réimse ar leith (mura bhfuil ach réimse amháin ann a shonraítear "
"in:meth: `distint`). Réamhshocraíonn ``field_name`` don eochair phríomhúil."

msgid ""
"If you pass ``in_bulk()`` an empty list, you'll get an empty dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú liosta folamh ar ``in_bulk () ``, gheobhaidh tú foclóir "
"folamh."

msgid "``iterator()``"
msgstr "``iterator () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aiterator()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``aiterator () ``"

msgid ""
"Evaluates the ``QuerySet`` (by performing the query) and returns an iterator "
"(see :pep:`234`) over the results, or an asynchronous iterator "
"(see :pep:`492`) if you call its asynchronous version ``aiterator``."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé meastóireacht ar an ``QuerySet`` (tríd an bhfiosrú a dhéanamh) "
"agus filleann sé athraitheoir (féach: pep: `234`) thar na torthaí, nó "
"athraitheoir asincrónach (féach: pep: `492`) má ghlaonn tú ar a leagan "
"asincrónach ``aiterator``."

msgid ""
"A ``QuerySet`` typically caches its results internally so that repeated "
"evaluations do not result in additional queries. In contrast, ``iterator()`` "
"will read results directly, without doing any caching at the ``QuerySet`` "
"level (internally, the default iterator calls ``iterator()`` and caches the "
"return value). For a ``QuerySet`` which returns a large number of objects "
"that you only need to access once, this can result in better performance and "
"a significant reduction in memory."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth cuireann “QuerySet” a thorthaí a chosc go hinmheánach ionas nach "
"mbíonn ceisteanna breise mar thoradh ar mheastóireachtaí arís agus arís "
"eile. I gcodarsnacht leis sin, léifidh ``iterator () ``torthaí go díreach, "
"gan aon chaching a dhéanamh ag an leibhéal ``QuerySet` (go hinmheánach, "
"glaonn an t-iterator réamhshocraithe ``iterator ()`` agus cuireann sé an "
"luach tuairisceáin). Maidir le ``QuerySet` a thugann líon mór rudaí ar ais "
"nach gá duit rochtain a fháil ach uair amháin, d'fhéadfadh feidhmíocht níos "
"fearr agus laghdú suntasach ar chuimhne a bheith mar thoradh air seo."

msgid ""
"Note that using ``iterator()`` on a ``QuerySet`` which has already been "
"evaluated will force it to evaluate again, repeating the query."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirfidh úsáid ``iterator () ``ar `QuerySet`` a "
"rinneadh meastóireacht cheana féin iallach air a mheas arís, ag athdhéanamh "
"an cheist."

msgid ""
"``iterator()`` is compatible with previous calls to ``prefetch_related()`` "
"as long as ``chunk_size`` is given. Larger values will necessitate fewer "
"queries to accomplish the prefetching at the cost of greater memory usage."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``iterator () ``comhoiriúnach le glaonna roimhe seo chuig "
"``prefetch_related ()`` fad is a thugtar ``chunk_size``. Beidh níos lú "
"ceisteanna ag teastáil ó luachanna níos mó chun an réamhghabháil a chur i "
"gcrích ar chostas níos mó úsáide cuimhne."

msgid ""
"On some databases (e.g. Oracle, `SQLite <https://www.sqlite.org/"
"limits.html#max_variable_number>`_), the maximum number of terms in an SQL "
"``IN`` clause might be limited. Hence values below this limit should be "
"used. (In particular, when prefetching across two or more relations, a "
"``chunk_size`` should be small enough that the anticipated number of results "
"for each prefetched relation still falls below the limit.)"
msgstr ""
"Ar roinnt bunachair sonraí (m.sh. Oracle, `SQLite`_ < https://www.sqlite.org/"
"limits.html#max_variable_number>), d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh uaslíon téarmaí i "
"gclásal SQL ``IN ``teoranta. Dá bhrí sin ba chóir luachanna faoi bhun an "
"teorainn seo a úsáid. (Go háirithe, nuair a bhíonn dhá chaidreamh nó níos mó "
"á réamhghabháil agat, ba chóir go mbeadh `chunk_size`` beag go leor go "
"dtitfidh an líon na dtorthaí a bhfuil súil leis do gach caidreamh "
"réamhfhaighte faoi bhun an teorainn fós.)"

msgid ""
"So long as the QuerySet does not prefetch any related objects, providing no "
"value for ``chunk_size`` will result in Django using an implicit default of "
"2000."
msgstr ""
"Chomh fada agus nach bhfaigheann an QuerySet aon rudaí gaolmhara roimh ré, "
"ní úsáidfidh Django réamhshocrú intuigthe 2000 mar thoradh ar aon luach a "
"sholáthar do `chunk_size``."

msgid ""
"Depending on the database backend, query results will either be loaded all "
"at once or streamed from the database using server-side cursors."
msgstr ""
"Ag brath ar chúlcheann an bhunachar sonraí, luchtálfar torthaí fiosrúcháin "
"uile ag an am céanna nó a shruthú ón mbunachar sonraí ag baint úsáide as "
"cúrsóirí taobh an fhre"

msgid "With server-side cursors"
msgstr "Le cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"Oracle and :ref:`PostgreSQL <postgresql-server-side-cursors>` use server-"
"side cursors to stream results from the database without loading the entire "
"result set into memory."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Oracle agus:ref: `PostgreSQL <postgresql-server-side-"
"cursors>`cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí chun torthaí a shruthlú ón mbunachar "
"sonraí gan an tacar toradh iomlán a luchtú isteach i gcuimhne."

msgid "The Oracle database driver always uses server-side cursors."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann tiománaí bunachar sonraí Oracle cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"With server-side cursors, the ``chunk_size`` parameter specifies the number "
"of results to cache at the database driver level. Fetching bigger chunks "
"diminishes the number of round trips between the database driver and the "
"database, at the expense of memory."
msgstr ""
"Le cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí, sonraíonn an paraiméadar ``chunk_size`` "
"líon na dtorthaí le taisce ag leibhéal tiománaí an bhunachar sonraí. "
"Laghdaíonn píosaí níos mó a fháil líon na dturais babhta idir tiománaí an "
"bhunachar sonraí agus an bunachar sonraí, ar chostas na cuimhne."

msgid ""
"On PostgreSQL, server-side cursors will only be used when "
"the :setting:`DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS <DATABASE-"
"DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS>` setting is ``False``. Read :ref:`transaction-"
"pooling-server-side-cursors` if you're using a connection pooler configured "
"in transaction pooling mode. When server-side cursors are disabled, the "
"behavior is the same as databases that don't support server-side cursors."
msgstr ""
"<DATABASE-DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS>Ar PostgreSQL, ní úsáidfear cúrsóirí "
"taobh an fhreastalaí ach nuair is é an socrú: setting: "
"`DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS ``False``. léitheo:ref: `transaction-pooling-"
"server-side-cursors` má tá poiblí nasc á úsáid agat atá cumraithe i mód "
"comhionannaithe idirbheart. Nuair a dhéantar cúrsóirí taobh an fhreastalaí a "
"dhíchumasú, tá an t-iompar mar an gcéanna le bunachair sonraí nach dtacaíonn "
"le cúrsóirí taobh an f"

msgid "Without server-side cursors"
msgstr "Gan cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí"

msgid ""
"MySQL doesn't support streaming results, hence the Python database driver "
"loads the entire result set into memory. The result set is then transformed "
"into Python row objects by the database adapter using the ``fetchmany()`` "
"method defined in :pep:`249`."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn MySQL le torthaí sruthú, dá bhrí sin luchtaíonn tiománaí "
"bunachar sonraí Python an toradh iomlán atá leagtha síos Ansin déantar an "
"tacar torthaí a athrú go rudaí sraithe Python ag an oiriúnaitheoir bunachar "
"sonraí ag baint úsáide as an modh ``fetchmany () ``atá sainmhínithe in:pep: "
"`249`."

msgid ""
"SQLite can fetch results in batches using ``fetchmany()``, but since SQLite "
"doesn't provide isolation between queries within a connection, be careful "
"when writing to the table being iterated over. See :ref:`sqlite-isolation` "
"for more information."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le SQLite torthaí a fháil i mbaisceanna ag baint úsáide as "
"``fetchmany () ``, ach ós rud é nach soláthraíonn SQLite aonrú idir "
"ceisteanna laistigh de nasc, bí cúramach agus tú ag scríobh chuig an tábla "
"atá á athrá. Féach: ref: `sqlite-isolation` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"The ``chunk_size`` parameter controls the size of batches Django retrieves "
"from the database driver. Larger batches decrease the overhead of "
"communicating with the database driver at the expense of a slight increase "
"in memory consumption."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an paraiméadar ``chunk_size`` méid na mbaisceanna a aisghabhann "
"Django ón tiománaí bunachar sonraí. Laghdaíonn baisceanna níos mó lasbhaird "
"cumarsáide leis an tiománaí bunachar sonraí ar chostas méadú beag ar "
"thomhaltas cuimhne."

msgid ""
"So long as the QuerySet does not prefetch any related objects, providing no "
"value for ``chunk_size`` will result in Django using an implicit default of "
"2000, a value derived from `a calculation on the psycopg mailing list "
"<https://www.postgresql.org/message-id/4D2F2C71.8080805%40dndg.it>`_:"
msgstr ""
"< https://www.postgresql.org/message-id/4D2F2C71.8080805%40dndg.it>Chomh "
"fada agus nach bhfaigheann an QuerySet aon rudaí gaolmhara roimh ré, ní "
"sholáthraíonn aon luach do `chunk_size`` mar thoradh ar Django réamhshocrú "
"intuigthe de 2000, luach a dhíorthaítear ó `ríomh ar an liosta seoltaí "
"psycopg`_:"

msgid ""
"Assuming rows of 10-20 columns with a mix of textual and numeric data, 2000 "
"is going to fetch less than 100KB of data, which seems a good compromise "
"between the number of rows transferred and the data discarded if the loop is "
"exited early."
msgstr ""
"Ag glacadh leis sraitheanna de 10-20 colún le meascán de shonraí téacsúla "
"agus uimhriúla, tá 2000 chun níos lú ná 100KB sonraí a fháil, rud is cosúil "
"gur comhréiteach maith é idir líon na sraitheanna a aistrítear agus na "
"sonraí a scriosadh má imeádtar an lúb go luath."

msgid "``latest()``"
msgstr "``is déanaí () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``alatest()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``alatest () ``"

msgid "Returns the latest object in the table based on the given field(s)."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an réad is déanaí sa tábla ar ais bunaithe ar na réimsí (í) ar "
"leith."

msgid ""
"This example returns the latest ``Entry`` in the table, according to the "
"``pub_date`` field::"
msgstr ""
"Tugann an sampla seo an `Entry`` is déanaí sa tábla, de réir réimse "
"``pub_date``:"

msgid ""
"You can also choose the latest based on several fields. For example, to "
"select the ``Entry`` with the earliest ``expire_date`` when two entries have "
"the same ``pub_date``::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an ceann is déanaí a roghnú bunaithe ar roinnt réimsí. Mar "
"shampla, chun an `Entry`` a roghnú leis an ``expire_date`` is luaithe nuair "
"a bhíonn an `pub_date`` céanna ag dhá iontráil:"

msgid ""
"The negative sign in ``'-expire_date'`` means to sort ``expire_date`` in "
"*descending* order. Since ``latest()`` gets the last result, the ``Entry`` "
"with the earliest ``expire_date`` is selected."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn an comhartha diúltach in ```'-expire_date'` ``dáta deighilte`` a "
"shórtáil san ordú*downing*. Ós rud é go bhfaigheann ``latest () ``an toradh "
"deireanach, roghnaítear an ``Entry`` leis an ``expire_date`` is luaithe."

msgid ""
"If your model's :ref:`Meta <meta-options>` "
"specifies :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.get_latest_by`, you can omit any "
"arguments to ``earliest()`` or ``latest()``. The fields specified "
"in :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.get_latest_by` will be used by default."
msgstr ""
"Má shonraíonn do mhúnlaí:ref: `Meta <meta-options>`: attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.get_latest_by`, is féidir leat aon argóintí a "
"fhágáil go ``early () ``nó ``latest ()``. Úsáidfear na réimsí a shonraítear "
"in:attr: `~django.db.models.options.get_latest_by` de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`get()`, ``earliest()`` and ``latest()`` "
"raise :exc:`~django.db.models.Model.DoesNotExist` if there is no object with "
"the given parameters."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `get () `, ``() ``agus ``latest ()`` 'ardaithe:exc: "
"`~django.db.models.model.doesNotExist` mura bhfuil aon rud ann leis na "
"paraiméadair a thugtar."

msgid ""
"Note that ``earliest()`` and ``latest()`` exist purely for convenience and "
"readability."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil ``is luaithe () ``agus ``is déanaí ()`` ann ach "
"ar mhaithe le háisiúlacht agus inléiteacht."

msgid "``earliest()`` and ``latest()`` may return instances with null dates."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh ```is luaithe () ``agus ``latest ()`` cásanna a thabhairt ar ais "
"le dátaí neall."

msgid ""
"Since ordering is delegated to the database, results on fields that allow "
"null values may be ordered differently if you use different databases. For "
"example, PostgreSQL and MySQL sort null values as if they are higher than "
"non-null values, while SQLite does the opposite."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go ndéantar ordú a tharmligtear chuig an mbunachar sonraí, féadfar "
"torthaí ar réimsí a cheadaíonn luachanna neall a ordú ar bhealach difriúil "
"Mar shampla, déanann PostgreSQL agus MySQL luachanna null a shórtáil amhail "
"is dá mbeadh siad níos airde ná luachanna neamh-niall, agus déanann SQLite a "
"mhalairt."

msgid "You may want to filter out null values::"
msgstr "B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat luachanna null a scagadh amach::"

msgid "``earliest()``"
msgstr "``is luaithe () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aearliest()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aearly () ``"

msgid ""
"Works otherwise like :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.latest` except "
"the direction is changed."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sé ar shlí eile cosúil:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.latest` ach amháin go n-athraítear an treo."

msgid "``first()``"
msgstr "```chéad () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``afirst()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ```first () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns the first object matched by the queryset, or ``None`` if there is no "
"matching object. If the ``QuerySet`` has no ordering defined, then the "
"queryset is automatically ordered by the primary key. This can affect "
"aggregation results as described in :ref:`aggregation-ordering-interaction`."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an chéad réad a mheaitseáil leis an tacar fiosrúcháin, nó "
"``None`` mura bhfuil aon rud meaitseála ann. Mura bhfuil aon ordú "
"sainmhínithe ag an ``QuerySet`, ansin ordaítear an tacar fiosrúcháin go "
"huathoibríoch ag an eochair phríomhúil. Féadfaidh sé seo dul i bhfeidhm ar "
"thorthaí comhiomlánaithe mar a thuairiscítear in:ref: `comhiomlán-ordú-"
"idirghníomhach"

msgid ""
"Note that ``first()`` is a convenience method, the following code sample is "
"equivalent to the above example::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur modh áisiúlachta é ``first () `, tá an sampla cód seo "
"a leanas comhionann leis an sampla thuas:"

msgid "``last()``"
msgstr "```deireanach () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``alast()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``alast () ``"

msgid ""
"Works like  :meth:`first()`, but returns the last object in the queryset."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sé cosúil le: meth: `first () `, ach filleann sé an rud deireanach "
"sa tacar ceisteanna."

msgid "``aggregate()``"
msgstr "``comhiomlán () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aaggregate()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aaggregate () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns a dictionary of aggregate values (averages, sums, etc.) calculated "
"over the ``QuerySet``. Each argument to ``aggregate()`` specifies a value "
"that will be included in the dictionary that is returned."
msgstr ""
"Tugann foclóir ar ais de luachanna comhiomlána (meáin, suimeanna, srl.) arna "
"ríomh thar an ``QuerySet`. Sonraíonn gach argóint le ``comhiomlán () ``luach "
"a chuirfear san áireamh sa fhoclóir a thugtar ar ais."

msgid ""
"The aggregation functions that are provided by Django are described in "
"`Aggregation Functions`_ below. Since aggregates are also :doc:`query "
"expressions </ref/models/expressions>`, you may combine aggregates with "
"other aggregates or values to create complex aggregates."
msgstr ""
"Déantar cur síos ar na feidhmeanna comhiomlánaithe a sholáthraíonn Django i "
"`Feidhmeanna Comhiomlánacha`_ thíos. Ós rud é go bhfuil comhiomlánaithe "
"freis:doc: `léirithe fiosraithe', féadfaidh tú comhiomláin a chomhcheangal "
"le comhiomlán</ref/models/expressions> acha nó luachanna eile chun "
"comhiomlánacha casta a chruthú."

msgid ""
"Aggregates specified using keyword arguments will use the keyword as the "
"name for the annotation. Anonymous arguments will have a name generated for "
"them based upon the name of the aggregate function and the model field that "
"is being aggregated. Complex aggregates cannot use anonymous arguments and "
"must specify a keyword argument as an alias."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfidh comhiomlánaithe a shonraítear ag úsáid argóintí eochairfhocal an "
"eochairfhocal mar ainm don anótáil Beidh ainm ag argóintí gan ainm a "
"ghintear dóibh bunaithe ar ainm na feidhme chomhiomlán agus ar an réimse "
"samhail atá á chomhiomlánú. Ní féidir le comhiomlánaithe casta argóintí gan "
"ainm a úsáid agus ní mór argóint eochairfhocal a shonrú mar ailias"

msgid ""
"For example, when you are working with blog entries, you may want to know "
"the number of authors that have contributed blog entries:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, nuair a bhíonn tú ag obair le hiontrálacha blag, b'fhéidir gur "
"mhaith leat a fháil amach líon na n-údar a chuir iontrálacha blag leis:"

msgid ""
"By using a keyword argument to specify the aggregate function, you can "
"control the name of the aggregation value that is returned:"
msgstr ""
"Trí argóint eochairfhocal a úsáid chun an fheidhm chomhiomlán a shonrú, is "
"féidir leat ainm an luach comhiomlánaithe a chuirtear ar ais a rialú:"

msgid "``exists()``"
msgstr "``ann () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aexists()``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aexists () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the :class:`.QuerySet` contains any results, and "
"``False`` if not. This tries to perform the query in the simplest and "
"fastest way possible, but it *does* execute nearly the same query as a "
"normal :class:`.QuerySet` query."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ``True`` má tá aon torthaí an:class: `.QuerySet`, agus ``False`` "
"mura bhfuil. Déanann sé seo iarracht an cheist a dhéanamh ar an mbealach is "
"simplí agus is gasta is féidir, ach déanann sé* beagnach an cheist céanna a "
"fhorghníomhú le fiosrúchán gnáth:class: `.querySet`."

msgid ""
":meth:`~.QuerySet.exists` is useful for searches relating to the existence "
"of any objects in a :class:`.QuerySet`, particularly in the context of a "
"large :class:`.QuerySet`."
msgstr ""
":meth: `~.queryset.exists` úsáideach le haghaidh cuardaigh a bhaineann le "
"bheith ann aon rudaí in a:class: `.QuerySet`, go háirithe i gcomhthéacs "
"mór:class: `.QuerySet`."

msgid "To find whether a queryset contains any items::"
msgstr "Chun a fháil amach an bhfuil aon earraí i tacar fiosrúcháin:"

msgid "Which will be faster than::"
msgstr "Cé a bheidh níos gasta ná:"

msgid ""
"... but not by a large degree (hence needing a large queryset for efficiency "
"gains)."
msgstr ""
"... ach ní ar leibhéal mór (dá bhrí sin teastaíonn tacar fiosrúcháin mór "
"uait le haghaidh gnóthachain éifeachtúlachta)."

msgid ""
"Additionally, if a ``some_queryset`` has not yet been evaluated, but you "
"know that it will be at some point, then using ``some_queryset.exists()`` "
"will do more overall work (one query for the existence check plus an extra "
"one to later retrieve the results) than using ``bool(some_queryset)``, which "
"retrieves the results and then checks if any were returned."
msgstr ""
"Ina theannta sin, mura ndearnadh meastóireacht ar `some_queryset`` fós, ach "
"tá a fhios agat go mbeidh sé ag pointe éigin, ansin déanfaidh "
"`some_queryset.exists () ``níos mó obair fhoriomlán (ceist amháin maidir "
"leis an seiceáil ann móide ceann breise chun na torthaí a aisghabháil níos "
"déanaí) ná `bool (some_queryset) `a úsáid, a aisghabhann na torthaí agus "
"ansin seiceálann an raibh aon cheann ann ar ais."

msgid "``contains()``"
msgstr "``tá ()``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``acontains()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``contains () ``"

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the :class:`.QuerySet` contains ``obj``, and ``False`` "
"if not. This tries to perform the query in the simplest and fastest way "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ``True`` má tá ``obj`` sa :class: `.QuerySet`, agus ``False`` mura "
"bhfuil. Déanann sé seo iarracht an cheist a dhéanamh ar an mbealach is "
"simplí agus is gasta is féidir."

msgid ""
":meth:`contains` is useful for checking an object membership in "
"a :class:`.QuerySet`, particularly in the context of a "
"large :class:`.QuerySet`."
msgstr ""
":meth: Tá `contains` úsáideach chun ballraíocht réad a sheiceáil in a:class: "
"`.QuerySet`, go háirithe i gcomhthéacs mór:class: `.QuerySet`."

msgid "To check whether a queryset contains a specific item::"
msgstr "Chun a sheiceáil an bhfuil mír ar leith i tacar fiosrúcháin:"

msgid ""
"This will be faster than the following which requires evaluating and "
"iterating through the entire queryset::"
msgstr ""
