msgid "Performance considerations"
msgstr "Creithniúcháin"

msgid ""
"Be cautious about using nested queries and understand your database server's "
"performance characteristics (if in doubt, benchmark!). Some database "
"backends, most notably MySQL, don't optimize nested queries very well. It is "
"more efficient, in those cases, to extract a list of values and then pass "
"that into the second query. That is, execute two queries instead of one::"
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach faoi cheisteanna neadaithe a úsáid agus tuig tréithe "
"feidhmíochta do fhreastalaí bunachar sonraí (má tá amhras ort, tagarmharc!). "
"Ní dhéanann roinnt cúltaca bunachar sonraí, go háirithe MySQL, ceisteanna "
"neadaithe a bharrfheabhsú go han-mhaith. Tá sé níos éifeachtaí, sna cásanna "
"sin, liosta luachanna a bhaint agus ansin é a chur isteach sa dara ceist. Is "
"é sin, déan dhá cheist a fhorghníomhú in ionad ceann amháin:"

msgid ""
"Note the ``list()`` call around the Blog ``QuerySet`` to force execution of "
"the first query. Without it, a nested query would be executed, "
"because :ref:`querysets-are-lazy`."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara an ghlao ``list () ``timpeall an Blag ``QuerySet`` chun "
"an chéad cheist a chur i bhfeidhm. Gan é, déanfaí ceist neadaithe a "
"fhorghníomhú, toisc go ndéanfaí: ref: `querysets-are-lazy`."

msgid "``gt``"
msgstr "``gt``"

msgid "Greater than."
msgstr "Níos mó ná."

msgid "``gte``"
msgstr "``gte``"

msgid "Greater than or equal to."
msgstr "Níos mó ná nó comhionann leis."

msgid "``lt``"
msgstr "``lt``"

msgid "Less than."
msgstr "Níos lú ná."

msgid "``lte``"
msgstr "```lte``"

msgid "Less than or equal to."
msgstr "Níos lú ná nó cothrom le."

msgid "Case-sensitive starts-with."
msgstr "Tosaíonn cás-íogair - le."

msgid ""
"SQLite doesn't support case-sensitive ``LIKE`` statements; ``startswith`` "
"acts like ``istartswith`` for SQLite."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn SQLite le ráitis ``LIKE ``atá íogair ó cháis; gníomhaíonn "
"```startswith` mar `istartswith` do SQLite."

msgid "``istartswith``"
msgstr "``istartswith`"

msgid "Case-insensitive starts-with."
msgstr "Tosaíonn cás-neamh-íogair - le."

msgid "Case-sensitive ends-with."
msgstr "Críochna cás-íogair - le."

msgid ""
"SQLite doesn't support case-sensitive ``LIKE`` statements; ``endswith`` acts "
"like ``iendswith`` for SQLite. Refer to the :ref:`database note <sqlite-"
"string-matching>` documentation for more."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn SQLite le ráitis ``LIKE`` íogair cás-íogair; gníomhaíonn "
"```endswith` mar ``iendswith` do SQLite. Féach ar an doiciméadach:ref: "
"`bunachar sonraí <sqlite-string-matching>`le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "``iendswith``"
msgstr "```Idirleith``"

msgid "Case-insensitive ends-with."
msgstr "Críochtaí cás-neamh-íogair - le."

msgid "``range``"
msgstr "``raon ``"

msgid "Range test (inclusive)."
msgstr "Tástáil raon (cuimsitheach)."

msgid ""
"You can use ``range`` anywhere you can use ``BETWEEN`` in SQL — for dates, "
"numbers and even characters."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``raon ``a úsáid in áit ar bith is féidir leat ``BETWEEN`` a "
"úsáid i SQL - le haghaidh dátaí, uimhreacha agus fiú carachtair."

msgid ""
"Filtering a ``DateTimeField`` with dates won't include items on the last "
"day, because the bounds are interpreted as \"0am on the given date\". If "
"``pub_date`` was a ``DateTimeField``, the above expression would be turned "
"into this SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Ní chuimsíonn scagadh ``DateTimefield` le dátaí míreanna ar an lá deiridh, "
"toisc go léirmhínítear na teorainneacha mar “0am ar an dáta ar leith”. Dá "
"mbeadh ``pub_date`` ina `DateTimefield``, déanfaí an abairt thuas a iompú "
"isteach sa SQL seo:"

msgid "Generally speaking, you can't mix dates and datetimes."
msgstr "Go ginearálta, ní féidir leat dátaí agus dáta a mheascadh."

msgid "``date``"
msgstr "``Dáta ``"

msgid ""
"For datetime fields, casts the value as date. Allows chaining additional "
"field lookups. Takes a date value."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta-am, caitheann an luach mar dháta. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé luach dáta."

msgid ""
"(No equivalent SQL code fragment is included for this lookup because "
"implementation of the relevant query varies among different database "
"engines.)"
msgstr ""
"(Níl aon bhrúin coibhéiseach cód SQL san áireamh don chuardach seo toisc go "
"n-athraíonn cur i bhfeidhm na fiosrúcháin ábhartha i measc innill bhun"

msgid ""
"When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, fields are converted to the current time "
"zone before filtering. This requires :ref:`time zone definitions in the "
"database <database-time-zone-definitions>`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: SETTING: Is é `USE_TZ` ``True``, déantar réimsí a thiontú go dtí an "
"crios ama reatha sula ndéantar iad a scagadh. <database-time-zone-"
"definitions>Éilíonn sé seo: ref: `sainmhínithe crios ama sa bhunachar sonraí "
"`."

msgid "``year``"
msgstr "``bliant``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, an exact year match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer year."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, cluiche bliana cruinn. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé bliain slámhshláir."

msgid "(The exact SQL syntax varies for each database engine.)"
msgstr "(Athraíonn an comhréir cruinn SQL do gach inneall bunachar sonraí.)"

msgid ""
"When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, datetime fields are converted to the "
"current time zone before filtering. This requires :ref:`time zone "
"definitions in the database <database-time-zone-definitions>`."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: Socrú: Is é `USE_TZ` ``True``, déantar réimsí dáta-ama a thiontú go "
"dtí an crios ama reatha sula ndéantar iad a scagadh. <database-time-zone-"
"definitions>Éilíonn sé seo: ref: `sainmhínithe crios ama sa bhunachar sonraí "
"`."

msgid "``iso_year``"
msgstr "``iso_bliain``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, an exact ISO 8601 week-numbering year match. "
"Allows chaining additional field lookups. Takes an integer year."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, comhoiriúnú bliana uimhrithe seachtaine "
"cruinn ISO 8601. Ligeann sé cuardaigh réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé "
"bliain slámhshláir."

msgid "``month``"
msgstr "``mhí``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, an exact month match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer 1 (January) through 12 (December)."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, cluiche míosa cruinn. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé sláimhir 1 (Eanáir) trí 12 (Nollaig)."

msgid "``day``"
msgstr "``Lae``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, an exact day match. Allows chaining additional "
"field lookups. Takes an integer day."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, cluiche lá cruinn. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé lá sláireach."

msgid ""
"Note this will match any record with a pub_date on the third day of the "
"month, such as January 3, July 3, etc."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirfidh sé seo aon taifead a mheaitseáil le dáta "
"pub_date ar an tríú lá den mhí, mar shampla 3 Eanáir, 3 Iúil, srl."

msgid "``week``"
msgstr "``seachtaine``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, return the week number (1-52 or 53) according "
"to `ISO-8601 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO-8601>`_, i.e., weeks start "
"on a Monday and the first week contains the year's first Thursday."
msgstr ""
"Mai< https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO-8601> dir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, "
"cuir ar ais uimhir na seachtaine (1-52 nó 53) de réir `ISO-8601`_, ie, "
"tosaíonn seachtainí Dé Luain agus tá an chéad Déardaoin na bliana sa chéad "
"seachtain."

msgid "``week_day``"
msgstr "``Lae_na seachtaine``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, a 'day of the week' match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta-am, cluiche 'lá na seachtaine'. Ligeann sé "
"cuardaigh réimse breise a shlánú."

msgid ""
"Takes an integer value representing the day of week from 1 (Sunday) to 7 "
"(Saturday)."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé luach sláimhir a léiríonn lá na seachtaine ó 1 (Dé Domhnaigh) go 7 "
"(Dé Sathairn)."

msgid ""
"Note this will match any record with a ``pub_date`` that falls on a Monday "
"(day 2 of the week), regardless of the month or year in which it occurs. "
"Week days are indexed with day 1 being Sunday and day 7 being Saturday."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirfidh sé seo aon taifead a mheaitseáil le "
"``pub_date`` a thiteann Dé Luain (lá 2 den tseachtain), beag beann ar an mí "
"nó an bhliain ina dtarlaíonn sé. Déantar laethanta na seachtaine a innéacsú "
"agus lá 1 é Dé Domhnaigh agus lá 7 ina Dé Sathairn."

msgid "``iso_week_day``"
msgstr "``Lae_iso_seachtaine``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, an exact ISO 8601 day of the week match. "
"Allows chaining additional field lookups."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta-am, cluiche cruinn lá ISO 8601 den "
"tseachtain. Ligeann sé cuardaigh réimse breise a shlánú."

msgid ""
"Takes an integer value representing the day of the week from 1 (Monday) to 7 "
"(Sunday)."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé luach sláimhir a léiríonn lá na seachtaine ó 1 (Luan) go 7 (Dé "
"Domhnaigh)."

msgid ""
"Note this will match any record with a ``pub_date`` that falls on a Monday "
"(day 1 of the week), regardless of the month or year in which it occurs. "
"Week days are indexed with day 1 being Monday and day 7 being Sunday."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcuirfidh sé seo aon taifead a mheaitseáil le "
"``pub_date`` a thiteann Dé Luain (lá 1 den tseachtain), beag beann ar an mí "
"nó an bhliain ina dtarlaíonn sé. Déantar laethanta na seachtaine a innéacsú "
"agus lá 1 é Dé Luan agus lá 7 é Dé Domhnaigh."

msgid "``quarter``"
msgstr "``Ráith``"

msgid ""
"For date and datetime fields, a 'quarter of the year' match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer value between 1 and 4 "
"representing the quarter of the year."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus dáta, cluiche 'ceathrú den bhliain'. Ligeann sé "
"cuardaigh réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé luach sláimhir idir 1 agus 4 a "
"léiríonn ráithe den bhliain."

msgid ""
"Example to retrieve entries in the second quarter (April 1 to June 30)::"
msgstr ""
"Sampla chun iontrálacha a aisghabháil sa dara ráithe (1 Aibreán go 30 "
"Meitheamh):"

msgid "``time``"
msgstr "```Am ``"

msgid ""
"For datetime fields, casts the value as time. Allows chaining additional "
"field lookups. Takes a :class:`datetime.time` value."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta-ama, caitheann an luach mar am. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Glacann sé: aicme: luach `datetime.time`."

msgid "``hour``"
msgstr "``uair an chloig``"

msgid ""
"For datetime and time fields, an exact hour match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer between 0 and 23."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus ama, meaitseáil uair an chloig cruinn. Ligeann sé "
"cuardaigh réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé sláimhir idir 0 agus 23."

msgid "``minute``"
msgstr "``nóiméad``"

msgid ""
"For datetime and time fields, an exact minute match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer between 0 and 59."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus ama, cluiche beacht nóiméad. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé sláimhir idir 0 agus 59."

msgid "``second``"
msgstr "```an dara ``"

msgid ""
"For datetime and time fields, an exact second match. Allows chaining "
"additional field lookups. Takes an integer between 0 and 59."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le réimsí dáta agus ama, an dara cluiche cruinn. Ligeann sé cuardaigh "
"réimse breise a shlánú. Tógann sé sláimhir idir 0 agus 59."

msgid "``isnull``"
msgstr "``isnull``"

msgid ""
"Takes either ``True`` or ``False``, which correspond to SQL queries of ``IS "
"NULL`` and ``IS NOT NULL``, respectively."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé ``True`` nó `False``, a fhreagraíonn do cheisteanna SQL de `IS "
"NULL`` agus ``IS NOT NULL``, faoi seach."

msgid "``regex``"
msgstr "``Regex``"

msgid "Case-sensitive regular expression match."
msgstr "Meaitseáil léirithe rialta íogair do chás-"

msgid ""
"The regular expression syntax is that of the database backend in use. In the "
"case of SQLite, which has no built in regular expression support, this "
"feature is provided by a (Python) user-defined REGEXP function, and the "
"regular expression syntax is therefore that of Python's ``re`` module."
msgstr ""
"Is é an comhréiteach abairt rialta ná cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí atá in "
"úsáid. I gcás SQLite, nach bhfuil aon tacaíocht léirithe ionsuite aige, "
"soláthraíonn feidhm REGEXP (Python) atá sainmhínithe ag úsáideoir an ghné "
"seo, agus dá bhrí sin is é an comhréiteach abairt rialta modúl `re`` Python."

msgid ""
"Using raw strings (e.g., ``r'foo'`` instead of ``'foo'``) for passing in the "
"regular expression syntax is recommended."
msgstr ""
"Moltar teaghráin amh a úsáid (m.sh., `r'foo'`` in ionad ``'foo'``) chun "
"comhréiteach an abairt rialta a chur isteach."

msgid "``iregex``"
msgstr "``iregex``"

msgid "Case-insensitive regular expression match."
msgstr "Meaitseáil léirithe rialta neamh-íogair."

msgid "Aggregation functions"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna comhiomlán"

msgid ""
"Django provides the following aggregation functions in the "
"``django.db.models`` module. For details on how to use these aggregate "
"functions, see :doc:`the topic guide on aggregation </topics/db/"
"aggregation>`. See the :class:`~django.db.models.Aggregate` documentation to "
"learn how to create your aggregates."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django na feidhmeanna comhiomlánaithe seo a leanas sa mhodúl "
"``django.db.models``. Le haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas na feidhmeanna "
"comhiomlána seo a úsáid, féach:doc: `an treoir ábhair ar chomhiomlán' </"
"topics/db/aggregation>. Féach an doiciméadach:class: "
"`~django.db.models.aggregate` chun foghlaim conas do chomhiomláin a chruthú."

msgid ""
"SQLite can't handle aggregation on date/time fields out of the box. This is "
"because there are no native date/time fields in SQLite and Django currently "
"emulates these features using a text field. Attempts to use aggregation on "
"date/time fields in SQLite will raise ``NotSupportedError``."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le SQLite comhiomlánú a láimhseáil ar réimsí dáta/ama as an "
"mbosca. Tá sé seo toisc nach bhfuil aon réimsí dáta/ama dúchasacha i SQLite "
"agus déanann Django aithris ar na gnéithe seo faoi láthair ag baint úsáide "
"as réimse téacs. Ardóidh iarrachtaí comhiomlánú ar réimsí dáta/ama i SQLite "
"``NotSupportedError``."

msgid "Empty querysets or groups"
msgstr "Ceisteanna nó grúpaí folamh"

msgid ""
"Aggregation functions return ``None`` when used with an empty ``QuerySet`` "
"or group. For example, the ``Sum`` aggregation function returns ``None`` "
"instead of ``0`` if the ``QuerySet`` contains no entries or for any empty "
"group in a non-empty ``QuerySet``. To return another value instead, define "
"the ``default`` argument. ``Count`` is an exception to this behavior; it "
"returns ``0`` if the ``QuerySet`` is empty since ``Count`` does not support "
"the ``default`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Tugann feidhmeanna comhiomlánaithe ``None`` ar ais nuair a úsáidtear iad le "
"``QuerySet` nó grúpa folamh. Mar shampla, filleann an fheidhm "
"chomhiomlánaithe ``Sum`` ``None`` in ionad ``0`` mura bhfuil aon iontrálacha "
"sa ``QuerySet`` nó d'aon ghrúpa folamh i ``QuerySet`` neamh-folamh. Chun "
"luach eile a thabhairt ar ais ina ionad sin, sainmhínigh an argóint "
"``réamhshocraithe``. Is eisceacht é ``Count`` ón iompar seo; filleann sé "
"``0`` má tá an ``QuerySet`` folamh ós rud é nach dtacaíonn ``Count`` leis an "
"argóint ``réamhshocraithe``."

msgid "All aggregates have the following parameters in common:"
msgstr "Tá na paraiméadair seo a leanas i gcoiteann ag gach comhiomlán:"

msgid ""
"Strings that reference fields on the model, transforms of the field, "
"or :doc:`query expressions </ref/models/expressions>`."
msgstr ""
"Teagáin a thagraíonn réimsí ar an tsamhail, athraíonn an réimse, nó:doc: "
"`abairtí fiosraitheach' </ref/models/expressions>."

msgid "``output_field``"
msgstr "``réimseach_aschuir``"

msgid ""
"An optional argument that represents the :doc:`model field </ref/models/"
"fields>` of the return value"
msgstr ""
"Argóint roghnach a léiríonn na:doc: `réimse samhail` den luach tuairisceáin "
"</ref/models/fields>"

msgid ""
"When combining multiple field types, Django can only determine the "
"``output_field`` if all fields are of the same type. Otherwise, you must "
"provide the ``output_field`` yourself."
msgstr ""
"Agus cineálacha réimse iolracha á gcomhcheangal agat, ní féidir le Django "
"ach an `output_field` a chinneadh má tá gach réimse den chineál céanna. "
"Seachas sin, ní mór duit an `output_field`` a sholáthar duit féin."

msgid "``filter``"
msgstr "``Scagair``"

msgid ""
"An optional :class:`Q object <django.db.models.Q>` that's used to filter the "
"rows that are aggregated."
msgstr ""
"Rud roghnach: class: `Q <django.db.models.Q>`a úsáidtear chun na sraitheanna "
"atá comhiomlánaithe a scagadh."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`conditional-aggregation` and :ref:`filtering-on-annotations` for "
"example usage."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: `comhiomlánú coinníollach` agus:ref: `filtering-on-annotations` "
"mar shampla úsáid."

msgid ""
"An optional argument that allows specifying a value to use as a default "
"value when the queryset (or grouping) contains no entries."
msgstr ""
"Argóint roghnach a cheadaíonn luach a shonrú le húsáid mar luach "
"réamhshocraithe nuair nach bhfuil aon iontrálacha sa tacar ceisteanna (nó an "
"grúpáil)."

msgid "``**extra``"
msgstr "``**breise``"

msgid ""
"Keyword arguments that can provide extra context for the SQL generated by "
"the aggregate."
msgstr ""
"Argóintí eochairfhocal ar féidir leo comhthéacs breise a sholáthar don SQL a "
"ghineann an comhiomlán"

msgid "``Avg``"
msgstr "``Avg``"

msgid ""
"Returns the mean value of the given expression, which must be numeric unless "
"you specify a different ``output_field``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé meánluach an abairt a thugtar ar ais, a chaithfidh a bheith "
"uimhriúil mura sonraíonn tú ``output_field` difriúil."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__avg``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__avg``"

msgid ""
"Return type: ``float`` if input is ``int``, otherwise same as input field, "
"or ``output_field`` if supplied. If the queryset or grouping is empty, "
"``default`` is returned."
msgstr ""
"Cineál tuairisceáin: ``float`` má tá an t-ionchur ``int``, ar shlí eile mar "
"an réimse ionchuir, nó ``output_field`` má sholáthraítear. Má tá an tacar "
"fiosrúcháin nó an grúpáil folamh, cuirtear ``réamhshocraithe`` ar ais."

msgid ""
"Optional. If ``distinct=True``, ``Avg`` returns the mean value of unique "
"values. This is the SQL equivalent of ``AVG(DISTINCT <field>)``. The default "
"value is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Má tá ``Distinct=True``, filleann ``Avg`` meánluach na luachanna "
"uathúla ar ais. <field>Is é seo an coibhéis SQL le ``AVG (DISTINCT) ``. Is é "
"“False” an luach réamhshocraithe."

msgid "``Count``"
msgstr "``Comhaireant``"

msgid ""
"Returns the number of objects that are related through the provided "
"expression. ``Count('*')`` is equivalent to the SQL ``COUNT(*)`` expression."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais líon na rudaí a bhaineann tríd an abairt a chuirtear ar "
"fáil. Tá ``Count ('*') ``comhionann leis an abairt SQL ``COUNT (*)``."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__count``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__count``"

msgid "Return type: ``int``"
msgstr "Cineál tuairisceáin: ``int``"

msgid ""
"Optional. If ``distinct=True``, the count will only include unique "
"instances. This is the SQL equivalent of ``COUNT(DISTINCT <field>)``. The "
"default value is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Má tá `Distinct=True``, ní chuimsíonn an comhaireamh ach cásanna "
"uathúla. Is é seo an coibhéis SQL le ``COUNT (DISTINCT<field>) ``. Is é "
"“False” an luach réamhshocraithe."

msgid "``Max``"
msgstr "``Uasmhéad``"

msgid "Returns the maximum value of the given expression."
msgstr "Tugann sé luach uasta an léirithe a thugtar ar ais."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__max``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__max``"

msgid ""
"Return type: same as input field, or ``output_field`` if supplied. If the "
"queryset or grouping is empty, ``default`` is returned."
msgstr ""
"Cineál tuairisceáin: mar an gcéanna le réimse ionchuir, nó ``output_field`` "
"má sholáthraítear. Má tá an tacar ceisteanna nó an grúpáil folamh, cuirtear "
"``réamhshocraithe`` ar ais."

msgid "``Min``"
msgstr "``Mion``"

msgid "Returns the minimum value of the given expression."
msgstr "Tugann sé luach íosta na léirithe tugtha ar ais."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__min``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__min``"

msgid "``StdDev``"
msgstr "``Stddev``"

msgid "Returns the standard deviation of the data in the provided expression."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé diall caighdeánach na sonraí san abairt a chuirtear ar fáil ar ais."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__stddev``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__stddev``"

msgid ""
"Optional. By default, ``StdDev`` returns the population standard deviation. "
"However, if ``sample=True``, the return value will be the sample standard "
"deviation."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. De réir réamhshocraithe, filleann ``stdDev`` an diall caighdeánach "
"daonra ar ais. Mar sin féin, má tá ``sample=True``, is é an luach "
"tuairisceáin an diall caighdeánach samplach."

msgid "``Sum``"
msgstr "``Sum``"

msgid "Computes the sum of all values of the given expression."
msgstr "Ríomhann sé suim na luachanna uile den abairt ar leith."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__sum``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__sum``"

msgid ""
"Optional. If ``distinct=True``, ``Sum`` returns the sum of unique values. "
"This is the SQL equivalent of ``SUM(DISTINCT <field>)``. The default value "
"is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Má tá ``Distinct=True``, filleann ``Sum`` suim na luachanna "
"uathúla. Is é seo an coibhéis SQL le ``SUM (DISTINCT<field>) ``. Is é "
"“False” an luach réamhshocraithe."

msgid "``Variance``"
msgstr "``Athraithe``"

msgid "Returns the variance of the data in the provided expression."
msgstr "Tugann sé athrú na sonraí san abairt a chuirtear ar fáil ar ais."

msgid "Default alias: ``<field>__variance``"
msgstr "<field>Ainm réamhshocraithe: ``__variance``"

msgid ""
"Optional. By default, ``Variance`` returns the population variance. However, "
"if ``sample=True``, the return value will be the sample variance."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. De réir réamhshocraithe, filleann ``Athraitheacht ``an t-athrú "
"daonra ar ais. Mar sin féin, má tá ``sample=True``, is é an luach "
"tuairisceáin an t-athrú samplach."

msgid "Query-related tools"
msgstr "Uirlisí a bhaineann le fiosrú"

msgid ""
"This section provides reference material for query-related tools not "
"documented elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an chuid seo ábhar tagartha d'uirlisí a bhaineann le "
"fiosrúcháin nach ndéanfar"

msgid "``Q()`` objects"
msgstr "``Q () ``rudaí"

msgid ""
"A ``Q()`` object represents an SQL condition that can be used in database-"
"related operations. It's similar to how an :class:`F() <django.db.models.F>` "
"object represents the value of a model field or annotation. They make it "
"possible to define and reuse conditions. These can be negated using the "
"``~`` (``NOT``) operator, and combined using operators such as ``|`` "
"(``OR``), ``&`` (``AND``), and ``^`` (``XOR``). See :ref:`complex-lookups-"
"with-q`."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn réad ``Q () ``riocht SQL is féidir a úsáid in oibríochtaí a "
"bhaineann le bunachar sonraí. Tá sé cosúil leis an gcaoi a léiríonn réad "
"an:class: `F () <django.db.models.F>`luach réimse samhail nó anótála. "
"Déanann siad coinníollacha a shainiú agus a athúsáid. Is féidir iad seo a "
"dhiúltú ag baint úsáide as an oibreoir ``~`` (``NOT ``), agus a chur le "
"chéile ag baint úsáide as oibreoirí mar `|`` (``OR``), ``&`` (``AND``), agus "
"``^`` (`XOR``). Féach: ref: `complex-lookups-with-q`."

msgid "``Prefetch()`` objects"
msgstr "``Prefetch () ``rudaí"

msgid ""
"The ``Prefetch()`` object can be used to control the operation "
"of :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related()`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an réad ``Prefetch () ``a úsáid chun oibriú: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.prefetch_related () `a rialú."

msgid ""
"The ``lookup`` argument describes the relations to follow and works the same "
"as the string based lookups passed "
"to :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related()`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann an argóint ``lookup`` cur síos ar na caidrimh atá le leanúint agus "
"oibríonn sé mar an gcéanna leis na cuardaigh sreanga-bhunaithe a chuirtear "
"chuig: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related () `. Mar "
"shampla:"

msgid ""
"The ``queryset`` argument supplies a base ``QuerySet`` for the given lookup. "
"This is useful to further filter down the prefetch operation, or to "
"call :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.select_related()` from the "
"prefetched relation, hence reducing the number of queries even further:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an argóint ``Queryset ``bonn ``QuerySet`` don chuardach ar "
"leith. Tá sé seo úsáideach chun an oibríocht réamhfhillte a scagadh síos, nó "
"glaoch ar: meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.select_related () `ón "
"ngaol réamhfhaighte, agus mar sin laghdaítear líon na gceisteanna níos mó "
"fós:"

msgid ""
"The ``to_attr`` argument sets the result of the prefetch operation to a "
"custom attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an argóint `to_attr`` toradh na hoibríochta réamhfhillte go tréith "
"saincheaptha:"

msgid ""
"When using ``to_attr`` the prefetched result is stored in a list. This can "
"provide a significant speed improvement over traditional "
"``prefetch_related`` calls which store the cached result within a "
"``QuerySet`` instance."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a úsáidtear ``to_attr``, stóráiltear an toradh réamhfhaighte i liosta. "
"Féadann sé seo feabhas suntasach luais a sholáthar thar ghlaonna "
"traidisiúnta ``prefetch_related` a stóráilíonn an toradh taisceáilte "
"laistigh de shampla ``QuerySet`."

msgid "``prefetch_related_objects()``"
msgstr "``rudaí prefetch_gaolmhara () ``"

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aprefetch_related_objects()``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``aprefetch_related_objects () ``"

msgid ""
"Prefetches the given lookups on an iterable of model instances. This is "
"useful in code that receives a list of model instances as opposed to a "
"``QuerySet``; for example, when fetching models from a cache or "
"instantiating them manually."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann sé na cuardaigh a thugtar roimh ré ar chásanna samhail atá "
"inathraithe. Tá sé seo úsáideach sa chód a fhaigheann liosta de na cásanna "
"samhail seachas ``QuerySet`; mar shampla, nuair a bhíonn samhlacha á "
"bhfaigheann tú ó taisce nó iad ag instanciú de láimh."

msgid ""
"Pass an iterable of model instances (must all be of the same class) and the "
"lookups or :class:`Prefetch` objects you want to prefetch for. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Rith athraitheach cásanna samhail (caithfidh gach duine a bheith den rang "
"céanna) agus na rudaí cuardaigh nó:class: `Prefetch` is mian leat "
"réamhfhaighteacht dóibh. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"When using multiple databases with ``prefetch_related_objects``, the "
"prefetch query will use the database associated with the model instance. "
"This can be overridden by using a custom queryset in a related lookup."
msgstr ""
"Agus bunachair sonraí iolracha á n-úsáid agat le "
"``prefetch_related_objects``, úsáidfidh an ceist réamhfhreastail an bunachar "
"sonraí a bhaineann leis an samhail samhail. Is féidir é seo a shárú trí "
"thacar ceisteanna saincheaptha a úsáid i gcuardach gaolmhar."

msgid "``FilteredRelation()`` objects"
msgstr "``FilteredRelation () ``rudaí"

msgid "The name of the field on which you'd like to filter the relation."
msgstr "Ainm an réimse ar mhaith leat an gaol a scagadh air."

msgid "A :class:`~django.db.models.Q` object to control the filtering."
msgstr "A: Aicme: `~ Django.db.Models.q` in aghaidh an scagadh a rialú."

msgid ""
"``FilteredRelation`` is used with :meth:`~.QuerySet.annotate()` to create an "
"``ON`` clause when a ``JOIN`` is performed. It doesn't act on the default "
"relationship but on the annotation name (``pizzas_vegetarian`` in example "
"below)."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear ``FilteredRelation`` le:meth: `~.queryset.annotate () `chun clásal "
"``ON`` a chruthú nuair a dhéantar ``JOIN``. Ní ghníomhaíonn sé ar an "
"gcaidreamh réamhshocraithe ach ar an ainm anótála (``pizzas_vegetarian`` i "
"sampla thíos)."

msgid ""
"For example, to find restaurants that have vegetarian pizzas with "
"``'mozzarella'`` in the name:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun bialanna a fháil a bhfuil pizzes vegetarian acu le "
"```mozzarella`` san ainm:"

msgid ""
"If there are a large number of pizzas, this queryset performs better than:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá líon mór píosaí ann, feidhmíonn an tacar ceisteanna seo níos fearr ná:"

msgid ""
"because the filtering in the ``WHERE`` clause of the first queryset will "
"only operate on vegetarian pizzas."
msgstr ""
"toisc nach n-oibreoidh an scagadh i gclásal ``WHERE`` den chéad tacar "
"fiosrúcháin ach ar phiotsaí vegetarian."

msgid "``FilteredRelation`` doesn't support:"
msgstr "Ní thacaíonn ``FilteredRelation`` le:"

msgid ":meth:`.QuerySet.only` and :meth:`~.QuerySet.prefetch_related`."
msgstr ": meth: `.queryset.only` agus:meth: `~.queryset.prefetch_related`."

msgid ""
"A :class:`~django.contrib.contenttypes.fields.GenericForeignKey` inherited "
"from a parent model."
msgstr ""
"A: Class: `~django.contrib.contentTypes.Fields.GenericForeignKey` "
"oidhreachta ó mhúnla tuismitheora."

msgid "Related objects reference"
msgstr "Tagairt rudaí gaolmhara"

msgid ""
"A \"related manager\" is a manager used in a one-to-many or many-to-many "
"related context. This happens in two cases:"
msgstr ""
"Is bainisteoir é “bainisteoir gaolmhar” a úsáidtear i gcomhthéacs gaolmhar "
"duine le go leor nó go leor. Tarlaíonn sé seo i dhá chás:"

msgid ""
"The \"other side\" of a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` relation. That "
"is::"
msgstr ""
"An “taobh eile” de a:class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey` gaol. Is é sin::"

msgid ""
"In the above example, the methods below will be available on the manager "
"``blog.entry_set``."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, beidh na modhanna thíos ar fáil ar an mbainisteoir "
"``blog.entry_set``."

msgid "Both sides of a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` relation ::"
msgstr "An dá thaobh de a:class: `~Django.db.Models.ManyTomanyField` gaol:"

msgid ""
"In this example, the methods below will be available both on "
"``topping.pizza_set`` and on ``pizza.toppings``."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, beidh na modhanna thíos ar fáil ar ``topping.pizza_set`` agus "
"ar `pizza.toppings``."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aadd``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``aadd``"

msgid "Adds the specified model objects to the related object set."
msgstr "Cuireann sé na rudaí samhail sonraithe leis an tacar réad gaolmhar."

msgid ""
"In the example above, in the case of a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` "
"relationship, :meth:`QuerySet.update() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>` is used to perform the update. "
"This requires the objects to already be saved."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.update>Sa sampla thuas, i gcás caidreamh "
"a:class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`, úsáidtear:: meth: `QuerySet.Update "
"() `chun an nuashonrú a dhéanamh. Éilíonn sé seo go ndéanfar na rudaí a "
"shábháil cheana féin."

msgid ""
"You can use the ``bulk=False`` argument to instead have the related manager "
"perform the update by calling ``e.save()``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an argóint ``Bulk=False`` a úsáid chun an bainisteoir "
"gaolmhar an nuashonrú a dhéanamh ina ionad sin trí ghlaoch ar ``e.save () ``."

msgid ""
"Using ``add()`` with a many-to-many relationship, however, will not call any "
"``save()`` methods (the ``bulk`` argument doesn't exist), but rather create "
"the relationships using :meth:`QuerySet.bulk_create() "
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>`. If you need to execute some "
"custom logic when a relationship is created, listen to "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed` signal, which will trigger "
"``pre_add`` and ``post_add`` actions."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.bulk_create>Ag baint úsáide as `add () ``le "
"caidreamh go leor, áfach, ní ghlaofar aon mhodhanna ``save ()`` (níl an "
"argóint ``bulk`` ann), ach cruthófar na caidrimh ag baint úsáid:meth: "
"`QuerySet.bulk_create () `. Más gá duit roinnt loighic saincheaptha a "
"fhorghníomhú nuair a chruthaítear caidreamh, éist leis an gcomhartha: data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed`, a spreagfaidh gníomhartha "
"``pre_add`` agus ``post_add``."

msgid ""
"Using ``add()`` on a relation that already exists won't duplicate the "
"relation, but it will still trigger signals."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhúbailt an gaol a úsáid `add () ``ar ghaol atá ann cheana féin, ach "
"spreagfaidh sé comharthaí fós."

msgid ""
"For many-to-many relationships ``add()`` accepts either model instances or "
"field values, normally primary keys, as the ``*objs`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le caidrimh go go leor glacann `add () ``le cásanna samhail nó "
"luachanna réimse, eochracha bunscoile de ghnáth, mar argóint ``*objs``."

msgid ""
"Use the ``through_defaults`` argument to specify values for the "
"new :ref:`intermediate model <intermediary-manytomany>` instance(s), if "
"needed. You can use callables as values in the ``through_defaults`` "
"dictionary and they will be evaluated once before creating any intermediate "
"instance(s)."
msgstr ""
"<intermediary-manytomany>Úsáid an argóint `through_defaults`` chun luachanna "
"a shonrú do shampla nua:ref: `samhail idirmheán`, más gá. Is féidir leat "
"glaonna a úsáid mar luachanna sa fhoclóir `through_defaults` agus déanfar "
"iad a mheas uair amháin sula gcruthófar aon sampla (í) idirmheánach."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``acreate``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``acreate``"

msgid ""
"Creates a new object, saves it and puts it in the related object set. "
"Returns the newly created object:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé réad nua, sábhálann sé agus cuireann sé sa tacar réad gaolmhar "
"é. Tugann an réad nua-chruthaithe ar ais:"

msgid "This is equivalent to (but simpler than):"
msgstr "Tá sé seo coibhéiseach le (ach níos simplí ná):"

msgid ""
"Note that there's no need to specify the keyword argument of the model that "
"defines the relationship. In the above example, we don't pass the parameter "
"``blog`` to ``create()``. Django figures out that the new ``Entry`` object's "
"``blog`` field should be set to ``b``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach gá argóint eochairfhocal an tsamhail a shonrú a "
"shainmhíníonn an caidreamh. Sa sampla thuas, ní chuirimid an paraiméadar "
"``blog ``ar aghaidh chuig ``create ()``. Figireann Django amach gur chóir "
"réimse ``blog ``réad nua ``Entry`` a shocrú go ``b``."

msgid ""
"Use the ``through_defaults`` argument to specify values for the "
"new :ref:`intermediate model <intermediary-manytomany>` instance, if needed. "
"You can use callables as values in the ``through_defaults`` dictionary."
msgstr ""
"<intermediary-manytomany>Úsáid an argóint `through_defaults`` chun luachanna "
"a shonrú don shampla nua:ref: `samhail idirmheán`, más gá. Is féidir leat "
"glaonna a úsáid mar luachanna sa fhoclóir `through_defaults``."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aremove``"
msgstr "* Leagan asincrón*: ``aremove``"

msgid "Removes the specified model objects from the related object set:"
msgstr "Baineann na rudaí samhail sonraithe as an tacar réad gaolmhar:"

msgid ""
"Similar to :meth:`add()`, ``e.save()`` is called in the example above to "
"perform the update. Using ``remove()`` with a many-to-many relationship, "
"however, will delete the relationships "
"using :meth:`QuerySet.delete()<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>` "
"which means no model ``save()`` methods are called; listen to "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed` signal if you wish to "
"execute custom code when a relationship is deleted."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le:meth: `add () `, tugtar ``e.save () ``sa sampla thuas chun an "
"nuashonrú a dhéanamh. Ag baint úsáide as `remove () ``le caidreamh go leor, "
"scriosfar na caidrimh ag baint úsáid:meth: `QuerySet.delete () "
"`<django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete>rud a chiallaíonn nach dtugtar "
"modhanna samhail ``save ()``; éist leis an comhartha: data: "
"`~django.db.models.signals.m2m_changed` más mian leat cód saincheaptha a "
"chur i bhfeidhm nuair a scriostar caidreamh."

msgid ""
"For many-to-many relationships ``remove()`` accepts either model instances "
"or field values, normally primary keys, as the ``*objs`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le caidrimh go leor glacann ``remove () ``le cásanna samhail nó "
"luachanna réimse, eochracha príomhúla de ghnáth, mar argóint ``*objs``."

msgid ""
"For :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` objects, this method only exists "
"if ``null=True``. If the related field can't be set to ``None`` (``NULL``), "
"then an object can't be removed from a relation without being added to "
"another. In the above example, removing ``e`` from ``b.entry_set()`` is "
"equivalent to doing ``e.blog = None``, and because the "
"``blog`` :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` doesn't have ``null=True``, "
"this is invalid."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le rudaí: Class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`, níl an modh seo ann "
"ach má tá ``Null=True``. Mura féidir an réimse gaolmhar a shocrú go ``None`` "
"(`NULL``), ansin ní féidir réad a bhaint as gaol gan é a chur le ceann eile. "
"Sa sampla thuas, tá `e`` a bhaint as ``b.entry_set () ``comhionann le "
"``e.blog = None`` a dhéanamh, agus toisc nach bhfuil ``Null=True`` ag an "
"``blog``:class: `~django.db.models.foreignKey`, tá sé seo neamhbhailí."

msgid ""
"For :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` objects, this method accepts a "
"``bulk`` argument to control how to perform the operation. If ``True`` (the "
"default), ``QuerySet.update()`` is used. If ``bulk=False``, the ``save()`` "
"method of each individual model instance is called instead. This triggers "
"the :data:`~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` "
"and :data:`~django.db.models.signals.post_save` signals and comes at the "
"expense of performance."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le rudaí: Class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`, glacann an modh seo "
"le argóint ``bulk`` chun rialú a dhéanamh conas an oibríocht a dhéanamh. Má "
"tá ``True`` (an réamhshocrú), úsáidtear ``QuerySet.Update () ``. Má tá "
"``Bulk=false ``, tugtar an modh ``save ()`` de gach samhail aonair ina "
"ionad. Spreagann sé seo comharthaí: `~django.db.models.signals.pre_save` "
"agus:data: `~django.db.models.signals.post_save` agus tagann sé ar chostas "
"na feidhmíochta."

msgid ""
"For many-to-many relationships, the ``bulk`` keyword argument doesn't exist."
msgstr "Maidir le caidrimh go leor, níl an argóint eochairfhocal ``bulk`` ann."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aclear``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aclear``"

msgid "Removes all objects from the related object set:"
msgstr "Baineann gach rud as an tacar réad gaolmhar:"

msgid ""
"Note this doesn't delete the related objects -- it just disassociates them."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach scriosann sé seo na rudaí gaolmhara - dícheanglaíonn "
"sé ach iad."

msgid ""
"Just like ``remove()``, ``clear()`` is only available "
"on :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`\\s where ``null=True`` and it also "
"accepts the ``bulk`` keyword argument."
msgstr ""
"Díreach mar ``remove () ``, níl `clear ()`` ar fáil ach ar:class: "
"`~django.db.models.foreignKey`\\ s ina bhfuil ``null=true`` agus glacann sé "
"leis an argóint eochairfhocal ``bulk`` freisin."

msgid "*Asynchronous version*: ``aset``"
msgstr "*Leagan asincrón*: ``aset``"

msgid "Replace the set of related objects:"
msgstr "Cuir an tacar rudaí gaolmhara in ionad:"

msgid ""
"This method accepts a ``clear`` argument to control how to perform the "
"operation. If ``False`` (the default), the elements missing from the new set "
"are removed using ``remove()`` and only the new ones are added. If "
"``clear=True``, the ``clear()`` method is called instead and the whole set "
"is added at once."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an modh seo le argóint ``soiléir ``chun rialú a dhéanamh ar conas an "
"oibríocht a dhéanamh. Má tá ``False`` (an réamhshocraithe), baintear na "
"heilimintí atá in easnamh ón tacar nua ag baint úsáide as ``remove () ``agus "
"ní chuirtear ach na cinn nua leis. Má tá ``clear=True``, tugtar an modh "
"``clear () ``ina ionad sin agus cuirtear an tacar iomlán leis ag an am "
"céanna."

msgid ""
"For :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` objects, the ``bulk`` argument is "
"passed on to :meth:`add` and :meth:`remove`."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le rudaí: Class: `~Django.db.Models.ForeignKey`, cuirtear an argóint "
"``bulk`` ar aghaidh chuig:meth: `add` agus:meth: `remove`."

msgid ""
"Note that since ``set()`` is a compound operation, it is subject to race "
"conditions. For instance, new objects may be added to the database in "
"between the call to ``clear()`` and the call to ``add()``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara ós rud é gur oibríocht chumaisc é ``set () ``, go bhfuil "
"sé faoi réir coinníollacha cine. Mar shampla, féadfar rudaí nua a chur leis "
"an mbunachar sonraí idir an glao chun ``clear () ``agus an glao chun ``add "
"()``."

msgid ""
"For many-to-many relationships ``set()`` accepts a list of either model "
"instances or field values, normally primary keys, as the ``objs`` argument."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le caidrimh go leor glacann `set () ``liosta de chásanna samhail nó "
"luachanna réimse, eochracha príomhúla de ghnáth, mar argóint ``objs``."

msgid ""
"Note that ``add()``, ``aadd()``, ``create()``, ``acreate()``, ``remove()``, "
"``aremove()``, ``clear()``, ``aclear()``, ``set()``, and ``aset()`` all "
"apply database changes immediately for all types of related fields. In other "
"words, there is no need to call ``save()``/``asave()`` on either end of the "
"relationship."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfeidhmíonn ``add () ``, `aadd ()``, `create () ``, "
"`acreate ()``, `remove () ``, `aremove ()``, ``clear () ``, `aclear ()``, "
"`set () ``, `set ()``, agus ``aset () ``athruithe láithreach do gach cineál "
"réimsí gaolmhara. Is é sin le rá, ní gá glaoch ar `save () ```/``asave () "
"``ar cheachtar deireadh an chaidrimh."

msgid ""
"If you use :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.prefetch_related`, the "
"``add()``, ``aadd()``, ``remove()``, ``aremove()``, ``clear()``, "
"``aclear()``, ``set()``, and ``aset()`` methods clear the prefetched cache."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann t:meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.prefetch_related`, an "
"`add () ``, `aadd ()``, ``remove () ``, `aremove ()``, ``clear () ``, "
"``clear ()``, `aclear () ``, `set ()`` agus Glanann modhanna ``aset () ``an "
"taisce réamhfhaighte."

msgid "Paginator"
msgstr "Paginator"

msgid ""
"Django provides a few classes that help you manage paginated data -- that "
"is, data that's split across several pages, with \"Previous/Next\" links. "
"These classes live in :source:`django/core/paginator.py`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django cúpla rang a chuidíonn leat sonraí leathanaigh a "
"bhainistiú - is é sin, sonraí atá roinnte ar fud roinnt leathanaigh, le "
"naisc “Roimhe Sea/Ar Aghaidh”. Tá na ranganna seo ina gcónaí in:source: "
"`django/core/paginator.py`."

msgid ""
"For examples, see the :doc:`Pagination topic guide </topics/pagination>`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh samplaí, féach an:doc: `Treoir ábhair leathanacha' </topics/"
"pagination>."

msgid "``Paginator`` class"
msgstr "Aicme ``Paginator``"

msgid ""
"A paginator acts like a sequence of :class:`Page` when using ``len()`` or "
"iterating it directly."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn leathanaigh cosúil le seicheamh de:class: `Leathanach` nuair a "
"úsáidtear `len () ``nó é ag athrá go díreach."

msgid ""
"Required. A list, tuple, ``QuerySet``, or other sliceable object with a "
"``count()`` or ``__len__()`` method. For consistent pagination, "
"``QuerySet``\\s should be ordered, e.g. with "
"an :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.order_by` clause or with a "
"default :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.ordering` on the model."
msgstr ""
"Riachtanach. Liosta, tuple, ``QuerySet``, nó réad eile atá inslithe le modh "
"``count () ``nó ``__len__ ()``. Le haghaidh leathanaigh chomhsheasmhach, ba "
"cheart ``QuerySet``\\ s a ordú, m.sh. le an:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.query.queryset.order_by` clásal nó le clásal "
"réamhshocraithe:attr: `~Django.db.Models.Options.Ordering` ar an tsamhail."

msgid "Performance issues paginating large ``QuerySet``\\s"
msgstr "Saincheisteanna feidhmíochta ag leathanaigh mhóra ``QuerySet``"

msgid ""
"If you're using a ``QuerySet`` with a very large number of items, requesting "
"high page numbers might be slow on some databases, because the resulting "
"``LIMIT``/``OFFSET`` query needs to count the number of ``OFFSET`` records "
"which takes longer as the page number gets higher."
msgstr ""
"Má tá “QuerySet” á úsáid agat le líon an-mhór míreanna, d'fhéadfadh go "
"mbeadh uimhreacha ard leathanaigh a iarraidh mall ar roinnt bunachair "
"sonraí, toisc go gcaithfidh an cheist `LIMIT`` /`OFFSET`` a chomhaireamh "
"líon na dtaifid ``OFFSET`` a thógann níos faide de réir mar a théann uimhir "
"an leathanaigh níos airde."

msgid ""
"Required. The maximum number of items to include on a page, not including "
"orphans (see the :attr:`~Paginator.orphans` optional argument below)."
msgstr ""
"Riachtanach. An líon uasta na míreanna atá le cur san áireamh ar leathanach, "
"gan dílleachtaí san áireamh (féach an argóint roghnach: attr: "
"`~Paginator.orphans` thíos)."

msgid ""
"Optional. Use this when you don't want to have a last page with very few "
"items. If the last page would normally have a number of items less than or "
"equal to ``orphans``, then those items will be added to the previous page "
"(which becomes the last page) instead of leaving the items on a page by "
"themselves. For example, with 23 items, ``per_page=10``, and ``orphans=3``, "
"there will be two pages; the first page with 10 items and the second (and "
"last) page with 13 items. ``orphans`` defaults to zero, which means pages "
"are never combined and the last page may have one item."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Úsáid é seo nuair nach dteastaíonn uait leathanach deireanach a "
"bheith agat le mórán earraí. Más rud é go mbeadh roinnt míreanna níos lú ná "
"nó cothrom le `orphans`` sa leathanach deireanach, cuirfear na míreanna sin "
"leis an leathanach roimhe seo (arb é an leathanach deireanach) in ionad na "
"míreanna a fhágáil ar leathanach leo féin. Mar shampla, le 23 mír, "
"``per_page=10``, agus ``orphans=3``, beidh dhá leathanach ann; an chéad "
"leathanach le 10 mír agus an dara leathanach (agus deireanach) le 13 mír. Tá "
"'orphans' réamhshocraithe go nialas, rud a chiallaíonn nach ndéantar "
"leathanaigh a chomhcheangal riamh agus d'fhéadfadh mír amháin a bheith ag an "
"leathanach deireanach."

msgid ""
"Optional. Whether or not the first page is allowed to be empty.  If "
"``False`` and ``object_list`` is  empty, then an ``EmptyPage`` error will be "
"raised."
msgstr ""
"Roghnach. Cibé an gceadaítear don chéad leathanach a bheith folamh nó nach "
"bhfuil. Má tá ``False`` agus ``object_list`` folamh, ansin ardófar earráid "
"``EmptyPage``."

msgid ""
"The ``error_messages`` argument lets you override the default messages that "
"the paginator will raise. Pass in a dictionary with keys matching the error "
"messages you want to override. Available error message keys are: "
"``invalid_page``, ``min_page``, and ``no_results``."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an argóint ``error_messages`` duit na teachtaireachtaí "
"réamhshocraithe a ardóidh an paginator a shárú. Pas isteach i bhfoclóir le "
"heochracha a mheaitseálann leis na teachtaireachtaí earráide is mian leat a "
"shárú. Is iad na heochracha teachtaireachta earráide atá ar fáil ná: "
"``invalid_page``, `min_page``, agus ``no_results``."

msgid "For example, here is the default error message:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, seo an teachtaireacht earráide réamhshocraithe:"

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`Page` object with the given 1-based index, while also "
"handling out of range and invalid page numbers."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceáin a: aicme: réad `Leathanach` leis an t-innéacs bunaithe ar 1 a "
"thugtar, agus uimhreacha leathanaigh lasmuigh de raon agus neamhbhailí a láim"

msgid ""
"If the page isn't a number, it returns the first page. If the page number is "
"negative or greater than the number of pages, it returns the last page."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an leathanach ina uimhir, filleann sé an chéad leathanach ar "
"ais. Má tá uimhir an leathanaigh diúltach nó níos mó ná líon na leathanaigh, "
"filleann sé an leathanach deireanach ar ais."

msgid ""
"Raises an :exc:`EmptyPage` exception only if you specify ``Paginator(..., "
"allow_empty_first_page=False)`` and the ``object_list`` is empty."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn eisceacht an:exc: `EmptyPage` ach má shonraíonn tú ``Paginator "
"(..., allow_empty_first_page=False) ``agus tá an `object_list`` folamh."

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`Page` object with the given 1-based index. "
"Raises :exc:`PageNotAnInteger` if the ``number`` cannot be converted to an "
"integer by calling ``int()``. Raises :exc:`EmptyPage` if the given page "
"number doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceáin a: aicme: réad `Leathanach` leis an innéacs 1-bhunaithe a "
"thugtar. Ardaithe:exc: `PageNotanInteger` mura féidir an ``uimhre`` a "
"thiontú go sláimhir trí ``int () ``a ghlaoch. Ardaithe:exc: `EmptyPage` mura "
"bhfuil an uimhir leathanaigh a thugtar ann."

msgid ""
"Returns a 1-based list of page numbers similar "
"to :attr:`Paginator.page_range`, but may add an ellipsis to either or both "
"sides of the current page number when :attr:`Paginator.num_pages` is large."
msgstr ""
"Tugann liosta 1-bhunaithe ar ais d'uimhreacha leathanaigh cosúil la:attr: "
"`Paginator.page_range`, ach féadfaidh sé ellipsis a chur le ceachtar nó ar "
"an dá thaobh den uimhir leathanaigh reatha nuai:attr: `Paginator.num_pages` "
"mór."

msgid ""
"The number of pages to include on each side of the current page number is "
"determined by the ``on_each_side`` argument which defaults to 3."
msgstr ""
"Cinntear líon na leathanaigh atá le cur san áireamh ar gach taobh den uimhir "
"leathanaigh reatha ag an argóint ``on_each_side`` atá réamhshocraithe go 3."

msgid ""
"The number of pages to include at the beginning and end of page range is "
"determined by the ``on_ends`` argument which defaults to 2."
msgstr ""
"Cinntear líon na leathanaigh atá le cur san áireamh ag tús agus ag deireadh "
"raon leathanaigh ag an argóint `on_ends`` atá réamhshocraithe go 2."

msgid ""
"For example, with the default values for ``on_each_side`` and ``on_ends``, "
"if the current page is 10 and there are 50 pages, the page range will be "
"``[1, 2, '…', 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, '…', 49, 50]``. This will result in "
"pages 7, 8, and 9 to the left of and 11, 12, and 13 to the right of the "
"current page as well as pages 1 and 2 at the start and 49 and 50 at the end."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, leis na luachanna réamhshocraithe do ``on_each_side`` agus "
"``on_ends``, má tá an leathanach reatha 10 agus má tá 50 leathanach ann, "
"beidh raon an leathanaigh ``[1, 2, '...', 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, '...', "
"49, 50]``. Mar thoradh air seo beidh leathanaigh 7, 8, agus 9 ar thaobh na "
"láimhe clé de agus 11, 12, agus 13 ar dheis den leathanach reatha chomh "
"maith le leathanaigh 1 agus 2 ag an tús agus 49 agus 50 ag an deireadh."

msgid "Raises :exc:`InvalidPage` if the given page number doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe:exc: `Invalidpage` mura bhfuil an uimhir leathanaigh thugtar ann."

msgid ""
"A translatable string used as a substitute for elided page numbers in the "
"page range returned by :meth:`~Paginator.get_elided_page_range`. Default is "
"``'…'``."
msgstr ""
"Sreang inaistrithe a úsáidtear mar ionad d'uimhreacha leathanaigh éilithe sa "
"raon leathanaigh ar ais ag: meth: `~paginator.get_elided_page_range`. Is é "
"réamhshocraithe ``'... '``."

msgid "The total number of objects, across all pages."
msgstr "Líon iomlán na rudaí, ar fud na leathanaigh go léir."

msgid ""
"When determining the number of objects contained in ``object_list``, "
"``Paginator`` will first try calling ``object_list.count()``. If "
"``object_list`` has no ``count()`` method, then ``Paginator`` will fall back "
"to using ``len(object_list)``. This allows objects, such as ``QuerySet``, to "
"use a more efficient ``count()`` method when available."
msgstr ""
"Agus líon na rudaí atá i `object_list`` á chinneadh, déanfaidh `Paginator`` "
"iarracht ar ``object_list.count () ``a ghlaoch ar dtús. Mura bhfuil modh "
"``count () ``ag `object_list``, ansin tiocfaidh ``Paginator`` ar ais ar "
"``len (object_list)`` a úsáid. Ligeann sé seo do rudaí, mar shampla "
"``QuerySet`, modh ``count () ``níos éifeachtaí a úsáid nuair atá ar fáil."

msgid "The total number of pages."
msgstr "Líon iomlán na leathanaigh."

msgid ""
"A 1-based range iterator of page numbers, e.g. yielding ``[1, 2, 3, 4]``."
msgstr ""
"Athraitheoir raon 1-bhunaithe d'uimhreacha leathanaigh, m.sh. ag toradh "
"``[1, 2, 3, 4]``."

msgid "``Page`` class"
msgstr "Aicme ``Leathanach``"

msgid ""
"You usually won't construct ``Page`` objects by hand -- you'll get them by "
"iterating :class:`Paginator`, or by using :meth:`Paginator.page`."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth ní thógfaidh tú rudaí ``Page`` de láimh - gheobhaidh tú iad "
"trí:class: `Paginator` a athrá, nó trí:meth: `Paginator.page` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"A page acts like a sequence of :attr:`Page.object_list` when using ``len()`` "
"or iterating it directly."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn leathanach cosúil le seicheamh de:attr: `Page.Object_List` nuair "
"a úsáidtear `len () ``nó ag athrá go díreach é."

msgid "Returns ``True`` if there's a next page."
msgstr "Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá an chéad leathanach eile ann."

msgid "Returns ``True`` if there's a previous page."
msgstr "Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá leathanach roimhe seo ann."

msgid "Returns ``True`` if there's a next **or** previous page."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá an chéad leathanach eile **nó ** roimhe seo "
"ann."

msgid ""
"Returns the next page number. Raises :exc:`InvalidPage` if next page doesn't "
"exist."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an chéad uimhir leathanaigh eile ar ais. Ardaithe:exc: `Invalidpage` "
"mura bhfuil an chéad leathanach eile ann."

msgid ""
"Returns the previous page number. Raises :exc:`InvalidPage` if previous page "
"doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Tugann uimhir leathanaigh roimhe seo ar ais. Ardaithe:exc: `InvalidPage` "
"mura bhfuil an leathanach roimhe seo ann."

msgid ""
"Returns the 1-based index of the first object on the page, relative to all "
"of the objects in the paginator's list. For example, when paginating a list "
"of 5 objects with 2 objects per page, the second "
"page's :meth:`~Page.start_index` would return ``3``."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé innéacs 1-bhunaithe an chéad réad ar an leathanach, i gcoibhneas "
"leis na rudaí go léir i liosta an paginéora. Mar shampla, nuair a bheidh "
"liosta de 5 rud á ndéanamh leathanaigh le 2 rud in aghaidh an leathanaigh, "
"chuirfeadh an dara leathanach's:meth: `~page.start_index` ar ais ``3``."

msgid ""
"Returns the 1-based index of the last object on the page, relative to all of "
"the objects in the paginator's list. For example, when paginating a list of "
"5 objects with 2 objects per page, the second page's :meth:`~Page.end_index` "
"would return ``4``."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an t-innéacs 1-bhunaithe den réad deireanach ar an leathanach, i "
"gcoibhneas leis na rudaí go léir i liosta an leathanaigh. Mar shampla, nuair "
"a chuirtear liosta de 5 rud le 2 rud in aghaidh an leathanaigh á leathanaigh "
"á leathanaigh, chuirfeadh an dara leathanach's:meth: `~page.end_index` ar "
"ais ``4``."

msgid "The list of objects on this page."
msgstr "An liosta na rudaí ar an leathanach seo."

msgid "The 1-based page number for this page."
msgstr "An uimhir leathanaigh 1-bhunaithe don leathanach seo."

msgid "The associated :class:`Paginator` object."
msgstr "An réad comhcheangail:class: `Paginator`."

msgid ""
"A base class for exceptions raised when a paginator is passed an invalid "
"page number."
msgstr ""
"Aicme bonn le haghaidh eisceachtaí a ardaítear nuair a chuirtear uimhir "
"leathanaigh neamhbhailí ar phaginator."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`Paginator.page` method raises an exception if the requested page "
"is invalid (i.e. not an integer) or contains no objects. Generally, it's "
"enough to catch the ``InvalidPage`` exception, but if you'd like more "
"granularity, you can catch either of the following exceptions:"
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn an modh: Meth: `Paginator.page` eisceacht mura bhfuil an leathanach "
"iarrtha neamhbhailí (ie nach sláimhir) nó nach bhfuil aon rudaí ann. Go "
"ginearálta, is leor an eisceacht ``Invalidpage`` a ghabháil, ach más mian "
"leat níos mó gráinneachta, is féidir leat ceachtar de na heisceachtaí seo a "
"leanas a ghabháil:"

msgid ""
"Raised when :meth:`~Paginator.page` is given a value that isn't an integer."
msgstr "Ardaítear nuai:meth: `~Paginator.page` tugtar luach nach sláimhir é."

msgid ""
"Raised when :meth:`~Paginator.page` is given a valid value but no objects "
"exist on that page."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear nuai:meth: `~Paginator.page` tugtar luach bailí ach níl aon rud "
"ann ar an leathanach sin."

msgid ""
"Both of the exceptions are subclasses of :exc:`InvalidPage`, so you can "
"handle them both with ``except InvalidPage``."
msgstr ""
"Is fo-aicmí iad an dá eisceacht de:exc: `InvalidPage`, ionas gur féidir leat "
"iad a láimhseáil le ``ach amháin InvalidPage``."

msgid "Request and response objects"
msgstr "Rudaí iarratais agus freagartha"

msgid "Quick overview"
msgstr "Forbhreathnú tapa"

msgid ""
"Django uses request and response objects to pass state through the system."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django rudaí iarratais agus freagartha chun stát a rith tríd an "
"gcóras."

msgid ""
"When a page is requested, Django creates an :class:`HttpRequest` object that "
"contains metadata about the request. Then Django loads the appropriate view, "
"passing the :class:`HttpRequest` as the first argument to the view function. "
"Each view is responsible for returning an :class:`HttpResponse` object."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a iarrtar leathanach, cruthaíonn Django réad: class: `HttpRequest` ina "
"bhfuil meiteashonraí faoin iarratas. Ansin luchtaíonn Django an dearcadh "
"cuí, ag rith an:class: `HttpRequest` mar an chéad argóint chuig an bhfeidhm "
"amharc. Tá gach radharc freagrach as réad: class: `HttpResponse` a thabhairt "
"ar ais."

msgid ""
"This document explains the APIs for :class:`HttpRequest` "
"and :class:`HttpResponse` objects, which are defined in "
"the :mod:`django.http` module."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo na APIs le haghaidh rudaí: class: `HttpRequest` "
"agus:class: `HttpResponse`, atá sainmhínithe sa mhodúl:mod: `django.http`."

msgid "``HttpRequest`` objects"
msgstr "``HttpRequest`` rudaí"

msgid "All attributes should be considered read-only, unless stated otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir gach tréith a mheas go léite amháin, mura luaitear a mhalairt."

msgid ""
"A string representing the scheme of the request (``http`` or ``https`` "
"usually)."
msgstr "Sreang a léiríonn scéim an iarratais (``http`` nó `https`` de ghnáth)."

msgid ""
"The raw HTTP request body as a bytestring. This is useful for processing "
"data in different ways than conventional HTML forms: binary images, XML "
"payload etc. For processing conventional form data, "
"use :attr:`HttpRequest.POST`."
msgstr ""
"An comhlacht iarratais amh-HTTP mar bytestring. Tá sé seo úsáideach chun "
"sonraí a phróiseáil ar bhealaí éagsúla ná foirmeacha traidisiúnta HTML: "
"íomhánna dénártha, ualach pá XML srl Chun sonraí foirme traidisiúnta a "
"phróiseáil, bain úsáid as: attr: `HttpRequest.post`."

msgid ""
"You can also read from an ``HttpRequest`` using a file-like interface "
"with :meth:`HttpRequest.read` or :meth:`HttpRequest.readline`. Accessing the "
"``body`` attribute *after* reading the request with either of these I/O "
"stream methods will produce a ``RawPostDataException``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat léamh freisin ó `HttpRequest`` ag baint úsáide as comhéadan "
"cosúil le comhad le:meth: `HttpRequest.read` nó:meth: "
"`HttpRequest.readline`. Tabharfar ``RawPostDataException`` a rochtain ar an "
"tréith ``corp ``*tar éis * an iarraidh a léamh le ceachtar de na modhanna "
"srutha I/O seo."

msgid ""
"A string representing the full path to the requested page, not including the "
"scheme, domain, or query string."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an cosán iomlán chuig an leathanach iarrtha, gan an scéim, "
"an fearann nó an teaghrán fiosrúcháin san áireamh."

msgid "Example: ``\"/music/bands/the_beatles/\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” /ceol/banda/the_beatles/\"``"

msgid ""
"Under some web server configurations, the portion of the URL after the host "
"name is split up into a script prefix portion and a path info portion. The "
"``path_info`` attribute always contains the path info portion of the path, "
"no matter what web server is being used. Using this instead "
"of :attr:`~HttpRequest.path` can make your code easier to move between test "
"and deployment servers."
msgstr ""
"Faoi roinnt cumraíochtaí freastalaí gréasáin, roinntear an chuid den URL tar "
"éis an ainm óstach i gcuid réimír script agus i gcuid faisnéise cosáin. Tá "
"an chuid faisnéise cosáin den chosán sa tréith `path_info`` i gcónaí, is "
"cuma cén freastalaí gréasáin atá á úsáid. Ag baint úsáide as seo in "
"ionad:attr: `~httpRequest.path` is féidir le do chód a dhéanamh níos éasca "
"bogadh idir freastalaithe tástála agus imscartha."

msgid ""
"For example, if the ``WSGIScriptAlias`` for your application is set to ``\"/"
"minfo\"``, then ``path`` might be ``\"/minfo/music/bands/the_beatles/\"`` "
"and ``path_info`` would be ``\"/music/bands/the_beatles/\"``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá an ``WSGiscriptalias`` d'iarratas socraithe go ``” /"
"minfo\"``, ansin d'fhéadfadh ``path`` a bheith``” /minfo/music/bands/"
"the_beatles/\"`` agus `path_info`` a bheadh ``” /music/bands/the_beatles/"
"\"``."

msgid ""
"A string representing the HTTP method used in the request. This is "
"guaranteed to be uppercase. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an modh HTTP a úsáidtear san iarratas. Ráthaítear go "
"mbeidh sé seo uachtaracha. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"A string representing the current encoding used to decode form submission "
"data (or ``None``, which means the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting is "
"used). You can write to this attribute to change the encoding used when "
"accessing the form data. Any subsequent attribute accesses (such as reading "
"from :attr:`GET` or :attr:`POST`) will use the new ``encoding`` value. "
"Useful if you know the form data is not in the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` "
"encoding."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an t-ionchódú reatha a úsáidtear chun sonraí aighneachta "
"foirme a dhíchódú (nó ``None``, rud a chiallaíonn an socrú: "
"`DEFAULT_CHARSET` a úsáidtear an socrú: `DEFAULT_CHARSET`). Féadfaidh tú "
"scríobh chuig an tréith seo chun an t-ionchódú a úsáidtear a athrú agus tú "
"ag rochtain ar shonraí Úsáidfidh aon rochtain tréithe ina dhiaidh sin (mar "
"shampla léamh ó:attr: `GET` nó: attr: `POST `) an luach ``encoding`` nua. "
"Úsáideach má tá a fhios agat nach bhfuil na sonraí foirme san ionchódú: "
"setting: `DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid ""
"A string representing the MIME type of the request, parsed from the "
"``CONTENT_TYPE`` header."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn cineál MIME an iarratais, a pháirsítear ón gceannteideal "
"``CONTENT_TYPE``."

msgid ""
"A dictionary of key/value parameters included in the ``CONTENT_TYPE`` header."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir de pharaiméadair eochair/luacha atá san áireamh sa cheanntásc "
"``CONTENT_TYPE``."

msgid ""
"A dictionary-like object containing all given HTTP GET parameters. See "
"the :class:`QueryDict` documentation below."
msgstr ""
"Rud cosúil le foclóir ina bhfuil gach paraiméadar HTTP GET a thugtar. Féach "
"an doiciméadúint:class: `QueryDict` thíos."

msgid ""
"A dictionary-like object containing all given HTTP POST parameters, "
"providing that the request contains form data. See the :class:`QueryDict` "
"documentation below. If you need to access raw or non-form data posted in "
"the request, access this through the :attr:`HttpRequest.body` attribute "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Rud cosúil le foclóir ina bhfuil gach paraiméadar HTTP POST a thugtar, ar "
"choinníoll go bhfuil sonraí foirme san iarratas. Féach an "
"doiciméadach:class: `QueryDict` thíos. Más gá duit rochtain a fháil ar "
"shonraí amha nó neamh-fhoirme a chuirtear san iarratas, rochtain a fháil air "
"seo tríd an tréith: attr: `HttpRequest.body `ina ionad."

msgid ""
"It's possible that a request can come in via POST with an empty ``POST`` "
"dictionary -- if, say, a form is requested via the POST HTTP method but does "
"not include form data. Therefore, you shouldn't use ``if request.POST`` to "
"check for use of the POST method; instead, use ``if request.method == "
"\"POST\"`` (see :attr:`HttpRequest.method`)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir go bhféadfadh iarratas teacht isteach trí POST le foclóir folamh "
"``POST ``- má iarrtar foirm tríd an modh POST HTTP ach nach bhfuil sonraí "
"foirme san áireamh ann. Dá bhrí sin, níor chóir duit `if request.post`` a "
"úsáid chun seiceáil maidir le húsáid an modh POST; ina ionad sin, bain úsáid "
"as ``if request.method == “POST\"`` (féach: attr: `HttpRequest.method`)."

msgid "``POST`` does *not* include file-upload information. See :attr:`FILES`."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuimsíonn ``POST ```` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` `` ` Féach: attr: "
"`COMHAID`."

msgid "A dictionary containing all cookies. Keys and values are strings."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil na fianáin go léir. Is teaghráin iad eochracha agus "
"luachanna."

msgid ""
"A dictionary-like object containing all uploaded files. Each key in "
"``FILES`` is the ``name`` from the ``<input type=\"file\" name=\"\">``. Each "
"value in ``FILES`` is "
"an :class:`~django.core.files.uploadedfile.UploadedFile`."
msgstr ""
"Rud cosúil le foclóir ina bhfuil gach comhad uaslódáilte. <input "
"type=\"file\" name=\"\">Is é gach eochair i `FILES`` an `ainm ```` ón ```` "
"`` `. Is é gach luach i `FILES`` ná: aicme: "
"`~django.core.files.uploadedfile.uploadedfile`."

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/files` for more information."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/topics/files` le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid ""
"``FILES`` will only contain data if the request method was POST and the "
"``<form>`` that posted to the request had ``enctype=\"multipart/form-"
"data\"``. Otherwise, ``FILES`` will be a blank dictionary-like object."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh sonraí i ``FILES`` ach amháin má bhí POST an modh iarratais agus "
"má bhí ``enctype=\"multipart/form-data\"`` ag an ``<form>`` a chuir post "
"chuig an iarraidh. Seachas sin, is réad bán cosúil le foclóir é `FILES``."

msgid ""
"A dictionary containing all available HTTP headers. Available headers depend "
"on the client and server, but here are some examples:"
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil gach ceanntásc HTTP atá ar fáil. Braitheann ceanntála atá "
"ar fáil ar an gcliant agus ar an bhfreastalaí, ach seo roinnt samplaí:"

msgid "``CONTENT_LENGTH`` -- The length of the request body (as a string)."
msgstr "``CONTENT_LENGTH`` - Fad an chomhlachta iarratais (mar shreang)."

msgid "``CONTENT_TYPE`` -- The MIME type of the request body."
msgstr "``CONTENT_TYPE`` - Cineál MIME an chomhlachta iarratais."

msgid "``HTTP_ACCEPT`` -- Acceptable content types for the response."
msgstr "``HTTP_ACCEPT`` - Cineálacha ábhair inghlactha don fhreagra."

msgid "``HTTP_ACCEPT_ENCODING`` -- Acceptable encodings for the response."
msgstr "``HTTP_ACCEPT_ENCODING`` - Ionchódaithe inghlactha don fhreagra."

msgid "``HTTP_ACCEPT_LANGUAGE`` -- Acceptable languages for the response."
msgstr "``HTTP_ACCEPT_LANGUAGE`` -- Teangacha inghlactha don fhreagra."

msgid "``HTTP_HOST`` -- The HTTP Host header sent by the client."
msgstr "``HTTP_HOST`` - An ceannteideal Óstach HTTP a sheol an cliant."

msgid "``HTTP_REFERER`` -- The referring page, if any."
msgstr "``HTTP_REFERER`` - An leathanach tagartha, más ann."

msgid "``HTTP_USER_AGENT`` -- The client's user-agent string."
msgstr "``HTTP_USER_AGENT`` -- Sreang gníomhaire úsáideora an chliaint."

msgid "``QUERY_STRING`` -- The query string, as a single (unparsed) string."
msgstr ""
"``QUERY_STRING`` - An teaghrán fiosrúcháin, mar shreang aonair "
"(neamhpháirseáilte)."

msgid "``REMOTE_ADDR`` -- The IP address of the client."
msgstr "``REMOTE_ADDR`` - Seoladh IP an chliaint."

msgid "``REMOTE_HOST`` -- The hostname of the client."
msgstr "``REMOTE_HOST`` - Ainm óstach an chliaint."

msgid "``REMOTE_USER`` -- The user authenticated by the web server, if any."
msgstr ""
"``REMOTE_USER`` - An t-úsáideoir a fhíordheimhnigh an fhreastalaí gréasáin, "
"más ann."

msgid "``REQUEST_METHOD`` -- A string such as ``\"GET\"`` or ``\"POST\"``."
msgstr "``REQUEST_METHOD`` -- Sreang mar ``\"GET\"`` nó ``\"POST\"``."

msgid "``SERVER_NAME`` -- The hostname of the server."
msgstr "``SERVER_NAME`` - Ainm óstach an fhreastalaí."

msgid "``SERVER_PORT`` -- The port of the server (as a string)."
msgstr "``SERVER_PORT`` - Calafort an fhreastalaí (mar shreang)."

msgid ""
"With the exception of ``CONTENT_LENGTH`` and ``CONTENT_TYPE``, as given "
"above, any HTTP headers in the request are converted to ``META`` keys by "
"converting all characters to uppercase, replacing any hyphens with "
"underscores and adding an ``HTTP_`` prefix to the name. So, for example, a "
"header called ``X-Bender`` would be mapped to the ``META`` key "
"``HTTP_X_BENDER``."
msgstr ""
"Seachas ``CONTENT_LENGTH`` agus `CONTENT_TYPE``, mar a thugtar thuas, "
"déantar aon cheannteidil HTTP san iarratas a thiontú go heochracha `META`` "
"trí gach carachtar a thiontú go uachchlóir, béim a chur in ionad aon "
"bhreitheanna agus réimír `HTTP_`` a chur leis an ainm. Mar sin, mar shampla, "
"déanfaí ceanntásc ar a dtugtar ``X-Bender`` a mhapáil leis an eochair "
"``META`` ``HTTP_X_BENDER``."

msgid ""
"Note that :djadmin:`runserver` strips all headers with underscores in the "
"name, so you won't see them in ``META``. This prevents header-spoofing based "
"on ambiguity between underscores and dashes both being normalizing to "
"underscores in WSGI environment variables. It matches the behavior of web "
"servers like Nginx and Apache 2.4+."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go mbaineann: djadmin: `runserver` gach ceannteideal le "
"béim san ainm, ionas nach bhfeicfidh tú iad i `META``. Cuireann sé seo cosc "
"ar cheannteanntáil bunaithe ar dhébhríocht idir béim agus scaoileanna araon "
"ag normalú le béim i n-athróga timpeallachta WSGI. Meaitseálann sé le "
"hiompar freastalaithe gréasáin cosúil le Nginx agus Apache 2.4+."

msgid ""
":attr:`HttpRequest.headers` is a simpler way to access all HTTP-prefixed "
"headers, plus ``CONTENT_LENGTH`` and ``CONTENT_TYPE``."
msgstr ""
":attr: Is bealach níos simplí é `HttpRequest.headers` chun rochtain a fháil "
"ar gach ceannteideal réamhshocraithe HTTP, móide ``CONTENT_LENGTH`` agus "
"``CONTENT_TYPE``."

msgid ""
"A case insensitive, dict-like object that provides access to all HTTP-"
"prefixed headers (plus ``Content-Length`` and ``Content-Type``) from the "
"request."
msgstr ""
"Rud cás-neamh-íogair, cosúil le dict a sholáthraíonn rochtain ar gach "
"ceannteideal réamhshocraithe HTTP (móide ``Content-Fad ``agus ``Content-"
"Type``) ón iarratas."

msgid ""
"The name of each header is stylized with title-casing (e.g. ``User-Agent``) "
"when it's displayed. You can access headers case-insensitively:"
msgstr ""
"Déantar ainm gach ceanntásc a stíliú le teidil cásáil (m.sh. ``Gníomhaire "
"Usáideora ``) nuair a thaispeántar é. Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar "
"cheanntásca go mí-íogair:"

msgid ""
"For use in, for example, Django templates, headers can also be looked up "
"using underscores in place of hyphens:"
msgstr ""
"Le húsáid i dteimpléid Django, mar shampla, is féidir ceanntásca a fheiceáil "
"suas freisin ag baint úsáide as béim in ionad hiphens:"

msgid ""
"An instance of :class:`~django.urls.ResolverMatch` representing the resolved "
"URL. This attribute is only set after URL resolving took place, which means "
"it's available in all views but not in middleware which are executed before "
"URL resolving takes place (you can use it in :meth:`process_view` though)."
msgstr ""
"Sampla de:class: `~django.urls.resolverMatch` a léiríonn an URL réitithe. Ní "
"shocraítear an tréith seo ach tar éis réiteach URL a dhéanamh, rud a "
"chiallaíonn go bhfuil sé ar fáil i ngach radharc ach ní i lár a "
"fhorghníomhaítear sula ndéantar réiteach URL (is féidir leat é a úsáid "
"in:meth: `process_view` áfach)."

msgid "Attributes set by application code"
msgstr "Tréithe socraithe de réir cód iarratais"

msgid ""
"Django doesn't set these attributes itself but makes use of them if set by "
"your application."
msgstr ""
"Ní shocraíonn Django na tréithe seo féin ach úsáideann sé iad má shocraíonn "
"d'fheidhmchlár iad."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`url` template tag will use its value as the ``current_app`` "
"argument to :func:`~django.urls.reverse()`."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfidh an clib teimpléad:ttag: `url `a luach mar an argóint ``current_app "
"``to:func: `~django.urls.reverse ()`."

msgid ""
"This will be used as the root URLconf for the current request, overriding "
"the :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF` setting. See :ref:`how-django-processes-a-"
"request` for details."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear é seo mar an URLConf fréimhe don iarratas reatha, ag cur thar an "
"socrú: setting: `ROOT_URLCONF`. Féach: ref: `how django-processes-a-request` "
"le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"``urlconf`` can be set to ``None`` to revert any changes made by previous "
"middleware and return to using the :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir ``urlconf`` a shocrú go ``None`` chun aon athruithe a rinne "
"middleware roimhe seo a chur ar ais agus filleadh ar an: setting: "
"`ROOT_URLCONF` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"This will be used instead of :setting:`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER` "
"for the current request. See :ref:`custom-error-reports` for details."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear é seo in ionad:setting: `DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER` don "
"iarratas reatha. Féach: Ref: `custom-earror-reports `le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"This will be used instead of :setting:`DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER` for the "
"current request. See :ref:`custom-error-reports` for details."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear é seo in ionad:setting: `DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER` don iarratas "
"reatha. Féach: Ref: `custom-earror-reports `le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Attributes set by middleware"
msgstr "Tréithe arna leagan síos ag middleware"

msgid ""
"Some of the middleware included in Django's contrib apps set attributes on "
"the request. If you don't see the attribute on a request, be sure the "
"appropriate middleware class is listed in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn cuid de na middleware atá san áireamh in aipeanna contrib Django "
"tréithe ar an iarratas. Mura bhfeiceann tú an tréith ar iarratas, bí cinnte "
"go bhfuil an rang lár-earraí cuí liostaithe in:setting: `MIDDLEWARE`."

msgid ""
"From the :class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware`: A "
"readable and writable, dictionary-like object that represents the current "
"session."
msgstr ""
"Ón:class: `~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware`: Rud "
"inléite agus inscríofa, cosúil le foclóir a léiríonn an seisiún reatha."

msgid ""
"From the :class:`~django.contrib.sites.middleware.CurrentSiteMiddleware`: An "
"instance of :class:`~django.contrib.sites.models.Site` "
"or :class:`~django.contrib.sites.requests.RequestSite` as returned "
"by :func:`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site()` representing "
"the current site."
msgstr ""
"Ón:class: `~django.contrib.sites.middleware.currentsiteMiddleware`: Sampla "
"de:class: `~django.contrib.sites.models.site` nó:class: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.requestsite` mar a thug ar ais ar:func: "
"`~django.contrib.sites.shortcuts.get_current_site () `a léiríonn an "
"láithreán reatha."

msgid ""
"From the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`: "
"An instance of :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` representing the currently logged-"
"in user. If the user isn't currently logged in, ``user`` will be set to an "
"instance of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AnonymousUser`. You can tell "
"them apart with :attr:`~django.contrib.auth.models.User.is_authenticated`, "
"like so::"
msgstr ""
"Ón:class: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`: Sampla "
"de:setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL` a léiríonn an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach "
"faoi láthair. Mura bhfuil an t-úsáideoir logáilte isteach faoi láthair, "
"socraítear ``user`` ar shampla de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.anonymousUser`. Is féidir leat iad a insint óna "
"chéile la:attr: `~django.contrib.auth.models.user.is_Authenticated`, mar sin:"

msgid ""
"The :meth:`auser` method does the same thing but can be used from async "
"contexts."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an modh: Meth: `auser` an rud céanna ach is féidir é a úsáid ó "
"chomhthéacsanna async."

msgid ""
"From the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`: "
"Coroutine. Returns an instance of :setting:`AUTH_USER_MODEL` representing "
"the currently logged-in user. If the user isn't currently logged in, "
"``auser`` will return an instance "
"of :class:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AnonymousUser`. This is similar to "
"the :attr:`user` attribute but it works in async contexts."
msgstr ""
"Ón:aicme: `~django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware`: "
"Coroutine. Tugann sé sampla de:setting: `AUTH_USER_MODEL` a léiríonn an t-"
"úsáideoir atá logáilte isteach faoi láthair. Mura bhfuil an t-úsáideoir "
"logáilte isteach faoi láthair, cuirfidh ``auser`` sampla de:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.anonymousUser` ar ais. Tá sé seo cosúil leis an "
"tréith: attr: `user` ach oibríonn sé i gcomhthéacsanna async."

msgid ""
"Returns the originating host of the request using information from the "
"``HTTP_X_FORWARDED_HOST`` (if :setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` is enabled) "
"and ``HTTP_HOST`` headers, in that order. If they don't provide a value, the "
"method uses a combination of ``SERVER_NAME`` and ``SERVER_PORT`` as detailed "
"in :pep:`3333`."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé óstach tionscnaimh an iarratais ag baint úsáide as faisnéis ó na "
"ceannteidil ``HTTP_X_FORWARDED_HOST`` (ife:setting: `USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` "
"cumasaithe) agus `HTTP_HOST``, san ord sin. Mura soláthraíonn siad luach, "
"úsáideann an modh teaglaim de ``SERVER_NAME`` agus ``SERVER_PORT`` mar a "
"mionsonraítear in:pep: `3333`."

msgid "Example: ``\"127.0.0.1:8000\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``\"127.0.0. 1:8000 “``"

msgid ""
"Raises ``django.core.exceptions.DisallowedHost`` if the host is not "
"in :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS` or the domain name is invalid according "
"to :rfc:`1034`/:rfc:`1035 <1035>`."
msgstr ""
"<1035>Ardaíonn sé ``django.core.exceptions.disallowedHost`` mura bhfuil an t-"
"óstach in:setting: `ALLOWED_HOSTS` nó go bhfuil an t-ainm fearainn "
"neamhbhailí de réir: rfc: `1034`/:rfc: `1035`."

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~HttpRequest.get_host()` method fails when the host is behind "
"multiple proxies. One solution is to use middleware to rewrite the proxy "
"headers, as in the following example::"
msgstr ""
"Teipeann ar an modh: Meth: `~HttpRequest.get_host () `nuair a bhíonn an t-"
"óstach taobh thiar de iolracha seachfhreastaí. Réiteach amháin is ea "
"middleware a úsáid chun na ceannteidil seachfhreastalaí a athscríobh, mar "
"atá sa sampla seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"This middleware should be positioned before any other middleware that relies "
"on the value of :meth:`~HttpRequest.get_host()` -- for "
"instance, :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` "
"or :class:`~django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware`."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir an middleware seo a shuíomh roimh aon mheán-earraí eile atá ag "
"brath ar luach: `~HttpRequest.get_host () `-- mar shampla, :class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` nó:class: "
"`~django.middleware.csrfviewMiddleware`."

msgid ""
"Returns the originating port of the request using information from the "
"``HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PORT`` (if :setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT` is enabled) "
"and ``SERVER_PORT`` ``META`` variables, in that order."
msgstr ""
"Tugann calafort tionscnaimh an iarratais ar ais ag baint úsáide as faisnéis "
"ó na hathróga `HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PORT`` (ife:setting: `USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT` "
"cumasaithe) agus ``SERVER_PORT`` ``META`` athróga, san ord sin."

msgid "Returns the ``path``, plus an appended query string, if applicable."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an ``path`` ar ais, móide teaghrán ceisteanna curtha leis, más "
"infheidhme."

msgid "Example: ``\"/music/bands/the_beatles/?print=true\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” /ceol/banda/the_beatles/? print=true\"``"

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`get_full_path`, but uses :attr:`path_info` instead "
"of :attr:`path`."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `get_full_path`, ach úsáideann sé: attr: `path_info` in "
"ionad:attr: `path`."

msgid "Example: ``\"/minfo/music/bands/the_beatles/?print=true\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” /minfo/music/banna/the_beatles/? print=true\"``"

msgid ""
"Returns the absolute URI form of ``location``. If no location is provided, "
"the location will be set to ``request.get_full_path()``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an fhoirm iomlán URI de ``suíomh ``ar ais. Mura gcuirtear aon "
"suíomh ar fáil, socraítear an suíomh go ``request.get_full_path () ``."

msgid ""
"If the location is already an absolute URI, it will not be altered. "
"Otherwise the absolute URI is built using the server variables available in "
"this request. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Más URI iomlán é an suíomh cheana féin, ní athrófar é. Seachas sin tógtar an "
"URI iomlán ag baint úsáide as na hathróga freastalaí atá ar fáil san "
"iarratas seo. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Mixing HTTP and HTTPS on the same site is discouraged, "
"therefore :meth:`~HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri()` will always generate an "
"absolute URI with the same scheme the current request has. If you need to "
"redirect users to HTTPS, it's best to let your web server redirect all HTTP "
"traffic to HTTPS."
msgstr ""
"Tá díspreagadh HTTP agus HTTPS a mheascadh ar an suíomh céanna, mar sin "
"ginfidh: meth: `~HttpRequest.build_absolute_URI () `URI iomlán i gcónaí leis "
"an scéim chéanna atá ag an iarratas reatha. Más gá duit úsáideoirí a atreorú "
"chuig HTTPS, is fearr ligean do do fhreastalaí gréasáin gach trácht HTTP a "
"atreorú chuig HTTPS."

msgid ""
"Returns a cookie value for a signed cookie, or raises a "
"``django.core.signing.BadSignature`` exception if the signature is no longer "
"valid. If you provide the ``default`` argument the exception will be "
"suppressed and that default value will be returned instead."
msgstr ""
"Tugann luach fianán ar ais do fhianán sínithe, nó ardaíonn sé eisceacht "
"``django.core.signing.badsignature`` mura bhfuil an síniú bailí a "
"thuilleadh. Má sholáthraíonn tú an argóint ``réamhshocraithe`` cuirfear an t-"
"eisceacht faoi chois agus cuirfear an luach réamhshocraithe sin ar ais ina "
"ionad sin."

msgid ""
"The optional ``salt`` argument can be used to provide extra protection "
"against brute force attacks on your secret key. If supplied, the ``max_age`` "
"argument will be checked against the signed timestamp attached to the cookie "
"value to ensure the cookie is not older than ``max_age`` seconds."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an argóint roghnach `salann` a úsáid chun cosaint bhreise a "
"sholáthar i gcoinne ionsaithe fórsa brúite ar d'eochair rúnda. Má "
"sholáthraítear é, déanfar an argóint ``max_age`` a sheiceáil i gcoinne an "
"stampa ama sínithe atá ceangailte leis an luach fianáin chun a chinntiú nach "
"bhfuil an fianán níos sine ná ``max_age`` soicind."

msgid ""
"See :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/signing>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `síniú cripteagrafach' le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise. </topics/"
"signing>"

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the request is secure; that is, if it was made with "
"HTTPS."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá an t-iarratas slán; is é sin, má rinneadh é "
"le HTTPS."

msgid ""
"Returns the preferred mime type from ``media_types``, based on the "
"``Accept`` header, or ``None`` if the client does not accept any of the "
"provided types."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Assuming the client sends an ``Accept`` header of ``text/html,application/"
"json;q=0.8``:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the mime type includes parameters, these are also considered when "
"determining the preferred media type. For example, with an ``Accept`` header "
"of ``text/vcard;version=3.0,text/html;q=0.5``, the return value of "
"``request.get_preferred_type()`` depends on the available media types:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"(For further details on how content negotiation is performed, "
"see :rfc:`9110#section-12.5.1`.)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
