"``HttpRequest`` a chur ar aghaidh go díreach chuig parser XML amsúil:class: "
"`~xml.etree.elementTree.ElementTree`::"

msgid "``QueryDict`` objects"
msgstr "Rud ``Querydict``"

msgid ""
"In an :class:`HttpRequest` object, the :attr:`~HttpRequest.GET` "
"and :attr:`~HttpRequest.POST` attributes are instances of "
"``django.http.QueryDict``, a dictionary-like class customized to deal with "
"multiple values for the same key. This is necessary because some HTML form "
"elements, notably ``<select multiple>``, pass multiple values for the same "
"key."
msgstr ""
"I réad:class: `HttpRequest`, is cásanna de `Django.http.QueryDict`` iad "
"tréithe: `~HttpRequest.Get` agus:attr: `~HttpRequest.post `, aicme cosúil le "
"foclóir saincheaptha chun déileáil le luachanna iolracha don eochair "
"chéanna. Tá sé seo riachtanach toisc go dtéann roinnt eilimintí foirme HTML, "
"go háiri <select multiple>the ```, luachanna iolracha don eochair chéanna."

msgid ""
"The ``QueryDict``\\ s at ``request.POST`` and ``request.GET`` will be "
"immutable when accessed in a normal request/response cycle. To get a mutable "
"version you need to use :meth:`QueryDict.copy`."
msgstr ""
"Beidh na `QueryDict``\\ s ag `Request.Post`` agus ``Request.Get`` "
"inathraithe nuair a bhíonn rochtain orthu i ngnáthtimthriall iarrata/"
"freagartha. Chun leagan inathraithe a fháil ní mór duit: meth: "
"`Querydict.copy` a úsáid."

msgid ""
":class:`QueryDict` implements all the standard dictionary methods because "
"it's a subclass of dictionary. Exceptions are outlined here:"
msgstr ""
":class: Cuireann `QueryDict` na modhanna caighdeánacha foclóra go léir i "
"bhfeidhm toisc gur fo-aicme fo-fhoclóir é. Tá eisceachtaí leagtha amach "
"anseo:"

msgid "Instantiates a ``QueryDict`` object based on ``query_string``."
msgstr "Cuireann sé réad ``Querydict`` bunaithe ar ``query_string``."

msgid ""
"If ``query_string`` is not passed in, the resulting ``QueryDict`` will be "
"empty (it will have no keys or values)."
msgstr ""
"Mura gcuirtear ``query_string`` isteach, beidh an `Querydict`` mar thoradh "
"air folamh (ní bheidh aon eochracha ná luachanna aige)."

msgid ""
"Most ``QueryDict``\\ s you encounter, and in particular those at "
"``request.POST`` and ``request.GET``, will be immutable. If you are "
"instantiating one yourself, you can make it mutable by passing "
"``mutable=True`` to its ``__init__()``."
msgstr ""
"Beidh an chuid is mó de ``Querydict`` a thagann leat, agus go háirithe iad "
"siúd ag ``Request.Post`` agus ``Request.Get``, neathraithe. Má tá ceann á "
"dhéanamh agat féin, is féidir leat é a dhéanamh inathraithe trí "
"``mutable=True`` a chur chuig a ``__init__ () ``."

msgid ""
"Strings for setting both keys and values will be converted from ``encoding`` "
"to ``str``. If ``encoding`` is not set, it defaults "
"to :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET`."
msgstr ""
"Déanfar teaghráin chun eochracha agus luachanna a shocrú a thiontú ó "
"``encoding`` go `str``. Mura bhfuil ``encoding`` socraithe, déanann sé "
"réamhshocraithe:setting: `DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid ""
"Creates a new ``QueryDict`` with keys from ``iterable`` and each value equal "
"to ``value``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé ``QueryDict`` nua le heochracha ó ``iterable`` agus gach luach "
"atá comhionann le ``luach``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Returns the last value for the given key; or an empty list (``[]``) if the "
"key exists but has no values. Raises "
"``django.utils.datastructures.MultiValueDictKeyError`` if the key does not "
"exist. (This is a subclass of Python's standard :exc:`KeyError`, so you can "
"stick to catching ``KeyError``.)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sets the given key to ``[value]`` (a list whose single element is "
"``value``). Note that this, as other dictionary functions that have side "
"effects, can only be called on a mutable ``QueryDict`` (such as one that was "
"created via :meth:`QueryDict.copy`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an eochair a thugtar go ``[luach]`` (liosta a bhfuil a ghné aonair "
"``luach``). Tabhair faoi deara nach féidir é seo, mar fheidhmeanna foclóra "
"eile a bhfuil fo-iarsmaí acu, a ghlaoch ach ar `Querydict`` athraithe (mar "
"shampla ceann a cruthaíodh via: meth: `Querydict.copy`)."

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` if the given key is set. This lets you do, e.g., ``if "
"\"foo\" in request.GET``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ar ais ``True`` má tá an eochair tugtha socraithe. Ligeann sé seo "
"duit, m.sh., `if “foo” in request.get`` a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"Uses the same logic as :meth:`__getitem__`, with a hook for returning a "
"default value if the key doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé an loighic chéanna amha:meth: `__getitem__`, le crúca chun "
"luach réamhshocraithe a thabhairt ar ais mura bhfuil an eochair ann."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`dict.setdefault`, except it uses :meth:`__setitem__` internally."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `dict.setdefault`, ach amháin go n-úsáideann sé: meth: "
"`__setitem__` go hinmheánach."

msgid ""
"Takes either a ``QueryDict`` or a dictionary. Like :meth:`dict.update`, "
"except it *appends* to the current dictionary items rather than replacing "
"them. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé ``Querydict`` nó foclóir. Cosúil le: Meth: `dict.update`, seachas "
"aigh* cuireann sé leis na míreanna foclóra reatha seachas iad a chur in "
"ionad. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`dict.items`, except this uses the same last-value logic "
"as :meth:`__getitem__` and returns an iterator object instead of a view "
"object. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `dict.items`, ach amháin go n-úsáideann sé seo an loighic "
"luach deiridh céanna mar: meth: `__getitem__` agus filleann sé réad "
"athraitheora in ionad réad amharc. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`dict.values`, except this uses the same last-value logic "
"as :meth:`__getitem__` and returns an iterator instead of a view object. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `dict.values`, ach amháin go n-úsáideann sé seo an loighic "
"luach deiridh céanna mar: meth: `__getitem__` agus filleann sé athraitheoir "
"in ionad réad amharc. Mar shampla:"

msgid "In addition, ``QueryDict`` has the following methods:"
msgstr "Ina theannta sin, tá na modhanna seo a leanas ag ``Querydict``:"

msgid ""
"Returns a copy of the object using :func:`copy.deepcopy`. This copy will be "
"mutable even if the original was not."
msgstr ""
"Tugann cóip den réad ar ais ag baint úsáid:func: `copy.deepcopy`. Beidh an "
"cóip seo inathraithe fiú mura raibh an bunaidh."

msgid ""
"Returns a list of the data with the requested key. Returns an empty list if "
"the key doesn't exist and ``default`` is ``None``. It's guaranteed to return "
"a list unless the default value provided isn't a list."
msgstr ""
"Tugann liosta de na sonraí ar ais leis an eochair iarrtha. Tugann liosta "
"folamh ar ais mura bhfuil an eochair ann agus is é ``réamhshocraithe`` "
"``None``. Ráthaítear liosta a thabhairt ar ais mura bhfuil liosta an luach "
"réamhshocraithe a chuirtear ar fáil."

msgid "Sets the given key to ``list_`` (unlike :meth:`__setitem__`)."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an eochair a thugtar go ``list_`` (gan cosúil: meth: "
"`__setitem__`)."

msgid "Appends an item to the internal list associated with key."
msgstr "Cuireann sé mír leis an liosta inmheánach a bhaineann leis an eochair."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`setdefault`, except it takes a list of values instead of a "
"single value."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `setdefault`, ach amháin go dtógann sé liosta luachanna in "
"ionad luach amháin."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`items()`, except it includes all values, as a list, for each "
"member of the dictionary. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `items () `, ach amháin go n-áirítear leis na luachanna go "
"léir, mar liosta, do gach ball den fhoclóir. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Returns a list of values for the given key and removes them from the "
"dictionary. Raises ``KeyError`` if the key does not exist. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann liosta luachanna ar ais don eochair a thugtar agus baineann sé iad ón "
"bhfoclóir. Ardaíonn sé ``Keyerror`` mura bhfuil an eochair ann. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Removes an arbitrary member of the dictionary (since there's no concept of "
"ordering), and returns a two value tuple containing the key and a list of "
"all values for the key. Raises ``KeyError`` when called on an empty "
"dictionary. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé ball treallach den fhoclóir (ós rud é nach bhfuil aon choincheap "
"ordaithe ann), agus tugann sé tuple dhá luach ina bhfuil an eochair agus "
"liosta de na luachanna go léir don eochair. Ardaíonn sé ``Keyerror`` nuair a "
"ghairtear ar fhoclóir folamh. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``dict`` representation of ``QueryDict``. For every (key, list) "
"pair in ``QueryDict``, ``dict`` will have (key, item), where item is one "
"element of the list, using the same logic as :meth:`QueryDict.__getitem__`:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé ionadaíocht ``dict`` ar ``Querydict`` ar ais. I gcás gach péire "
"(eochair, liosta) i `QueryDict``, beidh (eochair, mír) ag ``dict``, áit a "
"bhfuil mír eilimint amháin den liosta, ag baint úsáide as an loighic chéanna "
"amha:meth: `QueryDict. __getitem__`:"

msgid "Returns a string of the data in query string format. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Filleann sreang de na sonraí i bhformáid sreangán fiosrúcháin. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"Use the ``safe`` parameter to pass characters which don't require encoding. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid an paraiméadar ``sábháilte`` chun carachtair nach dteastaíonn ionchódú "
"uathu a rith. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``HttpResponse`` objects"
msgstr "``HttpResponse`` rudaí"

msgid ""
"In contrast to :class:`HttpRequest` objects, which are created automatically "
"by Django, :class:`HttpResponse` objects are your responsibility. Each view "
"you write is responsible for instantiating, populating, and returning "
"an :class:`HttpResponse`."
msgstr ""
"I gcodarsnacht le:class: rudaí `HttpRequest`, a chruthaíonn Django go "
"huathoibríoch, :class: Is iad rudaí `HttpResponse` freagracht ort. Tá gach "
"radharc a scríobhann tú freagrach as: class: `HttpResponse` a chur ar "
"aghaidh, a dhaonrú agus a thabhairt ar ais."

msgid "The :class:`HttpResponse` class lives in the :mod:`django.http` module."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rang:class: `HttpResponse` ina gcónaí sa mhodúl:mod: `django.http`."

msgid "Passing strings"
msgstr "Steaghráin a rith"

msgid ""
"Typical usage is to pass the contents of the page, as a string, bytestring, "
"or :class:`memoryview`, to the :class:`HttpResponse` constructor:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an úsáid tipiciúil ná ábhar an leathanaigh, mar shreang, bytestring, "
"nó:class: `memoryview`, a chur chuig an tógálaí:class: `HttpResponse`:"

msgid ""
"But if you want to add content incrementally, you can use ``response`` as a "
"file-like object:"
msgstr ""
"Ach más mian leat ábhar a chur le chéile, is féidir leat ``freagra ``a úsáid "
"mar réad cosúil le comhad:"

msgid "Passing iterators"
msgstr "Athraitheoirí a rith"

msgid ""
"Finally, you can pass ``HttpResponse`` an iterator rather than strings. "
"``HttpResponse`` will consume the iterator immediately, store its content as "
"a string, and discard it. Objects with a ``close()`` method such as files "
"and generators are immediately closed."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, is féidir leat `HttpResponse`` a chur ar athraitheoir "
"seachas teaghráin. Itheoidh ``HttpResponse`` an t-athraitheoir láithreach, "
"stóráilfidh sé a ábhar mar shreang, agus caitheann sé é. Dúntar rudaí le "
"modh ``close () ``mar shampla comhaid agus gineadóirí láithreach."

msgid ""
"If you need the response to be streamed from the iterator to the client, you "
"must use the :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` class instead."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit an freagra a shruthú ón iterator chuig an gcliant, ní mór duit "
"an rang:class: `StreamInghttPresponse` a úsáid ina ionad."

msgid "Setting header fields"
msgstr "Réimsí ceanntásc a shoc"

msgid ""
"To set or remove a header field in your response, "
"use :attr:`HttpResponse.headers`:"
msgstr ""
"Chun réimse ceanntásc a shocrú nó a bhaint i do fhreagra, bain úsáid:attr: "
"`HttpResponse.headers`:"

msgid ""
"You can also manipulate headers by treating your response like a dictionary:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ceanntásca a ionramháil freisin trí do fhreagra a chóireáil "
"mar fhoclóir:"

msgid ""
"This proxies to ``HttpResponse.headers``, and is the original interface "
"offered by ``HttpResponse``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé seo seachfhálaí chuig `HttpResponse.Headers``, agus is é an "
"comhéadan bunaidh a thairgeann `HttpResponse``."

msgid ""
"When using this interface, unlike a dictionary, ``del`` doesn't raise "
"``KeyError`` if the header field doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn an comhéadan seo á úsáid agat, murab ionann agus foclóir, ní "
"ardaíonn ``del`` `Keyerror`` mura bhfuil an réimse ceannteideal ann."

msgid "You can also set headers on instantiation:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat ceanntásca a shocrú freisin ar instantiation:"

msgid ""
"For setting the ``Cache-Control`` and ``Vary`` header fields, it is "
"recommended to use the :func:`~django.utils.cache.patch_cache_control` "
"and :func:`~django.utils.cache.patch_vary_headers` methods "
"from :mod:`django.utils.cache`, since these fields can have multiple, comma-"
"separated values. The \"patch\" methods ensure that other values, e.g. added "
"by a middleware, are not removed."
msgstr ""
"Chun na réimsí ceanntásc ``Cache-Control`` agus ``Vary`` a shocrú, moltar na "
"modhanna: func: `~django.utils.cache.patch_cache_control` agus:func: "
"`~django.utils.cache.patch_vary_headers` a úsáid ó:mod: "
"`django.utils.cache`, ós rud é gur féidir luachanna iolracha, scartha le "
"camóg a bheith ag na réimsí seo. Cinntíonn na modhanna “paiste” nach "
"mbaintear luachanna eile, m.sh. a chuireann meán-earraí leis."

msgid ""
"HTTP header fields cannot contain newlines. An attempt to set a header field "
"containing a newline character (CR or LF) will raise ``BadHeaderError``"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir línte nua a bheith i réimsí ceanntásc HTTP. Ardóidh iarracht "
"réimse ceanntásc ina bhfuil carachtar líne nua (CR nó LF) a shocrú "
"``BadHeaderROR``"

msgid "Telling the browser to treat the response as a file attachment"
msgstr ""
"Ag rá leis an mbrabhsálaí an freagra a chaitheamh mar cheangaltán comhad"

msgid ""
"To tell the browser to treat the response as a file attachment, set the "
"``Content-Type`` and ``Content-Disposition`` headers. For example, this is "
"how you might return a Microsoft Excel spreadsheet:"
msgstr ""
"Chun a rá don bhrabhsálaí caitheamh leis an bhfreagra mar cheangaltán "
"comhad, socraigh na ceannteidil ``Content-Type`` agus ``Content-"
"Disposition`. Mar shampla, seo mar a d'fhéadfá scarbhileog Microsoft Excel a "
"thabhairt ar ais:"

msgid ""
"There's nothing Django-specific about the ``Content-Disposition`` header, "
"but it's easy to forget the syntax, so we've included it here."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon rud Django-sonrach faoin gceannteideal ``Content-Disposition`, ach "
"is furasta dearmad a dhéanamh ar an gcomhréir, mar sin tá sé curtha san "
"áireamh anseo."

msgid ""
"A bytestring representing the content, encoded from a string if necessary."
msgstr "Bytestring a léiríonn an t-ábhar, ionchódaithe ó shreang más gá."

msgid ""
"A string representation of :attr:`HttpResponse.content`, decoded using the "
"response's :attr:`HttpResponse.charset` (defaulting to ``UTF-8`` if empty)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A :py:obj:`http.cookies.SimpleCookie` object holding the cookies included in "
"the response."
msgstr ""
"A: py:obj: réad `http.cookies.simplecookie` a choinníonn na fianáin san "
"áireamh sa fhreagra."

msgid ""
"A case insensitive, dict-like object that provides an interface to all HTTP "
"headers on the response, except a ``Set-Cookie`` header. See :ref:`setting-"
"header-fields` and :attr:`HttpResponse.cookies`."
msgstr ""
"Rud cás-neamhíogair, cosúil le dict a sholáthraíonn comhéadan do gach "
"ceannteideal HTTP ar an bhfreagra, seachas ceannteideal `Set-Cookie`. Féach: "
"Ref: `socruithe ceanncheadr-fields` agus:attr: `HttpResponse.cookies`."

msgid ""
"A string denoting the charset in which the response will be encoded. If not "
"given at ``HttpResponse`` instantiation time, it will be extracted from "
"``content_type`` and if that is unsuccessful, the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` "
"setting will be used."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an tacar charta ina ndéanfar an freagra a ionchódú. Mura "
"dtugtar é ag am institiúcháin ``HttpResponse``, bainfear as `content_type`` "
"é agus mura n-éireoidh leis sin, úsáidfear an socrú:setting: "
"`DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid "The :rfc:`HTTP status code <9110#section-15>` for the response."
msgstr "<9110 #section -15>An: RFC: `Cód stádais HTTP` don fhreagra."

msgid ""
"Unless :attr:`reason_phrase` is explicitly set, modifying the value of "
"``status_code`` outside the constructor will also modify the value of "
"``reason_phrase``."
msgstr ""
"Unless:attr: Socraítear `réasúna_phrase` go sainráite, modhnófar luach "
"```status_code`` lasmuigh den tógálaí luach ``réas_phrase`` a mhodhnú "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"The HTTP reason phrase for the response. It uses the :rfc:`HTTP standard's "
"<9110#section-15.1>` default reason phrases."
msgstr ""
"An frása chúis HTTP don fhreagra. <9110 #section -15.1>Úsáideann sé na "
"frásaí cúis réamhshocraithe: rfc: `HTTP caighdeán' s."

msgid ""
"Unless explicitly set, ``reason_phrase`` is determined by the value "
"of :attr:`status_code`."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil sé socraithe go sainráite, socraítear ``réas_phrase`` ag luach: "
"attr: `status_code`."

msgid "This is always ``False``."
msgstr "Tá sé seo i gcónaí ``bréag``."

msgid ""
"This attribute exists so middleware can treat streaming responses "
"differently from regular responses."
msgstr ""
"Tá an tréith seo ann ionas gur féidir le middleware freagraí sruthú a "
"chaitheamh go difriúil ó fhreagairtí rialta"

msgid "``True`` if the response has been closed."
msgstr "``Fíor`` má tá an freagra dúnta."

msgid ""
"Instantiates an ``HttpResponse`` object with the given page content, content "
"type, and headers."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé réad ``HttpResponse`` leis an ábhar leathanaigh, an cineál "
"ábhair agus na ceannteidil a thugtar."

msgid ""
"``content`` is most commonly an iterator, bytestring, :class:`memoryview`, "
"or string. Other types will be converted to a bytestring by encoding their "
"string representation. Iterators should return strings or bytestrings and "
"those will be joined together to form the content of the response."
msgstr ""
"Is minic gurb é ``content`` ná iterator, bytestring, :class: `memoryview`, "
"nó teaghrán. Déanfar cineálacha eile a thiontú go bytestring tríd a n-"
"ionadaíocht teaghrán a ionchódú. Ba chóir d'athraitheoirí teaghráin nó "
"bytestrings a thabhairt ar ais agus déanfar iad sin a cheangal le chéile "
"chun ábhar an fhreagra a fhoirmiú."

msgid ""
"``content_type`` is the MIME type optionally completed by a character set "
"encoding and is used to fill the HTTP ``Content-Type`` header. If not "
"specified, it is formed by ``'text/html'`` and "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` settings, by default: ``\"text/html; "
"charset=utf-8\"``."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``content_type`` an cineál MIME a chomhlánann go roghnach ag ionchódú "
"tacar carachtair agus úsáidtear é chun an ceannteideal HTTP ``Content-Type`` "
"a líonadh. Mura sonraítear é, cruthaítear é le ``'text/html'`` agus "
"socruithe: `DEFAULT_CHARSET` agus socruithe: ``DEFAULT_CHARSET`, de réir "
"réamhshocraithe: ``\"text/html; charset = utf-8\"``."

msgid ""
"``status`` is the :rfc:`HTTP status code <9110#section-15>` for the "
"response. You can use Python's :py:class:`http.HTTPStatus` for meaningful "
"aliases, such as ``HTTPStatus.NO_CONTENT``."
msgstr ""
"<9110 #section -15>Is é ``status ``an:rfc: `cód stádais HTTP` don fhreagra. "
"Is féidir leat úsáid a bhaint as Python's:py:class: `http.httpStatus` le "
"haghaidh ainmneacha bríocha, mar shampla ``HttpStatus.no_content``."

msgid ""
"``reason`` is the HTTP response phrase. If not provided, a default phrase "
"will be used."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``réas`` an frása freagartha HTTP. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, úsáidfear "
"abairt réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"``charset`` is the charset in which the response will be encoded. If not "
"given it will be extracted from ``content_type``, and if that is "
"unsuccessful, the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting will be used."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``charset`` an charset ina ndéanfar an freagra a ionchódú. Mura dtugtar "
"é bainfear as `content_type``, agus mura n-éiríonn leis sin, úsáidfear an "
"socrú: setting: `DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid "``headers`` is a :class:`dict` of HTTP headers for the response."
msgstr "Is é ``headers`` a: aicme: `dict` ceannteidil HTTP don fhreagra."

msgid ""
"Sets the given header name to the given value. Both ``header`` and ``value`` "
"should be strings."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn an t-ainm ceanntásc tugtha don luach tugtha. Ba chóir go mbeadh "
"``ceannteannair`` agus `luach`` araon teaghráin."

msgid ""
"Deletes the header with the given name. Fails silently if the header doesn't "
"exist. Case-insensitive."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé an ceanntásc leis an ainm tugtha. Teipeann sé go ciúin mura "
"bhfuil an ceanntásc ann. Cás-neamh-íogair."

msgid "Returns the value for the given header name. Case-insensitive."
msgstr "Tugann sé an luach don ainm ceanntásc tugtha ar ais. Cás-neamh-íogair."

msgid ""
"Returns the value for the given header, or an ``alternate`` if the header "
"doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an luach don cheanntásc a thugtar, nó ``malart`` mura bhfuil an "
"ceannteideal ann."

msgid ""
"Returns ``True`` or ``False`` based on a case-insensitive check for a header "
"with the given name."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé “True`` nó `False`` bunaithe ar sheiceáil cás-neamh-íogair do "
"cheanntásc leis an ainm tugtha."

msgid "Acts like :meth:`dict.items` for HTTP headers on the response."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhartha cosúil:meth: `dict.items` do cheanntásca HTTP ar an bhfreagra."

msgid "Sets a header unless it has already been set."
msgstr "Socraíonn sé ceanntásc mura bhfuil sé socraithe cheana féin."

msgid ""
"Sets a cookie. The parameters are the same as in "
"the :class:`~http.cookies.Morsel` cookie object in the Python standard "
"library."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn fianán. Tá na paraiméadair mar an gcéanna le réad fianáin: class: "
"`~http.cookies.morsel` sa leabharlann caighdeánach Python."

msgid ""
"``max_age`` should be a :class:`~datetime.timedelta` object, an integer "
"number of seconds, or ``None`` (default) if the cookie should last only as "
"long as the client's browser session. If ``expires`` is not specified, it "
"will be calculated."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh ``max_age`` a:class: `~datetime.timedelta` réad, líon "
"sláireach soicind, nó ``None`` (réamhshocraithe) más chóir go mairfeadh an "
"fianán ach chomh fada agus seisiún brabhsálaí an chliaint. Mura sonraítear "
"```deigh', ríomhfar é."

msgid ""
"``expires`` should either be a string in the format ``\"Wdy, DD-Mon-YY "
"HH:MM:SS GMT\"`` or a ``datetime.datetime`` object in UTC. If ``expires`` is "
"a ``datetime`` object, the ``max_age`` will be calculated."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh ``expires`` ina shreang sa fhormáid ``\"Wdy, DD-mon-yy "
"HH:MM:SS GMT\"` nó réad ``datetime.datetime`` i UTC. Más réad ``datetime`` é "
"``scaipe``, ríomhfar an ``max_age``."

msgid ""
"Use ``domain`` if you want to set a cross-domain cookie. For example, "
"``domain=\"example.com\"`` will set a cookie that is readable by the domains "
"www.example.com, blog.example.com, etc. Otherwise, a cookie will only be "
"readable by the domain that set it."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``domain`` más mian leat fianán tras-fearainn a shocrú. Mar shampla, "
"socraíonn ``domain=\"example.com\"`` fianán atá inléite ag na fearainn "
"www.example.com, blog.example.com, srl. Seachas sin, ní bheidh fianán "
"inléite ach ag an bhfearann a shocraigh é."

msgid ""
"Use ``secure=True`` if you want the cookie to be only sent to the server "
"when a request is made with the ``https`` scheme."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``secure=true`` mura dteastaíonn uait nach seolfar an fianán chuig an "
"bhfreastalaí ach nuair a dhéantar iarratas leis an scéim ``https``."

msgid ""
"Use ``httponly=True`` if you want to prevent client-side JavaScript from "
"having access to the cookie."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid `HttpOnly=True`` más mian leat JavaScript taobh an chliaint a chosc ó "
"rochtain a bheith agat ar an bhfianán."

msgid ""
"HttpOnly_ is a flag included in a Set-Cookie HTTP response header. It's part "
"of the :rfc:`RFC 6265 <6265#section-4.1.2.6>` standard for cookies and can "
"be a useful way to mitigate the risk of a client-side script accessing the "
"protected cookie data."
msgstr ""
"Is bratach é HTTPOnly_ atá san áireamh i gceannteideal freagartha Set-Cookie "
"HTTP. Tá sé mar chuid den <6265 #section -4.1.2.6> chaighdeán:rfc: `RFC "
"6265` le haghaidh fianáin agus féadann sé a bheith ina bhealach úsáideach "
"chun an baol go bhfaighidh script taobh an chliaint rochtain ar na sonraí "
"cosanta fianán a mhaolú."

msgid ""
"Use ``samesite='Strict'`` or ``samesite='Lax'`` to tell the browser not to "
"send this cookie when performing a cross-origin request. `SameSite`_ isn't "
"supported by all browsers, so it's not a replacement for Django's CSRF "
"protection, but rather a defense in depth measure."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``sameSite='strict'`` nó ``sameSite='Lax'`` chun a rá don bhrabhsálaí "
"gan an fianán seo a sheoladh agus iarratas tras-bhunús á dhéanamh agat. Ní "
"thacaíonn gach brabhsálaí le `SameSite`_, mar sin ní athsholáthar é ar "
"chosaint CSRF Django, ach beart cosanta domhain é."

msgid ""
"Use ``samesite='None'`` (string) to explicitly state that this cookie is "
"sent with all same-site and cross-site requests."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``sameSite='none'`` (teaghrán) chun a rá go sainráite go seoltar an "
"fianán seo le gach iarratas ar an láithreán céanna agus tras-láithreán."

msgid ""
":rfc:`RFC 6265 <6265#section-6.1>` states that user agents should support "
"cookies of at least 4096 bytes. For many browsers this is also the maximum "
"size. Django will not raise an exception if there's an attempt to store a "
"cookie of more than 4096 bytes, but many browsers will not set the cookie "
"correctly."
msgstr ""
":rfc: Deir `RFC 6265` gur cheart do ghníomhairí úsáideora tacú <6265 "
"#section -6.1> le fianáin de 4096 bait ar a laghad. I gcás go leor "
"brabhsálaithe is é seo an méid is mó freisin. Ní ardóidh Django eisceacht má "
"dhéantar iarracht fianán níos mó ná 4096 byte a stóráil, ach ní shocróidh go "
"leor brabhsálaithe an fianán i gceart."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`~HttpResponse.set_cookie()`, but :doc:`cryptographic signing </"
"topics/signing>` the cookie before setting it. Use in conjunction "
"with :meth:`HttpRequest.get_signed_cookie`. You can use the optional "
"``salt`` argument for added key strength, but you will need to remember to "
"pass it to the corresponding :meth:`HttpRequest.get_signed_cookie` call."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: Meth: `~HttpResponse.set_cookie () `, ach: doc: `sí</topics/"
"signing> niú cripteagrafac` an fianán sula socraíonn sé é. Úsáid i gcomhar "
"le:meth: `HttpRequest.get_signed_cookie`. Is féidir leat an argóint roghnach "
"``salt`` a úsáid le haghaidh neart eochair bhreise, ach beidh ort cuimhneamh "
"air a chur ar aghaidh chuig an nglao comhfhreagrach: meth: "
"`HttpRequest.get_signed_cookie`."

msgid ""
"Deletes the cookie with the given key. Fails silently if the key doesn't "
"exist."
msgstr ""
"Scriosann sé an fianán leis an eochair a thugtar. Teipeann sé go ciúin mura "
"bhfuil an eochair ann."

msgid ""
"Due to the way cookies work, ``path`` and ``domain`` should be the same "
"values you used in ``set_cookie()`` -- otherwise the cookie may not be "
"deleted."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a oibríonn fianáin, ba chóir go mbeadh `path`` "
"agus ``domain`` na luachanna céanna a d'úsáid tú i ``set_cookie ()`` - ar "
"shlí eile ní fhéadfar an fianán a scriosadh."

msgid ""
"This method is called at the end of the request directly by the WSGI server."
msgstr ""
"Glaonn an freastalaí WSGI ar an modh seo go díreach ag deireadh an iarratais."

msgid "This method makes an :class:`HttpResponse` instance a file-like object."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an modh seo réad cosúil le comhad mar shampla an:class: "
"`HttpResponse`."

msgid ""
"Returns the value of :attr:`HttpResponse.content`. This method makes "
"an :class:`HttpResponse` instance a stream-like object."
msgstr ""
"Tugann luach: attr: `HttpResponse.content` ar ais. Déanann an modh seo réad "
"cosúil le sruth mar shampla an:class: `HttpResponse`."

msgid ""
"Always ``False``. This method makes an :class:`HttpResponse` instance a "
"stream-like object."
msgstr ""
"I gcónaí ``Bréag``. Déanann an modh seo réad cosúil le sruth mar shampla "
"an:class: `HttpResponse`."

msgid ""
"Always ``True``. This method makes an :class:`HttpResponse` instance a "
"stream-like object."
msgstr ""
"“Fíor” i gcónaí. Déanann an modh seo réad cosúil le sruth mar shampla "
"an:class: `HttpResponse`."

msgid ""
"Writes a list of lines to the response. Line separators are not added. This "
"method makes an :class:`HttpResponse` instance a stream-like object."
msgstr ""
"Scríobhann liosta línte don fhreagra. Ní chuirtear deighilteoirí líne leis. "
"Déanann an modh seo réad cosúil le sruth mar shampla an:class: "
"`HttpResponse`."

msgid "``HttpResponse`` subclasses"
msgstr "Fo-aicmí `HttpResponse``"

msgid ""
"Django includes a number of ``HttpResponse`` subclasses that handle "
"different types of HTTP responses. Like ``HttpResponse``, these subclasses "
"live in :mod:`django.http`."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Django roinnt fo-aicmí `HttpResponse` a láimhseálann cineálacha "
"éagsúla freagraí HTTP. Cosúil le `HttpResponse``, tá na fo-aicmí seo ina "
"gcónaí in:mod: `django.http`."

msgid ""
"The first argument to the constructor is required -- the path to redirect "
"to. This can be a fully qualified URL (e.g. ``'https://www.yahoo.com/"
"search/'``), an absolute path with no domain (e.g. ``'/search/'``), or even "
"a relative path (e.g. ``'search/'``). In that last case, the client browser "
"will reconstruct the full URL itself according to the current path."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The constructor accepts an optional ``preserve_request`` keyword argument "
"that defaults to ``False``, producing a response with a 302 status code. If "
"``preserve_request`` is ``True``, the status code will be 307 instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "See :class:`HttpResponse` for other optional constructor arguments."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This read-only attribute represents the URL the response will redirect to "
"(equivalent to the ``Location`` response header)."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn an tréith léite amháin seo an URL a atreoróidh an freagra chuig "
"(comhionann leis an gceannteideal freagartha ``Suíomh ``)."

msgid "The ``preserve_request`` argument was added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Like :class:`HttpResponseRedirect`, but it returns a permanent redirect "
"(HTTP status code 301) instead of a \"found\" redirect (status code 302). "
"When ``preserve_request=True``, the response's status code is 308."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The constructor doesn't take any arguments and no content should be added to "
"this response. Use this to designate that a page hasn't been modified since "
"the user's last request (status code 304)."
msgstr ""
"Ní ghlacann an tógálaí aon argóintí agus níor cheart aon ábhar a chur leis "
"an bhfreagra seo. Úsáid é seo chun a ainmniú nár modhnaíodh leathanach ó "
"iarratas deireanach an úsáideora (cód stádais 304)."

msgid "Acts just like :class:`HttpResponse` but uses a 400 status code."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn sé díreach cosúil:class: `HttpResponse` ach úsáideann sé cód "
"stádais 400."

msgid "Acts just like :class:`HttpResponse` but uses a 404 status code."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn sé díreach cosúil:class: `HttpResponse` ach úsáideann sé cód "
"stádais 404."

msgid "Acts just like :class:`HttpResponse` but uses a 403 status code."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn sé díreach cosúil:class: `HttpResponse` ach úsáideann sé cód "
"stádais 403."

msgid ""
"Like :class:`HttpResponse`, but uses a 405 status code. The first argument "
"to the constructor is required: a list of permitted methods (e.g. ``['GET', "
"'POST']``)."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: class: `HttpResponse`, ach úsáideann sé cód stádais 405. "
"Teastaíonn an chéad argóint don tógálaí: liosta de na modhanna ceadaithe "
"(m.sh. ``['GET', 'POST']``)."

msgid "Acts just like :class:`HttpResponse` but uses a 410 status code."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn sé díreach cosúil:class: `HttpResponse` ach úsáideann sé cód "
"stádais 410."

msgid "Acts just like :class:`HttpResponse` but uses a 500 status code."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn sé díreach cosúil:class: `HttpResponse` ach úsáideann sé cód "
"stádais 500."

msgid ""
"If a custom subclass of :class:`HttpResponse` implements a ``render`` "
"method, Django will treat it as emulating "
"a :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse`, and the "
"``render`` method must itself return a valid response object."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann fo-aicme saincheaptha de:class: `HttpResponse` modh ``render`` "
"i bhfeidhm, caithfidh Django é mar aithris a: a:class: "
"`~django.template.response.simpletemplateResponse`, agus caithfidh an modh "
"``render`` réad freagartha bailí a thabhairt ar ais féin."

msgid "Custom response classes"
msgstr "Ranganna freagartha saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"If you find yourself needing a response class that Django doesn't provide, "
"you can create it with the help of :py:class:`http.HTTPStatus`. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má bhíonn rang freagartha ag teastáil uait nach soláthraíonn Django, is "
"féidir leat é a chruthú le cabhair ó:py:class: `http.httpStatus`. Mar "
"shampla::"

msgid "``JsonResponse`` objects"
msgstr "``JSONResponse`` rudaí"

msgid ""
"An :class:`HttpResponse` subclass that helps to create a JSON-encoded "
"response. It inherits most behavior from its superclass with a couple "
"differences:"
msgstr ""
"An:class: fo-aicme `HttpResponse` a chabhraíonn le freagra ionchódaithe JSON "
"a chruthú. Oidhreacht aige an chuid is mó d'iompar óna sáraicme le lánúin "
"difríochtaí:"

msgid ""
"Its default ``Content-Type`` header is set to :mimetype:`application/json`."
msgstr ""
"Tá a cheanntásc réamhshocraithe ``Content-Type`` socraithe ag:mimetype: "
"`application/json`."

msgid ""
"The first parameter, ``data``, should be a ``dict`` instance. If the "
"``safe`` parameter is set to ``False`` (see below) it can be any JSON-"
"serializable object."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an chéad pharaiméadar, ``sonraí ``, mar shampla ``dict``. "
"Má tá an paraiméadar ``sábháilte ``socraithe go ``False`` (féach thíos) is "
"féidir é a bheith ar aon réad inserializable JSON."

msgid ""
"The ``encoder``, which defaults "
"to :class:`django.core.serializers.json.DjangoJSONEncoder`, will be used to "
"serialize the data. See :ref:`JSON serialization <serialization-formats-"
"json>` for more details about this serializer."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidfear an ``encoder``, atá réamhshocraithe to:class: "
"`django.core.serializers.json.djangojsonEncoder`, chun na sonraí a "
"shraitheadh. Féach: Ref: `JSON sraitheoireacht <serialization-formats-"
"json>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoin sraitheoir seo."

msgid ""
"The ``safe`` boolean parameter defaults to ``True``. If it's set to "
"``False``, any object can be passed for serialization (otherwise only "
"``dict`` instances are allowed). If ``safe`` is ``True`` and a non-``dict`` "
"object is passed as the first argument, a :exc:`TypeError` will be raised."
msgstr ""
"Tá an paraiméadar boolean ``sábháilte ``réamhshocraithe go ``True``. Má tá "
"sé socraithe go ``False``, is féidir aon rud a chur ar aghaidh le haghaidh "
"sraitheadh (ar shlí eile ní cheadaítear ach cásanna ``dict``). Má tá "
"``sábháilte`` ``True`` agus má chuirtear réad neamh-``dict`` ar aghaidh mar "
"an chéad argóint, ardófar a:exc: `TypeError`."

msgid ""
"The ``json_dumps_params`` parameter is a dictionary of keyword arguments to "
"pass to the ``json.dumps()`` call used to generate the response."
msgstr ""
"Is foclóir argóintí eochairfhocal é an paraiméadar ``json_dumps_params`` le "
"dul chuig an nglao ``json.dumps () ``a úsáidtear chun an freagra a ghiniúint."

msgid "Typical usage could look like:"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh cuma a bheith ar úsáid tipiciúil:"

msgid "Serializing non-dictionary objects"
msgstr "Rud neamh-fhoclóra a shraitheadh"

msgid ""
"In order to serialize objects other than ``dict`` you must set the ``safe`` "
"parameter to ``False``:"
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn rudaí seachas `dict`` a shraitheadh ní mór duit an paraiméadar "
"``sábháilte`` a shocrú go ``False``:"

msgid "Without passing ``safe=False``, a :exc:`TypeError` will be raised."
msgstr "Gan dul ar ``safe=False``, ardófar a:exc: `TypeError`."

msgid ""
"Note that an API based on ``dict`` objects is more extensible, flexible, and "
"makes it easier to maintain forwards compatibility. Therefore, you should "
"avoid using non-dict objects in JSON-encoded response."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil API bunaithe ar rudaí ``dict`` níos "
"leathnaithe, níos solúbtha, agus go ndéanann sé níos éasca comhoiriúnacht ar "
"aghaidh a choinneáil. Dá bhrí sin, ba cheart duit rudaí neamh-dict a "
"sheachaint i bhfreagra ionchódaithe JSON."

msgid ""
"Before the `5th edition of ECMAScript <https://262.ecma-international.org/"
"5.1/#sec-11.1.4>`_ it was possible to poison the JavaScript ``Array`` "
"constructor. For this reason, Django does not allow passing non-dict objects "
"to the :class:`~django.http.JsonResponse` constructor by default.  However, "
"most modern browsers implement ECMAScript 5 which removes this attack "
"vector. Therefore it is possible to disable this security precaution."
msgstr ""
"Roimh an `5ú eagrán de ECMAScript`_ bhí sé indéanta an tógálaí JavaScript "
"``< https://262.ecma-international.org/5.1/#sec-11.1.4> Array` a nimhiú. Ar "
"an gcúis seo, ní cheadaíonn Django rudaí neamh-dict a chur chuig an tógálaí: "
"class: `~django.http.jsonResponse` de réir réamhshocraithe. Mar sin féin, "
"cuireann mórchuid na bhrabhsálaithe nua-aimseartha ECMAScript 5 i bhfeidhm a "
"bhaineann leis an veicte Dá bhrí sin is féidir an réamhchúram slándála seo a "
"dhíchumasú."

msgid "Changing the default JSON encoder"
msgstr "An t-ionchódóir JSON réamhshocraithe a"

msgid ""
"If you need to use a different JSON encoder class you can pass the "
"``encoder`` parameter to the constructor method:"
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit rang ionchódóra JSON difriúil a úsáid is féidir leat an "
"paraiméadar ``encoder` a chur ar aghaidh chuig an modh tógálaí:"

msgid "``StreamingHttpResponse`` objects"
msgstr "``Streaminghttpreresponse`` rudaí"

msgid ""
"The :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` class is used to stream a response from "
"Django to the browser."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear an rang:class: `StreamInghttPresponse` chun freagra a shruthlú ó "
"Django chuig an mbrabhsálaí."

msgid "Advanced usage"
msgstr "Úsáid chun cinn"

msgid ""
":class:`StreamingHttpResponse` is somewhat advanced, in that it is important "
"to know whether you'll be serving your application synchronously under WSGI "
"or asynchronously under ASGI, and adjust your usage appropriately."
msgstr ""
":class: Tá `StreamInghttPresponse` beagán chun cinn, sa mhéid go bhfuil sé "
"tábhachtach a fháil amach an mbeidh tú ag freastal ar d'iarratas go "
"sioncrónach faoi WSGI nó go gascrónach faoi ASGI, agus d'úsáid a choigeartú "
"go cuí."

msgid "Please read these notes with care."
msgstr "Léigh na nótaí seo go cúramach le do thoil."

msgid ""
"An example usage of :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` under WSGI is streaming "
"content when generating the response would take too long or uses too much "
"memory. For instance, it's useful for :ref:`generating large CSV files "
"<streaming-csv-files>`."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid shamplach de:class: `StreamInghttPresponse` faoi WSGI is ea ábhar a "
"shruthlú nuair a thógfadh an freagra rófhada nó úsáideadh an iomarca "
"cuimhne. <streaming-csv-files>Mar shampla, tá sé úsáideach le haghaidh: ref: "
"`comhaid mhóra CSV a ghiniúint `."

msgid ""
"There are performance considerations when doing this, though. Django, under "
"WSGI, is designed for short-lived requests. Streaming responses will tie a "
"worker process for the entire duration of the response. This may result in "
"poor performance."
msgstr ""
"Tá breithnithe feidhmíochta ann agus é seo á dhéanamh agat, áfach. Tá "
"Django, faoi WSGI, deartha le haghaidh iarratais ghearrshaoil. Ceanglóidh "
"freagraí sruthú próiseas oibrithe ar feadh tréimhse iomlán na freagartha. "
"D'fhéadfadh droch-fheidhmíocht a bheith mar thoradh air seo"

msgid ""
"Generally speaking, you would perform expensive tasks outside of the request-"
"response cycle, rather than resorting to a streamed response."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, déanfá tascanna daor lasmuigh den timthriall iarrata-"
"freagartha, seachas dul i ngleic le freagra sruthaithe."

msgid ""
"When serving under ASGI, however, a :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` need not "
"stop other requests from being served whilst waiting for I/O. This opens up "
"the possibility of long-lived requests for streaming content and "
"implementing patterns such as long-polling, and server-sent events."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag freastalú faoi ASGI, áfach, ní gá a: class: "
"`StreamInghttPrésponse` stop a chur ar iarratais eile a sheirbheáil agus iad "
"ag fanacht le I/O. Osclaíonn sé seo an fhéidearthacht iarratais fadré ar "
"ábhar sruthú agus patrúin a chur i bhfeidhm mar vótaíocht fhada, agus "
"imeachtaí a sheoltar ó fhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"Even under ASGI note, :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` should only be used in "
"situations where it is absolutely required that the whole content isn't "
"iterated before transferring the data to the client. Because the content "
"can't be accessed, many middleware can't function normally. For example the "
"``ETag`` and ``Content-Length`` headers can't be generated for streaming "
"responses."
msgstr ""
"Fiú amháin faoi nóta ASGI, níor cheart: `StreamInghttPresponse` a úsáid ach "
"amháin i gcásanna ina bhfuil sé riachtanach go hiomlán nach ndéantar an t-"
"ábhar iomlán a athrú sula n-aistrítear na sonraí chuig an gcliant. Toisc "
"nach féidir rochtain a fháil ar an ábhar, ní féidir le go leor middleware "
"feidhmiú de ghnáth. Mar shampla ní féidir na ceannteidil ``Etag`` agus "
"``Content-Length`` a ghiniúint le haghaidh freagraí sruthú."

msgid ""
"The :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` is not a subclass "
"of :class:`HttpResponse`, because it features a slightly different API. "
"However, it is almost identical, with the following notable differences:"
msgstr ""
"Ní fo-aicme de:class: `HttpResponse` é an:class: `HttpResponse`, toisc go "
"bhfuil API beagán difriúil aige. Mar sin féin, tá sé beagnach comhionann, "
"leis na difríochtaí suntasacha seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"It should be given an iterator that yields bytestrings, :class:`memoryview`, "
"or strings as content. When serving under WSGI, this should be a sync "
"iterator. When serving under ASGI, then it should be an async iterator."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir athraitheoir a thabhairt dó a thugann bytestrings, :class: "
"`memoryview`, nó teaghráin mar ábhar. Agus tú ag freastal faoi WSGI, ba "
"chóir go mbeadh sé seo ina athraitheoir sioncronaithe. Agus tú ag freastal "
"faoi ASGI, ba chóir go mbeadh sé ina athraitheoir async."

msgid ""
"You cannot access its content, except by iterating the response object "
"itself. This should only occur when the response is returned to the client: "
"you should not iterate the response yourself."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar a ábhar, ach amháin tríd an réad "
"freagartha féin a athrá. Níor chóir go dtarlódh sé seo ach nuair a chuirtear "
"an freagra ar ais chuig an gcliant: níor cheart duit an freagra a athrú duit "
"féin."

msgid ""
"Under WSGI the response will be iterated synchronously. Under ASGI the "
"response will be iterated asynchronously. (This is why the iterator type "
"must match the protocol you're using.)"
msgstr ""
"Faoi WSGI déanfar an freagra a athdhéanamh go sioncrónach. Faoi ASGI déanfar "
"an freagra a athrá go asincrónach. (Sin é an fáth go gcaithfidh an cineál "
"iterator an prótacal atá á úsáid agat a mheaitseáil.)"

msgid ""
"To avoid a crash, an incorrect iterator type will be mapped to the correct "
"type during iteration, and a warning will be raised, but in order to do this "
"the iterator must be fully-consumed, which defeats the purpose of using "
"a :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` at all."
msgstr ""
"Chun timpiste a sheachaint, déanfar cineál athraitheora mícheart a mhapáil "
"leis an gcineál ceart le linn athraithe, agus ardófar rabhadh, ach chun é "
"seo a dhéanamh caithfear an t-athraitheoir a ithe go hiomlán, rud a "
"sháraíonn an cuspóir a: class: `StreamInghttPresponse` a úsáid ar chor ar "
"bith."

msgid ""
"It has no ``content`` attribute. Instead, it has "
"a :attr:`~StreamingHttpResponse.streaming_content` attribute. This can be "
"used in middleware to wrap the response iterable, but should not be consumed."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon tréith ``ábhar ``aige. Ina áit sin, tá a: attr: "
"`~StreamInghttPresponse.streaming_content` tréith aige. Is féidir é seo a "
"úsáid i lár earraí chun an freagra a fhilleadh in-athrá, ach níor cheart é a "
"ithe."

msgid ""
"It has no ``text`` attribute, as it would require iterating the response "
"object."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You cannot use the file-like object ``tell()`` or ``write()`` methods. Doing "
"so will raise an exception."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leat na modhanna réad cosúil le comhad ``tell () ``nó `scríobh "
"()`` a úsáid. Má dhéantar é sin, beidh eisceacht ann."

msgid ""
"The :class:`HttpResponseBase` base class is common "
"between :class:`HttpResponse` and :class:`StreamingHttpResponse`."
msgstr ""
"Tá an bunaicme: Class: `HttpResponseBase` coitianta idir: aicme: "
"`HttpResponse` agus:class: `StreamInghttPresponse`."

msgid ""
"An iterator of the response content, bytestring encoded according "
"to :attr:`HttpResponse.charset`."
msgstr ""
"Athraitheoir ar an ábhar freagartha, ionchódaithe bytestring de réir: attr: "
"`HttpResponse.charSet`."

msgid "This is always ``True``."
msgstr "Tá sé seo i gcónaí ``Fíor`."

msgid ""
"Boolean indicating whether :attr:`StreamingHttpResponse.streaming_content` "
"is an asynchronous iterator or not."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a léiríonn an bhfuil: attr: "
"`StreamInghttPresponse.streaming_content` is iterator asincrónach nó nach "
"bhfuil."

msgid ""
"This is useful for middleware needing to "
"wrap :attr:`StreamingHttpResponse.streaming_content`."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach do mheánearraí a theastaíonn uathu fillte:attr: "
"`StreamInghttPresponse.streaming_content`."

msgid "Handling disconnects"
msgstr "Dícheangail láimhseáil"

msgid ""
"If the client disconnects during a streaming response, Django will cancel "
"the coroutine that is handling the response. If you want to clean up "
"resources manually, you can do so by catching the "
"``asyncio.CancelledError``::"
msgstr ""
"Má dhícheanglaíonn an cliant le linn freagra sruthú, cuirfidh Django an "
"coroutine atá ag láimhseáil an freagra ar ceal. Más mian leat acmhainní a "
"ghlanadh de láimh, is féidir leat é sin a dhéanamh tríd an "
"`Asyncio.CancelleDerror`` a ghabháil:"

msgid ""
"This example only shows how to handle client disconnection while the "
"response is streaming. If you perform long-running operations in your view "
"before returning the ``StreamingHttpResponse`` object, then you may also "
"want to :ref:`handle disconnections in the view <async-handling-disconnect>` "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"Ní thaispeánann an sampla seo ach conas dícheangal cliant a láimhseáil agus "
"an freagra ag sruthú. <async-handling-disconnect>Má dhéanann tú oibríochtaí "
"fadtéarmacha i do thuairim sula bhfilleann tú an réad "
"``StreaminghttPresponse`` ar ais, ansin b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat freis:ref: "
"`dícheangail a láimhseáil sa radharc `féin."

msgid "``FileResponse`` objects"
msgstr "Rudaí ``FileResponse``"

msgid ""
":class:`FileResponse` is a subclass of :class:`StreamingHttpResponse` "
"optimized for binary files. It uses :pep:`wsgi.file_wrapper <3333#optional-"
"platform-specific-file-handling>` if provided by the wsgi server, otherwise "
"it streams the file out in small chunks."
msgstr ""
":class: Is fo-aicme é `FileResponse` de:class: `StreamInghttPresponse` "
"optamaithe do chomhaid dénártha. Úsáideann sé: pep: `wsgi.file_wrapper` má "
"sholáthraíonn an freastalaí <3333 #optional -platform-specific-file-"
"handling> wsgi, ar shlí eile sruthaíonn sé an comhad amach i gcodanna beaga."

msgid ""
"If ``as_attachment=True``, the ``Content-Disposition`` header is set to "
"``attachment``, which asks the browser to offer the file to the user as a "
"download. Otherwise, a ``Content-Disposition`` header with a value of "
"``inline`` (the browser default) will be set only if a filename is available."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``as_attachment=True``, socraítear an ceannteideal ``Content-"
"Disposition` go ``attachment``, a iarrann ar an mbrabhsálaí an comhad a "
"thairiscint don úsáideoir mar íoslódáil. Seachas sin, ní shocrófar ceanntásc "
"``Content-Disposition` le luach ``inline`` (réamhshocraithe an bhrabhsálaí) "
"ach amháin má tá ainm comhaid ar fáil."

msgid ""
"If ``open_file`` doesn't have a name or if the name of ``open_file`` isn't "
"appropriate, provide a custom file name using the ``filename``  parameter. "
"Note that if you pass a file-like object like ``io.BytesIO``, it's your task "
"to ``seek()`` it before passing it to ``FileResponse``."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ainm ag ``open_file`` nó mura bhfuil ainm `open_file`` "
"oiriúnach, tabhair ainm comhaid saincheaptha ag baint úsáide as an "
"paraiméadar ``file``. Tabhair faoi deara má chuireann tú réad cosúil le "
"comhad cosúil le ``IO.Bytesio``, is é do chúram ``search () ``é sula "
"ndéantar é a chur chuig `FileResponse``."

msgid ""
"The ``Content-Length`` header is automatically set when it can be guessed "
"from the content of ``open_file``."
msgstr ""
"Socraítear an ceannteideal ``Content-Length`` go huathoibríoch nuair is "
"féidir é a thuairisciú ó ábhar ``open_file``."

msgid ""
"The ``Content-Type`` header is automatically set when it can be guessed from "
"the ``filename``, or the name of ``open_file``."
msgstr ""
"Socraítear an ceannteideal ``Content-Type`` go huathoibríoch nuair is féidir "
"é a thuairisciú ón ``ainm comhad ``, nó ainm `open_file``."

msgid ""
"``FileResponse`` accepts any file-like object with binary content, for "
"example a file open in binary mode like so:"
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``FileResponse`` le haon rud cosúil le comhad le hábhar dénártha, "
"mar shampla comhad oscailte i mód dénártha mar sin:"

msgid ""
"The file will be closed automatically, so don't open it with a context "
"manager."
msgstr ""
"Dúnfar an comhad go huathoibríoch, mar sin ná oscail é le bainisteoir "
"comhthéacs."

msgid "Use under ASGI"
msgstr "Úsáid faoi ASGI"

msgid ""
"Python's file API is synchronous. This means that the file must be fully "
"consumed in order to be served under ASGI."
msgstr ""
"Tá API comhad Python sioncrónach. Ciallaíonn sé seo go gcaithfear an comhad "
"a ithe go hiomlán chun é a sheirbheáil faoi ASGI."

msgid ""
"In order to stream a file asynchronously you need to use a third-party "
"package that provides an asynchronous file API, such as `aiofiles <https://"
"github.com/Tinche/aiofiles>`_."
msgstr ""
"< https://github.com/Tinche/aiofiles>D'fhonn comhad a shruthú go hincrónach "
"ní mór duit pacáiste tríú páirtí a úsáid a sholáthraíonn API comhad "
"asincrónach, mar shampla `aiofiles`_."

msgid ""
"This method is automatically called during the response initialization and "
"set various headers (``Content-Length``, ``Content-Type``, and ``Content-"
"Disposition``) depending on ``open_file``."
msgstr ""
"Glaofar an modh seo go huathoibríoch le linn an tionscnamh freagartha agus "
"socraítear ceannteidil éagsúla (``Content-Fad ``, `Content-Type``, agus`` "
"Content-Disposition ``) ag brath ar ``oscailte_comhad``."

msgid "``HttpResponseBase`` class"
msgstr "Aicme ``HttpResponseBase``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`HttpResponseBase` class is common to all Django responses. It "
"should not be used to create responses directly, but it can be useful for "
"type-checking."
msgstr ""
"Tá an rang:class: `HttpResponseBase` coitianta do gach freagra Django. Níor "
"chóir é a úsáid chun freagraí a chruthú go díreach, ach d'fhéadfadh sé a "
"bheith úsáideach chun cineál-sheiceáil."

msgid "``SchemaEditor``"
msgstr "``SchemaEditor``"

msgid ""
"Django's migration system is split into two parts; the logic for calculating "
"and storing what operations should be run (``django.db.migrations``), and "
"the database abstraction layer that turns things like \"create a model\" or "
"\"delete a field\" into SQL - which is the job of the ``SchemaEditor``."
msgstr ""
"Tá córas imirce Django roinnte ina dhá chuid; an loighic chun na "
"hoibríochtaí ba chóir a reáchtáil a ríomh agus a stóráil "
"(`django.db.migrations`), agus an ciseal tearbhaithe bunachar sonraí a "
"chasann rudaí cosúil le “samhail a chruthú” nó “réimse a scriosadh” isteach "
"i SQL - arb é post an `SchemaEditor``."

msgid ""
"It's unlikely that you will want to interact directly with ``SchemaEditor`` "
"as a normal developer using Django, but if you want to write your own "
"migration system, or have more advanced needs, it's a lot nicer than writing "
"SQL."
msgstr ""
"Ní dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh idirghníomhú go díreach le `SchemaEditor` "
"mar ghnáthfhorbróir ag baint úsáide as Django, ach más mian leat do chóras "
"imirce féin a scríobh, nó má tá riachtanais níos airde agat, tá sé i bhfad "
"níos deise ná SQL a scríobh."

msgid ""
"Each database backend in Django supplies its own version of "
"``SchemaEditor``, and it's always accessible via the "
"``connection.schema_editor()`` context manager::"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn gach cúltaca bunachar sonraí i Django a leagan féin de "
"“SchemaEditor”, agus tá sé inrochtana i gcónaí tríd an mbainisteoir "
"comhthéacs ``connection.schema_editor () ``:"

msgid ""
"It must be used via the context manager as this allows it to manage things "
"like transactions and deferred SQL (like creating ``ForeignKey`` "
"constraints)."
msgstr ""
"Caithfear é a úsáid tríd an mbainisteoir comhthéacs mar ligeann sé seo dó "
"rudaí cosúil le hidirbhearta agus SQL iarchurtha a bhainistiú (cosúil le "
"srianta ``ForeignKey` a chruthú)."

msgid ""
"It exposes all possible operations as methods, that should be called in the "
"order you wish changes to be applied. Some possible operations or types of "
"change are not possible on all databases - for example, MyISAM does not "
"support foreign key constraints."
msgstr ""
"Nochtann sé gach oibríocht féideartha mar mhodhanna, ba chóir iad a ghlaoch "
"san ord is mian leat go ndéanfaí athruithe a chur i bhfeidhm. Ní féidir "
"roinnt oibríochtaí nó cineálacha athraithe féideartha indéanta ar gach "
"bunachar sonraí - mar shampla, ní thacaíonn MyISAM le príomhshrianta "
"eachtracha."

msgid ""
"If you are writing or maintaining a third-party database backend for Django, "
"you will need to provide a ``SchemaEditor`` implementation in order to work "
"with Django's migration functionality - however, as long as your database is "
"relatively standard in its use of SQL and relational design, you should be "
"able to subclass one of the built-in Django ``SchemaEditor`` classes and "
"tweak the syntax a little."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag scríobh nó ag cothabháil cúltaca bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí do "
"Django, beidh ort cur i bhfeidhm `SchemaEditor` a sholáthar d'fhonn oibriú "
"le feidhmiúlacht imirce Django - áfach, fad is atá do bhunachar sonraí "
"réasúnta caighdeánach maidir lena úsáid SQL agus dearadh coibhneasta, ba "
"cheart go mbeadh tú in ann ceann de na ranganna Django `SchemaEditor` "
"ionsuite agus an comhréiteach beagán."

msgid "``execute()``"
msgstr "```fhorghníomhú () ``"

msgid ""
"Executes the SQL statement passed in, with parameters if supplied. This is a "
"wrapper around the normal database cursors that allows capture of the SQL to "
"a ``.sql`` file if the user wishes."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn sé an ráiteas SQL a rith isteach, le paraiméadair má "
"sholáthraítear iad. Is fillteán é seo timpeall na ngnáthchúrsóirí bunachar "
"sonraí a cheadaíonn an SQL a ghabháil chuig comhad `.sql` más mian leis an "
"úsáideoir."

msgid "``create_model()``"
msgstr "``create_model () ``"

msgid ""
"Creates a new table in the database for the provided model, along with any "
"unique constraints or indexes it requires."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaíonn sé tábla nua sa bhunachar sonraí don tsamhail a chuirtear ar "
"fáil, chomh maith le haon srianta nó innéacsanna uathúla a theastaíonn uaidh."

msgid "``delete_model()``"
msgstr "``scrios_model () ``"

msgid ""
"Drops the model's table in the database along with any unique constraints or "
"indexes it has."
msgstr ""
"Titeann tábla an tsamhail sa bhunachar sonraí mar aon le haon srianta nó "
"innéacsanna uathúla atá aige."

msgid "``add_index()``"
msgstr "``Add_index () ``"

msgid "Adds ``index`` to ``model``’s table."
msgstr "Cuireann sé ``index`` le tábla ``samhail`."

msgid "``remove_index()``"
msgstr "``innéacs a bhaint () ``"

msgid "Removes ``index`` from ``model``’s table."
msgstr "Baineann sé ``index`` ó thábla ``samhail`."

msgid "``rename_index()``"
msgstr "``Innéacs athainmnithe () ``"

msgid "Renames ``old_index`` from ``model``’s table to ``new_index``."
msgstr "Athainmnigh ``old_index ``ó thábla ``model`` go `new_index``."

msgid "``add_constraint()``"
msgstr "``Add_Constraint () ``"

msgid "Adds ``constraint`` to ``model``'s table."
msgstr "Cuireann sé ``sriant`` le tábla ``samhail`."

msgid "``remove_constraint()``"
msgstr "```scrionadh a bhaint () ``"

msgid "Removes ``constraint`` from ``model``'s table."
msgstr "Baineann sé ``sriant`` ó thábla ``samhail`."

msgid "``alter_unique_together()``"
msgstr "``alter_unique_together () ``"

msgid ""
"Changes a model's :attr:`~django.db.models.Options.unique_together` value; "
"this will add or remove unique constraints from the model's table until they "
"match the new value."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn luach samhail 's:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.options.unique_Together`; cuirfidh sé seo srianta uathúla "
"leis nó bainfidh sé seo ó thábla an tsamhail go dtí go n-oireann siad an "
"luach nua."

msgid "``alter_index_together()``"
msgstr "``alter_index_le chéile () ``"

msgid ""
"Changes a model's ``index_together`` value; this will add or remove indexes "
"from the model's table until they match the new value."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn sé luach ``index_together ``samhail; cuirfidh sé seo innéacsanna "
"nó bainfidh sé as tábla an tsamhail go dtí go n-oireann siad an luach nua."

msgid "``alter_db_table()``"
msgstr "``alter_db_table () ``"

msgid "Renames the model's table from ``old_db_table`` to ``new_db_table``."
msgstr "Athainmnigh tábla an tsamhail ó ``old_db_table`` go ``new_db_table``."

msgid "``alter_db_table_comment()``"
msgstr "``alter_db_table_comment () ``"

msgid "Change the ``model``’s table comment to ``new_db_table_comment``."
msgstr "Athraigh trácht tábla “model” go `new_db_table_comment``."

msgid "``alter_db_tablespace()``"
msgstr "``alter_db_tablespace () ``"

msgid "Moves the model's table from one tablespace to another."
msgstr "Bogann sé tábla an tsamhail ó spás tábla amháin go ceann eile."

msgid "``add_field()``"
msgstr "``Add_field () ``"

msgid ""
"Adds a column (or sometimes multiple) to the model's table to represent the "
"field. This will also add indexes or a unique constraint if the field has "
"``db_index=True`` or ``unique=True``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé colún (nó uaireanta iolrach) le tábla an tsamhail chun an réimse "
"a léiriú. Cuirfidh sé seo innéacsanna nó srian uathúil leis freisin má tá "
"`db_index = true`` nó ``unique=true`` sa réimse."

msgid ""
"If the field is a ``ManyToManyField`` without a value for ``through``, "
"instead of creating a column, it will make a table to represent the "
"relationship. If ``through`` is provided, it is a no-op."
msgstr ""
"Más é an réimse ``ManyTomanyField`` gan luach do ``trí ``,,``,, ``, 'in "
"ionad colún a chruthú, déanfaidh sé tábla chun an caidreamh a léiriú. Má "
"chuirtear ``trí ``ar fáil, is neamh-op é."

msgid ""
"If the field is a ``ForeignKey``, this will also add the foreign key "
"constraint to the column."
msgstr ""
"Más ``ForeignKey`` an réimse, cuirfidh sé seo an srian eochair eachtrach "
"leis an gcolún freisin."

msgid "``remove_field()``"
msgstr "``réimse a bhaint ()``"

msgid ""
"Removes the column(s) representing the field from the model's table, along "
"with any unique constraints, foreign key constraints, or indexes caused by "
"that field."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé an colúin/na colúin a léiríonn an réimse ó thábla an tsamhail, "
"mar aon le haon srianta uathúla, príomhshrianta eachtracha, nó innéacsanna "
"de bharr an réimse sin."

msgid ""
"If the field is a ManyToManyField without a value for ``through``, it will "
"remove the table created to track the relationship. If ``through`` is "
"provided, it is a no-op."
msgstr ""
"Más ManyTomanyField é an réimse gan luach do ``through ``, bainfidh sé an "
"tábla a cruthaíodh chun an caidreamh a rianú. Má chuirtear ``trí ``ar fáil, "
"is neamh-op é."

msgid "``alter_field()``"
msgstr "``alter_field () ``"

msgid ""
"This transforms the field on the model from the old field to the new one. "
"This includes changing the name of the column "
"(the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.db_column` attribute), changing the type "
"of the field (if the field class changes), changing the ``NULL`` status of "
"the field, adding or removing field-only unique constraints and indexes, "
"changing primary key, and changing the destination of ``ForeignKey`` "
"constraints."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn sé seo an réimse ar an tsamhail ón sean-réimse go dtí an ceann "
"nua. Áirítear leis seo ainm an cholúin a athrú (the:attr: "
"`~django.db.models.field.db_column` tréith), cineál an réimse a athrú (má "
"athraíonn an rang réimse), stádas `NULL`` an réimse a athrú, srianta agus "
"innéacsanna uathúla réimse a chur nó a bhaint, agus ceann scríbe srianta "
"`Foreign` a athrú."

msgid ""
"The most common transformation this cannot do is transforming a "
"``ManyToManyField`` into a normal Field or vice-versa; Django cannot do this "
"without losing data, and so it will refuse to do it. "
"Instead, :meth:`.remove_field` and :meth:`.add_field` should be called "
"separately."
msgstr ""
"Is é an claochlú is coitianta nach féidir leis seo a dhéanamh ná "
"``ManyTomanyField` a athrú go gnáthRéimse nó a mhalairt; Ní féidir le Django "
"é seo a dhéanamh gan sonraí a chailleadh, agus mar sin diúltóidh sé é a "
"dhéanamh. Ina áit sin, ba chóir :meth: `.remove_field` agus:meth: "
"`.add_field` a ghlaoch ar leithligh."

msgid ""
"If the database has the ``supports_combined_alters``, Django will try and do "
"as many of these in a single database call as possible; otherwise, it will "
"issue a separate ALTER statement for each change, but will not issue ALTERs "
"where no change is required."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an ``supports_combined_alters`` sa bhunachar sonraí, déanfaidh Django "
"iarracht an oiread díobh seo a dhéanamh i nglao bunachar sonraí amháin agus "
"is féidir; ar shlí eile, eiseoidh sé ráiteas ALTER ar leithligh do gach "
"athrú, ach ní eiseoidh sé ALTERanna nuair nach bhfuil aon athrú ag teastáil."

msgid "All attributes should be considered read-only unless stated otherwise."
msgstr "Ba chóir gach tréith a mheas go léite amháin mura luaitear a mhalairt."

msgid "``connection``"
msgstr "``nasc``"

msgid ""
"A connection object to the database. A useful attribute of the connection is "
"``alias`` which can be used to determine the name of the database being "
"accessed."
msgstr ""
"Réad ceangail leis an mbunachar sonraí. Is tréith úsáideach den nasc ná "
"``alias`` ar féidir a úsáid chun ainm an bhunachar sonraí atá á rochtain "
"agat a chinneadh."

msgid ""
"This is useful when doing data migrations for :ref:`migrations with multiple "
"databases <data-migrations-and-multiple-databases>`."
msgstr ""
"<data-migrations-and-multiple-databases>Tá sé seo úsáideach agus imirce "
"sonraí á ndéanamh le haghaidh: ref: `imirce le bunachair sonraí iolracha `."

msgid ""
"Be careful when you override settings, especially when the default value is "
"a non-empty list or dictionary, such as :setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS`. Make "
"sure you keep the components required by the features of Django you wish to "
"use."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach nuair a sháraigh tú socruithe, go háirithe nuair is liosta nó "
"foclóir neamh-folamh é an luach réamhshocraithe, mar shampla:setting: "
"`STATICFILES_FINDERS`. Déan cinnte go gcoinníonn tú na comhpháirteanna a "
"theastaíonn ó ghnéithe Django is mian leat a úsáid."

msgid "Core Settings"
msgstr "Socruithe lárnacha"

msgid ""
"Here's a list of settings available in Django core and their default values. "
"Settings provided by contrib apps are listed below, followed by a topical "
"index of the core settings. For introductory material, see "
"the :doc:`settings topic guide </topics/settings>`."
msgstr ""
"Seo liosta de na socruithe atá ar fáil i gcroí Django agus a luachanna "
"réamhshocraithe. Tá socruithe a sholáthraíonn aipeanna contrib liostaithe "
"thíos, agus innéacs tráthúil de na croí-shocruithe ina dhiaidh sin. Le "
"haghaidh ábhar tosaigh, féach an:doc: treoir ábhair `socruithe `</topics/"
"settings>."

msgid "``ABSOLUTE_URL_OVERRIDES``"
msgstr "``URL_ABSOLUTE_OVERRIDES``"

msgid "Default: ``{}`` (Empty dictionary)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``{}`` (Foclóir folamh)"

msgid ""
"A dictionary mapping ``\"app_label.model_name\"`` strings to functions that "
"take a model object and return its URL. This is a way of inserting or "
"overriding ``get_absolute_url()`` methods on a per-installation basis. "
"Example::"
msgstr ""
"Tá foclóir ag mapáil ``\"app_label.model_name\"`` teaghrán chuig feidhmeanna "
"a thógann réad samhail agus a chuireann a URL ar ais. Is bealach é seo chun "
"modhanna ``get_absolute_url () ``a chur isteach nó a shárú ar bhonn in "
"aghaidh an tsuiteála. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"The model name used in this setting should be all lowercase, regardless of "
"the case of the actual model class name."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an t-ainm samhail a úsáidtear sa suíomh seo go léir líon "
"beag, beag beann ar chás ainm aicme iarbhír an tsamhail."

msgid "``ADMINS``"
msgstr "``RIARACHÁIN ``"

msgid "Default: ``[]`` (Empty list)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``[]`` (Liosta folamh)"

msgid ""
"A list of all the people who get code error notifications. "
"When :setting:`DEBUG=False <DEBUG>` "
"and :class:`~django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler` is configured "
"in :setting:`LOGGING` (done by default), Django emails these people the "
"details of exceptions raised in the request/response cycle."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na daoine go léir a fhaigheann fógraí earráide cód. Nuair: "
"Setting: `debug = false <DEBUG>`agus:class: "
"`~django.utils.log.adminEmailHandler` cumraithe in:setting: `LOGGING` "
"(déanta de réir réamhshocraithe), ríomhphostálann Django na sonraí "
"eisceachtaí a ardaíodh sa timthriall iarrata/freagartha do na daoine seo."

msgid ""
"Each item in the list should be a tuple of (Full name, email address). "
"Example::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh gach mír sa liosta ina tuple de (Ainm iomlán, seoladh "
"ríomhphoist). Sampla::"

msgid "``ALLOWED_HOSTS``"
msgstr "``ÓSTÁLACHA CEADAITHEAD``"

msgid ""
"A list of strings representing the host/domain names that this Django site "
"can serve. This is a security measure to prevent :ref:`HTTP Host header "
"attacks <host-headers-virtual-hosting>`, which are possible even under many "
"seemingly-safe web server configurations."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na teaghráin a léiríonn na hainmneacha óstaí/fearainn ar féidir "
"leis an suíomh Django seo freastal orthu. Is beart slándála é seo chun cosc "
"a choisc:ref: `Ionsaithe ceanntásc Óstach HTTP <host-headers-virtual-"
"hosting>`, atá indéanta fiú faoi go leor cumraíochtaí freastalaí gréasáin "
"atá cosúil go bhfuil siad sábháilte."

msgid ""
"Values in this list can be fully qualified names (e.g. "
"``'www.example.com'``), in which case they will be matched against the "
"request's ``Host`` header exactly (case-insensitive, not including port). A "
"value beginning with a period can be used as a subdomain wildcard: "
"``'.example.com'`` will match ``example.com``, ``www.example.com``, and any "
"other subdomain of ``example.com``. A value of ``'*'`` will match anything; "
"in this case you are responsible to provide your own validation of the "
"``Host`` header (perhaps in a middleware; if so this middleware must be "
"listed first in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE`)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le luachanna sa liosta seo a bheith ina ainmneacha láncháilithe "
"(m.sh. ```www.example.com'``), agus sa chás sin déanfar iad a mheaitseáil i "
"gcoinne ceannteideal ``Óst` an iarratais go díreach (cás-neamh-íogair, gan "
"calafort san áireamh). Is féidir luach a thosaíonn le tréimhse a úsáid mar "
"fho-chárta fiáin: meaitneoidh ``'.example.com'`` ``example.com``, "
"`www.example.com``, agus aon fho-fhearann eile de `example.com``. "
"Meaitneoidh luach ``*'`` rud ar bith; sa chás seo tá tú freagrach as do "
"bhailíochtú féin a sholáthar ar an gceannteideal ``Host`` (b'fhéidir i lár- "
"earraí; más amhlaidh ní mór an middleware seo a liostú ar dtús in:setting: "
"`MIDDLEWARE`)."

msgid ""
"Django also allows the `fully qualified domain name (FQDN)`_ of any entries. "
"Some browsers include a trailing dot in the ``Host`` header which Django "
"strips when performing host validation."
msgstr ""
"Ceadaíonn Django freisin `ainm fearainn láncháilithe (FQDN) `_ d'aon "
"iontrálacha. Cuimsíonn roinnt brabhsálaithe ponc críochnaitheach sa "
"cheanntásc ``Óst` a stiallann Django agus bailíochtú óstach á ndéanamh."

msgid ""
"If the ``Host`` header (or ``X-Forwarded-Host`` "
"if :setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` is enabled) does not match any value in "
"this list, the :meth:`django.http.HttpRequest.get_host()` method will "
"raise :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation`."
msgstr ""
"Mura n-oireann an ceannteideal ``Host`` (nó ``X-Forwarded-Host`` "
"más:setting: `USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` cumasaithe) aon luach ar an liosta seo, "
"ardóidh an modh:meth: `Django.http.httpRequest.get_host () `: exc: "
"`~Django.core.exceptions.suspiciousoperation:exc: "
"`~Django.core.exceptions.suspicoUsoperations.SuspiciousOperations.”."

msgid ""
"When :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True`` and ``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` is empty, the host "
"is validated against ``['.localhost', '127.0.0.1', '[::1]']``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn: Setting: `DEBUG` ``True`` agus ``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` folamh, "
"bailítear an t-óstach i gcoinne ``['.localhost', '127.0.0.1', '[::1]']``."

msgid ""
"``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` is also :ref:`checked when running tests <topics-testing-"
"advanced-multiple-hosts>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-testing-advanced-multiple-hosts>Tá ``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` freis:ref: "
"`seiceáilte agus tástálacha á reáchtáil `."

msgid ""
"This validation only applies "
"via :meth:`~django.http.HttpRequest.get_host()`; if your code accesses the "
"``Host`` header directly from ``request.META`` you are bypassing this "
"security protection."
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaineann an bailíochtú seo ach via: meth: "
"`~django.http.httpRequest.get_host () `; má rochtaíonn do chód ar an "
"gceannteideal ``Host`` go díreach ó ``Request.Meta`` tá tú ag seachaint an "
"chosaint slándála seo."

msgid "``APPEND_SLASH``"
msgstr "``APPEND_SLASH``"

msgid "Default: ``True``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Fíor`"

msgid ""
"When set to ``True``, if the request URL does not match any of the patterns "
"in the URLconf and it doesn't end in a slash, an HTTP redirect is issued to "
"the same URL with a slash appended. Note that the redirect may cause any "
"data submitted in a POST request to be lost."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh sé socraithe go `True``, mura n-oireann URL an iarratais aon "
"cheann de na patrúin san URLConf agus mura gcríochnaíonn sé i slash, "
"eisítear atreorú HTTP chuig an URL céanna le slash curtha leis. Tabhair faoi "
"deara gur féidir leis an atreorú a bheith ina chúis le haon sonraí a "
"chuirtear isteach in iarratas POST a chailleadh"

msgid ""
"The :setting:`APPEND_SLASH` setting is only used "
"if :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` is installed "
"(see :doc:`/topics/http/middleware`). See also :setting:`PREPEND_WWW`."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáidtear an socrú: Setting: `APPEND_SLASH` ach má tá: class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` suiteáilte (féach: doc: `/"
"topics/http/middleware`). Féach freis:socrú: `PREPEND_WWW`."

msgid "``CACHES``"
msgstr "``CÁIS``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary containing the settings for all caches to be used with Django. "
"It is a nested dictionary whose contents maps cache aliases to a dictionary "
"containing the options for an individual cache."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil na socruithe do gach taisce le húsáid le Django. Is "
"foclóir neadaithe é a léarscálann a n-ábhar ainmneacha taisce chuig foclóir "
"ina bhfuil na roghanna le haghaidh taisce aonair."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`CACHES` setting must configure a ``default`` cache; any number "
"of additional caches may also be specified. If you are using a cache backend "
"other than the local memory cache, or you need to define multiple caches, "
"other options will be required. The following cache options are available."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór don socrú: Socrú: `CACHES` taisce ``réamhshocraithe`` a chumrú; "
"féadfar aon líon taisce breise a shonrú freisin. Má tá cúltaca taisce á "
"úsáid agat seachas an taisce cuimhne áitiúil, nó má theastaíonn uait "
"iolracha a shainiú, beidh roghanna eile ag teastáil. Tá na roghanna taisce "
"seo a leanas ar fáil."

msgid "``BACKEND``"
msgstr "```CÚLT``"

msgid "Default: ``''`` (Empty string)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``\"``(Sreang folamh)"

msgid "The cache backend to use. The built-in cache backends are:"
msgstr "An cúltaca taisce le húsáid. Is iad na cúltaca taisce ionsuite:"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.db.DatabaseCache'``"
msgstr "```Django.Core.Cache.Backends.db.DatabaseCache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.dummy.DummyCache'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Core.Cache.Backends.Dummy.DummyCache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.filebased.FileBasedCache'``"
msgstr "```Django.Core.Cache.Backends.FileBased.FileBasedCache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.locmem.LocMemCache'``"
msgstr "```Django.Core.Cache.Backends.Locmem.LocMemCache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.memcached.PyMemcacheCache'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Core.Cache.Backends.Memcached.PymemCacheCache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.memcached.PyLibMCCache'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Core.Cache.Backends.memcached.pylibmccache'``"

msgid "``'django.core.cache.backends.redis.RedisCache'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Core.Cache.Backends.Redis.RedisCache'``"

msgid ""
"You can use a cache backend that doesn't ship with Django by "
"setting :setting:`BACKEND <CACHES-BACKEND>` to a fully-qualified path of a "
"cache backend class (i.e. ``mypackage.backends.whatever.WhateverCache``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cúltaca taisce nach seolann le Django a úsáid trí shocrú: "
"`BACKEND `chuig cosán láncháilithe <CACHES-BACKEND>de rang cúltaca taisce "
"(ie ``MyPackage.Backends.whatever.whateverCache``)."

msgid "``KEY_FUNCTION``"
msgstr "``EOCHAIRFHEIDHME``"

msgid ""
"A string containing a dotted path to a function (or any callable) that "
"defines how to compose a prefix, version and key into a final cache key. The "
"default implementation is equivalent to the function::"
msgstr ""
"Sreang ina bhfuil cosán poncanach chuig feidhm (nó aon ghlaoch) a "
"shainmhíníonn conas réimír, leagan agus eochair a chumadh isteach i eochair "
"taisce deiridh. Tá an cur i bhfeidhm réamhshocraithe comhionann leis an "
"bhfeidhm:"

msgid ""
"You may use any key function you want, as long as it has the same argument "
"signature."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh tú aon phríomhfheidhm a theastaíonn uait a úsáid, fad is atá an "
"síniú argóint céanna aige."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_key_transformation>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_key_transformation>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "``KEY_PREFIX``"
msgstr "``EOCHAIR_RÉAMH``"

msgid ""
"A string that will be automatically included (prepended by default) to all "
"cache keys used by the Django server."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a chuirfear san áireamh go huathoibríoch (réamhshocraithe de réir "
"réamhshocraithe) chuig gach eochair taisce a úsáideann an freastalaí Django."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_key_prefixing>` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_key_prefixing>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "``LOCATION``"
msgstr "``SUÍOMH``"

msgid ""
"The location of the cache to use. This might be the directory for a file "
"system cache, a host and port for a memcache server, or an identifying name "
"for a local memory cache. e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"Suíomh an taisce le húsáid. D'fhéadfadh gurb é seo an eolaire do taisce "
"chórais chomhaid, óstach agus calafort do fhreastalaí memcache, nó ainm "
"aitheantais do taisce cuimhne áitiúil. m.sh.:"

msgid "``OPTIONS``"
msgstr "``ROGHANNAÍ``"

msgid "Default: ``None``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Níl ``"

msgid ""
"Extra parameters to pass to the cache backend. Available parameters vary "
"depending on your cache backend."
msgstr ""
"Paraiméadair bhreise le dul chuig an gcúltaca taisce. Athraíonn paraiméadair "
"atá ar fáil ag brath ar do chúltaca taisce."

msgid ""
"Some information on available parameters can be found in the :ref:`cache "
"arguments <cache_arguments>` documentation. For more information, consult "
"your backend module's own documentation."
msgstr ""
"<cache_arguments>Is féidir roinnt faisnéise faoi pharaiméadair atá ar fáil a "
"fháil sa doiciméadúiséireacht: ref: `cache argóintí `. Le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"faisnéise, téigh i gcomhairle le cáipéisíocht do mhodúl cúlt"

msgid "``TIMEOUT``"
msgstr "``TIMEOUT``"

msgid "Default: ``300``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``300`"

msgid ""
"The number of seconds before a cache entry is considered stale. If the value "
"of this setting is ``None``, cache entries will not expire. A value of ``0`` "
"causes keys to immediately expire (effectively \"don't cache\")."
msgstr ""
"Meastar go bhfuil líon na soicind roimh iontráil taisce seasmhach. Más luach "
"an socraithe seo ``None``, ní rachaidh iontrálacha taisce in éag. Fágann "
"luach ``0`` go rachaidh eochracha in éag láithreach (go héifeachtach “ná "
"taisceáil”)."

msgid "``VERSION``"
msgstr "``LEAGAN``"

msgid "Default: ``1``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``1``"

msgid ""
"The default version number for cache keys generated by the Django server."
msgstr ""
"An uimhir leagan réamhshocraithe d'eochracha taisce a ghineann an freastalaí "
"Django."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`cache documentation <cache_versioning>` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach na:ref: `cáipéisíocht taiscéala <cache_versioning>`le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh faisnéise."

msgid "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ALIAS``"
msgstr "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_ALIAS``"

msgid "Default: ``'default'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'default'``"

msgid ""
"The cache connection to use for the :ref:`cache middleware <the-per-site-"
"cache>`."
msgstr ""
"<the-per-site-cache>An nasc taisce le húsáid don: ref: `cache middleware `."

msgid "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX``"
msgstr "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_KEY_PREFIX``"

msgid ""
"A string which will be prefixed to the cache keys generated by "
"the :ref:`cache middleware <the-per-site-cache>`. This prefix is combined "
"with the :setting:`KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>` setting; it does not "
"replace it."
msgstr ""
"<the-per-site-cache>Sreang a bheidh réamhshocraithe leis na heochracha "
"taisce a ghineann an: ref: `cache middleware `. Comhcheanglaítear an réimír "
"seo leis an socrú: setting: `KEY_PREFIX <CACHES-KEY_PREFIX>`; ní chuireann "
"sé in ionad é."

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/cache`."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/topics/cache`."

msgid "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS``"
msgstr "``CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SOICIND``"

msgid "Default: ``600``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``600`"

msgid ""
"The default integer number of seconds to cache a page for the :ref:`cache "
"middleware <the-per-site-cache>`."
msgstr ""
"<the-per-site-cache>An líon iomláir réamhshocraithe soicind chun leathanach "
"a thaisceadh don: ref: `cache middleware `."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_AGE``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_AOS``"

msgid "Default: ``31449600`` (approximately 1 year, in seconds)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``31449600`` (thart ar 1 bhliain, i soicindí)"

msgid "The age of CSRF cookies, in seconds."
msgstr "Aois fianáin CSRF, i soicindí."

msgid ""
"The reason for setting a long-lived expiration time is to avoid problems in "
"the case of a user closing a browser or bookmarking a page and then loading "
"that page from a browser cache. Without persistent cookies, the form "
"submission would fail in this case."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chúis le am éaga fadtréimhse a shocrú fadhbanna a sheachaint i gcás "
"úsáideoir ag dúnadh brabhsálaí nó leathanach a leabharmharcáil agus ansin an "
"leathanach sin a luchtú ó taisce brabhsálaí. Gan fianáin leanúnacha, "
"theipfeadh ar an aighneacht foirme sa chás seo."

msgid ""
"Some browsers (specifically Internet Explorer) can disallow the use of "
"persistent cookies or can have the indexes to the cookie jar corrupted on "
"disk, thereby causing CSRF protection checks to (sometimes intermittently) "
"fail. Change this setting to ``None`` to use session-based CSRF cookies, "
"which keep the cookies in-memory instead of on persistent storage."
msgstr ""
"Féadann roinnt brabhsálaithe (go sonrach Internet Explorer) fianáin "
"leanúnacha a úsáid nó féadfaidh siad na hinnéacsanna don phróca fianán a "
"bheith truaillithe ar dhiosca, rud a fhágann go dteipfidh seiceálacha "
"cosanta CSRF (uaireanta go tréimhseach). Athraigh an socrú seo go ``None "
"``chun fianáin CSRF bunaithe ar sheisiún a úsáid, a choinníonn na fianáin i "
"gcuimhne seachas ar stóráil leanúnach."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_DOMAIN``"

msgid ""
"The domain to be used when setting the CSRF cookie.  This can be useful for "
"easily allowing cross-subdomain requests to be excluded from the normal "
"cross site request forgery protection.  It should be set to a string such as "
"``\".example.com\"`` to allow a POST request from a form on one subdomain to "
"be accepted by a view served from another subdomain."
msgstr ""
"An fearann atá le húsáid agus an fianán CSRF á shocrú. Is féidir leis seo a "
"bheith úsáideach chun ligean go héasca iarratais thrasfho-fhearann a eisiamh "
"ón ngnáthchosaint bréifneach iarratais thrasláithreáin. Ba chóir é a shocrú "
"ar shreang mar ``” .example.com\"`` chun ligean d'iarratas POST ó fhoirm ar "
"fhoirm ar fhoirm amháin glacadh le dearcadh a sheirbheáiltear ó fho-fhearann "
"eile."

msgid ""
"Please note that the presence of this setting does not imply that Django's "
"CSRF protection is safe from cross-subdomain attacks by default - please see "
"the :ref:`CSRF limitations <csrf-limitations>` section."
msgstr ""
"<csrf-limitations>Tabhair faoi deara le do thoil nach dtugann láithreacht an "
"socrú seo le tuiscint go bhfuil cosaint CSRF Django sábháilte ó ionsaithe "
"tras-fho-fearainn de réir réamhshocraithe - féach an ranna:ref: "
"`Teorainneacha CSRF `."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_HTTPONLY``"

msgid "Default: ``False``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Fréag``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use ``HttpOnly`` flag on the CSRF cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, client-side JavaScript will not be able to access the CSRF cookie."
msgstr ""
"Cibé an bhratach `HttpOnly` a úsáid ar an bhfianán CSRF. Má tá sé seo "
"socraithe ar ``True``, ní bheidh JavaScript taobh an chliaint in ann "
"rochtain a fháil ar an bhfianán CSRF."

msgid ""
"Designating the CSRF cookie as ``HttpOnly`` doesn't offer any practical "
"protection because CSRF is only to protect against cross-domain attacks. If "
"an attacker can read the cookie via JavaScript, they're already on the same "
"domain as far as the browser knows, so they can do anything they like "
"anyway. (XSS is a much bigger hole than CSRF.)"
msgstr ""
"Ní thugann an fianán CSRF a ainmniú mar `HttpOnly` aon chosaint phraiticiúil "
"toisc nach bhfuil CSRF ach chun cosaint a dhéanamh ar ionsaithe tras-"
"fearainn. Más féidir le hionsaitheoir an fianán a léamh trí JavaScript, tá "
"siad ar an bhfearann céanna cheana féin chomh fada agus is eol don "
"bhrabhsálaí, ionas gur féidir leo aon rud is mian leo a dhéanamh ar aon nós. "
"(Is poll i bhfad níos mó é XSS ná CSRF.)"

msgid ""
"Although the setting offers little practical benefit, it's sometimes "
"required by security auditors."
msgstr ""
"Cé nach dtugann an suíomh mórán sochair phraiticiúil, uaireanta teastaíonn "
"iniúchóirí slándála é"

msgid ""
"If you enable this and need to send the value of the CSRF token with an AJAX "
"request, your JavaScript must pull the value :ref:`from a hidden CSRF token "
"form input <acquiring-csrf-token-from-html>` instead of :ref:`from the "
"cookie <acquiring-csrf-token-from-cookie>`."
msgstr ""
"<acquiring-csrf-token-from-cookie>Má chumasaíonn tú é seo agus má "
"theastaíonn uait luach an chomhartha CSRF a sheoladh le hiarratas AJAX, ní "
"mór do JavaScript an luach:ref: `ó ionchur foirm chomhartha CSRF i bhfolach "
"`in <acquiring-csrf-token-from-html>ionad:ref: `ón bhfianán` a tharraingt."

msgid "See :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` for details on ``HttpOnly``."
msgstr ""
"Féach: SETTING: `SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` le haghaidh sonraí ar `HTTPONLY``."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_NAME``"
msgstr "```AINM_CSRF_COOKIE``"

msgid "Default: ``'csrftoken'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'csrftoken'``"

msgid ""
"The name of the cookie to use for the CSRF authentication token. This can be "
"whatever you want (as long as it's different from the other cookie names in "
"your application). See :doc:`/ref/csrf`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm na fianáin le húsáid le haghaidh comhartha fíordheimhnithe CSRF. Is "
"féidir leis seo a bheith cibé rud is mian leat (fad is atá sé difriúil ó na "
"hainmneacha fianán eile i d'iarratas). Féach: doc: `/ref/csrf`."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_PATH``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_PATH``"

msgid "Default: ``'/'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'/'``"

msgid ""
"The path set on the CSRF cookie. This should either match the URL path of "
"your Django installation or be a parent of that path."
msgstr ""
"An cosán atá leagtha síos ar an bhfianán CSRF. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo "
"comhoiriúnach le cosán URL do shuiteála Django nó a bheith ina thuismitheoir "
"ar an gcosán sin."

msgid ""
"This is useful if you have multiple Django instances running under the same "
"hostname. They can use different cookie paths, and each instance will only "
"see its own CSRF cookie."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach má tá cásanna iolracha Django agat ag rith faoin ainm "
"óstach céanna. Is féidir leo cosáin éagsúla fianán a úsáid, agus ní "
"fheicfidh gach cás ach a fhianán CSRF féin."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_SAMESITE``"

msgid "Default: ``'Lax'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'Lax'``"

msgid ""
"The value of the `SameSite`_ flag on the CSRF cookie. This flag prevents the "
"cookie from being sent in cross-site requests."
msgstr ""
"Luach an bhratach `SameSite`_ ar an bhfianán CSRF. Cuireann an bratach seo "
"cosc ar an bhfianán a sheoladh in iarratais tras-láithreáin."

msgid "See :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` for details about ``SameSite``."
msgstr ""
"Féach:SETTING: `SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE` le haghaidh sonraí faoi `Samesite``."

msgid "``CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE``"
msgstr "``CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use a secure cookie for the CSRF cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, the cookie will be marked as \"secure\", which means browsers may "
"ensure that the cookie is only sent with an HTTPS connection."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu fianán slán a úsáid don fhianán CSRF. Má tá sé seo socraithe ar "
"``True``, marcálfar an fianán mar “slán”, rud a chiallaíonn go bhféadfadh "
"brabhsálaithe a chinntiú nach seoltar an fianán ach le nasc HTTPS."

msgid "``CSRF_USE_SESSIONS``"
msgstr "``SEISIÚINT_ÚSÁID_CSRF``"

msgid ""
"Whether to store the CSRF token in the user's session instead of in a "
"cookie. It requires the use of :mod:`django.contrib.sessions`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu an comhartha CSRF a stóráil i seisiún an úsáideora in ionad i "
"bhfianán. Éilíonn sé úsáid:mod: `django.contrib.sesions`."

msgid ""
"Storing the CSRF token in a cookie (Django's default) is safe, but storing "
"it in the session is common practice in other web frameworks and therefore "
"sometimes demanded by security auditors."
msgstr ""
"Tá an comhartha CSRF a stóráil i bhfianán (réamhshocrú Django) sábháilte, "
"ach is cleachtas coitianta é a stóráil sa seisiún i gcreataí gréasáin eile "
"agus dá bhrí sin éilíonn iniúchóirí slándála uaireanta."

msgid ""
"Since the :ref:`default error views <error-views>` require the CSRF "
"token, :class:`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware` must "
"appear in :setting:`MIDDLEWARE` before any middleware that may raise an "
"exception to trigger an error view (such "
"as :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied`) if you're using "
"``CSRF_USE_SESSIONS``. See :ref:`middleware-ordering`."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go dteastaíonn comhartha <error-views>CSRF uir:ref: "
"`réamhshocraithe earráidí `, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.sessions.middleware.sessionMiddleware` le feiceáil "
"in:setting: `MIDDLEWARE` roimh aon middleware a d'fhéadfadh eisceacht a ardú "
"chun amharc earráide a spreagadh (mar shampla:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.perdenied`) má tá tú ag baint úsáide as "
"``CSRF_USE_SESSIONS``. Féach: ref: `middleware-ording`."

msgid "``CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW``"
msgstr "``CSRF_FAILURE_VIEW``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.views.csrf.csrf_failure'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'django.views.csrf.csrf_failure'``"

msgid ""
"A dotted path to the view function to be used when an incoming request is "
"rejected by the :doc:`CSRF protection </ref/csrf>`. The function should have "
"this signature::"
msgstr ""
"Conair poncaí chuig an bhfeidhm amharc atá le húsáid nuair a dhiúltaítear "
"iarratas isteach ag na:doc: `Cosaint CSRF` </ref/csrf>. Ba chóir go mbeadh "
"an síniú seo ag an bhfeidhm:"

msgid ""
"where ``reason`` is a short message (intended for developers or logging, not "
"for end users) indicating the reason the request was rejected. It should "
"return an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseForbidden`."
msgstr ""
"i gcás gur teachtaireacht ghearr (atá beartaithe d'fhorbróirí nó logála, ní "
"d'úsáideoirí deiridh) a léiríonn an chúis a dhiúltaíodh don iarratas. Ba "
"chóir dó filleadh an:class: `~django.http.httpResponseForbidden`."

msgid ""
"``django.views.csrf.csrf_failure()`` accepts an additional ``template_name`` "
"parameter that defaults to ``'403_csrf.html'``. If a template with that name "
"exists, it will be used to render the page."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``django.views.csrf.csrf_failure () ``le paraiméadar breise "
"``template_name`` atá réamhshocraithe go ``403_csrf.html'``. Má tá teimpléad "
"leis an ainm sin ann, úsáidfear é chun an leathanach a rinneadh."

msgid "``CSRF_HEADER_NAME``"
msgstr "```CSRF_HEADER_AINM``"

msgid "Default: ``'HTTP_X_CSRFTOKEN'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'HTTP_X_CSRFTOKEN'``"

msgid "The name of the request header used for CSRF authentication."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an cheanntásc iarratais a úsáidtear le haghaidh fíordheimhniú CSRF."

msgid ""
"As with other HTTP headers in ``request.META``, the header name received "
"from the server is normalized by converting all characters to uppercase, "
"replacing any hyphens with underscores, and adding an ``'HTTP_'`` prefix to "
"the name. For example, if your client sends a ``'X-XSRF-TOKEN'`` header, the "
"setting should be ``'HTTP_X_XSRF_TOKEN'``."
msgstr ""
"Mar is amhlaidh le ceannteidil HTTP eile i `Request.meta``, normalaítear an "
"t-ainm ceannteidil a fhaightear ón bhfreastalaí trí gach carachtar a thiontú "
"go uachtarchlóir, aon bhriseanna a chur in ionad béim, agus réimír "
"``'HTTP_'` a chur leis an ainm. Mar shampla, má sheolann do chliant "
"ceannteideal ``'X-XSRF-TOKEN'``, ba chóir go mbeadh an socrú "
"```HTTP_X_XSRF_TOKEN'`."

msgid "``CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS``"
msgstr "``CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS``"

msgid "A list of trusted origins for unsafe requests (e.g. ``POST``)."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de bhunús iontaofa le haghaidh iarratais neamhshábháilte (m.sh. `POST "
"``)."

msgid ""
"For requests that include the ``Origin`` header, Django's CSRF protection "
"requires that header match the origin present in the ``Host`` header."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le hiarratais ina n-áirítear an ceannteideal ``Bunaidh ``, éilíonn "
"cosaint CSRF Django go n-oireann an ceannteideal an tionscnamh atá i láthair "
"sa cheannteideal ``Óst`."

msgid ""
"For a :meth:`secure <django.http.HttpRequest.is_secure>` unsafe request that "
"doesn't include the ``Origin`` header, the request must have a ``Referer`` "
"header that matches the origin present in the ``Host`` header."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le hiar <django.http.HttpRequest.is_secure>ratas neamhshábháilte "
"a:meth: `slán `nach n-áirítear an ceannteideal ``Bunaidh ``, ní mór "
"ceannteideal ``Referer`` a bheith ag an iarraidh a mheaitseálann leis an "
"mbunús atá i láthair sa cheannteideal ``Óst`."

msgid ""
"These checks prevent, for example, a ``POST`` request from "
"``subdomain.example.com`` from succeeding against ``api.example.com``. If "
"you need cross-origin unsafe requests, continuing the example, add "
"``'https://subdomain.example.com'`` to this list (and/or ``http://...`` if "
"requests originate from an insecure page)."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann na seiceálacha seo cosc, mar shampla, ar iarratas ``POST ``ó "
"`subdomain.example.com`` go n-éireoidh leo i gcoinne `api.example.com``. Má "
"theastaíonn iarratais neamhshábháilte tras-bhunús uait, ag leanúint leis an "
"sampla, cuir ```https://subdomain.example.com '`leis an liosta seo (agus/nó "
"``http://... ``má thagann iarratais ó leathanach neamhchinnte)."

msgid ""
"The setting also supports subdomains, so you could add ``'https://"
"*.example.com'``, for example, to allow access from all subdomains of "
"``example.com``."
msgstr ""
"Tacaíonn an socrú le fo-fhearann freisin, ionas gur féidir leat ``'https://"
"*.example.com '``a chur leis, mar shampla, chun rochtain a cheadú ó gach fo-"
"fhearann de `example.com``."

msgid "``DATABASES``"
msgstr "``BUNACHAIR SONRAÍ``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary containing the settings for all databases to be used with "
"Django. It is a nested dictionary whose contents map a database alias to a "
"dictionary containing the options for an individual database."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil na socruithe do gach bunachar sonraí le húsáid le Django. "
"Is foclóir neadaithe é a léarscáil a n-ábhar ailias bunachar sonraí go "
"foclóir ina bhfuil na roghanna do bhunachar sonraí aonair."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`DATABASES` setting must configure a ``default`` database; any "
"number of additional databases may also be specified."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór don socrú: “BUNACHAR SONRAÍ” bunachar sonraí “réamhshocraithe” a "
"chumrú; féadfar aon líon bunachar sonraí breise a shonrú freisin."

msgid ""
"The simplest possible settings file is for a single-database setup using "
"SQLite. This can be configured using the following::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an comhad socruithe is simplí is féidir le socrú bunachar sonraí aonair "
"ag baint úsáide as SQLite. Is féidir é seo a chumrú trí na rudaí seo a "
"leanas a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"When connecting to other database backends, such as MariaDB, MySQL, Oracle, "
"or PostgreSQL, additional connection parameters will be required. See "
"the :setting:`ENGINE <DATABASE-ENGINE>` setting below on how to specify "
"other database types. This example is for PostgreSQL::"
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag nascadh le cúltaca bunachar sonraí eile, mar shampla MariaDB, "
"MySQL, Oracle, nó PostgreSQL, beidh paraiméadair nasc breise ag teastáil. "
"Féach an socrú:setting: `ENGINE <DATABASE-ENGINE>`thíos maidir le conas "
"cineálacha eile bunachar sonraí a shonrú. Tá an sampla seo le haghaidh "
"PostgreSQL::"

msgid ""
"The following inner options that may be required for more complex "
"configurations are available:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na roghanna istigh seo a leanas a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag teastáil le "
"haghaidh cumraíochtaí níos casta ar fáil:"

msgid "``ATOMIC_REQUESTS``"
msgstr "``IARRATAITHE_ATOMIC``"

msgid ""
"Set this to ``True`` to wrap each view in a transaction on this database. "
"See :ref:`tying-transactions-to-http-requests`."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é seo go ``True`` chun gach radharc a fhilleadh in idirbheart ar an "
"mbunachar sonraí seo. Féach:ref: `tiing-idirbheartaí-go-http-"
"iarrataireachtaí `."

msgid "``AUTOCOMMIT``"
msgstr "``AUTOCOMIT``"

msgid ""
"Set this to ``False`` if you want to :ref:`disable Django's transaction "
"management <deactivate-transaction-management>` and implement your own."
msgstr ""
"<deactivate-transaction-management>Socraigh é seo go `False`` más mian leat: "
"ref: `bainistíocht idirbheart Django a dhíchumasú `agus cuir tú féin i "
"bhfeidhm."

msgid "``ENGINE``"
msgstr "``INNEAL``"

msgid "The database backend to use. The built-in database backends are:"
msgstr ""
"An cúltaca bunachar sonraí le húsáid. Is iad na cúltaca bunachar sonraí "
"ionsuite:"

msgid "``'django.db.backends.postgresql'``"
msgstr "``'django.db.backends.postgresql'``"

msgid "``'django.db.backends.mysql'``"
msgstr "``'django.db.backends.mysql'``"

msgid "``'django.db.backends.sqlite3'``"
msgstr "``'django.db.backends.sqlite3'``"

msgid "``'django.db.backends.oracle'``"
msgstr "``'django.db.backends.oracle'``"

msgid ""
"You can use a database backend that doesn't ship with Django by setting "
"``ENGINE`` to a fully-qualified path (i.e. ``mypackage.backends.whatever``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cúltaca bunachar sonraí a úsáid nach seolann le Django trí "
"“ENGINE” a shocrú go cosán láncháilithe (ie ``mypackage.backends.whatever``)."

msgid "``HOST``"
msgstr "``ÓSTACH``"

msgid ""
"Which host to use when connecting to the database. An empty string means "
"localhost. Not used with SQLite."
msgstr ""
"Cén óstach le húsáid agus tú ag nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí. Ciallaíonn "
"sreang folamh localhost. Ní úsáidtear le SQLite."

msgid ""
"If this value starts with a forward slash (``'/'``) and you're using MySQL, "
"MySQL will connect via a Unix socket to the specified socket. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má thosaíonn an luach seo le slash ar aghaidh (``'/'`) agus má tá MySQL á "
"úsáid agat, ceanglóidh MySQL trí soicéad Unix leis an soicéad sonraithe. Mar "
"shampla::"

msgid ""
"If you're using MySQL and this value *doesn't* start with a forward slash, "
"then this value is assumed to be the host."
msgstr ""
"Má tá MySQL á úsáid agat agus nach dtosaíonn an luach seo* le slach ar "
"aghaidh, glactar leis gurb é an luach seo an t-óstach."

msgid ""
"If you're using PostgreSQL, by default (empty :setting:`HOST`), the "
"connection to the database is done through UNIX domain sockets ('local' "
"lines in ``pg_hba.conf``). If your UNIX domain socket is not in the standard "
"location, use the same value of ``unix_socket_directory`` from "
"``postgresql.conf``. If you want to connect through TCP sockets, "
"set :setting:`HOST` to 'localhost' or '127.0.0.1' ('host' lines in "
"``pg_hba.conf``). On Windows, you should always define :setting:`HOST`, as "
"UNIX domain sockets are not available."
msgstr ""
"Má tá PostgreSQL á úsáid agat, de réir réamhshocraithe (folam:setting: "
"`HOST`), déantar an nasc leis an mbunachar sonraí trí soicéid fearainn UNIX "
"(línte 'áitiúla' i `pg_hba.conf``). Mura bhfuil do soicéad fearainn UNIX sa "
"suíomh caighdeánach, bain úsáid as an luach céanna de "
"``unix_socket_directory ``ó `postgresql.conf``. Más mian leat nascadh trí "
"soicéid TCP, socraí:setting: `HOST` go 'localhost' nó '127.0.0.1' (línte "
"'óstach' i `pg_hba.conf``). Ar Windows, ba cheart duit sainmhíniú i "
"gcónaí:setting: `HOST`, toisc nach bhfuil soicéid fearainn UNIX ar fáil."

msgid "``NAME``"
msgstr "```AINM ``"

msgid ""
"The name of the database to use. For SQLite, it's the full path to the "
"database file. When specifying the path, always use forward slashes, even on "
"Windows (e.g. ``C:/homes/user/mysite/sqlite3.db``)."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an bhunachar sonraí le húsáid. Maidir le SQLite, is é an cosán iomlán "
"chuig an gcomhad bunachar sonraí. Agus an cosán á shonrú agat, bain úsáid as "
"slashes ar aghaidh i gcónaí, fiú ar Windows (m.sh. ``C: /homes/user/mysite/"
"sqlite3.db``)."

msgid "``CONN_MAX_AGE``"
msgstr "``CONN_MAX_AOS``"

msgid "Default: ``0``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``0``"

msgid ""
"The lifetime of a database connection, as an integer of seconds. Use ``0`` "
"to close database connections at the end of each request — Django's "
"historical behavior — and ``None`` for unlimited :ref:`persistent database "
"connections <persistent-database-connections>`."
msgstr ""
"Saolré nasc bunachar sonraí, mar shláimhir soicind. <persistent-database-"
"connections>Úsáid ``0`` chun naisc bunachar sonraí a dhúnadh ag deireadh "
"gach iarratais - iompar stairiúil Django - agus ``None ``le haghaidh "
"neamhtheoranna:ref: `naisc bunachar sonraí leanúnacha `."

msgid "``CONN_HEALTH_CHECKS``"
msgstr "``SEICEÁLACHA SLÁINTE CONN``"

msgid ""
"If set to ``True``, existing :ref:`persistent database connections "
"<persistent-database-connections>` will be health checked before they are "
"reused in each request performing database access. If the health check "
"fails, the connection will be reestablished without failing the request when "
"the connection is no longer usable but the database server is ready to "
"accept and serve new connections (e.g. after database server restart closing "
"existing connections)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe go ``True``, déan <persistent-database-connections>far "
"seiceáil sláinte atá ann: ref: `naisc bunachar sonraí leanúnacha 'sula n-"
"athúsáidtear iad i ngach iarratas a dhéanann rochtain ar bhunachar sonraí. "
"Má theipeann ar an seiceáil sláinte, athbhunófar an nasc gan teip ar an "
"iarratas nuair nach bhfuil an nasc inúsáidte a thuilleadh ach tá an "
"freastalaí bunachar sonraí réidh chun naisc nua a ghlacadh agus a "
"sheirbheáil (m.sh. tar éis freastalaí bunachar sonraí a atosú a dhúnadh"

msgid ""
"Extra parameters to use when connecting to the database. Available "
"parameters vary depending on your database backend."
msgstr ""
"Paraiméadair bhreise le húsáid agus tú ag nascadh leis an mbunachar "
"Athraíonn na paraiméadair atá ar fáil ag brath ar do chúltaca bunachar"

msgid ""
"Some information on available parameters can be found in the :doc:`Database "
"Backends </ref/databases>` documentation. For more information, consult your "
"backend module's own documentation."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir roinnt faisnéise faoi pharaiméadair atá ar fáil a fháil sa "
"dhoiciméadúiséireacht: Doc: `</ref/databases> Bunachar Sonraí Backends`. Le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, téigh i gcomhairle le cáipéisíocht do mhodúl "
"cúlt"

msgid "``PASSWORD``"
msgstr "``PASFHOCAL ``"

msgid ""
"The password to use when connecting to the database. Not used with SQLite."
msgstr ""
"An pasfhocal le húsáid agus tú ag nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí. Ní "
"úsáidtear le SQLite."

msgid "``PORT``"
msgstr "``CALAFOIRT'"

msgid ""
"The port to use when connecting to the database. An empty string means the "
"default port. Not used with SQLite."
msgstr ""
"An calafort le húsáid agus tú ag nascadh leis an mbunachar sonraí. "
"Ciallaíonn sreang folamh an calafort réamhshocraithe. Ní úsáidtear le SQLite."

msgid "``TIME_ZONE``"
msgstr "``CRIOS_AMA``"

msgid ""
"A string representing the time zone for this database connection or "
"``None``. This inner option of the :setting:`DATABASES` setting accepts the "
"same values as the general :setting:`TIME_ZONE` setting."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an crios ama don nasc bunachar sonraí seo nó ``None``. "
"Glacann an rogha istigh seo den socrú: setting: `DATABASES` leis na "
"luachanna céanna leis an socrú ginearált:setting: `TIME_ZONE`."

msgid ""
"When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, reading datetimes from the database "
"returns aware datetimes with the timezone set to this option's value if not "
"``None``, or to UTC otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: Setting: ```True`` `USE_TZ`, filleann dáta léitheoireachta ón "
"mbunachar sonraí dáta ar an eolas uaireanta agus an crios ama atá socraithe "
"ar luach an rogha seo mura bhfuil ``None``, nó go UTC ar shlí eile."

msgid "When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``False``, it is an error to set this option."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: SETTING: `USE_TZ` ``False``, is earráid é an rogha seo a shocrú."

msgid ""
"If the database backend doesn't support time zones (e.g. SQLite, MySQL, "
"Oracle), Django reads and writes datetimes in local time according to this "
"option if it is set and in UTC if it isn't."
msgstr ""
"Mura dtacaíonn cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí le criosanna ama (m.sh. SQLite, "
"MySQL, Oracle), léann agus scríobhann Django dáta-amanna in am áitiúil de "
"réir an rogha seo má tá sé socraithe agus i UTC mura bhfuil sé."

msgid ""
"Changing the connection time zone changes how datetimes are read from and "
"written to the database."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn athrú an chrios ama nasc an chaoi a léitear dáta-amanna ón "
"mbunachar sonraí agus a scríobh chuig."

msgid ""
"If Django manages the database and you don't have a strong reason to do "
"otherwise, you should leave this option unset. It's best to store datetimes "
"in UTC because it avoids ambiguous or nonexistent datetimes during daylight "
"saving time changes. Also, receiving datetimes in UTC keeps datetime "
"arithmetic simple — there's no need to consider potential offset changes "
"over a DST transition."
msgstr ""
"Má bhainistíonn Django an bunachar sonraí agus nach bhfuil cúis láidir agat "
"a mhalairt a dhéanamh, ba cheart duit an rogha seo a fhágáil gan socrú. Is "
"fearr amanna dáta a stóráil in UTC toisc go seachnaíonn sé amanna dáta "
"débhríoch nó nach bhfuil ann le linn athruithe ama sábhála solais an lae. "
"Chomh maith leis sin, coinníonn uimhríocht dáta-ama simplí a fháil in UTC - "
"ní gá athruithe fritháireamh féideartha a mheas thar aistriú DST."

msgid ""
"If you're connecting to a third-party database that stores datetimes in a "
"local time rather than UTC, then you must set this option to the appropriate "
"time zone. Likewise, if Django manages the database but third-party systems "
"connect to the same database and expect to find datetimes in local time, "
"then you must set this option."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag nascadh le bunachar sonraí tríú páirtí a stórálann dáta in am "
"áitiúil seachas UTC, ansin ní mór duit an rogha seo a shocrú go dtí an crios "
"ama cuí. Mar an gcéanna, má bhainistíonn Django an bunachar sonraí ach má "
"nascann córais tríú páirtí leis an mbunachar sonraí céanna agus má tá súil "
"leo dáta a fháil in am áitiúil, ansin ní mór duit an rogha seo a shocrú."

msgid ""
"If the database backend supports time zones (e.g., PostgreSQL), then the "
"database connection's time zone is set to this value."
msgstr ""
"Má thacaíonn cúltaca an bhunachar sonraí le criosanna ama (m.sh., "
"PostgreSQL), ansin socraítear crios ama an nasc bunachar sonraí go dtí an "
"luach seo."

msgid ""
"Although setting the ``TIME_ZONE`` option is very rarely needed, there are "
"situations where it becomes necessary. Specifically, it's recommended to "
"match the general :setting:`TIME_ZONE` setting when dealing with raw queries "
"involving date/time functions like PostgreSQL's ``date_trunc()`` or "
"``generate_series()``, especially when generating time-based series that "
"transition daylight savings."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil gá go han-annamh ag teastáil an rogha ``TIME_ZONE`` a shocrú, "
"tá cásanna ann ina bhfuil sé riachtanach. Go sonrach, moltar an socrú "
"ginearált:setting: `TIME_ZONE` a mheaitseáil agus tú ag déileáil le "
"ceisteanna amh a bhaineann le feidhmeanna dáta/ama cosúil le `date_trunc () "
"`PostgreSQL nó `generate_series () ``, go háirithe agus sraitheanna bunaithe "
"ama á ghiniúint a aistríonn coigilteas solais."

msgid ""
"This value can be changed at any time, the database will handle the "
"conversion of datetimes to the configured time zone."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an luach seo a athrú ag am ar bith, láimhseálfaidh an bunachar "
"sonraí tiontú dáta-amanna go dtí an crios ama cumraithe."

msgid ""
"However, this has a downside: receiving all datetimes in local time makes "
"datetime arithmetic more tricky — you must account for possible offset "
"changes over DST transitions."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, tá míbhuntáiste aige seo: bíonn uimhríocht dáta níos deacra "
"uimhríocht dáta-ama go léir a fháil in am áitiúil - ní mór duit cuntas a "
"thabhairt ar athruithe féideartha fritháireamh ar aistrithe"

msgid ""
"Consider converting to local time explicitly with ``AT TIME ZONE`` in raw "
"SQL queries instead of setting the ``TIME_ZONE`` option."
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar thiontú go am áitiúil go sainráite le ``AT TIME ZONE`` i "
"gceisteanna amh SQL in ionad an rogha ``TIME_ZONE`` a shocrú."

msgid "``DISABLE_SERVER_SIDE_CURSORS``"
msgstr "``CÚRSAÍ TAOBH FREASTALAÍ_DÍCHUMASACHA``"

msgid ""
"Set this to ``True`` if you want to disable the use of server-side cursors "
"with :meth:`.QuerySet.iterator`. :ref:`transaction-pooling-server-side-"
"cursors` describes the use case."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é seo go ``True`` más mian leat úsáid cúrsaí taobh an fhreastalaí a "
"dhíchumasú le: meth: `.queryset.iterator`. :ref: `transaction-pooling-server-"
"side-cursors` cur síos ar an gcás úsáide."

msgid "This is a PostgreSQL-specific setting."
msgstr "Is suíomh atá sonrach le PostgreSQL é seo."

msgid "``USER``"
msgstr "``ÚSÁIDEOIR ``"

msgid ""
"The username to use when connecting to the database. Not used with SQLite."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm úsáideora le húsáid agus tú ag ceangal leis an mbunachar sonraí Ní "
"úsáidtear le SQLite."

msgid "``TEST``"
msgstr "``TÁSTÁLA``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary of settings for test databases; for more details about the "
"creation and use of test databases, see :ref:`the-test-database`."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir socruithe do bhunachar sonraí tástála; le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí "
"faoi chruthú agus úsáid bunachair sonraí tástála, féach:ref: `the-test-"
"database`."

msgid "Here's an example with a test database configuration::"
msgstr "Seo sampla le cumraíocht bunachar sonraí tástála:"

msgid "The following keys in the ``TEST`` dictionary are available:"
msgstr "Tá na heochracha seo a leanas sa fhoclóir ``TEST`` ar fáil:"

msgid "``CHARSET``"
msgstr "``CHARSET``"

msgid ""
"The character set encoding used to create the test database. The value of "
"this string is passed directly through to the database, so its format is "
"backend-specific."
msgstr ""
"An t-ionchódú tacar carachtair a úsáidtear chun an bunachar sonraí tástála a "
"Cuirtear luach an teaghráin seo go díreach chuig an mbunachar sonraí, mar "
"sin tá a fhormáid go sonrach le cúltaca."

msgid ""
"Supported by the PostgreSQL_ (``postgresql``) and MySQL_ (``mysql``) "
"backends."
msgstr ""
"Le tacaíocht ó na cúltaca PostgreSQL (`postgresql``) agus MySQL_ (``mysql``)."

msgid "``COLLATION``"
msgstr "``COMHLÁNÚ ``"

msgid ""
"The collation order to use when creating the test database. This value is "
"passed directly to the backend, so its format is backend-specific."
msgstr ""
"An t-ordú comhlánaithe le húsáid agus an bunachar sonraí tástála á chruthú. "
"Cuirtear an luach seo ar aghaidh go díreach chuig an gcúltaca, mar sin tá a "
"fhormáid go sonrach le cúltaca."

msgid ""
"Only supported for the ``mysql`` backend (see the `MySQL manual`_ for "
"details)."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear ach leis an gcúltaca ``mysql`` (féach an `lámhleabhar MySQL `_ "
"le haghaidh sonraí)."

msgid "``DEPENDENCIES``"
msgstr "``SPLEÁCHAIS ``"

msgid ""
"Default: ``['default']``, for all databases other than ``default``, which "
"has no dependencies."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: ``['réamhshocraithe']``, do gach bunachar sonraí seachas "
"``default``, nach bhfuil aon spleáchais aige."

msgid ""
"The creation-order dependencies of the database. See the documentation "
"on :ref:`controlling the creation order of test databases <topics-testing-"
"creation-dependencies>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Sspleáchais ordú cruthaithe an bhunachar sonraí. Féach an doiciméadú ar:ref: "
"`ord cruthaithe bunachar sonraí tástála a rialú <topics-testing-creation-"
"dependencies>`le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``MIGRATE``"
msgstr "```IMIRCE``"

msgid ""
"When set to ``False``, migrations won't run when creating the test database. "
"This is similar to setting ``None`` as a value "
"in :setting:`MIGRATION_MODULES`, but for all apps."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh sé socraithe ar `False`, ní rithfidh imirce agus an bunachar "
"sonraí tástála á gcruthú. Tá sé seo cosúil le ``None`` a shocrú mar luach "
"in:setting: `MIGRATION_MODULES`, ach do gach aip."

msgid "``MIRROR``"
msgstr "``SCÁTHÁN``"

msgid ""
"The alias of the database that this database should mirror during testing. "
"It depends on transactions and therefore must be used "
"within :class:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase` instead "
"of :class:`~django.test.TestCase`."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm den bhunachar sonraí ba chóir go mbeadh an bunachar sonraí seo a "
"scáthú le linn Braitheann sé ar idirbhearta agus dá bhrí sin caithfear é a "
"úsáid laistigh de: class: `~django.test.transactionTestCase` in ionad:class: "
"`~django.test.testcase`."

msgid ""
"This setting exists to allow for testing of primary/replica (referred to as "
"master/slave by some databases) configurations of multiple databases. See "
"the documentation on :ref:`testing primary/replica configurations <topics-"
"testing-primaryreplica>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tá an suíomh seo ann chun cumraíochtaí bunscoil/macasamhail (dá ngairtear "
"máistir/sclábhaí ag roinnt bunachair sonraí) a thástáil ar bhunachar sonraí "
"iolracha. <topics-testing-primaryreplica>Féach an doiciméadú ar:ref: "
"`cumraíochtaí bunscoile/macasamhail a thástáil `le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "The name of database to use when running the test suite."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an bhunachar sonraí le húsáid agus an tsraith tástála á reáchtáil."

msgid ""
"If the default value (``None``) is used with the SQLite database engine, the "
"tests will use a memory resident database. For all other database engines "
"the test database will use the name ``'test_' + DATABASE_NAME``."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáidtear an luach réamhshocraithe (``None ``) le hinneall bunachar "
"sonraí SQLite, úsáidfidh na tástálacha bunachar sonraí cónaitheoirí cuimhne. "
"Maidir le gach inneall bunachar sonraí eile úsáidfidh an bunachar sonraí "
"tástála an t-ainm ```test_'+DATABASE_NAME``."

msgid "See :ref:`the-test-database`."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `bunachar sonraí tástála'."

msgid "``TEMPLATE``"
msgstr "``TEIMPLÉAD``"

msgid ""
"The name of a `template`_ (e.g. ``'template0'``) from which to create the "
"test database."
msgstr ""
"Ainm `teimpléad`_ (m.sh. ```teimpléad0'`) as a chruthófar bunachar sonraí "
"tástála."

msgid "``CREATE_DB``"
msgstr "``CRUTHAITHE_DB``"

msgid "This is an Oracle-specific setting."
msgstr "Is suíomh atá sonrach le Oracle é seo."

msgid ""
"If it is set to ``False``, the test tablespaces won't be automatically "
"created at the beginning of the tests or dropped at the end."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe ar `False``, ní chruthófar na spásanna tástála go "
"huathoibríoch ag tús na dtástálacha nó ní chruthófar na spásanna tástála ag "
"an deireadh."

msgid "``CREATE_USER``"
msgstr "``CHRUTHAITHE_ÚSÁIDEOIR``"

msgid ""
"If it is set to ``False``, the test user won't be automatically created at "
"the beginning of the tests and dropped at the end."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe ar `False``, ní chruthófar an t-úsáideoir tástála go "
"huathoibríoch ag tús na dtástálacha agus titeoidh sé ag an deireadh."

msgid ""
"The username to use when connecting to the Oracle database that will be used "
"when running tests. If not provided, Django will use ``'test_' + USER``."
msgstr ""
"An t-ainm úsáideora le húsáid agus tú ag ceangal le bunachar sonraí Oracle a "
"úsáidfear agus tástálacha á reáchtáil Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, úsáidfidh "
"Django ```'test_'+USER``."

msgid ""
"The password to use when connecting to the Oracle database that will be used "
"when running tests. If not provided, Django will generate a random password."
msgstr ""
"An focal faire le húsáid agus tú ag nascadh le bunachar sonraí Oracle a "
"úsáidfear agus tástálacha á reáchtáil. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, ginfidh "
"Django pasfhocal randamach."

msgid "``ORACLE_MANAGED_FILES``"
msgstr "``COMHAD BAINISTITHE ORACLE``"

msgid ""
"If set to ``True``, Oracle Managed Files (OMF) tablespaces will be "
"used. :setting:`DATAFILE` and :setting:`DATAFILE_TMP` will be ignored."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe ar ``True``, úsáidfear spásanna tábla Comhaid Bainistithe "
"Oracle (OMF). :setting: `DATAFILE` agus:setting: `DATAFILE_TMP` déanfar "
"neamhaird."

msgid "``TBLSPACE``"
msgstr "``TBLSPACE``"

msgid ""
"The name of the tablespace that will be used when running tests. If not "
"provided, Django will use ``'test_' + USER``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an spás tábla a úsáidfear agus tástálacha á reáchtáil. Mura gcuirtear "
"ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django ```'test_'+USER``."

msgid "``TBLSPACE_TMP``"
msgstr "``TBLSPACE_TMP``"

msgid ""
"The name of the temporary tablespace that will be used when running tests. "
"If not provided, Django will use ``'test_' + USER + '_temp'``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an spás tábla sealadach a úsáidfear agus tástálacha á reáchtáil. Mura "
"gcuirtear ar fáil, úsáidfidh Django ```'test_'+ USER + '_temp'``."

msgid "``DATAFILE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE``"

msgid ""
"The name of the datafile to use for the TBLSPACE. If not provided, Django "
"will use ``TBLSPACE + '.dbf'``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm na fille sonraí le húsáid don TBLSPACE. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, "
"úsáidfidh Django ``TBLSPACE + '.dbf'``."

msgid "``DATAFILE_TMP``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_TMP``"

msgid ""
"The name of the datafile to use for the TBLSPACE_TMP. If not provided, "
"Django will use ``TBLSPACE_TMP + '.dbf'``."
msgstr ""
"Ainm na sonraí le húsáid don TBLSPACE_TMP. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, úsáidfidh "
"Django ``TBLSPACE_TMP + '.dbf'``."

msgid "``DATAFILE_MAXSIZE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_MAXSIZE``"

msgid "Default: ``'500M'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ```500M ``"

msgid "The maximum size that the DATAFILE is allowed to grow to."
msgstr "An méid uasta a cheadaítear don DATAFILE fás air."

msgid "``DATAFILE_TMP_MAXSIZE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_TMP_MAXSIZE``"

msgid "The maximum size that the DATAFILE_TMP is allowed to grow to."
msgstr "An méid uasta a cheadaítear don DATAFILE_TMP fás."

msgid "``DATAFILE_SIZE``"
msgstr "``MÉID_DATAFILE``"

msgid "Default: ``'50M'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'50M'``"

msgid "The initial size of the DATAFILE."
msgstr "Méid tosaigh an DATAFILE."

msgid "``DATAFILE_TMP_SIZE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_TMP_SIZE``"

msgid "The initial size of the DATAFILE_TMP."
msgstr "Méid tosaigh an DATAFILE_TMP."

msgid "``DATAFILE_EXTSIZE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_EXTSIZE``"

msgid "Default: ``'25M'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'25M'``"

msgid ""
"The amount by which the DATAFILE is extended when more space is required."
msgstr ""
"An méid a leathnaítear an DATAFILE nuair a bhíonn níos mó spáis ag teastáil."

msgid "``DATAFILE_TMP_EXTSIZE``"
msgstr "``DATAFILE_TMP_EXTSIZE``"

msgid ""
"The amount by which the DATAFILE_TMP is extended when more space is required."
msgstr ""
"An méid a leathnaítear an DATAFILE_TMP nuair a bhíonn níos mó spáis ag "
"teastáil."

msgid "``DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE``"
msgstr "``SONRA_UASLÓDÁIL_MÉID_CUIMHNEACHÁIN UASTA ``"

msgid "Default: ``2621440`` (i.e. 2.5 MB)."
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: `2621440`` (ie 2.5 MB)."

msgid ""
"The maximum size in bytes that a request body may be before "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` (``RequestDataTooBig``) "
"is raised. The check is done when accessing ``request.body`` or "
"``request.POST`` and is calculated against the total request size excluding "
"any file upload data. You can set this to ``None`` to disable the check. "
"Applications that are expected to receive unusually large form posts should "
"tune this setting."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an méid uasta i mbeátaí a d'fhéadfadh comhlacht iarratais a bheith "
"roimh a:exc: `~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` "
"(``RequestDataToObig``). Déantar an seiceáil nuair a bhíonn rochtain agat ar "
"``request.body`` nó ``request.post`` agus ríomhtar é i gcoinne méid iomlán "
"an iarratais gan aon sonraí uaslódála comhad a áireamh. Is féidir leat é seo "
"a shocrú go ``None ``chun an seic a dhíchumasú. Ba chóir d'iarratais a "
"bhfuiltear ag súil go bhfaighidh poist foirme neamhghnách mór an suíomh"

msgid ""
"The amount of request data is correlated to the amount of memory needed to "
"process the request and populate the GET and POST dictionaries. Large "
"requests could be used as a denial-of-service attack vector if left "
"unchecked. Since web servers don't typically perform deep request "
"inspection, it's not possible to perform a similar check at that level."
msgstr ""
"Tá an méid sonraí iarratais comhghaolmhar leis an méid cuimhne atá ag "
"teastáil chun an t-iarratas a phróiseáil agus na foclóirí GET agus POST a "
"líonadh. D'fhéadfaí iarratais mhóra a úsáid mar veicteoir ionsaí diúltaithe "
"seirbhíse má fhágtar gan seiceáil. Ós rud é nach ndéanann freastalaithe "
"gréasáin iniúchadh domhain iarratais de ghnáth, ní féidir seiceáil den "
"chineál céanna a dhéanamh ag an leibhéal sin."

msgid "See also :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`."

msgid "``DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_NUMBER_FIELDS``"
msgstr "``SONRA_UASLÓDÁIL_UIMHREACH_RÉIMSÍ UASGHAIR``"

msgid "Default: ``1000``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``1000``"

msgid ""
"The maximum number of parameters that may be received via GET or POST before "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` (``TooManyFields``) is "
"raised. You can set this to ``None`` to disable the check. Applications that "
"are expected to receive an unusually large number of form fields should tune "
"this setting."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an líon uasta na bparaiméadair a d'fhéadfaí a fháil trí GET nó "
"POST roimh a:exc: `~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` "
"(``ToomanyFields``). Is féidir leat é seo a shocrú go ``None ``chun an seic "
"a dhíchumasú. Ba chóir d'iarratais a bhfuiltear ag súil go bhfaighidh líon "
"neamhghnách mór réimsí foirme an socrú seo a"

msgid ""
"The number of request parameters is correlated to the amount of time needed "
"to process the request and populate the GET and POST dictionaries. Large "
"requests could be used as a denial-of-service attack vector if left "
"unchecked. Since web servers don't typically perform deep request "
"inspection, it's not possible to perform a similar check at that level."
msgstr ""
"Tá líon na bparaiméadair iarratais comhghaolmhar leis an méid ama a "
"theastaíonn chun an t-iarratas a phróiseáil agus na foclóirí GET agus POST a "
"líonadh. D'fhéadfaí iarratais mhóra a úsáid mar veicteoir ionsaí diúltaithe "
"seirbhíse má fhágtar gan seiceáil. Ós rud é nach ndéanann freastalaithe "
"gréasáin iniúchadh domhain iarratais de ghnáth, ní féidir seiceáil den "
"chineál céanna a dhéanamh ag an leibhéal sin."

msgid "``DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_NUMBER_FILES``"
msgstr "``SONRAÍ_UASLÓDÁIL_UIMHREACH_COMHAID ``"

msgid "Default: ``100``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``100``"

msgid ""
"The maximum number of files that may be received via POST in a ``multipart/"
"form-data`` encoded request before "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` (``TooManyFiles``) is "
"raised. You can set this to ``None`` to disable the check. Applications that "
"are expected to receive an unusually large number of file fields should tune "
"this setting."
msgstr ""
"Ardaítear an líon uasta comhaid a d'fhéadfaí a fháil trí POST in iarratas "
"ionchódaithe ``multipart/form-data ``roimh a:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` (`ToomanyFiles``). Is féidir "
"leat é seo a shocrú go ``None ``chun an seic a dhíchumasú. Ba chóir "
"d'iarratais a bhfuiltear ag súil go bhfaighidh líon neamhghnách mór réimsí "
"comhad an suíomh seo a dhí"

msgid ""
"The number of accepted files is correlated to the amount of time and memory "
"needed to process the request. Large requests could be used as a denial-of-"
"service attack vector if left unchecked. Since web servers don't typically "
"perform deep request inspection, it's not possible to perform a similar "
"check at that level."
msgstr ""
"Tá comhghaol ag líon na gcomhad a nglactar leis an méid ama agus cuimhne a "
"theastaíonn chun an iarratas a phróiseáil. D'fhéadfaí iarratais mhóra a "
"úsáid mar veicteoir ionsaí diúltaithe seirbhíse má fhágtar gan seiceáil. Ós "
"rud é nach ndéanann freastalaithe gréasáin iniúchadh domhain iarratais de "
"ghnáth, ní féidir seiceáil den chineál céanna a dhéanamh ag an leibhéal sin."

msgid "``DATABASE_ROUTERS``"
msgstr "``RÓDAIRÍ_BUNACHAR SONRAÍ``"

msgid ""
"The list of routers that will be used to determine which database to use "
"when performing a database query."
msgstr ""
"Liosta na ródairí a úsáidfear chun a chinneadh cén bunachar sonraí atá le "
"húsáid agus ceist bunachar sonraí á ndéanamh agat."

msgid ""
"See the documentation on :ref:`automatic database routing in multi database "
"configurations <topics-db-multi-db-routing>`."
msgstr ""
"<topics-db-multi-db-routing>Féach an doiciméadú ar:ref: `ródú uathoibríoch "
"bunachar sonraí i cumraíochtaí ilbhunachar sonraí `."

msgid "``DATE_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_DÁTA``"

msgid "Default: ``'N j, Y'`` (e.g. ``Feb. 4, 2003``)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'N j, Y'`` (m.sh. ``4 Feabhra, 2003``)"

msgid ""
"The default formatting to use for displaying date fields in any part of the "
"system. Note that the locale-dictated format has higher precedence and will "
"be applied instead. See :tfilter:`allowed date format strings <date>`."
msgstr ""
"An formáidiú réamhshocraithe le húsáid chun réimsí dáta a thaispeáint in aon "
"chuid den chóras. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an "
"bhformáid áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad sin. <date>Féach: "
"TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting:`TIME_FORMAT` "
"and :setting:`SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:setting: `DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting: `TIME_FORMAT` "
"agus:setting: `SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`."

msgid "``DATE_INPUT_FORMATS``"
msgstr "``FORMÁIDÍ DÁTA_IONCHUIRIÚCHÁIN ``"

msgid ""
"A list of formats that will be accepted when inputting data on a date field. "
"Formats will be tried in order, using the first valid one. Note that these "
"format strings use Python's :ref:`datetime module syntax <strftime-strptime-"
"behavior>`, not the format strings from the :tfilter:`date` template filter."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na formáidí a nglacfar leo agus sonraí á ionchur isteach i réimse "
"dáta. Déanfar triail a bhaint as formáidí in ord, ag baint úsáide as an "
"gcéad cheann bailí. Tabhair faoi deara go n-úsáideann na teaghráin formáide "
"seo comhréir modúl Python: ref: `datetime '<strftime-strptime-behavior>, ní "
"na teaghráin formáide ón scagaire teimpléad:tfilter: `dáta`."

msgid ""
"The locale-dictated format has higher precedence and will be applied instead."
msgstr ""
"Tá tosaíocht níos airde ag an bhformáid áitiúil agus cuirfear i bhfeidhm ina "
"ionad sin."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS` and :setting:`TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS` agus:SETTING: "
"`TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."

msgid "``DATETIME_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_DÁTAIME``"

msgid "Default: ``'N j, Y, P'`` (e.g. ``Feb. 4, 2003, 4 p.m.``)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'N j, Y, P'`` (m.sh. ``4 Feabhra, 2003, 4 p.m.``)"

msgid ""
"The default formatting to use for displaying datetime fields in any part of "
"the system. Note that the locale-dictated format has higher precedence and "
"will be applied instead. See :tfilter:`allowed date format strings <date>`."
msgstr ""
"An formáidiú réamhshocraithe le húsáid chun réimsí dáta-ama a thaispeáint in "
"aon chuid den chóras. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag "
"an bhformáid áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad sin. "
"<date>Féach: TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT`, :setting:`TIME_FORMAT` "
"and :setting:`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT`, :setting: `TIME_FORMAT` agus:setting: "
"`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`."

msgid "``DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS``"
msgstr "``FORMÁIDÍ DÁTAIME_IONCHUIRIÚCHÁIN ``"

msgid ""
"A list of formats that will be accepted when inputting data on a datetime "
"field. Formats will be tried in order, using the first valid one. Note that "
"these format strings use Python's :ref:`datetime module syntax <strftime-"
"strptime-behavior>`, not the format strings from the :tfilter:`date` "
"template filter. Date-only formats are not included as datetime fields will "
"automatically try :setting:`DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` in last resort."
msgstr ""
"Liosta formáidí a nglacfar leo agus sonraí á ionchur isteach ar réimse dáta-"
"ama. Déanfar triail a bhaint as formáidí in ord, ag baint úsáide as an gcéad "
"cheann bailí. Tabhair faoi deara go n-úsáideann na teaghráin formáide seo "
"comhréir modúl Python: ref: `datetime '<strftime-strptime-behavior>, ní na "
"teaghráin formáide ón scagaire teimpléad:tfilter: `dáta`. Ní chuirtear "
"formáidí dáta amháin san áireamh mar go ndéanfaidh réimsí dáta-ama iarracht "
"go huathoibríoch: setting: `DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` sa rogha deireanach."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` and :setting:`TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` agus:socrú: `TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."

msgid "A boolean that turns on/off debug mode."
msgstr "Boolean a chasann ar/as modh dífhabhtaithe."

msgid "Never deploy a site into production with :setting:`DEBUG` turned on."
msgstr ""
"Ná imscaradh suíomh riamh i dtáirgeadh le: socrú: `DEBUG` a chasadh air."

msgid ""
"One of the main features of debug mode is the display of detailed error "
"pages. If your app raises an exception when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``True``, "
"Django will display a detailed traceback, including a lot of metadata about "
"your environment, such as all the currently defined Django settings (from "
"``settings.py``)."
msgstr ""
"Ceann de phríomhghnéithe an mhodh dífhabhtaithe ná leathanaigh earráide "
"mionsonraithe a thaispeáint. Má ardaíonn d'aip eisceacht nuair a bhíonn: "
"socrú: `DEBUG` ``True``, taispeánfaidh Django rianú mionsonraithe, lena n-"
"áirítear go leor meiteashonraí faoi do thimpeallacht, mar shampla na "
"socruithe Django atá sainmhínithe faoi láthair (ó `settings.py``)."

msgid ""
"As a security measure, Django will *not* include settings that might be "
"sensitive, such as :setting:`SECRET_KEY`. Specifically, it will exclude any "
"setting whose name includes any of the following:"
msgstr ""
"Mar bheart slándála, * ní chuimseoidh Django socruithe a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith íogair, mar shampla:setting: `SECRET_KEY`. Go sonrach, eisifaidh sé "
"aon socrú a chuimsíonn a n-ainm aon cheann de na nithe seo a leanas:"

msgid "``'API'``"
msgstr "```'API'``"

msgid "``'KEY'``"
msgstr "```'EOCHAIR'`"

msgid "``'PASS'``"
msgstr "```'PASS'``"

msgid "``'SECRET'``"
msgstr "```'RÚNAÍ'`"

msgid "``'SIGNATURE'``"
msgstr "```'SÍNIÚ'`"

msgid "``'TOKEN'``"
msgstr "```'TOKEN'``"

msgid ""
"Note that these are *partial* matches. ``'PASS'`` will also match PASSWORD, "
"just as ``'TOKEN'`` will also match TOKENIZED and so on."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur cluichí páirtitheach* iad seo. Meaitneoidh ``'PASS'`` "
"PASSWORD freisin, díreach mar a mheaitseálfaidh ``'TOKEN'` TOKENIZED agus "
"mar sin de freisin."

msgid ""
"Still, note that there are always going to be sections of your debug output "
"that are inappropriate for public consumption. File paths, configuration "
"options and the like all give attackers extra information about your server."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, tabhair faoi deara go mbeidh codanna de d'aschur dífhabhtaithe "
"ann i gcónaí atá míchuí le haghaidh tomhaltas poiblí. Tugann cosáin comhad, "
"roghanna cumraíochta agus a leithéid go léir faisnéis bhreise "
"d'ionsaitheoirí faoi do fhre"

msgid ""
"It is also important to remember that when running with :setting:`DEBUG` "
"turned on, Django will remember every SQL query it executes. This is useful "
"when you're debugging, but it'll rapidly consume memory on a production "
"server."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach cuimhneamh freisin go gcuimhneoidh Django ar gach ceist "
"SQL a fhorghníomhaíonn sé nuair a bheidh ag rith le:setting: `DEBUG` air. Tá "
"sé seo úsáideach nuair a bhíonn tú ag dífhabhtú, ach ídífidh sé cuimhne go "
"tapa ar fhreastalaí táirgeachta."

msgid ""
"Finally, if :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``, you also need to properly set "
"the :setting:`ALLOWED_HOSTS` setting. Failing to do so will result in all "
"requests being returned as \"Bad Request (400)\"."
msgstr ""
"Faoi dheireadh, más é: setting: `DEBUG` ``False``, ní mór duit an socrú: "
"setting: `ALLOWED_HOSTS` a shocrú i gceart freisin. Mura ndéantar é sin, "
"beidh gach iarratas ar ais mar “Droch-iarratas (400)”."

msgid ""
"The default :file:`settings.py` file created by :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>` sets ``DEBUG = True`` for convenience."
msgstr ""
"<startproject>Leagann an comhad réamhshocraithe:file: `settings.py` a "
"chruthaí:djadmin: `django-admin startproject ```DEBUG = True`` le haghaidh "
"áisiúlachta."

msgid "``DEBUG_PROPAGATE_EXCEPTIONS``"
msgstr "```EISCEACHTAIS_IOMADAITHE_DEBUG``"

msgid ""
"If set to ``True``, Django's exception handling of view functions "
"(:data:`~django.conf.urls.handler500`, or the debug view if :setting:`DEBUG` "
"is ``True``) and logging of 500 responses (:ref:`django-request-logger`) is "
"skipped and exceptions propagate upward."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé socraithe go `True``, déantar láimhseáil eisceachta Django ar "
"fheidhmeanna amharc (:data: `~django.conf.urls.handler500`, nó an dearcadh "
"dífhabhtaithe ife:setting: `DEBUG` `True``) agus logáil 500 freagra (:ref: "
"`django-request-logger`) agus iomadú eisceachtaí aníos."

msgid ""
"This can be useful for some test setups. It shouldn't be used on a live site "
"unless you want your web server (instead of Django) to generate \"Internal "
"Server Error\" responses. In that case, make sure your server doesn't show "
"the stack trace or other sensitive information in the response."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis seo a bheith úsáideach do roinnt socruithe tástála. Níor "
"chóir é a úsáid ar shuíomh beo mura dteastaíonn uait do fhreastalaí gréasáin "
"(in ionad Django) freagraí “Earráid Freastalaí Inmheánach” a ghiniúint. Sa "
"chás sin, déan cinnte nach dtaispeánann do fhreastalaí an rian cruach nó "
"faisnéis íogair eile sa fhreagra."

msgid "``DECIMAL_SEPARATOR``"
msgstr "``DEIGHILTEOIR DEACHIMAL``"

msgid "Default: ``'.'`` (Dot)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'.'` (Ponc)"

msgid "Default decimal separator used when formatting decimal numbers."
msgstr "Déileálóir deachúil réamhshocraithe a úsáidtear agus uimhreacha"

msgid ""
"Note that the locale-dictated format has higher precedence and will be "
"applied instead."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an bhformáid áitiúil "
"agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad sin."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING`, :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"and :setting:`USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `NUMBER_GROUPING`, :setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"agus:setting: `USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."

msgid "``DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD``"
msgstr "``RÉAMHSHOCRAITHE_AUTO_FIELD``"

msgid "Default: ``'``:class:`django.db.models.AutoField`\\ ``'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: `````:class: `Django.db.Models.AutoField`\\ ````"

msgid ""
"Default primary key field type to use for models that don't have a field "
"with :attr:`primary_key=True <django.db.models.Field.primary_key>`."
msgstr ""
"<django.db.models.Field.primary_key>Cineál réimse eochair phríomhúil "
"réamhshocraithe le húsáid le haghaidh samhlacha nach bhfuil réimse acu "
"le:attr: `primary_key=True `."

msgid "Migrating auto-created through tables"
msgstr "Aimirce uathoibríoch a cruthaíodh"

msgid ""
"The value of ``DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`` will be respected when creating new auto-"
"created through tables for many-to-many relationships."
msgstr ""
"Meas a thabhairt ar luach `DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`` nuair a chruthaítear "
"uathoibríoch nua trí tháblaí le haghaidh caidrimh go leor."

msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the primary keys of existing auto-created through tables "
"cannot currently be updated by the migrations framework."
msgstr ""
"Ar an drochuair, ní féidir leis an gcreat imirce príomh-eochracha atá ann "
"cheana a cruthaíodh trí tháblaí a nuashonrú faoi láthair."

msgid ""
"This means that if you switch the value of ``DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`` and then "
"generate migrations, the primary keys of the related models will be updated, "
"as will the foreign keys from the through table, but the primary key of the "
"auto-created through table will not be migrated."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo má athraíonn tú luach ``DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD`` agus ansin "
"imirce a ghineann tú, nuashonrófar eochracha príomhúil na samhlacha "
"gaolmhara, mar aon leis na heochracha eachtracha ón tábla trí thráid, ach ní "
"imirfear príomh-eochair an tábla uathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"In order to address this, you should add "
"a :class:`~django.db.migrations.operations.RunSQL` operation to your "
"migrations to perform the required ``ALTER TABLE`` step. You can check the "
"existing table name through ``sqlmigrate``, ``dbshell``, or with the field’s "
"``remote_field.through._meta.db_table`` property."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn aghaidh a thabhairt air seo, ba chóir duit oibríocht a:class: "
"`~django.db.migrations.operations.runsql` a chur le d'imirce chun an chéim "
"``ALTER TABLE`` riachtanach a dhéanamh. Is féidir leat an t-ainm tábla atá "
"ann cheana a sheiceáil trí `sqlmigrate``, `dbshell``, nó le "
"`remote_field.through an réimse. Maoin _meta.db_table ``."

msgid ""
"Explicitly defined through models are already handled by the migrations "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an córas imirce láimhseáil cheana féin a shainmhínítear go sainráite "
"trí"

msgid ""
"Allowing automatic migrations for the primary key of existing auto-created "
"through tables :ticket:`may be implemented at a later date <32674>`."
msgstr ""
"<32674>Imirce uathoibríoch a cheadú don phríomh-eochair an uathoibríoch atá "
"ann cheana a chruthaítear trí tháblaí: ticéad: féadfar 'a chur i bhfeidhm"

msgid "``DEFAULT_CHARSET``"
msgstr "``DEFAULT_CHARSET``"

msgid "Default: ``'utf-8'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'utf-8'``"

msgid ""
"Default charset to use for all ``HttpResponse`` objects, if a MIME type "
"isn't manually specified. Used when constructing the ``Content-Type`` header."
msgstr ""
"Charset réamhshocraithe le húsáid do gach rud ``HttpResponse`, mura ndéantar "
"cineál MIME a shonrú de láimh. Úsáidtear agus an ceannteideal ``Content-"
"Type`` á thógáil."

msgid "``DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER``"
msgstr "``TUAIRISEOIRÍ_EISCEACHTÁIL_RÉAMHSHOCRAITHE``"

msgid "Default: ``'``:class:`django.views.debug.ExceptionReporter`\\ ``'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: `````:class: `Django.Views.debug.ExceptionReporter`\\ ````"

msgid ""
"Default exception reporter class to be used if none has been assigned to "
"the :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` instance yet. See :ref:`custom-error-"
"reports`."
msgstr ""
"Aicme tuairisceoir eisceachta réamhshocraithe le húsáid mura bhfuil aon "
"duine sannta don shampla:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` fós. Féach: "
"tagairt: `tuarascálacha saincheaptha earráid`."

msgid "``DEFAULT_EXCEPTION_REPORTER_FILTER``"
msgstr "``SCAGAIR_TUAIRISCITHEOIRÍ_EISCEACHTÁIL_RÉAMHSHOCRAITHE``"

msgid ""
"Default: ``'``:class:`django.views.debug.SafeExceptionReporterFilter`\\ ``'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: `````:class: "
"`django.views.debug.safeExceptionReporterFilter`\\ ````"

msgid ""
"Default exception reporter filter class to be used if none has been assigned "
"to the :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` instance yet. See :ref:`Filtering "
"error reports<filtering-error-reports>`."
msgstr ""
"Aicme scagaire tuairisceachta eisceachta réamhshocraithe le húsáid mura "
"sannadh aon rud don shampla:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` fós. "
"<filtering-error-reports>Féach: tagairt: `Tuarascálacha earráide scagtha `."

msgid "``DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL``"
msgstr "``DEFAULT_FROM_RÍOMHPHOST``"

msgid "Default: ``'webmaster@localhost'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'stiúrthóir gréasáin @localhost '``"

msgid ""
"Default email address for automated correspondence from the site manager(s). "
"This address is used in the ``From:`` header of outgoing emails and can take "
"any format valid in the chosen email sending protocol."
msgstr ""
"Seoladh ríomhphoist réamhshocraithe le haghaidh comhfhreagras uathoibrithe ó "
"bhainisteoir an láithreáin Úsáidtear an seoladh seo sa cheanntásc ``From: "
"``de ríomhphoist amach agus féadann sé aon fhormáid a ghlacadh bailí sa "
"phrótacal seolta ríomhphoist roghnaithe."

msgid ""
"This doesn't affect error messages sent to :setting:`ADMINS` "
"and :setting:`MANAGERS`. See :setting:`SERVER_EMAIL` for that."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann sé seo difear do theachtaireachtaí earráide a sheoltar "
"chuig:setting: `ADMINS` agus:setting: `MANAGERS`. Féach: SETTING: "
"`SERVER_EMAIL` chuige sin."

msgid "``DEFAULT_INDEX_TABLESPACE``"
msgstr "``RÉAMHSHOCRAITHE_INDEX_TABLESPACE``"

msgid ""
"Default tablespace to use for indexes on fields that don't specify one, if "
"the backend supports it (see :doc:`/topics/db/tablespaces`)."
msgstr ""
"Spás tábla réamhshocraithe le húsáid le haghaidh innéacsanna ar réimsí nach "
"sonraíonn ceann amháin, má thacaíonn an cúltaca leis (féach: doc: `/topics/"
"db/tablespaces`)."

msgid "``DEFAULT_TABLESPACE``"
msgstr "``DEFAULT_TABLESPACE``"

msgid ""
"Default tablespace to use for models that don't specify one, if the backend "
"supports it (see :doc:`/topics/db/tablespaces`)."
msgstr ""
"Spás tábla réamhshocraithe le húsáid le haghaidh samhlacha nach sonraíonn "
"ceann amháin, má thacaíonn an cúltaca leis (féach: doc: `/topics/db/"
"tablespaces`)."

msgid "``DISALLOWED_USER_AGENTS``"
msgstr "``GNÍOMHAIRÍ_ÚSÁIDEOIR_NEAMHCHEADAITHE``"

msgid ""
"List of compiled regular expression objects representing User-Agent strings "
"that are not allowed to visit any page, systemwide. Use this for bots/"
"crawlers. This is only used if ``CommonMiddleware`` is installed (see :doc:`/"
"topics/http/middleware`)."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na rudaí léirithe rialta tiomsaithe a léiríonn teaghráin "
"Gníomhaire Úsáideora nach bhfuil cead acu cuairt a thabhairt ar aon "
"leathanach, Úsáid é seo le haghaidh bots/crawlers. Ní úsáidtear é seo ach "
"amháin má tá ``CommonMiddleware`` suiteáilte (féach: doc: `/topics/http/"
"middleware`)."

msgid "``EMAIL_BACKEND``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_BACKEND``"

msgid ""
"Default: ``'``:class:`django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend`\\ ``'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: `````:class: "
"`django.core.mail.backends.smtp.emailBackend`\\ ````"

msgid ""
"The backend to use for sending emails. For the list of available backends "
"see :ref:`topic-email-backends`."
msgstr ""
"An cúltaca le húsáid chun ríomhphoist a sheoladh. Le haghaidh liosta na "
"gcúltaca atá ar fáil féach:ref: `topic-email-backends`."

msgid "``EMAIL_FILE_PATH``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_FILE_PATH``"

msgid "Default: Not defined"
msgstr "Réamhshocrú: Gan sainmhíniú"

msgid ""
"The directory used by the :ref:`file email backend <topic-email-file-"
"backend>` to store output files."
msgstr ""
"An eolaire a úsáideann an: ref: `backend ríomhphoist comhad <topic-email-"
"file-backend>`chun comhaid aschuir a stóráil."

msgid "``EMAIL_HOST``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_ÓST``"

msgid "Default: ``'localhost'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'localhost'``"

msgid "The host to use for sending email."
msgstr "An t-óstach le húsáid chun ríomhphost a sheoladh."

msgid "See also :setting:`EMAIL_PORT`."
msgstr "Féach freisin: socrú: `EMAIL_PORT`."

msgid "``EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_HOST_PASFHOCAL ``"

msgid ""
"Password to use for the SMTP server defined in :setting:`EMAIL_HOST`. This "
"setting is used in conjunction with :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_USER` when "
"authenticating to the SMTP server. If either of these settings is empty, "
"Django won't attempt authentication."
msgstr ""
"Pasfhocal le húsáid don fhreastalaí SMTP atá sainmhínithe in:setting: "
"`EMAIL_HOST`. Úsáidtear an socrú seo i gcomhar le:setting: `EMAIL_HOST_USER` "
"agus tú ag fíordheimhniú chuig an bhfreastalaí SMTP. Má tá ceachtar de na "
"socruithe seo folamh, ní dhéanfaidh Django iarracht fíordheimhniú."

msgid "See also :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_USER`."
msgstr "Féach freisin: socrú: `EMAIL_HOST_USER`."

msgid "``EMAIL_HOST_USER``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_HOST_ÚSÁIDEOIR ``"

msgid ""
"Username to use for the SMTP server defined in :setting:`EMAIL_HOST`. If "
"empty, Django won't attempt authentication."
msgstr ""
"Ainm úsáideora le húsáid don fhreastalaí SMTP atá sainmhínithe in:setting: "
"`EMAIL_HOST`. Má tá sé folamh, ní dhéanfaidh Django iarracht fíordheimhniú."

msgid "See also :setting:`EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD`."

msgid "``EMAIL_PORT``"
msgstr "```RÍOMHPHOST_PORT ``"

msgid "Default: ``25``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``25``"

msgid "Port to use for the SMTP server defined in :setting:`EMAIL_HOST`."
msgstr ""
"Port le húsáid don fhreastalaí SMTP atá sainmhínithe in:setting: "
"`EMAIL_HOST`."

msgid "``EMAIL_SUBJECT_PREFIX``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_ÁBHAIR_RÉAMH``"

msgid "Default: ``'[Django] '``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'[Django] '``"

msgid ""
"Subject-line prefix for email messages sent with "
"``django.core.mail.mail_admins`` or ``django.core.mail.mail_managers``. "
"You'll probably want to include the trailing space."
msgstr ""
"Réimír líne ábhair do theachtaireachtaí ríomhphoist a sheoltar le "
"``django.core.mail.mail_admins`` nó ``django.core.mail.mail_managers``. Is "
"dócha go mbeidh tú ag iarraidh an spás siar a áireamh."

msgid "``EMAIL_USE_LOCALTIME``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_ÚSÁID_ÁITIÚIL TIM``"

msgid ""
"Whether to send the SMTP ``Date`` header of email messages in the local time "
"zone (``True``) or in UTC (``False``)."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu an ceannteideal SMTP ``Dáta ``de theachtaireachtaí ríomhphoist a "
"sheoladh sa chrios ama áitiúil (``True``) nó i UTC (``False``)."

msgid "``EMAIL_USE_TLS``"
msgstr "```RÍOMHPHOST_ÚSÁID_TLS``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use a TLS (secure) connection when talking to the SMTP server. "
"This is used for explicit TLS connections, generally on port 587. If you are "
"experiencing hanging connections, see the implicit TLS "
"setting :setting:`EMAIL_USE_SSL`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu nasc TLS (slán) a úsáid agus tú ag caint leis an bhfreastalaí SMTP. "
"Úsáidtear é seo le haghaidh naisc shoiléire TLS, go ginearálta ar chalafort "
"587. Má tá naisc crochta agat, féach an socrú intuigthe TLS: setting: "
"`EMAIL_USE_SSL`."

msgid "``EMAIL_USE_SSL``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_ÚSÁID_SSL``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use an implicit TLS (secure) connection when talking to the SMTP "
"server. In most email documentation this type of TLS connection is referred "
"to as SSL. It is generally used on port 465. If you are experiencing "
"problems, see the explicit TLS setting :setting:`EMAIL_USE_TLS`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu nasc intuigthe TLS (slán) a úsáid agus tú ag caint leis an "
"bhfreastalaí SMTP. I bhformhór na ndoiciméadaithe ríomhphoist tugtar SSL ar "
"an gcineál seo nasc TLS. Úsáidtear é go ginearálta ar chalafort 465. Má tá "
"fadhbanna agat, féach an socrú sainráite TLS: setting: `EMAIL_USE_TLS`."

msgid ""
"Note that :setting:`EMAIL_USE_TLS`/:setting:`EMAIL_USE_SSL` are mutually "
"exclusive, so only set one of those settings to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil: setting: `EMAIL_USE_TLS`/:SETTING: "
"`EMAIL_USE_SSL` frithpháirteach, mar sin ní shocraigh ach ceann de na "
"socruithe sin go ``True``."

msgid "``EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_SSL_CERTFILE``"

msgid ""
"If :setting:`EMAIL_USE_SSL` or :setting:`EMAIL_USE_TLS` is ``True`` and the "
"secure connection to the SMTP server requires client authentication, use "
"this setting to specify the path to a PEM-formatted certificate chain file, "
"which must be used in conjunction with :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE`` should not be used with a self-signed server "
"certificate or a certificate from a private certificate authority (CA). In "
"such cases, the server's certificate (or the root certificate of the private "
"CA) should be installed into the system's CA bundle. This can be done by "
"following platform-specific instructions for installing a root CA "
"certificate, or by using OpenSSL's ``SSL_CERT_FILE`` or ``SSL_CERT_DIR`` "
"environment variables to specify a custom certificate bundle (if modifying "
"the system bundle is not possible or desired)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more complex scenarios, the "
"SMTP :class:`~django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend` can be subclassed "
"to add root certificates to its ``ssl_context`` "
"using :meth:`python:ssl.SSLContext.load_verify_locations`."
msgstr ""

msgid "``EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_SSL_KEYFILE``"

msgid ""
"If :setting:`EMAIL_USE_SSL` or :setting:`EMAIL_USE_TLS` is ``True``, you can "
"optionally specify the path to a PEM-formatted private key file for client "
"authentication of the SSL connection along "
"with :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that setting :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE` "
"and :setting:`EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE` doesn't result in any certificate checking. "
"They're passed to the underlying SSL connection. Please refer to the "
"documentation of Python's :meth:`python:ssl.SSLContext.wrap_socket` function "
"for details on how the certificate chain file and private key file are "
"handled."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach mbíonn aon seiceáil deimhnithe mar thoradh ar "
"shocting:setting: `EMAIL_SSL_CERTFILE` agus:setting: `EMAIL_SSL_KEYFILE`. "
"Cuirtear iad ar aghaidh chuig an nasc SSL bunúsach. Féach do thoil do "
"dhoiciméadú feidhm Python: Meth: `Python: ssl.sslContext.wrap_socket` le "
"haghaidh sonraí maidir le conas a láimhseálfar an comhad slabhra deimhnithe "
"agus comhad eochair phríobháideach."

msgid "``EMAIL_TIMEOUT``"
msgstr "``RÍOMHPHOST_TIMEOUT``"

msgid ""
"Specifies a timeout in seconds for blocking operations like the connection "
"attempt."
msgstr ""
"Sonraíonn sé ama i soicindí chun oibríochtaí a bhlocáil cosúil leis an "
"iarracht nasc."

msgid "``FILE_UPLOAD_HANDLERS``"
msgstr "``LÁIMHSEÁLAITHE COMHAI_UASLÓDÁLAÍ``"

msgid ""
"A list of handlers to use for uploading. Changing this setting allows "
"complete customization -- even replacement -- of Django's upload process."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de láimhseálaithe le húsáid le haghaidh uaslódála. Ligeann an socrú "
"seo a athrú saincheaptha iomlán - fiú athsholáthar - próiseas uaslódála "
"Django."

msgid "See :doc:`/topics/files` for details."
msgstr "Féach: doc: `/topics/files` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE``"
msgstr "``FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MÉIDE_CUIMHNEACH``"

msgid ""
"The maximum size (in bytes) that an upload will be before it gets streamed "
"to the file system. See :doc:`/topics/files` for details."
msgstr ""
"An méid uasta (i mbeátaí) a bheidh uaslódáil sula ndéantar é a shruthú chuig "
"an gcóras comhaid. Féach: doc: `/topics/files` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "See also :setting:`DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`."

msgid "``FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS``"
msgstr "``CEADÚNA_STIÚRTHÓIREACH_UASLÓDÁIL_COMHAD ``"

msgid ""
"The numeric mode to apply to directories created in the process of uploading "
"files."
msgstr ""
"An modh uimhriúil le cur i bhfeidhm ar eolairí a cruthaíodh sa phróiseas "
"comhaid a uaslódáil."

msgid ""
"This setting also determines the default permissions for collected static "
"directories when using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command. "
"See :djadmin:`collectstatic` for details on overriding it."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann an socrú seo na ceadanna réamhshocraithe d'eolairí statacha "
"bailithe agus an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` á n-úsáid "
"agat. Féach: Djadmin: `collectstatic` le haghaidh sonraí maidir leis a shárú."

msgid ""
"This value mirrors the functionality and caveats of "
"the :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` setting."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn an luach seo feidhmiúlacht agus rabhadh an shocraithe:setting: "
"`FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS`."

msgid "``FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS``"
msgstr "``CEADÚNA_UASLÓDÁIL_FILE``"

msgid "Default: ``0o644``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``0o644``"

msgid ""
"The numeric mode (i.e. ``0o644``) to set newly uploaded files to. For more "
"information about what these modes mean, see the documentation "
"for :func:`os.chmod`."
msgstr ""
"An modh uimhriúil (ie ``0o644``) chun comhaid nua-uaslódáilte a shocrú "
"chuige. Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise faoin méid a chiallaíonn na modhanna "
"seo, féach an doiciméadú le haghaidh: func: `os.chmod`."

msgid ""
"If ``None``, you'll get operating-system dependent behavior. On most "
"platforms, temporary files will have a mode of ``0o600``, and files saved "
"from memory will be saved using the system's standard umask."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``Níl ``, gheobhaidh tú iompar spleách ar an gcóras oibriúcháin. Ar "
"fhormhór na n-ardán, beidh modh `0o600` ag comhaid shealadacha, agus "
"sábhálfar comhaid a shábháiltear ó chuimhne ag baint úsáide as umask "
"caighdeánach an chórais."

msgid ""
"For security reasons, these permissions aren't applied to the temporary "
"files that are stored in :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR`."
msgstr ""
"Ar chúiseanna slándála, ní chuirtear na ceadanna seo i bhfeidhm ar na "
"comhaid shealadacha atá stóráilte in:setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR`."

msgid ""
"This setting also determines the default permissions for collected static "
"files when using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command. "
"See :djadmin:`collectstatic` for details on overriding it."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann an socrú seo na ceadanna réamhshocraithe do chomhaid statacha "
"bailithe agus an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` á n-úsáid "
"agat. Féach: Djadmin: `collectstatic` le haghaidh sonraí maidir leis a shárú."

msgid "**Always prefix the mode with** ``0o`` **.**"
msgstr "** Réamhítear an modh i gcónaí le** ``0o' ** . **"

msgid ""
"If you're not familiar with file modes, please note that the ``0o`` prefix "
"is very important: it indicates an octal number, which is the way that modes "
"must be specified. If you try to use ``644``, you'll get totally incorrect "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú eolach ar mhodhanna comhaid, tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil an "
"réimír ``0` an-tábhachtach: léiríonn sé uimhir ochtúil, arb é sin an bealach "
"a chaithfear modhanna a shonrú. Má dhéanann tú iarracht ``644` a úsáid, "
"gheobhaidh tú iompar go hiomlán mícheart."

msgid "``FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR``"
msgstr "``FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR``"

msgid ""
"The directory to store data to (typically files larger "
"than :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`) temporarily while uploading "
"files. If ``None``, Django will use the standard temporary directory for the "
"operating system. For example, this will default to ``/tmp`` on \\*nix-style "
"operating systems."
msgstr ""
"An eolaire chun sonraí a stóráil chuig (de ghnáth comhaid níos mó ná: "
"setting: `FILE_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE`) go sealadach agus comhaid á "
"uaslódáil. Má tá ``None ``, úsáidfidh Django an eolaire sealadach "
"caighdeánach don chóras oibriúcháin. Mar shampla, réamhshocróidh sé seo go "
"``/tmp`` ar chórais oibriúcháin\\ *nix-style."

msgid "``FIRST_DAY_OF_WEEK``"
msgstr "```CHÉAD_LAETH_DEN TSEACHTAINE``"

msgid "Default: ``0`` (Sunday)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``0`` (Dé Domhnaigh)"

msgid ""
"A number representing the first day of the week. This is especially useful "
"when displaying a calendar. This value is only used when not using format "
"internationalization, or when a format cannot be found for the current "
"locale."
msgstr ""
"Uimhir a léiríonn an chéad lá den tseachtain. Tá sé seo úsáideach go "
"háirithe agus féilire á thaispeáint. Ní úsáidtear an luach seo ach nuair "
"nach n-úsáidtear idirnáisiúnú formáid, nó nuair nach féidir formáid a fháil "
"don áitiúil reatha."

msgid ""
"The value must be an integer from 0 to 6, where 0 means Sunday, 1 means "
"Monday and so on."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh an luach a bheith ina shláimhir ó 0 go 6, áit a chiallaíonn 0 Dé "
"Domhnaigh, ciallaíonn 1 Luain agus mar sin de."

msgid "``FIXTURE_DIRS``"
msgstr "``FIXTURE_DIRS``"

msgid ""
"List of directories searched for :ref:`fixture <fixtures-explanation>` "
"files, in addition to the ``fixtures`` directory of each application, in "
"search order."
msgstr ""
"Liosta na n-eolair <fixtures-explanation>í a chuardaíodh ar chomhaid: ref: "
"`fixture `, i dteannta leis an eolaire ``daingneáin ``de gach feidhmchlár, "
"in ord cuardaigh."

msgid ""
"Note that these paths should use Unix-style forward slashes, even on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur chóir go n-úsáidfeadh na cosáin seo slashes ar "
"aghaidh i stíl Unix, fiú ar Windows."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`initial-data-via-fixtures` and :ref:`topics-testing-fixtures`."
msgstr ""
"Féach: tagairt: `topics-tástála-daingneáin tosaitheach` agus:ref: `topics-"
"tástála-daingneáin `."

msgid "``FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME``"
msgstr "```AINM_SCRIPT_FORCE``"

msgid ""
"If not ``None``, this will be used as the value of the ``SCRIPT_NAME`` "
"environment variable in any HTTP request. This setting can be used to "
"override the server-provided value of ``SCRIPT_NAME``, which may be a "
"rewritten version of the preferred value or not supplied at all. It is also "
"used by :func:`django.setup()` to set the URL resolver script prefix outside "
"of the request/response cycle (e.g. in management commands and standalone "
"scripts) to generate correct URLs when ``FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME`` is provided."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ``None ``, úsáidfear é seo mar luach an athróg comhshaoil "
"``SCRIPT_NAME`` in aon iarratas HTTP. Is féidir an socrú seo a úsáid chun an "
"luach “SCRIPT_NAME” a sholáthraíonn an freastalaí a shárú, ar d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith ina leagan athscríofa den luach is fearr nó nach soláthraítear ar "
"chor ar bith. Úsáidtear é freisin ó:func: `django.setup () `chun réimír "
"script réiteach URL a shocrú lasmuigh den timthriall iarrata/freagartha "
"(m.sh. in orduithe bainistíochta agus scripteanna neamhspleácha) chun "
"URLanna cearta a ghiniúint nuair a chuirtear `FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME`` ar fáil."

msgid "``FORM_RENDERER``"
msgstr "``FOIRM_RENDERER``"

msgid "Default: ``'``:class:`django.forms.renderers.DjangoTemplates`\\ ``'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: `````:class: `django.forms.renderers.djangoTemplates`\\ ````"

msgid ""
"The class that renders forms and form widgets. It must implement :ref:`the "
"low-level render API <low-level-widget-render-api>`. Included form renderers "
"are:"
msgstr ""
"An rang a léiríonn foirmeacha agus a fhoirmíonn giuirléidí. <low-level-"
"widget-render-api>Caithfidh sé: ref: `an API rindreála ísealleibhéil `a chur "
"i bhfeidhm. Is iad na láithreoirí foirmeacha san áireamh:"

msgid "``'``:class:`django.forms.renderers.DjangoTemplates`\\ ``'``"
msgstr "``````:class: `Django.Forms.renderers.djangoTemplates`\\ ````"

msgid "``'``:class:`django.forms.renderers.Jinja2`\\ ``'``"
msgstr "``'```:class: `Django.Forms.renderers.jinja2`\\ ````"

msgid "``'``:class:`django.forms.renderers.TemplatesSetting`\\ ``'``"
msgstr "``````:class: `Django.Forms.Renderers.TemplateSetting`\\ `````"

msgid "``FORMS_URLFIELD_ASSUME_HTTPS``"
msgstr "``FOIRMS_URLFIELD_ASSUME_HTTPS``"

msgid ""
"Set this transitional setting to ``True`` to opt into using ``\"https\"`` as "
"the new default value of :attr:`URLField.assume_scheme "
"<django.forms.URLField.assume_scheme>` during the Django 5.x release cycle."
msgstr ""
"<django.forms.URLField.assume_scheme>Socraigh an suíomh idirthréimhseach seo "
"go `True`` chun roghnú ``\"https\"`` a úsáid mar an luach réamhshocraithe "
"nua de:attr: `URLFIELD.ASSUME_SCHEME `le linn timthriall scaoilte Django 5.x."

msgid "``FORMAT_MODULE_PATH``"
msgstr "``MODÚL_BHEALACH_FORMÁID``"

msgid ""
"A full Python path to a Python package that contains custom format "
"definitions for project locales. If not ``None``, Django will check for a "
"``formats.py`` file, under the directory named as the current locale, and "
"will use the formats defined in this file."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán Python chuig pacáiste Python ina bhfuil sainmhínithe formáid "
"saincheaptha le haghaidh áitiúla tionscadail. Mura bhfuil ``None``, "
"seiceálfaidh Django le haghaidh comhad ``formats.py`, faoin eolaire a "
"ainmnítear mar an áitiúil reatha, agus úsáideoidh sé na formáidí atá "
"sainmhínithe sa chomhad seo."

msgid ""
"The name of the directory containing the format definitions is expected to "
"be named using :term:`locale name` notation, for example ``de``, ``pt_BR``, "
"``en_US``, etc."
msgstr ""
"Táthar ag súil go n-ainmníofar ainm an eolaire ina bhfuil na sainmhínithe "
"formáide ag baint úsáid:term: notáil `ainm áitiúil, mar shampla ``de``, "
"`pt_br``, ``en_us``, srl."

msgid ""
"For example, if :setting:`FORMAT_MODULE_PATH` is set to ``mysite.formats``, "
"and current language is ``en`` (English), Django will expect a directory "
"tree like:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá: setting: `FORMAT_MODULE_PATH` socraithe go "
"``mysite.formats``, agus is é `en ``(Béarla) an teanga reatha, beidh Django "
"ag súil le crann eolaire mar:"

msgid "You can also set this setting to a list of Python paths, for example::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an socrú seo a shocrú freisin ar liosta de chosáin Python, "
"mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"When Django searches for a certain format, it will go through all given "
"Python paths until it finds a module that actually defines the given format. "
"This means that formats defined in packages farther up in the list will take "
"precedence over the same formats in packages farther down."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chuardaíonn Django ar fhormáid áirithe, rachaidh sé trí gach cosán "
"Python a thugtar go dtí go bhfaighidh sé modúl a shainmhíníonn an fhormáid a "
"thugtar Ciallaíonn sé seo go mbeidh tosaíocht ag formáidí a shainmhínítear i "
"bpacáistí níos faide ar an liosta thar na formáidí céanna i bpacáistí níos "
"faide síos."

msgid "Available formats are:"
msgstr "Is iad na formáidí atá ar fáil ná:"

msgid ":setting:`DATE_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `DATE_FORMAT`"

msgid ":setting:`DATE_INPUT_FORMATS`"
msgstr ":setting: `DATE_INPUT_FORMATS`"

msgid ":setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`,"
msgstr ":setting: `DATETIME_FORMAT`,"

msgid ":setting:`DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS`"
msgstr ":setting: `DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS`"

msgid ":setting:`DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`"

msgid ":setting:`FIRST_DAY_OF_WEEK`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `FIRST_DAY_OF_WEEK`"

msgid ":setting:`MONTH_DAY_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `MONTH_DAY_FORMAT`"

msgid ":setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `NUMBER_GROUPING`"

msgid ":setting:`SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`"

msgid ":setting:`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`"

msgid ":setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`"
msgstr ":socrú: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`"

msgid ":setting:`TIME_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":socrú: `TIME_FORMAT`"

msgid ":setting:`TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `TIME_INPUT_FORMATS`"

msgid ":setting:`YEAR_MONTH_FORMAT`"
msgstr ":shocrú: `YEAR_MONTH_FORMAT`"

msgid "``IGNORABLE_404_URLS``"
msgstr "``URLACHA NEAMHCHOITIANTA 404_``"

msgid ""
"List of compiled regular expression objects describing URLs that should be "
"ignored when reporting HTTP 404 errors via email (see :doc:`/howto/error-"
"reporting`). Regular expressions are matched against :meth:`request's full "
"paths <django.http.HttpRequest.get_full_path>` (including query string, if "
"any). Use this if your site does not provide a commonly requested file such "
"as ``favicon.ico`` or ``robots.txt``."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na rudaí léirithe rialta tiomsaithe ag cur síos ar URLanna ar "
"chóir neamhaird a dhéanamh agus earráidí HTTP 404 á thuairisciú trí "
"ríomhphost (féach: doc: `/howto/error-reporting`). Déantar nathanna rialta a "
"mheaitseáil in aghaidh: meth: `bealaí iomlána iarrata "
"<django.http.HttpRequest.get_full_path>`(lena n-áirítear sreang ceisteanna, "
"más ann). Úsáid é seo mura soláthraíonn do shuíomh comhad a iarrtar go "
"coitianta mar ``favicon.ico' nó ``robots.txt``."

msgid ""
"This is only used "
"if :class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` is enabled "
"(see :doc:`/topics/http/middleware`)."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáidtear é seo ach má tá: class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware` cumasaithe (féach: "
"doc: `/topics/http/middleware`)."

msgid "``INSTALLED_APPS``"
msgstr "``APPS_SHUITEÁIL``"

msgid ""
"A list of strings designating all applications that are enabled in this "
"Django installation. Each string should be a dotted Python path to:"
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na teaghráin a ainmníonn gach feidhmchlár atá cumasaithe sa "
"suiteáil Django seo. Ba chóir go mbeadh gach sreang ina chonair Python "
"poncaithe chuig:"

msgid "an application configuration class (preferred), or"
msgstr "aicme cumraíochta feidhmchláir (is fearr), nó"

msgid "a package containing an application."
msgstr "pacáiste ina bhfuil iarratas."

msgid ":doc:`Learn more about application configurations </ref/applications>`."
msgstr ""
":doc: `Tuilleadh eolais a fhoghlaim faoi chumraíochtaí feidhmchláir</ref/"
"applications> `."

msgid "Use the application registry for introspection"
msgstr "Úsáid clárlann an fheidhmchláir le haghaidh ionfhios"

msgid ""
"Your code should never access :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` directly. "
"Use :attr:`django.apps.apps` instead."
msgstr ""
"Níor cheart rochtain a fháil ar do chód riamh: setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` go "
"díreach. Úsáid: attr: `django.apps.apps` ina ionad."

msgid ""
"Application names and labels must be unique "
"in             :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh ainmneacha agus lipéid iarratais a bheith uathúil in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`"

msgid ""
"Application :attr:`names <django.apps.AppConfig.name>` — the dotted Python "
"path to the application package — must be unique. There is no way to include "
"the same application twice, short of duplicating its code under another name."
msgstr ""
"Iarratas: Attr: `ainmneacha <django.apps.AppConfig.name>`- an cosán Python "
"poncanach chuig an bpacáiste iarratais - caithfidh a bheith uathúil. Níl aon "
"bhealach ann an feidhmchlár céanna a áireamh faoi dhó, gan a chód a dhúbailt "
"faoi ainm eile."

msgid ""
"Application :attr:`labels <django.apps.AppConfig.label>` — by default the "
"final part of the name — must be unique too. For example, you can't include "
"both ``django.contrib.auth`` and ``myproject.auth``. However, you can "
"relabel an application with a custom configuration that defines a "
"different :attr:`~django.apps.AppConfig.label`."
msgstr ""
"Iarratas: ATTR: `lipéid <django.apps.AppConfig.label>`- de réir "
"réamhshocraithe caithfidh an chuid deiridh den ainm - a bheith uathúil "
"freisin. Mar shampla, ní féidir leat ``django.contrib.auth`` agus "
"``myproject.auth`` araon a chur san áireamh. Mar sin féin, is féidir leat "
"feidhmchlár a athlipéadú le cumraíocht saincheaptha a shainmhíníonn "
"difríocht: attr: `~django.apps.appconfig.label`."

msgid ""
"These rules apply regardless of whether :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` references "
"application configuration classes or application packages."
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhm ag na rialacha seo beag beann ar: tagraíonn setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS` aicmí cumraíochta feidhmchláir nó pacáistí feidhmchláir."

msgid ""
"When several applications provide different versions of the same resource "
"(template, static file, management command, translation), the application "
"listed first in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` has precedence."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a sholáthraíonn roinnt feidhmchlár leaganacha éagsúla den acmhainn "
"chéanna (teimpléad, comhad statach, ordú bainistíochta, aistriúchán), tá "
"tosaíocht ag an bhfeidhmchlár atá liostaithe ar dtús in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "``INTERNAL_IPS``"
msgstr "``IPS_INMHEÁN``"

msgid "A list of IP addresses, as strings, that:"
msgstr "Liosta de sheoltaí IP, mar teaghráin, go bhfuil:"

msgid ""
"Allow the :func:`~django.template.context_processors.debug` context "
"processor to add some variables to the template context."
msgstr ""
"Lig don phróiseálaí comhthéacs: func: "
"`~django.template.context_processors.debug` roinnt athróg a chur le "
"comhthéacs an teimpléid."

msgid ""
"Can use the :ref:`admindocs bookmarklets <admindocs-bookmarklets>` even if "
"not logged in as a staff user."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an leabharmharcanna:ref: `admindocs bookmarklets <admindocs-"
"bookmarklets>`a úsáid fiú mura bhfuil sé logáilte isteach mar úsáideoir "
"foirne."

msgid ""
"Are marked as \"internal\" (as opposed to \"EXTERNAL\") "
"in :class:`~django.utils.log.AdminEmailHandler` emails."
msgstr ""
"Tá siad marcáilte mar “inmheánach” (seachas “EXTERNAL”) in:class: "
"`~django.utils.log.adminEmailHandler` ríomhphoist."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_CODE``"
msgstr "``CÓD_TEANGA``"

msgid "Default: ``'en-us'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'en-us'``"

msgid ""
"A string representing the language code for this installation. This should "
"be in standard :term:`language ID format <language code>`. For example, U.S. "
"English is ``\"en-us\"``. See also the `list of language identifiers`_ "
"and :doc:`/topics/i18n/index`."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an cód teanga don tsuiteáil seo. <language code>Ba chóir "
"go mbeadh sé seo i gcaighdeán:term: `formáid ID teanga `. Mar shampla, is é "
"Béarla na SA ``\"en-us\"``. Féach freisin an `liosta na n-aitheantóirí "
"teanga`_ agus:doc: `/topics/i18n/index`."

msgid "It serves three purposes:"
msgstr "Freastalaíonn sé trí chuspóir:"

msgid ""
"If the locale middleware isn't in use, it decides which translation is "
"served to all users."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an meán-earraí áitiúla in úsáid, cinneann sé cén t-aistriúchán a "
"sheirbheálfar do gach úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"If the locale middleware is active, it provides a fallback language in case "
"the user's preferred language can't be determined or is not supported by the "
"website. It also provides the fallback translation when a translation for a "
"given literal doesn't exist for the user's preferred language."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an láithreán gréasáin gníomhach, soláthraíonn sé teanga aisghabhála i "
"gcás nach féidir an teanga is fearr leis an úsáideoir a chinneadh nó nach "
"dtacaíonn an suíomh Gréasáin leis. Soláthraíonn sé an t-aistriúchán ar ais "
"freisin nuair nach bhfuil aistriúchán do litriúil ar leith ann don teanga is "
"fearr leis an úsáideoir."

msgid ""
"If localization is explicitly disabled via the :tfilter:`unlocalize` filter "
"or the :ttag:`{% localize off %}<localize>` tag, it provides fallback "
"localization formats which will be applied instead. See :ref:`controlling "
"localization in templates <topic-l10n-templates>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéantar logánú a dhíchumasú go sainráite tríd an scagair:tfilter: "
"`unlocalize` nó an chlibe:ttag: `{% localize off%}<localize>`, soláthraíonn "
"sé formáidí logánaithe fillte a chuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad sin. "
"Féach:ref: `logánú a rialú i dteimpléid <topic-l10n-templates>`le haghaidh "
"sonraí."

msgid "See :ref:`how-django-discovers-language-preference` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `how django-discovers-language-preference` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_AGE``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁIN AOIS ``"

msgid "Default: ``None`` (expires at browser close)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``None`` (in éag nuair a dhún an bhrabhsálaí)"

msgid "The age of the language cookie, in seconds."
msgstr "Aois na fianán teanga, i soicindí."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_DOMAIN``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁINE_FEARAIN``"

msgid ""
"The domain to use for the language cookie. Set this to a string such as "
"``\"example.com\"`` for cross-domain cookies, or use ``None`` for a standard "
"domain cookie."
msgstr ""
"An fearann le húsáid don fhianán teanga. Socraigh é seo go sreang mar "
"``\"example.com\"`` le haghaidh fianáin tras-fearainn, nó bain úsáid as "
"``None ``le haghaidh fianán fearainn caighdeánach."

msgid ""
"Be cautious when updating this setting on a production site. If you update "
"this setting to enable cross-domain cookies on a site that previously used "
"standard domain cookies, existing user cookies that have the old domain will "
"not be updated. This will result in site users being unable to switch the "
"language as long as these cookies persist. The only safe and reliable option "
"to perform the switch is to change the language cookie name permanently (via "
"the :setting:`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_NAME` setting) and to add a middleware that "
"copies the value from the old cookie to a new one and then deletes the old "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach agus an suíomh seo á nuashonrú agat ar shuíomh táirgeachta. Má "
"nuashonraíonn tú an socrú seo chun fianáin tras-fhearann a chumasú ar "
"shuíomh a d'úsáid fianáin fearainn caighdeánacha roimhe seo, ní nuashonrófar "
"fianáin úsáideora atá ann cheana a bhfuil an sean-fearainn Mar thoradh air "
"seo ní bheidh úsáideoirí an láithreáin in ann an teanga a athrú chomh fada "
"agus a leanfaidh na fianáin seo. Is é an t-aon rogha sábháilte agus iontaofa "
"chun an lasc a dhéanamh ná ainm na fianán teanga a athrú go buan (tríd an "
"socrú: `LANGUAGE_COOKIE_NAME`) agus meán-earraí a chur leis a chóipeálann an "
"luach ón sean-fhianán go ceann nua agus ansin scriosann sé an seancheann."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_HTTPONLY``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁIN_HTTPONLY``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use ``HttpOnly`` flag on the language cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, client-side JavaScript will not be able to access the language "
"cookie."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu an bhratach `HttpOnly`` a úsáid ar an bhfianán teanga. Má tá sé seo "
"socraithe ar ``True``, ní bheidh JavaScript taobh an chliaint in ann "
"rochtain a fháil ar an bhfianán teanga."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_NAME``"
msgstr "``AINM_FIANÁIN TEANGA``"

msgid "Default: ``'django_language'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'django_langue'``"

msgid ""
"The name of the cookie to use for the language cookie. This can be whatever "
"you want (as long as it's different from the other cookie names in your "
"application). See :doc:`/topics/i18n/index`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm na fianán atá le húsáid don fhianán teanga. Is féidir leis seo a bheith "
"cibé rud is mian leat (fad is atá sé difriúil ó na hainmneacha fianán eile i "
"d'iarratas). Féach: doc: `/topics/i18n/index`."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_PATH``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁIN BHEALAIGH``"

msgid ""
"The path set on the language cookie. This should either match the URL path "
"of your Django installation or be a parent of that path."
msgstr ""
"An cosán atá leagtha síos ar an bhfianán teanga. Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo "
"comhoiriúnach le cosán URL do shuiteála Django nó a bheith ina thuismitheoir "
"ar an gcosán sin."

msgid ""
"This is useful if you have multiple Django instances running under the same "
"hostname. They can use different cookie paths and each instance will only "
"see its own language cookie."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach má tá cásanna iolracha Django agat ag rith faoin ainm "
"óstach céanna. Is féidir leo cosáin éagsúla fianán a úsáid agus ní fheicfidh "
"gach cás ach a fianán teanga féin."

msgid ""
"Be cautious when updating this setting on a production site. If you update "
"this setting to use a deeper path than it previously used, existing user "
"cookies that have the old path will not be updated. This will result in site "
"users being unable to switch the language as long as these cookies persist. "
"The only safe and reliable option to perform the switch is to change the "
"language cookie name permanently (via the :setting:`LANGUAGE_COOKIE_NAME` "
"setting), and to add a middleware that copies the value from the old cookie "
"to a new one and then deletes the one."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach agus an suíomh seo á nuashonrú agat ar shuíomh táirgeachta. Má "
"nuashonraíonn tú an socrú seo chun cosán níos doimhne a úsáid ná mar a "
"úsáideadh sé roimhe seo, ní nuashonrófar fianáin úsáideora atá ann cheana a "
"bhfuil an sean-chosán Mar thoradh air seo ní bheidh úsáideoirí an láithreáin "
"in ann an teanga a athrú chomh fada agus a leanann na fianáin seo. Is é an t-"
"aon rogha sábháilte agus iontaofa chun an lasc a dhéanamh ná ainm na fianán "
"teanga a athrú go buan (tríd an socrú: `LANGUAGE_COOKIE_NAME`), agus meán-"
"earraí a chur leis a chóipeálann an luach ón sean-fhianán go ceann nua agus "
"ansin scriosann sé an ceann."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_SAMESITE``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁN_COMHCHOSAITHE``"

msgid ""
"The value of the `SameSite`_ flag on the language cookie. This flag prevents "
"the cookie from being sent in cross-site requests."
msgstr ""
"Luach an bhratach `SameSite`_ ar an bhfianán teanga. Cuireann an bratach seo "
"cosc ar an bhfianán a sheoladh in iarratais tras-láithreáin."

msgid "``LANGUAGE_COOKIE_SECURE``"
msgstr "``TEANGA_FIANÁINE_SLÁNDÁLA``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use a secure cookie for the language cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, the cookie will be marked as \"secure\", which means browsers may "
"ensure that the cookie is only sent under an HTTPS connection."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu fianán slán a úsáid don fhianán teanga. Má tá sé seo socraithe ar "
"``True``, marcálfar an fianán mar “slán”, rud a chiallaíonn go bhféadfaidh "
"brabhsálaithe a chinntiú nach seoltar an fianán ach faoi nasc HTTPS."

msgid "``LANGUAGES``"
msgstr "``TEANGACHA ``"

msgid ""
"Default: A list of all available languages. This list is continually growing "
"and including a copy here would inevitably become rapidly out of date. You "
"can see the current list of translated languages by looking "
"in :source:`django/conf/global_settings.py`."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: Liosta de na teangacha go léir atá ar fáil. Tá an liosta "
"seo ag fás i gcónaí agus is cinnte go mbeadh cóip a áireamh anseo as dáta go "
"tapa. Is féidir leat an liosta reatha de na dteangacha aistrithe a fheiceáil "
"trí:source: `django/conf/global_settings.py`."

msgid ""
"The list is a list of 2-tuples in the format (:term:`language code<language "
"code>`, ``language name``) -- for example, ``('ja', 'Japanese')``. This "
"specifies which languages are available for language selection. See :doc:`/"
"topics/i18n/index`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an liosta de dhá thuples san fhormáid (:term: `cód teanga <language "
"code>`, ``ainm teanga ``) -- mar shampla,`` ('ja', 'Seapáinis') ``. "
"Sonraíonn sé seo cé na teangacha atá ar fáil le haghaidh roghnú teanga. "
"Féach: doc: `/topics/i18n/index`."

msgid ""
"Generally, the default value should suffice. Only set this setting if you "
"want to restrict language selection to a subset of the Django-provided "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, ba chóir go leor an luach réamhshocraithe. Socraigh an socrú "
"seo ach más mian leat roghnú teanga a theorannú go fo-thacar de na teangacha "
"a sholáthraítear Django."

msgid ""
"If you define a custom :setting:`LANGUAGES` setting, you can mark the "
"language names as translation strings using "
"the :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy` function."
msgstr ""
"Má shainmhíníonn tú socrú saincheap:setting: `LANGUAGES`, is féidir leat na "
"hainmneacha teanga a mharcáil mar teaghráin aistriúcháin ag baint úsáide as "
"an bhfeidhm:func: `~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy`."

msgid "Here's a sample settings file::"
msgstr "Seo comhad socruithe samplach::"

msgid "``LANGUAGES_BIDI``"
msgstr "``TEANGACH_BIDI``"

msgid ""
"Default: A list of all language codes that are written right-to-left. You "
"can see the current list of these languages by looking in :source:`django/"
"conf/global_settings.py`."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: Liosta de na cóid teanga go léir atá scríofa ar dheis go "
"clé. Is féidir leat an liosta reatha de na teangacha seo a fheiceáil "
"trí:source: `django/conf/global_settings.py`."

msgid ""
"The list contains :term:`language codes<language code>` for languages that "
"are written right-to-left."
msgstr ""
"Tá an liosta: téarma: `cóid teanga <language code>`do theangacha atá scríofa "
"ar dheis go clé."

msgid ""
"Generally, the default value should suffice. Only set this setting if you "
"want to restrict language selection to a subset of the Django-provided "
"languages. If you define a custom :setting:`LANGUAGES` setting, the list of "
"bidirectional languages may contain language codes which are not enabled on "
"a given site."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, ba chóir go leor an luach réamhshocraithe. Socraigh an socrú "
"seo ach más mian leat roghnú teanga a theorannú go fo-thacar de na teangacha "
"a sholáthraítear Django. Má shainmhíníonn tú socrú saincheap:setting: "
"`LANGUAGES`, d'fhéadfadh go mbeadh cóid teanga nach bhfuil cumasaithe ar "
"shuíomh ar leith i liosta na dteangacha déthreoracha."

msgid "``LOCALE_PATHS``"
msgstr "``COSÁIN ÁITIÚLA ``"

msgid ""
"A list of directories where Django looks for translation files. "
"See :ref:`how-django-discovers-translations`."
msgstr ""
"Liosta d'eolairí ina bhfuil Django ag lorg comhaid aistriúcháin. Féach:ref: "
"`cona-django-aimsitheach-aistriúcháin`."

msgid ""
"Django will look within each of these paths for the ``<locale_code>/"
"LC_MESSAGES`` directories containing the actual translation files."
msgstr ""
"Breathnóidh Django laistigh de gach ceann de na cosáin seo do na heolairí "
"``<locale_code>/LC_MESSAGES`` ina bhfuil na comhaid aistriúcháin iarbhír."

msgid "``LOGGING``"
msgstr "``LOGÁIL ISTEACH ``"

msgid "Default: A logging configuration dictionary."
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: Foclóir cumraíochta logála."

msgid ""
"A data structure containing configuration information. When not-empty, the "
"contents of this data structure will be passed as the argument to the "
"configuration method described in :setting:`LOGGING_CONFIG`."
msgstr ""
"Struchtúr sonraí ina bhfuil faisnéis chumraíochta. Nuair nach bhfuil sé "
"folamh, cuirfear ábhar an struchtúir sonraí seo ar aghaidh mar argóint chuig "
"an modh cumraíochta a thuairiscítear in:setting: `LOGGING_CONFIG`."

msgid ""
"Among other things, the default logging configuration passes HTTP 500 server "
"errors to an email log handler when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``. See "
"also :ref:`configuring-logging`."
msgstr ""
"I measc rudaí eile, cuireann an chumraíocht logála réamhshocraithe earráidí "
"freastalaí HTTP 500 chuig láimhseálaí logála ríomhphoist nuai:socrú: “DEBUG” "
"ná `False``. Féach freis:ref: `configuring-loging`."

msgid ""
"You can see the default logging configuration by looking in :source:`django/"
"utils/log.py`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an chumraíocht logála réamhshocraithe a fheiceáil trí "
"fhéachaint isteach: source: `django/utils/log.py`."

msgid "``LOGGING_CONFIG``"
msgstr "``LOGING_CONFIG``"

msgid "Default: ``'logging.config.dictConfig'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'Loging.config.dictConfig'``"

msgid ""
"A path to a callable that will be used to configure logging in the Django "
"project. Points at an instance of Python's :ref:`dictConfig <logging-config-"
"dictschema>` configuration method by default."
msgstr ""
"Conair chuig glaoch a úsáidfear chun logáil isteach i dtionscadal Django a "
"chumrú. <logging-config-dictschema>Pointí ag cás de Python's:ref: modh "
"cumraíochta `DictConfig` de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"If you set :setting:`LOGGING_CONFIG` to ``None``, the logging configuration "
"process will be skipped."
msgstr ""
"Má shocraíonn tú: socrú: `LOGGING_CONFIG` go ``None``, scipeánfar an "
"próiseas cumraíochta logála."

msgid "``MANAGERS``"
msgstr "``BAINISTEOIRÍ ``"

msgid ""
"A list in the same format as :setting:`ADMINS` that specifies who should get "
"broken link notifications "
"when :class:`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkEmailsMiddleware` is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""
"Liosta san fhormáid chéanna amha:setting: `ADMINS` a shonraíonn cé ar chóir "
"fógraí nasc briste a fháil nuai:class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.BrokenLinkemailsMiddleware` cumasaithe."

msgid "``MEDIA_ROOT``"
msgstr "``MEDIA_FRÉAMH``"

msgid ""
"Absolute filesystem path to the directory that will hold :doc:`user-uploaded "
"files </topics/files>`."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán córas comhaid chuig an eolaire a bheidh ina choimeád:doc: "
"`comhaid uaslódáilte úsáideora `. </topics/files>"

msgid "Example: ``\"/var/www/example.com/media/\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” /var/www/example.com/media/\"``"

msgid "See also :setting:`MEDIA_URL`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `MEDIA_URL`."

msgid ""
":setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` and :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` must have different values. "
"Before :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` was introduced, it was common to rely or "
"fallback on :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` to also serve static files; however, since "
"this can have serious security implications, there is a validation check to "
"prevent it."
msgstr ""
":setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` agus:setting: `STATIC_ROOT` caithfidh luachanna "
"difriúla a bheith aige. Roimhe sul:SETTING: `STATIC_ROOT` tugtha isteach, "
"bhí sé coitianta brath nó titim siar ar:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT` chun comhaid "
"statacha a sheirbheáil freisin; áfach, ós rud é go bhféadfadh impleachtaí "
"slándála tromchúiseacha a bheith aige seo, tá seiceáil bailíochtaithe ann "
"chun é a chosc."

msgid "``MEDIA_URL``"
msgstr "``MEDIA_URL ``"

msgid ""
"URL that handles the media served from :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`, used "
"for :doc:`managing stored files </topics/files>`. It must end in a slash if "
"set to a non-empty value. You will need to :ref:`configure these files to be "
"served <serving-uploaded-files-in-development>` in both development and "
"production environments."
msgstr ""
"URL a láimhseálann na meáin a sheirbheáiltear ó:setting: `MEDIA_ROOT`, a "
"úsáidtear le haghaidh: doc: `comhaid stóráilte </topics/files> a bhainistiú. "
"Caithfidh sé deireadh a chur le slasc má tá sé socraithe ar luach neamh-"
"folamh. Beidh ort: ref: `na comhaid seo a chumrú le seirbheáil <serving-"
"uploaded-files-in-development>`i dtimpeallachtaí forbartha agus táirgeachta "
"araon."

msgid ""
"If you want to use ``{{ MEDIA_URL }}`` in your templates, add "
"``'django.template.context_processors.media'`` in the "
"``'context_processors'`` option of :setting:`TEMPLATES`."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat ``{{MEDIA_URL}}`` a úsáid i do theimpléid, cuir "
"```django.template.context_processors.media'` sa rogha "
"```context_processors'` de:setting: `TEMPLATES`."

msgid "Example: ``\"https://media.example.com/\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” https://media.example.com/ “``"

msgid ""
"There are security risks if you are accepting uploaded content from "
"untrusted users! See the security guide's topic on :ref:`user-uploaded-"
"content-security` for mitigation details."
msgstr ""
"Tá rioscaí slándála ann má tá tú ag glacadh le hábhar uaslódáilte ó "
"úsáideoirí neam Féach ábhar an treoir slándála ar:ref: `user-uploaded-"
"content-security` le haghaidh sonraí maolaithe."

msgid ""
":setting:`MEDIA_URL` and :setting:`STATIC_URL` must have different values. "
"See :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` for more details."
msgstr ""
":setting: Caithfidh luachanna difriúla a bheith ag `MEDIA_URL` agus:setting: "
"`STATIC_URL`. Féach: Socrú: `MEDIA_ROOT` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`MEDIA_URL` is a relative path, then it will be prefixed by the "
"server-provided value of ``SCRIPT_NAME`` (or ``/`` if not set). This makes "
"it easier to serve a Django application in a subpath without adding an extra "
"configuration to the settings."
msgstr ""
"Más: Socrú: Is cosán coibhneasta é `MEDIA_URL`, ansin déanfar é a "
"réamhshocrú ag an luach ``SCRIPT_NAME`` a sholáthraíonn an freastalaí (nó ``/"
"`` mura bhfuil sé socraithe). Fágann sé seo go bhfuil sé níos éasca "
"feidhmchlár Django a sheirbheáil i bhfochonair gan cumraíocht bhreise a chur "
"leis na socruithe."

msgid "``MIDDLEWARE``"
msgstr "``MEÁN-EARRAÍ ``"

msgid "A list of middleware to use. See :doc:`/topics/http/middleware`."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de mheán-earraí le húsáid. Féach: doc: `/topics/http/middleware `."

msgid "``MIGRATION_MODULES``"
msgstr "``MODÚL_IMIRCE``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary specifying the package where migration modules can be found on "
"a per-app basis. The default value of this setting is an empty dictionary, "
"but the default package name for migration modules is ``migrations``."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir a shonraíonn an pacáiste inar féidir modúil imirce a fháil ar bhonn "
"in aghaidh an aip. Is foclóir folamh é luach réamhshocraithe an socrú seo, "
"ach is é “imirceacháin” ainm an phacáiste réamhshocraithe do mhodúil imirce."

msgid ""
"In this case, migrations pertaining to the ``blog`` app will be contained in "
"the ``blog.db_migrations`` package."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, beidh imirce a bhaineann leis an aip ``blog`` sa phacáiste "
"``blog.db_migrations``."

msgid ""
"If you provide the ``app_label`` argument, :djadmin:`makemigrations` will "
"automatically create the package if it doesn't already exist."
msgstr ""
"Má sholáthraíonn tú an argóint ``app_label``, cruthóidh: djadmin: "
"`makemigrations` an pacáiste go huathoibríoch mura bhfuil sé ann cheana féin."

msgid ""
"When you supply ``None`` as a value for an app, Django will consider the app "
"as an app without migrations regardless of an existing ``migrations`` "
"submodule. This can be used, for example, in a test settings file to skip "
"migrations while testing (tables will still be created for the apps' "
"models). To disable migrations for all apps during tests, you can set "
"the :setting:`MIGRATE <TEST_MIGRATE>` to ``False`` instead. If "
"``MIGRATION_MODULES`` is used in your general project settings, remember to "
"use the :option:`migrate --run-syncdb` option if you want to create tables "
"for the app."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a sholáthraíonn tú ``None`` mar luach d'aip, measfaidh Django an aip "
"mar aip gan imirce beag beann ar fho-mhodúl ``imirce`` atá ann cheana. Is "
"féidir é seo a úsáid, mar shampla, i gcomhad socruithe tástála chun imirce a "
"scipeáil agus tú ag tástáil (cruthófar táblaí fós do mhúnlaí na n-aipeanna). "
"Chun imirce do gach aip a dhíchumasú le linn tástálacha, is féidir leat an: "
"socrú: `MIGRATE `go `False`<TEST_MIGRATE>` ina ionad. Má úsáidtear "
"``MIGRATION_MODULES`` i do shocruithe ginearálta tionscadail, cuimhnigh an "
"roghna:option: `migration --run-syncdb` a úsáid más mian leat táblaí a "
"chruthú don aip."

msgid "``MONTH_DAY_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_LAETH_MHÍ``"

msgid "Default: ``'F j'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'F j'``"

msgid ""
"The default formatting to use for date fields on Django admin change-list "
"pages -- and, possibly, by other parts of the system -- in cases when only "
"the month and day are displayed."
msgstr ""
"An formáidiú réamhshocraithe le húsáid le haghaidh réimsí dáta ar "
"leathanaigh liosta athraithe riaracháin Django - agus, b'fhéidir, ag codanna "
"eile den chóras - i gcásanna nach dtaispeántar ach an mhí agus an lá."

msgid ""
"For example, when a Django admin change-list page is being filtered by a "
"date drilldown, the header for a given day displays the day and month. "
"Different locales have different formats. For example, U.S. English would "
"say \"January 1,\" whereas Spanish might say \"1 Enero.\""
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, nuair a bhíonn leathanach liosta athraithe riaracháin Django á "
"scagadh ag druileáil dáta, taispeánann an ceannteideal do lá ar leith an lá "
"agus an mhí. Tá formáidí éagsúla ag áitiúla éagsúla. Mar shampla, déarfadh "
"Béarla na SA “1 Eanáir,” ach d'fhéadfadh an Spáinnis a rá “1 Enero.”"

msgid ""
"Note that the corresponding locale-dictated format has higher precedence and "
"will be applied instead."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an bhformáid "
"chomhfhreagrach áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad."

msgid ""
"See :tfilter:`allowed date format strings <date>`. See "
"also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT`, :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting:`TIME_FORMAT` "
"and :setting:`YEAR_MONTH_FORMAT`."
msgstr ""
"<date>Féach: TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `. Féach "
"freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT`, :setting: `DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting: "
"`TIME_FORMAT` agus:setting: `YEAR_MONTH_FORMAT`."

msgid "``NUMBER_GROUPING``"
msgstr "``UIMHREACH_GHRÚPÁIL ``"

msgid "Number of digits grouped together on the integer part of a number."
msgstr ""
"Líon na ndigití atá grúpáilte le chéile ar an gcuid sláireach d'uimhir."

msgid ""
"Common use is to display a thousand separator. If this setting is ``0``, "
"then no grouping will be applied to the number. If this setting is greater "
"than ``0``, then :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` will be used as the separator "
"between those groups."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid choitianta ná míle deighilteoir a thaispeáint. Más é an socrú seo "
"``0``, ansin ní chuirfear aon ghrúpáil i bhfeidhm ar an uimhir. Má tá an "
"socrú seo níos mó ná `0``, ansin úsáidfear: setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"mar an deighilteoir idir na grúpaí sin."

msgid ""
"Some locales use non-uniform digit grouping, e.g. ``10,00,00,000`` in "
"``en_IN``. For this case, you can provide a sequence with the number of "
"digit group sizes to be applied. The first number defines the size of the "
"group preceding the decimal delimiter, and each number that follows defines "
"the size of preceding groups. If the sequence is terminated with ``-1``, no "
"further grouping is performed. If the sequence terminates with a ``0``, the "
"last group size is used for the remainder of the number."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann roinnt áiteanna grúpáil dhigit neamh-aonfhoirmeach, m.sh. "
"``10,00,00,000`` i `En_in``. Maidir leis an gcás seo, is féidir leat "
"seicheamh a sholáthar le líon na méideanna grúpa dhigit atá le cur i "
"bhfeidhm. Sainmhíníonn an chéad uimhir méid an ghrúpa roimh an teorannach "
"deachúil, agus sainmhíníonn gach uimhir a leanann méid na ngrúpaí roimhe "
"seo. Má chuirtear deireadh leis an seicheamh le ``-1``, ní dhéantar aon "
"ghrúpáil bhreise. Má chríochnaíonn an seicheamh le ``0``, úsáidtear méid an "
"ghrúpa deireanach don chuid eile den uimhir."

msgid "Example tuple for ``en_IN``::"
msgstr "Sampla tuple le haghaidh ``en_in``:"

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`, :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"and :setting:`USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`, :setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` "
"agus:setting: `USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."

msgid "``PREPEND_WWW``"
msgstr "``PREPEND_WWW``"

msgid ""
"Whether to prepend the \"www.\" subdomain to URLs that don't have it. This "
"is only used if :class:`~django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware` is "
"installed (see :doc:`/topics/http/middleware`). See "
"also :setting:`APPEND_SLASH`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé an ndéanfar an fo-fhearann “www.” a phleanáil chuig URLanna nach bhfuil "
"sé acu. Ní úsáidtear é seo ach má tá: class: "
"`~django.middleware.common.commonMiddleware` suiteáilte (féach: doc: `/"
"topics/http/middleware`). Féach freis:socrú: `APPEND_SLASH`."

msgid "``ROOT_URLCONF``"
msgstr "``ROOT_URLCONF``"

msgid ""
"A string representing the full Python import path to your root URLconf, for "
"example ``\"mydjangoapps.urls\"``. Can be overridden on a per-request basis "
"by setting the attribute ``urlconf`` on the incoming ``HttpRequest`` object. "
"See :ref:`how-django-processes-a-request` for details."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an cosán iomlán allmhairithe Python chuig do URLConf "
"fréimhe, mar shampla ``\"mydjangoapps.urls\"`. Is féidir é a shárú ar bhonn "
"in aghaidh iarratais tríd an tréith ``urlconf`` a shocrú ar an réad "
"``HttpRequest`` atá ag teacht isteach. Féach: ref: `how django-processes-a-"
"request` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``SECRET_KEY``"
msgstr "``EOCHAIR_RÚNA``"

msgid ""
"A secret key for a particular Django installation. This is used to "
"provide :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/signing>`, and should be set to "
"a unique, unpredictable value."
msgstr ""
"Eochair rúnda do shuiteáil Django áirithe. Úsáidtear é seo chun: doc: `síniú "
"cripteagrafach' a sholáthar, agus ba chóir é a shocrú go luach u</topics/"
"signing> athúil, nach féidir a thuar."

msgid ""
":djadmin:`django-admin startproject <startproject>` automatically adds a "
"randomly-generated ``SECRET_KEY`` to each new project."
msgstr ""
":djadmin: Cuireann `django-admin startproject ```SECRET_KEY`<startproject>` "
"a ghintear go randamach go huathoibríoch le gach tionscadal nua."

msgid ""
"Uses of the key shouldn't assume that it's text or bytes. Every use should "
"go through :func:`~django.utils.encoding.force_str` "
"or :func:`~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` to convert it to the desired "
"type."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir go nglacfadh úsáidí an eochair leis gur téacs nó beáit é. Ba "
"chóir go mbeadh gach úsáid trí:func: `~django.utils.encoding.force_str` nó: "
"func: `~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` chun é a thiontú go dtí an cineál "
"atá ag teastáil."

msgid "Django will refuse to start if :setting:`SECRET_KEY` is not set."
msgstr "Diúltóidh Django tosú mura bhfuil: setting: `SECRET_KEY` socraithe."

msgid "**Keep this value secret.**"
msgstr "** Coinnigh an luach seo faoi rún. **"

msgid ""
"Running Django with a known :setting:`SECRET_KEY` defeats many of Django's "
"security protections, and can lead to privilege escalation and remote code "
"execution vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Scaoileann Django ag rith le: socrú: `SECRET_KEY` go leor de chosaintí "
"slándála Django, agus d'fhéadfadh méadú pribhléid agus leochaileachtaí "
"forghníomhú iargúlta cód a bheith mar thoradh air."

msgid "The secret key is used for:"
msgstr "Úsáidtear an eochair rúnda le haghaidh:"

msgid ""
"All :doc:`sessions </topics/http/sessions>` if you are using any other "
"session backend than ``django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache``, or are "
"using the "
"default :meth:`~django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser.get_session_auth_hash()`."
msgstr ""
"All:doc: `sessions` má tá aon chúltaca seisiúin eile á úsáid agat seachas "
"``django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache`` </topics/http/sessions>, nó má tá "
"tú ag úsáid an réamhshocraithe:meth: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.models.abstractbaseUser.get_session_auth_hash () `."

msgid ""
"All :doc:`messages </ref/contrib/messages>` if you are "
"using :class:`~django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.CookieStorage` "
"or :class:`~django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.FallbackStorage`."
msgstr ""
"Gach: Doc: `teachtaireachtaí `má tá tú ag baint úsáide:class: "
"`~django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.cookieStorage` nó</ref/contrib/"
"messages> :class: "
"`~django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.fallbackStorage`."

msgid "All :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.PasswordResetView` tokens."
msgstr ""
"Gach: Class: comharthaí `~django.contrib.auth.views.passwordResetView`."

msgid ""
"Any usage of :doc:`cryptographic signing </topics/signing>`, unless a "
"different key is provided."
msgstr ""
"Aon úsáid ar:doc: `síniú cripteagrafach', mura gcuirtear eochair dhifriúil "
"ar fáil. </topics/signing>"

msgid ""
"When a secret key is no longer set as :setting:`SECRET_KEY` or contained "
"within :setting:`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` all of the above will be invalidated. "
"When rotating your secret key, you should move the old key "
"to :setting:`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` temporarily. Secret keys are not used for "
"passwords of users and key rotation will not affect them."
msgstr ""
"Nuair nach bhfuil eochair rúnda socraithe a thuilleadh mar: setting: "
"`SECRET_KEY` nó atá ann laistigh de: setting: `SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` beidh "
"gach ceann de na rudaí thuas neamhbhailí. Agus do eochair rúnda á rothlú "
"agat, ba chóir duit an sean-eochair a bhogadh chuig: setting: "
"`SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS` go sealadach. Ní úsáidtear eochracha rúnda le "
"haghaidh pasfhocail úsáideoirí agus ní bheidh tionchar ag rothlú eochair "
"orthu."

msgid ""
"The default :file:`settings.py` file created by :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>` creates a unique ``SECRET_KEY`` for convenience."
msgstr ""
"<startproject>Cruthaíonn an comhad réamhshocraithe:file: `settings.py` a "
"chruthaí:djadmin: `django-admin startproject `uathúil ``SECRET_KEY`` le "
"haghaidh áisiúlachta."

msgid "``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS``"
msgstr "``EOCHAIR_FALLBACKS``"

msgid "Default: ``[]``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``[]``"

msgid ""
"A list of fallback secret keys for a particular Django installation. These "
"are used to allow rotation of the ``SECRET_KEY``."
msgstr ""
"Liosta d'eochracha rúnda tagtha le haghaidh suiteáil Django áirithe. "
"Úsáidtear iad seo chun rothlú an ``SECRET_KEY`` a cheadú."

msgid ""
"In order to rotate your secret keys, set a new ``SECRET_KEY`` and move the "
"previous value to the beginning of ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS``. Then remove the "
"old values from the end of the ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` when you are ready "
"to expire the sessions, password reset tokens, and so on, that make use of "
"them."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn d'eochracha rúnda a rothlú, socraigh ``SECRET_KEY`` nua agus bog an "
"luach roimhe seo go dtí tús ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS``. Ansin bain na "
"seanluachanna ó dheireadh an ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` nuair a bheidh tú "
"réidh chun na seisiúin, na comharthaí athshocraithe pasfhocal, agus mar sin "
"de, a úsáideann iad a chur in éag."

msgid ""
"Signing operations are computationally expensive. Having multiple old key "
"values in ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` adds additional overhead to all checks "
"that don't match an earlier key."
msgstr ""
"Tá oibríochtaí sínithe costasach go ríomhaireachta. Cuireann sean-"
"eochrluachanna iolracha agat i ``SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS`` lasbhreas breise le "
"gach seiceáil nach n-oireann le heochair níos luaithe."

msgid ""
"As such, fallback values should be removed after an appropriate period, "
"allowing for key rotation."
msgstr ""
"Dá bhrí sin, ba cheart luachanna titim a bhaint tar éis tréimhse chuí, rud a "
"cheadaíonn rothlú eochair."

msgid ""
"Uses of the secret key values shouldn't assume that they are text or bytes. "
"Every use should go through :func:`~django.utils.encoding.force_str` "
"or :func:`~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` to convert it to the desired "
"type."
msgstr ""
"Níor chóir go nglacfadh úsáidí na príomhluachanna rúnda leis gur téacs nó "
"béite iad. Ba chóir go mbeadh gach úsáid trí:func: "
"`~django.utils.encoding.force_str` nó: func: "
"`~django.utils.encoding.force_bytes` chun é a thiontú go dtí an cineál atá "
"ag teastáil."

msgid "``SECURE_CONTENT_TYPE_NOSNIFF``"
msgstr "``CINEÁL_ÁBHAR SLÁNDÁILTE_NOSNIFF``"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` "
"sets the :ref:`x-content-type-options` header on all responses that do not "
"already have it."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, socraíonn an:class: `~django.middleware.securityMiddleware` "
"ceannteideal: :ref: `x-content-type-options` ar gach freagra nach bhfuil sé "
"ann cheana féin."

msgid "``SECURE_CROSS_ORIGIN_OPENER_POLICY``"
msgstr "``BEARTAS OSCAILTEOIREACH_THRAS_BUNAIDH SLÁNDÁILTE ``"

msgid "Default: ``'same-origin'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: `````bhunús céann'`"

msgid ""
"Unless set to ``None``, "
"the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` sets "
"the :ref:`cross-origin-opener-policy` header on all responses that do not "
"already have it to the value provided."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil sé socraithe ar ``None``, socraíonn an:class: "
"`~django.middleware.securityMiddleware` an ceannteideal: :ref: `cross-origin-"
"opener-policy` ar gach freagra nach bhfuil sé ar an luach a chuirtear ar "
"fáil cheana féin."

msgid "``SECURE_HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS``"
msgstr "``SLÁNDA_HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS``"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` "
"adds the ``includeSubDomains`` directive to the :ref:`http-strict-transport-"
"security` header. It has no effect unless :setting:`SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS` is "
"set to a non-zero value."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, cuireann an:class: `~django.middleware.securityMiddleware` "
"an treoir `includeSubdomains`` leis an gceannteideal: `http-strict-transport-"
"security`. Níl aon éifeacht aige gan leith:leagtar síos: "
"`SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS` socraítear go luach neamh-nialasach."

msgid ""
"Setting this incorrectly can irreversibly (for the value "
"of :setting:`SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS`) break your site. Read the :ref:`http-"
"strict-transport-security` documentation first."
msgstr ""
"Má shocraíonn sé seo go mícheart is féidir le do shuíomh a bhriseadh go "
"neamh-inchúlghabháilte (maidir le luach: SETING: `SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS`). "
"Léigh an doiciméad:ref: `http-strict-transport-security` ar dtús."

msgid "``SECURE_HSTS_PRELOAD``"
msgstr "``SLÁNDA_HSTS_PRELOAD``"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` "
"adds the ``preload`` directive to the :ref:`http-strict-transport-security` "
"header. It has no effect unless :setting:`SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS` is set to a "
"non-zero value."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``True``, cuireann an:class: `~django.middleware.securityMiddleware` "
"an treoir ``preload`` leis an gceannteideal: `http-strict-transport-"
"security`. Níl aon éifeacht aige gan leithéid: socraítear "
"`SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS` go luach neamh-nialasach."

msgid "``SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS``"
msgstr "``SLÁNDA_HSTS_SOICIND``"

msgid ""
"If set to a non-zero integer value, "
"the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` sets "
"the :ref:`http-strict-transport-security` header on all responses that do "
"not already have it."
msgstr ""
"Má tá luach sláimhir neamh-nialasach leagtha síos, socraíonn an "
"ceannteideal: :ref: `http-strict-transport-security` ar gach freagra nach "
"bhfuil sé ann cheana féin."

msgid ""
"Setting this incorrectly can irreversibly (for some time) break your site. "
"Read the :ref:`http-strict-transport-security` documentation first."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir é seo a shocrú go mícheart do shuíomh a bhriseadh go dochreidte "
"(ar feadh tamaill). Léigh an doiciméad:ref: `http-strict-transport-security` "
"ar dtús."

msgid "``SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER``"
msgstr "``SLÁNT_PROXY_SSL_HEADER``"

msgid ""
"A tuple representing an HTTP header/value combination that signifies a "
"request is secure. This controls the behavior of the request object's "
"``is_secure()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Tuple a léiríonn teaglaim ceannair/luach HTTP a thugann le fios go bhfuil "
"iarratas slán. Rialaíonn sé seo iompar modh ``is_secure () ``an réad "
"iarratais."

msgid ""
"By default, ``is_secure()`` determines if a request is secure by confirming "
"that a requested URL uses ``https://``. This method is important for "
"Django's CSRF protection, and it may be used by your own code or third-party "
"apps."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, cinneann ``is_secure () ``an bhfuil iarratas slán "
"trí dheimhniú go n-úsáideann URL iarrtha ``https: //``. Tá an modh seo "
"tábhachtach do chosaint CSRF Django, agus féadfaidh do chód féin nó aipeanna "
"tríú páirtí é a úsáid."

msgid ""
"If your Django app is behind a proxy, though, the proxy may be "
"\"swallowing\" whether the original request uses HTTPS or not. If there is a "
"non-HTTPS connection between the proxy and Django then ``is_secure()`` would "
"always return ``False`` -- even for requests that were made via HTTPS by the "
"end user. In contrast, if there is an HTTPS connection between the proxy and "
"Django then ``is_secure()`` would always return ``True`` -- even for "
"requests that were made originally via HTTP."
msgstr ""
"Má tá d'aip Django taobh thiar de sheachfhreastalaí, áfach, b'fhéidir go "
"bhfuil an seachfhreastalaí ag “shlogadh” cibé an úsáideann an t-iarratas "
"bunaidh HTTPS nó nach Má tá nasc neamh-HTTPS idir an seachfhreastalaí agus "
"Django ansin chuirfeadh ``is_secure () ``ar ais ``False`` i gcónaí - fiú le "
"haghaidh iarratais a rinne an t-úsáideoir deiridh trí HTTPS. I gcodarsnacht "
"leis sin, má tá nasc HTTPS idir an seachfhreastalaí agus Django ansin "
"chuirfeadh ``is_secure () ``ar ais ``True`` i gcónaí - fiú le haghaidh "
"iarratais a rinneadh ar dtús trí HTTP."

msgid ""
"In this situation, configure your proxy to set a custom HTTP header that "
"tells Django whether the request came in via HTTPS, and set "
"``SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER`` so that Django knows what header to look for."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás seo, cumraigh do sheachfhreastalaí chun ceanntásc saincheaptha HTTP "
"a shocrú a insíonn do Django an tháinig an t-iarratas isteach trí HTTPS, "
"agus socraigh ``SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER`` ionas go mbeidh a fhios ag Django "
"cén ceannteideal atá le lorg."

msgid ""
"Set a tuple with two elements -- the name of the header to look for and the "
"required value. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh tuple le dhá ghné - ainm an cheanntásc le cuardach agus an luach "
"riachtanach. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"This tells Django to trust the ``X-Forwarded-Proto`` header that comes from "
"our proxy and that the request is guaranteed to be secure (i.e., it "
"originally came in via HTTPS) when:"
msgstr ""
"Deir sé seo le Django muinín a bheith agat as an gceannteideal ``X-Forwarded-"
"Proto`` a thagann ónár seachfhreastalaí agus go ráthaítear go mbeidh an t-"
"iarratas slán (ie, tháinig sé isteach ar dtús trí HTTPS) nuair:"

msgid "the header value is ``'https'``, or"
msgstr "is é an luach ceanntásc ``'https'``, nó"

msgid ""
"its initial, leftmost value is ``'https'`` in the case of a comma-separated "
"list of protocols (e.g. ``'https,http,http'``)."
msgstr ""
"is é a luach tosaigh, is clé ná ``'https'`` i gcás liosta prótacail scartha "
"le camóg (m.sh. ```https, http, http'``)."

msgid ""
"You should *only* set this setting if you control your proxy or have some "
"other guarantee that it sets/strips this header appropriately."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit* ach an socrú seo a shocrú má rialaíonn tú do "
"sheachfhreastalaí nó má tá ráthaíocht éigin eile agat go socraí/stiallann sé "
"an ceannteideal seo go cuí."

msgid ""
"Note that the header needs to be in the format as used by ``request.META`` "
"-- all caps and likely starting with ``HTTP_``. (Remember, Django "
"automatically adds ``'HTTP_'`` to the start of x-header names before making "
"the header available in ``request.META``.)"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go gcaithfidh an ceannteideal a bheith sa fhormáid mar a "
"úsáideann ``Request.meta`` - gach caipín agus is dócha go dtosaíonn le "
"``HTTP_``. (Cuimhnigh, cuireann Django ``'HTTP_'`` go huathoibríoch le tús "
"ainmneacha x-cheannteideal sula gcuireann an ceannteideal ar fáil i "
"``Request.meta``.)"

msgid ""
"**Modifying this setting can compromise your site's security. Ensure you "
"fully understand your setup before changing it.**"
msgstr ""
"** Féadfaidh an socrú seo a mhodhnú slándáil do shuíomh a chur i gcur "
"Cinntigh go dtuigeann tú do shocrú go hiomlán sula n-athraíonn tú **"

msgid ""
"Make sure ALL of the following are true before setting this (assuming the "
"values from the example above):"
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil GACH ceann de na rudaí seo a leanas fíor sula "
"gcuirtear é seo a shocrú (glacadh leis na luachanna ón sampla thuas"

msgid "Your Django app is behind a proxy."
msgstr "Tá d'aip Django taobh thiar de sheachfhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"Your proxy strips the ``X-Forwarded-Proto`` header from all incoming "
"requests, even when it contains a comma-separated list of protocols. In "
"other words, if end users include that header in their requests, the proxy "
"will discard it."
msgstr ""
"Stíorálann do sheachfhreastalaí an ceannteideal ``X-Forwarded-Proto`` ó gach "
"iarratas atá ag teacht isteach, fiú nuair a bhíonn liosta prótacail scartha "
"le camóg ann. Is é sin le rá, má chuimsíonn úsáideoirí deiridh an ceanntásc "
"sin ina n-iarratais, caithfidh an seachfhreastalaí é."

msgid ""
"Your proxy sets the ``X-Forwarded-Proto`` header and sends it to Django, but "
"only for requests that originally come in via HTTPS."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn do sheachfhreastalaí an ceannteideal ``X-Forwarded-Proto`` agus "
"seolann sé chuig Django é, ach amháin le haghaidh iarratais a thagann "
"isteach trí HTTPS ar dtús."

msgid ""
"If any of those are not true, you should keep this setting set to ``None`` "
"and find another way of determining HTTPS, perhaps via custom middleware."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil aon cheann acu sin fíor, ba cheart duit an socrú seo a "
"choinneáil socraithe go ``None ``agus bealach eile a fháil chun HTTPS a "
"chinneadh, b'fhéidir trí mheán-earraí saincheaptha."

msgid "``SECURE_REDIRECT_EXEMPT``"
msgstr "``SLÁNDA_ATHREDIRECT_EISEOLÚINT``"

msgid ""
"If a URL path matches a regular expression in this list, the request will "
"not be redirected to HTTPS. "
"The :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` strips leading "
"slashes from URL paths, so patterns shouldn't include them, e.g. "
"``SECURE_REDIRECT_EXEMPT = [r'^no-ssl/$', …]``. "
"If :setting:`SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` is ``False``, this setting has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Má mheaitseálann cosán URL le léiriú rialta sa liosta seo, ní atreorófar an "
"t-iarratas chuig HTTPS. Stíleann an: Class: "
"`~django.middleware.security.securityMiddleware` slascanna a threoraíonn ó "
"chosáin URL, mar sin níor cheart iad a bheith san áireamh ar phatrúin, m.sh. "
"`SECURE_REDIRECT_EXEMPT = [r'^no-ssl/$',...] ``. Má tá: SETTING: "
"`SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` ``False``, níl aon éifeacht ag an socrú seo."

msgid "``SECURE_REFERRER_POLICY``"
msgstr "``BEARTAS ATREORÓIR_SLÁNDÁLA``"

msgid ""
"If configured, the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` "
"sets the :ref:`referrer-policy` header on all responses that do not already "
"have it to the value provided."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé cumraithe, socraíonn an:class: "
"`~django.middleware.securityMiddleware` an ceannteideal: ref: `referrer-"
"policy` ar gach freagra nach bhfuil sé ar an luach a chuirtear ar fáil "
"cheana féin."

msgid "``SECURE_SSL_HOST``"
msgstr "``SSL_ÓST_SÁBHÁILTE``"

msgid ""
"If a string (e.g. ``secure.example.com``), all SSL redirects will be "
"directed to this host rather than the originally-requested host (e.g. "
"``www.example.com``). If :setting:`SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` is ``False``, this "
"setting has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Má tá teaghrán ann (m.sh. `secure.example.com``), déanfar gach athsheoladh "
"SSL a threorú chuig an óstach seo seachas an t-óstach a iarrtar bunaidh "
"(m.sh. ``www.example.com``). Má tá: SETTING: `SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` "
"``False``, níl aon éifeacht ag an socrú seo."

msgid "``SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT``"
msgstr "``SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT``"

msgid ""
"If ``True``, "
"the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware` :ref:`redirects "
"<ssl-redirect>` all non-HTTPS requests to HTTPS (except for those URLs "
"matching a regular expression listed in :setting:`SECURE_REDIRECT_EXEMPT`)."
msgstr ""
"<ssl-redirect>Má tá ``True``, an:class: "
"`~django.middleware.securityMiddleware`:ref: `atreoraíonn `gach iarratas "
"neamh-HTTPS chuig HTTPS (ach amháin na URLanna sin a mheaitseálann le abairt "
"rialta atá liostaithe in:setting: `SECURE_REDIRECT_EXEMPT`)."

msgid ""
"If turning this to ``True`` causes infinite redirects, it probably means "
"your site is running behind a proxy and can't tell which requests are secure "
"and which are not. Your proxy likely sets a header to indicate secure "
"requests; you can correct the problem by finding out what that header is and "
"configuring the :setting:`SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER` setting accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Má chruthaíonn athatreoruithe gan teorainn é seo a chasadh go `True``, is "
"dócha go bhfuil do shuíomh ag rith taobh thiar de seachfhreastalaí agus nach "
"féidir leo a rá cé na hiarratais atá slán agus cé nach bhfuil. Is dócha go "
"socraíonn do sheachfhreastalaí ceanntásc chun iarrataí slán a chur in iúl; "
"is féidir leat an fhadhb a cheartú trí fháil amach cad é an ceannteideal sin "
"agus an socrú:setting: `SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER` a chumrú dá réir."

msgid "``SERIALIZATION_MODULES``"
msgstr "``MODÚL_SRAITHEACH``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary of modules containing serializer definitions (provided as "
"strings), keyed by a string identifier for that serialization type. For "
"example, to define a YAML serializer, use::"
msgstr ""
"Foclóir modúil ina bhfuil sainmhínithe serializer (curtha ar fáil mar "
"teaghráin), eochairte ag aitheantóir teaghrán don chineál sraitheach sin. "
"Mar shampla, chun serializer YAML a shainiú, bain úsáid as:"

msgid "``SERVER_EMAIL``"
msgstr "``FREASTALAÍ_RÍOMHPHOST``"

msgid "Default: ``'root@localhost'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'root @localhost '``"

msgid ""
"The email address that error messages come from, such as those sent "
"to :setting:`ADMINS` and :setting:`MANAGERS`. This address is used in the "
"``From:`` header and can take any format valid in the chosen email sending "
"protocol."
msgstr ""
"An seoladh ríomhphoist as a dtagann teachtaireachtaí earráide, mar shampla "
"iad siúd a sheoltar chuig:setting: `ADMINS` agus:setting: `MANAGERS`. "
"Úsáidtear an seoladh seo sa cheanntásc ``From: ``agus féadann sé aon "
"fhormáid a ghlacadh bailí sa phrótacal seolta ríomhphoist roghnaithe."

msgid "Why are my emails sent from a different address?"
msgstr "Cén fáth a sheoltar mo ríomhphoist ó sheoladh difriúil?"

msgid ""
"This address is used only for error messages. It is *not* the address that "
"regular email messages sent with :func:`~django.core.mail.send_mail` come "
"from; for that, see :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL`."
msgstr ""

msgid "``SHORT_DATE_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_DÁTA_GEARR``"

msgid "Default: ``'m/d/Y'`` (e.g. ``12/31/2003``)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ```M/D/Y'`` (m.sh. ``12/31/2003 ``)"

msgid ""
"An available formatting that can be used for displaying date fields on "
"templates. Note that the corresponding locale-dictated format has higher "
"precedence and will be applied instead. See :tfilter:`allowed date format "
"strings <date>`."
msgstr ""
"Formáidiú atá ar fáil is féidir a úsáid chun réimsí dáta a thaispeáint ar "
"theimpléid. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an "
"bhformáid chomhfhreagrach áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad. "
"<date>Féach: TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `."

msgid "See also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT` and :setting:`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT` agus:socrú: `SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`."

msgid "``SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_DÁTA GEARRTHA``"

msgid "Default: ``'m/d/Y P'`` (e.g. ``12/31/2003 4 p.m.``)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ```M/D/Y P'`` (m.sh. ``12/31/2003 4 p.m.``)"

msgid ""
"An available formatting that can be used for displaying datetime fields on "
"templates. Note that the corresponding locale-dictated format has higher "
"precedence and will be applied instead. See :tfilter:`allowed date format "
"strings <date>`."
msgstr ""
"Formáidiú atá ar fáil is féidir a úsáid chun réimsí dáta-ama a thaispeáint "
"ar theimpléid. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an "
"bhformáid chomhfhreagrach áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad. "
"<date>Féach: TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `."

msgid "See also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT` and :setting:`SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT` agus:socrú: `SHORT_DATE_FORMAT`."

msgid "``SIGNING_BACKEND``"
msgstr "```SIGNING_BACKEND``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.core.signing.TimestampSigner'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Django.Core.Signing.TimeStampSigner'` `"

msgid "The backend used for signing cookies and other data."
msgstr "An cúltaca a úsáidtear chun fianáin agus sonraí eile a shíniú."

msgid "See also the :doc:`/topics/signing` documentation."
msgstr "Féach freisin an doiciméadach:doc: `/topics/signing`."

msgid "``SILENCED_SYSTEM_CHECKS``"
msgstr "``SEICEÁLACH_CHÓRAIS CIOSTAITHE ``"

msgid ""
"A list of identifiers of messages generated by the system check framework "
"(i.e. ``[\"models.W001\"]``) that you wish to permanently acknowledge and "
"ignore. Silenced checks will not be output to the console."
msgstr ""
"Liosta d'aitheantóirí teachtaireachtaí a ghineann creat seiceála an chórais "
"(ie ``[\"Models.W001\"] `) ar mhaith leat aitheantas a thabhairt go buan "
"agus neamhaird a dhéanamh orthu. Ní aschur seiceálacha ciúnaithe chuig an "
"gconsól."

msgid "See also the :doc:`/ref/checks` documentation."
msgstr "Féach freisin an doiciméadach:doc: `/ref/checks`."

msgid "``STORAGES``"
msgstr "``STÓRÁLAÍ``"

msgid ""
"A dictionary containing the settings for all storages to be used with "
"Django. It is a nested dictionary whose contents map a storage alias to a "
"dictionary containing the options for an individual storage."
msgstr ""
"Foclóir ina bhfuil na socruithe do gach stóráil le húsáid le Django. Is "
"foclóir neadaithe é a léarscáil a n-ábhar ailias stórála chuig foclóir ina "
"bhfuil na roghanna le haghaidh stórála aonair."

msgid ""
"Storages can have any alias you choose. However, there are two aliases with "
"special significance:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le stórais aon alias a roghnaíonn tú a bheith acu. Mar sin féin, "
"tá dhá ainm le tábhacht speisialta:"

msgid ""
"``default`` for :doc:`managing files </topics/files>`. "
"``'``:class:`django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage`\\ ``'`` is the "
"default storage engine."
msgstr ""
"``default`` le haghaidh: doc: `comhaid a bhainistiú' </topics/files>. "
"```````:class: `Django.Core.Files.Storage.FileSystemStorage`\\ ````is é an t-"
"inneall stórála réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"``staticfiles`` for :doc:`managing static files </ref/contrib/staticfiles>`. "
"``'``:class:`django.contrib.staticfiles.storage.StaticFilesStorage`\\ ``'`` "
"is the default storage engine."
msgstr ""
"``staticfiles`` le haghaidh: doc: `comhaid statacha a bhainistiú' </ref/"
"contrib/staticfiles>. ```````:class: "
"`Django.contrib.staticFiles.Storage.staticFilesStorage`\\ ````is é an t-"
"inneall stórála réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"The following is an example ``settings.py`` snippet defining a custom file "
"storage called ``example``::"
msgstr ""
"Seo a leanas sampla ``settings.py`` snippet a shainmhíníonn stóráil comhaid "
"saincheaptha ar a dtugtar ``example``:"

msgid ""
"``OPTIONS`` are passed to the ``BACKEND`` on initialization in ``**kwargs``."
msgstr "Cuirtear ``ROGHANN`` chuig an `BACKEND`` ar thionscnamh i `**kwargs``."

msgid ""
"A ready-to-use instance of the storage backends can be retrieved "
"from :data:`django.core.files.storage.storages`. Use a key corresponding to "
"the backend definition in :setting:`STORAGES`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir sampla réidh le húsáid de na cúltaca stórála a aisghabháil ó:data: "
"`django.core.files.storage.storages`. Úsáid eochair a fhreagraíonn don "
"sainmhíniú cúltaca in:setting: `STORAGES`."

msgid "Is my value merged with the default value?"
msgstr "An bhfuil mo luach cumaisc leis an luach réamhshocraithe?"

msgid ""
"Defining this setting overrides the default value and is *not* merged with "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Sáraíonn an socrú seo a shainiú an luach réamhshocraithe agus níl* níl* "
"cumasc leis."

msgid "``TEMPLATES``"
msgstr "``TEIMPLÉID``"

msgid ""
"A list containing the settings for all template engines to be used with "
"Django. Each item of the list is a dictionary containing the options for an "
"individual engine."
msgstr ""
"Liosta ina bhfuil na socruithe do gach innill teimpléad le húsáid le Django. "
"Is foclóir é gach mír den liosta ina bhfuil na roghanna le haghaidh inneall "
"aonair."

msgid ""
"Here's a setup that tells the Django template engine to load templates from "
"the ``templates`` subdirectory inside each installed application::"
msgstr ""
"Seo socrú a insíonn d'inneall teimpléid Django teimpléid a luchtú ón bhfo-"
"eolaire ``teimpléid ``taobh istigh de gach feidhmchlár suiteáilte::"

msgid "The following options are available for all backends."
msgstr "Tá na roghanna seo a leanas ar fáil do gach cúltaca."

msgid "The template backend to use. The built-in template backends are:"
msgstr "An cúltaca teimpléad le húsáid. Is iad na cúltaca teimpléad ionsuite:"

msgid "``'django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates'``"
msgstr "```Django.Template.Backends.Django.DjangoTemplates'``"

msgid "``'django.template.backends.jinja2.Jinja2'``"
msgstr "```Django.Template.Backends.Jinja2.Jinja2'``"

msgid ""
"You can use a template backend that doesn't ship with Django by setting "
"``BACKEND`` to a fully-qualified path (i.e. "
"``'mypackage.whatever.Backend'``)."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cúltaca teimpléad nach seolann le Django a úsáid trí "
"``BACKEND`` a shocrú go cosán láncháilithe (ie "
"```MyPackage.whatever.backend'``)."

msgid "Default: see below"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: féach thíos"

msgid ""
"The alias for this particular template engine. It's an identifier that "
"allows selecting an engine for rendering. Aliases must be unique across all "
"configured template engines."
msgstr ""
"An alias don inneall teimpléad áirithe seo. Is aitheantóir é a cheadaíonn "
"inneall a roghnú le haghaidh rindreála. Caithfidh ainmneacha a bheith "
"uathúil ar fud gach innill teimpléad cumraithe"

msgid ""
"It defaults to the name of the module defining the engine class, i.e. the "
"next to last piece of :setting:`BACKEND <TEMPLATES-BACKEND>`, when it isn't "
"provided. For example if the backend is ``'mypackage.whatever.Backend'`` "
"then its default name is ``'whatever'``."
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraíonn sé ainm an mhodúil a shainníonn rang an innill, i.e. an "
"chéad phíosa deireanach de: setting: `BACKEND <TEMPLATES-BACKEND>`, nuair "
"nach gcuirtear ar fáil é. Mar shampla más é ``'MyPackage.whatever.backend'`` "
"an cúltaca ansin is é ``whatever'` a ainm réamhshocraithe."

msgid "``DIRS``"
msgstr "```DIRS``"

msgid ""
"Directories where the engine should look for template source files, in "
"search order."
msgstr ""
"Eolairí inar chóir don inneall comhaid foinse teimpléad a lorg, in ord "
"cuardaigh."

msgid "``APP_DIRS``"
msgstr "``APP_DIRS``"

msgid ""
"Whether the engine should look for template source files inside installed "
"applications."
msgstr ""
"Cibé an chóir don inneall comhaid foinse teimpléad a lorg taobh istigh "
"d'fheidhmchlá"

msgid ""
"The default :file:`settings.py` file created by :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>` sets ``'APP_DIRS': True``."
msgstr ""
"<startproject>Leagann an comhad réamhshocraithe:file: `settings.py` a "
"chruthaí:djadmin: `django-admin startproject ````APP_DIRS': True``."

msgid "Default: ``{}`` (Empty dict)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``{}`` (Ordú folamh)"

msgid ""
"Extra parameters to pass to the template backend. Available parameters vary "
"depending on the template backend. "
"See :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` "
"and :class:`~django.template.backends.jinja2.Jinja2` for the options of the "
"built-in backends."
msgstr ""
"Paraiméadair bhreise le dul chuig an gcúltaca teimpléid. Athraíonn "
"paraiméadair atá ar fáil ag brath ar an gcúl teimpléid Féach: Class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` agus:class: "
"`~django.template.backends.jinja2.jinja2` le haghaidh roghanna na gcúltaca "
"ionsuite."

msgid "``TEST_RUNNER``"
msgstr "``TÁST_RUNNER``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.test.runner.DiscoverRunner'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Django.Test.Runner.DiscoverRunner'` `"

msgid ""
"The name of the class to use for starting the test suite. See :ref:`other-"
"testing-frameworks`."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an ranga le húsáid chun an tsraith tástála a thosú. Féach: ref: "
"`creataí tástála eile'."

msgid "``TEST_NON_SERIALIZED_APPS``"
msgstr "``TÁSTÁIL_NEAM_AIPEANNA SRAITHEACH``"

msgid ""
"In order to restore the database state between tests for "
"``TransactionTestCase``\\s and database backends without transactions, "
"Django will :ref:`serialize the contents of all apps <test-case-serialized-"
"rollback>` when it starts the test run so it can then reload from that copy "
"before running tests that need it."
msgstr ""
"D'fhonn stát an bunachar sonraí a athbhunú idir tástálacha do "
"`TransactionTestCase`` agus cúltaca bunachar sonraí gan idirbhearta, "
"déanfaidh Django: ref: `sraitheadh ábhar na n-aipeanna uile <test-case-"
"serialized-rollback>`nuair a thosaíonn sé an rith tástála ionas gur féidir "
"leis an gcóip sin a athluchtú sula ndéanann sé tástálacha a theastaíonn "
"uathu."

msgid ""
"This slows down the startup time of the test runner; if you have apps that "
"you know don't need this feature, you can add their full names in here (e.g. "
"``'django.contrib.contenttypes'``) to exclude them from this serialization "
"process."
msgstr ""
"Moillíonn sé seo am tosaithe an rádálaí tástála; má tá aipeanna agat a fhios "
"uait nach dteastaíonn an ghné seo uathu, is féidir leat a n-ainmneacha "
"iomlána a chur anseo (m.sh. ``django.contrib.contenttypes``) chun iad a "
"eisiamh ón bpróiseas sraitheach seo."

msgid "``THOUSAND_SEPARATOR``"
msgstr "``MÍLTE DEIGHILTEOIR ``"

msgid "Default: ``','`` (Comma)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``', '``(Coma)"

msgid ""
"Default thousand separator used when formatting numbers. This setting is "
"used only when :setting:`USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` is ``True`` "
"and :setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING` is greater than ``0``."
msgstr ""
"Míle deighilteoir réamhshocraithe a úsáidtear agus u Ní úsáidtear an socrú "
"seo ach nuair:setting: `USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` ``True`` agus:setting: "
"`NUMBER_GROUPING` níos mó ná ``0``."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING`, :setting:`DECIMAL_SEPARATOR` "
"and :setting:`USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `NUMBER_GROUPING`, :setting: `DECIMAL_SEPARATOR` "
"agus:setting: `USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."

msgid "``TIME_FORMAT``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_AIM``"

msgid "Default: ``'P'`` (e.g. ``4 p.m.``)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'P'`` (m.sh. ``4 p.m.``)"

msgid ""
"The default formatting to use for displaying time fields in any part of the "
"system. Note that the locale-dictated format has higher precedence and will "
"be applied instead. See :tfilter:`allowed date format strings <date>`."
msgstr ""
"An formáidiú réamhshocraithe le húsáid chun réimsí ama a thaispeáint in aon "
"chuid den chóras. Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil tosaíocht níos airde ag an "
"bhformáid áitiúil agus go gcuirfear i bhfeidhm ina ionad sin. <date>Féach: "
"TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `."

msgid "See also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT` and :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT` agus:socrú: `DATETIME_FORMAT`."

msgid "``TIME_INPUT_FORMATS``"
msgstr "``FORMÁID_IONCHUIR_AMA ``"

msgid ""
"A list of formats that will be accepted when inputting data on a time field. "
"Formats will be tried in order, using the first valid one. Note that these "
"format strings use Python's :ref:`datetime module syntax <strftime-strptime-"
"behavior>`, not the format strings from the :tfilter:`date` template filter."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na formáidí a nglacfar leo agus sonraí á ionchur isteach ar réimse "
"ama. Déanfar triail a bhaint as formáidí in ord, ag baint úsáide as an gcéad "
"cheann bailí. Tabhair faoi deara go n-úsáideann na teaghráin formáide seo "
"comhréir modúl Python: ref: `datetime '<strftime-strptime-behavior>, ní na "
"teaghráin formáide ón scagaire teimpléad:tfilter: `dáta`."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` and :setting:`DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freisin: socrú: `DATE_INPUT_FORMATS` agus:setting: "
"`DATETIME_INPUT_FORMATS`."

msgid "Default: ``'America/Chicago'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'Meiriceá/Chicago'``"

msgid ""
"A string representing the time zone for this installation. See the `list of "
"time zones`_."
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an crios ama don suiteáil seo. Féach an `liosta criosanna "
"ama`_."

msgid ""
"Since Django was first released with the :setting:`TIME_ZONE` set to "
"``'America/Chicago'``, the global setting (used if nothing is defined in "
"your project's ``settings.py``) remains ``'America/Chicago'`` for backwards "
"compatibility. New project templates default to ``'UTC'``."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é gur eisíodh Django den chéad uair leis an: setting: `TIME_ZONE` "
"socraithe go ``'America/Chicago'`, fanann an suíomh domhanda (a úsáidtear "
"mura bhfuil aon rud sainmhínithe i `settings.py`` do thionscadail) "
"``Meiricea/Chicago'` le haghaidh comhoiriúnacht ar ais. Teimpléid nua "
"tionscadail réamhshocraithe go ``'UTC'``."

msgid ""
"Note that this isn't necessarily the time zone of the server. For example, "
"one server may serve multiple Django-powered sites, each with a separate "
"time zone setting."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach gá gurb é seo crios ama an fhreastalaí. Mar shampla, "
"féadfaidh freastalaí amháin freastal ar iliomad suíomhanna faoi thiomáint "
"Django, gach ceann acu le socrú crios ama ar leithligh."

msgid ""
"When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``False``, this is the time zone in which Django "
"will store all datetimes. When :setting:`USE_TZ` is ``True``, this is the "
"default time zone that Django will use to display datetimes in templates and "
"to interpret datetimes entered in forms."
msgstr ""
"Nuair: SETTING: Is é `USE_TZ` ``False``, is é seo an crios ama ina "
"stóráilfidh Django gach dáta ama. Nuair: SETTING: Is é `USE_TZ` ``True``, is "
"é seo an crios ama réamhshocraithe a úsáidfidh Django chun dáta-amanna a "
"thaispeáint i dteimpléid agus chun dáta a iontráiltear i bhfoirmeacha a "
"léirmhíniú."

msgid ""
"On Unix environments (where :func:`time.tzset` is implemented), Django sets "
"the ``os.environ['TZ']`` variable to the time zone you specify in "
"the :setting:`TIME_ZONE` setting. Thus, all your views and models will "
"automatically operate in this time zone. However, Django won't set the "
"``TZ`` environment variable if you're using the manual configuration option "
"as described in :ref:`manually configuring settings <settings-without-django-"
"settings-module>`. If Django doesn't set the ``TZ`` environment variable, "
"it's up to you to ensure your processes are running in the correct "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"Ar thimpeallachtaí Unix (áit a chuirtear: func: `time.tzset` i bhfeidhm), "
"socraíonn Django an athróg ``os.environ ['TZ'] ``don chrios ama a shonraíonn "
"tú sa socrú: `TIME_ZONE`. Mar sin, oibreoidh do thuairimí agus samhlacha go "
"léir go huathoibríoch sa chrios ama seo. <settings-without-django-settings-"
"module>Mar sin féin, ní shocróidh Django an t-athróg comhshaoil ``TZ`` má tá "
"an rogha cumraíochta láimhe á úsáid agat mar a thuairiscítear in:ref: "
"`socruithe a chumrú de láimh `. Mura socraíonn Django an t-athróg comhshaoil "
"``TZ`, is fútsa atá sé a chinntiú go bhfuil do phróisis ag rith sa "
"timpeallacht cheart."

msgid ""
"Django cannot reliably use alternate time zones in a Windows environment. If "
"you're running Django on Windows, :setting:`TIME_ZONE` must be set to match "
"the system time zone."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir le Django criosanna ama malartacha a úsáid go hiontaofa i "
"dtimpeallacht Windows. Má tá Django á reáchtáil agat ar Windows, "
"caithfear :setting: `TIME_ZONE` a shocrú chun crios ama an chórais a "
"mheaitseáil."

msgid "``USE_I18N``"
msgstr "``USE_I18N``"

msgid ""
"A boolean that specifies whether Django's translation system should be "
"enabled. This provides a way to turn it off, for performance. If this is set "
"to ``False``, Django will make some optimizations so as not to load the "
"translation machinery."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a shonraíonn an chóir córas aistriúcháin Django a chumasú. "
"Soláthraíonn sé seo bealach chun é a mhúchadh, le haghaidh feidhmíochta. Má "
"shocraítear é seo go `False`, déanfaidh Django roinnt optamaithe ionas nach "
"luchtfaidh sé an t-innealra aistriúcháin."

msgid "See also :setting:`LANGUAGE_CODE` and :setting:`USE_TZ`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `LANGUAGE_CODE` agus:socrú: `USE_TZ`."

msgid ""
"The default :file:`settings.py` file created by :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>` includes ``USE_I18N = True`` for convenience."
msgstr ""
"<startproject>Cuimsíonn an comhad réamhshocraithe:file: `settings.py` a "
"chruthaí:djadmin: `django-admin startproject ```USE_I18N = True`` le "
"haghaidh áisiúlachta."

msgid "``USE_THOUSAND_SEPARATOR``"
msgstr "``ÚSÁID_MÍLTE DEIGHILTEOIR ``"

msgid ""
"A boolean that specifies whether to display numbers using a thousand "
"separator. When set to ``True``, Django will format numbers using "
"the :setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING` and :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR` settings. "
"The latter two settings may also be dictated by the locale, which takes "
"precedence."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a shonraíonn an bhfuil uimhreacha le taispeáint ag baint úsáide as "
"míle deighilteoir. Nuair a bheidh sé socraithe go ``True``, déanfaidh Django "
"uimhreacha a fhormáidiú ag baint úsáide as socruithe:: `NUMBER_GROUPING` "
"agus:setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`. Is féidir leis an áitiúil a shocrú an dá "
"shocrú deireanach freisin, a ghlacann tosaíocht."

msgid ""
"See also :setting:`DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`, :setting:`NUMBER_GROUPING` "
"and :setting:`THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."
msgstr ""
"Féach freis:socrú: `DECIMAL_SEPARATOR`, :setting: `NUMBER_GROUPING` "
"agus:setting: `THOUSAND_SEPARATOR`."

msgid "``USE_TZ``"
msgstr "``ÚSÁID_TZ ``"

msgid ""
"A boolean that specifies if datetimes will be timezone-aware by default or "
"not. If this is set to ``True``, Django will use timezone-aware datetimes "
"internally."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a shonraíonn an mbeidh amanna dáta ar an eolas ó chrios ama de réir "
"réamhshocraithe nó nach bhfuil. Má tá sé seo socraithe go ``True``, "
"úsáidfidh Django amanna dáta atá ar an eolas faoi chrios ama go hinmheánach."

msgid ""
"When ``USE_TZ`` is False, Django will use naive datetimes in local time, "
"except when parsing ISO 8601 formatted strings, where timezone information "
"will always be retained if present."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn `USE_TZ`` bréagach, úsáidfidh Django amanna dáta naif in am "
"áitiúil, ach amháin nuair a dhéantar teaghráin formáidithe ISO 8601 á "
"pháirseáil, áit a gcoinneofar faisnéis crios ama i gcónaí má tá sé i láthair."

msgid "See also :setting:`TIME_ZONE` and :setting:`USE_I18N`."
msgstr "Féach freis:socrú: `TIME_ZONE` agus:socrú: `USE_I18N`."

msgid "``USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST``"
msgstr "``ÚSÁID_X_FORWARDED_ÓST``"

msgid ""
"A boolean that specifies whether to use the ``X-Forwarded-Host`` header in "
"preference to the ``Host`` header. This should only be enabled if a proxy "
"which sets this header is in use."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a shonraíonn an gceanntásc ``X-Forwarded-Host`` a úsáid mar rogha ar "
"an gceannteideal ``Host``. Níor chóir é seo a chumasú ach amháin má tá "
"seachfhreastalaí a leagann an ceanntásc seo in úsáid."

msgid ""
"This setting takes priority over :setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT`. "
"Per :rfc:`7239#section-5.3`, the ``X-Forwarded-Host`` header can include the "
"port number, in which case you shouldn't use :setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT`."
msgstr ""
"Glacann an socrú seo tosaíocht thair:setting: `USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT`. "
"Per:RFC: `7239 #section -5.3`, is féidir leis an gceannteideal ``X-Forwarded-"
"Host`` uimhir an chalafoirt a áireamh, agus sa chás sin níor chóir "
"duit:setting: `USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT` a úsáid."

msgid "``USE_X_FORWARDED_PORT``"
msgstr "```ÚSÁID_X_FORWARDED_PORT ``"

msgid ""
"A boolean that specifies whether to use the ``X-Forwarded-Port`` header in "
"preference to the ``SERVER_PORT`` ``META`` variable. This should only be "
"enabled if a proxy which sets this header is in use."
msgstr ""
"Boolean a shonraíonn an gceanntásc ``X-Forwarded-Port`` a úsáid mar rogha "
"leis an athróg ``SERVER_PORT`` ``META``. Níor chóir é seo a chumasú ach "
"amháin má tá seachfhreastalaí a leagann an ceanntásc seo in úsáid."

msgid ":setting:`USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` takes priority over this setting."
msgstr ":setting: Glacann `USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST` tosaíocht thar an socrú seo."

msgid "``WSGI_APPLICATION``"
msgstr "``WSGI_IARRATAS``"

msgid ""
"The full Python path of the WSGI application object that Django's built-in "
"servers (e.g. :djadmin:`runserver`) will use. The :djadmin:`django-admin "
"startproject <startproject>` management command will create a standard "
"``wsgi.py`` file with an ``application`` callable in it, and point this "
"setting to that ``application``."
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán Python an réad feidhmchláir WSGI a úsáidfidh freastalaithe "
"ionsuite Django (e.g.:djadmin: `runserver`). Cruthóidh an t-ordú bainist "
"<startproject>íochta: Djadmin: `django-admin startproject `comhad "
"caighdeánach `wsgi.py` le ``feidhmchlár ``is féidir a ghlaoch ann, agus "
"cuirfidh an socrú seo chuig an ``feidhmchlár`` sin."

msgid ""
"If not set, the return value of ``django.core.wsgi.get_wsgi_application()`` "
"will be used. In this case, the behavior of :djadmin:`runserver` will be "
"identical to previous Django versions."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil sé socraithe, úsáidfear luach tuairisceáin "
"``django.core.wsgi.get_wsgi_application () ``. Sa chás seo, beidh iompar: "
"djadmin: `runserver` comhionann le leaganacha Django roimhe seo."

msgid "``YEAR_MONTH_FORMAT``"
msgstr "FORMÁID ``BLIAN_MHÍOS``"

msgid "Default: ``'F Y'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'F Y'``"

msgid ""
"The default formatting to use for date fields on Django admin change-list "
"pages -- and, possibly, by other parts of the system -- in cases when only "
"the year and month are displayed."
msgstr ""
"An formáidiú réamhshocraithe le húsáid le haghaidh réimsí dáta ar "
"leathanaigh liosta athraithe riaracháin Django - agus, b'fhéidir, ag codanna "
"eile den chóras - i gcásanna nach dtaispeántar ach an bhliain agus an mhí."

msgid ""
"For example, when a Django admin change-list page is being filtered by a "
"date drilldown, the header for a given month displays the month and the "
"year. Different locales have different formats. For example, U.S. English "
"would say \"January 2006,\" whereas another locale might say \"2006/January."
"\""
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, nuair a bhíonn leathanach liosta athraithe riaracháin Django á "
"scagadh ag druileáil dáta, taispeánann an ceannteideal do mhí ar leith an "
"mhí agus an bhliain. Tá formáidí éagsúla ag áitiúla éagsúla. Mar shampla, "
"déarfadh Béarla na SA “Eanáir 2006,” ach d'fhéadfadh áitiúil eile a rá “2006/"
"Eanáir.”"

msgid ""
"See :tfilter:`allowed date format strings <date>`. See "
"also :setting:`DATE_FORMAT`, :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting:`TIME_FORMAT` "
"and :setting:`MONTH_DAY_FORMAT`."
msgstr ""
"<date>Féach: TFilter: `teaghráin formáid dáta ceadaithe `. Féach "
"freis:socrú: `DATE_FORMAT`, :setting: `DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting: "
"`TIME_FORMAT` agus:setting: `MONTH_DAY_FORMAT`."

msgid "``X_FRAME_OPTIONS``"
msgstr "``ROGHANNA X_FRAME``"

msgid "Default: ``'DENY'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'DENY'``"

msgid ""
"The default value for the X-Frame-Options header used "
"by :class:`~django.middleware.clickjacking.XFrameOptionsMiddleware`. See "
"the :doc:`clickjacking protection </ref/clickjacking/>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"An luach réamhshocraithe don cheanntásc X-Frame-Options a úsáideann "
"ar:class: `~django.middleware.clickjacking.xframeOptionsMiddleware`. Féach "
"an doiciméad:doc: `click</ref/clickjacking/> jacking cosant'."

msgid "Auth"
msgstr "Authas"

msgid "Settings for :mod:`django.contrib.auth`."
msgstr "Socruithe le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.auth`."

msgid "``AUTHENTICATION_BACKENDS``"
msgstr "``BACKENDATION_BACKENDS``"

msgid "Default: ``['django.contrib.auth.backends.ModelBackend']``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``['django.contrib.auth.backends.modelBackend']``"

msgid ""
"A list of authentication backend classes (as strings) to use when attempting "
"to authenticate a user. See the :ref:`authentication backends documentation "
"<authentication-backends>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Liosta d'aicmí cúltaca fíordheimhnithe (mar teaghráin) le húsáid agus tú ag "
"iarraidh úsáideoir a fhíordheimhniú. <authentication-backends>Féach na:ref: "
"`doiciméadú cúltaca fíordheimhniúcháin `le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``AUTH_USER_MODEL``"
msgstr "``AUTH_USER_MODEL ``"

msgid "Default: ``'auth.User'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ```Auth.user'``"

msgid "The model to use to represent a User. See :ref:`auth-custom-user`."
msgstr ""
"An tsamhail atá le húsáid chun ionadaíocht a dhéanamh ar Úsáideoir. Féach: "
"ref: `auth-custom-user`."

msgid ""
"You cannot change the AUTH_USER_MODEL setting during the lifetime of a "
"project (i.e. once you have made and migrated models that depend on it) "
"without serious effort. It is intended to be set at the project start, and "
"the model it refers to must be available in the first migration of the app "
"that it lives in. See :ref:`auth-custom-user` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir leat an socrú AUTH_USER_MODEL a athrú le linn shaolré tionscadail "
"(i.e. nuair a bheidh samhlacha déanta agus imirce agat atá ag brath air) gan "
"iarracht tromchúiseach. Tá sé i gceist é a shocrú ag tús an tionscadail, "
"agus caithfidh an tsamhail a thagraíonn sé a bheith ar fáil sa chéad imirce "
"den aip ina gcónaíonn sé ann. Féach: ref: `auth-custom-user` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL``"
msgstr "``LOG_REDIRECT_URL ``"

msgid "Default: ``'/accounts/profile/'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'/cuntais/próifíl/'``"

msgid ""
"The URL or :ref:`named URL pattern <naming-url-patterns>` where requests are "
"redirected after login when "
"the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.LoginView` doesn't get a ``next`` GET "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"An URL nó:ref: `patrún URL ainmnithe <naming-url-patterns>`ina ndéantar "
"iarratais a atreorú tar éis logáil isteach nuair nach bhfaigheann an:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.views.loginView` paraiméadar GET ``next``."

msgid "``LOGIN_URL``"
msgstr "``LOG_URL``"

msgid "Default: ``'/accounts/login/'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'/cuntais/logáil isteach /'``"

msgid ""
"The URL or :ref:`named URL pattern <naming-url-patterns>` where requests are "
"redirected for login when using "
"the :func:`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` "
"decorator, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.LoginRequiredMixin`, :class:`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.AccessMixin`, "
"or when :class:`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.LoginRequiredMiddleware` is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"An URL nó:ref: `patrún URL ainmnithe `ina n- <naming-url-"
"patterns>atreoraítear iarratais ar logáil isteach nuair a úsáidtear an:func: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.decorators.login_required` decorator, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.loginrequiredMixin`, :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.mixins.accessin`, nó when :class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.middleware.loginrequiredMiddleware` suiteáilte."

msgid "``LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL``"
msgstr "``LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URL ``"

msgid ""
"The URL or :ref:`named URL pattern <naming-url-patterns>` where requests are "
"redirected after logout if :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.LogoutView` "
"doesn't have a ``next_page`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"An URL nó:ref: `patrún URL ainmnithe <naming-url-patterns>`ina ndéantar "
"iarratais a atreorú tar éis logáil amach ias:class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.views.logoutview` tréith ``next_page``."

msgid ""
"If ``None``, no redirect will be performed and the logout view will be "
"rendered."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``None``, ní dhéanfar aon athsheoladh agus déanfar an radharc logála "
"amach a léiriú."

msgid "``PASSWORD_RESET_TIMEOUT``"
msgstr "``PASFHOCAL_RESET_TIMEOUT``"

msgid "Default: ``259200`` (3 days, in seconds)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``259200` (3 lá, i soicindí)"

msgid "The number of seconds a password reset link is valid for."
msgstr "Tá líon na soicind a bhfuil nasc athshocraithe pasfhocal bailí dóibh."

msgid ""
"Used by the :class:`~django.contrib.auth.views.PasswordResetConfirmView`."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear ag an: class: "
"`~django.contrib.auth.views.passwordResetConfirmView`."

msgid ""
"Reducing the value of this timeout doesn't make any difference to the "
"ability of an attacker to brute-force a password reset token. Tokens are "
"designed to be safe from brute-forcing without any timeout."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann luach an t-ama seo a laghdú aon difríocht ar chumas ionsaitheora "
"comhartha athshocraithe pasfhocal a chur i bhfeidhm go brútal. Tá comharthaí "
"deartha le bheith sábháilte ó fhorfheidhmiú brúite gan aon am amach."

msgid ""
"This timeout exists to protect against some unlikely attack scenarios, such "
"as someone gaining access to email archives that may contain old, unused "
"password reset tokens."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-am seo ann chun cosaint a dhéanamh i gcoinne roinnt cásanna "
"ionsaithe nach dócha, mar shampla duine a fhaigheann rochtain ar chartlanna "
"ríomhphoist a d'fhéadfadh sean-chomharthaí athshocraithe pasfho"

msgid "``PASSWORD_HASHERS``"
msgstr "``PASSWORD_HASHERS``"

msgid "See :ref:`auth_password_storage`."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `auth_password_storage`."

msgid "``AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS``"
msgstr "``BAILÍOCHTAITHEOIR_PASSWORD_AUTH``"

msgid ""
"The list of validators that are used to check the strength of user's "
"passwords. See :ref:`password-validation` for more details. By default, no "
"validation is performed and all passwords are accepted."
msgstr ""
"Liosta na mbailíochtóirí a úsáidtear chun neart pasfhocail an úsáideora a "
"sheiceáil. Féach:ref: `bailíochtú pasfhocal` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí. "
"De réir réamhshocraithe, ní dhéantar aon bhailíochtú agus glactar le gach "
"pasfhocal."

msgid "Messages"
msgstr "Teachtaireachtaí"

msgid "Settings for :mod:`django.contrib.messages`."
msgstr "Socruithe le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.messages`."

msgid "``MESSAGE_LEVEL``"
msgstr "``LEIBHÉAL_TEACHTAIREACHTAÍ ``"

msgid "Default: ``messages.INFO``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``Messages.info``"

msgid ""
"Sets the minimum message level that will be recorded by the messages "
"framework. See :ref:`message levels <message-level>` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé an leibhéal íosta teachtaireachta a thaifeadfar ag creat na "
"teachtaireachtaí. Féach: tagairt: `leibhéil teachtaireachtaí <message-"
"level>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "Avoiding circular imports"
msgstr "Allmhairithe ciorclach"

msgid ""
"If you override ``MESSAGE_LEVEL`` in your settings file and rely on any of "
"the built-in constants, you must import the constants module directly to "
"avoid the potential for circular imports, e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"Má sháraigh tú ``MESSAGE_LEVEL`` i do chomhad socruithe agus má bhíonn tú ag "
"brath ar aon cheann de na comhsheasmhainní ionsuite, ní mór duit an modúl "
"comhsheasmhach a allmhairiú go díreach chun an fhéidearthacht allmhairí "
"ciorclach a sheachaint, m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"If desired, you may specify the numeric values for the constants directly "
"according to the values in the above :ref:`constants table <message-level-"
"constants>`."
msgstr ""
"<message-level-constants>Más mian leat, féadfaidh tú na luachanna uimhriúla "
"do na comhsheasmhainní a shonrú go díreach de réir na luachanna sa "
"thuas:ref: `tábla comhsheasmhainne`."

msgid "``MESSAGE_STORAGE``"
msgstr "``TEACHTAIREACHTAÍ STÓRÁLA``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.FallbackStorage'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: "
"``'Django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.fallbackStorage'``"

msgid "Controls where Django stores message data. Valid values are:"
msgstr ""
"Rialuithe áit a stórálann Django sonraí teachtaireachtaí. Is iad na "
"luachanna bailí:"

msgid "``'django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.FallbackStorage'``"
msgstr "```Django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.fallbackstorage'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.messages.storage.session.SessionStorage'``"
msgstr "```Django.Contrib.Messages.Storage.Session.SessionStorage'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.CookieStorage'``"
msgstr "```Django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.cookieIestorage'`"

msgid ""
"See :ref:`message storage backends <message-storage-backends>` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Féach: tagairt: `cúltaca stórála teachtaireachtaí <message-storage-"
"backends>`le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"The backends that use cookies "
"-- :class:`~django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.CookieStorage` "
"and :class:`~django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.FallbackStorage` -- "
"use the value "
"of :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN`, :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE` "
"and :setting:`SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` when setting their cookies."
msgstr ""
"Na cúltaca a úsáideann fianáin --:class: "
"`~django.contrib.messages.storage.cookie.cookieStorage` agus:class: "
"`~django.contrib.messages.storage.fallback.fallbackStorage` -- bain úsáid as "
"luach:setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN`, :setting: "
"`SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE` :setting: `SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` agus a gcuid "
"fianáin á leagan síos agat."

msgid "``MESSAGE_TAGS``"
msgstr "``TAG_TEACHTAIREACHTAÍ ``"

msgid ""
"This sets the mapping of message level to message tag, which is typically "
"rendered as a CSS class in HTML. If you specify a value, it will extend the "
"default. This means you only have to specify those values which you need to "
"override. See :ref:`message-displaying` above for more details."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé seo mapáil leibhéal teachtaireachta go clib teachtaireachta, a "
"léirítear de ghnáth mar rang CSS i HTML. Má shonraíonn tú luach, leathnóidh "
"sé an réamhshocrú. Ciallaíonn sé seo nach gá duit ach na luachanna sin a "
"chaithfidh tú a shárú a shonrú. Féach: Ref: `teachtaireachtaí taispeántaí` "
"thuas le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"If you override ``MESSAGE_TAGS`` in your settings file and rely on any of "
"the built-in constants, you must import the ``constants`` module directly to "
"avoid the potential for circular imports, e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"Má sháraigh tú ``MESSAGE_TAGS`` i do chomhad socruithe agus má bhíonn tú ag "
"brath ar aon cheann de na comhsheasmhainní ionsuite, ní mór duit an modúl "
"``constants` a allmhairiú go díreach chun an fhéidearthacht allmhairí "
"ciorclach a sheachaint, m.sh.:"

msgid "Sessions"
msgstr "Seisiúin"

msgid "Settings for :mod:`django.contrib.sessions`."
msgstr "Socruithe le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.sessions`."

msgid "``SESSION_CACHE_ALIAS``"
msgstr "``SEISIÓN_CACHE_ALIAS``"

msgid ""
"If you're using :ref:`cache-based session storage <cached-sessions-"
"backend>`, this selects the cache to use."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag baint úsáidea:ref: `stóráil seisiúin bunaithe ar taisce <cached-"
"sessions-backend>`, roghnaíonn sé seo an taisce le húsáid."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_AGE``"
msgstr "``SEISIÓN_COOKIE_AOS``"

msgid "Default: ``1209600`` (2 weeks, in seconds)"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``1209600` (2 seachtaine, i soicindí)"

msgid "The age of session cookies, in seconds."
msgstr "Aois na bhfianáin seisiúin, i soicindí."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN``"
msgstr "``SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN``"

msgid ""
"The domain to use for session cookies. Set this to a string such as "
"``\"example.com\"`` for cross-domain cookies, or use ``None`` for a standard "
"domain cookie."
msgstr ""
"An fearainn le húsáid le haghaidh fianáin seisiúin. Socraigh é seo go sreang "
"mar ``\"example.com\"`` le haghaidh fianáin tras-fearainn, nó bain úsáid as "
"``None ``le haghaidh fianán fearainn caighdeánach."

msgid ""
"To use cross-domain cookies with :setting:`CSRF_USE_SESSIONS`, you must "
"include a leading dot (e.g. ``\".example.com\"``) to accommodate the CSRF "
"middleware's referer checking."
msgstr ""
"Chun fianáin tras-fearainn a úsáid la:setting: `CSRF_USE_SESSIONS`, ní mór "
"duit ponc tosaigh a áireamh (m.sh. ``” .example.com\"``) chun freastal ar "
"sheiceáil atreoraithe meán-earraí CSRF."

msgid ""
"Be cautious when updating this setting on a production site. If you update "
"this setting to enable cross-domain cookies on a site that previously used "
"standard domain cookies, existing user cookies will be set to the old "
"domain. This may result in them being unable to log in as long as these "
"cookies persist."
msgstr ""
"Bí cúramach agus an suíomh seo á nuashonrú agat ar shuíomh táirgeachta. Má "
"nuashonraíonn tú an socrú seo chun fianáin tras-fearainn a chumasú ar "
"shuíomh a d'úsáid fianáin fearainn caighdeánacha roimhe seo, socraítear "
"fianáin úsáideora atá ann cheana ar an sean-fhearann D'fhéadfadh sé seo go "
"mbeidh siad in ann logáil isteach chomh fada agus a leanann na fianáin seo."

msgid ""
"This setting also affects cookies set by :mod:`django.contrib.messages`."
msgstr ""
"Bíonn tionchar ag an socrú seo freisin ar fhianáin arna leagan síos ar:mod: "
"`django.contrib.messages`."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY``"
msgstr "``SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use ``HttpOnly`` flag on the session cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, client-side JavaScript will not be able to access the session "
"cookie."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu an bhratach `HttpOnly` a úsáid ar an bhfianán seisiúin. Má tá sé "
"seo socraithe ar ``True``, ní bheidh JavaScript taobh an chliaint in ann "
"rochtain a fháil ar an bhfianán seisiúin."

msgid ""
"HttpOnly_ is a flag included in a Set-Cookie HTTP response header. It's part "
"of the :rfc:`6265#section-4.1.2.6` standard for cookies and can be a useful "
"way to mitigate the risk of a client-side script accessing the protected "
"cookie data."
msgstr ""
"Is bratach é HTTPOnly_ atá san áireamh i gceannteideal freagartha Set-Cookie "
"HTTP. Tá sé mar chuid den chaighdeán:rfc: `6265 #section -4.1.2.6` le "
"haghaidh fianáin agus féadann sé a bheith ina bhealach úsáideach chun an "
"baol go bhfaighidh script taobh an chliaint rochtain ar na sonraí cosanta "
"fianán a mhaolú."

msgid ""
"This makes it less trivial for an attacker to escalate a cross-site "
"scripting vulnerability into full hijacking of a user's session. There "
"aren't many good reasons for turning this off. Your code shouldn't read "
"session cookies from JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Fágann sé seo nach bhfuil sé chomh tábhachtach d'ionsaitheoir leochaileacht "
"scripteála tras-láithreáin a mhéadú go seisiún úsáideora a fhuadach iomlán. "
"Níl go leor cúiseanna maithe ann chun é seo a mhúchadh. Níor chóir do chód "
"fianáin seisiúin a léamh ó JavaScript."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_NAME``"
msgstr "```SESSION_COOKIE_NAME``"

msgid "Default: ``'sessionid'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'seisión``"

msgid ""
"The name of the cookie to use for sessions. This can be whatever you want "
"(as long as it's different from the other cookie names in your application)."
msgstr ""
"Ainm na fianán le húsáid le haghaidh seisiúin. Is féidir leis seo a bheith "
"cibé rud is mian leat (fad is atá sé difriúil ó na hainmneacha fianán eile i "
"d'iarratas)."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_PATH``"
msgstr "``SEISIÓN_COOKIE_PATH``"

msgid ""
"The path set on the session cookie. This should either match the URL path of "
"your Django installation or be parent of that path."
msgstr ""
"An cosán atá leagtha amach ar an bhfianán seisiúin. Ba chóir go n-oireann sé "
"seo cosán URL do shuiteála Django nó a bheith ina thuismitheoir ar an gcosán "
"sin."

msgid ""
"This is useful if you have multiple Django instances running under the same "
"hostname. They can use different cookie paths, and each instance will only "
"see its own session cookie."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo úsáideach má tá cásanna iolracha Django agat ag rith faoin ainm "
"óstach céanna. Is féidir leo cosáin éagsúla fianán a úsáid, agus ní "
"fheicfidh gach cás ach a fhianán seisiúin féin."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE``"
msgstr "``SEISIÓN_FIANÁINE_SAMESITE``"

msgid ""
"The value of the `SameSite`_ flag on the session cookie. This flag prevents "
"the cookie from being sent in cross-site requests thus preventing CSRF "
"attacks and making some methods of stealing session cookie impossible."
msgstr ""
"Luach an bhratach `SameSite`_ ar an bhfianán seisiúin. Cuireann an bratach "
"seo cosc ar an bhfianán a sheoladh isteach in iarratais tras-láithreáin agus "
"mar sin cosc a chur ar ionsaithe CSRF agus rud a fhágann go bhfuil roinnt "
"modhanna chun fianán"

msgid "Possible values for the setting are:"
msgstr "Is iad na luachanna féideartha don socrú:"

msgid ""
"``'Strict'``: prevents the cookie from being sent by the browser to the "
"target site in all cross-site browsing context, even when following a "
"regular link."
msgstr ""
"``'Strict``: cuireann an brabhsálaí cosc ar an bhfianán a sheoladh chuig an "
"spriocshuíomh i ngach comhthéacs brabhsála tras-láithreáin, fiú nuair a "
"bhíonn nasc rialta á leanúint agat."

msgid ""
"For example, for a GitHub-like website this would mean that if a logged-in "
"user follows a link to a private GitHub project posted on a corporate "
"discussion forum or email, GitHub will not receive the session cookie and "
"the user won't be able to access the project. A bank website, however, most "
"likely doesn't want to allow any transactional pages to be linked from "
"external sites so the ``'Strict'`` flag would be appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, do shuíomh Gréasáin cosúil le GitHub chiallódh sé seo má "
"leanann úsáideoir logáilte nasc chuig tionscadal príobháideach GitHub a "
"chuirtear ar fhóram plé corparáideach nó ríomhphost, ní gheobhaidh GitHub an "
"fianán seisiúin agus ní bheidh an t-úsáideoir in ann rochtain a fháil ar an "
"tionscadal. Is dóichí nach bhfuil suíomh Gréasáin bainc ag iarraidh cead a "
"cheadú aon leathanaigh idirghníomhaíochta a nascadh ó shuíomhanna "
"seachtracha mar sin bheadh an bhratach ``Strict`` oiriúnach."

msgid ""
"``'Lax'`` (default): provides a balance between security and usability for "
"websites that want to maintain user's logged-in session after the user "
"arrives from an external link."
msgstr ""
"``'Lax'`` (réamhshocraithe): soláthraíonn cothromaíocht idir slándáil agus "
"inúsáidteacht do shuíomhanna gréasáin atá ag iarraidh seisiún logáilte "
"isteach an úsáideora a choinneáil tar éis don úsáideoir teacht ó nasc "
"seachtrach."

msgid ""
"In the GitHub scenario, the session cookie would be allowed when following a "
"regular link from an external website and be blocked in CSRF-prone request "
"methods (e.g. ``POST``)."
msgstr ""
"Sa chás GitHub, ceadaíodh an fianán seisiúin nuair a leanfaí nasc rialta ó "
"shuíomh Gréasáin seachtrach agus cuirfí bac ar mhodhanna iarratais CSRF "
"(m.sh. `POST ``)."

msgid ""
"``'None'`` (string): the session cookie will be sent with all same-site and "
"cross-site requests."
msgstr ""
"```None'`` (teaghrán): seolfar an fianán seisiúin le gach iarratas ar an "
"láithreán céanna agus tras-láithreán."

msgid "``False``: disables the flag."
msgstr "``False``: díchumasaíonn an bratach."

msgid ""
"Modern browsers provide a more secure default policy for the ``SameSite`` "
"flag and will assume ``Lax`` for cookies without an explicit value set."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn brabhsálaithe nua-aimseartha beartas réamhshocraithe níos "
"sábháilte don bhratach ``SameSite`` agus glacfaidh siad le ``Lax`` le "
"haghaidh fianáin gan luach follasach soiléir."

msgid "``SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE``"
msgstr "``SEISIÚN_FIANÁIN SHÁBHÁILTE``"

msgid ""
"Whether to use a secure cookie for the session cookie. If this is set to "
"``True``, the cookie will be marked as \"secure\", which means browsers may "
"ensure that the cookie is only sent under an HTTPS connection."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu fianán slán a úsáid don fhianán seisiúin. Má tá sé seo socraithe ar "
"``True``, marcálfar an fianán mar “slán”, rud a chiallaíonn go bhféadfaidh "
"brabhsálaithe a chinntiú nach seoltar an fianán ach faoi nasc HTTPS."

msgid ""
"Leaving this setting off isn't a good idea because an attacker could capture "
"an unencrypted session cookie with a packet sniffer and use the cookie to "
"hijack the user's session."
msgstr ""
"Ní smaoineamh maith é an socrú seo a fhágáil mar d'fhéadfadh ionsaitheoir "
"fianán seisiúin neamhchriptithe a ghabháil le sniffer paicéad agus an fianán "
"a úsáid chun seisiún an úsáideora a fhuadadh."

msgid "``SESSION_ENGINE``"
msgstr "``INNEAL_SEISIÚNA``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.db'``"
msgstr "Réamhshocraithe: ``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.db'``"

msgid "Controls where Django stores session data. Included engines are:"
msgstr ""
"Rialuithe ina stórálann Django sonraí seisiúin. Is iad na hinnill san "
"áireamh:"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.db'``"
msgstr "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.db'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.file'``"
msgstr "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.file'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache'``"
msgstr "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.cache'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db'``"
msgstr "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.cached_db'``"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.signed_cookies'``"
msgstr "``'django.contrib.sessions.backends.signed_cookies'``"

msgid "See :ref:`configuring-sessions` for more details."
msgstr "Féach: ref: `seisiúin cumraitheach` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "``SESSION_EXPIRE_AT_BROWSER_CLOSE``"
msgstr "``SEISIÚIN_DEIGH_AT_BRABHSÁLAÍ_DÚNTA ``"

msgid ""
"Whether to expire the session when the user closes their browser. "
"See :ref:`browser-length-vs-persistent-sessions`."
msgstr ""
"Cibé an rachaidh an seisiún in éag nuair a dhúnn an úsáideoir a bhrabhsála "
"Féach:ref: `brabhsálaí-length-vs-seisiúin persistent-s`."

msgid "``SESSION_FILE_PATH``"
msgstr "``SESSION_FILE_PATH``"

msgid ""
"If you're using file-based session storage, this sets the directory in which "
"Django will store session data. When the default value (``None``) is used, "
"Django will use the standard temporary directory for the system."
msgstr ""
"Má tá stóráil seisiúin comhadbhunaithe á úsáid agat, socraíonn sé seo an "
"eolaire ina stóráilfidh Django sonraí seisiúin. Nuair a úsáidtear an luach "
"réamhshocraithe (``None ``), úsáidfidh Django an eolaire sealadach "
"caighdeánach don chóras."

msgid "``SESSION_SAVE_EVERY_REQUEST``"
msgstr "``SEISIÚN_SÁBHA_GACH IARRAT``"

msgid ""
"Whether to save the session data on every request. If this is ``False`` "
"(default), then the session data will only be saved if it has been modified "
"-- that is, if any of its dictionary values have been assigned or deleted. "
"Empty sessions won't be created, even if this setting is active."
msgstr ""
"Cibé acu sonraí an tseisiúin a shábháil ar gach iarratas. Más é seo "
"``False`` (réamhshocraithe), ansin ní shábhálfar sonraí an tseisiúin ach má "
"tá siad modhnaithe - is é sin, má shanntar nó scriosadh aon cheann dá "
"luachanna foclóra. Ní chruthófar seisiúin folamh, fiú má tá an suíomh seo "
"gníomhach."

msgid "``SESSION_SERIALIZER``"
msgstr "``SESSION_SERIALIZER``"

msgid "Default: ``'django.contrib.sessions.serializers.JSONSerializer'``"
msgstr ""
"Réamhshocraithe: ``'Django.contrib.sessions.serializers.jsonSerializer'``"

msgid ""
"Full import path of a serializer class to use for serializing session data. "
"Included serializer is:"
msgstr ""
"Conair iomlán iompórtála ranga serializer le húsáid chun sonraí seisiúin a "
"shraitheadh. Is é an sraitheoir san áireamh:"

msgid "``'django.contrib.sessions.serializers.JSONSerializer'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Contrib.Sessions.Serializers.JSONSerializer'``"

msgid "See :ref:`session_serialization` for details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `session_serialization` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Sites"
msgstr "Suíomhanna"

msgid "Settings for :mod:`django.contrib.sites`."
msgstr "Socruithe le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.sites`."

msgid "``SITE_ID``"
msgstr "``ID_LÁITHREACH``"

msgid ""
"The ID, as an integer, of the current site in the ``django_site`` database "
"table. This is used so that application data can hook into specific sites "
"and a single database can manage content for multiple sites."
msgstr ""
"An ID, mar shláimhir, an láithreáin reatha sa tábla bunachar sonraí "
"``django_site``. Úsáidtear é seo ionas gur féidir le sonraí feidhmchláir dul "
"isteach i suíomhanna ar leith agus gur féidir le bunachar sonraí amháin "
"ábhar a bhainistiú do shuíomhanna iolr"

msgid "Static Files"
msgstr "Comhaid Statach"

msgid "Settings for :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles`."
msgstr "Socruithe le haghaidh: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles`."

msgid "``STATIC_ROOT``"
msgstr "``FRÉAMH_STATIC``"

msgid ""
"The absolute path to the directory where :djadmin:`collectstatic` will "
"collect static files for deployment."
msgstr ""
"An cosán iomlán chuig an eolaire ina mbailfidh: djadmin: `collectstatic` "
"comhaid statacha le haghaidh imscartha."

msgid "Example: ``\"/var/www/example.com/static/\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``” /var/www/example.com/static/\"``"

msgid ""
"If the :doc:`staticfiles</ref/contrib/staticfiles>` contrib app is enabled "
"(as in the default project template), the :djadmin:`collectstatic` "
"management command will collect static files into this directory. See the "
"how-to on :doc:`managing static files</howto/static-files/index>` for more "
"details about usage."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an aip contrib: doc: `staticfiles` cumasaithe (mar atá sa te@@</ref/"
"contrib/staticfiles> impléad réamhshocraithe tionscadail), baileoidh an t-"
"ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` comhaid statacha san eolaire "
"seo. Féach an conas ar: doc: `comhaid statacha a bhainistiú' le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí faoin úsáid .</howto/static-files/index>"

msgid ""
"This should be an initially empty destination directory for collecting your "
"static files from their permanent locations into one directory for ease of "
"deployment; it is **not** a place to store your static files permanently. "
"You should do that in directories that will be found by :doc:`staticfiles</"
"ref/contrib/staticfiles>`’s :setting:`finders<STATICFILES_FINDERS>`, which "
"by default, are ``'static/'`` app sub-directories and any directories you "
"include in :setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS`)."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh sé seo ina eolaire ceann scríbe folamh i dtosach chun do "
"chuid comhad statacha a bhailiú óna n-áiteanna buana isteach i eolaire "
"amháin chun éasca a imscaradh; ní** áit é chun do chuid comhad statacha a "
"stóráil go buan. Ba chóir duit é sin a dhéanamh in eolairí a "
"gheobhaidh: :doc: `staticfiles`'s:setting: `finders `</ref/contrib/"
"staticfiles><STATICFILES_FINDERS>, atá de réir réamhshocraithe, fo-eolairí "
"aip ``static/'`` agus aon eolairí a chuimsíonn tú in:setting: "
"`STATICFILES_DIRS`)."

msgid "``STATIC_URL``"
msgstr "``STATIC_URL ``"

msgid ""
"URL to use when referring to static files located in :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`."
msgstr ""
"URL le húsáid agus tú ag tagairt do chomhaid statacha atá suite in:setting: "
"`STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid "Example: ``\"static/\"`` or ``\"https://static.example.com/\"``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``\"statach/\"`` nó ``” https://static.example.com/ “``"

msgid ""
"If not ``None``, this will be used as the base path for :ref:`asset "
"definitions<form-asset-paths>` (the ``Media`` class) and "
"the :doc:`staticfiles app</ref/contrib/staticfiles>`."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ``None``, úsáidfear é seo mar bhonn cosán le haghaidh: ref: "
"`sainmhínithe sócmhainní</ref/contrib/staticfiles> <form-asset-paths>`(an "
"rang ``Meáin ``) agus an aip: doc: `staticfiles`."

msgid "It must end in a slash if set to a non-empty value."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh sé deireadh a chur le slasc má tá sé socraithe ar luach neamh-"
"folamh."

msgid ""
"You may need to :ref:`configure these files to be served in development "
"<serving-static-files-in-development>` and will definitely need to do "
"so :doc:`in production </howto/static-files/deployment>`."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go mbeidh ort: ref: `na comhaid seo a chumrú le seirbheáil i "
"bhforbairt </howto/static-files/deployment> <serving-static-files-in-"
"development>`agus is cinnte go mbeidh ort é sin a dhéanamh: doc: `i "
"dtáirgeadh`."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`STATIC_URL` is a relative path, then it will be prefixed by the "
"server-provided value of ``SCRIPT_NAME`` (or ``/`` if not set). This makes "
"it easier to serve a Django application in a subpath without adding an extra "
"configuration to the settings."
msgstr ""
"Más: Socrú: Is cosán coibhneasta é `STATIC_URL`, ansin déanfar é a "
"réamhshocrú ag an luach ``SCRIPT_NAME`` a sholáthraíonn an freastalaí (nó ``/"
"`` mura bhfuil sé socraithe). Fágann sé seo go bhfuil sé níos éasca "
"feidhmchlár Django a sheirbheáil i bhfochonair gan cumraíocht bhreise a chur "
"leis na socruithe."

msgid "``STATICFILES_DIRS``"
msgstr "``COMHAD STATIC_DIRS``"

msgid ""
"This setting defines the additional locations the staticfiles app will "
"traverse if the ``FileSystemFinder`` finder is enabled, e.g. if you use "
"the :djadmin:`collectstatic` or :djadmin:`findstatic` management command or "
"use the static file serving view."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an socrú seo na suíomhanna breise a thrasnóidh an aip "
"staticfiles má chumasaítear an aimsitheoir ``FilesystemFinder``, m.sh. má "
"úsáideann tú an ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` nó: djadmin: "
"`findstatic` nó má úsáideann tú an radharc statach a sheirbheáil."

msgid ""
"This should be set to a list of strings that contain full paths to your "
"additional files directory(ies) e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir é seo a shocrú ar liosta teaghráin ina bhfuil cosáin iomlána chuig "
"d'eolaire (í) comhaid bhreise m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"Note that these paths should use Unix-style forward slashes, even on Windows "
"(e.g. ``\"C:/Users/user/mysite/extra_static_content\"``)."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur chóir go n-úsáidfeadh na cosáin seo sliotáin ar "
"aghaidh i stíl Unix, fiú ar Windows (m.sh. ``\"C: /Users/User/MySite/"
"Extra_Static_Content\"``)."

msgid "Prefixes (optional)"
msgstr "Réamhréamhacha (roghnach)"

msgid ""
"In case you want to refer to files in one of the locations with an "
"additional namespace, you can **optionally** provide a prefix as ``(prefix, "
"path)`` tuples, e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"Sa chás gur mhaith leat tagairt a dhéanamh do chomhaid i gceann de na "
"háiteanna le spás ainmneacha breise, is féidir leat**go roghnaí** réimír a "
"sholáthar mar thuples ``(réimír, cosán)``, m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"For example, assuming you have :setting:`STATIC_URL` set to ``'static/'``, "
"the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command would collect the \"stats\" "
"files in a ``'downloads'`` subdirectory of :setting:`STATIC_ROOT`."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ag glacadh leis go bhfuil: setting: `STATIC_URL` socraithe agat "
"go ``'static/'``, baileodh an t-ordú bainistíochta: djadmin: `collectstatic` "
"na comhaid “stats” i bhfo-eolaire ``'downloads'`` de:setting: `STATIC_ROOT`."

msgid ""
"This would allow you to refer to the local file ``'/opt/webfiles/stats/"
"polls_20101022.tar.gz'`` with ``'/static/downloads/polls_20101022.tar.gz'`` "
"in your templates, e.g.:"
msgstr ""
"Ligfeadh sé seo duit tagairt a dhéanamh don chomhad áitiúil ```'/opt/"
"webfiles/stats/polls_20101022.tar.gz'`` le ``'/static/downloads/"
"polls_20101022.tar.gz'` i do theimpléid, m.sh.:"

msgid "``STATICFILES_FINDERS``"
msgstr "``AIMSITHEOIRÍ COMHAID STATAICE``"

msgid ""
"The list of finder backends that know how to find static files in various "
"locations."
msgstr ""
"Liosta na gcúltaca aimsitheora a bhfuil a fhios acu conas comhaid statacha a "
"aimsiú in áiteanna éagsúla."

msgid ""
"The default will find files stored in the :setting:`STATICFILES_DIRS` "
"setting (using ``django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.FileSystemFinder``) and "
"in a ``static`` subdirectory of each app (using "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.AppDirectoriesFinder``). If multiple "
"files with the same name are present, the first file that is found will be "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Gheobhaidh an réamhshocrú comhaid atá stóráilte sa socrú:setting: "
"`STATICFILES_DIRS` (ag baint úsáide as "
"``Django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.filesystemfinder``) agus i bhfo-eolaire "
"`static`` de gach aip (ag baint úsáide as "
"``Django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.appDirectoriesFinder``). Má tá comhad "
"iolracha leis an ainm céanna i láthair, úsáidfear an chéad chomhad a "
"fhaightear."

msgid ""
"One finder is disabled by default: "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.DefaultStorageFinder``. If added to "
"your :setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS` setting, it will look for static files "
"in the default file storage as defined by the ``default`` key in "
"the :setting:`STORAGES` setting."
msgstr ""
"Tá aimsitheoir amháin díchumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe: "
"``Django.contrib.staticfiles.finders.defaultStorageFinder``. Má chuirtear le "
"do shuíomh:: `STATICFILES_FINDERS`, cuardóidh sé comhaid statacha sa stóráil "
"comhaid réamhshocraithe mar a shainmhínítear leis an eochair ``default`` sa "
"socrú: `STORAGES`."

msgid ""
"When using the ``AppDirectoriesFinder`` finder, make sure your apps can be "
"found by staticfiles by adding the app to the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"setting of your site."
msgstr ""
"Agus an aimsitheoir ``AppDirectoriesFinder` á úsáid agat, déan cinnte gur "
"féidir do chuid aipeanna a aimsiú trí staticfiles tríd an aip a chur leis an "
"socrú: `INSTALLED_APPS` ar do shuíomh."

msgid ""
"Static file finders are currently considered a private interface, and this "
"interface is thus undocumented."
msgstr ""
"Meastar go bhfuil aimsitheoirí comhad statacha ina chomhéadan príobháideach "
"faoi láthair, agus mar sin níl an comhéadan seo gan doiciméadú"

