msgid ""
"A list of all the signals that Django sends. All built-in signals are sent "
"using the :meth:`~django.dispatch.Signal.send` method."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na comharthaí go léir a sheolann Django. Seoltar na comharthaí "
"ionsuite go léir ag baint úsáide as an modh: meth: "
"`~django.dispch.signal.send`."

msgid ""
"See the documentation on the :doc:`signal dispatcher </topics/signals>` for "
"information regarding how to register for and receive signals."
msgstr ""
"Féach an doiciméadú ara:doc: `seoltóir comhartha` le haghaidh faisnéise "
"maidir le con</topics/signals> as clárú le haghaidh comharthaí agus a fháil."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`authentication framework </topics/auth/index>` sends :ref:`signals "
"when a user is logged in / out <topics-auth-signals>`."
msgstr ""
"</topics/auth/index> <topics-auth-signals>Seolann an:doc: `creat "
"fíordheimhniúcháin`: ref: `comharthaí nuair a bhíonn úsáideoir logáilte "
"isteach/amach `."

msgid "Model signals"
msgstr "Comharthaí múnla"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.db.models.signals` module defines a set of signals sent by "
"the model system."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an modúl:MOD: `django.db.models.signals` sraith comharthaí a "
"sheolann an córas samhail."

msgid ""
"Signals can make your code harder to maintain. Consider implementing a "
"helper method on a :ref:`custom manager <custom-managers>`, to both update "
"your models and perform additional logic, or else :ref:`overriding model "
"methods <overriding-model-methods>` before using model signals."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le comharthaí do chód a dhéanamh níos deacra a chothabháil. "
"<overriding-model-methods>Smaoinigh ar mhodh cúntóra a <custom-managers>chur "
"i bhfeidhm ar a:ref: `bainisteoir saincheapaithe`, chun do mhúnlaí a "
"nuashonrú agus loighic bhreise a dhéanamh, nó eile: ref: `modhanna samhail "
"forchoitianta `sula n-úsáidtear comharthaí samhail."

msgid ""
"Many of these signals are sent by various model methods like ``__init__()`` "
"or :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` that you can override in your own "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar go leor de na comharthaí seo trí mhodhanna samhail éagsúla mar "
"``__init__ () ``nó:meth: `~django.db.models.model.save` ar féidir leat "
"athshlánú i do chód féin."

msgid ""
"If you override these methods on your model, you must call the parent class' "
"methods for these signals to be sent."
msgstr ""
"Má sháraíonn tú na modhanna seo ar do mhúnla, ní mór duit modhanna an ranga "
"tuismitheora a ghlaoch chun na comharthaí seo a sheoladh."

msgid ""
"Note also that Django stores signal handlers as weak references by default, "
"so if your handler is a local function, it may be garbage collected.  To "
"prevent this, pass ``weak=False`` when you call the "
"signal's :meth:`~django.dispatch.Signal.connect`."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin go stórálann Django láimhseálaithe comhartha mar "
"thagairtí laga de réir réamhshocraithe, mar sin más feidhm áitiúil é do "
"láimhseálaí, d'fhéadfadh sé a bheith bailithe truflais. Chun é seo a chosc, "
"pas ``Weak = False`` nuair a ghlaonn tú ar an comhartha`s:meth: "
"`~Django.Dispatch.Signal.Connect`."

msgid ""
"Model signals ``sender`` model can be lazily referenced when connecting a "
"receiver by specifying its full application label. For example, an "
"``Question`` model defined in the ``polls`` application could be referenced "
"as ``'polls.Question'``. This sort of reference can be quite handy when "
"dealing with circular import dependencies and swappable models."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir tagairt a dhéanamh go leisciúil do chomharthaí samhail “seoltóir” "
"agus glacadóir á nascadh trína lipéad feidhmchláir iomlán a shonrú. Mar "
"shampla, d'fhéadfaí tagairt a thabhairt do mhúnla ``Ceiste`` a "
"shainmhínítear san fheidhmchlár ``polls`` mar ``Polls.question'``. Is féidir "
"leis an gcineál tagartha seo a bheith áisiúil go leor agus tú ag déileáil le "
"spleáchais iompórtála ciorclacha agus samhlacha inmhal"

msgid "``pre_init``"
msgstr "``Pre_init``"

msgid ""
"Whenever you instantiate a Django model, this signal is sent at the "
"beginning of the model's ``__init__()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Aon uair a chuireann tú samhail Django, seoltar an comhartha seo ag tús modh "
"``__init__ () ``an tsamhail."

msgid "The model class that just had an instance created."
msgstr "Cruthaíodh an rang samhail nach raibh ach sampla ann."

msgid "``args``"
msgstr "``args``"

msgid "A list of positional arguments passed to ``__init__()``."
msgstr "Liosta de na hargóintí seasaimh a chuirtear chuig ``__init__ () ``."

msgid "``kwargs``"
msgstr "```Kwargs``"

msgid "A dictionary of keyword arguments passed to ``__init__()``."
msgstr "Cuireadh foclóir argóintí eochairfhocal chuig ``__init__ () ``."

msgid "For example, the :doc:`tutorial </intro/tutorial02>` has this line::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, tá an líne seo ag an:doc: `teagorial</intro/tutorial02> `:"

msgid "The arguments sent to a :data:`pre_init` handler would be:"
msgstr ""
"Is iad seo a leanas na hargóintí a sheoladh chuig a:data: `pre_init` "
"láimhseálaí:"

msgid "``Question`` (the class itself)"
msgstr "``Ceist ``(an rang féin)"

msgid ""
"``[]`` (an empty list because there were no positional arguments passed to "
"``__init__()``)"
msgstr ""
"``[]`` (liosta folamh toisc nach raibh aon argóintí seasaimh ann chuig "
"``__init__ () ``)"

msgid ""
"``{'question_text': \"What's new?\",`` ``'pub_date': datetime.datetime(2012, "
"2, 26, 13, 0, 0, 775217, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}``"
msgstr ""
"``{'question_text': “Cad atá nua?” , ``````pub_date': datetime.datetime "
"(2012, 2, 26, 13, 0, 0, 775217, tzinfo = datetime.timezone.UTC)}``"

msgid "``post_init``"
msgstr "``post_init``"

msgid ""
"Like pre_init, but this one is sent when the ``__init__()`` method finishes."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le pre_init, ach seoltar an ceann seo nuair a chríochnaíonn an modh "
"``__init__ () ``."

msgid "As above: the model class that just had an instance created."
msgstr "Mar atá thuas: an rang samhail nach raibh ach sampla cruthaithe aige."

msgid "The actual instance of the model that's just been created."
msgstr "An sampla iarbhír den tsamhail atá díreach cruthaithe."

msgid ""
":attr:`instance._state <django.db.models.Model._state>` isn't set before "
"sending the ``post_init`` signal, so ``_state`` attributes always have their "
"default values. For example, ``_state.db`` is ``None``."
msgstr ""
":attr: `sampla. Ní shocraítear _state <django.db.models.Model._state>`sula "
"seoltar an comhartha ``post_init``, mar sin bíonn a luachanna "
"réamhshocraithe i gcónaí ag tréithe ``_state``. Mar shampla, is é "
"``_state.db`` ``None``."

msgid ""
"For performance reasons, you shouldn't perform queries in receivers of "
"``pre_init`` or ``post_init`` signals because they would be executed for "
"each instance returned during queryset iteration."
msgstr ""
"Ar chúiseanna feidhmíochta, níor cheart duit fiosrúcháin a dhéanamh i "
"nglacadóirí comharthaí ``pre_init`` nó `post_init`` toisc go ndéanfaí iad a "
"fhorghníomhú do gach cás a chuirtear ar ais le linn athraithe ceisteanna."

msgid "``pre_save``"
msgstr "``Pre_save``"

msgid ""
"This is sent at the beginning of a "
"model's :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` method."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar é seo ag tús modh samhail 's:meth: `~django.db.models.model.save`."

msgid "The model class."
msgstr "An rang samhail."

msgid "The actual instance being saved."
msgstr "An cás iarbhír á shábháil."

msgid "``raw``"
msgstr "```raw``"

msgid ""
"A boolean; ``True`` if the model is saved exactly as presented (i.e. when "
"loading a :ref:`fixture <fixtures-explanation>`). One should not query/"
"modify other records in the database as the database might not be in a "
"consistent state yet."
msgstr ""
"<fixtures-explanation>Boolean; ``True`` má shábháiltear an tsamhail go "
"díreach mar a chuirtear i láthair (ie agus a: ref: `daingneán `á luchtú). "
"Níor chóir taifid eile sa bhunachar sonraí a fhiosrú/a mhodhnú mar b'fhéidir "
"nach mbeadh an bunachar sonraí i riocht comhsheasmhach fós."

msgid "The database alias being used."
msgstr "An ailias bunachar sonraí atá á n-úsáid."

msgid "``update_fields``"
msgstr "``réimsí nuashonraithe``"

msgid ""
"The set of fields to update as passed to :meth:`.Model.save`, or ``None`` if "
"``update_fields`` wasn't passed to ``save()``."
msgstr ""
"An tacar réimsí le nuashonrú mar a chuirtear chuig: meth: `.model.save`, nó "
"``None`` mura ritheadh ``update_fields`` chuig `save () ``."

msgid "``post_save``"
msgstr "``post_save``"

msgid ""
"Like :data:`pre_save`, but sent at the end of "
"the :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` method."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: data: `pre_save`, ach seoltar ag deireadh an modh:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.save`."

msgid "``created``"
msgstr "``cruthaithe``"

msgid "A boolean; ``True`` if a new record was created."
msgstr "A boolean; ``True`` má cruthaíodh taifead nua."

msgid "``pre_delete``"
msgstr "``pre_scrios``"

msgid ""
"Sent at the beginning of a model's :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.delete` "
"method and a queryset's :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Seoladh ag tús modh samhail's:meth: `~django.db.models.model.delete` agus "
"modh ceisteanna 's:meth: `~django.db.models.query.queryset.delete`."

msgid "The actual instance being deleted."
msgstr "An cás iarbhír á scriosadh."

msgid ""
"The ``Model`` or ``QuerySet`` instance from which the deletion originated, "
"that is, the instance whose ``delete()`` method was invoked."
msgstr ""

msgid "``post_delete``"
msgstr "``post_delete``"

msgid ""
"Like :data:`pre_delete`, but sent at the end of a "
"model's :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.delete` method and a "
"queryset's :meth:`~django.db.models.query.QuerySet.delete` method."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le: data: `pre_delete`, ach seoltar ag deireadh samhail's:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.delete` modh agus modh queryset's:meth: "
"`~django.db.models.queryset.delete`."

msgid ""
"Note that the object will no longer be in the database, so be very careful "
"what you do with this instance."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach mbeidh an réad sa bhunachar sonraí a thuilleadh, mar "
"sin bí an-chúramach cad a dhéanann tú leis an gcás seo."

msgid "``m2m_changed``"
msgstr "``m2m_athraithe``"

msgid ""
"Sent when a :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` is changed on a model "
"instance. Strictly speaking, this is not a model signal since it is sent by "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`, but since it complements "
"the :data:`pre_save`/:data:`post_save` "
"and :data:`pre_delete`/:data:`post_delete` when it comes to tracking changes "
"to models, it is included here."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar nuair a athraítear a:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` ar "
"shampla samhail. Go docht, ní comhartha samhail é seo ós rud é go seolann "
"an: class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField` é, ach ós rud é go "
"gcomhlíonann sé an:data: `pre_save`/:data: `post_save` agus:data: "
"`pre_delete`/:data: `post_delete` maidir le hathruithe ar mhúnlaí a rianú, "
"tá sé san áireamh anseo."

msgid ""
"The intermediate model class describing "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`. This class is automatically "
"created when a many-to-many field is defined; you can access it using the "
"``through`` attribute on the many-to-many field."
msgstr ""
"An rang samhail idirmheánach ag cur síos ar:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField`. Cruthaítear an rang seo go "
"huathoibríoch nuair a shainmhínítear réimse go leor; is féidir leat rochtain "
"a fháil air ag baint úsáide as an tréith ``trí ``ar an réimse go leor."

msgid ""
"The instance whose many-to-many relation is updated. This can be an instance "
"of the ``sender``, or of the class "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField` is related to."
msgstr ""
"An cás a nuashonraítear a gcaidreamh go leor le go leor. Is féidir seo a "
"bheith ina shampla den ``seoltóir`, nó den rang a bhaineann le:class: "
"`~django.db.models.manyToManyField`."

msgid "``action``"
msgstr "``Gníomha``"

msgid ""
"A string indicating the type of update that is done on the relation. This "
"can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""
"Sreang a léiríonn an cineál nuashonraithe a dhéantar ar an ngaol. Is féidir "
"seo a bheith ar cheann de na nithe seo a leanas:"

msgid "``\"pre_add\"``"
msgstr "``\"pre_add “``"

msgid "Sent *before* one or more objects are added to the relation."
msgstr "Seoltaí* roimh* cuirtear réad amháin nó níos mó leis an ngaol."

msgid "``\"post_add\"``"
msgstr "``\"post_add “``"

msgid "Sent *after* one or more objects are added to the relation."
msgstr "Seoltaí* tar éis * cuirtear réad amháin nó níos mó leis an ngaol."

msgid "``\"pre_remove\"``"
msgstr "``\"réamh_bhaint” ``"

msgid "Sent *before* one or more objects are removed from the relation."
msgstr "Seoltaí* roimh* baintear réad amháin nó níos mó ón gcaidreamh."

msgid "``\"post_remove\"``"
msgstr "``\"post_remove\"``"

msgid "Sent *after* one or more objects are removed from the relation."
msgstr "Seoltaí* tar éis * baintear réad amháin nó níos mó ón gcaidreamh."

msgid "``\"pre_clear\"``"
msgstr "``\"réamh-ghlanaire\"``"

msgid "Sent *before* the relation is cleared."
msgstr "Seoltaí* roimh* glanfar an gaol."

msgid "``\"post_clear\"``"
msgstr "``\"post_clear\"``"

msgid "Sent *after* the relation is cleared."
msgstr "Seoltaí* ina dhiaithe* glantar an gaol."

msgid ""
"Indicates which side of the relation is updated (i.e., if it is the forward "
"or reverse relation that is being modified)."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn sé cén taobh den chaidreamh a nuashonraítear (ie, más é an gaol "
"tosaigh nó droim atá á mhodhnú)."

msgid ""
"The class of the objects that are added to, removed from or cleared from the "
"relation."
msgstr ""
"Aicme na rudaí a chuirtear leis an gcaidreamh, a bhaintear uaidh nó a "
"ghlantar uaidh."

msgid "``pk_set``"
msgstr "``pk_set``"

msgid ""
"For the ``pre_add`` and ``post_add`` actions, this is a set of primary key "
"values that will be, or have been, added to the relation. This may be a "
"subset of the values submitted to be added, since inserts must filter "
"existing values in order to avoid a database ``IntegrityError``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis na gníomhartha ``pre_add`` agus ``post_add``, is sraith "
"príomhluachanna é seo a chuirfear leis an ngaol nó a chuirfear leis an "
"ngaol. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a bheith ina fho-thacar de na luachanna a "
"chuirtear isteach le cur leis, ós rud é go gcaithfidh iontráil luachanna atá "
"ann cheana a scagadh d'fhonn bunachar sonraí ``IntegrityError`` a sheachaint."

msgid ""
"For the ``pre_remove`` and ``post_remove`` actions, this is a set of primary "
"key values that was submitted to be removed from the relation. This is not "
"dependent on whether the values actually will be, or have been, removed. In "
"particular, non-existent values may be submitted, and will appear in "
"``pk_set``, even though they have no effect on the database."
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis na gníomhartha ``pre_remove`` agus ``post_remove``, is sraith de "
"phríomhluachanna é seo a cuireadh isteach le fáil a bhaint as an ngaol. Ní "
"bhíonn sé seo ag brath ar cibé an mbainfear na luachanna i ndáiríre, nó an "
"ndearnadh na luachanna bainte. Go háirithe, féadfar luachanna nach bhfuil "
"ann a chur isteach, agus beidh siad le feiceáil in `pk_set``, cé nach bhfuil "
"aon éifeacht acu ar an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid "For the ``pre_clear`` and ``post_clear`` actions, this is ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis na gníomhartha ``pre_clear`` agus ``post_clear``, is é seo "
"``None``."

msgid ""
"For example, if a ``Pizza`` can have multiple ``Topping`` objects, modeled "
"like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, más féidir le ``Pizza`` rudaí iolracha ``Topping ``a bheith "
"aige, samhaltaithe mar seo:"

msgid "If we connected a handler like this::"
msgstr "Má cheangail muid láimhseálaí mar seo:"

msgid "and then did something like this:"
msgstr "agus ansin rinne rud éigin mar seo:"

msgid ""
"the arguments sent to a :data:`m2m_changed` handler (``toppings_changed`` in "
"the example above) would be:"
msgstr ""
"is iad na hargóintí a sheoltar chuig a:data: `m2m_changed` handler "
"(``toppings_changed`` sa sampla thuas):"

msgid "``Pizza.toppings.through`` (the intermediate m2m class)"
msgstr "``Pizza.Toppings.Through ``(an rang idirmheánach m2m)"

msgid "``p`` (the ``Pizza`` instance being modified)"
msgstr "``p`` (an cás ``Pizza`` á mhodhnú)"

msgid "``\"pre_add\"`` (followed by a separate signal with ``\"post_add\"``)"
msgstr ""
"``\"pre_add\"`` (ina dhiaidh sin comhartha ar leithligh le ``\"post_add\"``)"

msgid ""
"``False`` (``Pizza`` contains "
"the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`, so this call modifies the "
"forward relation)"
msgstr ""
"``False`` (`Pizza`` tá an: aicme: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`, mar "
"sin athraíonn an glao seo an gaol tosaigh)"

msgid "``Topping`` (the class of the objects added to the ``Pizza``)"
msgstr "``Topping`` (aicme na rudaí a chuirtear leis an ``Pizza``)"

msgid "``{t.id}`` (since only ``Topping t`` was added to the relation)"
msgstr "``{t.id}`` (ós rud é nach cuireadh ach ``Topping t`` leis an ngaol)"

msgid "``\"default\"`` (since the default router sends writes here)"
msgstr ""
"``\"réamhshocraithe\"`` (ós rud é go seolann an ródaire réamhshocraithe "
"scríobhann anseo)"

msgid "And if we would then do something like this:"
msgstr "Agus dá ndéanfaimis rud éigin mar seo ansin:"

msgid "the arguments sent to a :data:`m2m_changed` handler would be:"
msgstr ""
"is iad na hargóintí a sheoltar chuig a:data: `m2m_changed` láimhseálaí:"

msgid "``t`` (the ``Topping`` instance being modified)"
msgstr "``t`` (an cás ``Topping`` á mhodhnú)"

msgid ""
"``\"pre_remove\"`` (followed by a separate signal with ``\"post_remove\"``)"
msgstr ""
"``\"pre_remove\"`` (ina dhiaidh sin comhartha ar leithligh le "
"``\"post_remove\"``)"

msgid ""
"``True`` (``Pizza`` contains the :class:`~django.db.models.ManyToManyField`, "
"so this call modifies the reverse relation)"
msgstr ""
"``True`` (`Pizza`` tá sean:class: `~django.db.models.manyToManyField`, mar "
"sin athraíonn an glao seo an gaol droim)"

msgid "``Pizza`` (the class of the objects removed from the ``Topping``)"
msgstr "``Pizza`` (aicme na rudaí a bhaintear ón ``Topping``)"

msgid "``{p.id}`` (since only ``Pizza p`` was removed from the relation)"
msgstr "``{p.id}`` (ós rud é nach baineadh ach `Pizza p`` ón gcaidreamh)"

msgid "``class_prepared``"
msgstr "``rang_ullmhaithe``"

msgid ""
"Sent whenever a model class has been \"prepared\" -- that is, once a model "
"has been defined and registered with Django's model system. Django uses this "
"signal internally; it's not generally used in third-party applications."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar aon uair a ullmhaíodh rang samhail - is é sin, nuair a bheidh "
"samhail sainmhínithe agus cláraithe le córas samhail Django. Úsáideann "
"Django an comhartha seo go hinmheánach; ní úsáidtear é i bhfeidhmchláir tríú "
"páirtí"

msgid ""
"Since this signal is sent during the app registry population process, "
"and :meth:`AppConfig.ready() <django.apps.AppConfig.ready>` runs after the "
"app registry is fully populated, receivers cannot be connected in that "
"method. One possibility is to connect them ``AppConfig.__init__()`` instead, "
"taking care not to import models or trigger calls to the app registry."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go seoltar an comhartha seo le linn phróisis daonra an chlárlann "
"aipeanna, agus ritheann: meth: `AppConfig.ready () "
"<django.apps.AppConfig.ready>`tar éis do chlárlann an aip a bheith daonra go "
"hiomlán, ní féidir glacadóirí a nascadh sa mhodh sin. Féidearthacht amháin "
"ná iad a nascadh ``AppConfig. __init__ () ``ina ionad sin, ag tabhairt aire "
"gan samhlacha a iompórtáil nó glaonna a spreagadh chuig clárlann an aip."

msgid "Arguments that are sent with this signal:"
msgstr "Argóintí a sheoltar leis an gcomhartha seo:"

msgid "The model class which was just prepared."
msgstr "An rang samhail a bhí díreach ullmhaithe."

msgid "Management signals"
msgstr "Comharthaí bainistíochta"

msgid "Signals sent by :doc:`django-admin </ref/django-admin>`."
msgstr "Comharthaí a sheoltar ar:doc: `django-admin` </ref/django-admin>."

msgid "``pre_migrate``"
msgstr "``réamh-imirce``"

msgid ""
"Sent by the :djadmin:`migrate` command before it starts to install an "
"application. It's not emitted for applications that lack a ``models`` module."
msgstr ""
"Seolta ag an ordú:djadmin: `migrate` sula dtosaíonn sé ag suiteáil "
"feidhmchlár. Ní astaítear é d'iarratais nach bhfuil modúl “samhlacha” nach "
"bhfuil modúl acu."

msgid ""
"An :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance for the application about to be "
"migrated/synced."
msgstr ""
"An:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` mar shampla don fheidhmchlár atá ar tí a "
"imirce/sioncrónú."

msgid "``app_config``"
msgstr "``app_config``"

msgid "Same as ``sender``."
msgstr "Mar an gcéanna le ``seoltó`."

msgid "``verbosity``"
msgstr "``Dearbhacht``"

msgid ""
"Indicates how much information ``manage.py`` is printing on screen. See "
"the :option:`--verbosity` flag for details."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn sé cé mhéad faisnéise atá `manage.py`` a phriontáil ar an scáileán. "
"Féach an brat:option: `--verbosity` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"Functions which listen for :data:`pre_migrate` should adjust what they "
"output to the screen based on the value of this argument."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart d'fheidhmeanna a éisteann le:data: `pre_migrate` an méid a "
"aschuireann siad ar an scáileán a choigeartú bunaithe ar luach an argóint "
"seo."

msgid "``interactive``"
msgstr "``idirghníomhach``"

msgid ""
"If ``interactive`` is ``True``, it's safe to prompt the user to input things "
"on the command line. If ``interactive`` is ``False``, functions which listen "
"for this signal should not try to prompt for anything."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``idirghníomhach` ``True``, tá sé sábháilte an t-úsáideoir a spreagadh "
"chun rudaí a ionchur ar an líne ordaithe. Más “False” é ``idirghníomhach``, "
"níor cheart feidhmeanna a éisteann leis an gcomhartha seo iarracht a "
"dhéanamh rud ar bith a spreagadh."

msgid ""
"For example, the :mod:`django.contrib.auth` app only prompts to create a "
"superuser when ``interactive`` is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, ní spreagann an aip: mod: `django.contrib.auth` ach "
"sárúsáideoir a chruthú nuair a bhíonn ``idirghníomh`` `True``."

msgid "``stdout``"
msgstr "``stdout``"

msgid "A stream-like object where verbose output should be redirected."
msgstr "Rud cosúil le sruth inar chóir aschur fhearbose a atreorú."

msgid "The alias of database on which a command will operate."
msgstr "An t-ailias an bhunachar sonraí ar a n-oibreoidh ordú."

msgid "``plan``"
msgstr "``plean``"

msgid ""
"The migration plan that is going to be used for the migration run. While the "
"plan is not public API, this allows for the rare cases when it is necessary "
"to know the plan. A plan is a list of 2-tuples with the first item being the "
"instance of a migration class and the second item showing if the migration "
"was rolled back (``True``) or applied (``False``)."
msgstr ""
"An plean imirce atá le húsáid don imirce a reáchtáil. Cé nach API poiblí é "
"an plean, ceadaíonn sé seo do na cásanna neamhchoitianta nuair is gá an "
"plean a fháil amach. Is é plean liosta de dhá thúpla agus is é an chéad mhír "
"mar shampla aicme imirce agus an dara mír a léiríonn an t-imirce ar rolladh "
"ar ais (``True``) nó an cuireadh i bhfeidhm (``False``)."

msgid "``apps``"
msgstr "``aipeanna ``"

msgid ""
"An instance of :data:`Apps <django.apps>` containing the state of the "
"project before the migration run. It should be used instead of the "
"global :attr:`apps <django.apps.apps>` registry to retrieve the models you "
"want to perform operations on."
msgstr ""
"Sampla de:data: `Apps <django.apps>`ina bhfuil staid an tionscadail sula "
"ritheann an imirce. Ba chóir é a úsáid in ionad an chlárlann domhanda: attr: "
"`apps <django.apps.apps>`chun na samhlacha a theastaíonn uait oibríochtaí a "
"dhéanamh orthu a aisghabháil."

msgid "``post_migrate``"
msgstr "``post_migrate``"

msgid ""
"Sent at the end of the :djadmin:`migrate` (even if no migrations are run) "
"and :djadmin:`flush` commands. It's not emitted for applications that lack a "
"``models`` module."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar ag deireadh na horduithe: djadmin: `migrate` (fiú mura reáchtáiltear "
"aon imirce) agus:djadmin: `flush`. Ní astaítear é d'iarratais nach bhfuil "
"modúl “samhlacha” nach bhfuil modúl acu."

msgid ""
"Handlers of this signal must not perform database schema alterations as "
"doing so may cause the :djadmin:`flush` command to fail if it runs during "
"the :djadmin:`migrate` command."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór do láimhseálaithe an chomhartha seo athruithe scéime bunachar sonraí "
"a dhéanamh mar d'fhéadfadh go dteipfeadh ar an ordú:djadmin: `flush `má "
"ritheann sé le linn an orduithe: djadmin: `migrate`."

msgid ""
"An :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance for the application that was "
"just installed."
msgstr ""
"An:class: `~django.apps.appconfig` sampla don fheidhmchlár a bhí díreach "
"suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"Functions which listen for :data:`post_migrate` should adjust what they "
"output to the screen based on the value of this argument."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart d'fheidhmeanna a éisteann le:data: `post_migrate` an méid a "
"aschuireann siad ar an scáileán a choigeartú bunaithe ar luach an argóint "
"seo."

msgid ""
"The database alias used for synchronization. Defaults to the ``default`` "
"database."
msgstr ""
"An alias bunachar sonraí a úsáidtear le haghaidh sioncrónú. Réamhshocraithe "
"chuig an mbunachar sonraí ``default``."

msgid ""
"The migration plan that was used for the migration run. While the plan is "
"not public API, this allows for the rare cases when it is necessary to know "
"the plan. A plan is a list of 2-tuples with the first item being the "
"instance of a migration class and the second item showing if the migration "
"was rolled back (``True``) or applied (``False``)."
msgstr ""
"An plean imirce a úsáideadh don imirce a reáchtáil. Cé nach API poiblí é an "
"plean, ceadaíonn sé seo do na cásanna neamhchoitianta nuair is gá an plean a "
"fháil amach. Is é plean liosta de dhá thúpla agus is é an chéad mhír mar "
"shampla aicme imirce agus an dara mír a léiríonn an t-imirce ar rolladh ar "
"ais (``True``) nó an cuireadh i bhfeidhm (``False``)."

msgid ""
"An instance of :data:`Apps <django.apps.apps>` containing the state of the "
"project after the migration run. It should be used instead of the "
"global :attr:`apps <django.apps.apps>` registry to retrieve the models you "
"want to perform operations on."
msgstr ""
"Sampla de:data: `Apps <django.apps.apps>`ina bhfuil staid an tionscadail tar "
"éis an imirce a reáchtáil. Ba chóir é a úsáid in ionad an chlárlann "
"domhanda: attr: `apps <django.apps.apps>`chun na samhlacha a theastaíonn "
"uait oibríochtaí a dhéanamh orthu a aisghabháil."

msgid ""
"For example, you could register a callback in "
"an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` like this::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá glaoch ar ais a chlárú in an:class: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig` mar seo:"

msgid ""
"If you provide an :class:`~django.apps.AppConfig` instance as the sender "
"argument, please ensure that the signal is registered "
"in :meth:`~django.apps.AppConfig.ready`. ``AppConfig``\\s are recreated for "
"tests that run with a modified set of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` (such as "
"when settings are overridden) and such signals should be connected for each "
"new ``AppConfig`` instance."
msgstr ""
"Má sholáthraíonn tú sampla: class: `~django.apps.appconfig` mar argóint an "
"tseoltóra, déan cinnte go bhfuil an comhartha cláraithe in:meth: "
"`~django.apps.appconfig.ready`. Ag athchruthú ``AppConfig`` le haghaidh "
"tástálacha a ritheann le tacar modhnaithe de:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` "
"(amhail nuair a dhéantar socruithe a sháraigh) agus ba chóir comharthaí den "
"sórt sin a nascadh le haghaidh gach cás nua ``AppConfig``."

msgid "Request/response signals"
msgstr "Comharthaí iarrata/freagartha"

msgid "Signals sent by the core framework when processing a request."
msgstr "Comharthaí a sheolann an croíchreat agus iarratas á phróiseáil."

msgid ""
"Signals can make your code harder to maintain. Consider :doc:`using a "
"middleware </topics/http/middleware>` before using request/response signals."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le comharthaí do chód a dhéanamh níos deacra a chothabháil. "
"Smaoinigh ar: doc: `meán-earraí a úsáid 'sula n-úsáidtear comharthaí iarrata/"
"freagartha. </topics/http/middleware>"

msgid "``request_started``"
msgstr "``iarraidh_tosaith``"

msgid "Sent when Django begins processing an HTTP request."
msgstr "Seoltar nuair a thosaíonn Django ag próiseáil iarratas HTTP."

msgid ""
"The handler class -- e.g. ``django.core.handlers.wsgi.WsgiHandler`` -- that "
"handled the request."
msgstr ""
"An rang láimhseálaithe -- m.sh. ``Django.Core.Handlers.wsgi.wsgiHandler`` -- "
"a láimhseáil leis an iarraidh."

msgid "``environ``"
msgstr "``Comhshaol`"

msgid "The ``environ`` dictionary provided to the request."
msgstr "An foclóir ``timpeallach`` a chuirtear ar fáil don iarratas."

msgid "``request_finished``"
msgstr "``iarraidh_críochnaithe``"

msgid "Sent when Django finishes delivering an HTTP response to the client."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar nuair a chríochnaíonn Django freagra HTTP a sheachadadh don chliant."

msgid "The handler class, as above."
msgstr "An rang láimhseálaithe, mar atá thuas."

msgid "``got_request_exception``"
msgstr "``Got_iarrth_eisceacht``"

msgid ""
"This signal is sent whenever Django encounters an exception while processing "
"an incoming HTTP request."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar an comhartha seo aon uair a thagann Django le heisceacht agus "
"iarratas HTTP ag teacht isteach á phróiseáil."

msgid "Unused (always ``None``)."
msgstr "Gan úsáid (i gcónaí ``Non ``)."

msgid "The :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object."
msgstr "An réad: aicme: `~django.http.httpRequest`."

msgid "Test signals"
msgstr "Comharthaí tástála"

msgid "Signals only sent when :ref:`running tests <running-tests>`."
msgstr ""
"<running-tests>Ní sheoltar comharthaí ach nuair:ref: `tástálacha reatha `."

msgid "``setting_changed``"
msgstr "``setting_athraithe``"

msgid ""
"This signal is sent when the value of a setting is changed through the "
"``django.test.TestCase.settings()`` context manager or "
"the :func:`django.test.override_settings` decorator/context manager."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar an comhartha seo nuair a athraítear luach socrú tríd an mbainisteoir "
"comhthéacs ``django.test.testcase.settings () ``nó an: func: "
"`django.test.override_settings` maisiúcháin/bainisteoir comhthéacs."

msgid ""
"It's actually sent twice: when the new value is applied (\"setup\") and when "
"the original value is restored (\"teardown\"). Use the ``enter`` argument to "
"distinguish between the two."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar é faoi dhó i ndáiríre: nuair a chuirtear an luach nua i bhfeidhm "
"(“socrú”) agus nuair a athshlántar an luach bunaidh (“teardown”). Úsáid an "
"argóint ``enter ``chun idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir an dá cheann."

msgid ""
"You can also import this signal from ``django.core.signals`` to avoid "
"importing from ``django.test`` in non-test situations."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an comhartha seo a iompórtáil ó ``django.core.signals`` chun "
"allmhairiú ó `django.test`` a sheachaint i gcásanna neamh-tástála."

msgid "The settings handler."
msgstr "An láimhseálaí socruithe."

msgid "``setting``"
msgstr "``Socraithe``"

msgid "The name of the setting."
msgstr "Ainm an suímh."

msgid ""
"The value of the setting after the change. For settings that initially don't "
"exist, in the \"teardown\" phase, ``value`` is ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Luach an shocraithe tar éis an athraithe. Maidir le socruithe nach bhfuil "
"ann i dtosach, sa chéim “teardown”, is é ``luach`` ``None``."

msgid "``enter``"
msgstr "``Cuir isteach ``"

msgid "A boolean; ``True`` if the setting is applied, ``False`` if restored."
msgstr ""
"Boolean; ``True`` má chuirtear an socrú i bhfeidhm, ``False`` má "
"athchóiritear é."

msgid "``template_rendered``"
msgstr "``teimpléad_rinneadh ``"

msgid ""
"Sent when the test system renders a template. This signal is not emitted "
"during normal operation of a Django server -- it is only available during "
"testing."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar nuair a dhéanann an córas tástála teimpléad a léiriú. Ní astaítear "
"an comhartha seo le linn gnáthoibriú freastalaí Django - níl sé ar fáil ach "
"le linn tástála."

msgid "The :class:`~django.template.Template` object which was rendered."
msgstr "An réad: Class: `~Django.Template.Template` a rinneadh."

msgid "``template``"
msgstr "``Teimpléad``"

msgid "Same as sender"
msgstr "Mar an gcéanna le seoltóir"

msgid "``context``"
msgstr "``comhthéacs``"

msgid ""
"The :class:`~django.template.Context` with which the template was rendered."
msgstr "An: class: `~django.template.context` ar rinneadh an teimpléad leis."

msgid "Database Wrappers"
msgstr "Fillteáin Bunachar Sonraí"

msgid ""
"Signals sent by the database wrapper when a database connection is initiated."
msgstr ""
"Comharthaí a sheolann an fillteoir bunachar sonraí nuair a thioctar nasc "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid "``connection_created``"
msgstr "``nasc_cruthaithead``"

msgid ""
"Sent when the database wrapper makes the initial connection to the "
"database.  This is particularly useful if you'd like to send any post "
"connection commands to the SQL backend."
msgstr ""
"Seoltar nuair a dhéanann fillteoir an bunachar sonraí an nasc tosaigh leis "
"an mbunachar sonraí. Tá sé seo úsáideach go háirithe más mian leat aon "
"orduithe nasc poist a sheoladh chuig an gcúltaca SQL."

msgid ""
"The database wrapper class -- i.e. "
"``django.db.backends.postgresql.DatabaseWrapper`` or "
"``django.db.backends.mysql.DatabaseWrapper``, etc."
msgstr ""
"An rang timfhilleadh bunachar sonraí - ie "
"``Django.db.backends.postgresql.databaseWrapper`` nó "
"``Django.db.backends.mysql.databaseWrapper``, srl."

msgid ""
"The database connection that was opened. This can be used in a multiple-"
"database configuration to differentiate connection signals from different "
"databases."
msgstr ""
"An nasc bunachar sonraí a osclaíodh. Is féidir é seo a úsáid i gcumraíocht "
"ilbhunachar sonraí chun comharthaí nasc a idirdhealú ó bhunachair sonraí éag"

msgid "``TemplateResponse`` and ``SimpleTemplateResponse``"
msgstr "``TemplateResponse`` agus ``SimpleTemplateResponse``"

msgid ""
"Standard :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` objects are static structures. "
"They are provided with a block of pre-rendered content at time of "
"construction, and while that content can be modified, it isn't in a form "
"that makes it easy to perform modifications."
msgstr ""
"Caighdeán:aicme: Is struchtúir statacha iad rudaí "
"`~django.http.HttpResponse`. Cuirtear bloc d'ábhar réamh-rindreáilte ar fáil "
"dóibh tráth na tógála, agus cé gur féidir an t-ábhar sin a mhodhnú, níl sé i "
"bhfoirm a fhágann go bhfuil sé éasca modhnuithe a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"However, it can sometimes be beneficial to allow decorators or middleware to "
"modify a response *after* it has been constructed by the view. For example, "
"you may want to change the template that is used, or put additional data "
"into the context."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, is féidir go mbeadh sé tairbheach uaireanta ligean do "
"mhaisitheoirí nó meán-earraí freagra a mhodhnó* tar éis dó* é a thógáil ag "
"an dearcadh. Mar shampla, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an teimpléad a úsáidtear "
"a athrú, nó sonraí breise a chur sa chomhthéacs."

msgid ""
"TemplateResponse provides a way to do just that. Unlike "
"basic :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` objects, TemplateResponse objects "
"retain the details of the template and context that was provided by the view "
"to compute the response. The final output of the response is not computed "
"until it is needed, later in the response process."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn TemplateResponse bealach chun é sin a dhéanamh. Murab ionann "
"agus rudaí bunús:class: `~django.http.httpResponse`, coinníonn rudaí "
"TemplateResponse sonraí an teimpléid agus an chomhthéacs a chuir an dearcadh "
"ar fáil chun an freagra a ríomh. Ní ríomhtar aschur deiridh an fhreagra go "
"dtí go mbeidh sé ag teastáil, níos déanaí sa phróiseas freagartha."

msgid "``SimpleTemplateResponse`` objects"
msgstr "``rudaí SimpleTemplateResponse``"

msgid ""
"The name of the template to be rendered. Accepts a backend-dependent "
"template object (such as those returned "
"by :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template()`), the name of a template, "
"or a list of template names."
msgstr ""
"Ainm an teimpléid atá le déanamh. Glacann sé le réad teimpléad atá ag brath "
"ar chúlra (amhail iad siúd ar ais ar:func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template () `), ainm teimpléad, nó liosta "
"ainmneacha teimpléad."

msgid "Example: ``['foo.html', 'path/to/bar.html']``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``['foo.html', 'path/to/bar.html']``"

msgid ""
"The context data to be used when rendering the template. It must be "
"a :class:`dict`."
msgstr ""
"Na sonraí comhthéacs atá le húsáid agus an teimpléad á rindreáil. Caithfidh "
"sé a: aicme: `dict`."

msgid "Example: ``{'foo': 123}``"
msgstr "Sampla: ``{'foo': 123}``"

msgid ""
"The current rendered value of the response content, using the current "
"template and context data."
msgstr ""
"Luach reatha a rinneadh an ábhair freagartha, ag baint úsáide as an "
"teimpléad reatha agus na sonraí comhthéacs."

msgid "A boolean indicating whether the response content has been rendered."
msgstr "Boolean a léiríonn an bhfuil an t-ábhar freagartha a rinneadh."

msgid ""
"Instantiates a :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse` "
"object with the given template, context, content type, HTTP status, and "
"charset."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé réad a:class: `~Django.Template.Response.SimpleTemplateResponse` "
"leis an teimpléad, an comhthéacs, an cineál ábhair, stádas HTTP, agus tacar "
"charta ar leith."

msgid ""
"A backend-dependent template object (such as those returned "
"by :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template()`), the name of a template, "
"or a list of template names."
msgstr ""
"Rud teimpléad atá ag brath ar chúlra (amhail iad siúd a d'fhaigh:func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template () `), ainm teimpléad, nó liosta "
"ainmneacha teimpléad."

msgid ""
"A :class:`dict` of values to add to the template context. By default, this "
"is an empty dictionary."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: `ordach` luachanna le cur le comhthéacs an teimpléid. De réir "
"réamhshocraithe, is foclóir folamh é seo."

msgid "``content_type``"
msgstr "``cineál_ábhar ``"

msgid ""
"The value included in the HTTP ``Content-Type`` header, including the MIME "
"type specification and the character set encoding. If ``content_type`` is "
"specified, then its value is used. Otherwise, ``'text/html'`` is used."
msgstr ""
"An luach atá san áireamh sa cheanntásc HTTP ``Content-Type``, lena n-"
"áirítear an tsonraíocht cineál MIME agus an ionchódú tacar carachtair. Má "
"shonraítear ``content_type``, ansin úsáidtear a luach. Seachas sin, "
"úsáidtear ``'text/html'``."

msgid "``status``"
msgstr "``stádas``"

msgid "The HTTP status code for the response."
msgstr "An cód stádais HTTP don fhreagra."

msgid "``charset``"
msgstr "``charset``"

msgid ""
"The charset in which the response will be encoded. If not given it will be "
"extracted from ``content_type``, and if that is unsuccessful, "
"the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting will be used."
msgstr ""
"An charset ina ndéanfar an freagra a ionchódú. Mura dtugtar é bainfear as "
"`content_type``, agus mura n-éiríonn leis sin, úsáidfear an socrú: setting: "
"`DEFAULT_CHARSET`."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`NAME <TEMPLATES-NAME>` of a template engine to use for loading "
"the template."
msgstr ""
"An: Socrú: `AINM <TEMPLATES-NAME>`inneall teimpléad le húsáid chun an "
"teimpléad a luchtú."

msgid "``headers``"
msgstr "``ceannair``"

msgid "A :class:`dict` of HTTP headers to add to the response."
msgstr "A: aicme: `ordach` ceanntásca HTTP le cur leis an bhfreagra."

msgid ""
"Preprocesses context data that will be used for rendering a template. "
"Accepts a :class:`dict` of context data. By default, returns the "
"same :class:`dict`."
msgstr ""
"Réamhphróiseálann sonraí comhthéacs a úsáidfear chun teimpléad a rindreáil. "
"Glacann sé: aicme: `ordach` sonraí comhthéacs. De réir réamhshocraithe, "
"filleann sé an chéanna: class: `dict`."

msgid "Override this method in order to customize the context."
msgstr "Athraigh an modh seo d'fhonn an comhthéacs a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Resolves the template instance to use for rendering. Accepts a backend-"
"dependent template object (such as those returned "
"by :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template()`), the name of a template, "
"or a list of template names."
msgstr ""
"Réitíonn sé an tsampla teimpléid le húsáid le haghaidh rindreáil. Glacann sé "
"le réad teimpléad atá ag brath ar chúlra (amhail iad siúd ar ais ar:func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template () `), ainm teimpléad, nó liosta "
"ainmneacha teimpléad."

msgid "Returns the backend-dependent template object instance to be rendered."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an tsampla réad teimpléad atá ag brath ar chúlra atá le léiriú"

msgid "Override this method in order to customize template loading."
msgstr "Athraigh an modh seo d'fhonn luchtú teimpléad a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"Add a callback that will be invoked after rendering has taken place. This "
"hook can be used to defer certain processing operations (such as caching) "
"until after rendering has occurred."
msgstr ""
"Cuir glaoch ar ais a ghairmfear tar éis an rindreáil a dhéanamh. Is féidir "
"an crúca seo a úsáid chun oibríochtaí próiseála áirithe (mar shampla "
"caching) a chur siar go dtí go mbeidh rindreáil tarlú."

msgid ""
"If the :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse` has already "
"been rendered, the callback will be invoked immediately."
msgstr ""
"Má rinneadh an:class: `~django.template.Response.SimpleTemplateResponse` "
"cheana féin, cuirfear an glaoch ar ais láithreach."

msgid ""
"When called, callbacks will be passed a single argument -- the "
"rendered :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse` instance."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a thugtar air, cuirfear argóint amháin ar ais - an t-áis "
"rendered:class: `~django.template.response.simpleTemplateResponse`."

msgid ""
"If the callback returns a value that is not ``None``, this will be used as "
"the response instead of the original response object (and will be passed to "
"the next post rendering callback etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Má thugann an glaoch ar ais luach nach ``None``, úsáidfear é seo mar "
"fhreagra in ionad an réad freagartha bunaidh (agus cuirfear ar aghaidh chuig "
"an gcéad phost eile ag déanamh glaonna aisghlaonna srl.)"

msgid ""
"Sets ``response.content`` to the result obtained "
"by :attr:`SimpleTemplateResponse.rendered_content`, runs all post-rendering "
"callbacks, and returns the resulting response object."
msgstr ""
"Socraíonn sé ``response.content`` don toradh a fhaightear ar:attr: "
"`SimpleTemplateResponse.rendered_content`, ritheann sé gach glaonna iar-"
"rindreála, agus filleann sé an réad freagartha mar thoradh air."

msgid ""
"``render()`` will only have an effect the first time it is called. On "
"subsequent calls, it will return the result obtained from the first call."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh éifeacht ag `render () ``ach an chéad uair a thugtar air. Ar "
"ghlaonna ina dhiaidh sin, cuirfidh sé an toradh a fhaightear ón gcéad ghlao "
"ar ais."

msgid "``TemplateResponse`` objects"
msgstr "Rudaí ``TemplateResponse``"

msgid ""
"``TemplateResponse`` is a subclass "
"of :class:`~django.template.response.SimpleTemplateResponse` that knows "
"about the current :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest`."
msgstr ""
"Is fo-aicme é ``TemplateResponse`` de:class: "
"`~django.template.response.simpletemplateResponse` a bhfuil a fhios aige "
"faoin reatha:class: `~django.http.httpRequest`."

msgid ""
"Instantiates a :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` object "
"with the given request, template, context, content type, HTTP status, and "
"charset."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé réad a:class: `~django.template.response.templateResponse` leis "
"an iarraidh, an teimpléad, an comhthéacs, an cineál ábhair, stádas HTTP, "
"agus tacar charta a thugtar."

msgid "An :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` instance."
msgstr "An:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` sampla."

msgid "The rendering process"
msgstr "An próiseas rindreála"

msgid ""
"Before a :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse` instance can be "
"returned to the client, it must be rendered. The rendering process takes the "
"intermediate representation of template and context, and turns it into the "
"final byte stream that can be served to the client."
msgstr ""
"Roimh a:class: `~Django.Template.Response.TemplateResponse` is féidir sampla "
"a thabhairt ar ais chuig an gcliant, caithfear é a léiriú. Glacann an "
"próiseas rindreála léiriú idirmheánach teimpléad agus comhthéacs, agus "
"casann sé isteach sa sruth béite deiridh is féidir a sheirbheáil don chliant."

msgid ""
"There are three circumstances under which a ``TemplateResponse`` will be "
"rendered:"
msgstr "Tá trí imthosca ann ina ndéanfar ``TemplateResponse`` a thaispeáint:"

msgid ""
"When the ``TemplateResponse`` instance is explicitly rendered, using "
"the :meth:`SimpleTemplateResponse.render()` method."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a dhéantar an cás ``TemplateResponse`` a léiriú go sainráite, ag baint "
"úsáide as an modh:meth: `SimpleTemplateResponse.render () `."

msgid ""
"When the content of the response is explicitly set by assigning "
"``response.content``."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraítear ábhar an fhreagra go sainráite trí ``freagra.content`` a "
"shannadh."

msgid ""
"After passing through template response middleware, but before passing "
"through response middleware."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis dul trí mheán-earraí freagartha teimpléad, ach sula dtéann sé trí "
"mheán-earraí freagartha."

msgid ""
"A ``TemplateResponse`` can only be rendered once. The first call "
"to :meth:`SimpleTemplateResponse.render` sets the content of the response; "
"subsequent rendering calls do not change the response content."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir ``TemplateResponse`` a léiriú ach uair amháin. Socraíonn an chéad "
"ghlao chuig:meth: `SimpleTemplateResponse.render` ábhar an fhreagra; ní "
"athraíonn glaonna rindreála ina dhiaidh sin an t-ábhar freagartha."

msgid ""
"However, when ``response.content`` is explicitly assigned, the change is "
"always applied. If you want to force the content to be re-rendered, you can "
"reevaluate the rendered content, and assign the content of the response "
"manually:"
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, nuair a shanntar `response.content`` go sainráite, cuirtear an "
"t-athrú i bhfeidhm i gcónaí. Más mian leat iallach a chur ar an ábhar a "
"athléiriú, is féidir leat an t-ábhar a rindreáiltear a athmheas, agus ábhar "
"na freagartha a shannadh de láimh:"

msgid "Post-render callbacks"
msgstr "Aisghlaonna iar-rindreála"

msgid ""
"Some operations -- such as caching -- cannot be performed on an unrendered "
"template. They must be performed on a fully complete and rendered response."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir roinnt oibríochtaí - mar shampla caching - a dhéanamh ar "
"theimpléad neamh-rindreáilte. Ní mór iad a dhéanamh ar fhreagra iomlán "
"iomlán agus a rinneadh."

msgid ""
"If you're using middleware, you can do that. Middleware provides multiple "
"opportunities to process a response on exit from a view. If you put behavior "
"in the response middleware, it's guaranteed to execute after template "
"rendering has taken place."
msgstr ""
"Má tá middleware á úsáid agat, is féidir leat é sin a dhéanamh. Soláthraíonn "
"Middleware go leor deiseanna chun freagra a phróiseáil ar imeacht ó radharc. "
"Má chuireann tú iompar sa mheán-earraí freagartha, ráthaítear go "
"bhforghníomhaítear é tar éis rindreáil teimpléid a bheith tarlú."

msgid ""
"However, if you're using a decorator, the same opportunities do not exist. "
"Any behavior defined in a decorator is handled immediately."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, má tá maisitheoir á úsáid agat, níl na deiseanna céanna ann. "
"Láimhseálfar aon iompar a shainmhínítear i maisitheoir láithreach."

msgid ""
"To compensate for this (and any other analogous use "
"cases), :class:`TemplateResponse` allows you to register callbacks that will "
"be invoked when rendering has completed. Using this callback, you can defer "
"critical processing until a point where you can guarantee that rendered "
"content will be available."
msgstr ""
"Chun cúiteamh as seo (agus aon chásanna úsáide comhchosúla eile), "
"tugann :class: `TemplateResponse` deis duit aisghlaonna a chlárú a "
"ghairmfear nuair a bheidh an rindreáil críochnaithe. Ag baint úsáide as an "
"aisghlao seo, is féidir leat próiseáil chriticiúil a chur ar siar go dtí "
"pointe inar féidir leat a ráthú go mbeidh ábhar rindreáilte ar fáil."

msgid ""
"To define a post-render callback, define a function that takes a single "
"argument -- response -- and register that function with the template "
"response::"
msgstr ""
"Chun glaonna iar-rindreála a shainiú, sainmhínigh feidhm a ghlacann argóint "
"amháin - freagra - agus cláraigh an fheidhm sin leis an bhfreagra teimpléid:"

msgid ""
"``my_render_callback()`` will be invoked after the ``mytemplate.html`` has "
"been rendered, and will be provided the fully "
"rendered :class:`TemplateResponse` instance as an argument."
msgstr ""
"Gairmfear ``my_render_callback () ``tar éis don `mytemplate.html`` a "
"rindreáil, agus cuirfear an sampla iomlán:class: `TemplateResponse` ar fáil "
"mar argóint."

msgid ""
"If the template has already been rendered, the callback will be invoked "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"Má rinneadh an teimpléad cheana féin, cuirfear an glaoch ar ais láithreach."

msgid "Using ``TemplateResponse`` and ``SimpleTemplateResponse``"
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as ``TemplateResponse`` agus ``SimpleTemplateResponse``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`TemplateResponse` object can be used anywhere that a "
"normal :class:`django.http.HttpResponse` can be used. It can also be used as "
"an alternative to calling :func:`~django.shortcuts.render()`."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: Is féidir réad `TemplateResponse` a úsáid in áit ar féidir "
"gnáth:class: `django.http.httpResponse` a úsáid. Is féidir é a úsáid freisin "
"mar mhalairt ar glao:func: `~django.shortcuts.render () `."

msgid ""
"For example, the following view returns a :class:`TemplateResponse` with a "
"template and a context containing a queryset::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, filleann an radharc seo a leanas a:class: `TemplateResponse` le "
"teimpléad agus comhthéacs ina bhfuil tacar ceisteanna:"

msgid "The Django template language: for Python programmers"
msgstr "Teanga teimpléad Django: do ríomhchláraitheoirí Python"

msgid ""
"This document explains the Django template system from a technical "
"perspective -- how it works and how to extend it. If you're looking for "
"reference on the language syntax, see :doc:`/ref/templates/language`."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo córas teimpléid Django ó pheirspictíocht theicniúil "
"- conas a oibríonn sé agus conas é a leathnú. Má tá tagairt á lorg agat "
"maidir le comhréiteach na teanga, féach:doc: `/ref/templates/language`."

msgid ""
"It assumes an understanding of templates, contexts, variables, tags, and "
"rendering. Start with the :ref:`introduction to the Django template language "
"<template-language-intro>` if you aren't familiar with these concepts."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé le tuiscint ar theimpléid, comhthéacsanna, athróga, clibeanna "
"agus rindreáil. Tosaigh leis an: ref: `réamhrá don teanga teimpléid Django "
"<template-language-intro>`mura bhfuil tú eolach ar na coincheapa seo."

msgid "Using the template system in Python is a three-step process:"
msgstr "Is próiseas trí chéim é an córas teimpléid a úsáid i Python:"

msgid "You configure an :class:`Engine`."
msgstr "Cumraíonn tú an:class: `Inneall`."

msgid "You compile template code into a :class:`Template`."
msgstr "Tiomsaíonn tú cód teimpléad isteach i a:class: `Teimpléad`."

msgid "You render the template with a :class:`Context`."
msgstr "Déanann tú an teimpléad a: class: `Context`."

msgid ""
"Django projects generally rely on the :ref:`high level, backend agnostic "
"APIs <template-engines>` for each of these steps instead of the template "
"system's lower level APIs:"
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth braitheann tionscadail Django ar:ref: `ardleibhéal, APIs "
"agnóstacha cúltaca <template-engines>`do gach ceann de na céimeanna seo in "
"ionad APIs leibhéal níos ísle an chórais teimpléid:"

msgid ""
"For each :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend "
"in the :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting, Django instantiates "
"an :class:`Engine`. :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` "
"wraps :class:`Engine` and adapts it to the common template backend API."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le gach ceann: aicme: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` sa socrú: `TEMPLATES`, "
"déanann Django ain:class: `Engine`. :class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates` fillteann:class: `Engine` "
"agus cuireann sé in oiriúint don API cúltaca teimpléad coitianta."

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.template.loader` module provides functions such "
"as :func:`~django.template.loader.get_template` for loading templates. They "
"return a ``django.template.backends.django.Template`` which wraps the "
"actual :class:`django.template.Template`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an modúl: mod: `django.template.loader` feidhmeanna mar: func: "
"`~django.template.loader.get_template` chun teimpléid a luchtú. Filleann "
"siad ``django.template.backends.django.template`` a fhilleann an "
"fhíor:class: `django.template.template`."

msgid ""
"The ``Template`` obtained in the previous step has "
"a :meth:`~django.template.backends.base.Template.render` method which "
"marshals a context and possibly a request into a :class:`Context` and "
"delegates the rendering to the underlying :class:`Template`."
msgstr ""
"Tá a: meth: `~django.template.backends.base.template.base.template.render` "
"modh a fuarthas sa chéim roimhe seo a mharsaíonn comhthéacs agus b'fhéidir "
"iarratas isteach i a:class: `Context` agus a thosclaíonn an rindreáil chuig "
"an bun:class: `Template`."

msgid "Configuring an engine"
msgstr "Inneall a chumrú"

msgid ""
"If you are using "
"the :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` backend, this "
"probably isn't the documentation you're looking for. An instance of the "
"``Engine`` class described below is accessible using the ``engine`` "
"attribute of that backend and any attribute defaults mentioned below are "
"overridden by what's passed "
"by :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag úsáid an backend: :class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates`, is dócha nach é seo an "
"doiciméadú atá á lorg agat. Tá sampla den aicme ``Engine`` a thuairiscítear "
"thíos inrochtana ag baint úsáide as tréith ``inneal`` den chúltaca sin agus "
"cuirtear aon réamhshocraithe tréithe a luaitear thíos ag an méid a chuirtear "
"trí:class: `~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates`."

msgid ""
"When instantiating an ``Engine`` all arguments must be passed as keyword "
"arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Agus “Inneall” á dtionscnamh, caithfear gach argóint a rith mar argóintí "
"eochairfhocal:"

msgid ""
"``dirs`` is a list of directories where the engine should look for template "
"source files. It is used to configure :class:`filesystem.Loader "
"<django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader>`."
msgstr ""
"Is liosta eolairí é ``dirs`` inar chóir don inneall comhaid foinse teimpléad "
"a lorg. <django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader>Úsáidtear é chun: class: "
"`FileSystem.loader `a chumrú."

msgid "It defaults to an empty list."
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe go liosta folamh."

msgid "``app_dirs`` only affects the default value of ``loaders``. See below."
msgstr ""
"Ní théann `app_dirs`` i bhfeidhm ach ar luach réamhshocraithe ``loaders``. "
"Féach thíos."

msgid "It defaults to ``False``."
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid "``autoescape`` controls whether HTML autoescaping is enabled."
msgstr "Rialaíonn ``autoescape`` an bhfuil autoescaping HTML cumasaithe."

msgid "It defaults to ``True``."
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe go ``True``."

msgid "Only set it to ``False`` if you're rendering non-HTML templates!"
msgstr ""
"Socraigh é go ``False`` ach má tá teimpléid neamh-HTML á rindreáil agat!"

msgid ""
"``context_processors`` is a list of dotted Python paths to callables that "
"are used to populate the context when a template is rendered with a request. "
"These callables take a request object as their argument and return "
"a :class:`dict` of items to be merged into the context."
msgstr ""
"Is é `context_processors`` liosta de chosáin poncaireacha Python chuig "
"glaonna a úsáidtear chun an comhthéacs a líonadh nuair a dhéantar teimpléad "
"a léiriú le hiarratas. Glacann na glaonna seo réad iarratais mar argóint "
"agus filleann siad a: class: `dict` d'earraí atá le cumasc sa chomhthéacs."

msgid "See :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Féach: Class: `~django.template.requestContext` le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"faisnéise."

msgid ""
"``debug`` is a boolean that turns on/off template debug mode. If it is "
"``True``, the template engine will store additional debug information which "
"can be used to display a detailed report for any exception raised during "
"template rendering."
msgstr ""
"Is boolean é ``debug`` a chasann air/as modh dífhabhtaithe teimpléad. Más "
"“True” é, stóráilfidh an t-inneall teimpléid faisnéis bhreise dífhabhtaithe "
"is féidir a úsáid chun tuarascáil mhionsonraithe a thaispeáint d'aon "
"eisceacht a ardaítear le linn rindreáil teimpléad."

msgid ""
"``loaders`` is a list of template loader classes, specified as strings. Each "
"``Loader`` class knows how to import templates from a particular source. "
"Optionally, a tuple can be used instead of a string. The first item in the "
"tuple should be the ``Loader`` class name, subsequent items are passed to "
"the ``Loader`` during initialization."
msgstr ""
"Is liosta d'aicmí lódóirí teimpléad é ``loaders`, a shonraítear mar "
"teaghráin. Tá a fhios ag gach rang ``Loader` conas teimpléid a iompórtáil ó "
"fhoinse áirithe. Go roghnach, is féidir tuple a úsáid in ionad sreang. Ba "
"chóir gurb é an chéad mhír sa tuple ainm aicme ``Loader ``, cuirtear "
"míreanna ina dhiaidh sin chuig an ``Loader`` le linn an tionscnaimh."

msgid "It defaults to a list containing:"
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe ar liosta ina bhfuil:"

msgid "``'django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader'``"
msgstr "``'Django.Template.Loaders.FileSystem.Loader'``"

msgid ""
"``'django.template.loaders.app_directories.Loader'`` if and only if "
"``app_dirs`` is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"``'Django.Template.Loaders.App_Directories.Loader'`` más rud é agus amháin "
"má tá ``app_dirs`` ``True``."

msgid ""
"These loaders are then wrapped "
"in :class:`django.template.loaders.cached.Loader`."
msgstr ""
"Ansin filtear na luchtóirí seo in:class: "
"`django.template.loaders.cached.loader`."

msgid "See :ref:`template-loaders` for details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `template-loaders` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"``string_if_invalid`` is the output, as a string, that the template system "
"should use for invalid (e.g. misspelled) variables."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``string_if_invalid`` an t-aschur, mar shreang, ar chóir don chóras "
"teimpléid a úsáid le haghaidh athróga neamhbhailí (m.sh. mí-litrithe)."

msgid "It defaults to the empty string."
msgstr "Déanann sé réamhshocraithe don teaghrán folamh."

msgid "See :ref:`invalid-template-variables` for details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `invalid-template-athraitheoir` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``file_charset`` is the charset used to read template files on disk."
msgstr ""
"Is é `file_charset`` an charset a úsáidtear chun comhaid teimpléad a léamh "
"ar dhiosca."

msgid "It defaults to ``'utf-8'``."
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe go ``'utf-8'``."

msgid ""
"``'libraries'``: A dictionary of labels and dotted Python paths of template "
"tag modules to register with the template engine. This is used to add new "
"libraries or provide alternate labels for existing ones. For example::"
msgstr ""
"```leabharlanna``: Foclóir lipéid agus cosáin poncanna Python de mhodúil "
"clibeanna teimpléad le clárú leis an inneall teimpléad. Úsáidtear é seo chun "
"leabharlanna nua a chur leis nó lipéid mhalartacha a sholáthar do na cinn "
"atá ann Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Libraries can be loaded by passing the corresponding dictionary key to "
"the :ttag:`{% load %}<load>` tag."
msgstr ""
"<load>Is féidir leabharlanna a luchtú tríd an eochair chomhfhreagrach "
"foclóra a rith chuig an gclibe:ttag: `{% load%}`."

msgid ""
"``'builtins'``: A list of dotted Python paths of template tag modules to add "
"to :doc:`built-ins </ref/templates/builtins>`. For example::"
msgstr ""
"```builtins'``: Liosta de na cosáin poncaí Python de mhodúil clibeanna "
"teimpléad le cur la:doc: `builtin</ref/templates/builtins> s'. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"Tags and filters from built-in libraries can be used without first calling "
"the :ttag:`{% load %}<load>` tag."
msgstr ""
"<load>Is féidir clibeanna agus scagairí ó leabharlanna ionsuite a úsáid gan "
"glaoch ar dtús ar an gclibe:ttag: `{% load%}`."

msgid ""
"Returns the underlying :class:`Engine` from the first "
"configured :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` engine. "
"Raises :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ImproperlyConfigured` if no engines are "
"configured."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an bunlin:class: `Engine` ón gcéad inneall cumraithe:class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates`. Ardaithe:exc: "
"`~Django.Core.Exceptions.ImProperlyConfigured` mura bhfuil aon innill "
"chumraithe."

msgid ""
"It's required for preserving APIs that rely on a globally available, "
"implicitly configured engine. Any other use is strongly discouraged."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé ag teastáil chun APIs a chaomhnú atá ag brath ar inneall cumraithe go "
"domhanda atá cumraithe go hinmheánach. Déantar aon úsáid eile a dhíspreagadh "
"go láidir."

msgid ""
"Compiles the given template code and returns a :class:`Template` object."
msgstr ""
"Tiomsaíonn sé an cód teimpléad a thugtar agus cuireann sé ar ais a:class: "
"`Teimpléad` réad."

msgid ""
"Loads a template with the given name, compiles it and returns "
"a :class:`Template` object."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn teimpléad leis an ainm tugtha, tiomsaíonn sé é agus filleann sé "
"a: class: `Teimpléad` réad."

msgid ""
"Like :meth:`~Engine.get_template`, except it takes a list of names and "
"returns the first template that was found."
msgstr ""
"Cos:Meth: `~Engine.get_Template`, ach amháin go dtógann sé liosta ainmneacha "
"agus tugann sé an chéad teimpléad a fuarthas ar ais."

msgid "Loading a template"
msgstr "Teimpléad á luchtú"

msgid ""
"The recommended way to create a :class:`Template` is by calling the factory "
"methods of "
"the :class:`Engine`: :meth:`~Engine.get_template`, :meth:`~Engine.select_template` "
"and :meth:`~Engine.from_string`."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach a mholtar chun a:class: `Template` a chruthú ná modhanna "
"monarchan an: class: `Engine`: :meth: `~Engine.get_Template`, :meth: "
"`~Engine.select_Template` agus:meth: `~Engine.from_string`."

msgid ""
"In a Django project where the :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting defines "
"a :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` engine, it's "
"possible to instantiate a :class:`Template` directly. If more than "
"one :class:`~django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates` engine is "
"defined, the first one will be used."
msgstr ""
"I dtionscadal Django ina sainmhíníonn an socrú:setting: `TEMPLATES` a:class: "
"`~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates`, is féidir a:class: "
"`Template` a chur isteach go díreach. Má shainmhínítear níos mó ná inneall "
"amháin: class: `~django.template.backends.django.djangoTemplates`, úsáidfear "
"an chéad cheann."

msgid ""
"This class lives at ``django.template.Template``. The constructor takes one "
"argument — the raw template code::"
msgstr ""
"Tá an rang seo ina chónaí ag ``Django.Template.Template``. Glacann an "
"tógálaí argóint amháin - an cód teimpléad amh::"

msgid "Behind the scenes"
msgstr "Taobh thiar de na radhairc"

msgid ""
"The system only parses your raw template code once -- when you create the "
"``Template`` object. From then on, it's stored internally as a tree "
"structure for performance."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann an córas do chód teimpléad amh a pháirseáil ach uair amháin - "
"nuair a chruthaíonn tú an réad ``Teimpléad`. Ón sin ar aghaidh, stóráiltear "
"é go hinmheánach mar struchtúr crann le haghaidh feidhmíochta."

msgid ""
"Even the parsing itself is quite fast. Most of the parsing happens via a "
"single call to a single, short, regular expression."
msgstr ""
"Tá fiú an parsáil féin tapa go leor. Tarlaíonn an chuid is mó den pháirseáil "
"trí ghlao amháin ar léiriú amháin, gearr, rialta."

msgid "Rendering a context"
msgstr "Comhthéacs a rindreáil"

msgid ""
"Once you have a compiled :class:`Template` object, you can render a context "
"with it. You can reuse the same template to render it several times with "
"different contexts."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh réad tiomsaithe:class: `Template` agat, is féidir leat "
"comhthéacs a rinneadh leis. Is féidir leat an teimpléad céanna a athúsáid "
"chun é a dhéanamh arís agus arís eile le comhthéacsanna éagsúla"

msgid ""
"The constructor of ``django.template.Context`` takes an optional argument — "
"a dictionary mapping variable names to variable values."
msgstr ""
"Tógann tógálaí ``Django.Template.Context`` argóint roghnach - foclóir a "
"mhapáil ainmneacha athraitheacha chuig luachanna athraitheacha."

msgid "Three optional keyword arguments can also be specified:"
msgstr "Is féidir trí argóint eochairfhocal roghnach a shonrú freisin:"

msgid ""
"``use_l10n`` overrides whether values will be localized by default. If set "
"to ``True`` numbers and dates will be formatted based on locale."
msgstr ""
"Sáraíonn ``use_l10n`` cibé an mbeidh luachanna logánaithe de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Má tá sé socraithe go ``True`` déanfar uimhreacha agus "
"dátaí a fhormáidiú bunaithe ar an áitiúil."

msgid "It defaults to ``None``."
msgstr "Tá sé réamhshocraithe go ``None``."

msgid "See :ref:`topic-l10n-templates` for details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `topic-l10n-templates` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
"``use_tz`` overrides whether dates are converted to the local time when "
"rendered in a template. If set to ``True`` all dates will be rendered using "
"the local timezone. This takes precedence over :setting:`USE_TZ`."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn ``use_tz`` cibé an ndéantar dátaí a thiontú go dtí an am áitiúil "
"nuair a dhéantar iad a rinneadh i dteimpléad. Má tá sé socraithe ar ``True`` "
"déanfar gach dáta a léiriú ag baint úsáide as an crios ama áitiúil. Tá "
"tosaíocht air seo thar: setting: `USE_TZ`."

msgid "See :ref:`time-zones-in-templates` for details."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `criosanna ama-in-theimpléid` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "For example usage, see :ref:`playing-with-context` below."
msgstr "Mar shampla úsáid, féach:ref: `playing-with-context` thíos."

msgid ""
"Call the :class:`Template` object's ``render()`` method with "
"a :class:`Context` to \"fill\" the template:"
msgstr ""
"Glaoigh ar an modh `render () ``réad: `Teimpléad` le a:class: `Context` chun "
"an teimpléad a “líonadh”:"

msgid "Variables and lookups"
msgstr "Athróga agus cuardaigh"

msgid ""
"Variable names must consist of any letter (A-Z), any digit (0-9), an "
"underscore (but they must not start with an underscore) or a dot."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór go mbeadh aon litir (A-Z), aon dhigit (0-9), béim (ach níor chóir "
"dóibh tosú le béim) nó ponc ar ainmneacha athróga."

msgid ""
"Dots have a special meaning in template rendering. A dot in a variable name "
"signifies a **lookup**. Specifically, when the template system encounters a "
"dot in a variable name, it tries the following lookups, in this order:"
msgstr ""
"Tá brí speisialta ag poncanna i rindreáil teimpléad. Léiríonn ponc in ainm "
"athraitheach**cuardach**. Go sonrach, nuair a bhíonn an córas teimpléid ag "
"teacht le ponc in ainm athraitheach, déanann sé iarracht na cuardaigh seo a "
"leanas, san ord seo:"

msgid "Dictionary lookup. Example: ``foo[\"bar\"]``"
msgstr "Cuardach foclóra. Sampla: ``foo [\"bar\"] ``"

msgid "Attribute lookup. Example: ``foo.bar``"
msgstr "Cuardach tréithe. Sampla: ``foo.bar``"

msgid "List-index lookup. Example: ``foo[bar]``"
msgstr "Cuardach liosta-innéacs. Sampla: ``foo [bar] ``"

msgid ""
"Note that \"bar\" in a template expression like ``{{ foo.bar }}`` will be "
"interpreted as a literal string and not using the value of the variable "
"\"bar\", if one exists in the template context."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go léirmhínítear “barra” i abairt teimpléid cosúil le "
"``{{foo.bar}}`` mar shreang litriúil agus gan úsáid luach an athróg “barra”, "
"má tá ceann ann i gcomhthéacs an teimpléid."

msgid ""
"The template system uses the first lookup type that works. It's short-"
"circuit logic. Here are a few examples:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an córas teimpléid an chéad chineál cuardaigh a oibríonn. Is "
"loighic ghearrchiorcad é. Seo cúpla sampla:"

msgid ""
"If any part of the variable is callable, the template system will try "
"calling it. Example:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá aon chuid den athróg inghlaoch, déanfaidh an córas teimpléid iarracht "
"glaoch air. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"Callable variables are slightly more complex than variables which only "
"require straight lookups. Here are some things to keep in mind:"
msgstr ""
"Tá athróga inghlaonta beagán níos casta ná athróga nach dteastaíonn ach "
"cuardach díreach uathu. Seo roinnt rudaí le coinneáil i gcuimhne:"

msgid ""
"If the variable raises an exception when called, the exception will be "
"propagated, unless the exception has an attribute "
"``silent_variable_failure`` whose value is ``True``. If the exception *does* "
"have a ``silent_variable_failure`` attribute whose value is ``True``, the "
"variable will render as the value of the engine's ``string_if_invalid`` "
"configuration option (an empty string, by default). Example:"
msgstr ""
"Má ardaíonn an t-athróg eisceacht nuair a thugtar air, iomadófar an "
"eisceacht, mura bhfuil tréith ``silent_variable_failure`` ag an eisceacht a "
"luach ``True``. Má tá tréith ``silent_variable_failure`` ag an eisceacht **, "
"a bhfuil a luach ``True``, tabharfaidh an t-athróg mar luach rogha "
"cumraíochta ``string_if_invalid`` an innill (teaghrán folamh, de réir "
"réamhshocraithe). Sampla:"

msgid ""
"Note that :exc:`django.core.exceptions.ObjectDoesNotExist`, which is the "
"base class for all Django database API ``DoesNotExist`` exceptions, has "
"``silent_variable_failure = True``. So if you're using Django templates with "
"Django model objects, any ``DoesNotExist`` exception will fail silently."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil: exc: "
"`Django.Core.Exceptions.ObjectDoesNotExist`, arb é an bunaicme do gach "
"eisceacht API bunachar sonraí Django ``doesNotExist``, ag "
"`silent_variable_fail = True``. Mar sin má tá teimpléid Django á úsáid agat "
"le rudaí samhail Django, teipeann ar aon eisceacht `DoesNotExist` go ciúin."

msgid ""
"A variable can only be called if it has no required arguments. Otherwise, "
"the system will return the value of the engine's ``string_if_invalid`` "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir athróg a ghlaoch ach mura bhfuil aon argóintí riachtanacha aige. "
"Seachas sin, cuirfidh an córas luach rogha `string_if_invalid`` an innill ar "
"ais."

msgid ""
"There can be side effects when calling some variables, and it'd be either "
"foolish or a security hole to allow the template system to access them."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh fo-iarsmaí a bheith ann agus tú ag glaoch ar roinnt athróga, "
"agus bheadh sé amhnach nó poll slándála chun ligean don chóras teimpléid "
"rochtain a fháil orthu."

msgid ""
"A good example is the :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.delete` method on each "
"Django model object. The template system shouldn't be allowed to do "
"something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Sampla maith is ea an modh: meth: `~django.db.models.model.delete` ar gach "
"réad samhail Django. Níor chóir go mbeadh cead ag an gcóras teimpléid rud "
"éigin mar seo a dhéanamh:"

msgid ""
"To prevent this, set an ``alters_data`` attribute on the callable variable. "
"The template system won't call a variable if it has ``alters_data=True`` "
"set, and will instead replace the variable with ``string_if_invalid``, "
"unconditionally.  The dynamically-"
"generated :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.delete` "
"and :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.save` methods on Django model objects get "
"``alters_data=True`` automatically. Example::"
msgstr ""
"Chun é seo a chosc, socraigh tréith ``alters_data`` ar an athróg inghlaonta. "
"Ní ghlaoifidh an córas teimpléid athróg má tá ``alters_data=True`` tacar "
"aige, agus ina ionad sin cuirfidh sé `string_if_invalid`` in ionad an "
"athróg, gan choinníollacha. Faigheann na modhanna: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.delete` agus: meth: `~django.db.models.model.save` "
"ar rudaí samhail Django ``alters_data=true`` go huathoibríoch. Sampla::"

msgid ""
"Occasionally you may want to turn off this feature for other reasons, and "
"tell the template system to leave a variable uncalled no matter what.  To do "
"so, set a ``do_not_call_in_templates`` attribute on the callable with the "
"value ``True``.  The template system then will act as if your variable is "
"not callable (allowing you to access attributes of the callable, for "
"example)."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an ghné seo a mhúchadh ar chúiseanna "
"eile, agus insint don chóras teimpléid athróg a fhágáil gan glaoch is cuma "
"cad é. Chun é sin a dhéanamh, socraigh tréith ``do_not_call_in_templates`` "
"ar an luach ``True``. Gníomhóidh an córas teimpléid ansin amhail is mura "
"bhfuil d'athróg inghlaonta (ligeann duit rochtain a fháil ar thréithe an "
"inghlaonta, mar shampla)."

msgid "How invalid variables are handled"
msgstr "Conas a láimhseáiltear athróga"

msgid ""
"Generally, if a variable doesn't exist, the template system inserts the "
"value of the engine's ``string_if_invalid`` configuration option, which is "
"set to ``''`` (the empty string) by default."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, mura bhfuil athróg ann, cuireann an córas teimpléid luach "
"rogha cumraíochta ``string_if_invalid`` an innill isteach, atá socraithe go "
"````(an teaghrán folamh) de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Filters that are applied to an invalid variable will only be applied if "
"``string_if_invalid`` is set to ``''`` (the empty string). If "
"``string_if_invalid`` is set to any other value, variable filters will be "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirfear scagairí a chuirtear i bhfeidhm ar athróg neamhbhailí ach "
"amháin má shocraítear ``string_if_invalid`` go ````(an teaghrán folamh). Má "
"tá ``string_if_invalid`` socraithe ar aon luach eile, déanfar neamhaird ar "
"scagairí athraitheacha."

msgid ""
"This behavior is slightly different for the ``if``, ``for`` and ``regroup`` "
"template tags. If an invalid variable is provided to one of these template "
"tags, the variable will be interpreted as ``None``. Filters are always "
"applied to invalid variables within these template tags."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-iompar seo beagán difriúil do na clibeanna teimpléad ``if ``, `for`` "
"agus ``athghrúpa``. Má chuirtear athróg neamhbhailí ar fáil do cheann de na "
"clibeanna teimpléad seo, léirmhínítear an t-athróg mar ``None``. Cuirtear "
"scagairí i bhfeidhm i gcónaí ar athróga neamhbhailí laisti"

msgid ""
"If ``string_if_invalid`` contains a ``'%s'``, the format marker will be "
"replaced with the name of the invalid variable."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``string_if_invalid`` ``%s'``, cuirfear ainm an athróg neamhbhailí in "
"ionad an marcóra formáide."

msgid "For debug purposes only!"
msgstr "Chun críocha dífhabhtaithe amháin!"

msgid ""
"While ``string_if_invalid`` can be a useful debugging tool, it is a bad idea "
"to turn it on as a 'development default'."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir le `string_if_invalid`` a bheith ina uirlis dífhabhtaithe "
"úsáideach, is droch-smaoineamh é a chasadh air mar 'réamhshocrú forbartha'."

msgid ""
"Many templates, including some of Django's, rely upon the silence of the "
"template system when a nonexistent variable is encountered. If you assign a "
"value other than ``''`` to ``string_if_invalid``, you will experience "
"rendering problems with these templates and sites."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann go leor teimpléid, lena n-áirítear cuid de Django, ar thús an "
"chórais teimpléid nuair a bhíonn athróg nach bhfuil ann. Má shannann tú "
"luach seachas ``\"``do `string_if_invalid``, beidh fadhbanna rindreála agat "
"leis na teimpléid agus na suíomhanna seo."

msgid ""
"Generally, ``string_if_invalid`` should only be enabled in order to debug a "
"specific template problem, then cleared once debugging is complete."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, níor cheart ``string_if_invalid`` a chumasú ach d'fhonn fadhb "
"teimpléad ar leith a dhífhabhtú, ansin a ghlanadh nuair a bheidh dífhabhtú "
"críochnaithe."

msgid "Built-in variables"
msgstr "Athróga ionsuite"

msgid ""
"Every context contains ``True``, ``False`` and ``None``. As you would "
"expect, these variables resolve to the corresponding Python objects."
msgstr ""
"I ngach comhthéacs tá ``True``, `Fréag`` agus ``None``. Mar a bheadh ag súil "
"leat, réitíonn na hathróga seo ar na rudaí comhfhreagracha Python"

msgid "Limitations with string literals"
msgstr "Teorainneacha le litríochtaí teaghrán"

msgid ""
"Django's template language has no way to escape the characters used for its "
"own syntax. For example, the :ttag:`templatetag` tag is required if you need "
"to output character sequences like ``{%`` and ``%}``."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon bhealach ag teanga teimpléad Django éalú ó na carachtair a úsáidtear "
"dá chomhréir féin. Mar shampla, teastaíonn an clibe:ttag: `templatetag` más "
"gá duit seicheamh carachtair mar ``{%`` agus ``%}`` a aschur."

msgid ""
"A similar issue exists if you want to include these sequences in template "
"filter or tag arguments. For example, when parsing a block tag, Django's "
"template parser looks for the first occurrence of ``%}`` after a ``{%``. "
"This prevents the use of ``\"%}\"`` as a string literal. For example, a "
"``TemplateSyntaxError`` will be raised for the following expressions:"
msgstr ""
"Tá saincheist den chineál céanna ann más mian leat na seicheamh seo a chur "
"san áireamh i scagaire teimpléid nó i gclibeanna Mar shampla, agus clib bloc "
"á pháirseáil, féachann parser teimpléad Django ar an gcéad tarlú de ``%} "
"``tar éis`` {%``. Cuireann sé seo cosc ar ``\"%} \"``a úsáid mar shreang "
"litriúil. Mar shampla, ardófar ``TemplateSyntaxError`` do na nathanna seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"The same issue can be triggered by using a reserved sequence in filter "
"arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an tsaincheist chéanna a spreagadh trí sheicheamh áirithe a úsáid "
"in argóintí scagaire:"

msgid ""
"If you need to use strings with these sequences, store them in template "
"variables or use a custom template tag or filter to workaround the "
"limitation."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit teaghráin a úsáid leis na seicheamh seo, stóráil iad in athróga "
"teimpléad nó bain úsáid as clib nó scagaire teimpléad saincheaptha chun an "
"teorannú a réiteach."

msgid "Playing with ``Context`` objects"
msgstr "Ag imirt le rudaí ``Context``"

msgid ""
"Most of the time, you'll instantiate :class:`Context` objects by passing in "
"a fully-populated dictionary to ``Context()``. But you can add and delete "
"items from a ``Context`` object once it's been instantiated, too, using "
"standard dictionary syntax:"
msgstr ""
"An chuid is mó den am, cuirfidh tú rudaí:class: `Context` trí fhoclóir lán-"
"dhaonra a chur isteach chuig ``Context () ``. Ach is féidir leat míreanna a "
"chur leis agus a scriosadh ó réad ``Context`` nuair a bheidh sé curtha "
"isteach freisin, ag baint úsáide as comhréir caighdeánach foclóra:"

msgid ""
"Returns the value for ``key`` if ``key`` is in the context, else returns "
"``otherwise``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an luach le haghaidh ``eochair`` má tá ``eochair`` sa chomhthéacs, "
"arís eile filleann ````eile ``."

msgid ""
"If ``key`` is in the context, returns its value. Otherwise inserts ``key`` "
"with a value of ``default`` and returns ``default``."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``eochair`` sa chomhthéacs, filleann sé a luach ar ais. Seachas sin "
"cuireann sé isteach ``eochair`` le luach ``default`` agus tugann sé "
"``default`` ar ais."

msgid ""
"A ``Context`` object is a stack. That is, you can ``push()`` and ``pop()`` "
"it. If you ``pop()`` too much, it'll raise "
"``django.template.ContextPopException``:"
msgstr ""
"Is cruach é réad ``Context``. Is é sin, is féidir leat ``bhrú () ``agus "
"``pop ()`` é. Má tá tú ``pop () ``an iomarca, ardóidh sé "
"``django.template.contextPopException``:"

msgid ""
"You can also use ``push()`` as a context manager to ensure a matching "
"``pop()`` is called."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``push () ``a úsáid freisin mar bhainisteoir comhthéacs chun "
"a chinntiú go dtugtar meaitseáil ``pop ()``."

msgid ""
"All arguments passed to ``push()`` will be passed to the ``dict`` "
"constructor used to build the new context level."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfear gach argóint a chuirtear chuig `push () ``chuig an tógálaí ``dict`` "
"a úsáidtear chun an leibhéal comhthéacs nua a thógáil."

msgid ""
"In addition to ``push()`` and ``pop()``, the ``Context`` object also defines "
"an ``update()`` method. This works like ``push()`` but takes a dictionary as "
"an argument and pushes that dictionary onto the stack instead of an empty "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le ``push () ``agus `pop ()``, sainmhíníonn an réad ``Context`` "
"modh ``update () ``freisin. Oibríonn sé seo cosúil le ``push () ``ach "
"glacann sé foclóir mar argóint agus brúíonn sé an foclóir sin ar an gcruach "
"in ionad ceann folamh."

msgid ""
"Like ``push()``, you can use ``update()`` as a context manager to ensure a "
"matching ``pop()`` is called."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le ``push () ``, is féidir leat ``update ()`` a úsáid mar "
"bhainisteoir comhthéacs chun a chinntiú go dtugtar meaitseáil ``pop () ``."

msgid ""
"Using a ``Context`` as a stack comes in handy in :ref:`some custom template "
"tags <howto-writing-custom-template-tags>`."
msgstr ""
"<howto-writing-custom-template-tags>Tagann ``Context`` a úsáid mar chruac "
"úsáideach in:ref: `roinnt clibeanna teimpléad saincheapaithe`."

msgid ""
"Using ``flatten()`` method you can get whole ``Context`` stack as one "
"dictionary including builtin variables."
msgstr ""
"Ag baint úsáide as modh ``flatten () ``is féidir leat cruach ``Context`` "
"iomlán a fháil mar fhoclóir amháin lena n-áirítear athróga tógála."

msgid ""
"A ``flatten()`` method is also internally used to make ``Context`` objects "
"comparable."
msgstr ""
"Úsáidtear modh `flatten () ``go hinmheánach freisin chun rudaí ``Context`` a "
"dhéanamh inchomparáide."

msgid ""
"Result from ``flatten()`` can be useful in unit tests to compare ``Context`` "
"against ``dict``::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an toradh ó `flatten () ``a bheith úsáideach i dtástálacha "
"aonaid chun comparáid a dhéanamh idir ``Context`` i gcoinne ``dict``:"

msgid "Using ``RequestContext``"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ``requestContext``"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a special :class:`~django.template.Context` class, "
"``django.template.RequestContext``, that acts slightly differently from the "
"normal ``django.template.Context``. The first difference is that it takes "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` as its first argument. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le rang speisialt:class: `~django.template.context`, "
"``Django.Template.requestContext``, a ghníomhaíonn beagán difriúil ón "
"ngnáth`django.template.context``. Is é an chéad difríocht ná go dtógann sé "
"an:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` mar a chéad argóint. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"The second difference is that it automatically populates the context with a "
"few variables, according to the engine's ``context_processors`` "
"configuration option."
msgstr ""
"Is é an dara difríocht ná go ndéanann sé an comhthéacs a líonadh go "
"huathoibríoch le cúpla athróg, de réir rogha cumraíochta "
"``context_processors' an innill."

msgid ""
"The ``context_processors`` option is a list of callables -- called **context "
"processors** -- that take a request object as their argument and return a "
"dictionary of items to be merged into the context. In the default generated "
"settings file, the default template engine contains the following context "
"processors::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an rogha `context_processors`` liosta de ghlaonna -- ar a dtugtar "
"**próiseálaithe comhthéacsa** -- a ghlacann réad iarratais mar argóint agus "
"a thugann foclóir míreanna atá le cumasc sa chomhthéacs. Sa chomhad "
"socruithe réamhshocraithe a ghintear, tá na próiseálaithe comhthéacs seo a "
"leanas san inneall teimpléid réamh"

msgid ""
"In addition to these, :class:`RequestContext` always enables "
"``'django.template.context_processors.csrf'``.  This is a security related "
"context processor required by the admin and other contrib apps, and, in case "
"of accidental misconfiguration, it is deliberately hardcoded in and cannot "
"be turned off in the ``context_processors`` option."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis seo, cumasaíonn :class: `RequestContext` "
"```django.template.context_processors.csrf'`` i gcónaí. Is próiseálaí "
"comhthéacs a bhaineann le slándáil é seo a éilíonn an riarachán agus "
"aipeanna contrib eile, agus, i gcás míchchumraíochta de thaisme, déantar é a "
"chóstáil isteach d'aon ghnó agus ní féidir é a mhúchadh sa rogha "
"`context_processors`."

msgid ""
"Each processor is applied in order. That means, if one processor adds a "
"variable to the context and a second processor adds a variable with the same "
"name, the second will override the first. The default processors are "
"explained below."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear gach próiseálaí i bhfeidhm in ord. Ciallaíonn sé sin, má chuireann "
"próiseálaí amháin athróg leis an gcomhthéacs agus má chuireann an dara "
"próiseálaí athróg leis an ainm céanna, cuirfidh an dara ceann ar an gcéad "
"cheann. Mínítear na próiseálaithe réamhshocraithe thíos"

msgid "When context processors are applied"
msgstr "Nuair a bhíonn próiseálaithe comhthéacs"

msgid ""
"Context processors are applied on top of context data. This means that a "
"context processor may overwrite variables you've supplied to "
"your :class:`Context` or :class:`RequestContext`, so take care to avoid "
"variable names that overlap with those supplied by your context processors."
msgstr ""
"Déantar próiseálaithe comhthéacs i bhfeidhm ar bharr sonraí comhthéacs "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo go bhféadfadh próiseálaí comhthéacs athróga a sholáthraigh "
"tú do d:class: `Context` nó:class: `RequestContext`, mar sin bí cúramach "
"ainmneacha athraitheacha a sheachaint a fhorluíonn leo siúd a sholáthraíonn "
"do phróiseálaithe comhthéacs."

msgid ""
"If you want context data to take priority over context processors, use the "
"following pattern::"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat go dtógfadh sonraí comhthéacs tosaíocht ar phróiseálaithe "
"comhthéacs, bain úsáid as an patrún seo a leanas"

msgid ""
"Django does this to allow context data to override context processors in "
"APIs such as :func:`~django.shortcuts.render` "
"and :class:`~django.template.response.TemplateResponse`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann Django é seo chun ligean do shonraí comhthéacs próiseálaithe "
"comhthéacs a shárú in APIs mar: func: `~django.shortcuts.render` agus:class: "
"`~django.template.response.templateResponse`."

msgid ""
"Also, you can give :class:`RequestContext` a list of additional processors, "
"using the optional, third positional argument, ``processors``. In this "
"example, the :class:`RequestContext` instance gets an ``ip_address`` "
"variable::"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, is féidir leat liosta de phróiseálaithe breise a "
"thabhar:class: `RequestContext`, ag baint úsáide as an tríú argóint roghnach "
"suímh, ``próiseálaithe ``. Sa sampla seo, faigheann an sampla:class: "
"`requestContext` athróg ``ip_address ``:"

msgid "Built-in template context processors"
msgstr "Próiseálaithe comhthéacs teimplé"

msgid "Here's what each of the built-in processors does:"
msgstr "Seo a dhéanann gach ceann de na próiseálaithe ionsuite:"

msgid "``django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth``"
msgstr "``django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain these "
"variables:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh na hathróga seo i ngach "
"``RequestContext``:"

msgid ""
"``user`` -- An ``auth.User`` instance representing the currently logged-in "
"user (or an ``AnonymousUser`` instance, if the client isn't logged in)."
msgstr ""
"``user`` -- Sampla ``Auth.user`` a léiríonn an t-úsáideoir atá logáilte "
"isteach faoi láthair (nó sampla ``AnonymousUser`, mura bhfuil an cliant "
"logáilte isteach)."

msgid ""
"``perms`` -- An instance of "
"``django.contrib.auth.context_processors.PermWrapper``, representing the "
"permissions that the currently logged-in user has."
msgstr ""
"``perms`` -- Sampla de "
"`django.contrib.auth.context_processors.permWrapper``, a léiríonn na "
"ceadanna atá ag an úsáideoir logáilte isteach faoi láthair."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.debug``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.debug``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain these "
"two variables -- but only if your :setting:`DEBUG` setting is set to "
"``True`` and the request's IP address (``request.META['REMOTE_ADDR']``) is "
"in the :setting:`INTERNAL_IPS` setting:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh an dá athróg seo i ngach "
"``RequestContext`` - ach amháin má tá do shuíomh: `DEBUG` socraithe go "
"`True`` agus seoladh IP an iarratais (``Request.meta ['REMOTE_ADDR'] ``) sa "
"socrú: `INTERNAL_IPS`:"

msgid ""
"``debug`` -- ``True``. You can use this in templates to test whether you're "
"in :setting:`DEBUG` mode."
msgstr ""
"``debug`` -- ``Fíor-``. Is féidir leat é seo a úsáid i dteimpléid chun a "
"thástáil an bhfuil tú i mód: socrú: `DEBUG`."

msgid ""
"``sql_queries`` -- A list of ``{'sql': ..., 'time': ...}`` dictionaries, "
"representing every SQL query that has happened so far during the request and "
"how long it took. The list is in order by database alias and then by query. "
"It's lazily generated on access."
msgstr ""
"``sql_queries`` -- Liosta de ``{'sql':..., 'time':...}`` foclóirí, a "
"léiríonn gach ceist SQL a tharla go dtí seo le linn an iarratais agus cé "
"chomh fada a thóg sé. Tá an liosta in ord de réir alias bunachar sonraí agus "
"ansin trí cheist. Gintear sé go leisciúil ar rochtain."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.i18n``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.i18n``"

msgid "``LANGUAGES`` -- The value of the :setting:`LANGUAGES` setting."
msgstr "``LANGUAGES`` - Luach an shocraithe:setting: `LANGUAGES`."

msgid ""
"``LANGUAGE_BIDI`` -- ``True`` if the current language is a right-to-left "
"language, e.g. Hebrew, Arabic. ``False`` if it's a left-to-right language, "
"e.g. English, French, German."
msgstr ""
"``LANGUAGE_BIDI`` - ``True`` má tá teanga reatha ina theanga ar dheis go "
"clé, m.sh. an Eabhrais, Araibis. ``Fréag`` más teanga de chlé go deis í, "
"m.sh. Béarla, Fraincis, Gearmáinis."

msgid ""
"``LANGUAGE_CODE`` -- ``request.LANGUAGE_CODE``, if it exists. Otherwise, the "
"value of the :setting:`LANGUAGE_CODE` setting."
msgstr ""
"``LANGUAGE_COD`` -- ``REQUEST.LANGUAGE_COD``, má tá sé ann. Seachas sin, "
"luach an socrú: setting: `LANGUAGE_CODE`."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`i18n template tags <i18n-template-tags>` for template tags that "
"generate the same values."
msgstr ""
"Féach: ref: clibeanna teimpléad `i18n <i18n-template-tags>`le haghaidh "
"clibeanna teimpléad a ghineann na luachanna céanna."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.media``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.media ``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain a "
"variable ``MEDIA_URL``, providing the value of the :setting:`MEDIA_URL` "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh athróg ``MEDIA_URL` i ngach "
"``RequestContext``, ag soláthar luach an socruithe: `MEDIA_URL`."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.static``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.static``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain a "
"variable ``STATIC_URL``, providing the value of the :setting:`STATIC_URL` "
"setting."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh athróg ``STATIC_URL` i ngach "
"``RequestContext``, ag soláthar luach an socruithe: `STATIC_URL`."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.csrf``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.csrf``"

msgid ""
"This processor adds a token that is needed by the :ttag:`csrf_token` "
"template tag for protection against :doc:`Cross Site Request Forgeries </ref/"
"csrf>`."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an próiseálaí seo comhartha a theastaíonn ó chlib teimpléad:ttag: "
"`csrf_token` le haghaidh cosanta in aghaidh: doc: `Cross Site Request "
"Forgeries` </ref/csrf>."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.request``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.request``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain a "
"variable ``request``, which is the current :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh athróg ``request`` i ngach "
"`requestContext``, arb é sin an reatha:class: `~django.http.httpRequest`."

msgid "``django.template.context_processors.tz``"
msgstr "``django.template.context_processors.tz``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain a "
"variable ``TIME_ZONE``, providing the name of the currently active time zone."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh athróg ``TIME_ZONE`` i ngach "
"`RequestContext``, ag soláthar ainm an chrios ama atá gníomhach faoi láthair."

msgid "``django.contrib.messages.context_processors.messages``"
msgstr ""
"``django.contrib.teachtaireachtaí context_processors.teachtaireachtaí ``"

msgid ""
"If this processor is enabled, every ``RequestContext`` will contain these "
"two variables:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá an próiseálaí seo cumasaithe, beidh an dá athróg seo i ngach "
"``RequestContext``:"

msgid ""
"``messages`` -- A list of messages (as strings) that have been set via "
"the :doc:`messages framework </ref/contrib/messages>`."
msgstr ""
"``teachtaireachtaí ``- Liosta teachtaireachtaí (mar theagáin) atá socraithe "
"trí:doc: `teachtaireachtaí creata'. </ref/contrib/messages>"

msgid ""
"``DEFAULT_MESSAGE_LEVELS`` -- A mapping of the message level names "
"to :ref:`their numeric value <message-level-constants>`."
msgstr ""
"<message-level-constants>``DEFAULT_MESSAGE_LEVELS`` - Mapáil ar ainmneacha "
"leibhéal na teachtaireachta chuig:ref: `a luach uimhriúil `."

msgid "Writing your own context processors"
msgstr "Scríobh do phróiseálaithe comhthéacs"

msgid ""
"A context processor has a simple interface: It's a Python function that "
"takes one argument, an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object, and returns "
"a dictionary that gets added to the template context."
msgstr ""
"Tá comhéadan simplí ag próiseálaí comhthéacs: Is feidhm Python é a thógann "
"argóint amháin, an:class: `~django.http.httpRequest` réad, agus a thugann "
"foclóir ar ais a chuirtear le comhthéacs an teimpléid."

msgid ""
"For example, to add the :setting:`DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` setting to every "
"context::"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, chun an socrú:setting: `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` a chur le gach "
"comhthéacs::"

msgid ""
"Custom context processors can live anywhere in your code base. All Django "
"cares about is that your custom context processors are pointed to by the "
"``'context_processors'`` option in your :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting — or "
"the ``context_processors`` argument of :class:`~django.template.Engine` if "
"you're using it directly."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le próiseálaithe comhthéacs saincheaptha maireachtáil áit ar bith "
"i do Is é an cúram le Django ná go ndéanann an rogha ``context_processors'` "
"i do shocrú: `TEMPLATES` - nó an argóint ``context_processors`` de:class: "
"`~django.template.ENGINE` má tá tú ag úsáid go díreach é."

msgid "Loading templates"
msgstr "Teimpléid á lódáil"

msgid ""
"Generally, you'll store templates in files on your filesystem rather than "
"using the low-level :class:`~django.template.Template` API yourself. Save "
"templates in a directory specified as a **template directory**."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, stóráilfidh tú teimpléid i gcomhaid ar do chóras comhaid "
"seachas an API ísealleibhéil: class: `~django.template.template` a úsáid tú "
"féin. Sábháil teimpléid in eolaire a shonraítear mar eolaire teimpléad**."

msgid ""
"Django searches for template directories in a number of places, depending on "
"your template loading settings (see \"Loader types\" below), but the most "
"basic way of specifying template directories is by using the :setting:`DIRS "
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>` option."
msgstr ""
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>Déanann Django cuardach ar eolairí teimpléid i roinnt "
"áiteanna, ag brath ar do shocruithe luchtaithe teimpléad (féach “Cineálacha "
"lódóra” thíos), ach is é an bealach is bunúsaí chun eolairí teimpléad a "
"shonrú ná an rogha: socrú: `DIRS `a úsáid."

msgid "The :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` option"
msgstr "<TEMPLATES-DIRS>An rogha: Socrú: `DIRS`"

msgid ""
"Tell Django what your template directories are by using the :setting:`DIRS "
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>` option in the :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting in your "
"settings file — or the ``dirs`` argument "
"of :class:`~django.template.Engine`. This should be set to a list of strings "
"that contain full paths to your template directories::"
msgstr ""
"Inis do Django cad iad d'eolair <TEMPLATES-DIRS>í teimpléad tríd an rogha: "
"setting: `DIRS `a úsáid sa socrú: `TEMPLATES` i do chomhad socruithe - nó an "
"argóint `dirs`` de:class: `~DJANGO.TEMPLATE.ENGINE`. Ba chóir é seo a shocrú "
"ar liosta teaghráin ina bhfuil cosáin iomlána chuig d'eolairí teimpléid::"

msgid ""
"Your templates can go anywhere you want, as long as the directories and "
"templates are readable by the web server. They can have any extension you "
"want, such as ``.html`` or ``.txt``, or they can have no extension at all."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le do theimpléid dul áit ar bith is mian leat, fad is atá na "
"heolairí agus na teimpléid inléite ag an bhfreastalaí gréasáin. Is féidir "
"leo aon síneadh a theastaíonn uait a bheith acu, mar shampla ``.html`` nó "
"``.txt``, nó ní féidir leo aon síneadh a bheith acu ar chor ar bith."

msgid "Loader types"
msgstr "Cineálacha lódóra"

msgid ""
"By default, Django uses a filesystem-based template loader, but Django comes "
"with a few other template loaders, which know how to load templates from "
"other sources."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáideann Django lódóir teimpléad bunaithe ar "
"chóras comhaid, ach tagann Django le cúpla luchtaire teimpléad eile, a "
"bhfuil a fhios acu conas teimpléid a luchtú ó fhoinsí eile."

msgid ""
"Some of these other loaders are disabled by default, but you can activate "
"them by adding a ``'loaders'`` option to your ``DjangoTemplates`` backend in "
"the :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting or passing a ``loaders`` argument "
"to :class:`~django.template.Engine`. ``loaders`` should be a list of strings "
"or tuples, where each represents a template loader class. Here are the "
"template loaders that come with Django:"
msgstr ""
"Tá cuid de na luchtóirí eile seo díchumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe, ach "
"is féidir leat iad a ghníomhachtú trí rogha ``'loaders'` a chur le do "
"chúlcheann ``DjangoTemplates`` sa socrú:setting: `TEMPLATES` nó argóint "
"``loaders`` a chur chuig:class: `~django.template.ENGINE`. Ba chóir go "
"mbeadh “loaders” ina liosta de shreangáin nó tupáil, áit a léiríonn gach "
"ceann acu rang lódóra teimpléid. Seo iad na lódálaithe teimpléad a thagann "
"le Django:"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.filesystem.Loader``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Filesystem.Loader``"

msgid ""
"Loads templates from the filesystem, according to :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-"
"DIRS>`."
msgstr ""
"<TEMPLATES-DIRS>Luchtaíonn teimpléid ón gcóras comhaid, de réir: socrú: "
"`DIRS `."

msgid ""
"This loader is enabled by default. However it won't find any templates until "
"you set :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` to a non-empty list::"
msgstr ""
"Tá an lódóir seo cumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe. Mar sin féin ní "
"gheobhaidh sé aon teimpléid go dtí go socraíonn tú: socrú: `DIRS <TEMPLATES-"
"DIRS>`ar liosta neamh-folamh::"

msgid ""
"You can also override ``'DIRS'`` and specify specific directories for a "
"particular filesystem loader::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat ``DIRS'`` a shárú freisin agus eolairí ar leith a shonrú le "
"haghaidh lódóir córas comhaid áirithe:"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.app_directories.Loader``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.App_Directories.Loader``"

msgid ""
"Loads templates from Django apps on the filesystem. For each app "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, the loader looks for a ``templates`` "
"subdirectory. If the directory exists, Django looks for templates in there."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn teimpléid ó aipeanna Django ar an gcóras comhaid. I gcás gach aip "
"in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS`, féachann an lódóir fo-eolaire ``teimpléid ``. "
"Má tá an eolaire ann, féachann Django teimpléid ann."

msgid ""
"This means you can store templates with your individual apps. This also "
"helps to distribute Django apps with default templates."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat teimpléid a stóráil le d'aipeanna aonair. "
"Cuidíonn sé seo freisin le apps Django a dháileadh le teimpléid "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid "For example, for this setting::"
msgstr "Mar shampla, don socrú seo:"

msgid ""
"...then ``get_template('foo.html')`` will look for ``foo.html`` in these "
"directories, in this order:"
msgstr ""
"... ansin cuardóidh ``get_template ('foo.html') ```foo.html`` sna heolairí "
"seo, san ord seo:"

msgid "``/path/to/myproject/polls/templates/``"
msgstr "``/cosáin/to/mo thionscad/truailleach/teimpléidí/``"

msgid "``/path/to/myproject/music/templates/``"
msgstr "``/cosáin/to/mo thionscad/ceol/teimpléidí/``"

msgid "... and will use the one it finds first."
msgstr "... agus úsáidfidh sé an ceann a aimsíonn sé ar dtús."

msgid ""
"The order of :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` is significant! For example, if you "
"want to customize the Django admin, you might choose to override the "
"standard ``admin/base_site.html`` template, from ``django.contrib.admin``, "
"with your own ``admin/base_site.html`` in ``myproject.polls``. You must then "
"make sure that your ``myproject.polls`` comes *before* "
"``django.contrib.admin`` in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, otherwise "
"``django.contrib.admin``’s will be loaded first and yours will be ignored."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-ordú de:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` suntasach! Mar shampla, más mian "
"leat riarachán Django a shaincheapadh, b'fhéidir go roghnaíonn tú an "
"teimpléad caighdeánach ``admin/base_site.html` a shárú, ó "
"``django.contrib.admin ``, le do `admin/base_site.html`` féin i "
"``myproject.polls``. Ní mór duit a chinntiú ansin go dtagann do "
"``myproject.polls`` *roim* ``django.contrib.admin`` in:setting: "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`, ar shlí eile luchtálfar ``django.contrib.admin`` ar dtús "
"agus déanfar neamhaird ar do chuid féin."

msgid ""
"Note that the loader performs an optimization when it first runs: it caches "
"a list of which :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` packages have a ``templates`` "
"subdirectory."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go ndéanann an lódóir barrfheabhsú nuair a ritheann sé ar "
"dtús: cuireann sé liosta díobh a bhfuil fo-eolaire ``teimpléid ``ag "
"pacáistí: 'SETTING: `INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid ""
"You can enable this loader by setting :setting:`APP_DIRS <TEMPLATES-"
"APP_DIRS>` to ``True``::"
msgstr ""
"<TEMPLATES-APP_DIRS>Is féidir leat an lódóir seo a chumasú trí shocrú: "
"socrú: `APP_DIRS `go ``True``:"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.cached.Loader``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader``"

msgid ""
"While the Django template system is quite fast, if it needs to read and "
"compile your templates every time they're rendered, the overhead from that "
"can add up."
msgstr ""
"Cé go bhfuil córas teimpléid Django tapa go leor, más gá dó do theimpléid a "
"léamh agus a thiomsú gach uair a dhéantar iad a léiriú, is féidir leis an "
"lasbhreas as sin cur suas."

msgid ""
"You configure the cached template loader with a list of other loaders that "
"it should wrap. The wrapped loaders are used to locate unknown templates "
"when they're first encountered. The cached loader then stores the compiled "
"``Template`` in memory. The cached ``Template`` instance is returned for "
"subsequent requests to load the same template."
msgstr ""
"Cumraíonn tú an lódóir teimpléad taisceáilte le liosta de luchtóirí eile ar "
"chóir dó fillteadh. Úsáidtear na lódálaithe fillte chun teimpléid anaithnid "
"a aimsiú nuair a bhíonn siad ar dtús. Ansin stóráilíonn an lódóir "
"taisceáilte an ``Teimpléad` tiomsaithe i gcuimhne. Cuirtear an cás "
"“Teimpléad” a chosc ar ais le haghaidh iarratais ina dhiaidh sin chun an "
"teimpléad céanna a luchtú."

msgid ""
"This loader is automatically enabled if :setting:`OPTIONS['loaders'] "
"<TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>` isn't specified."
msgstr ""
"Cumasaítear an lódóir seo go huathoibríoch mura ndéantar: socrú: `OPTIONS "
"['loader'] <TEMPLATES-OPTIONS>`a shonrú."

msgid ""
"You can manually specify template caching with some custom template loaders "
"using settings like this::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat taiscáil teimpléad a shonrú de láimh le roinnt lódóirí "
"teimpléad saincheaptha ag baint úsáide as socruithe"

msgid ""
"All of the built-in Django template tags are safe to use with the cached "
"loader, but if you're using custom template tags that come from third party "
"packages, or that you wrote yourself, you should ensure that the ``Node`` "
"implementation for each tag is thread-safe. For more information, "
"see :ref:`template tag thread safety considerations "
"<template_tag_thread_safety>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach ceann de na clibeanna teimpléad Django ionsuite sábháilte le húsáid "
"leis an lódóir taisce, ach má tá clibeanna teimpléad saincheaptha á úsáid "
"agat a thagann ó phacáistí tríú páirtí, nó a scríobh tú tú féin, ba cheart "
"duit a chinntiú go bhfuil cur i bhfeidhm ``Node ``do gach clib sábháilte ó "
"snáithe. <template_tag_thread_safety>Le haghaidh tuilleadh faisnéise, "
"féach:ref: `breithnithe sábháilteachta snáithe clib teimpléad"

msgid "``django.template.loaders.locmem.Loader``"
msgstr "``Django.Template.Loaders.Locmem.Loader``"

msgid "Loads templates from a Python dictionary. This is useful for testing."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn teimpléid ó fhoclóir Python. Tá sé seo úsáideach le haghaidh "
"tástála."

msgid "This loader takes a dictionary of templates as its first argument::"
msgstr "Glacann an lódóir seo foclóir teimpléid mar an chéad argóint:"

msgid "This loader is disabled by default."
msgstr "Tá an lódóir seo díchumasaithe de réir réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"Django uses the template loaders in order according to the ``'loaders'`` "
"option. It uses each loader until a loader finds a match."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann Django na lódálaithe teimpléad in ord de réir an rogha "
"```loaders'. Úsáideann sé gach lódóir go dtí go bhfaigheann lódóir cluiche."

msgid "Custom loaders"
msgstr "Luchtaithe saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"It's possible to load templates from additional sources using custom "
"template loaders. Custom ``Loader`` classes should inherit from "
"``django.template.loaders.base.Loader`` and define the ``get_contents()`` "
"and ``get_template_sources()`` methods."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir teimpléid a luchtú ó fhoinsí breise ag baint úsáide as luchtóirí "
"teimpléad sain Ba chóir go n-oidhreodh ranganna saincheaptha ``Loader`` ó "
"`django.template.loaders.base.loader`` agus na modhanna ``get_contents () "
"``agus ``get_template_sources ()`` a shainiú."

msgid "Loader methods"
msgstr "Modhanna lódóra"

msgid ""
"Loads templates from a given source, such as the filesystem or a database."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn teimpléid ó fhoinse ar leith, mar shampla an córas comhaid nó "
"bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"A method that takes a ``template_name`` and "
"yields :class:`~django.template.base.Origin` instances for each possible "
"source."
msgstr ""
"Modh a thógann ``template_name`` agus a thugann torthaige:class: "
"`~django.template.base.origin` cásanna do gach foinse féideartha."

msgid ""
"For example, the filesystem loader may receive ``'index.html'`` as a "
"``template_name`` argument.  This method would yield origins for the full "
"path of ``index.html`` as it appears in each template directory the loader "
"looks at."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, féadfaidh lódóir an chórais chomhaid ``index.html'`` a fháil "
"mar argóint ``template_name``. Tabharfadh an modh seo bunús don chonair "
"iomlán “index.html” mar atá le feiceáil i ngach eolaire teimpléad a "
"bhreathnaíonn an lódóir air."

msgid ""
"The method doesn't need to verify that the template exists at a given path, "
"but it should ensure the path is valid. For instance, the filesystem loader "
"makes sure the path lies under a valid template directory."
msgstr ""
"Ní gá don modh a fhíorú go bhfuil an teimpléad ann ag cosán ar leith, ach ba "
"cheart dó a chinntiú go bhfuil an cosán bailí. Mar shampla, cinntíonn lódóir "
"an chórais chomhaid go bhfuil an cosán faoi eolaire teimpléad bailí."

msgid ""
"Returns the contents for a template given "
"a :class:`~django.template.base.Origin` instance."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an t-ábhar do theimpléad a thugtar a: class: "
"`~django.template.base.origin` sampla."

msgid ""
"This is where a filesystem loader would read contents from the filesystem, "
"or a database loader would read from the database. If a matching template "
"doesn't exist, this should raise "
"a :exc:`~django.template.TemplateDoesNotExist` error."
msgstr ""
"Seo an áit a léifeadh lódóir córas comhaid ábhar ón gcóras comhaid, nó go "
"léifeadh lódóir bunachar sonraí ón mbunachar sonraí. Mura bhfuil teimpléad "
"meaitseála ann, ba chóir dó seo earráid a:exc: "
"`~django.template.templateDoesNotExist` a ardú."

msgid ""
"Returns a ``Template`` object for a given ``template_name`` by looping "
"through results from :meth:`get_template_sources` and "
"calling :meth:`get_contents`. This returns the first matching template. If "
"no template is found, :exc:`~django.template.TemplateDoesNotExist` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé réad ``Template`` ar ais do ``template_name`` ar leith trí lupáil "
"trí thorthaí ó:meth: `get_template_sources` agus glaoch: meth: "
"`get_contents`. Filleann sé seo an chéad teimpléad meaitseála. Mura "
"bhfaightear aon teimpléad, ardaítear :exc: "
"`~django.template.templateDoesNotExist`."

msgid ""
"The optional ``skip`` argument is a list of origins to ignore when extending "
"templates. This allow templates to extend other templates of the same name. "
"It also used to avoid recursion errors."
msgstr ""
"Is é an argóint roghnach `skip ``ná liosta de bhunús le neamhaird a dhéanamh "
"agus teimpléid á leathnú. Ligeann sé seo teimpléid teimpléid eile den ainm "
"céanna a leathnú. D'úsáid sé freisin chun earráidí athshlánaithe a "
"sheachaint."

msgid ""
"In general, it is enough to define :meth:`get_template_sources` "
"and :meth:`get_contents` for custom template loaders. ``get_template()`` "
"will usually not need to be overridden."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, is leor sainmhíniú: meth: `get_template_sources` agus:meth: "
"`get_contents` le haghaidh lódóirí teimpléad saincheaptha. De ghnáth ní gá "
"`get_template () ``a shárú."

msgid "Building your own"
msgstr "Tógáil do chuid féin"

msgid ""
"For examples, read the :source:`source code for Django's built-in loaders "
"<django/template/loaders>`."
msgstr ""
"<django/template/loaders>Mar shamplaí, léigh an:source: `cód foinse do "
"luchtóirí ionsuite Django`."

msgid "Template origin"
msgstr "Bunús teimpléad"

msgid ""
"Templates have an ``origin`` containing attributes depending on the source "
"they are loaded from."
msgstr ""
"Tá “bunús” ag teimpléid ina bhfuil tréithe ag brath ar an bhfoinse as a "
"luchtaítear iad."

msgid ""
"The path to the template as returned by the template loader. For loaders "
"that read from the file system, this is the full path to the template."
msgstr ""
"An cosán chuig an teimpléad mar a chuir an lódóir teimpléid ar ais. Maidir "
"le luchtóirí a léann ón gcóras comhaid, is é seo an cosán iomlán chuig an "
"teimpléad."

msgid ""
"If the template is instantiated directly rather than through a template "
"loader, this is a string value of ``<unknown_source>``."
msgstr ""
"<unknown_source>Má dhéantar an teimpléad a thionscnamh go díreach seachas "
"trí lódóir teimpléid, is luach teaghrán é seo de ```."

msgid "The relative path to the template as passed into the template loader."
msgstr ""
"An cosán coibhneasta chuig an teimpléad mar a rith isteach sa lódóir "
"teimpléad"

msgid ""
"If the template is instantiated directly rather than through a template "
"loader, this is ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéantar an teimpléad a thionscnamh go díreach seachas trí lódóir "
"teimpléid, is é seo ``None``."

msgid "The template loader instance that constructed this ``Origin``."
msgstr "An tsampla lódóir teimpléad a thóg an ``Bunaid' seo."

msgid ""
":class:`django.template.loaders.cached.Loader` requires all of its wrapped "
"loaders to set this attribute, typically by instantiating the ``Origin`` "
"with ``loader=self``."
msgstr ""
":class: `Django.Template.Loaders.Cached.Loader` éilíonn ar a luchtóirí "
"fillte go léir an tréith seo a shocrú, de ghnáth tríd an ``Origin`` a chur "
"isteach le ``loader=self``."

msgid "Built-in template tags and filters"
msgstr "Clibeanna teimpléad ionsuite agus scagair"

msgid ""
"This document describes Django's built-in template tags and filters. It is "
"recommended that you use the :doc:`automatic documentation </ref/contrib/"
"admin/admindocs>`, if available, as this will also include documentation for "
"any custom tags or filters installed."
msgstr ""
"Déanann an doiciméad seo cur síos ar chlibeanna agus scagairí teimpléad ion "
"Moltar duit an doiciméadú uathoibríoch: doc: a úsáid, má tá sé ar fáil, mar "
"beidh cáipéisíocht ann freisin le haghaidh aon chlibeanna nó scagairí "
"saincheaptha atá suiteáilte </ref/contrib/admin/admindocs>."

msgid "Built-in tag reference"
msgstr "Tagairt clibeanna ionsuite"

msgid "``autoescape``"
msgstr "``autoescape``"

msgid ""
"Controls the current auto-escaping behavior. This tag takes either ``on`` or "
"``off`` as an argument and that determines whether auto-escaping is in "
"effect inside the block. The block is closed with an ``endautoescape`` "
"ending tag."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn sé an t-iompar uathoibríoch reatha. Tógann an chlib seo ``on`` nó "
"``off ``mar argóint agus cinneann sé sin an bhfuil éalú uathoibríoch i "
"bhfeidhm taobh istigh den bhloc. Tá an bloc dúnta le clib deireadh "
"``endautoescape``."

msgid "Sample usage:"
msgstr "Úsáid samplach:"

msgid ""
"When auto-escaping is in effect, all content derived from variables has HTML "
"escaping applied before placing the result into the output (but after any "
"filters are applied). This is equivalent to manually applying "
"the :tfilter:`escape` filter to each variable."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn éalú uathoibríoch i bhfeidhm, tá éalú HTML i bhfeidhm ag gach "
"ábhar a dhíorthaítear ó athróga sula gcuirtear an toradh isteach san aschur "
"(ach tar éis aon scagairí a chur i bhfeidhm). Tá sé seo comhionann leis an "
"scagaire: tfilter: `escape` a chur i bhfeidhm de láimh ar gach athróg."

msgid ""
"The only exceptions are variables already marked as \"safe\" from escaping. "
"Variables could be marked as \"safe\" by the code which populated the "
"variable, by applying the :tfilter:`safe` or :tfilter:`escape` filters, or "
"because it's the result of a previous filter that marked the string as "
"\"safe\"."
msgstr ""
"Is iad na heisceachtaí amháin ná athróga atá marcáilte cheana féin mar "
"“sábháilte” ó éalú. D'fhéadfaí athróga a mharcáil mar “sábháilte” leis an "
"gcód a rinne an athróg, tríd na scagairí:tfilter: `safe` nó: tfilter: "
"`escape` a chur i bhfeidhm, nó toisc gurb é toradh scagaire roimhe seo a "
"mharcálaigh an sreang mar “sábháilte”."

