msgstr "Úsáid:"

msgid ""
"The ``{% lorem %}`` tag can be used with zero, one, two or three arguments. "
"The arguments are:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir an chlib ``{% lorem%}`` a úsáid le nialas, aon, dhá nó trí "
"argóint. Is iad na hargóintí:"

msgid "``count``"
msgstr "``comhaireant``"

msgid ""
"A number (or variable) containing the number of paragraphs or words to "
"generate (default is 1)."
msgstr ""
"Uimhir (nó athróg) ina bhfuil líon na míreanna nó na bhfocal le giniúint (is "
"é 1 réamhshocraithe)."

msgid "``method``"
msgstr "``modh``"

msgid ""
"Either ``w`` for words, ``p`` for HTML paragraphs or ``b`` for plain-text "
"paragraph blocks (default is ``b``)."
msgstr ""
"Ceachtar ``w`` le haghaidh focail, ``p`` do mhíreanna HTML nó ``b`` do "
"mbloic mhír gnáthtéacs (is é ``b`` réamhshocraithe ná ``b``)."

msgid "``random``"
msgstr "``randam``"

msgid ""
"The word ``random``, which if given, does not use the common paragraph "
"(\"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet...\") when generating text."
msgstr ""
"An focal ``randam``, nach n-úsáideann an mhír choiteann (“Lorem ipsum dolor "
"sit amet...”) agus téacs á ghiniúint."

msgid "``{% lorem %}`` will output the common \"lorem ipsum\" paragraph."
msgstr "``{% lorem%}`` aschur an mhír choitianta “lorem ipsum”."

msgid ""
"``{% lorem 3 p %}`` will output the common \"lorem ipsum\" paragraph and two "
"random paragraphs each wrapped in HTML ``<p>`` tags."
msgstr ""
"<p>Aschur ``{% lorem 3 p%} `an mhír choitianta “lorem ipsum” agus dhá mhír "
"randamach gach ceann atá fillte i gclibeanna HTML```."

msgid "``{% lorem 2 w random %}`` will output two random Latin words."
msgstr "Aschur ``{% lorem 2 w randamach%}`` dhá fhocal randamacha Laidine."

msgid "``now``"
msgstr "``anois``"

msgid ""
"Displays the current date and/or time, using a format according to the given "
"string. Such string can contain format specifiers characters as described in "
"the :tfilter:`date` filter section."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánann sé an dáta agus/nó an t-am reatha, ag baint úsáide as formáid de "
"réir an teaghrán tugtha. Is féidir carachtair sonraitheoirí formáide a "
"bheith i sreang den sórt sin mar a thuairiscítear sa chuid scagaire: "
"tfilter: `dáta`."

msgid ""
"Note that you can backslash-escape a format string if you want to use the "
"\"raw\" value. In this example, both \"o\" and \"f\" are backslash-escaped, "
"because otherwise each is a format string that displays the year and the "
"time, respectively:"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur féidir leat teaghrán formáide a éalú ar ais más mian "
"leat an luach “amh” a úsáid. Sa sampla seo, tá “o” agus “f” araon éalaithe "
"le cúltaca, mar ar shlí eile is teaghrán formáide é gach ceann acu a "
"thaispeánann an bhliain agus an t-am, faoi seach:"

msgid "This would display as \"It is the 4th of September\"."
msgstr "Taispeánfaí sé seo mar “Is é an 4 Meán Fómhair é”."

msgid ""
"The format passed can also be one of the predefined "
"ones :setting:`DATE_FORMAT`, :setting:`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting:`SHORT_DATE_FORMAT` "
"or :setting:`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`. The predefined formats may vary "
"depending on the current locale and if :doc:`/topics/i18n/formatting` is "
"enabled, e.g.:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an bhformáid a rith a bheith ar cheann de na cinn "
"réamhshainithe freisin: setting: `DATE_FORMAT`, :setting: "
"`DATETIME_FORMAT`, :setting: `SHORT_DATE_FORMAT` nó:setting: "
"`SHORT_DATETIME_FORMAT`. Féadfaidh na formáidí réamhshainithe a bheith "
"éagsúil ag brath ar an áitiúil reatha agus má tá: doc: `/topics/i18n/"
"formatting` cumasaithe, m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"You can also use the syntax ``{% now \"Y\" as current_year %}`` to store the "
"output (as a string) inside a variable. This is useful if you want to use "
"``{% now %}`` inside a template tag like :ttag:`blocktranslate` for example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an comhréir ``{% now “Y” a úsáid mar current_year%}`` chun an "
"t-aschur (mar shreang) a stóráil taobh istigh d'athróg. Tá sé seo úsáideach "
"más mian leat ``{% now%}`` a úsáid taobh istigh de chlib teimpléad "
"cosúil:ttag: `blocktranslate` mar shampla:"

msgid "``querystring``"
msgstr "``ceisteanna ceiste``"

msgid ""
"Outputs a URL-encoded formatted query string based on the provided "
"parameters."
msgstr ""
"Aschur sreang ceisteanna formáidithe ionchódaithe URL bunaithe ar na "
"paraiméadair a chuirtear ar fáil."

msgid ""
"This tag requires a :class:`~django.http.QueryDict` instance, which defaults "
"to :attr:`request.GET <django.http.HttpRequest.GET>` if none is provided."
msgstr ""
"<django.http.HttpRequest.GET>Éilíonn an chlib seo a: class: "
"`~django.http.QueryDict` sampla, atá réamhshocraithe to:attr: `request.get "
"`mura gcuirtear aon rud ar fáil."

msgid ""
"If the :class:`~django.http.QueryDict` is empty and no additional parameters "
"are provided, an empty string is returned. Otherwise, the result includes a "
"leading ``\"?\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using ``request.GET`` as default"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as ``request.get`` mar réamhshocraithe"

msgid ""
"To use ``request.GET`` as the default ``QueryDict`` instance, the "
"``django.template.context_processors.request`` context processor should be "
"enabled. If it's not enabled, you must either explicitly pass the "
"``request`` object into the template context, or provide a ``QueryDict`` "
"instance to this tag."
msgstr ""
"Chun ``request.get`` a úsáid mar shampla réamhshocraithe ``QueryDict``, ba "
"chóir an próiseálaí comhthéacs "
"``django.template.context_processors.request`` a chumasú. Mura bhfuil sé "
"cumasaithe, ní mór duit an réad ``iarraidh` a chur go sainráite isteach i "
"gcomhthéacs an teimpléid, nó sampla ``QueryDict' a sholáthar don chlib seo."

msgid "Basic usage"
msgstr "Úsáid bunúsach"

msgid ""
"Outputs the current query string verbatim. So if the query string is ``?"
"color=green``, the output would be ``?color=green``."
msgstr ""
"Aisíonn sé an teaghrán fiosrúcháin reatha focal focal. Mar sin má tá an "
"teaghrán ceisteanna ``? dath = glas ``, bheadh an t-aschur``? dath = glas ``."

msgid ""
"Outputs the current query string with the addition of the ``size`` "
"parameter. Following the previous example, the output would be ``?"
"color=green&size=M``."
msgstr ""
"Aisíonn sé an teaghrán fiosrúcháin reatha leis an bparaiméadar ``méid ``a "
"chur leis. Tar éis an sampla roimhe seo, bheadh an t-aschur ``? Dath = glas "
"& Méid = M ``."

msgid "Custom QueryDict"
msgstr "QueryDict Saincheaptha"

msgid ""
"You can provide a custom ``QueryDict`` to be used instead of "
"``request.GET``. So if ``my_query_dict`` is ``<QueryDict: {'color': ['blue']}"
">``, this outputs ``?color=blue``."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat saincheaptha ``QueryDict`` a sholáthar le húsáid in ionad "
"``request.get``. <QueryDict: {'color': ['blue']} >Mar sin má tá "
"``my_query_dict`` ```, aschur seo ``? dath = gorm ``."

msgid "Setting items"
msgstr "Míreanna a shocrú"

msgid ""
"Adds or modifies parameters in the query string. Each keyword argument will "
"be added to the query string, replacing any existing value for that key. For "
"instance, if the current query string is ``?color=green``, the output will "
"be ``?color=red&size=S``."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé nó modhnóidh sé paraiméadair sa sreang fiosrúcháin. Cuirfear "
"gach argóint eochairfhocal leis an sreangán fiosrúcháin, ag ionad aon luach "
"atá ann cheana don eochair sin. Mar shampla, más é ``an teaghrán ceisteanna "
"reatha? dath = glas ``, beidh an t-aschur``? Dath = dearg & Méid = S ``."

msgid "Removing items"
msgstr "Míreanna a bhaint"

msgid ""
"Passing ``None`` as the value removes the parameter from the query string. "
"For example, if the current query string is ``?color=green&size=M``, the "
"output will be ``?size=M``."
msgstr ""
"Ag dul ``None ``mar an luach baineann an paraiméadar ón sreang fiosrúcháin. "
"Mar shampla, más é ``an teaghrán fiosrúcháin reatha? Dath = glas & méid = M "
"``, beidh an t-aschur``? Méid = m ``."

msgid "Handling lists"
msgstr "Liosta láimhseála"

msgid ""
"If ``my_list`` is ``[\"red\", \"blue\"]``, the output will be ``?"
"color=red&color=blue``, preserving the list structure in the query string."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``my_list`` ``[\"dearg”, “gorm\"]``, beidh an t-aschur ``? color = "
"red&color = gorm ``, ag caomhnú struchtúr an liosta sa sreang ceisteanna."

msgid "Dynamic usage"
msgstr "Úsáid dinimiciúil"

msgid ""
"A common example of using this tag is to preserve the current query string "
"when displaying a page of results, while adding a link to the next and "
"previous pages of results. For example, if the paginator is currently on "
"page 3, and the current query string is ``?color=blue&size=M&page=3``, the "
"following code would output ``?color=blue&size=M&page=4``:"
msgstr ""
"Sampla coitianta den chlib seo a úsáid is ea an sreang ceisteanna reatha a "
"chaomhnú agus leathanach torthaí á thaispeáint, agus nasc á chur leis na "
"chéad leathanaigh eile agus roimhe seo de na torthaí. Mar shampla, má tá an "
"paginator ar leathanach 3 faoi láthair, agus is é an teaghrán ceisteanna "
"reatha ``? color=gorm&size = M&page = 3``, aschur an cód seo a leanas ``? "
"Dath = gorm&méid = M & page = 4``:"

msgid ""
"You can also store the value in a variable. For example, if you need "
"multiple links to the same page, define it as:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an luach a stóráil in athróg freisin. Mar shampla, má "
"theastaíonn iliomad naisc uait leis an leathanach céanna, sainmhínigh é mar:"

msgid "``regroup``"
msgstr "``athghrúpa``"

msgid "Regroups a list of alike objects by a common attribute."
msgstr "Athghrúpaíonn sé liosta de na rudaí céanna de réir tréith choiteann."

msgid ""
"This complex tag is best illustrated by way of an example: say that "
"``cities`` is a list of cities represented by dictionaries containing "
"``\"name\"``, ``\"population\"``, and ``\"country\"`` keys:"
msgstr ""
"Is fearr an chlib casta seo a léiriú trí shampla: abair gur liosta cathracha "
"é `cathracha a léiríonn foclóirí ina bhfuil ``\"ainm\"``, ``daonra\"``, agus "
"```tír\"` eochracha:"

msgid ""
"...and you'd like to display a hierarchical list that is ordered by country, "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"... agus ba mhaith leat liosta ordlathach a ordaítear de réir tíre a "
"thaispeáint, mar seo:"

msgid "India"
msgstr "An India"

msgid "Mumbai: 19,000,000"
msgstr "Mumbai: 19,000,000"

msgid "Calcutta: 15,000,000"
msgstr "Calcutta: 15,000,000"

msgid "USA"
msgstr "STÁIT AONTAITHE"

msgid "New York: 20,000,000"
msgstr "Nua Eabhrac: 20,000,000"

msgid "Chicago: 7,000,000"
msgstr "Chicago: 7,000,000"

msgid "Japan"
msgstr "An tSeapáin"

msgid "Tokyo: 33,000,000"
msgstr "Tóiceo: 33,000,000"

msgid ""
"You can use the ``{% regroup %}`` tag to group the list of cities by "
"country. The following snippet of template code would accomplish this:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an chlib ``{% regroup%}`` a úsáid chun liosta na gcathracha a "
"ghrúpáil de réir tíre. Chuirfeadh an snippet seo a leanas de chód teimpléid "
"i gcrích é seo:"

msgid ""
"Let's walk through this example. ``{% regroup %}`` takes three arguments: "
"the list you want to regroup, the attribute to group by, and the name of the "
"resulting list. Here, we're regrouping the ``cities`` list by the "
"``country`` attribute and calling the result ``country_list``."
msgstr ""
"Siúlóimid tríd an sampla seo. ``{% regroup%}`` tógann trí argóint: an liosta "
"is mian leat a athghrúpáil, an tréith le grúpáil leis, agus ainm an liosta "
"mar thoradh air. Anseo, táimid ag athghrúpáil an liosta ``cathr`` de réir an "
"tréith ```country ``agus glaoimid ar an toradh ``lista_country``."

msgid ""
"``{% regroup %}`` produces a list (in this case, ``country_list``) of "
"**group objects**. Group objects are instances "
"of :py:func:`~collections.namedtuple` with two fields:"
msgstr ""
"Léirgeann ``{% regroup%} `liosta (sa chás seo, ``country_list``) d'**rudaí "
"grúpa**. Is cásanna iad rudaí grúpa de:py:func: `~collections.namedtuple` le "
"dhá réimse:"

msgid ""
"``grouper`` -- the item that was grouped by (e.g., the string \"India\" or "
"\"Japan\")."
msgstr ""
"``Grúpa`` - an mír a rinneadh grúpáil le (m.sh., an sreang “India” nó “An "
"tSeapáin”)."

msgid ""
"``list`` -- a list of all items in this group (e.g., a list of all cities "
"with country='India')."
msgstr ""
"``liosta`` - liosta de na míreanna uile sa ghrúpa seo (m.sh., liosta de na "
"cathracha go léir le tír = 'India')."

msgid ""
"Because ``{% regroup %}`` produces :py:func:`~collections.namedtuple` "
"objects, you can also write the previous example as:"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go dtáirgeann ``{% regroup%}``: py:func: `~collections.namedtuple` "
"rudaí, is féidir leat an sampla roimhe seo a scríobh mar:"

msgid ""
"Note that ``{% regroup %}`` does not order its input! Our example relies on "
"the fact that the ``cities`` list was ordered by ``country`` in the first "
"place. If the ``cities`` list did *not* order its members by ``country``, "
"the regrouping would naively display more than one group for a single "
"country. For example, say the ``cities`` list was set to this (note that the "
"countries are not grouped together):"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach n-ordaíonn ``{% regroup%}`` a ionchur! Braitheann ár "
"sampla ar an bhfíric gur ordaigh “tír” an liosta ``cathr`` sa chéad áit. Dá "
"n-ordódh liosta na `cathracha ```````````````baill ```````````````````````, "
"ní dhéanfadh an t-athghrúpáil níos mó ná grúpa amháin go naif do thír "
"amháin. Mar shampla, abair go raibh an liosta ``cathracha ``socraithe chuige "
"seo (tabhair faoi deara nach bhfuil na tíortha grúpáilte le chéile):"

msgid ""
"With this input for ``cities``, the example ``{% regroup %}`` template code "
"above would result in the following output:"
msgstr ""
"Leis an ionchur seo do `cathracha ``, bheadh an t-aschur seo a leanas mar "
"thoradh ar an gcód teimpléad`` {% athghrúpaí%} `thuas:"

msgid ""
"The easiest solution to this gotcha is to make sure in your view code that "
"the data is ordered according to how you want to display it."
msgstr ""
"Is é an réiteach is éasca ar an gotcha seo ná a chinntiú i do chód amharc go "
"ndéantar na sonraí a ordú de réir an chaoi ar mhaith leat iad a thaispeáint."

msgid ""
"Another solution is to sort the data in the template using "
"the :tfilter:`dictsort` filter, if your data is in a list of dictionaries:"
msgstr ""
"Réiteach eile is ea na sonraí sa teimpléad a shórtáil ag baint úsáide as an "
"scagair:tfilter: `dictsort`, má tá do chuid sonraí i liosta foclóirí:"

msgid "Grouping on other properties"
msgstr "Grúpáil ar airíonna eile"

msgid ""
"Any valid template lookup is a legal grouping attribute for the regroup tag, "
"including methods, attributes, dictionary keys and list items. For example, "
"if the \"country\" field is a foreign key to a class with an attribute "
"\"description,\" you could use:"
msgstr ""
"Is tréith grúpála dlíthiúil é aon chuardach teimpléad bailí don chlib "
"athghrúpála, lena n-áirítear modhanna, tréithe, eochracha foclóra agus "
"míreanna liosta. Mar shampla, más eochair eachtrach é an réimse “tíre” do "
"rang le tréith “cur síos”, d'fhéadfá úsáid a bhaint as:"

msgid ""
"Or, if ``country`` is a field with ``choices``, it will have "
"a :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.get_FOO_display` method available as an "
"attribute, allowing  you to group on the display string rather than the "
"``choices`` key:"
msgstr ""
"Nó, más réimse é ``country ```roghanna``, beidh a: meth: "
"`~django.db.models.model.get_foo_display` modh ar fáil mar thréith, rud a "
"ligfidh duit grúpáil ar an teaghrán taispeána seachas an eochair ``roghanna "
"``:"

msgid ""
"``{{ country.grouper }}`` will now display the value fields from the "
"``choices`` set rather than the keys."
msgstr ""
"Taispeánfaidh ``{{country.grouper}}`` anois na réimsí luacha ón tacar "
"``roghna`` seachas na heochracha."

msgid "``resetcycle``"
msgstr "``athshocraitheach``"

msgid ""
"Resets a previous `cycle`_ so that it restarts from its first item at its "
"next encounter. Without arguments, ``{% resetcycle %}`` will reset the last "
"``{% cycle %}`` defined in the template."
msgstr ""
"Athshocraíonn sé “timthriall” roimhe seo ionas go dtosóidh sé óna chéad mhír "
"ag an gcéad teagmháil eile. Gan argóintí, athshocróidh ``{% resetcycle%} "
"`an`` {% timthriall%}` deireanach a shainmhínítear sa teimpléad."

msgid "This example would return this HTML:"
msgstr "Chuirfeadh an sampla seo ar ais an HTML seo:"

msgid ""
"Notice how the first block ends with ``class=\"odd\"`` and the new one "
"starts with ``class=\"odd\"``. Without the ``{% resetcycle %}`` tag, the "
"second block would start with ``class=\"even\"``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara conas a chríochnaíonn an chéad bloc le ``class=\"odd\"`` "
"agus tosaíonn an ceann nua le ``class=\"odd\"``. Gan an chlib ``{% "
"resetcycle%}``, tosódh an dara bloc le ``class=\"even\"``."

msgid "You can also reset named cycle tags:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat clibeanna timthriall ainmnithe a athshocrú freisin:"

msgid ""
"In this example, we have both the alternating odd/even rows and a \"major\" "
"row every fifth row. Only the five-row cycle is reset when a category "
"changes."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, tá na sraitheanna neamhghair/fiú malartacha againn agus "
"sraith “mór” gach cúigiú sraith. Ní athshocraítear ach an timthriall cúig "
"shraith nuair a athraíonn catagóir."

msgid "``spaceless``"
msgstr "``gan spás ``"

msgid ""
"Removes whitespace between HTML tags. This includes tab characters and "
"newlines."
msgstr ""
"Baineann sé spás bán idir clibeanna HTML. Cuimsíonn sé seo carachtair "
"cluaisín agus línte nua."

msgid ""
"Only space between *tags* is removed -- not space between tags and text. In "
"this example, the space around ``Hello`` won't be stripped:"
msgstr ""
"Ní bhaintear ach spás idir *tags* - ní spás idir clibeanna agus téacs. Sa "
"sampla seo, ní scriosfar an spás timpeall ``Hello``:"

msgid "``templatetag``"
msgstr "``Teimpléad tag``"

msgid "Outputs one of the syntax characters used to compose template tags."
msgstr ""
"Aschur ceann de na carachtair chomhréireachta a úsáidtear chun clibeanna "
"teimpléad"

msgid ""
"The template system has no concept of \"escaping\" individual characters. "
"However, you can use the ``{% templatetag %}`` tag to display one of the "
"template tag character combinations."
msgstr ""
"Níl aon choincheap ag an gcóras teimpléid maidir le carachtair aonair "
"“éalú”. Mar sin féin, is féidir leat an chlib ``{% templatetag%}`` a úsáid "
"chun ceann de na teaglaim carachtair clib teimpléad a thaispeáint."

msgid "The argument tells which template bit to output:"
msgstr "Insíonn an argóint cén giotán teimpléid atá le haschur:"

msgid "Outputs"
msgstr "Aschuir"

msgid "``openblock``"
msgstr "``openblock``"

msgid "``{%``"
msgstr "``{%``"

msgid "``closeblock``"
msgstr "``cloing``"

msgid "``%}``"
msgstr "``%} ``"

msgid "``openvariable``"
msgstr "``openinathraithe``"

msgid "``{{``"
msgstr "``{{``"

msgid "``closevariable``"
msgstr "``dúnta inathraitheach``"

msgid "``}}``"
msgstr "``}}``"

msgid "``openbrace``"
msgstr "``openbrace``"

msgid "``{``"
msgstr "``{``"

msgid "``closebrace``"
msgstr "``Closebraice``"

msgid "``}``"
msgstr "``}``"

msgid "``opencomment``"
msgstr "``Tráchtaireacht oscail``"

msgid "``{#``"
msgstr "``{#``"

msgid "``closecomment``"
msgstr "``dlúthchomhlána``"

msgid "``#}``"
msgstr "``#} ``"

msgid ""
"See also the :ttag:`verbatim` tag for another way of including these "
"characters."
msgstr ""
"Féach freisin an clibe:ttag: `verbatim` le haghaidh bealach eile chun na "
"carachtair seo a áireamh."

msgid "``url``"
msgstr "``Url``"

msgid ""
"Returns an absolute path reference (a URL without the domain name) matching "
"a given view and optional parameters. Any special characters in the "
"resulting path will be encoded "
"using :func:`~django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri`."
msgstr ""
"Tugann tagairt cosán iomlán ar ais (URL gan ainm fearainn) a mheaitseálann "
"radharc ar leith agus paraiméadair roghnacha. Déanfar aon charachtair "
"speisialta sa chosán mar thoradh air a ionchódú ag baint úsáide as: func: "
"`~django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri`."

msgid ""
"This is a way to output links without violating the DRY principle by having "
"to hard-code URLs in your templates:"
msgstr ""
"Is bealach é seo chun naisc a aschur gan prionsabal DRY a shárú trí URLanna "
"a chódú crua i do theimpléid:"

msgid ""
"The first argument is a :ref:`URL pattern name <naming-url-patterns>`. It "
"can be a quoted literal or any other context variable. Additional arguments "
"are optional and should be space-separated values that will be used as "
"arguments in the URL. The example above shows passing positional arguments. "
"Alternatively you may use keyword syntax:"
msgstr ""
"<naming-url-patterns>Is é an chéad argóint a:ref: `Ainm patrún URL `. Is "
"féidir é a bheith ina athróg litriúil nó aon athróg comhthéacs eile. Tá "
"argóintí breise roghnach agus ba cheart go mbeadh luachanna scartha ó spás "
"iad a úsáidfear mar argóintí san URL. Taispeánann an sampla thuas ag rith "
"argóintí seasaimh. De rogha air is féidir leat comhréir eochairfhocal a "
"úsáid:"

msgid ""
"Do not mix both positional and keyword syntax in a single call. All "
"arguments required by the URLconf should be present."
msgstr ""
"Ná déan comhréir seasmhach agus eochairfhocal a mheascadh i nglao amháin. Ba "
"chóir go mbeadh gach argóint a éilíonn ag an URLConf i láthair."

msgid ""
"For example, suppose you have a view, ``app_views.client``, whose URLconf "
"takes a client ID (here, ``client()`` is a method inside the views file "
"``app_views.py``). The URLconf line might look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cuir i gcás go bhfuil amharc agat, ``app_views.client``, a "
"ghlacann a URLConf ID cliant (anseo, `client () `modh taobh istigh den "
"chomhad tuairimí ``app_views.py``). D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar líne "
"URLConf:"

msgid ""
"If this app's URLconf is included into the project's URLconf under a path "
"such as this:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá URLConf an aip seo san áireamh i URLConf an tionscadail faoi chonair "
"mar seo:"

msgid "...then, in a template, you can create a link to this view like this:"
msgstr ""
"... ansin, i dteimpléad, is féidir leat nasc a chruthú leis an radharc seo "
"mar seo:"

msgid "The template tag will output the string ``/clients/client/123/``."
msgstr "Aschróidh an chlib teimpléid an sreang ``/cliant/cliant/123/``."

msgid ""
"Note that if the URL you're reversing doesn't exist, you'll get "
"an :exc:`~django.urls.NoReverseMatch` exception raised, which will cause "
"your site to display an error page."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara mura bhfuil an URL atá á aisiompú agat ann, gheobhaidh tú "
"eisceacht: exc: `~django.urls.noReverseMatch` ardaithe, rud a fhágfaidh go "
"dtaispeánfaidh do shuíomh leathanach earráide."

msgid ""
"If you'd like to retrieve a URL without displaying it, you can use a "
"slightly different call:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat URL a aisghabháil gan é a thaispeáint, is féidir leat glao "
"beagán difriúil a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"The scope of the variable created by the  ``as var`` syntax is the ``{% "
"block %}`` in which the ``{% url %}`` tag appears."
msgstr ""
"Is é raon feidhme an athróg a chruthaíonn an chomhréir `as var`` an ``{% "
"block%}`` ina bhfuil an chlib ``{% url%}`` le feiceáil."

msgid ""
"This ``{% url ... as var %}`` syntax will *not* cause an error if the view "
"is missing. In practice you'll use this to link to views that are optional:"
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirfidh an comhréir seo ``{% url... as var%}`` ** ina chúis le earráid "
"má tá an radharc ar iarraidh. Go praiticiúil úsáidfidh tú é seo chun nasc a "
"dhéanamh le tuairimí atá roghnach:"

msgid ""
"If you'd like to retrieve a namespaced URL, specify the fully qualified name:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat URL spás ainmneacha a aisghabháil, sonraigh an t-ainm "
"láncháilithe:"

msgid ""
"This will follow the normal :ref:`namespaced URL resolution strategy <topics-"
"http-reversing-url-namespaces>`, including using any hints provided by the "
"context as to the current application."
msgstr ""
"Leanfaidh sé seo an straitéis gnáth:ref: `ainmspaced URL <topics-http-"
"reversing-url-namespaces>', lena n-áirítear aon leideanna a sholáthraíonn an "
"comhthéacs maidir leis an bhfeidhmchlár reatha a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Don't forget to put quotes around the URL pattern ``name``, otherwise the "
"value will be interpreted as a context variable!"
msgstr ""
"Ná déan dearmad luachana a chur timpeall an phatrún URL ``ainm ``, ar shlí "
"eile léirmhínífear an luach mar athróg comhthéacs!"

msgid "``verbatim``"
msgstr "``Verbatim``"

msgid ""
"Stops the template engine from rendering the contents of this block tag."
msgstr "Stopann inneall an teimpléid ó ábhar an chlib bloc seo a léiriú."

msgid ""
"A common use is to allow a JavaScript template layer that collides with "
"Django's syntax. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáid choitianta ná ciseal teimpléad JavaScript a cheadú a imbhuaileann le "
"comhréir Django. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"You can also designate a specific closing tag, allowing the use of ``{% "
"endverbatim %}`` as part of the unrendered contents:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat clib deiridh sonrach a ainmniú freisin, rud a cheadaíonn "
"úsáid ``{% endverbatim%}`` mar chuid den ábhar neamh-rindreáilte:"

msgid "``widthratio``"
msgstr "``Leithead leithead`"

msgid ""
"For creating bar charts and such, this tag calculates the ratio of a given "
"value to a maximum value, and then applies that ratio to a constant."
msgstr ""
"Chun barrachairteacha agus dá leithéid a chruthú, ríomhann an clib seo "
"cóimheas luach ar leith go luach uasta, agus ansin cuireann an cóimheas sin "
"i bhfeidhm ar thairiseach."

msgid ""
"If ``this_value`` is 175, ``max_value`` is 200, and ``max_width`` is 100, "
"the image in the above example will be 88 pixels wide (because 175/200 = "
".875; .875 * 100 = 87.5 which is rounded up to 88)."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``luach_seo ``175, `luach_maxe`` 200, agus ``max_width`` 100, beidh an "
"íomhá sa sampla thuas 88 picteilín ar leithead (mar 175/200 = .875; .875 * "
"100 = 87.5 atá cruinn suas go dtí 88)."

msgid ""
"In some cases you might want to capture the result of ``widthratio`` in a "
"variable. It can be useful, for instance, in a :ttag:`blocktranslate` like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"I roinnt cásanna b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat toradh ``leithead` a ghabháil in "
"athróg. Is féidir leis a bheith úsáideach, mar shampla, in a:ttag: "
"`blocktranslate` mar seo:"

msgid "``with``"
msgstr "``````"

msgid ""
"Caches a complex variable under a simpler name. This is useful when "
"accessing an \"expensive\" method (e.g., one that hits the database) "
"multiple times."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé athróg casta faoi ainm níos simplí. Tá sé seo úsáideach agus tú "
"ag rochtain ar mhodh “daor” (m.sh., ceann a bhuaileann an bunachar sonraí) "
"arís agus arís eile."

msgid ""
"The populated variable (in the example above, ``total``) is only available "
"between the ``{% with %}`` and ``{% endwith %}`` tags."
msgstr ""
"Níl an t-athróg daonra (sa sampla thuas, ``iomlán ``) ar fáil ach idir na "
"clibeanna`` {% with%} ``agus`` {% endwith%} ``."

msgid "You can assign more than one context variable:"
msgstr "Is féidir leat níos mó ná athróg comhthéacs amháin a shannadh:"

msgid ""
"The previous more verbose format is still supported: ``{% with "
"business.employees.count as total %}``"
msgstr ""
"Tacaítear fós leis an bhformáid níos fabhraí roimhe seo: ``{% with "
"business.staffes.count as total%}``"

msgid "Built-in filter reference"
msgstr "Tagairt scagaire tógtha"

msgid "``add``"
msgstr "``Cuir leis ``"

msgid "Adds the argument to the value."
msgstr "Cuireann sé an argóint leis an luach."

msgid "If ``value`` is ``4``, then the output will be ``6``."
msgstr "Más é ```luach`` ``4``, ansin is é ``6`` an t-aschur."

msgid ""
"This filter will first try to coerce both values to integers. If this fails, "
"it'll attempt to add the values together anyway. This will work on some data "
"types (strings, list, etc.) and fail on others. If it fails, the result will "
"be an empty string."
msgstr ""
"Déanfaidh an scagaire seo iarracht an dá luach a chur i bhfeidhm go "
