msgstr "Tiontaítear `& ``go `&``"

msgid ""
"Applying ``escape`` to a variable that would normally have auto-escaping "
"applied to the result will only result in one round of escaping being done. "
"So it is safe to use this function even in auto-escaping environments. If "
"you want multiple escaping passes to be applied, use "
"the :tfilter:`force_escape` filter."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanfar ach babhta amháin éalaithe mar thoradh ar “éalú” a chur i "
"bhfeidhm ar athróg a bheadh éalú uathoibríoch i bhfeidhm ar an toradh de "
"ghnáth. Mar sin tá sé sábháilte an fheidhm seo a úsáid fiú i dtimpeallachtaí "
"éalaithe uathoibríoch Más mian leat go gcuirfear pasanna éalaithe iolracha i "
"bhfeidhm, bain úsáid as an scagair:tfilter: `force_escape`."

msgid ""
"For example, you can apply ``escape`` to fields when :ttag:`autoescape` is "
"off:"
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, is féidir leat ``escape`` a chur i bhfeidhm ar réimsí "
"nuai:ttag: `autoescape` as:"

msgid "Chaining ``escape`` with other filters"
msgstr "“Éalú” a shlánú le scagairí eile"

msgid ""
"As mentioned in the :ttag:`autoescape` section, when filters including "
"``escape`` are chained together, it can result in unexpected outcomes if "
"preceding filters mark a potentially unsafe string as safe due to the lack "
"of escaping caused by :ttag:`autoescape` being ``off``."
msgstr ""
"Mar a luaitear sa rannait:ttag: `autoescape`, nuair a chuirtear scagairí "
"lena n-áirítear ``éalú ``slabhraithe le chéile, féadfaidh torthaí gan "
"choinne a bheith mar thoradh air má mharcálann scagairí roimhe seo sreang a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith sábháilte mar gheall ar an easpa éalaithe mar gheall "
"ar: ttag: `autoescape` a bheith `off``."

msgid ""
"In such cases, chaining ``escape`` would not reescape strings that have "
"already been marked as safe."
msgstr ""
"I gcásanna den sórt sin, ní dhéanfadh slabhraí ``éalú ````a athéalú "
"teaghráin atá marcáilte mar shábháilte cheana féin."

msgid ""
"This is especially important when using filters that operate on sequences, "
"for example :tfilter:`join`. If you need to escape each element in a "
"sequence, use the dedicated :tfilter:`escapeseq` filter."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo tábhachtach go háirithe nuair a úsáidtear scagairí a oibríonn ar "
"seicheamh, mar shampla:tfilter: `join`. Más gá duit gach eilimint a éalú i "
"seicheamh, bain úsáid as an scagaire tiomnaithe: tfilter: `escapeseq`."

msgid "``escapejs``"
msgstr "```éalaithe ``"

msgid ""
"Escapes characters for use as a whole JavaScript string literal, within "
"single or double quotes, as below. This filter does not make the string safe "
"for use in *\"JavaScript template literals\"* (the JavaScript backtick "
"syntax). Any other uses not listed above are not supported. It is generally "
"recommended that data should be passed using HTML ``data-`` attributes, or "
"the :tfilter:`json_script` filter, rather than in embedded JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Éalaíonn sé carachtair le húsáid mar shreang JavaScript iomlán liteartha, "
"laistigh de luachana aonair nó dúbailte, mar atá thíos. Ní dhéanann an "
"scagaire seo an sreang sábháilte le húsáid in*\"Litríochtaí teimpléad "
"JavaScript\"* (an comhréir backtick JavaScript). Ní thacaítear le haon "
"úsáidí eile nach bhfuil liostaithe thuas. Moltar go ginearálta gur chóir "
"sonraí a rith ag baint úsáide as tréithe HTML ``sonraí ``, nó an "
"scagair:tfilter: `json_script`, seachas i JavaScript leabaithe."

msgid "``escapeseq``"
msgstr "```Escapeseq``"

msgid ""
"Applies the :tfilter:`escape` filter to each element of a sequence. Useful "
"in conjunction with other filters that operate on sequences, such "
"as :tfilter:`join`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an scagaire: tfilter: `escape` i bhfeidhm ar gach eilimint de "
"seicheamh. Úsáideach i gcomhar le scagairí eile a oibríonn ar sheicheamh, "
"mar shampla:tfilter: `join`. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``filesizeformat``"
msgstr "``formáid comhaid ``"

msgid ""
"Formats the value like a 'human-readable' file size (i.e. ``'13 KB'``, "
"``'4.1 MB'``, ``'102 bytes'``, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Formáidigh an luach cosúil le méid comhad 'inléite ag an duine' (ie ``'13 "
"KB'``, ``4.1 MB'``, ```102 bytes'``, srl.)."

msgid "If ``value`` is 123456789, the output would be ``117.7 MB``."
msgstr "Más é “luach” 123456789, is é ``117.7 MB`` an t-aschur."

msgid "File sizes and SI units"
msgstr "Méideanna comhaid agus aonaid SI"

msgid ""
"Strictly speaking, ``filesizeformat`` does not conform to the International "
"System of Units which recommends using KiB, MiB, GiB, etc. when byte sizes "
"are calculated in powers of 1024 (which is the case here). Instead, Django "
"uses traditional unit names (KB, MB, GB, etc.) corresponding to names that "
"are more commonly used."
msgstr ""
"Go docht, ní chomhlíonann ``filesizeformat`` leis an gCóras Idirnáisiúnta "
"Aonaid a mholann KiB, MiB, GiB, srl a úsáid nuair a ríomhtar méideanna byte "
"i gcumhachtaí 1024 (rud atá an cás anseo). Ina áit sin, úsáideann Django "
"ainmneacha aonaid traidisiúnta (KB, MB, GB, srl.) A fhreagraíonn "
"d'ainmneacha a úsáidtear níos coitianta."

msgid "``first``"
msgstr "```chéad``"

