"Maps values for ``True``, ``False``, and (optionally) ``None``, to the "
"strings \"yes\", \"no\", \"maybe\", or a custom mapping passed as a comma-"
"separated list, and returns one of those strings according to the value:"
msgstr ""
"Léarscáil luachanna do ``True``, `False``, agus (roghnach) ``None ``, chuig "
"na teaghráin “yes”, “níl”, “b'fhéidir”, nó mapáil saincheaptha a rith mar "
"liosta scartha le camóg, agus filleann sé ceann de na teaghráin sin de réir "
"an luacha:"

msgid "``True``"
msgstr "``Fíor``"

msgid "``yes``"
msgstr "```tá ``"

msgid "``\"yeah,no,maybe\"``"
msgstr "``\"Sea, níl, b'fhéidir “``"

msgid "``yeah``"
msgstr "```Yeah``"

msgid "``False``"
msgstr "``Bréag``"

msgid "``no``"
msgstr "```ní``"

msgid "``maybe``"
msgstr "``d'fhéadfa``"

msgid "``\"yeah,no\"``"
msgstr "``\"sea, níl” ``"

msgid ""
"``no`` (converts ``None`` to ``False`` if no mapping for ``None`` is given)"
msgstr ""
"``No ``(athraíonn ``None`` go ``False`` mura dtugtar aon mhapáil le haghaidh "
"``None``)"

msgid "Internationalization tags and filters"
msgstr "Clibeanna agus scagairí idirnáisiúnta"

msgid ""
"Django provides template tags and filters to control each aspect "
"of :doc:`internationalization </topics/i18n/index>` in templates. They allow "
"for granular control of translations, formatting, and time zone conversions."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django clibeanna teimpléad agus scagairí chun gach gné de:doc: "
"`idirnáisiúnaíon` i dteimpléid a rial</topics/i18n/index> ú. Ceadaíonn siad "
"rialú gráinneach ar aistriúcháin, formáidiú agus tiontaithe crios ama."

msgid "``i18n``"
msgstr "``i18n``"

msgid ""
"This library allows specifying translatable text in templates. To enable it, "
"set :setting:`USE_I18N` to ``True``, then load it with ``{% load i18n %}``."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an leabharlann seo téacs inaistrithe a shonrú i dteimpl Chun é a "
"chumasú, socraí:setting: `USE_I18N` go ``True``, ansin luchtaigh é le ``{% "
"load i18n%} `."

msgid "See :ref:`specifying-translation-strings-in-template-code`."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `sonraí-aistriúcháin-strings-in-theimpléad-cód`."

msgid "``l10n``"
msgstr "``l10n``"

msgid ""
"This library provides control over the localization of values in templates. "
"You only need to load the library using ``{% load l10n %}``."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an leabharlann seo smacht ar logánú luachanna i dteimpléid. Ní "
"gá duit ach an leabharlann a luchtú ag baint úsáide as ``{% load l10n%}``."

msgid "See :ref:`topic-l10n-templates`."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `topic-l10n-templates`."

msgid "``tz``"
msgstr "``tz``"

msgid ""
"This library provides control over time zone conversions in templates. Like "
"``l10n``, you only need to load the library using ``{% load tz %}``, but "
"you'll usually also set :setting:`USE_TZ` to ``True`` so that conversion to "
"local time happens by default."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an leabharlann seo smacht ar thiontú crios ama i teimpléid. "
"Cosúil le ``l10n``, ní gá duit ach an leabharlann a luchtú ag baint úsáide "
"as ``{% load tz%}``, ach de ghnáth socraíonn tú freis:setting: `USE_TZ` go "
"``True`` ionas go dtarlóidh tiontú go am áitiúil de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid "See :ref:`time-zones-in-templates`."
msgstr "Féach:ref: `criosanna ama-in-theimpléid'."

msgid "Other tags and filters libraries"
msgstr "leabharlanna clibeanna agus scagairí eile"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a couple of other template-tag libraries that you have to "
"enable explicitly in your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting and enable in "
"your template with the :ttag:`{% load %}<load>` tag."
msgstr ""
"<load>Tagann Django le cúpla leabharlann clib teimpléad eile a chaithfidh tú "
"a chumasú go sainráite i do shuíomh: `INSTALLED_APPS` agus a chumasú i do "
"theimpléad leis an gclibe:ttag: `{% load%}`."

msgid ""
"A set of Django template filters useful for adding a \"human touch\" to "
"data. See :doc:`/ref/contrib/humanize`."
msgstr ""
"Sraith scagairí teimpléad Django atá úsáideach chun “teagmháil dhaonna” a "
"chur le sonraí. Féach: doc: `/ref/contrib/humanize`."

msgid "``static``"
msgstr "``statach``"

msgid ""
"To link to static files that are saved in :setting:`STATIC_ROOT` Django "
"ships with a :ttag:`static` template tag. If "
"the :mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` app is installed, the tag will serve "
"files using ``url()`` method of the storage specified by ``staticfiles`` "
"in :setting:`STORAGES`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Chun nasc a dhéanamh le comhaid statacha a shábháiltear in:setting: "
"`STATIC_ROOT` Seolann Django le clib teimpléad a:ttag: `static`. Má tá an "
"aip: mod: `django.contrib.staticfiles` suiteáilte, freastalóidh an clib "
"comhaid ag baint úsáide as modh ``url () `den stóráil a shonraítear le "
"``staticfiles`` in:setting: `STORAGES`. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"It is also able to consume standard context variables, e.g. assuming a "
"``user_stylesheet`` variable is passed to the template:"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé in ann athróga comhthéacs caighdeánacha a ithe freisin, m.sh. ag "
"glacadh leis go gcuirtear athróg ``user_stylesheet`` chuig an teimpléad:"

msgid ""
"If you'd like to retrieve a static URL without displaying it, you can use a "
"slightly different call:"
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat URL statach a aisghabháil gan é a thaispeáint, is féidir leat "
"glao beagán difriúil a úsáid:"

msgid "Using Jinja2 templates?"
msgstr "Ag baint úsáide as teimpléid Jinja2?"

msgid ""
"See :class:`~django.template.backends.jinja2.Jinja2` for information on "
"using the ``static`` tag with Jinja2."
msgstr ""
"Féach: Class: `~django.template.backends.jinja2.jinja2` le haghaidh "
"faisnéise maidir leis an gclib ``static`` a úsáid le Jinja2."

msgid "``get_static_prefix``"
msgstr "``get_static_prefix``"

msgid ""
"You should prefer the :ttag:`static` template tag, but if you need more "
"control over exactly where and how :setting:`STATIC_URL` is injected into "
"the template, you can use the :ttag:`get_static_prefix` template tag:"
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit an chlib teimpléad: ttag: `static`, ach má theastaíonn níos mó "
"smachta uait ar an áit go díreach agus cona:setting: `STATIC_URL` a "
"instealladh isteach sa teimpléad, is féidir leat clib teimpléad:ttag: "
"`get_static_prefix` a úsáid:"

msgid ""
"There's also a second form you can use to avoid extra processing if you need "
"the value multiple times:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an dara foirm ann freisin is féidir leat a úsáid chun próiseáil bhreise a "
"sheachaint má theastaíonn an luach uait arís agus arís eile:"

msgid "``get_media_prefix``"
msgstr "``get_media_prefix``"

msgid ""
"Similar to the :ttag:`get_static_prefix`, ``get_media_prefix`` populates a "
"template variable with the media prefix :setting:`MEDIA_URL`, e.g.:"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil leis an:ttag: `get_static_prefix`, ``get_media_prefix`` líonann "
"athróg teimpléad leis an réamhshocraithe:setting: `MEDIA_URL`, m.sh.:"

msgid ""
"By storing the value in a data attribute, we ensure it's escaped "
"appropriately if we want to use it in a JavaScript context."
msgstr ""
"Trí an luach a stóráil i dtréith sonraí, cinntímid go bhfuil sé éalaithe go "
"cuí más mian linn é a úsáid i gcomhthéacs JavaScript."

msgid ""
"Django's template engine provides a powerful mini-language for defining the "
"user-facing layer of your application, encouraging a clean separation of "
"application and presentation logic. Templates can be maintained by anyone "
"with an understanding of HTML; no knowledge of Python is required. For "
"introductory material, see :doc:`/topics/templates` topic guide."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn inneall teimpléid Django mion-theanga chumhachtach chun ciseal "
"d'iarratais atá os comhair an úsáideora a shainiú, ag spreagadh scaradh glan "
"ar loighic feidhmchláir agus cur i láthair. Is féidir le duine ar bith a "
"bhfuil tuiscint aige ar HTML teimpléid a choinneáil; níl aon eolas ag "
"teastáil ar Python. Maidir le hábhar tosaigh, féach:doc: treoir ábhair `/"
"topics/teimpléid`."

msgid ""
"For information on writing your own custom tags and filters, see :doc:`/"
"howto/custom-template-tags`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le do chlibeanna agus scagairí saincheaptha "
"féin a scríobh, féach: doc: `/howto/custom-template-tags`."

msgid ""
"To learn how to override templates in other Django applications, see :doc:`/"
"howto/overriding-templates`."
msgstr ""
"Chun foghlaim conas teimpléid a shárú in iarratais Django eile, féach:doc: `/"
"howto/overriding-temples`."

msgid "The Django template language"
msgstr "Teanga teimpléad Django"

msgid ""
"This document explains the language syntax of the Django template system. If "
"you're looking for a more technical perspective on how it works and how to "
"extend it, see :doc:`/ref/templates/api`."
msgstr ""
"Míníonn an doiciméad seo comhréir teanga an chórais teimpléid Django. Má tá "
"tú ag lorg peirspictíochta níos teicniúla ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn sé agus "
"conas é a leathnú, féach:doc: `/ref/templates/api`."

msgid ""
"Django's template language is designed to strike a balance between power and "
"ease. It's designed to feel comfortable to those used to working with HTML. "
"If you have any exposure to other text-based template languages, such as "
"Smarty_ or Jinja2_, you should feel right at home with Django's templates."
msgstr ""
"Tá teanga teimpléad Django deartha chun cothromaíocht a bhaint amach idir "
"cumhacht agus éascaíocht. Tá sé deartha chun mothú compordach dóibh siúd a "
"úsáidtear ag obair le HTML. Má tá aon nochtadh agat do theangacha teimpléad "
"téacs-bhunaithe eile, mar shampla Smarty_ nó Jinja2_, ba chóir go "
"mbraitheann tú i gceart sa bhaile le teimpléid Django."

msgid "Philosophy"
msgstr "Fealsúnacht"

msgid ""
"If you have a background in programming, or if you're used to languages "
"which mix programming code directly into HTML, you'll want to bear in mind "
"that the Django template system is not simply Python embedded into HTML. "
"This is by design: the template system is meant to express presentation, not "
"program logic."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cúlra agat sa chlárú, nó má tá tú cleachtaithe le teangacha a "
"mheascann cód cláir go díreach i HTML, beidh tú ag iarraidh a chur i "
"gcuimhne nach Python leabaithe i HTML amháin atá córas teimpléad Django. Tá "
"sé seo de réir dearaidh: tá sé i gceist ag an gcóras teimpléid cur i láthair "
"a chur in iúl, ní loighic"

msgid ""
"The Django template system provides tags which function similarly to some "
"programming constructs -- an :ttag:`if` tag for boolean tests, a :ttag:`for` "
"tag for looping, etc. -- but these are not simply executed as the "
"corresponding Python code, and the template system will not execute "
"arbitrary Python expressions. Only the tags, filters and syntax listed below "
"are supported by default (although you can add :doc:`your own extensions </"
"howto/custom-template-tags>` to the template language as needed)."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn córas teimpléad Django clibeanna a fheidhmíonn ar an gcosúil le "
"roinnt tógáil cláraithe -- an:ttag: `if `tag le haghaidh tástálacha boolean, "
"a:ttag: `for` tag le haghaidh lúpa, srl. - ach ní fhorghníomhtar iad seo go "
"simplí mar an cód Python comhfhreagrach, agus ní fhorghníomhaíonn an córas "
"teimpléid abairtí treallach Python. Ní thacaítear ach leis na clibeanna, na "
"scagairí agus na comhréiteach atá liostaithe thíos de réir réamhshocraithe "
"(cé gur féidir leat: doc: `do chuid síntí féin` a chur leis an teanga </"
"howto/custom-template-tags> teimpléid de réir mar is gá)."

msgid ""
"A template is a text file. It can generate any text-based format (HTML, XML, "
"CSV, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Is comhad téacs é teimpléad. Féadann sé aon fhormáid téacs-bhunaithe a "
"ghiniúint (HTML, XML, CSV, srl.)."

msgid ""
"A template contains **variables**, which get replaced with values when the "
"template is evaluated, and **tags**, which control the logic of the template."
msgstr ""
"Tá **athróga** i dteimpléad, a gcuirtear luachanna in ionad nuair a dhéantar "
"an teimpléad a mheas, agus **clibe**, a rialaíonn loighic an teimpléid."

msgid ""
"Below is a minimal template that illustrates a few basics. Each element will "
"be explained later in this document."
msgstr ""
"Seo thíos teimpléad íosta a léiríonn cúpla buneilimintí. Déanfar gach "
"eilimint a mhíniú níos déanaí sa doiciméad seo."

msgid ""
"Why use a text-based template instead of an XML-based one (like Zope's TAL)? "
"We wanted Django's template language to be usable for more than just XML/"
"HTML templates. You can use the template language for any text-based format "
"such as emails, JavaScript and CSV."
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth teimpléad téacs-bhunaithe a úsáid in ionad ceann XML bunaithe "
"(cosúil le TAL Zope)? Theastaigh uainn go mbeadh teanga teimpléid Django "
"inúsáidte le haghaidh níos mó ná teimpléid XML/HTML amháin. Is féidir leat "
"teanga an teimpléid a úsáid le haghaidh aon fhormáid téacs-bhunaithe mar "
"ríomhphoist, JavaScript agus CSV."

msgid "Variables"
msgstr "Athróga"

msgid ""
"Variables look like this: ``{{ variable }}``. When the template engine "
"encounters a variable, it evaluates that variable and replaces it with the "
"result. Variable names consist of any combination of alphanumeric characters "
"and the underscore (``\"_\"``) but may not start with an underscore, and may "
"not be a number. The dot (``\".\"``) also appears in variable sections, "
"although that has a special meaning, as indicated below. Importantly, *you "
"cannot have spaces or punctuation characters in variable names.*"
msgstr ""
"Breathnaíonn athróga mar seo: ``{{athróg}}``. Nuair a thagann an t-inneall "
"teimpléid le hathróg, déanann sé an t-athróg sin a mheas agus cuireann sé an "
"toradh in ionad é Is éard atá i ainmneacha athraitheacha aon teaglaim de "
"charachtair alfa-uimhriúla agus an béim (``\"_\"``) ach ní fhéadfaidh sé "
"tosú le béim, agus b'fhéidir nach bhfuil sé ina uimhir. Tá an ponc (``”. "
"“``) le feiceáil freisin i rannáin athraitheacha, cé go bhfuil brí "
"speisialta aige sin, mar a léirítear thíos. Tábhachtach, * ní féidir leat "
"spásanna nó carachtair poncaíochta a bheith agat in ainmneacha "
"athraitheacha. *"

msgid "Use a dot (``.``) to access attributes of a variable."
msgstr "Úsáid ponc (`.``) chun rochtain a fháil ar thréithe athróg."

msgid ""
"Technically, when the template system encounters a dot, it tries the "
"following lookups, in this order:"
msgstr ""
"Go teicniúil, nuair a thagann an córas teimpléid le ponc, déanann sé "
"iarracht na cuardaigh seo a leanas, san ord seo:"

msgid "Dictionary lookup"
msgstr "Cuardach foclóra"

msgid "Attribute or method lookup"
msgstr "Cuardach tréithe nó modh"

msgid "Numeric index lookup"
msgstr "Cuardach innéacs uimhriúil"

msgid ""
"If the resulting value is callable, it is called with no arguments. The "
"result of the call becomes the template value."
msgstr ""
"Má tá an luach mar thoradh air inghlaoch, tugtar air gan aon argóintí. Is é "
"toradh an ghlao an luach teimpléid."

msgid ""
"This lookup order can cause some unexpected behavior with objects that "
"override dictionary lookup. For example, consider the following code snippet "
"that attempts to loop over a ``collections.defaultdict``:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an ordú cuardaigh seo a bheith ina chúis le roinnt iompar gan "
"choinne le rudaí a sháraíonn cuardach foclóra Mar shampla, smaoinigh ar an "
"snippet cód seo a leanas a dhéanann iarracht lúbadh thar "
"`collections.defaultdict``:"

msgid ""
"Because dictionary lookup happens first, that behavior kicks in and provides "
"a default value instead of using the intended ``.items()`` method. In this "
"case, consider converting to a dictionary first."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go dtarlaíonn cuardach foclóra ar dtús, cuireann an t-iompar sin "
"isteach agus soláthraíonn sé luach réamhshocraithe in ionad an modh "
"beartaithe ``.items () `a úsáid. Sa chás seo, smaoinigh ar thiontú go "
"foclóir ar dtús."

msgid ""
"In the above example, ``{{ section.title }}`` will be replaced with the "
"``title`` attribute of the ``section`` object."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla thuas, cuirfear an tréith ``title`` den réad ``roinn ``in ionad`` "
"{{section.title}} ``."

msgid ""
"If you use a variable that doesn't exist, the template system will insert "
"the value of the ``string_if_invalid`` option, which is set to ``''`` (the "
"empty string) by default."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú athróg nach bhfuil ann, cuirfidh an córas teimpléid luach an "
"rogha ``string_if_invalid`` isteach, atá socraithe go ``\"``(an teaghrán "
"folamh) de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"Variable attributes that begin with an underscore may not be accessed as "
"they're generally considered private."
msgstr ""
"Ní fhéadfar rochtain a fháil ar thréithe athraitheacha a thosaíonn le béim "
"toisc go meastar go príobháideach iad de ghnáth."

msgid "You can modify variables for display by using **filters**."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat athróga a mhodhnú le taispeáint trí**scagairí** a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Filters look like this: ``{{ name|lower }}``. This displays the value of the "
"``{{ name }}`` variable after being filtered through the :tfilter:`lower` "
"filter, which converts text to lowercase. Use a pipe (``|``) to apply a "
"filter."
msgstr ""
"Breathnaíonn scagairí mar seo: ``{{ainm|níos ísle}}``. Taispeánann sé seo "
"luach an athróg ``{{name}}`` tar éis é a scagadh tríd an scagair:tfilter: "
"`lower`, a athraíonn téacs go litreacha beaga. Úsáid píopa (`| ``) chun "
"scagaire a chur i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"Filters can be \"chained.\" The output of one filter is applied to the next. "
"``{{ text|escape|linebreaks }}`` is a common idiom for escaping text "
"contents, then converting line breaks to ``<p>`` tags."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir scagairí a “slabhraithe.” <p>Cuirtear aschur scagaire amháin i "
"bhfeidhm ar an gcéad cheann eile. ``{{text|escape|linebreaks}} `is idiom "
"coitianta é chun ábhar téacs a éalú, ansin sosanna líne a thiontú go "
"clibeanna```."

msgid ""
"Some filters take arguments. A filter argument looks like this: ``{{ bio|"
"truncatewords:30 }}``. This will display the first 30 words of the ``bio`` "
"variable."
msgstr ""
"Tugann roinnt scagairí argóintí. Breathnaíonn argóint scagaire mar seo: "
"``{{bio|truncatewords:30}}``. Taispeánfaidh sé seo an chéad 30 focal den "
"athróg ``bio``."

msgid ""
"Filter arguments that contain spaces must be quoted; for example, to join a "
"list with commas and spaces you'd use ``{{ list|join:\", \" }}``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór argóintí scagaire ina bhfuil spásanna a lua; mar shampla, chun liosta "
"le camóga agus spásanna a bheith agat le ``{{list|join:”, \"}}``."

msgid ""
"Django provides about sixty built-in template filters. You can read all "
"about them in the :ref:`built-in filter reference <ref-templates-builtins-"
"filters>`. To give you a taste of what's available, here are some of the "
"more commonly used template filters:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django thart ar seasca scagaire teimpléad ionsuite <ref-"
"templates-builtins-filters>Is féidir leat gach rud fúthu a léamh in:ref: "
"`tagairt scagaire ionsuite `. Chun blas a thabhairt duit ar na rudaí atá ar "
"fáil, seo cuid de na scagairí teimpléid is coitianta a úsáidtear:"

msgid ":tfilter:`default`"
msgstr ":tfilter: `réamhshocraithe'"

