"ref/contrib/admin/admindocs`."

msgid "Tags"
msgstr "Clibeanna"

msgid ""
"Tags look like this: ``{% tag %}``. Tags are more complex than variables: "
"Some create text in the output, some control flow by performing loops or "
"logic, and some load external information into the template to be used by "
"later variables."
msgstr ""
"Breathnaíonn clibeanna mar seo: ``{% tag%}``. Tá clibeanna níos casta ná "
"athróga: Cruthaíonn cuid acu téacs san aschur, sreabhadh rialaithe roinnt "
"trí lúb nó loighic a dhéanamh, agus luchtaíonn cuid acu faisnéis sheachtrach "
"isteach sa teimpléad le húsáid ag athróga níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"Some tags require beginning and ending tags (i.e. ``{% tag %} ... tag "
"contents ... {% endtag %}``)."
msgstr ""
"Teastaíonn clibeanna tosaigh agus deireadh ó roinnt clibeanna (ie ``{% "
"tag%}... tag content... {% endtag%}``)."

msgid ""
"Django ships with about two dozen built-in template tags. You can read all "
"about them in the :ref:`built-in tag reference <ref-templates-builtins-"
"tags>`. To give you a taste of what's available, here are some of the more "
"commonly used tags:"
msgstr ""
"Loingíonn Django le thart ar dhá dhosaen clibeanna teimpléad ionsuite. <ref-"
"templates-builtins-tags>Is féidir leat gach rud fúthu a léamh in:ref: "
"`tagairt clibeanna ionsuite `. Chun blas a thabhairt duit ar na rudaí atá ar "
"fáil, seo cuid de na clibeanna is coitianta a úsáidtear:"

msgid ":ttag:`for`"
msgstr ":ttag: `do `"

