"Loop over each item in an array.  For example, to display a list of athletes "
"provided in ``athlete_list``:"
msgstr ""
"Lúb thar gach mír i sraith. Mar shampla, chun liosta lúthchleasaithe a "
"chuirtear ar fáil in `athlete_list`` a thaispeáint:"

msgid ":ttag:`if`, ``elif``, and ``else``"
msgstr ":ttag: `ife`, ``elif``, agus ``eile ```"

msgid ""
"Evaluates a variable, and if that variable is \"true\" the contents of the "
"block are displayed:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé athróg a mheas, agus má tá an athróg sin “fíor” taispeántar ábhar "
"an bhloc:"

msgid ""
"In the above, if ``athlete_list`` is not empty, the number of athletes will "
"be displayed by the ``{{ athlete_list|length }}`` variable. Otherwise, if "
"``athlete_in_locker_room_list`` is not empty, the message \"Athletes should "
"be out...\" will be displayed. If both lists are empty, \"No athletes.\" "
"will be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Sa mhéid thuas, mura bhfuil ``athlete_list`` folamh, taispeánfar líon na "
"lúthchleasaithe ag an athróg ``{{athlete_list|length}}``. Seachas sin, mura "
"bhfuil `athlete_in_locker_room_list`` folamh, taispeánfar an teachtaireacht "
"“Ba chóir go mbeadh lúthchleasaithe amach...”. Má tá an dá liosta folamh, "
"taispeánfar “Gan lúthchleasaithe.”"

msgid "You can also use filters and various operators in the :ttag:`if` tag:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat scagairí agus oibreoirí éagsúla a úsáid freisin sa chlib: "
"ttag: `if:"

msgid ""
"While the above example works, be aware that most template filters return "
"strings, so mathematical comparisons using filters will generally not work "
"as you expect. :tfilter:`length` is an exception."
msgstr ""
"Cé go n-oibríonn an sampla thuas, bí ar an eolas go bhfilleann an chuid is "
"mó de na scagairí teimpléid teaghráin, mar sin de ghnáth ní oibreoidh "
"comparáidí matamaitice :tfilter: Is eisceacht é `fad`."

msgid ":ttag:`block` and :ttag:`extends`"
msgstr ":ttag: `bloc` agus:ttag: `leathnaíneach`"

msgid ""
"Set up `template inheritance`_ (see below), a powerful way of cutting down "
"on \"boilerplate\" in templates."
msgstr ""
"Socraigh `oidhreacht teimpléad`_ (féach thíos), bealach cumhachtach chun "
"“boilerplate” a ghearradh síos i dteimpléid."

msgid ""
"Again, the above is only a selection of the whole list; see the :ref:`built-"
"in tag reference <ref-templates-builtins-tags>` for the complete list."
msgstr ""
"Arís, níl an méid thuas ach rogha den liosta iomlán; féach an:ref: `tagairt "
"clibeanna ionsuite <ref-templates-builtins-tags>`don liosta iomlán."

msgid ""
"You can also create your own custom template tags; see :doc:`/howto/custom-"
"template-tags`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat do chlibeanna teimpléad saincheaptha féin a chruthú freisin; "
"féach: doc: `/howto/custom-template-tags`."

msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Tuairimí"

msgid ""
"To comment-out part of a line in a template, use the comment syntax: ``{# #}"
"``."
msgstr ""
"Chun trácht a dhéanamh amach cuid de líne i dteimpléad, bain úsáid as an "
"gcomhréir tráchtaireachta: ``{# #}``."

msgid "For example, this template would render as ``'hello'``:"
msgstr "Mar shampla, rinneadh an teimpléad seo mar ``'hello'``:"

msgid "A comment can contain any template code, invalid or not. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir aon chód teimpléid a bheith i dtrácht, neamhbhailí nó nach bhfuil. "
"Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"This syntax can only be used for single-line comments (no newlines are "
"permitted between the ``{#`` and ``#}`` delimiters). If you need to comment "
"out a multiline portion of the template, see the :ttag:`comment` tag."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an comhréir seo a úsáid ach le haghaidh tuairimí aonlíne (ní "
"cheadaítear aon línte nua idir na teorainneacha ``{#`` agus `#}``). Más gá "
"duit trácht a dhéanamh ar chuid illíne den teimpléad, féach an clibe:ttag: "
"`comment`."

msgid "Template inheritance"
msgstr "Teimpléad oidhreacht"

msgid ""
"The most powerful -- and thus the most complex -- part of Django's template "
"engine is template inheritance. Template inheritance allows you to build a "
"base \"skeleton\" template that contains all the common elements of your "
"site and defines **blocks** that child templates can override."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chuid is cumhachtaí - agus dá bhrí sin an chuid is casta - d'inneall "
"teimpléad Django ná oidhreacht teimpléad. Ligeann oidhreacht teimpléad duit "
"teimpléad “cnámharlaigh” bonn a thógáil ina bhfuil na heilimintí coitianta "
"go léir de do shuíomh agus a shainmhíníonn t**bloic** ar féidir le teimpléid "
"leanaí a ath"

msgid "Let's look at template inheritance by starting with an example:"
msgstr "Breathnaímid ar oidhreacht teimpléid trí thosú le sampla:"

msgid ""
"This template, which we'll call ``base.html``, defines an HTML skeleton "
"document that you might use for a two-column page. It's the job of \"child\" "
"templates to fill the empty blocks with content."
msgstr ""
"Sainmhíníonn an teimpléad seo, a thabharfaimid ``base.html`, doiciméad "
"cnámharlaigh HTML a d'fhéadfá a úsáid le haghaidh leathanach dhá cholún. Is "
"obair teimpléid “leanbh” é na bloic folmha a líonadh le hábhar."

msgid ""
"In this example, the :ttag:`block` tag defines three blocks that child "
"templates can fill in. All the :ttag:`block` tag does is to tell the "
"template engine that a child template may override those portions of the "
"template."
msgstr ""
"Sa sampla seo, sainmhíníonn an clibe:ttag: `bloc` trí bhloc ar féidir le "
"teimpléid leanaí a líonadh isteach. Is é an clibe:ttag: `bloc` go léir ná "
"insint don inneall teimpléid go bhféadfadh teimpléad leanbh na codanna sin "
"den teimpléad a shárú."

msgid "A child template might look like this:"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh cuma seo a bheith ar theimpléad linbh:"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`extends` tag is the key here. It tells the template engine that "
"this template \"extends\" another template. When the template system "
"evaluates this template, first it locates the parent -- in this case, "
"\"base.html\"."
msgstr ""
"Is é an clib: ttag: `extens` an eochair anseo. Insíonn sé don inneall "
"teimpléid go leathnaíonn an teimpléad seo teimpléad eile. Nuair a dhéanann "
"an córas teimpléid measúnú ar an teimpléad seo, aimsíonn sé an tuismitheoir "
"ar dtús - sa chás seo, \"base.html”."

msgid ""
"At that point, the template engine will notice the three :ttag:`block` tags "
"in ``base.html`` and replace those blocks with the contents of the child "
"template. Depending on the value of ``blog_entries``, the output might look "
"like:"
msgstr ""
"Ag an bpointe sin, tabharfaidh inneall an teimpléid faoi deara na trí chlib: "
"ttag: `bloc` i `base.html`` agus cuirfidh ábhar an teimpléid linbh in ionad "
"na bloic sin. Ag brath ar luach ``blog_entries``, d'fhéadfadh cuma ar an "
"aschur:"

msgid ""
"Note that since the child template didn't define the ``sidebar`` block, the "
"value from the parent template is used instead. Content within a ``{% block "
"%}`` tag in a parent template is always used as a fallback."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara ós rud é nár sainmhínigh an teimpléad linbh an bloc "
"``taobharra`, go n-úsáidtear an luach ón teimpléad tuismitheora ina ionad. "
"Úsáidtear ábhar laistigh de chlib ``{% block%}`` i dteimpléad tuismitheora "
"mar fhriotán i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"You can use as many levels of inheritance as needed. One common way of using "
"inheritance is the following three-level approach:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an oiread leibhéil oidhreachta a úsáid agus is gá. Bealach "
"coitianta amháin chun oidhreacht a úsáid ná an cur chuige trí leibhéal seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"Create a ``base.html`` template that holds the main look-and-feel of your "
"site."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh teimpléad ``base.html` a choinníonn príomh-chuma agus mothú do "
"shuíomh."

msgid ""
"Create a ``base_SECTIONNAME.html`` template for each \"section\" of your "
"site. For example, ``base_news.html``, ``base_sports.html``. These templates "
"all extend ``base.html`` and include section-specific styles/design."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh teimpléad ``Base_SectionName.html ``do gach “rannóg” de do "
"shuíomh. Mar shampla, ``base_news.html``, ``base_sports.html``. Leathnaíonn "
"na teimpléid seo go léir ``base.html`` agus folaíonn stílea/dearadh roinn-"
"shonrach."

msgid ""
"Create individual templates for each type of page, such as a news article or "
"blog entry. These templates extend the appropriate section template."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh teimpléid aonair do gach cineál leathanaigh, mar shampla alt "
"nuachta nó iontráil blag. Leathnaíonn na teimpléid seo an teimpléad roinn cuí"

msgid ""
"This approach maximizes code reuse and helps to add items to shared content "
"areas, such as section-wide navigation."
msgstr ""
"Uasmhéadaíonn an cur chuige seo athúsáid cód agus cuidíonn sé le míreanna a "
"chur le réimsí ábhar roinnte, mar shampla nascleanúint ar fud an ranná"

msgid "Here are some tips for working with inheritance:"
msgstr "Seo roinnt leideanna chun oibriú le oidhreacht:"

msgid ""
"If you use :ttag:`{% extends %}<extends>` in a template, it must be the "
"first template tag in that template. Template inheritance won't work, "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Má úsáideann tú: ttag: `{% leathnaíonn%}<extends>` i dteimpléad, ní mór gurb "
"é an chéad chlib teimpléad sa teimpléad sin. Ní oibreoidh oidhreacht "
"teimpléid, ar shlí eile."

msgid ""
"More :ttag:`{% block %}<block>` tags in your base templates are better. "
"Remember, child templates don't have to define all parent blocks, so you can "
"fill in reasonable defaults in a number of blocks, then only define the ones "
"you need later. It's better to have more hooks than fewer hooks."
msgstr ""
"Tuilleadh: TTag: Tá clibeanna `{% block%}<block>` i do theimpléid bonn níos "
"fearr. Cuimhnigh, ní gá le teimpléid leanaí gach bloc tuismitheora a "
"shainiú, ionas gur féidir leat réamhshocruithe réasúnta a líonadh isteach i "
"roinnt bloic, ansin na cinn a theastaíonn uait a shainiú níos déanaí. Is "
"fearr níos mó crúcaí a bheith agat ná níos lú crúcaí."

msgid ""
"If you find yourself duplicating content in a number of templates, it "
"probably means you should move that content to a ``{% block %}`` in a parent "
"template."
msgstr ""
"Má aimsíonn tú féin ag dúbailt ábhar i roinnt teimpléid, is dócha go "
"gciallaíonn sé gur chóir duit an t-ábhar sin a bhogadh go ``{% block%} `i "
"dteimpléad tuismitheoirí."

msgid ""
"If you need to get the content of the block from the parent template, the "
"``{{ block.super }}`` variable will do the trick. This is useful if you want "
"to add to the contents of a parent block instead of completely overriding "
"it. Data inserted using ``{{ block.super }}`` will not be automatically "
"escaped (see the `next section`_), since it was already escaped, if "
"necessary, in the parent template."
msgstr ""
"Más gá duit ábhar an bhloc a fháil ón teimpléad tuismitheora, déanfaidh an "
"athróg ``{{block.super}}`` an cleas. Tá sé seo úsáideach más mian leat cur "
"le hábhar tuismitheoirí bloc in ionad é a shárú go hiomlán. Ní éalófar "
"sonraí a cuireadh isteach ag baint úsáide as ``{{block.super}}`` go "
"huathoibríoch (féach an `chéad roinn eile `_), ós rud é go raibh sé éalaithe "
"cheana féin, más gá, sa teimpléad tuismitheora."

msgid ""
"By using the same template name as you are inheriting from, :ttag:`{% "
"extends %}<extends>` can be used to inherit a template at the same time as "
"overriding it. Combined with ``{{ block.super }}``, this can be a powerful "
"way to make small customizations. "
"See :ref:`extending_an_overridden_template` in the *Overriding templates* "
"How-to for a full example."
msgstr ""
"Trí úsáid a bhaint as an ainm teimpléid céanna a bhfuil tú ag oidhreacht "
"uaidh, is <extends>féidir: ttag: `{%%}` a úsáid chun teimpléad a oidhreacht "
"ag an am céanna agus é a shárú. In éineacht le ``{{block.super}}``, is "
"féidir leis seo a bheith ina bhealach cumhachtach chun saincheaptha beaga a "
"dhéanamh. Féach:ref: `extending_an_overridden_template` sna teimpléid "
"*Overriding * Conas le haghaidh sampla iomlán."

msgid ""
"Variables created outside of a :ttag:`{% block %}<block>` using the template "
"tag ``as`` syntax can't be used inside the block. For example, this template "
"doesn't render anything:"
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir athróga a cruthaíodh lasmuigh de a:ttag: `{% block%}<block>` ag "
"baint úsáide as an gclib teimpléad ``as ``comhréiteach taobh istigh den "
"bhloc. Mar shampla, ní dhéanann an teimpléad seo aon rud:"

msgid ""
"For extra readability, you can optionally give a *name* to your ``{% "
"endblock %}`` tag. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh léiteachta breise, is féidir leat *ainm* a thabhairt go roghnach "
"do chlib ``{% endblock%}``. Mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"In larger templates, this technique helps you see which ``{% block %}`` tags "
"are being closed."
msgstr ""
"I dteimpléid níos mó, cabhraíonn an teicníc seo leat a fheiceáil cé na "
"clibeanna ``{% block%}`` atá á dhúnadh."

msgid ""
":ttag:`{% block %}<block>` tags are evaluated first. That's why the content "
"of a block is always overridden, regardless of the truthiness of surrounding "
"tags. For example, this template will *always* override the content of the "
"``title`` block:"
msgstr ""
":ttag: `{% block%}<block>` déantar clibeanna a mheas ar dtús. Sin an fáth go "
"ndéantar ábhar bloc a shárú i gcónaí, beag beann ar fhírinneacht na "
"gclibeanna máguaird. Mar shampla, cuirfidh an teimpléad seo *i gcónaí* ábhar "
"an bhloc ``teideal ``a shárú:"

msgid ""
"Finally, note that you can't define multiple :ttag:`block` tags with the "
"same name in the same template. This limitation exists because a block tag "
"works in \"both\" directions. That is, a block tag doesn't just provide a "
"hole to fill -- it also defines the content that fills the hole in the "
"*parent*. If there were two similarly-named :ttag:`block` tags in a "
"template, that template's parent wouldn't know which one of the blocks' "
"content to use."
msgstr ""
"Mar fhocal scoir, tabhair faoi deara nach féidir leat clibeanna iolracha: "
"ttag: `bloc` a shainiú leis an ainm céanna sa teimpléad céanna. Tá an "
"teorannú seo ann toisc go n-oibríonn bloc clib sa “dá threo”. Is é sin, ní "
"sholáthraíonn bloc clib ach poll le líonadh - sainmhíníonn sé freisin an t-"
"ábhar a líonann an poll san *tuismitheoir*. Dá mbeadh dhá chlib den chineál "
"céanna: ttag: `bloc` i dteimpléad, ní bheadh a fhios ag tuismitheoir an "
"teimpléid sin cén ceann de ábhar na mbloic le húsáid."

msgid "Automatic HTML escaping"
msgstr "Éalú uathoibríoch HTML"

msgid ""
"When generating HTML from templates, there's always a risk that a variable "
"will include characters that affect the resulting HTML. For example, "
"consider this template fragment:"
msgstr ""
"Agus HTML á ghiniúint agat ó theimpléid, tá baol ann i gcónaí go mbeidh "
"carachtair san athróg a théann i bhfeidhm ar an HTML mar thoradh air Mar "
"shampla, smaoinigh ar an mblúirt teimpléid seo"

msgid ""
"At first, this seems like a harmless way to display a user's name, but "
"consider what would happen if the user entered their name as this:"
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, is cosúil gur bealach neamhdhíobhálach é seo chun ainm úsáideora a "
"thaispeáint, ach smaoinigh ar cad a tharlódh dá gcuirfeadh an t-úsáideoir a "
"ainm isteach mar seo:"

msgid "With this name value, the template would be rendered as:"
msgstr "Leis an luach ainm seo, déanfaí an teimpléad a léiriú mar:"

msgid "...which means the browser would pop-up a JavaScript alert box!"
msgstr ""
"... rud a chiallaíonn go gcuirfeadh an brabhsálaí bosca foláirimh JavaScript!"

msgid "Similarly, what if the name contained a ``'<'`` symbol, like this?"
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, cad a tharlaíonn má bhí siombail ``'<'`` san ainm, mar "
"seo?"

msgid "That would result in a rendered template like this:"
msgstr "Bheadh teimpléad rindreáilte mar seo mar thoradh air sin:"

msgid ""
"...which, in turn, would result in the remainder of the web page being in "
"bold!"
msgstr ""
"... rud a d'fhágfadh, ina dhiaidh sin, go mbeadh an chuid eile den "
"leathanach gréasáin i dtrom!"

msgid ""
"Clearly, user-submitted data shouldn't be trusted blindly and inserted "
"directly into your web pages, because a malicious user could use this kind "
"of hole to do potentially bad things. This type of security exploit is "
"called a `Cross Site Scripting`_ (XSS) attack."
msgstr ""
"Is léir, níor cheart muinín a bheith ag sonraí a chuirtear isteach ag "
"úsáideoirí go dall agus a chur isteach go díreach i do leathanaigh "
"ghréasáin, toisc go bhféadfadh úsáideoir mailíseach poll den chineál seo a "
"úsáid chun rudaí a d'fhéad Tugtar ionsaí `Cross Site Scripting`_ (XSS) ar an "
"gcineál seo saothrú slándála."

msgid "To avoid this problem, you have two options:"
msgstr "Chun an fhadhb seo a sheachaint, tá dhá rogha agat:"

msgid ""
"One, you can make sure to run each untrusted variable through "
"the :tfilter:`escape` filter (documented below), which converts potentially "
"harmful HTML characters to unharmful ones. This was the default solution in "
"Django for its first few years, but the problem is that it puts the onus on "
"*you*, the developer / template author, to ensure you're escaping "
"everything. It's easy to forget to escape data."
msgstr ""
"Ceann amháin, is féidir leat a chinntiú go rith gach athróg neamhiontaofa "
"tríd an scagair:tfilter: `escape` (doiciméadaithe thíos), a athraíonn "
"carachtair HTML a d'fhéadfadh a bheith díobhálach go cinn neamhdhíobhálacha. "
"Ba é seo an réiteach réamhshocraithe i Django dá chéad chúpla bliain, ach is "
"í an fhadhb ná go gcuireann sé an t-ualach ar* uis*, an forbróir/údar "
"teimpléid, chun a chinntiú go bhfuil tú ag éalú ó gach rud. Tá sé éasca "
"dearmad a dhéanamh ar shonraí a éalú."

msgid ""
"Two, you can take advantage of Django's automatic HTML escaping. The "
"remainder of this section describes how auto-escaping works."
msgstr ""
"Dá cheann, is féidir leat leas a bhaint as éalú uathoibríoch HTML Django. "
"Déanann an chuid eile den chuid seo cur síos ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn éalú "
"uath"

msgid ""
"By default in Django, every template automatically escapes the output of "
"every variable tag. Specifically, these five characters are escaped:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe i Django, éalaíonn gach teimpléad aschur gach clib "
"athraitheach go huathoibríoch. Go sonrach, éalaítear na cúig charachtar seo:"

msgid ""
"Again, we stress that this behavior is on by default. If you're using "
"Django's template system, you're protected."
msgstr ""
"Arís, cuirimid béim go bhfuil an t-iompar seo ar siúl de réir "
"réamhshocraithe. Má tá córas teimpléad Django á úsáid agat, tá tú cosanta."

msgid "How to turn it off"
msgstr "Conas é a mhúchadh"

msgid ""
"If you don't want data to be auto-escaped, on a per-site, per-template level "
"or per-variable level, you can turn it off in several ways."
msgstr ""
"Mura dteastaíonn uait go n-éalfaí sonraí go huathoibríoch, ar leibhéal in "
"aghaidh an láithreáin, in aghaidh an teimpléid nó in aghaidh an leibhéal "
"athraithe, is féidir leat iad a mhúchadh ar bheal"

msgid ""
"Why would you want to turn it off? Because sometimes, template variables "
"contain data that you *intend* to be rendered as raw HTML, in which case you "
"don't want their contents to be escaped. For example, you might store a blob "
"of HTML in your database and want to embed that directly into your template. "
"Or, you might be using Django's template system to produce text that is "
"*not* HTML -- like an email message, for instance."
msgstr ""
"Cén fáth ar mhaith leat é a mhúchadh? Mar gheall ar uaireanta, tá sonraí i n-"
"athróga teimpléid a thugtar agat* a léiriú mar HTML amh, agus sa chás sin "
"níl tú ag iarraidh go n-éalfaí a n-ábhar. Mar shampla, d'fhéadfá blob HTML a "
"stóráil i do bhunachar sonraí agus gur mhaith leat é sin a leabú go díreach "
"i do theimpléad. Nó, b'fhéidir go bhfuil tú ag úsáid córas teimpléad Django "
"chun téacs ar* ní* HTML a tháirgeadh - cosúil le teachtaireacht ríomhphoist, "
"mar shampla."

msgid "For individual variables"
msgstr "Maidir le hathróga aonair"

msgid ""
"To disable auto-escaping for an individual variable, use the :tfilter:`safe` "
"filter:"
msgstr ""
"Chun éalú uathoibríoch a dhíchumasú le haghaidh athróg aonair, bain úsáid as "
"an scagair:tfilter: `safe`:"

msgid ""
"Think of *safe* as shorthand for *safe from further escaping* or *can be "
"safely interpreted as HTML*. In this example, if ``data`` contains "
"``'<b>'``, the output will be:"
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar *sábháilte* mar ghearrthóg d'*sábháilte ó éalú tuilleadh* nó "
"*is féidir é a léirmhíniú go sábháilte mar HTML*. <b>Sa sampla seo, má tá "
"```sonraí ```` ``, is é an t-aschur:"

msgid "For template blocks"
msgstr "Le haghaidh bloic teimpléad"

msgid ""
"To control auto-escaping for a template, wrap the template (or a particular "
"section of the template) in the :ttag:`autoescape` tag, like so:"
msgstr ""
"Chun éalú uathoibríoch le haghaidh teimpléad a rialú, fillte an teimpléad "
"(nó cuid áirithe den teimpléad) sa chlibe:ttag: `autoescape`, mar shampla:"

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`autoescape` tag takes either ``on`` or ``off`` as its argument. "
"At times, you might want to force auto-escaping when it would otherwise be "
"disabled. Here is an example template:"
msgstr ""
"Glacann an clibe:ttag: `autoescape` ``on`` nó ``off`` mar argóint. "
"Uaireanta, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat éalú uathoibríoch a chur i bhfeidhm "
"nuair a bheadh sé faoi mhíchumas Seo teimpléad sampla:"

msgid ""
"The auto-escaping tag passes its effect onto templates that extend the "
"current one as well as templates included via the :ttag:`include` tag, just "
"like all block tags. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an chlib éalaithe uathoibríoch a éifeacht ar theimpléid a "
"leathnaíonn an ceann reatha chomh maith le teimpléid atá san áireamh tríd an "
"gclibe:ttag: `include`, díreach cosúil le gach bloc chlib. Mar shampla:"

msgid "``base.html``"
msgstr "``Base.html``"

msgid "``child.html``"
msgstr "``Child.html``"

msgid ""
"Because auto-escaping is turned off in the base template, it will also be "
"turned off in the child template, resulting in the following rendered HTML "
"when the ``greeting`` variable contains the string ``<b>Hello!</b>``:"
msgstr ""
"<b>Toisc go bhfuil éalú uathoibríoch a mhúchadh sa bhonn teimpléad, múchfar "
"é freisin sa teimpléad linbh, agus mar thoradh air sin beidh an HTML "
"rindreáilte seo a leanas nuair a bhíonn an teaghrán ``Dia duit!</b> ``:"

msgid ""
"Generally, template authors don't need to worry about auto-escaping very "
"much. Developers on the Python side (people writing views and custom "
"filters) need to think about the cases in which data shouldn't be escaped, "
"and mark data appropriately, so things Just Work in the template."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, ní gá d'údair teimpléid a bheith buartha faoi éalú go "
"huathoibríoch go mór. Caithfidh forbróirí ar thaobh Python (daoine a "
"scríobhann tuairimí agus scagairí saincheaptha) smaoineamh ar na cásanna nár "
"chóir sonraí a éalú, agus sonraí a mharcáil go cuí, mar sin rudaí Just Work "
"sa teimpléad."

msgid ""
"If you're creating a template that might be used in situations where you're "
"not sure whether auto-escaping is enabled, then add an :tfilter:`escape` "
"filter to any variable that needs escaping. When auto-escaping is on, "
"there's no danger of the :tfilter:`escape` filter *double-escaping* data -- "
"the :tfilter:`escape` filter does not affect auto-escaped variables."
msgstr ""
"Má tá teimpléad á chruthú agat a d'fhéadfaí a úsáid i gcásanna nach bhfuil "
"tú cinnte an bhfuil éalú uathoibríoch cumasaithe, ansin cuir "
"scagair:tfilter: `escape` le haon athróg a chaithfidh éalú. Nuair a bhíonn "
"éalú uathoibríoch ar siúl, níl aon chontúirt ann go ndéanfaidh an "
"scagair:tfilter: `éalú `sonraí *éalú dúbailte* - ní dhéanann an "
"scagair:tfilter: `éalú` difear do athróga uathoibríoch éalaithe."

msgid "String literals and automatic escaping"
msgstr "Litríochtaí teaghráin agus éalú uathoibríoch"

msgid "As we mentioned earlier, filter arguments can be strings:"
msgstr ""
"Mar a luaigh muid níos luaithe, is féidir argóintí scagaire a bheith ina "
"teaghráin:"

msgid ""
"All string literals are inserted **without** any automatic escaping into the "
"template -- they act as if they were all passed through the :tfilter:`safe` "
"filter. The reasoning behind this is that the template author is in control "
"of what goes into the string literal, so they can make sure the text is "
"correctly escaped when the template is written."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear gach litríl teaghrán isteach ** gan aon éalú uathoibríoch isteach "
"sa teimpléad - gníomhaíonn siad amhail is dá gcuirfí iad uile tríd an "
"scagaire: tfilter: `safe`. Is é an réasúnaíocht atá taobh thiar de seo ná go "
"bhfuil an t-údar teimpléid i smacht ar an méid a théann isteach sa sreang "
"liteartha, ionas gur féidir leo a chinntiú go bhfuil an téacs éalaithe i "
"gceart nuair a scríobhtar"

msgid "This means you would write :"
msgstr "Ciallaíonn sé seo go scríobhfá:"

msgid "...rather than:"
msgstr "... seachas:"

msgid ""
"This doesn't affect what happens to data coming from the variable itself. "
"The variable's contents are still automatically escaped, if necessary, "
"because they're beyond the control of the template author."
msgstr ""
"Ní dhéanann sé seo difear don rud a tharlaíonn do shonraí a thagann ón "
"athróg féin. Éalaítear ábhar an athróg go huathoibríoch fós, más gá, toisc "
"go bhfuil siad lasmuigh de smacht údar an teimpléid."

msgid "Accessing method calls"
msgstr "Glaonna modh a rochtain"

msgid ""
"Most method calls attached to objects are also available from within "
"templates. This means that templates have access to much more than just "
"class attributes (like field names) and variables passed in from views. For "
"example, the Django ORM provides the :ref:`\"entry_set\"<topics-db-queries-"
"related>` syntax for finding a collection of objects related on a foreign "
"key. Therefore, given a model called \"comment\" with a foreign key "
"relationship to a model called \"task\" you can loop through all comments "
"attached to a given task like this:"
msgstr ""
"Tá an chuid is mó de na glaonna modh atá ceangailte le rudaí ar fáil ó "
"theimpléid laisti Ciallaíonn sé seo go bhfuil rochtain ag teimpléid ar i "
"bhfad níos mó ná tréithe ranga amháin (cosúil le hainmneacha réimse) agus "
"athróga a rith isteach ó thuairimí Mar shampla, soláthraíonn an ORM Django "
"comhréire:ref: `\"entry_set” <topics-db-queries-related>`chun bailiúchán "
"rudaí a bhaineann le heochair eachtrach a aimsiú. Dá bhrí sin, i bhfianaise "
"samhail ar a dtugtar “trácht” le príomhchaidreamh eachtrach le samhail ar a "
"dtugtar “tasc” is féidir leat lúb trí gach trácht atá ceangailte le tasc ar "
"leith mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Similarly, :doc:`QuerySets</ref/models/querysets>` provide a ``count()`` "
"method to count the number of objects they contain. Therefore, you can "
"obtain a count of all comments related to the current task with:"
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, soláthraíonn :doc: `QuerySets` modh</ref/models/"
"querysets> ``count () ``chun líon na rudaí atá iontu a chomhaireamh. Dá bhrí "
"sin, is féidir leat comhaireamh de na tuairimí go léir a bhaineann leis an "
"tasc reatha a fháil le:"

msgid ""
"You can also access methods you've explicitly defined on your own models:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rochtain a fháil ar mhodhanna atá sainmhínithe agat go "
"sainráite ar do chuid samhlacha féin:"

msgid "``models.py``"
msgstr "``models.py``"

msgid "``template.html``"
msgstr "``Teimpléad.html``"

msgid ""
"Because Django intentionally limits the amount of logic processing available "
"in the template language, it is not possible to pass arguments to method "
"calls accessed from within templates. Data should be calculated in views, "
"then passed to templates for display."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go gcuireann Django teorainn d'aon ghnó ar an méid próiseála loighic "
"atá ar fáil i dteanga na teimpléid, ní féidir argóintí a chur ar aghaidh "
"chuig glaonna modh a rochtaítear orthu ó laistigh Ba chóir sonraí a ríomh i "
"radhairc, ansin a chur chuig teimpléid le taispeáint."

msgid "Custom tag and filter libraries"
msgstr "Clib saincheaptha agus leabharlanna scagaire"

msgid ""
"Certain applications provide custom tag and filter libraries. To access them "
"in a template, ensure the application is in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` (we'd "
"add ``'django.contrib.humanize'`` for this example), and then use "
"the :ttag:`load` tag in a template:"
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn feidhmchláir áirithe leabharlanna clibeanna saincheaptha Chun "
"rochtain a fháil orthu i dteimpléad, cinntigh go bhfuil an feidhmchlár "
"in:setting: `INSTALLED_APPS` (chuirfimid ```django.contrib.humanize'` `leis "
"an sampla seo), agus ansin úsáid an clibe:ttag: `load` i dteimpléad:"

msgid ""
"In the above, the :ttag:`load` tag loads the ``humanize`` tag library, which "
"then makes the ``intcomma`` filter available for use. If you've "
"enabled :mod:`django.contrib.admindocs`, you can consult the documentation "
"area in your admin to find the list of custom libraries in your installation."
msgstr ""
"Sa mhéid thuas, luchtaíonn an clibe:ttag: `load` leabharlann clibeanna "
"``humanize``, rud a fhágann go bhfuil an scagaire ``intcomma` ar fáil le "
"húsáid ansin. Má tá: mod: `django.contrib.admindocs` cumasaithe agat, is "
"féidir leat dul i gcomhairle leis an réimse doiciméadaithe i do riarachán "
"chun liosta na leabharlanna saincheaptha i do shuiteáil a fháil."

msgid ""
"The :ttag:`load` tag can take multiple library names, separated by spaces. "
"Example:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leis an gclibe:ttag: `load `ilainmneacha leabharlainne a thógáil, "
"scartha le spásanna. Sampla:"

msgid ""
"See :doc:`/howto/custom-template-tags` for information on writing your own "
"custom template libraries."
msgstr ""
"Féach: doc: `/howto/custom-template-tags` le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le do "
"leabharlanna teimpléad saincheaptha féin a scríobh."

msgid "Custom libraries and template inheritance"
msgstr "Leabharlanna saincheaptha agus oidhreacht te"

msgid ""
"When you load a custom tag or filter library, the tags/filters are only made "
"available to the current template -- not any parent or child templates along "
"the template-inheritance path."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a luchtaíonn tú leabharlann clibeanna saincheaptha nó scagaire, ní "
"chuirtear na clibeanna/scagairí ar fáil ach don teimpléad reatha - ní aon "
"teimpléid tuismitheora nó leanbh ar feadh an chonair oidhreachta teimpléad."

msgid ""
"For example, if a template ``foo.html`` has ``{% load humanize %}``, a child "
"template (e.g., one that has ``{% extends \"foo.html\" %}``) will *not* have "
"access to the humanize template tags and filters. The child template is "
"responsible for its own ``{% load humanize %}``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, má tá ``{% load humanize%}`` i teimpléad ``foo.html``, ní "
"bheidh rochtain ag teimpléad leanbh (m.sh., ceann a bhfuil ``{% leathnaíonn "
"\"foo.html\"%}``) *ní bheidh rochtain ar na clibeanna agus na scagairí "
"teimpléad daonnaithe. Tá an teimpléad leanbh freagrach as a ``{% load "
"humanize%} `féin."

msgid "This is a feature for the sake of maintainability and sanity."
msgstr "Is gné é seo ar mhaithe le cothabháil agus sláine."

msgid ":doc:`The Templates Reference </ref/templates/index>`"
msgstr ":doc: `Tagairt na Teimpléid</ref/templates/index> '"

msgid ""
"Covers built-in tags, built-in filters, using an alternative template "
"language, and more."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn sé clibeanna ionsuite, scagairí ionsuite, ag baint úsáide as "
"teanga teimpléad malartach, agus"

msgid "Unicode data"
msgstr "Sonraí Unicode"

msgid "Django supports Unicode data everywhere."
msgstr "Tacaíonn Django le sonraí Unicode i ngach áit."

msgid ""
"This document tells you what you need to know if you're writing applications "
"that use data or templates that are encoded in something other than ASCII."
msgstr ""
"Insíonn an doiciméad seo duit cad is gá duit a bheith ar an eolas má tá tú "
"ag scríobh feidhmchláir a úsáideann sonraí nó teimpléid atá ionchódaithe i "
"rud éigin eile seachas ASCII."

msgid "Creating the database"
msgstr "An bunachar sonraí a chruthú"

msgid ""
"Make sure your database is configured to be able to store arbitrary string "
"data. Normally, this means giving it an encoding of UTF-8 or UTF-16. If you "
"use a more restrictive encoding -- for example, latin1 (iso8859-1) -- you "
"won't be able to store certain characters in the database, and information "
"will be lost."
msgstr ""
"Déan cinnte go bhfuil do bhunachar sonraí cumraithe chun a bheith in ann "
"sonraí sreangán treallach a stóráil De ghnáth, ciallaíonn sé seo ionchódú "
"UTF-8 nó UTF-16 a thabhairt dó. Má úsáideann tú ionchódú níos sriantacha - "
"mar shampla, latin1 (iso8859-1) - ní bheidh tú in ann carachtair áirithe a "
"stóráil sa bhunachar sonraí, agus caillfear faisnéis."

msgid ""
"MySQL users, refer to the `MySQL manual`_ for details on how to set or alter "
"the database character set encoding."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideoirí MySQL, féach ar an `lámhleabhar MySQL `_ le haghaidh sonraí "
"maidir le conas ionchódú tacar carachtair bunachar sonraí a shocrú nó a "
"athrú."

msgid ""
"PostgreSQL users, refer to the `PostgreSQL manual`_ for details on creating "
"databases with the correct encoding."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideoirí PostgreSQL, féach ar an `lámhleabhar PostgreSQL `_ le haghaidh "
"sonraí maidir le bunachair sonraí a chruthú leis an ionchódú ceart."

msgid ""
"Oracle users, refer to the `Oracle manual`_ for details on how to set "
"(`section 2`_) or alter (`section 11`_) the database character set encoding."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideoirí Oracle, féach ar an `lámhleabhar Oracle`_ le haghaidh sonraí "
"maidir le conas ionchódú tacar carachtar bunachar sonraí a shocrú (`alt 2`_) "
"nó a athrú (`alt 11`_)."

msgid ""
"SQLite users, there is nothing you need to do. SQLite always uses UTF-8 for "
"internal encoding."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideoirí SQLite, níl aon rud is gá duit a dhéanamh. Úsáideann SQLite UTF-8 "
"i gcónaí le haghaidh ionchódú inmheánach."

msgid ""
"All of Django's database backends automatically convert strings into the "
"appropriate encoding for talking to the database. They also automatically "
"convert strings retrieved from the database into strings. You don't even "
"need to tell Django what encoding your database uses: that is handled "
"transparently."
msgstr ""
"Tiontaíonn cúltaca bunachar sonraí go léir Django teaghráin go huathoibríoch "
"ina ionchódú cuí chun labhairt leis an mbunachar sonraí. Déanann siad "
"teaghráin a aisghabhadh ón mbunachar sonraí a thiontú go huathoi Ní gá duit "
"fiú a rá le Django cén ionchódú a úsáideann do bhunachar sonraí: déantar é "
"sin a láimhseáil go trédhearcach."

msgid "For more, see the section \"The database API\" below."
msgstr "Le haghaidh tuilleadh, féach an chuid “An API bunachar sonraí” thíos."

msgid "General string handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil teaghrán gin"

msgid ""
"Whenever you use strings with Django -- e.g., in database lookups, template "
"rendering or anywhere else -- you have two choices for encoding those "
"strings. You can use normal strings or bytestrings (starting with a 'b')."
msgstr ""
"Aon uair a úsáideann tú teaghráin le Django - m.sh. i lorg bunachar sonraí, "
"rindreáil teimpléad nó áit ar bith eile - tá dhá rogha agat chun na "
"teaghráin sin a ionchódú. Is féidir leat gnáthteaghráin nó bytestrings a "
"úsáid (ag tosú le 'b')."

msgid ""
"A bytestring does not carry any information with it about its encoding. For "
"that reason, we have to make an assumption, and Django assumes that all "
"bytestrings are in UTF-8."
msgstr ""
"Ní iompraíonn bytestring aon fhaisnéis leis faoina ionchódú. Ar an gcúis "
"sin, caithfimid toimhde a dhéanamh, agus glacann Django leis go bhfuil gach "
"bytestrings i UTF-8."

msgid ""
"If you pass a string to Django that has been encoded in some other format, "
"things will go wrong in interesting ways. Usually, Django will raise a "
"``UnicodeDecodeError`` at some point."
msgstr ""
"Má chuireann tú sreang chuig Django atá ionchódaithe i bhformáid éigin eile, "
"rachaidh rudaí mícheart ar bhealaí suimiúla. De ghnáth, ardóidh Django "
"``UnicodeDecodeError`` ag pointe éigin."

msgid ""
"If your code only uses ASCII data, it's safe to use your normal strings, "
"passing them around at will, because ASCII is a subset of UTF-8."
msgstr ""
"Mura n-úsáideann do chód ach sonraí ASCII, tá sé sábháilte do "
"ghnáthshreangáin a úsáid, agus iad a chur timpeall ar uacht, toisc gur fo-"
"thacar de UTF-8 é ASCII."

msgid ""
"Don't be fooled into thinking that if your :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` "
"setting is set to something other than ``'utf-8'`` you can use that other "
"encoding in your bytestrings! :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` only applies to the "
"strings generated as the result of template rendering (and email). Django "
"will always assume UTF-8 encoding for internal bytestrings. The reason for "
"this is that the :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting is not actually under "
"your control (if you are the application developer). It's under the control "
"of the person installing and using your application -- and if that person "
"chooses a different setting, your code must still continue to work. Ergo, it "
"cannot rely on that setting."
msgstr ""
"Ná bíodh a mhealladh ag smaoineamh má tá do socrú: setting: "
"`DEFAULT_CHARSET` socraithe ar rud éigin seachas ``utf-8'`` is féidir leat "
"an t-ionchódú eile sin a úsáid i do theagraí bytestrings! :setting: Ní "
"bhaineann `DEFAULT_CHARSET` ach leis na teaghráin a ghintear mar thoradh ar "
"rindreáil teimpléid (agus ríomhphost). Glacfaidh Django le hionchódú UTF-8 i "
"gcónaí le haghaidh bytestrings inmheánacha. Is é an chúis leis seo ná nach "
"bhfuil an socrú: setting: `DEFAULT_CHARSET` faoi do smacht i ndáiríre (más "
"tusa an forbróir feidhmchláir). Tá sé faoi smacht an duine atá ag suiteáil "
"agus ag úsáid d'iarratas - agus má roghnaíonn an duine sin suíomh difriúil, "
"caithfidh do chód leanúint ar aghaidh ag obair. Mar sin, ní féidir leis "
"brath ar an suíomh sin."

msgid ""
"In most cases when Django is dealing with strings, it will convert them to "
"strings before doing anything else. So, as a general rule, if you pass in a "
"bytestring, be prepared to receive a string back in the result."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna nuair a bhíonn Django ag déileáil le teaghráin, "
"tiontóidh sé iad go teaghráin sula ndéanfaidh sé aon rud eile. Mar sin, mar "
"riail ghinearálta, má théann tú i mbytestring, bí réidh le sreang a fháil ar "
"ais sa toradh."

msgid "Translated strings"
msgstr "Teagáin aistrithe"

msgid ""
"Aside from strings and bytestrings, there's a third type of string-like "
"object you may encounter when using Django. The framework's "
"internationalization features introduce the concept of a \"lazy "
"translation\" -- a string that has been marked as translated but whose "
"actual translation result isn't determined until the object is used in a "
"string. This feature is useful in cases where the translation locale is "
"unknown until the string is used, even though the string might have "
"originally been created when the code was first imported."
msgstr ""
"Seachas teaghráin agus bytestrings, tá tríú cineál réad cosúil le sreanga "
"ann a d'fhéadfá teacht ar aghaidh agus Django á úsáid agat. Tugann gnéithe "
"idirnáisiúnaithe an chreat coincheap “aistriúcháin leisciúil” isteach - "
"sreang atá marcáilte mar aistrithe ach nach gcinntear a thoradh aistriúcháin "
"iarbhír go dtí go n-úsáidtear an réad i sreang. Tá an ghné seo úsáideach i "
"gcásanna nach bhfuil an láithreán aistriúcháin ar eolas go dtí go n-"
"úsáidtear an sreang, cé go bhféadfadh gur cruthaíodh an teaghrán ar dtús "
"nuair a allmhairíodh an cód den chéad uair."

msgid ""
"Normally, you won't have to worry about lazy translations. Just be aware "
"that if you examine an object and it claims to be a "
"``django.utils.functional.__proxy__`` object, it is a lazy translation. "
"Calling ``str()`` with the lazy translation as the argument will generate a "
"string in the current locale."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ní bheidh ort a bheith buartha faoi aistriúcháin leisciúla. Bí ar "
"an eolas má scrúdaíonn tú réad agus maíonn sé gur ``django.utils.functional "
"é. __proxy__`` réad, is aistriúchán leisciúil é. Ag glaoch ar `str () ``leis "
"an aistriúchán leisciúil mar gheobhaidh an argóint teaghrán sa réigiún "
"reatha."

msgid ""
"For more details about lazy translation objects, refer to "
"the :doc:`internationalization </topics/i18n/index>` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí faoi rudaí aistriúcháin leisciúil, féach ar an "
"doiciméadach:doc: `</topics/i18n/index> idirnáisiúnaíon`."

msgid "Useful utility functions"
msgstr "feidhmeanna fóntais úsáideacha"

msgid ""
"Because some string operations come up again and again, Django ships with a "
"few useful functions that should make working with string and bytestring "
"objects a bit easier."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go dtagann roinnt oibríochtaí teaghráin suas arís agus arís eile, "
"seolann Django le cúpla feidhm úsáideach ar chóir go mbeadh sé níos éasca "
"oibriú le rudaí sreangán agus bytestring."

msgid "Conversion functions"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna tiontú"

msgid ""
"The ``django.utils.encoding`` module contains a few functions that are handy "
"for converting back and forth between strings and bytestrings."
msgstr ""
"Tá cúpla feidhm sa mhodúl ``django.utils.encoding`` atá áisiúil chun tiontú "
"anall agus anall idir teaghráin agus bytestrings."

msgid ""
"``smart_str(s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=False, errors='strict')`` "
"converts its input to a string. The ``encoding`` parameter specifies the "
"input encoding. (For example, Django uses this internally when processing "
"form input data, which might not be UTF-8 encoded.) The ``strings_only`` "
"parameter, if set to True, will result in Python numbers, booleans and "
"``None`` not being converted to a string (they keep their original types). "
"The ``errors`` parameter takes any of the values that are accepted by "
"Python's ``str()`` function for its error handling."
msgstr ""
"``smart_str (s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=false, errors='strict') "
"``athraíonn a ionchur go sreang. Sonraíonn an paraiméadar ``ionchód`` an "
"ionchódú ionchuir. (Mar shampla, úsáideann Django é seo go hinmheánach agus "
"sonraí ionchuir foirme á bpróiseáil, nach bhféadfadh a bheith ionchódaithe "
"UTF-8.) Mar thoradh ar an bparaiméadar `strings_only`, má tá sé socraithe go "
"True, ní thiontófar uimhreacha Python, booleans agus ``None`` go sreang "
"(coinníonn siad a gcineálacha bunaidh). Glacann an paraiméadar ``earráidí "
"``aon cheann de na luachanna a nglacann feidhm ``str ()`` Python lena "
"láimhseáil earráide."

msgid ""
"``force_str(s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=False, errors='strict')`` is "
"identical to ``smart_str()`` in almost all cases. The difference is when the "
"first argument is a :ref:`lazy translation <lazy-translations>` instance. "
"While ``smart_str()`` preserves lazy translations, ``force_str()`` forces "
"those objects to a string (causing the translation to occur). Normally, "
"you'll want to use ``smart_str()``. However, ``force_str()`` is useful in "
"template tags and filters that absolutely *must* have a string to work with, "
"not just something that can be converted to a string."
msgstr ""
"``force_str (s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=false, errors='strict') "
"``comhionann le ``smart_str ()`` i mbeagnach gach cás. Is é an difríocht "
"nuair is é an chéad argóint a: ref: `aistriúchán leisciúil <lazy-"
"translations>`sampla. Cé go gcaomhnóidh ``smart_str () ``aistriúcháin "
"leisciúla, cuireann ``force_str ()`` iallach ar na rudaí sin chuig teaghrán "
"(is cúis leis an aistriúchán tarlú). De ghnáth, beidh tú ag iarraidh "
"``smart_str () ``a úsáid. Mar sin féin, tá ``force_str () ``úsáideach i "
"gclibeanna teimpléad agus scagairí a bhfuil teaghrán aige go hiomlán* le "
"bheith ag obair leo, ní amháin rud is féidir a thiontú go sreang."

msgid ""
"``smart_bytes(s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=False, errors='strict')`` is "
"essentially the opposite of ``smart_str()``. It forces the first argument to "
"a bytestring. The ``strings_only`` parameter has the same behavior as for "
"``smart_str()`` and ``force_str()``. This is slightly different semantics "
"from Python's builtin ``str()`` function, but the difference is needed in a "
"few places within Django's internals."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``smart_bytes (s, encoding='utf-8', strings_only=false, errors='strict') "
"``go bunúsach a mhalairt de ``smart_str ()``. Cuireann sé iallach ar an "
"gcéad argóint chuig bytestring. Tá an t-iompar céanna ag an bparaiméadar "
"``strings_only`` agus le haghaidh ``smart_str () ``agus ``force_str ()``. Is "
"séimeantaic beagán difriúil é seo ó fheidhm 'str () ``tógáilte Python, ach "
"tá an difríocht ag teastáil i gcúpla áit laistigh de inmheánacha Django."

msgid ""
"Normally, you'll only need to use ``force_str()``. Call it as early as "
"possible on any input data that might be either a string or a bytestring, "
"and from then on, you can treat the result as always being a string."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ní bheidh ort ach ``force_str () ``a úsáid. Glaoigh air chomh "
"luath agus is féidir ar aon sonraí ionchuir a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ina "
"shreang nó ina mbeagán, agus as sin ar aghaidh, is féidir leat an toradh a "
"chóireáil mar shreang i gcónaí."

msgid "URI and IRI handling"
msgstr "Láimhseáil URI agus IRI"

msgid ""
"Web frameworks have to deal with URLs (which are a type of IRI). One "
"requirement of URLs is that they are encoded using only ASCII characters. "
"However, in an international environment, you might need to construct a URL "
"from an :rfc:`IRI <3987>` -- very loosely speaking, a :rfc:`URI <3986>` that "
"can contain Unicode characters. Use these functions for quoting and "
"converting an IRI to a URI:"
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh creataí gréasáin déileáil le URLanna (ar cineál IRI iad). "
"Riachtanas amháin a bhaineann le URLanna ná go ndéantar iad a ionchódú ag "
"baint úsáide as carachtair ASCII amháin. <3986>Mar sin féin, i "
"<3987>dtimpeallacht idirnáisiúnta, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort URL a thógáil ó "
"an:rfc: `IRI `-- go han-scaoilte, a:rfc: `URI` a d'fhéadfadh carachtair "
"Unicode a bheith ann. Úsáid na feidhmeanna seo chun IRI a lua agus a thiontú "
"go URI:"

msgid ""
"The :func:`django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri()` function, which implements "
"the conversion from IRI to URI as required by :rfc:`3987#section-3.1`."
msgstr ""
"An fheidhme:func: `django.utils.encoding.iri_to_uri () `, a chuireann an "
"tiontú ó IRI go URI i bhfeidhm mar a theastaíonn uir:rfc: `3987 #section "
"-3.1`."

msgid ""
"The :func:`urllib.parse.quote` and :func:`urllib.parse.quote_plus` functions "
"from Python's standard library."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmeanna:func: `urllib.parse.quote` agus:func: `urllib.parse.quote_plus` "
"ó leabharlann caighdeánach Python."

msgid ""
"These two groups of functions have slightly different purposes, and it's "
"important to keep them straight. Normally, you would use ``quote()`` on the "
"individual portions of the IRI or URI path so that any reserved characters "
"such as '&' or '%' are correctly encoded. Then, you apply ``iri_to_uri()`` "
"to the full IRI and it converts any non-ASCII characters to the correct "
"encoded values."
msgstr ""
"Tá cuspóirí beagán difriúil ag an dá ghrúpa feidhmeanna seo, agus tá sé "
"tábhachtach iad a choinneáil díreach. De ghnáth, úsáidfeá ``quote () ``ar na "
"codanna aonair den chosán IRI nó URI ionas go ndéantar aon charachtair "
"áirithe mar '&' nó '% 'a ionchódú i gceart. Ansin, cuireann tú `iri_to_uri "
"() ``i bhfeidhm ar an IRI iomlán agus athraíonn sé aon charachtair neamh-"
"ASCII go dtí na luachanna cearta ionchódaithe."

msgid ""
"Technically, it isn't correct to say that ``iri_to_uri()`` implements the "
"full algorithm in the IRI specification. It doesn't (yet) perform the "
"international domain name encoding portion of the algorithm."
msgstr ""
"Go teicniúil, níl sé ceart a rá go gcuireann ``iri_to_uri () ``an algartam "
"iomlán i bhfeidhm i sonraíocht IRI. Ní dhéanann sé (fós) an chuid ionchódú "
"ainm fearainn idirnáisiúnta den algartam."

msgid ""
"The ``iri_to_uri()`` function will not change ASCII characters that are "
"otherwise permitted in a URL. So, for example, the character '%' is not "
"further encoded when passed to ``iri_to_uri()``. This means you can pass a "
"full URL to this function and it will not mess up the query string or "
"anything like that."
msgstr ""
"Ní athróidh an fheidhm ``iri_to_uri () ``carachtair ASCII a cheadaítear ar "
"shlí eile i URL. Mar sin, mar shampla, ní ionchódaítear an carachtar '%' a "
"thuilleadh nuair a chuirtear ar aghaidh chuig ``iri_to_uri () ``. Ciallaíonn "
"sé seo gur féidir leat URL iomlán a chur chuig an bhfeidhm seo agus ní "
"chuirfidh sé praiseach ar an sreang fiosrúcháin nó aon rud mar sin."

msgid "An example might clarify things here:"
msgstr "D'fhéadfadh sampla rudaí a shoiléiriú anseo:"

msgid ""
"If you look carefully, you can see that the portion that was generated by "
"``quote()`` in the second example was not double-quoted when passed to "
"``iri_to_uri()``. This is a very important and useful feature. It means that "
"you can construct your IRI without worrying about whether it contains non-"
"ASCII characters and then, right at the end, call ``iri_to_uri()`` on the "
"result."
msgstr ""
"Má fhéachann tú go cúramach, is féidir leat a fheiceáil nár luadh dúbailte "
"an chuid a ghinigh le ``quote () ``sa dara sampla nuair a cuireadh chuig "
"`iri_to_uri ()``. Is gné an-tábhachtach agus úsáideach é seo. Ciallaíonn sé "
"gur féidir leat do IRI a thógáil gan a bheith buartha faoi an bhfuil "
"carachtair neamh-ASCII ann agus ansin, ag an deireadh, glaoch ar `iri_to_uri "
"() `ar an toradh."

msgid ""
"Similarly, Django provides :func:`django.utils.encoding.uri_to_iri()` which "
"implements the conversion from URI to IRI as per :rfc:`3987#section-3.2`."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, soláthraíonn Django: func: "
"`django.utils.encoding.uri_to_iri () `a chuireann an tiontú ó URI go IRI i "
"bhfeidhm mar: rfc: `3987 #section -3.2`."

msgid "An example to demonstrate:"
msgstr "Sampla chun a thaispeáint:"

msgid ""
"In the first example, the UTF-8 characters are unquoted. In the second, the "
"percent-encodings remain unchanged because they lie outside the valid UTF-8 "
"range or represent a reserved character."
msgstr ""
"Sa chéad shampla, ní luaitear na carachtair UTF-8. Sa dara ceann, fanann na "
"hinchódaithe céatadáin gan athrú toisc go bhfuil siad lasmuigh den raon "
"bailí UTF-8 nó go léiríonn siad carachtar forchoimeádta."

msgid ""
"Both ``iri_to_uri()`` and ``uri_to_iri()`` functions are idempotent, which "
"means the following is always true::"
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhmeanna ``iri_to_uri () ``agus ``uri_to_iri ()`` idempotent, rud a "
"chiallaíonn go bhfuil an méid seo a leanas fíor i gcónaí:"

msgid ""
"So you can safely call it multiple times on the same URI/IRI without risking "
"double-quoting problems."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin is féidir leat glaoch go sábháilte air arís agus arís eile ar an URI/"
"IRI céanna gan fadhbanna luachana dúbailte a chur i mbaol."

msgid ""
"Because all strings are returned from the database as ``str`` objects, model "
"fields that are character based (CharField, TextField, URLField, etc.) will "
"contain Unicode values when Django retrieves data from the database. This is "
"*always* the case, even if the data could fit into an ASCII bytestring."
msgstr ""
"Toisc go gcuirtear gach teaghráin ar ais ón mbunachar sonraí mar rudaí "
"`str`, beidh luachanna Unicode i réimsí samhail atá bunaithe ar charachtar "
"(CharField, TextField, URLField, srl.) Nuair a aisghabhann Django sonraí ón "
"mbunachar sonraí. Is é seo* i gcónaí* an cás, fiú dá bhféadfadh na sonraí "
"oiriúnach i mbytestring ASCII."

msgid ""
"You can pass in bytestrings when creating a model or populating a field, and "
"Django will convert it to strings when it needs to."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat dul isteach i mbytestrings agus tú ag cruthú samhail nó ag "
"daonrú réimse, agus déanfaidh Django é a thiontú go teaghráin nuair is gá dó."

msgid "Taking care in ``get_absolute_url()``"
msgstr "Ag tabhairt aire i ``get_absolute_url () ``"

msgid ""
"URLs can only contain ASCII characters. If you're constructing a URL from "
"pieces of data that might be non-ASCII, be careful to encode the results in "
"a way that is suitable for a URL. The :func:`~django.urls.reverse` function "
"handles this for you automatically."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir ach carachtair ASCII a bheith ag URLanna. Má tá URL á thógáil agat "
"ó phíosaí sonraí a d'fhéadfadh a bheith neamh-ASCII, bí cúramach na torthaí "
"a ionchódú ar bhealach atá oiriúnach do URL. Láimhseálann an fheidhm: Func: "
"`~django.urls.reverse` é seo duit go huathoibríoch."

msgid ""
"If you're constructing a URL manually (i.e., *not* using the ``reverse()`` "
"function), you'll need to take care of the encoding yourself. In this case, "
"use the ``iri_to_uri()`` and ``quote()`` functions that were documented "
"above_. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá URL á thógáil agat de láimh (ie, *ní* ag baint úsáide as an bhfeidhm "
"``reverse () `), beidh ort aire a thabhairt don ionchódú tú féin. Sa chás "
"seo, bain úsáid as na feidhmeanna ``iri_to_uri () ``agus ``quote ()`` a "
"doiciméadaíodh thuas_. Mar shampla::"

msgid ""
"This function returns a correctly encoded URL even if ``self.location`` is "
"something like \"Jack visited Paris & Orléans\". (In fact, the "
"``iri_to_uri()`` call isn't strictly necessary in the above example, because "
"all the non-ASCII characters would have been removed in quoting in the first "
"line.)"
msgstr ""
"Tugann an fheidhm seo URL ionchódaithe i gceart fiú má tá ``self.location`` "
"rud cosúil le “Thug Jack cuairt ar Pháras & Orléans”. (Go deimhin, níl an "
"glao `iri_to_uri () ``riachtanach go docht sa sampla thuas, toisc go mbainfí "
"na carachtair neamh-ASCII go léir agus iad ag lua sa chéad líne.)"

msgid "Use strings when creating templates manually::"
msgstr "Úsáid teaghráin agus teimpléid á chruthú de láimh:"

msgid ""
"But the common case is to read templates from the filesystem. If your "
"template files are not stored with a UTF-8 encoding, adjust "
"the :setting:`TEMPLATES` setting. The built-"
"in :py:mod:`~django.template.backends.django` backend provides the "
"``'file_charset'`` option to change the encoding used to read files from "
"disk."
msgstr ""
"Ach is é an cás coitianta ná teimpléid a léamh ón gcóras comhaid. Mura "
"stóráiltear do chuid comhad teimpléad le ionchódú UTF-8, déan an socrú: "
"socrú: `TEMPLATES` a choigeartú. Soláthraíonn an cúltaca ionsuite: py:mod: "
"`~django.template.backends.django` an rogha ```file_charset'` chun an t-"
"ionchódú a úsáidtear chun comhaid a léamh ón diosca a athrú."

msgid ""
"The :setting:`DEFAULT_CHARSET` setting controls the encoding of rendered "
"templates. This is set to UTF-8 by default."
msgstr ""
"Rialaíonn an socrú: SETTING: `DEFAULT_CHARSET` ionchódú teimpléid "
"rindreáilte. Tá sé seo socraithe go UTF-8 de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Template tags and filters"
msgstr "Clibeanna teimpléad agus scagair"

msgid ""
"A couple of tips to remember when writing your own template tags and filters:"
msgstr ""
"Cúpla leid le cuimhneamh agus do chlibeanna agus scagairí teimpléad féin á "
"scríobh:"

msgid ""
"Always return strings from a template tag's ``render()`` method and from "
"template filters."
msgstr ""
"Cuir teaghráin ar ais i gcónaí ó mhodh `render () ``chlib teimpléad agus ó "
"scagairí teimpléad."

msgid ""
"Use ``force_str()`` in preference to ``smart_str()`` in these places. Tag "
"rendering and filter calls occur as the template is being rendered, so there "
"is no advantage to postponing the conversion of lazy translation objects "
"into strings. It's easier to work solely with strings at that point."
msgstr ""
"Úsáid ``force_str () ``i rogha ``smart_str ()`` sna háiteanna seo. Tarlaíonn "
"rindreáil clibeanna agus glaonna scagaire de réir mar a bhíonn an teimpléad "
"á léiriú, mar sin níl aon bhuntáiste ann tiontú rudaí aistriúcháin leisciúil "
"a chur siar ina teaghráin. Tá sé níos éasca oibriú amháin le teaghráin ag an "
"bpointe sin."

msgid "Files"
msgstr "Comhaid"

msgid ""
"If you intend to allow users to upload files, you must ensure that the "
"environment used to run Django is configured to work with non-ASCII file "
"names. If your environment isn't configured correctly, you'll encounter "
"``UnicodeEncodeError`` exceptions when saving files with file names or "
"content that contains non-ASCII characters."
msgstr ""
"Má tá sé ar intinn agat ligean d'úsáideoirí comhaid a uaslódáil, ní mór duit "
"a chinntiú go bhfuil an timpeallacht a úsáidtear chun Django a reáchtáil "
"cumraithe chun oibriú le hainmneacha comhaid nach Mura bhfuil do "
"thimpeallacht cumraithe i gceart, beidh eisceachtaí `UnicodeEncodeError` "
"agat agus tú ag sábháil comhaid le hainmneacha comhaid nó ábhar ina bhfuil "
"carachtair neamh-ASCII."

msgid ""
"Filesystem support for UTF-8 file names varies and might depend on the "
"environment. Check your current configuration in an interactive Python shell "
"by running::"
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn tacaíocht chórais chomhaid d'ainmneacha comhaid UTF-8 agus "
"d'fhéadfadh sé go mbraitheann sé ar an gcomhshaol. Seiceáil do chumraíocht "
"reatha i bhlaosc idirghníomhach Python trí rith:"

msgid "This should output \"UTF-8\"."
msgstr "Ba chóir go n-aschur sé seo “UTF-8\"."

msgid ""
"The ``LANG`` environment variable is responsible for setting the expected "
"encoding on Unix platforms. Consult the documentation for your operating "
"system and application server for the appropriate syntax and location to set "
"this variable. See the :doc:`/howto/deployment/wsgi/modwsgi` for examples."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-athróg comhshaoil `LANG` freagrach as an ionchódú a bhfuil súil leis "
"a shocrú ar ardáin Unix. Téigh i gcomhairle leis na cáipéisíocht do do "
