msgid "``get_script_prefix()``"
msgstr "```get_script_prefix () ``"

msgid ""
"Normally, you should always use :func:`~django.urls.reverse` to define URLs "
"within your application. However, if your application constructs part of the "
"URL hierarchy itself, you may occasionally need to generate URLs. In that "
"case, you need to be able to find the base URL of the Django project within "
"its web server (normally, :func:`~django.urls.reverse` takes care of this "
"for you). In that case, you can call ``get_script_prefix()``, which will "
"return the script prefix portion of the URL for your Django project. If your "
"Django project is at the root of its web server, this is always ``\"/\"``."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ba chóir duit: func: `~django.urls.reverse` a úsáid i gcónaí chun "
"URLanna a shainiú laistigh de d'iarratas. Mar sin féin, má thógann "
"d'fheidhmchlár cuid den ordlathas URL féin, b'fhéidir go mbeidh ort URLanna "
"a ghiniúint ó am go chéile. Sa chás sin, ní mór duit a bheith in ann bunURL "
"an tionscadail Django a aimsiú laistigh dá fhreastalaí gréasáin (de ghnáth, "
"tugann: func: `~django.urls.reverse` aire dó seo duit). Sa chás sin, is "
"féidir leat glaoch ar ``get_script_prefix () ``, a thabharfaidh an chuid "
"réimír script den URL ar ais do thionscadal Django. Má tá do thionscadal "
"Django ag fréamh a fhreastalaí gréasáin, is é seo i gcónaí ``” /\"`."

msgid ""
"This function **cannot** be used outside of the request-response cycle since "
"it relies on values initialized during that cycle."
msgstr ""
"Ní féidir an fheidhm seo ** a úsáid lasmuigh den timthriall iarrata-"
"freagartha ós rud é go mbraitheann sé ar luachanna a thionscnaíodh le linn "
"na timthrialla sin."

msgid "``django.urls`` functions for use in URLconfs"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna ``django.urls ``le húsáid in URLConfs"

msgid "``path()``"
msgstr "``cosán () ``"

msgid "Returns an element for inclusion in ``urlpatterns``. For example::"
msgstr ""
"Tugann eilimint ar ais lena n-áireamh in ``urlpatterns``. Mar shampla::"

msgid "``route``"
msgstr "``beala``"

msgid ""
"The ``route`` argument should be a string "
"or :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy()` (see :ref:`translating-"
"urlpatterns`) that contains a URL pattern. The string may contain angle "
"brackets (like ``<username>`` above) to capture part of the URL and send it "
"as a keyword argument to the view. The angle brackets may include a "
"converter specification (like the ``int`` part of ``<int:section>``) which "
"limits the characters matched and may also change the type of the variable "
"passed to the view. For example, ``<int:section>`` matches a string of "
"decimal digits and converts the value to an ``int``."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an argóint ``route`` ina teaghrán nó:func: "
"`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy () `(féach:ref: `translating-"
"urlpatterns`) ina bhfuil patrún URL. D'fhéadfadh lúibíní uillinne a bheith "
"sa sreangán (cosúil le <username>```thuas) chun cuid den URL a ghabháil agus "
"é a sheoladh mar argóint eochairfhocal chuig an radharc. Féadfaidh "
"sonraíocht tiontaire a bheith san áireamh sna lúibíní uillinne (cosúil leis "
"an gcuid ``int ``de<int:section>``) a chuireann teorainn leis na carachtair "
"a mheaitseáiltear agus féadfaidh sé cineál an athróg a chuirtear chuig an "
"radharc a athrú freisin. Mar shampla, meaitseálann <int:section>```sreang "
"dhigit deachúil agus athraíonn sé an luach go `int``."

msgid ""
"When processing a request, Django starts at the first pattern in "
"``urlpatterns`` and makes its way down the list, comparing the requested URL "
"against each pattern until it finds one that matches. See :ref:`how-django-"
"processes-a-request` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Agus iarratas á phróiseáil, tosaíonn Django ag an gcéad phatrún in "
"`urlpatterns` agus déanann sé a bhealach síos an liosta, ag comparáid idir "
"an URL iarrtha i gcoinne gach patrún go dtí go bhfaigheann sé ceann a "
"mheaitseálann. Féach: ref: `how django-processes-a-request` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
"Patterns don't match GET and POST parameters, or the domain name. For "
"example, in a request to ``https://www.example.com/myapp/``, the URLconf "
"will look for ``myapp/``. In a request to ``https://www.example.com/myapp/?"
"page=3``, the URLconf will also look for ``myapp/``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mheaitseálann patrúin paraiméadair GET agus POST, nó an t-ainm fearainn. "
"Mar shampla, in iarratas chuig ``https://www.example.com/myapp/``, cuardóidh "
"an URLConf ``myapp/``. In iarratas chuig ``https://www.example.com/myapp/?"
"page=3``, cuardóidh an URLConf ``myapp/`` freisin."

msgid "``view``"
msgstr "```amharc``"

msgid ""
"The ``view`` argument is a view function or the result "
"of :meth:`~django.views.generic.base.View.as_view` for class-based views. It "
"can also be a :func:`django.urls.include`."
msgstr ""
"Is feidhm amharc é an argóint ``view`` nó toradh de:meth: "
"`~django.views.generic.base.view.as_view` le haghaidh tuairimí rang-"
"bhunaithe. Is féidir é a bheith freisin a:func: `django.urls.include`."

msgid ""
"When Django finds a matching pattern, it calls the specified view function "
"with an :class:`~django.http.HttpRequest` object as the first argument and "
"any \"captured\" values from the route as keyword arguments."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a aimsíonn Django patrún meaitseála, glaonn sé an fheidhm amharc "
"sonraithe le réad an:class: `~django.http.http.httpRequest` mar an chéad "
"argóint agus aon luachanna “gabháilte” ón mbealach mar argóintí "
"eochairfhocal."

msgid ""
"The ``kwargs`` argument allows you to pass additional arguments to the view "
"function or method. See :ref:`views-extra-options` for an example."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann an argóint ``kwargs ``duit argóintí breise a chur ar aghaidh chuig "
"an bhfeidhm nó an modh amharc. Féach:ref: `views-extra-options` mar shampla."

msgid ""
"Naming your URL lets you refer to it unambiguously from elsewhere in Django, "
"especially from within templates. This powerful feature allows you to make "
"global changes to the URL patterns of your project while only touching a "
"single file."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann ainmniú do URL duit tagairt a dhéanamh dó gan amhbhrí ó áiteanna "
"eile i Django, go háirithe ó theimpléid laistigh de. Ligeann an ghné "
"chumhachtach seo duit athruithe domhanda a dhéanamh ar phatrúin URL do "
"thionscadail agus gan teagmháil le comhad amháin."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`Naming URL patterns <naming-url-patterns>` for why the ``name`` "
"argument is useful."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `Patrúin URL a ainmniúch <naming-url-patterns>`maidir le cén fáth "
"go bhfuil an argóint ``ainm ``úsáideach."

msgid "``re_path()``"
msgstr "``re_path () ``"

msgid ""
"The ``route`` argument should be a string "
"or :func:`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy()` (see :ref:`translating-"
"urlpatterns`) that contains a regular expression compatible with "
"Python's :py:mod:`re` module. Strings typically use raw string syntax "
"(``r''``) so that they can contain sequences like ``\\d`` without the need "
"to escape the backslash with another backslash. When a match is made, "
"captured groups from the regular expression are passed to the view -- as "
"named arguments if the groups are named, and as positional arguments "
"otherwise. The values are passed as strings, without any type conversion."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh an argóint ``route`` ina teaghrán nó:func: "
"`~django.utils.translation.gettext_lazy () `(féach:ref: `translating-"
"urlpatterns`) ina bhfuil abairt rialta atá comhoiriúnach le modúl Python: "
"py:mod: `re`. Is iondúil go n-úsáideann teaghráin comhréir sreangán amh "
"(``r\"``) ionas gur féidir leo seicheamh mar ``\\ d`` a bheith iontu gan gá "
"an cúlghabháil a éalú le cúltaca eile. Nuair a dhéantar meaitseáil, cuirtear "
"grúpaí gabháilte ón léiriú rialta chuig an dearcadh - mar argóintí ainmnithe "
"má ainmnítear na grúpaí, agus mar argóintí seasaimh a shlí eile. Cuirtear na "
"luachanna ar aghaidh mar teaghráin, gan aon chineál comhshó."

msgid ""
"When a ``route`` ends with ``$`` the whole requested URL, matching "
"against :attr:`~django.http.HttpRequest.path_info`, must match the regular "
"expression pattern (:py:func:`re.fullmatch` is used)."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a chríochnaíonn ``ród`` le `$`` caithfidh an URL iomlán a iarrtar, a "
"mheaitseáil cois:attr: `~django.http.httpRequest.path_info`, an patrún "
"abairt rialta a mheaitseáil (:py:func: `re.fullmatch` úsáidtear)."

msgid ""
"The ``view``, ``kwargs`` and ``name`` arguments are the same as "
"for :func:`~django.urls.path()`."
msgstr ""
"Tá na hargóintí ``dearca``, `kwargs`` agus ``ainm ``mar an gcéanna le "
"haghaidh: func: `~django.urls.path () `."

msgid "``include()``"
msgstr "```san áireamh () ``"

msgid ""
"A function that takes a full Python import path to another URLconf module "
"that should be \"included\" in this place. Optionally, "
"the :term:`application namespace` and :term:`instance namespace` where the "
"entries will be included into can also be specified."
msgstr ""
"Feidhm a thógann cosán iomlán allmhairithe Python chuig modúl URLConf eile "
"ba chóir a bheith “san áireamh” san áit seo. Go roghnach, is féidir an:term: "
"`spás ainmneacha feidhmchláir` agus:term: `spás ainmneacha sampla` ina "
"gcuirfear na hiontrálacha san áireamh iontu a shonrú freisin."

msgid ""
"Usually, the application namespace should be specified by the included "
"module. If an application namespace is set, the ``namespace`` argument can "
"be used to set a different instance namespace."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth, ba cheart an modúl san áireamh spás ainmneacha an fheidhmchláir a "
"shonrú. Má shocraítear spás ainmneacha feidhmchláir, is féidir an argóint "
"``spás ainmneacha ``a úsáid chun spás ainmneacha sampla difriúil a shocrú."

msgid ""
"``include()`` also accepts as an argument either an iterable that returns "
"URL patterns or a 2-tuple containing such iterable plus the names of the "
"application namespaces."
msgstr ""
"Glacann ``include () ``mar argóint freisin le hathrinneach a thugann patrúin "
"URL ar ais nó le 2-tuple ina bhfuil athraitheach den sórt sin móide "
"ainmneacha spás ainmneacha an fheidhmchláir."

msgid "URLconf module (or module name)"
msgstr "Modúl URLConf (nó ainm an mhodúil)"

msgid "Instance namespace for the URL entries being included"
msgstr "Spás ainmneacha sampla do na hiontrálacha URL atá san áireamh"

msgid ""
"Iterable of :func:`~django.urls.path` and/or :func:`~django.urls.re_path` "
"instances."
msgstr ""
"Inathraithe o:func: `~django.urls.path` agus/nó :func: "
"`~django.urls.re_path` cásanna."

msgid "Application namespace for the URL entries being included"
msgstr "Spás ainmneacha feidhmchláir do na hiontrálacha URL atá san áireamh"

msgid "See :ref:`including-other-urlconfs` and :ref:`namespaces-and-include`."
msgstr ""
"Féach:ref: `including-ear-urlconfs` agus:ref: `spaces-ainmnea-agus-include`."

msgid "``register_converter()``"
msgstr "``tiontaire_cláraigh () ``"

msgid ""
"The function for registering a converter for use "
"in :func:`~django.urls.path()` ``route``\\s."
msgstr ""
"An fheidhm chun tiontaire a chlárú le húsáid in:func: `~django.urls.path () "
"```route``\\ s."

msgid ""
"The ``converter`` argument is a converter class, and ``type_name`` is the "
"converter name to use in path patterns. See :ref:`registering-custom-path-"
"converters` for an example."
msgstr ""
"Is aicme tiontaire é an argóint ``tiontaire``, agus is é `type_name`` an t-"
"ainm tiontaire le húsáid i bpatrúin cosáin. Féach:ref: `cláraithe "
"saincheapach-path-tionters` mar shampla."

msgid "Overriding existing converters is deprecated."
msgstr "Tá an tiontaire atá ann cheana a shárú."

msgid "``django.conf.urls`` functions for use in URLconfs"
msgstr "Feidhmeanna ``django.conf.urls ``le húsáid in URLConfs"

msgid "``static()``"
msgstr "``statach () ``"

msgid ""
"Helper function to return a URL pattern for serving files in debug mode::"
msgstr ""
"Feidhm chúntóra chun patrún URL a thabhairt ar ais chun comhaid a "
"sheirbheáil i mód dífhabhtaithe::"

msgid "``handler400``"
msgstr "``Handler400``"

msgid ""
"A callable, or a string representing the full Python import path to the view "
"that should be called if the HTTP client has sent a request that caused an "
"error condition and a response with a status code of 400."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir glaoch, nó sreang a léiríonn an cosán iomlán allmhairithe Python "
"chuig an radharc ba chóir a ghlaoch má sheol an cliant HTTP iarratas a "
"d'fhág riocht earráide agus freagra le cód stádais 400."

msgid ""
"By default, this is :func:`django.views.defaults.bad_request`. If you "
"implement a custom view, be sure it accepts ``request`` and ``exception`` "
"arguments and returns an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseBadRequest`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, is é seo: func: "
"`django.views.defaults.bad_request`. Má chuireann tú dearcadh saincheaptha i "
"bhfeidhm, bí cinnte go nglacann sé le hargóintí ``request`` agus "
"``exception`` agus tuairisceann sé an:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponseBadRequest`."

msgid "``handler403``"
msgstr "``Handler403``"

msgid ""
"A callable, or a string representing the full Python import path to the view "
"that should be called if the user doesn't have the permissions required to "
"access a resource."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir glaoch, nó sreang a léiríonn an cosán iomlán allmhairithe Python "
"chuig an radharc ar chóir a ghlaoch mura bhfuil na ceadanna a theastaíonn ag "
"an úsáideoir chun rochtain a fháil ar acmhainn."

msgid ""
"By default, this is :func:`django.views.defaults.permission_denied`. If you "
"implement a custom view, be sure it accepts ``request`` and ``exception`` "
"arguments and returns an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseForbidden`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, is é seo: func: "
"`django.views.defaults.permission_denied`. Má chuireann tú dearcadh "
"saincheaptha i bhfeidhm, bí cinnte go nglacann sé le hargóintí ``request`` "
"agus ``exception`` agus tuairisceann sé an:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponseForbidden`."

msgid "``handler404``"
msgstr "``Handler404 ``"

msgid ""
"A callable, or a string representing the full Python import path to the view "
"that should be called if none of the URL patterns match."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir glaoch, nó sreang a léiríonn cosán iomlán iompórtála Python chuig "
"an radharc ar chóir a ghlaoch mura n-oireann aon cheann de na patrúin URL."

msgid ""
"By default, this is :func:`django.views.defaults.page_not_found`. If you "
"implement a custom view, be sure it accepts ``request`` and ``exception`` "
"arguments and returns an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseNotFound`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, is é seo: func: "
"`django.views.defaults.page_not_found`. Má chuireann tú dearcadh "
"saincheaptha i bhfeidhm, bí cinnte go nglacann sé le hargóintí ``request`` "
"agus ``exception`` agus tuairisceann sé an:class: "
"`~django.http.httpResponseNotFound`."

msgid "``handler500``"
msgstr "``Handler500``"

msgid ""
"A callable, or a string representing the full Python import path to the view "
"that should be called in case of server errors. Server errors happen when "
"you have runtime errors in view code."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir glaoch, nó sreang a léiríonn an cosán iomlán allmhairithe Python "
"chuig an radharc ar chóir a ghlaoch i gcás earráidí freastalaí. Tarlaíonn "
"earráidí freastalaí nuair a bhíonn earráidí rith agat i gcód amharc."

msgid ""
"By default, this is :func:`django.views.defaults.server_error`. If you "
"implement a custom view, be sure it accepts a ``request`` argument and "
"returns an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseServerError`."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, is é seo: func: "
"`django.views.defaults.server_error`. Má chuireann tú dearcadh saincheaptha "
"i bhfeidhm, bí cinnte go nglacann sé le argóint ``request`` agus filleann sé "
"an:class: `~django.http.httpResponseservererror`."

msgid "Django Utils"
msgstr "Úsáideacha Django"

msgid ""
"This document covers all stable modules in ``django.utils``. Most of the "
"modules in ``django.utils`` are designed for internal use and only the "
"following parts can be considered stable and thus backwards compatible as "
"per the :ref:`internal release deprecation policy <internal-release-"
"deprecation-policy>`."
msgstr ""
"Clúdaíonn an doiciméad seo gach modúl cobhsaí i ``django.utils``. <internal-"
"release-deprecation-policy>Tá an chuid is mó de na modúil i `django.utils`` "
"deartha le haghaidh úsáide inmheánach agus ní féidir ach na codanna seo a "
"leanas a mheas go cobhsaí agus dá bhrí sin comhoiriúnach ar ais de réir "
"na:ref: `beartas díghníomhaíochta scaoilte inmheánach`."

msgid "``django.utils.cache``"
msgstr "``django.utils.cache``"

msgid ""
"This module contains helper functions for controlling HTTP caching. It does "
"so by managing the ``Vary`` header of responses. It includes functions to "
"patch the header of response objects directly and decorators that change "
"functions to do that header-patching themselves."
msgstr ""
"Tá feidhmeanna cúntóra sa mhodúl seo chun caismú HTTP a rialú. Déanann sé "
"amhlaidh trí cheannteideal freagraí ``Vary`` a bhainistiú. Cuimsíonn sé "
"feidhmeanna chun ceanntásc na rudaí freagartha a phaisteáil go díreach agus "
"maisitheoirí a athraíonn feidhmeanna chun an ceannteideal sin a dhéanamh iad "
"féin."

msgid "For information on the ``Vary`` header, see :rfc:`9110#section-12.5.5`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh faisnéise faoin gceannteideal ``Vary``, féach:rfc: `9110 "
"#section -12.5.5`."

msgid ""
"Essentially, the ``Vary`` HTTP header defines which headers a cache should "
"take into account when building its cache key. Requests with the same path "
"but different header content for headers named in ``Vary`` need to get "
"different cache keys to prevent delivery of wrong content."
msgstr ""
"Go bunúsach, sainmhíníonn an ceannteideal HTTP ``Vary`` cé na ceannteidil ba "
"chóir do taisce a chur san áireamh agus a eochair taisce á thógáil. Ní mór "
"d'iarratais leis an gcosán céanna ach ábhar ceanntásc difriúil do "
"cheanntásca a ainmnítear in ``Vary`` eochracha taisce éagsúla a fháil chun "
"ábhar mícheart a sheachadadh a"

msgid ""
"For example, :doc:`internationalization </topics/i18n/index>` middleware "
"would need to distinguish caches by the ``Accept-language`` header."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, :doc: bheadh ar mheánghearraí `idirnáisiúnaíochta` idirdhealú a "
"dhéanamh ar chaisce</topics/i18n/index> anna leis an gceannteideal ``Accept-"
"Teanga ``."

msgid ""
"This function patches the ``Cache-Control`` header by adding all keyword "
"arguments to it. The transformation is as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Paiseann an fheidhm seo an ceannteideal ``Cache-Control ``trí gach argóint "
"eochairfhocal a chur leis. Is é seo a leanas an claochlú:"

msgid ""
"All keyword parameter names are turned to lowercase, and underscores are "
"converted to hyphens."
msgstr ""
"Déantar gach ainm paraiméadar eochairfhocal a chasadh go litreacha beaga, "
"agus déantar béim a thiontú go hiphens."

msgid ""
"If the value of a parameter is ``True`` (exactly ``True``, not just a true "
"value), only the parameter name is added to the header."
msgstr ""
"Más luach paraiméadar ``True`` (go díreach ``True``, ní fíor-luach amháin), "
"ní chuirtear ach ainm an pharaiméadair leis an gceannteideal."

msgid ""
"All other parameters are added with their value, after applying ``str()`` to "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear na paraiméadair eile go léir lena luach, tar éis ``str () ``a chur "
"i bhfeidhm air."

msgid ""
"Returns the max-age from the response Cache-Control header as an integer (or "
"``None`` if it wasn't found or wasn't an integer)."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an t-aois uasta ar ais ón gceannteideal Cache-Control freagra mar "
"shláimhir (nó ``None`` mura bhfuarthas é nó mura raibh sé ina slámhshláir)."

msgid "Adds some useful headers to the given ``HttpResponse`` object:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé roinnt ceanntála úsáideacha leis an réad ``HttpResponse`` a "
"thugtar:"

msgid "``Expires``"
msgstr "``Deireadh ``"

msgid "``Cache-Control``"
msgstr "``Rialú Cache ``"

msgid "Each header is only added if it isn't already set."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuirtear gach ceannteideal leis ach mura bhfuil sé socraithe cheana féin."

msgid ""
"``cache_timeout`` is in seconds. The :setting:`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` "
"setting is used by default."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``cache_timeout`` i soicindí. Úsáidtear an socrú: SETTING: "
"`CACHE_MIDDLEWARE_SECONDS` de réir réamhshocraithe."

msgid "Adds an ``Expires`` header to the current date/time."
msgstr "Cuireann ceanntásc ``Expires`` leis an dáta/am reatha."

msgid ""
"Adds a ``Cache-Control: max-age=0, no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, "
"private`` header to a response to indicate that a page should never be "
"cached."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé ceannteideal ``Cache-Control: max-age = 0, no-cache, no-store, "
"must-athbhailíniú, príobháideach`` le freagra chun a léiriú nár chóir "
"leathanach a chosc riamh."

msgid ""
"Adds (or updates) the ``Vary`` header in the given ``HttpResponse`` object. "
"``newheaders`` is a list of header names that should be in ``Vary``. If "
"headers contains an asterisk, then ``Vary`` header will consist of a single "
"asterisk ``'*'``, according to :rfc:`9110#section-12.5.5`. Otherwise, "
"existing headers in ``Vary`` aren't removed."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann (nó nuashonraíonn sé) an ceannteideal ``Vary`` sa réad "
"``HttpResponse`` a thugtar. Is liosta d'ainmneacha ceanntásc is ea "
"``newheaders`` ar chóir a bheith i ``Vary``. Má tá réiltín i gceanntásca, "
"ansin beidh réiltín amháin ``*'`` comhdhéanta de cheanntásc ``Vary``, de "
"réir: rfc: `9110 #section -12.5.5`. Seachas sin, ní bhaintear ceanntásca atá "
"ann cheana i ``Vary``."

msgid ""
"Returns a cache key based on the request path. It can be used in the request "
"phase because it pulls the list of headers to take into account from the "
"global path registry and uses those to build a cache key to check against."
msgstr ""
"Tugann eochair taisce ar ais bunaithe ar an gcosán iarratais. Is féidir é a "
"úsáid i gcéim an iarratais toisc go dtarraingíonn sé liosta na gceanntásca "
"le cur san áireamh ón gclárlann cosáin domhanda agus úsáideann sé iad siúd "
"chun eochair taisce a thógáil chun seiceáil ina choinne."

msgid ""
"If there is no headerlist stored, the page needs to be rebuilt, so this "
"function returns ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil aon cheannliosta stóráilte ann, ní mór an leathanach a atógáil, "
"mar sin filleann an fheidhm seo ``None ``."

msgid ""
"Learns what headers to take into account for some request path from the "
"response object. It stores those headers in a global path registry so that "
"later access to that path will know what headers to take into account "
"without building the response object itself. The headers are named in the "
"``Vary`` header of the response, but we want to prevent response generation."
msgstr ""
"Foghlaimíonn sé cad iad na ceanntásca atá le cur san áireamh do chosán "
"iarratais éigin ón réad freagartha Stórálann sé na ceannteidil sin i "
"gclárlann cosáin domhanda ionas go mbeidh a fhios ag rochtain níos déanaí ar "
"an gcosán sin cad iad na ceanntásca atá le cur san áireamh gan an réad "
"Ainmnítear na ceanntásca i gceanntásc ``Vary`` den fhreagra, ach ba mhaith "
"linn giniúint freagartha a chosc."

msgid ""
"The list of headers to use for cache key generation is stored in the same "
"cache as the pages themselves. If the cache ages some data out of the cache, "
"this means that we have to build the response once to get at the Vary header "
"and so at the list of headers to use for the cache key."
msgstr ""
"Stóráiltear liosta na gceanntásca atá le húsáid le haghaidh giniúint eochair "
"taisce sa taisce céanna leis na leathanaigh féin. Má thugann an taisce "
"roinnt sonraí as an taisce, ciallaíonn sé seo go gcaithfimid an freagra a "
"thógáil uair amháin chun teacht ar an gceannteideal Vary agus mar sin ag "
"liosta na gceanntásc le húsáid don eochair taisce."

msgid "``django.utils.dateparse``"
msgstr "``django.utils.dateparse``"

msgid "The functions defined in this module share the following properties:"
msgstr ""
"Tá na hairíonna seo a leanas ag na feidhmeanna atá sainmhínithe sa mhodúl seo"

msgid ""
"They accept strings in ISO 8601 date/time formats (or some close "
"alternatives) and return objects from the corresponding classes in "
"Python's :mod:`datetime` module."
msgstr ""
"Glacann siad le teaghráin i bhformáidí dáta/ama ISO 8601 (nó roinnt roghanna "
"dlúth) agus filleann siad rudaí ó na ranganna comhfhreagracha i modúl "
"Python: MOD: `datetime`."

msgid ""
"They raise :exc:`ValueError` if their input is well formatted but isn't a "
"valid date or time."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn siad: exc: `ValueError` má tá a n-ionchur formáidithe go maith ach "
"nach dáta nó am bailí é."

msgid "They return ``None`` if it isn't well formatted at all."
msgstr ""
"Filleann siad ``None ``mura bhfuil sé formáidithe go maith ar chor ar bith."

msgid ""
"They accept up to picosecond resolution in input, but they truncate it to "
"microseconds, since that's what Python supports."
msgstr ""
"Glacann siad suas le taifeach picosecond in ionchur, ach cuireann siad é a "
"ghearradh go micreasoicind, ós rud é sin a thacaíonn Python le."

msgid "Parses a string and returns a :class:`datetime.date`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé teaghrán a pháirseáil agus a: class: `datetime.date` ar ais."

msgid "Parses a string and returns a :class:`datetime.time`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé teaghrán a pháirseáil agus a: class: `datetime.time` ar ais."

msgid ""
"UTC offsets aren't supported; if ``value`` describes one, the result is "
"``None``."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaítear le háirithe UTC; má chuireann ``luach`` cur síos ar cheann "
"amháin, is é ``None`` an toradh."

msgid "Parses a string and returns a :class:`datetime.datetime`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé teaghrán a pháirseáil agus a: class: `datetime.datetime` ar ais."

msgid ""
"UTC offsets are supported; if ``value`` describes one, the result's "
"``tzinfo`` attribute is a :class:`datetime.timezone` instance."
msgstr ""
"Tacaítear le hoiriúintí UTC; má chuireann ``value`` cur síos ar cheann "
"amháin, is é a: class: `datetime.timezone` tréith ``tzinfo`` an torthaí."

msgid "Parses a string and returns a :class:`datetime.timedelta`."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé teaghrán a pháirseáil agus a: class: `datetime.timedelta` ar ais."

msgid ""
"Expects data in the format ``\"DD HH:MM:SS.uuuuuu\"``, ``\"DD "
"HH:MM:SS,uuuuuu\"``,  or as specified by ISO 8601 (e.g. ``P4DT1H15M20S`` "
"which is equivalent to ``4 1:15:20``) or PostgreSQL's day-time interval "
"format (e.g. ``3 days 04:05:06``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá súil ag súil le sonraí san fhormáid ``\"DD HH:MM:SS.uuuuuuu\"``, ``\"DD "
"HH:MM:SS, uuuuuu\"``, nó mar a shonraítear le ISO 8601 (m.sh. "
"`P4DT1H15M20S`` atá coibhéis le ``4 1:15:20 ``) nó formáid eatramh lae-ama "
"PostgreSQL (m.sh. `3 lá 04:05:06``)."

msgid "``django.utils.decorators``"
msgstr "``django.utils.decorators ``"

msgid ""
"Converts a function decorator into a method decorator. It can be used to "
"decorate methods or classes; in the latter case, ``name`` is the name of the "
"method to be decorated and is required."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn maisitheoir feidhme ina mhaisitheoir modh. Is féidir é a úsáid "
"chun modhanna nó ranganna a mhaisiú; sa chás deireanach, is é ``ainm "
"``ainm`` ainm an mhodha atá le maisiú agus tá sé riachtanach."

msgid ""
"``decorator`` may also be a list or tuple of functions. They are wrapped in "
"reverse order so that the call order is the order in which the functions "
"appear in the list/tuple."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh “maisitheoir” ina liosta nó tiúpla feidhmeanna "
"freisin. Tá siad fillte in ord droim ionas gurb é an t-ordú glaonna an t-ord "
"ina bhfuil na feidhmeanna le feiceáil sa liosta/tuple."

msgid ""
"See :ref:`decorating class based views <decorating-class-based-views>` for "
"example usage."
msgstr ""
"Féach: tagairt: `tuairimí bunaithe ar rang a mhaisiú <decorating-class-based-"
"views>`mar shampla úsáid."

msgid ""
"Given a middleware class, returns a view decorator. This lets you use "
"middleware functionality on a per-view basis. The middleware is created with "
"no params passed."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar rang lár-earraí, filleann sé maisitheoir radharc ar ais. "
"Ligeann sé seo duit feidhmiúlacht middleware a úsáid ar bhonn aghaidh an "
"amharc. Cruthaítear an middleware gan aon pharams a rith."

msgid ""
"It assumes middleware that's compatible with the old style of Django 1.9 and "
"earlier (having methods like ``process_request()``, ``process_exception()``, "
"and ``process_response()``)."
msgstr ""
"Glacann sé le middleware atá comhoiriúnach le seanstíl Django 1.9 agus níos "
"luaithe (modhanna mar `process_request () ``, `process_exception ()``, agus "
"``process_response () ``)."

msgid ""
"Like ``decorator_from_middleware``, but returns a function that accepts the "
"arguments to be passed to the middleware_class. For example, "
"the :func:`~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page` decorator is created "
"from the ``CacheMiddleware`` like this::"
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le `decorator_from_middleware``, ach filleann feidhm a ghlacann leis "
"na hargóintí atá le cur chuig an middleware_class. Mar shampla, cruthaítear "
"maisitheoir:func: `~django.views.decorators.cache.cache_page` ón "
"`cacheMiddleware`` mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Marks a middleware as :ref:`synchronous-only <async-middleware>`. (The "
"default in Django, but this allows you to future-proof if the default ever "
"changes in a future release.)"
msgstr ""
"<async-middleware>Marcaíonn sé meán-earraí mar: ref: `synchronous-only `. "
"(An réamhshocrú i Django, ach tugann sé seo deis duit cruthúnas sa todhchaí "
"má athraíonn an réamhshocrú riamh i scaoileadh amach anseo.)"

msgid ""
"Marks a middleware as :ref:`asynchronous-only <async-middleware>`. Django "
"will wrap it in an asynchronous event loop when it is called from the WSGI "
"request path."
msgstr ""
"<async-middleware>Marcálann sé meán-earraí mar: ref: `asynchronous-only `. "
"Fillfidh Django é i lúb imeachta asincrónach nuair a ghlaofar air ón gcosán "
"iarratais WSGI."

msgid ""
"Marks a middleware as :ref:`sync and async compatible <async-middleware>`, "
"this allows to avoid converting requests. You must implement detection of "
"the current request type to use this decorator. See :ref:`asynchronous "
"middleware documentation <async-middleware>` for details."
msgstr ""
"Marcálann sé meán-earraí mar: ref: `sync agus async comhoiriúnach <async-"
"middleware>`, ceadaíonn sé seo iarratais a thiontú a sheachaint. Ní mór duit "
"braite an cineál iarratais reatha a chur i bhfeidhm chun an maisitheoir seo "
"a úsáid. <async-middleware>Féach: ref: `doiciméadú middleware asincrónach "
"`le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "``django.utils.encoding``"
msgstr "``django.utils.encoding``"

msgid ""
"Returns a ``str`` object representing arbitrary object ``s``. Treats "
"bytestrings using the ``encoding`` codec."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé réad ``str`` a léiríonn réad treallach ``s``. Déileálann sé le "
"bytestrings ag baint úsáide as an codec ``encoding``."

msgid ""
"If ``strings_only`` is ``True``, don't convert (some) non-string-like "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"Má tá ``strings_only`` ``True``, ná tiontaigh (roinnt) rudaí neamh-"
"shreangacha."

msgid "Determine if the object instance is of a protected type."
msgstr "Faigh amach an bhfuil an t-ábhar réada de chineál cosanta."

msgid ""
"Objects of protected types are preserved as-is when passed to "
"``force_str(strings_only=True)``."
msgstr ""
"Caomhnaítear rudaí de chineálacha cosanta mar atá nuair a chuirtear ar "
"aghaidh chuig ``force_str (strings_only=true) ``."

msgid ""
"Similar to ``smart_str()``, except that lazy instances are resolved to "
"strings, rather than kept as lazy objects."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le ``smart_str () ``, ach amháin go ndéantar cásanna leisciúla a "
"réiteach ar teaghráin, seachas a choinneáil mar rudaí leisciúla."

msgid ""
"Returns a bytestring version of arbitrary object ``s``, encoded as specified "
"in ``encoding``."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé leagan bytestring de réad treallach ``s``, ionchódaithe mar a "
"shonraítear i ``encoding``."

msgid ""
"Similar to ``smart_bytes``, except that lazy instances are resolved to "
"bytestrings, rather than kept as lazy objects."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le ``smart_bytes``, ach amháin go ndéantar cásanna leisciúla a "
"réiteach ar bytestrings, seachas a choinneáil mar rudaí leisciúla."

msgid ""
"Convert an Internationalized Resource Identifier (IRI) portion to a URI "
"portion that is suitable for inclusion in a URL."
msgstr ""
"Tiontaigh cuid Aitheantóir Acmhainní Idirnáisiúnta (IRI) go cuid URI atá "
"oiriúnach lena áireamh i URL."

msgid ""
"This is the algorithm from section 3.1 of :rfc:`3987#section-3.1`, slightly "
"simplified since the input is assumed to be a string rather than an "
"arbitrary byte stream."
msgstr ""
"Seo an algartam ó chuid 3.1 de:rfc: `3987 #section -3.1`, atá beagán "
"simplithe ós rud é go nglactar leis gur sreang é an t-ionchur seachas sruth "
"beot treallach."

msgid ""
"Takes an IRI (string or UTF-8 bytes) and returns a string containing the "
"encoded result."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé IRI (sreang nó UTF-8 bytes) agus filleann sé teaghrán ina bhfuil "
"an toradh ionchódaithe."

msgid ""
"Converts a Uniform Resource Identifier into an Internationalized Resource "
"Identifier."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn Aitheantóir Acmhainní Aonfhoirmeach ina Aitheantóir Acmhainní Idir"

msgid "This is an algorithm from section 3.2 of :rfc:`3987#section-3.2`."
msgstr "Is algartam é seo ó chuid 3.2 de:rfc: `3987 #section -3.2`."

msgid ""
"Takes a URI in ASCII bytes and returns a string containing the encoded "
"result."
msgstr ""
"Tógann sé URI i mbeátaí ASCII agus filleann sé teaghrán ina bhfuil an toradh "
"ionchódaithe."

msgid ""
"Convert a file system path to a URI portion that is suitable for inclusion "
"in a URL. The path is assumed to be either UTF-8 bytes, string, or "
"a :class:`~pathlib.Path`."
msgstr ""
"Tiontaigh cosán córais chomhaid go cuid URI atá oiriúnach le cuimsiú i URL. "
"Glactar leis gurb é an cosán UTF-8 bytes, string, nó a: class: "
"`~pathLib.path`."

msgid ""
"This method will encode certain characters that would normally be recognized "
"as special characters for URIs.  Note that this method does not encode the ' "
"character, as it is a valid character within URIs. See "
"``encodeURIComponent()`` JavaScript function for more details."
msgstr ""
"Ionchódfaidh an modh seo carachtair áirithe a d'aithníodh de ghnáth mar "
"charachtair speisialta do URIs. Tabhair faoi deara nach ndéanann an modh seo "
"an carachtar 'a ionchódú, toisc gur carachtar bailí é laistigh de URIs. "
"Féach feidhm JavaScript ``EncodeuriComponent () ``le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"sonraí."

msgid "Returns an ASCII string containing the encoded result."
msgstr "Filleann sé teaghrán ASCII ina bhfuil an toradh ionchódaithe."

msgid ""
"Escapes the unsafe characters from the path portion of a Uniform Resource "
"Identifier (URI)."
msgstr ""
"Éalaíonn sé na carachtair neamhshábháilte ón gcuid cosáin d'Aitheantóir "
"Acmhainní Aonfhoirmeach (URI)."

msgid "``django.utils.feedgenerator``"
msgstr "``django.utils.feedgenerator``"

msgid ""
"For simplifying the selection of a generator use "
"``feedgenerator.DefaultFeed`` which is currently ``Rss201rev2Feed``"
msgstr ""
"Chun roghnú gineadóir a shimpliú bain úsáid as ``FeedGenerator.defaultFeed`` "
"atá ``RSS201Rev2Feed`` faoi láthair"

msgid ""
"For definitions of the different versions of RSS, see: https://"
"web.archive.org/web/20110718035220/http://diveintomark.org/archives/"
"2004/02/04/incompatible-rss"
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh sainmhínithe ar na leaganacha éagsúla de RSS, féach: https://"
"web.archive.org/web/20110718035220/http://diveintomark.org/archives/"
"2004/02/04/incompatible-rss"

msgid "Creates a TagURI."
msgstr "Cruthaíonn TagUri."

msgid ""
"See https://web.archive.org/web/20110514113830/http://diveintomark.org/"
"archives/2004/05/28/howto-atom-id"
msgstr ""
"Féach https://web.archive.org/web/20110514113830/http://diveintomark.org/"
"archives/2004/05/28/howto-atom-id"

msgid "``Stylesheet``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Represents an RSS stylesheet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Required argument. The URL where the stylesheet is located."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An optional string containing the MIME type of the stylesheet. If not "
"specified, Django will attempt to guess it by using "
"Python's :py:func:`mimetypes.guess_type()`. Use ``mimetype=None`` if you "
"don't want your stylesheet to have a MIME type specified."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An optional string which will be used as the ``media`` attribute of the "
"stylesheet. Defaults to ``\"screen\"``. Use ``media=None`` if you don't want "
"your stylesheet to have a ``media`` attribute."
msgstr ""

msgid "``SyndicationFeed``"
msgstr "``SyndicationFeed``"

msgid ""
"Base class for all syndication feeds. Subclasses should provide ``write()``."
msgstr ""
"Aicme bonn do gach fotha sindiciúcháin. Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh fo-aicmí "
"`scríobh () ``a sholáthar."

msgid ""
"Initialize the feed with the given dictionary of metadata, which applies to "
"the entire feed."
msgstr ""
"Cuir tús leis an bhfoclóir meiteashonraí a thugtar, a bhaineann leis an "
"mbeatha iomlán."

msgid ""
"Any extra keyword arguments you pass to ``__init__`` will be stored in "
"``self.feed``."
msgstr ""
"Stórálfar aon argóintí eochairfhocal breise a chuireann tú chuig "
"``__init__`` i `self.feed``."

msgid ""
"``stylesheets`` should be a sequence of either strings "
"or :class:`Stylesheet` instances."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adds an item to the feed. All args are expected to be strings except "
"``pubdate`` and ``updateddate``, which are ``datetime.datetime`` objects, "
"and ``enclosures``, which is a list of ``Enclosure`` instances."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann mír leis an mbeatha. Táthar ag súil go mbeidh teaghráin iad gach "
"arg ach amháin ``pubdate`` agus ``updateddate``, ar rudaí "
"`datetime.datetime`` iad, agus ``enclosures``, ar liosta de chásanna "
"``Enclosure``."

msgid ""
"Return extra attributes to place on the root (i.e. feed/channel) element. "
"Called from ``write()``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair ar ais tréithe breise le cur ar an eilimint fréimhe (ie beath/"
"cainéal). Glaoigh ó ``write () ``."

msgid ""
"Add elements in the root (i.e. feed/channel) element. Called from "
"``write()``."
msgstr ""
"Cuir eilimintí san eilimint fréimhe (ie beath/cainéal). Glaoigh ó ``write () "
"``."

msgid "Add stylesheet information to the document. Called from ``write()``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Return extra attributes to place on each item (i.e. item/entry) element."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair ar ais tréithe breise le cur ar gach eilimint (ie ear/iontráil)."

msgid "Add elements on each item (i.e. item/entry) element."
msgstr "Cuir eilimintí ar gach eilimint (ie ear/iontráil)."

msgid ""
"Outputs the feed in the given encoding to ``outfile``, which is a file-like "
"object. Subclasses should override this."
msgstr ""
"Aisíonn sé an beatha san ionchódú a thugtar chuig ``outfile``, ar réad "
"cosúil le comhad é. Ba chóir go gcuirfeadh fo-aicmí é seo a chur"

msgid "Returns the feed in the given encoding as a string."
msgstr "Tugann an beatha ar ais san ionchódú a thugtar mar shreang."

msgid ""
"Returns the latest ``pubdate`` or ``updateddate`` for all items in the feed. "
"If no items have either of these attributes this returns the current UTC "
"date/time."
msgstr ""
"Filleann sé an ``pubdate`` nó ``updateddate`` is déanaí do gach earra sa "
"bhfotha. Mura bhfuil aon earraí ceachtar de na tréithe seo filleann sé seo "
"an dáta/am reatha UTC ar ais."

msgid "``Enclosure``"
msgstr "``Cumhd``"

msgid "Represents an RSS enclosure"
msgstr "Léiríonn sé imfhálú RSS"

