msgstr "``RSSFeed``"

msgid "``Rss201rev2Feed``"
msgstr "``RSS201REV2Feed``"

msgid "Spec: https://cyber.harvard.edu/rss/rss.html"
msgstr "Sonraíocht: https://cyber.harvard.edu/rss/rss.html"

msgid "``RssUserland091Feed``"
msgstr "``RSSuserland091Feed``"

msgid "Spec: http://backend.userland.com/rss091"
msgstr "Sonraíocht: http://backend.userland.com/rss091"

msgid "``Atom1Feed``"
msgstr "``Atom1Feed``"

msgid "Spec: :rfc:`4287`"
msgstr "Sonraíocht: :rfc: `4287`"

msgid "``django.utils.functional``"
msgstr "``django.utils.functional``"

msgid ""
"The ``@cached_property`` decorator caches the result of a method with a "
"single ``self`` argument as a property. The cached result will persist as "
"long as the instance does, so if the instance is passed around and the "
"function subsequently invoked, the cached result will be returned."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an maisitheoir ``@cached_property`` toradh modh le hargóint ``féin` "
"amháin mar mhaoin. Leanfaidh an toradh taisceáilte chomh fada agus a "
"dhéanann an cás, mar sin má chuirtear an cás timpeall agus má ghairmtear an "
"fheidhm ina dhiaidh sin, cuirfear an toradh taisceáilte ar ais."

msgid ""
"Consider a typical case, where a view might need to call a model's method to "
"perform some computation, before placing the model instance into the "
"context, where the template might invoke the method once more::"
msgstr ""
"Smaoinigh ar chás tipiciúil, ina bhféadfadh go mbeadh gá le dearcadh modh "
"samhail a ghlaoch chun ríomh éigin a dhéanamh, sula gcuirtear an t-áis "
"samhail isteach sa chomhthéacs, áit a bhféadfadh an teimpléad an modh a "
"ghairm arís:"

msgid "And in the template you would have:"
msgstr "Agus sa teimpléad bheadh agat:"

msgid ""
"Here, ``friends()`` will be called twice. Since the instance ``person`` in "
"the view and the template are the same, decorating the ``friends()`` method "
"with ``@cached_property`` can avoid that::"
msgstr ""
"Anseo, glaofar ar `cairde () ``faoi dhó. Ós rud é go bhfuil an cás "
"``pearsa`` sa radharc agus an teimpléad mar an gcéanna, is féidir an modh "
"``cairde () ``a mhaisiú le`` @cached_property ``a sheachaint:"

msgid ""
"Note that as the method is now a property, in Python code it will need to be "
"accessed appropriately::"
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara toisc gur maoin é an modh anois, i gcód Python caithfear "
"rochtain a fháil go cuí air::"

msgid ""
"The cached value can be treated like an ordinary attribute of the instance::"
msgstr "Is féidir an luach taisceáilte a chóireáil mar ghnáthtréith den chás:"

msgid ""
"Because of the way the :py:ref:`descriptor protocol <descriptor-invocation>` "
"works, using ``del`` (or ``delattr``) on a ``cached_property`` that hasn't "
"been accessed raises ``AttributeError``."
msgstr ""
"Mar gheall ar an mbealach a oibríonn an prótacal tuairiscí:py:ref: "
"`Descriptor`<descriptor-invocation>, ardaíonn ``del`` (nó `delattr``) ar "
"`cached_property`` nár rochtainíodh rochtain air ``AttributeError``."

msgid ""
"As well as offering potential performance advantages, ``@cached_property`` "
"can ensure that an attribute's value does not change unexpectedly over the "
"life of an instance. This could occur with a method whose computation is "
"based on ``datetime.now()``, or if a change were saved to the database by "
"some other process in the brief interval between subsequent invocations of a "
"method on the same instance."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le buntáistí feidhmíochta féideartha a thairiscint, is féidir le "
"``@cached_property`` a chinntiú nach n-athróidh luach tréithe gan choinne "
"thar shaol an cháis. D'fhéadfadh sé seo tarlú le modh a bhfuil a ríomh "
"bunaithe ar `datetime.now () ``, nó má shábháiltear athrú ar an mbunachar "
"sonraí trí phróiseas éigin eile san eatramh gairid idir inghairmithe modh "
"ina dhiaidh sin ar an gcás céanna."

msgid ""
"You can make cached properties of methods. For example, if you had an "
"expensive ``get_friends()`` method and wanted to allow calling it without "
"retrieving the cached value, you could write::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat airíonna taisceáilte modhanna a dhéanamh. Mar shampla, má bhí "
"modh daor ``get_friends () `agat agus má theastaigh uait é a ghlaoch gan an "
"luach taisceáilte a aisghabháil, d'fhéadfá scríobh:"

msgid ""
"While ``person.get_friends()`` will recompute the friends on each call, the "
"value of the cached property will persist until you delete it as described "
"above::"
msgstr ""
"Cé go ndéanfaidh ``person.get_friends () ``na cairde a athríomh ar gach "
"glao, leanfaidh luach na maoine a choscáil go dtí go scriosann tú í mar a "
"thuairiscítear thuas:"

msgid ""
"Similar to :py:func:`@classmethod <classmethod>`, the ``@classproperty`` "
"decorator converts the result of a method with a single ``cls`` argument "
"into a property that can be accessed directly from the class."
msgstr ""
"Cosúil le:py:func: `@classmethod`<classmethod>, athraíonn an maisitheoir "
"``@classproperty`` toradh modh le argóint ``cls`` amháin ina maoin ar féidir "
"rochtain a fháil go díreach ón rang."

msgid ""
"Django offers many utility functions (particularly in ``django.utils``) that "
"take a string as their first argument and do something to that string. These "
"functions are used by template filters as well as directly in other code."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann Django go leor feidhmeanna fóntais ar fáil (go háirithe i "
"``django.utils``) a ghlacann sreang mar an gcéad argóint agus a dhéanann rud "
"éigin leis an sreang sin. Úsáidtear na feidhmeanna seo ag scagairí teimpléid "
"chomh maith le go díreach i gcód eile."

msgid ""
"If you write your own similar functions and deal with translations, you'll "
"face the problem of what to do when the first argument is a lazy translation "
"object. You don't want to convert it to a string immediately, because you "
"might be using this function outside of a view (and hence the current "
"thread's locale setting will not be correct)."
msgstr ""
"Má scríobhann tú do chuid feidhmeanna comhchosúla féin agus má dhéileálann "
"tú le haistriúcháin, beidh fadhb agat cad atá le déanamh nuair is réad "
"aistriúcháin leisciúil é an chéad argóint. Níl tú ag iarraidh é a thiontú go "
"sreang láithreach, mar b'fhéidir go bhfuil an fheidhm seo á úsáid agat "
"lasmuigh de radharc (agus dá bhrí sin ní bheidh socrú áitiúil an snáithe "
"reatha ceart)."

msgid ""
"For cases like this, use the ``django.utils.functional.keep_lazy()`` "
"decorator. It modifies the function so that *if* it's called with a lazy "
"translation as one of its arguments, the function evaluation is delayed "
"until it needs to be converted to a string."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le cásanna mar seo, bain úsáid as an maisitheoir "
"``django.utils.functional.keep_lazy () ``. Athraíonn sé an fheidhm ionas "
"ionas gur* má thugtar air le haistriúchán leisciúil mar cheann dá argóintí, "
"cuirtear moill ar an meastóireacht feidhme go dtí go gcaithfear é a thiontú "
"go sreang."

msgid ""
"The ``keep_lazy()`` decorator takes a number of extra arguments (``*args``) "
"specifying the type(s) that the original function can return. A common use "
"case is to have functions that return text. For these, you can pass the "
"``str`` type to ``keep_lazy`` (or use the :func:`keep_lazy_text` decorator "
"described in the next section)."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an maisitheoir ``keep_lazy () ``roinnt argóintí breise (``*args``) a "
"shonraíonn an cineál/na cineálacha is féidir leis an bhfeidhm bhunaidh a "
"thabhairt ar ais. Cás úsáide coitianta is ea feidhmeanna a bheith agat a "
"thugann téacs ar ais. Chuige seo, is féidir leat an cineál ``str`` a chur "
"chuig `keep_lazy`` (nó bain úsáid as an maisitheoir: func: `keep_lazy_text` "
"a thuairiscítear sa chéad chuid eile)."

msgid ""
"Using this decorator means you can write your function and assume that the "
"input is a proper string, then add support for lazy translation objects at "
"the end."
msgstr ""
"Ciallaíonn an maisitheoir seo a úsáid gur féidir leat do fheidhm a scríobh "
"agus glacadh leis gur sreang ceart é an t-ionchur, ansin tacaíocht a chur le "
"haghaidh rudaí aistriúcháin leisciúil ag an deireadh."

msgid "A shortcut for ``keep_lazy(str)(func)``."
msgstr "Aicearra le haghaidh ``keep_lazy (str) (func) ``."

msgid ""
"If you have a function that returns text and you want to be able to take "
"lazy arguments while delaying their evaluation, you can use this decorator::"
msgstr ""
"Má tá feidhm agat a thugann téacs ar ais agus má theastaíonn uait a bheith "
"in ann argóintí leisciúla a ghlacadh agus tú ag moill ar a meastóireacht, is "
"féidir leat an maisitheoir seo a úsáid:"

msgid "``django.utils.html``"
msgstr "``django.utils.html``"

msgid ""
"Usually you should build up HTML using Django's templates to make use of its "
"autoescape mechanism, using the utilities in :mod:`django.utils.safestring` "
"where appropriate. This module provides some additional low level utilities "
"for escaping HTML."
msgstr ""
"De ghnáth ba chóir duit HTML a thógáil ag baint úsáide as teimpléid Django "
"chun a mheicníocht autoescape a úsáid, ag baint úsáide as na fóntais in:mod: "
"`django.utils.safestring` nuair is cuí. Soláthraíonn an modúl seo roinnt "
"fóntais leibhéal íseal breise chun HTML a éalú."

msgid ""
"Returns the given text with ampersands, quotes and angle brackets encoded "
"for use in HTML. The input is first coerced to a string and the output "
"has :func:`~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` applied."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé an téacs a thugtar ar ais le ampersandaí, luachana agus lúibíní "
"uillinne ionchódaithe le húsáid i HTML. Cuirtear iallach ar an ionchur ar "
"dtús chuig sreang agus tá: func: `~django.utils.safestring.mark_safe` curtha "
"i bhfeidhm ar an aschur."

msgid ""
"Similar to ``escape()``, except that it doesn't operate on preescaped "
"strings, so it will not double escape."
msgstr ""
