"Mar an gcéanna leis na leaganacha neamh-leisciúla thuas, ach ag baint úsáide "
"as forghní"

msgid "See :ref:`lazy translations documentation <lazy-translations>`."
msgstr "<lazy-translations>Féach:ref: `doiciméadú aistriúcháin leisciúil `."

msgid ""
"Marks strings for translation but doesn't translate them now. This can be "
"used to store strings in global variables that should stay in the base "
"language (because they might be used externally) and will be translated "
"later."
msgstr ""
"Marcálann sé teaghráin le haghaidh aistriúcháin ach ní aistríonn sé iad "
"anois. Is féidir é seo a úsáid chun teaghráin a stóráil in athróga domhanda "
"ar chóir dóibh fanacht sa bhuntheanga (toisc go bhféadfaí iad a úsáid go "
"seachtrach) agus aistrítear iad níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"Translates ``singular`` and ``plural`` and returns the appropriate string "
"based on ``number``."
msgstr ""
"Aistríonn ``singular`` agus `plural`` agus filleann sé an teaghrán cuí "
"bunaithe ar ``uimhre``."

msgid ""
"Translates ``singular`` and ``plural`` and returns the appropriate string "
"based on ``number`` and the ``context``."
msgstr ""
"Aistríonn ``singular`` agus `plural`` agus filleann sé an teaghrán cuí "
"bunaithe ar ``uimhre`` agus an `context``."

msgid ""
"Fetches the translation object for a given language and activates it as the "
"current translation object for the current thread."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann sé an réad aistriúcháin do theanga ar leith agus gníomhaíonn sé é "
"mar réad aistriúcháin reatha don snáithe reatha."

msgid ""
"Deactivates the currently active translation object so that further _ calls "
"will resolve against the default translation object, again."
msgstr ""
"Díghníomhachtaíonn sé an réad aistriúcháin atá gníomhach faoi láthair ionas "
"go réiteoidh glaonna breise i gcoinne an réad aistriúcháin"

msgid ""
"Makes the active translation object a ``NullTranslations()`` instance. This "
"is useful when we want delayed translations to appear as the original string "
"for some reason."
msgstr ""
"Déanann sé an réad aistriúcháin ghníomhach mar shampla ``NullTranslations () "
"``. Tá sé seo úsáideach nuair is mian linn go mbeadh aistriúcháin moillithe "
"le feiceáil mar an teaghrán bunaidh ar chúis"

msgid ""
"A Python context manager that uses :func:`django.utils.translation.activate` "
"to fetch the translation object for a given language, activates it as the "
"translation object for the current thread and reactivates the previous "
"active language on exit. Optionally, it can deactivate the temporary "
"translation on exit with :func:`django.utils.translation.deactivate` if the "
"``deactivate`` argument is ``True``. If you pass ``None`` as the language "
"argument, a ``NullTranslations()`` instance is activated within the context."
msgstr ""
"Gníomhaíonn bainisteoir comhthéacs Python a úsáide:func: "
"`django.utils.translation.activate` chun an réad aistriúcháin do theanga ar "
"leith a fháil, é a ghníomhachtú mar réad aistriúcháin don snáithe reatha "
"agus athghníomhachtaíonn sé an teanga ghníomhach roimhe seo ar imeacht. Go "
"roghnach, féadfaidh sé an t-aistriúchán sealadach a dhíghníomhachtú ar "
"imeacht le:func: `django.utils.translation.deactivate` má tá an argóint "
"``deactivate`` `True``. Má chuireann tú ``None`` mar argóint teanga, "
"cuirtear cás ``NullTranslations () ``i ngníomh laistigh den chomhthéacs."

msgid ""
"Checks whether there is a global language file for the given language code "
"(e.g. 'fr', 'pt_BR'). This is used to decide whether a user-provided "
"language is available."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann sé an bhfuil comhad teanga domhanda ann don chód teanga ar leith "
"(m.sh. 'fr', 'pt_br'). Úsáidtear é seo chun cinneadh a dhéanamh an bhfuil "
"teanga a sholáthraíonn an úsáideoir ar fáil."

msgid ""
"Returns the currently selected language code. Returns ``None`` if "
"translations are temporarily deactivated (by :func:`deactivate_all()` or "
"when ``None`` is passed to :func:`override()`)."
msgstr ""
"Tugann an cód teanga roghnaithe faoi láthair ar ais. Tugann ``None`` ar ais "
"má dhíghníomhachtar aistriúcháin go sealadach (trí:func: `deactivate_all () "
"`nó nuair a chuirtear ``None`` chuig :func: `override ()`)."

msgid "Returns selected language's BiDi layout:"
msgstr "Tugann leagan amach BiDi teanga roghnaithe:"

msgid "``False`` = left-to-right layout"
msgstr "``False`` = leagan amach ar chlé go deis"

msgid "``True`` = right-to-left layout"
msgstr "``True`` = leagan amach ar dheis go clé"

msgid ""
"Analyzes the request to find what language the user wants the system to "
"show. Only languages listed in settings.LANGUAGES are taken into account. If "
"the user requests a sublanguage where we have a main language, we send out "
"the main language."
msgstr ""
"Déanann anailís ar an iarratas chun a fháil amach cén teanga a theastaíonn "
"ón úsáideoir a thaispeáint. Ní chuirtear san áireamh ach teangacha atá "
"liostaithe i socruithe. Má iarrann an t-úsáideoir fotheanga ina bhfuil "
"príomhtheanga againn, seolfaimid an phríomhtheanga amach."

msgid ""
"If ``check_path`` is ``True``, the function first checks the requested URL "
"for whether its path begins with a language code listed in "
"the :setting:`LANGUAGES` setting."
msgstr ""
"Más é ``check_path`` ``True``, seiceálann an fheidhm an URL iarrtha ar dtús "
"cibé an dtosaíonn a chosán le cód teanga atá liostaithe sa socrú:setting: "
"`LANGUAGES`."

msgid ""
"Returns ``lang_code`` if it's in the :setting:`LANGUAGES` setting, possibly "
"selecting a more generic variant. For example, ``'es'`` is returned if "
"``lang_code`` is ``'es-ar'`` and ``'es'`` is in :setting:`LANGUAGES` but "
"``'es-ar'`` isn't."
msgstr ""
"Tugann sé 'lang_code`` ar ais má tá sé sa socrú: setting: `LANGUAGES`, "
"b'fhéidir leagan níos cineálacha a roghnú. Mar shampla, cuirtear ``es'`` ar "
"ais má tá ``lang_code`` ``es-ar'`` agus ```es'`` in:setting: `LANGUAGES` ach "
"níl ``es-ar'``."

msgid ""
"``lang_code`` has a maximum accepted length of 500 characters. "
"A :exc:`LookupError` is raised if ``lang_code`` exceeds this limit and "
"``strict`` is ``True``, or if there is no generic variant and ``strict`` is "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
"Tá an fad uasta glactha le 500 carachtar ag ``lang_code``. A: Exc: Ardaítear "
"`LookuPerror` má sháraíonn ``lang_code`` an teorainn seo agus má tá ``docht "
"``True``, nó mura bhfuil aon leagan cineálach ann agus má tá ``docht`` "
"`False``."

msgid ""
"If ``strict`` is ``False`` (the default), a country-specific variant may be "
"returned when neither the language code nor its generic variant is found. "
"For example, if only ``'es-co'`` is in :setting:`LANGUAGES`, that's returned "
"for ``lang_code``\\s like ``'es'`` and ``'es-ar'``. Those matches aren't "
"returned if ``strict=True``."
msgstr ""
"Más é ``docht ``False`` (an réamhshocrú), féadfar leagan tír-shonrach a "
"thabhairt ar ais nuair nach bhfaightear an cód teanga ná a leagan cineálach. "
"Mar shampla, mura bhfuil ach ``es-co'`` in:setting: `LANGUAGES`, cuirtear é "
"sin ar ais do ``lang_code``\\ s cosúil le ``'es'`` agus ``es-ar'``. Ní "
"chuirtear na cluichí sin ar ais má tá ``strict=True``."

msgid "Raises :exc:`LookupError` if nothing is found."
msgstr "Ardaithe:exc: `LookuPerror` mura bhfaightear aon rud."

msgid ""
"In older versions, ``lang_code`` values over 500 characters were processed "
"without raising a :exc:`LookupError`."
msgstr ""
"I leaganacha níos sine, próiseáilíodh luachanna ``lang_code`` os cionn 500 "
"carachtar gan a:exc: `LookuPerror` a ardú."

msgid "Turns a language name (en-us) into a locale name (en_US)."
msgstr "Tionann ainm teanga (en-us) ina ainm áitiúil (en_US)."

msgid ""
"Turns a Django template into something that is understood by ``xgettext``. "
"It does so by translating the Django translation tags into standard "
"``gettext`` function invocations."
msgstr ""
"Tionann teimpléad Django ina rud a thuigeann ``xgettext``. Déanann sé "
"amhlaidh trí na clibeanna aistriúcháin Django a aistriú go gcaighdeánacha "
"feidhme ``gettext``."

msgid "Writing validators"
msgstr "Bailíthe scríbhneoireachta"

msgid ""
"A validator is a callable that takes a value and raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if it doesn't meet some "
"criteria. Validators can be useful for reusing validation logic between "
"different types of fields."
msgstr ""
"Is bailíochtaire é bailíochtaire a ghlacann luach agus a ardaíonn a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` mura gcomhlíonann sé roinnt "
"critéir. Is féidir le bailíochtóirí a bheith úsáideach chun loighic "
"bailíochtaithe a athúsáid idir cineálacha éagsúla réimsí"

msgid "For example, here's a validator that only allows even numbers::"
msgstr "Mar shampla, seo bailíochtóir nach gceadaíonn ach fionuimhreacha:"

msgid ""
"You can add this to a model field via the "
"field's :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.validators` argument::"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat é seo a chur le réimse samhail tríd an argóint réimse "
"d's:attr: `~Django.db.Models.Field.Validators`:"

msgid ""
"Because values are converted to Python before validators are run, you can "
"even use the same validator with forms::"
msgstr ""
"Toisc go ndéantar luachanna a thiontú go Python sula ndéantar bailíochtóirí "
"a reáchtáil, is féidir leat an bailíochtóir céanna a úsáid fiú le foirmeacha:"

msgid ""
"You can also use a class with a ``__call__()`` method for more complex or "
"configurable validators. :class:`RegexValidator`, for example, uses this "
"technique. If a class-based validator is used in "
"the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.validators` model field option, you "
"should make sure it is :ref:`serializable by the migration framework "
"<migration-serializing>` by adding :ref:`deconstruct() <custom-deconstruct-"
"method>` and ``__eq__()`` methods."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat rang a úsáid freisin le modh ``__call__ () ``le haghaidh "
"bailíochtóirí níos casta nó níos cumraithe. :class: `RegExvalidator`, "
"úsáideann an teicníc seo mar shampla. <migration-serializing><custom-"
"deconstruct-method>Má úsáidtear bailíochtóir rang-bhunaithe sa rogha réimse "
"samhail: attr: `~django.db.Models.Field.Validators`, ba cheart duit a "
"chinntiú go bhfuil sé: ref: `inseriálaithe ag an gcreat imirce `trí:ref: "
"`deconstruct ()` agus ``__eq__ () `modhanna a chur leis."

msgid "How validators are run"
msgstr "Conas a reáchtáiltear bailíochtóirí"

msgid ""
"See the :doc:`form validation </ref/forms/validation>` for more information "
"on how validators are run in forms, and :ref:`Validating objects <validating-"
"objects>` for how they're run in models. Note that validators will not be "
"run automatically when you save a model, but if you are using "
"a :class:`~django.forms.ModelForm`, it will run your validators on any "
"fields that are included in your form. See the :doc:`ModelForm documentation "
"</topics/forms/modelforms>` for information on how model validation "
"interacts with forms."
msgstr ""
"</ref/forms/validation> <validating-objects>Féach an:doc: `bailíochtú "
"foirme` le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoin gcaoi a reáchtáiltear "
"bailíochtóirí i bhfoirmeacha, agus:ref: `Rudaí bailíochtaithe `maidir le "
"conas a reáchtáiltear iad i samhlacha. Tabhair faoi deara nach reáchtálfar "
"bailíochtóirí go huathoibríoch nuair a shábhálann tú samhail, ach má tá a: "
"class: `~django.forms.modelForm` á úsáid agat, reáchtálfaidh sé do "
"bhailíochtóirí ar aon réimsí atá san áireamh i d'fhoirm. Féach na:doc: "
"`Doiciméadú Modelfhoirme` le haghaidh faisnéise maidir le conas a "
"idirghníom</topics/forms/modelforms> haíonn bailíochtú samhail le foirmeacha."

msgid "Built-in validators"
msgstr "Bailíochtóirí tógtha"

msgid ""
"The :mod:`django.core.validators` module contains a collection of callable "
"validators for use with model and form fields. They're used internally but "
"are available for use with your own fields, too. They can be used in "
"addition to, or in lieu of custom ``field.clean()`` methods."
msgstr ""
"Tá bailiúchán bailíochtóirí inghlaonta sa mhodúl:MOD: "
"`django.core.validators `le húsáid le réimsí samhail agus foirm. Úsáidtear "
"iad go hinmheánach ach tá siad ar fáil le húsáid le do réimsí féin freisin. "
"Is féidir iad a úsáid i dteannta modhanna saincheaptha ``field.clean () `nó "
"in ionad modhanna saincheaptha."

msgid "``RegexValidator``"
msgstr "``RegExvalidator``"

msgid ""
"If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`regex`. Can be a regular expression string "
"or a pre-compiled regular expression."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ``None``, cuirfidh sé airí:attr: `regex`. Is féidir a bheith ina "
"shreang abairt rialta nó ina léiriú rialta réamhthiomsaithe."

msgid "If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`.message`."
msgstr "Mura bhfuil ``None``, cuireann sé airí:attr: `.message`."

msgid "If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`code`."
msgstr "Mura bhfuil ``None``, cuireann sé airí:attr: `cód`."

msgid "If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`inverse_match`."
msgstr "Mura bhfuil ``None``, fhilleadh:attr: `inverse_match`."

msgid ""
"If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`flags`. In that case, :attr:`regex` must "
"be a regular expression string, or :exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil ``None``, cuireann sé airí:attr: `bratacha `. Sa chás sin, "
"caithfidh :attr: `regex` a bheith ina teaghrán abairt rialta, nó:exc: "
"`TypeError` a ardaítear."

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` searches the provided ``value`` for a given "
"regular expression with :func:`re.search`. By default, raises "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with :attr:`message` "
"and :attr:`code` if a match **is not** found. Its behavior can be inverted "
"by setting :attr:`inverse_match` to ``True``, in which case "
"the :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` is raised when a match "
"**is** found."
msgstr ""
"A: Aicme: Cuardach `RegExvalidator` ar an `luach`` a chuirtear ar fáil le "
"haghaidh abairt rialta ar le:func: `re.search`. De réir réamhshocraithe, "
"ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le:attr: "
"`teachtaire` agus:attr: `code` mura bhfaightear meaitseach****. Is féidir a "
"iompar a inbhéartú trí shocrú: attr: `inverse_match` go ``True``, sa chás "
"sin ardaítear an:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` nuair a "
"aimsítear cluiche ****."

msgid ""
"The regular expression pattern to search for within the provided ``value``, "
"using :func:`re.search`. This may be a string or a pre-compiled regular "
"expression created with :func:`re.compile`. Defaults to the empty string, "
"which will be found in every possible ``value``."
msgstr ""
"An patrún abairt rialta le cuardach a dhéanamh laistigh den `luach`` a "
"chuirtear ar fáil, ag baint úsáid:func: `re.search`. D'fhéadfadh sé seo a "
"bheith ina shreang nó ina abairt rialta réamhthiomsaithe a cruthaíodh "
"le:func: `re.compile`. Réamhshocraithe don teaghrán folamh, a bheidh le fáil "
"i ngach ``luach`` féideartha."

msgid ""
"The error message used by :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"validation fails. Defaults to ``\"Enter a valid value\"``."
msgstr ""
"An teachtaireacht earráide a úsáideann ar:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar bhailíochtú. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``\"Cuir isteach luach bailí\"``."

msgid ""
"The error code used by :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"validation fails. Defaults to ``\"invalid\"``."
msgstr ""
"An cód earráide a úsáideann ar:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar bhailíochtú. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``\"neamhbhailí\"``."

msgid "The match mode for :attr:`regex`. Defaults to ``False``."
msgstr ""
"An modh meaitseála le haghaidh: attr: `regex`. Réamhshocraithe go ``False``."

msgid ""
"The :ref:`regex flags <python:contents-of-module-re>` used when compiling "
"the regular expression string :attr:`regex`. If :attr:`regex` is a pre-"
"compiled regular expression, and :attr:`flags` is "
"overridden, :exc:`TypeError` is raised. Defaults to ``0``."
msgstr ""
"An bhrataí: ref: `regex `a úsáidtear agus an teaghrán abairt ri "
"<python:contents-of-module-re>alta á thiomsú: attr: `regex`. Má tá: attr: "
"abairt rialta réamh-thiomsaithe é `regex`, agus:attr: `flags` a shárú, :exc: "
"`TypeError` ardaítear. Réamhshocraithe go ``0``."

msgid "``EmailValidator``"
msgstr "``Bailíochtaitheoir ríomhphost``"

msgid "If not ``None``, overrides :attr:`allowlist`."
msgstr "Mura bhfuil ``None``, cuirfidh sé airí:attr: `liosta`."

msgid ""
"An :class:`EmailValidator` ensures that a value looks like an email, and "
"raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with :attr:`message` "
"and :attr:`code` if it doesn't. Values longer than 320 characters are always "
"considered invalid."
msgstr ""
"Cinntíonn an:class: `EmailValidator` go bhfuil cuma luach cosúil le "
"ríomhphost, agus ardaíonn sé a:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le:attr: `teachtaire` agus:attr: "
"`code` mura ndéanann sé. Meastar go bhfuil luachanna níos faide ná 320 "
"carachtar neamhbhailí i gcó"

msgid ""
"The error message used by :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"validation fails. Defaults to ``\"Enter a valid email address\"``."
msgstr ""
"An teachtaireacht earráide a úsáideann ar:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar bhailíochtú. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``\"Cuir isteach seoladh ríomhphoist bailí\"``."

msgid ""
"Allowlist of email domains. By default, a regular expression (the "
"``domain_regex`` attribute) is used to validate whatever appears after the "
"``@`` sign. However, if that string appears in the ``allowlist``, this "
"validation is bypassed. If not provided, the default ``allowlist`` is "
"``['localhost']``. Other domains that don't contain a dot won't pass "
"validation, so you'd need to add them to the ``allowlist`` as necessary."
msgstr ""
"Liosta de na bhfearann ríomhphoist. De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáidtear "
"abairt rialta (an tréith ``domain_regex``) chun gach rud atá le feiceáil tar "
"éis an chomhartha ``@`` a bhailíochtú. Mar sin féin, má tá an sreang sin le "
"feiceáil sa ``liosta ceada``, seachtar an bailíochtú seo. Mura gcuirtear ar "
"fáil, is é “['localhost'] ``an réamhshocraithe ``liosta``. Ní rachaidh "
"fearainn eile nach bhfuil ponc iontu bailíochtú, mar sin bheadh ort iad a "
"chur leis an `liosta ceada`` de réir mar is gá."

msgid "``DomainNameValidator``"
msgstr "``DomainmValidator``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` subclass that ensures a value looks like a domain "
"name. Values longer than 255 characters are always considered invalid. IP "
"addresses are not accepted as valid domain names."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: fo-aicme `RegexValidator` a chinntíonn go bhfuil cuma luach cosúil "
"le ainm fearainn. Meastar go bhfuil luachanna níos faide ná 255 carachtar "
"neamhbhailí i gcó Ní ghlactar le seoltaí IP mar ainmneacha fearainn bailí."

msgid ""
"In addition to the optional arguments of its parent :class:`RegexValidator` "
"class, ``DomainNameValidator`` accepts an extra optional attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le hargóintí roghnacha a thuismitheoir:class: rang "
"`RegExvalidator`, glacann ``DomainNameValidator`` le tréith roghnach breise:"

msgid ""
"Determines whether to accept internationalized domain names, that is, domain "
"names that contain non-ASCII characters. Defaults to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Cinneann sé an nglactar le hainmneacha fearainn idirnáisiúnta, is é sin, "
"ainmneacha fearainn ina bhfuil carachtair neamh-ASCII. Réamhshocraithe go "
"``True``."

msgid "``URLValidator``"
msgstr "``UrlValidator``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` subclass that ensures a value looks like a URL, "
"and raises an error code of ``'invalid'`` if it doesn't. Values longer "
"than :attr:`max_length` characters are always considered invalid."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: fo-aicme `RegexValidator` a chinntíonn go bhfuil cuma URL ar "
"luach, agus a ardaíonn cód earráide ``'invalid'`` mura ndéanann sé. Meastar "
"go bhfuil luachanna níos faide ná: attr: `max_length `carachtair neamhbhailí "
"i gcónaí."

msgid ""
"Loopback addresses and reserved IP spaces are considered valid. Literal IPv6 "
"addresses (:rfc:`3986#section-3.2.2`) and Unicode domains are both supported."
msgstr ""
"Meastar go bhfuil seoltaí loopback agus spásanna IP curtha in áirithe bailí. "
"Tacaítear le seoltaí litriúla IPv6 (:rfc: `3986 #section -3.2.2`) agus "
"fearainn Unicode araon."

msgid ""
"In addition to the optional arguments of its parent :class:`RegexValidator` "
"class, ``URLValidator`` accepts an extra optional attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith le hargóintí roghnacha a thuismitheoir:class: rang "
"`RegExvalidator`, glacann ``URLValidator`` le tréith roghnach breise:"

msgid ""
"URL/URI scheme list to validate against. If not provided, the default list "
"is ``['http', 'https', 'ftp', 'ftps']``. As a reference, the IANA website "
"provides a full list of `valid URI schemes`_."
msgstr ""
"Liosta scéime URL/URI le bailíochtú ina choinne. Mura gcuirtear ar fáil, is "
"é an liosta réamhshocraithe ``['http', 'https', 'ftp', 'ftps']``. Mar "
"thagairt, soláthraíonn láithreán gréasáin IANA liosta iomlán de `scéimeanna "
"bailí URI `_."

msgid ""
"Values starting with ``file:///`` will not pass validation even when the "
"``file`` scheme is provided. Valid values must contain a host."
msgstr ""
"Ní rachaidh luachanna a thosaíonn le `file: ///`` bailíochtú fiú nuair a "
"chuirtear an scéim `comhad ``ar fáil. Caithfidh óstach a bheith i luachanna "
"bailí."

msgid ""
"The maximum length of values that could be considered valid. Defaults to "
"2048 characters."
msgstr ""
"An fad uasta na luachanna a d'fhéadfaí a mheas bailí. Réamhshocraithe go "
"2048 carachtar."

msgid "``validate_email``"
msgstr "``ríomhphost_bailíochta``"

msgid "An :class:`EmailValidator` instance without any customizations."
msgstr "An:class: `EmailValidator` sampla gan aon saincheaptha."

msgid "``validate_domain_name``"
msgstr "``ainm_fearainn bailaite``"

msgid "A :class:`DomainNameValidator` instance without any customizations."
msgstr "A: Class: `DomainNameValidator` sampla gan aon saincheaptha."

msgid "``validate_slug``"
msgstr "``bailate_slug``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` instance that ensures a value consists of only "
"letters, numbers, underscores or hyphens."
msgstr ""
"A: Aicme: Sampla `RegExValidator` a chinntíonn go bhfuil luach nach bhfuil "
"ach litreacha, uimhreacha, béim nó braithíní."

msgid "``validate_unicode_slug``"
msgstr "``bailate_unicode_slug``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` instance that ensures a value consists of only "
"Unicode letters, numbers, underscores, or hyphens."
msgstr ""
"A: Aicme: Sampla `RegExvalidator` a chinntíonn go bhfuil luach nach bhfuil "
"ach litreacha, uimhreacha, béim nó braithíní Unicode."

msgid "``validate_ipv4_address``"
msgstr "``bailate_ipv4_address ``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` instance that ensures a value looks like an IPv4 "
"address."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: Sampla `RegExValidator` a chinntíonn go bhfuil cuma luach cosúil "
"le seoladh IPv4."

msgid "``validate_ipv6_address``"
msgstr "``bailate_ipv6_address ``"

msgid "Uses ``django.utils.ipv6`` to check the validity of an IPv6 address."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé ``django.utils.ipv6`` chun bailíocht seoladh IPv6 a sheiceáil."

msgid "``validate_ipv46_address``"
msgstr "``bailate_ipv46_address ``"

msgid ""
"Uses both ``validate_ipv4_address`` and ``validate_ipv6_address`` to ensure "
"a value is either a valid IPv4 or IPv6 address."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann sé ``validate_ipv4_address ``agus ``validate_ipv6_address`` araon "
"chun a chinntiú gur seoladh bailí IPv4 nó IPv6 é luach."

msgid "``validate_comma_separated_integer_list``"
msgstr "``liosta_coma_iomlán bailíochtaí_scartha``"

msgid ""
"A :class:`RegexValidator` instance that ensures a value is a comma-separated "
"list of integers."
msgstr ""
"A: aicme: “RegExValidator” a chinntíonn go bhfuil luach ná liosta de "
"shláimhreacha scartha le camóg."

msgid "``int_list_validator``"
msgstr "``int_liost_bailíochtar``"

msgid ""
"Returns a :class:`RegexValidator` instance that ensures a string consists of "
"integers separated by ``sep``. It allows negative integers when "
"``allow_negative`` is ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Tuairisceáin a:class: `RegExValidator` sampla a chinntíonn go bhfuil sreang "
"comhdhéanta de shlánuimhreacha atá scartha le ``sep``. Ceadaíonn sé "
"sláimhreacha diúltacha nuair a bhíonn `allow_negative`` ``True``."

msgid "``MaxValueValidator``"
msgstr "``MaxValueValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'max_value'`` if ``value`` is greater than ``limit_value``, which may be a "
"callable."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```'max_value'` má tá ``lua`` níos mó ná ``limit_value``, a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith inghlaonta."

msgid "``MinValueValidator``"
msgstr "``Minvaluevalidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'min_value'`` if ``value`` is less than ``limit_value``, which may be a "
"callable."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```min_value'` má tá ``lua`` níos lú ná ``limit_value``, a d'fhéadfadh a "
"bheith inghlaonta."

msgid "``MaxLengthValidator``"
msgstr "``MaxLengthValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'max_length'`` if the length of ``value`` is greater than ``limit_value``, "
"which may be a callable."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```'max_long'`` má tá fad ``value`` níos mó ná ``limit_value``, a "
"d'fhéadfadh a bheith inghlaonta."

msgid "``MinLengthValidator``"
msgstr "``MinLengthValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'min_length'`` if the length of ``value`` is less than ``limit_value``, "
"which may be a callable."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```min_long`` má tá fad ``value`` níos lú ná ``limit_value``, a d'fhéadfadh "
"a bheith inghlaonta."

msgid "``DecimalValidator``"
msgstr "``DeimalValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with the following "
"codes:"
msgstr ""
"Ardaithe:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` leis na cóid seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid "``'max_digits'`` if the number of digits is larger than ``max_digits``."
msgstr "```'max_digits'`` má tá líon na ndigit níos mó ná ``max_digits``."

msgid ""
"``'max_decimal_places'`` if the number of decimals is larger than "
"``decimal_places``."
msgstr ""
"````max_decimal_places'`` má tá líon na ndeachmhálacha níos mó ná "
"``deach_places``."

msgid ""
"``'max_whole_digits'`` if the number of whole digits is larger than the "
"difference between ``max_digits`` and ``decimal_places``."
msgstr ""
"```'max_whole_digits'`` má tá líon na ndigit iomlána níos mó ná an difríocht "
"idir ``max_digits`` agus ``deach_places``."

msgid "``FileExtensionValidator``"
msgstr "``FileExtensionValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'invalid_extension'`` if the extension of ``value.name`` (``value`` is "
"a :class:`~django.core.files.File`) isn't found in ``allowed_extensions``. "
"The extension is compared case-insensitively with ``allowed_extensions``."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```invalid_extension'`` mura bhfaightear síneadh ``value.name`` (``value`` "
"a:class: `~django.core.files.file`) i `allowed_extensions``. Déantar an "
"síneadh a chur i gcomparáid go cás-neamhíogair le ``allowed_extensions``."

msgid ""
"Don't rely on validation of the file extension to determine a file's type. "
"Files can be renamed to have any extension no matter what data they contain."
msgstr ""
"Ná bí ag brath ar bhailíochtú an síneadh comhaid chun cineál comhaid a "
"chinneadh. Is féidir comhaid a athainmniú chun aon síneadh a bheith acu is "
"cuma cad iad na sonraí atá iontu."

msgid "``validate_image_file_extension``"
msgstr "``validate_image_file_extension``"

msgid ""
"Uses Pillow to ensure that ``value.name`` (``value`` is "
"a :class:`~django.core.files.File`) has `a valid image extension <https://"
"pillow.readthedocs.io/en/latest/handbook/image-file-formats.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"< https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/latest/handbook/image-file-"
"formats.html>Úsáideann sé Pillow chun a chinntiú go bhfuil síneadh bailí "
"íomhá ag ``value.name`` (``value``: a:class: `~django.core.files.file`)."

msgid "``ProhibitNullCharactersValidator``"
msgstr "``ProhibitNullCharactersValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if ``str(value)`` "
"contains one or more null characters (``'\\x00'``)."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má tá carachtar "
"null amháin nó níos mó sa ``str (value) ``(`'\\ x00'``)."

msgid ""
"The error message used by :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"validation fails. Defaults to ``\"Null characters are not allowed.\"``."
msgstr ""
"An teachtaireacht earráide a úsáideann ar:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar bhailíochtú. Ní "
"cheadaítear réamhshocraithe go ``\"carachtair neall.” ``."

msgid ""
"The error code used by :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` if "
"validation fails. Defaults to ``\"null_characters_not_allowed\"``."
msgstr ""
"An cód earráide a úsáideann ar:exc: "
"`~django.core.exceptions.validationError` má theipeann ar bhailíochtú. "
"Réamhshocraithe go ``\"null_caràcters_not_allowed\"``."

msgid "``StepValueValidator``"
msgstr "``StepValueValidator``"

msgid ""
"Raises a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.ValidationError` with a code of "
"``'step_size'`` if ``value`` is not an integral multiple of ``limit_value``, "
"which can be a float, integer or decimal value or a callable. When "
"``offset`` is set, the validation occurs against ``limit_value`` plus "
"``offset``. For example, for ``StepValueValidator(3, offset=1.4)`` valid "
"values include ``1.4``, ``4.4``, ``7.4``, ``10.4``, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Ardaíonn a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.validationError` le cód "
"```step_size'` mura bhfuil `value`` iolrach dhílis de `limit_value``, is "
"féidir a bheith ina luach snámhphointe, sláimhir nó deachúil nó inghlaoch. "
"Nuair a shocraítear ``offset``, tarlaíonn an bailíochtú i gcoinne "
"``limit_value`` móide ``offset``. Mar shampla, i gcás ``StepValueValidator "
"(3, offset = 1.4) ``tá luachanna bailí ```1.4``, `4.4``, `7.4``, `10.4``, "
"agus mar sin de."

msgid "Built-in Views"
msgstr "Radhairc Tógtha"

msgid ""
"Several of Django's built-in views are documented in :doc:`/topics/http/"
"views` as well as elsewhere in the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Déantar roinnt de na tuairimí ionsuite Django a dhoiciméadú in:doc: `/topics/"
"http/views` chomh maith le háiteanna eile sa doiciméadú."

msgid "Serving files in development"
msgstr "Freastal ar chomhaid atá i bhfor"

msgid ""
"There may be files other than your project's static assets that, for "
"convenience, you'd like to have Django serve for you in local development. "
"The :func:`~django.views.static.serve` view can be used to serve any "
"directory you give it. (This view is **not** hardened for production use and "
"should be used only as a development aid; you should serve these files in "
"production using a real front-end web server)."
msgstr ""
"D'fhéadfadh go mbeadh comhaid seachas sócmhainní statacha do thionscadail ar "
"mhaith leat, ar mhaithe le háisiúlacht, go bhfreastal Django duit i "
"bhforbairt áitiúil. Is féidir an dearcadh: Func: "
"`~django.views.static.serve` a úsáid chun freastal ar aon eolaire a thugann "
"tú dó. (Níl an dearcadh seo ** cruaite le húsáid táirgeachta agus níor "
"cheart é a úsáid ach mar chúnamh forbartha; ba cheart duit na comhaid seo a "
"sheirbheáil i dtáirgeadh ag baint úsáide as fíor-fhreastalaí gréasáin "
"tosaigh)."

msgid ""
"The most likely example is user-uploaded content in :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT`. "
"``django.contrib.staticfiles`` is intended for static assets and has no "
"built-in handling for user-uploaded files, but you can have Django serve "
"your :setting:`MEDIA_ROOT` by appending something like this to your URLconf::"
msgstr ""
"Is é an sampla is dóichí ná ábhar uaslódáilte ón úsáideoir in:setting: "
"`MEDIA_ROOT`. Tá ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` beartaithe le haghaidh "
"sócmhainní statacha agus níl aon láimhseáil ionsuite aige do chomhaid "
"uaslódáilte úsáideora, ach is féidir leat Django freastal ar do thú:setting: "
"`MEDIA_ROOT` trí rud éigin mar seo a chur le do URLConf::"

msgid ""
"Note, the snippet assumes your :setting:`MEDIA_URL` has a value of "
"``'media/'``. This will call the :func:`~django.views.static.serve` view, "
"passing in the path from the URLconf and the (required) ``document_root`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara, glacann an snippet le do: setting: tá luach ``'media/'`` "
"ag `MEDIA_URL`. Glaofar sé seo ar an amharc: :func: "
"`~django.views.static.serve`, ag dul sa chosán ón URLConf agus an "
"paraiméadar (riachtanach) ``document_root``."

msgid ""
"Since it can become a bit cumbersome to define this URL pattern, Django "
"ships with a small URL helper "
"function :func:`~django.conf.urls.static.static` that takes as parameters "
"the prefix such as :setting:`MEDIA_URL` and a dotted path to a view, such as "
"``'django.views.static.serve'``. Any other function parameter will be "
"transparently passed to the view."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go bhféadfadh sé a bheith beagán deacair an patrún URL seo a "
"shainiú, seolann Django le feidhm chúntóra beag URL: func: "
"`~django.conf.urls.static.static` a ghlacann mar pharaiméadair an réimír "
"amhail: setting: `MEDIA_URL` agus cosán ponctha chuig radharc, mar shampla "
"``django.views.static.serve'`. Cuirfear aon pharaiméadar feidhme eile ar "
"aghaidh go trédhearcach chuig an radharc."

msgid "Error views"
msgstr "Tuairimí earráide"

msgid ""
"Django comes with a few views by default for handling HTTP errors. To "
"override these with your own custom views, see :ref:`customizing-error-"
"views`."
msgstr ""
"Tagann Django le cúpla tuairim de réir réamhshocraithe chun earráidí HTTP a "
"láimhseáil. Chun iad seo a shárú le do thuairimí saincheaptha féin, "
"féach:ref: `customizing-error-views`."

msgid "The 404 (page not found) view"
msgstr "An radharc 404 (ní aimsíodh an leathanach)"

msgid ""
"When you raise :exc:`~django.http.Http404` from within a view, Django loads "
"a special view devoted to handling 404 errors. By default, it's the "
"view :func:`django.views.defaults.page_not_found`, which either produces a "
"\"Not Found\" message or loads and renders the template ``404.html`` if you "
"created it in your root template directory."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a ardaíonn tú: exc: `~django.http.http404` ó laistigh de radharc, "
"luchtaíonn Django dearcadh speisialta atá dírithe ar earráidí 404 a "
"láimhseáil. De réir réamhshocraithe, is é an view:func: "
"`django.views.defaults.page_not_found`, a tháirgeann teachtaireacht “Not "
"Found” nó a luchtaíonn agus a léiríonn an teimpléad ``404.html`` má "
"chruthaigh tú é i do eolaire teimpléad fréimhe."

msgid ""
"The default 404 view will pass two variables to the template: "
"``request_path``, which is the URL that resulted in the error, and "
"``exception``, which is a useful representation of the exception that "
"triggered the view (e.g. containing any message passed to a specific "
"``Http404`` instance)."
msgstr ""
"Cuirfidh an dearcadh réamhshocraithe 404 dhá athróg chuig an teimpléad: "
"`request_path``, arb é an URL a raibh an earráid mar thoradh air, agus "
"``exception``, ar léiriú úsáideach é ar an eisceacht a spreag an dearcadh "
"(m.sh. ina bhfuil aon teachtaireacht a chuirtear chuig `Http404` ar leith)."

msgid "Three things to note about 404 views:"
msgstr "Trí rud le tabhairt faoi deara faoi 404 tuairimí:"

msgid ""
"The 404 view is also called if Django doesn't find a match after checking "
"every regular expression in the URLconf."
msgstr ""
"Tugtar ar an radharc 404 freisin mura bhfaigheann Django meaitseáil tar éis "
"gach abairt rialta sa URLConf a sheiceáil."

msgid ""
"The 404 view is passed a :class:`~django.template.RequestContext` and will "
"have access to variables supplied by your template context processors (e.g. "
"``MEDIA_URL``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá an radharc 404 ag rith a:class: `~django.template.requestContext` agus "
"beidh rochtain aige ar athróga a sholáthraíonn do phróiseálaithe comhthéacs "
"teimpléad (m.sh. `MEDIA_URL``)."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`DEBUG` is set to ``True`` (in your settings module), then your "
"404 view will never be used, and your URLconf will be displayed instead, "
"with some debug information."
msgstr ""
"Má tá: Socrú: “DEBUG” socraithe go ``True`` (i do mhodúl socruithe), ansin "
"ní úsáidfear do radharc 404 riamh, agus taispeánfar do URLConf ina ionad "
"sin, le roinnt faisnéise dífhabhtaithe."

msgid "The 500 (server error) view"
msgstr "An radharc 500 (earráid freastalaí)"

msgid ""
"Similarly, Django executes special-case behavior in the case of runtime "
"errors in view code. If a view results in an exception, Django will, by "
"default, call the view ``django.views.defaults.server_error``, which either "
"produces a \"Server Error\" message or loads and renders the template "
"``500.html`` if you created it in your root template directory."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, déanann Django iompar cásanna speisialta i gcás "
"earráidí rith sa chód amharc. Má bhíonn eisceacht mar thoradh ar radharc, "
"glaoifidh Django, de réir réamhshocraithe, ar an amharc "
"``django.views.defaults.server_error``, a tháirgeann teachtaireacht “Earráid "
"Freastalaí” nó a luchtaíonn agus a léiríonn an teimpléad ``500.html`` má "
"chruthaigh tú é i d'eolaire teimpléad fréimhe."

msgid ""
"The default 500 view passes no variables to the ``500.html`` template and is "
"rendered with an empty ``Context`` to lessen the chance of additional errors."
msgstr ""
"Ní chuireann an dearcadh réamhshocraithe 500 aon athróg chuig an teimpléad "
"``500.html`` agus déantar é le `Context`` folamh chun an seans go mbeidh "
"earráidí breise a laghdú."

msgid ""
"If :setting:`DEBUG` is set to ``True`` (in your settings module), then your "
"500 view will never be used, and the traceback will be displayed instead, "
"with some debug information."
msgstr ""
"Má tá: Socrú: “DEBUG” socraithe go ``True`` (i do mhodúl socruithe), ansin "
"ní úsáidfear do radharc 500 riamh, agus taispeánfar an rianaireacht ina "
"ionad sin, le roinnt faisnéise dífhabhtaithe."

msgid "The 403 (HTTP Forbidden) view"
msgstr "An radharc 403 (HTTP Toirmiscthe)"

msgid ""
"In the same vein as the 404 and 500 views, Django has a view to handle 403 "
"Forbidden errors. If a view results in a 403 exception then Django will, by "
"default, call the view ``django.views.defaults.permission_denied``."
msgstr ""
"Sa chomh céanna leis na tuairimí 404 agus 500, tá dearcadh ag Django 403 "
"earráid Toirmiscthe a láimhseáil. Má bhíonn eisceacht 403 mar thoradh ar "
"radharc ansin glaoifidh Django, de réir réamhshocraithe, ar an radharc "
"``django.views.defaults.permission_denied``."

msgid ""
"This view loads and renders the template ``403.html`` in your root template "
"directory, or if this file does not exist, instead serves the text \"403 "
"Forbidden\", as per :rfc:`9110#section-15.5.4` (the HTTP 1.1 Specification). "
"The template context contains ``exception``, which is the string "
"representation of the exception that triggered the view."
msgstr ""
"Luchtaíonn agus tugann an radharc seo an teimpléad ``403.html`` i do eolaire "
"teimpléad fréimhe, nó mura bhfuil an comhad seo ann, freastalaíonn an téacs "
"“403 Toirmiscthe” ina ionad sin, mar: rfc: `9110 #section -15.5.4` (an "
"Sonraíocht HTTP 1.1). Tá ``eisceacht' sa chomhthéacs teimpléid, arb é sin an "
"léiriú teaghrán ar an eisceacht a spreag an dearcadh."

msgid ""
"``django.views.defaults.permission_denied`` is triggered by "
"a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied` exception. To deny access "
"in a view you can use code like this::"
msgstr ""
"Tá eisceacht a spreagtar ``django.views.defaults.permission_denied`` ag "
"a:exc: `~django.core.exceptions.permissionDenied`. Chun rochtain a dhiúltú i "
"radharc is féidir leat cód mar seo a úsáid:"

msgid "The 400 (bad request) view"
msgstr "An radharc 400 (droch-iarratas)"

msgid ""
"When a :exc:`~django.core.exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` is raised in "
"Django, it may be handled by a component of Django (for example resetting "
"the session data). If not specifically handled, Django will consider the "
"current request a 'bad request' instead of a server error."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a ardaítear a:exc: `~Django.Core.Exceptions.SuspiciousOperation` i "
"Django, féadfaidh comhpháirt de Django é a láimhseáil (mar shampla sonraí na "
"seisiúin a athshocrú). Mura ndéantar é a láimhseáil go sonrach, measfaidh "
"Django an t-iarratas reatha mar 'droch-iarrat' in ionad earráid freastalaí."

msgid ""
"``django.views.defaults.bad_request``, is otherwise very similar to the "
"``server_error`` view, but returns with the status code 400 indicating that "
"the error condition was the result of a client operation. By default, "
"nothing related to the exception that triggered the view is passed to the "
"template context, as the exception message might contain sensitive "
"information like filesystem paths."
msgstr ""
"Tá ``django.views.defaults.bad_request``, an-chosúil leis an radharc "
"``server_error``, ach filleann sé leis an gcód stádais 400 a léiríonn gurb é "
"an riocht earráide mar thoradh ar oibríocht cliant. De réir réamhshocraithe, "
"ní chuirtear aon rud a bhaineann leis an eisceacht a spreag an dearcadh "
"chuig comhthéacs an teimpléid, toisc go bhféadfadh faisnéis íogair cosúil le "
"cosáin chórais chomhaid a bheith sa teachtai"

msgid ""
"``bad_request`` views are also only used when :setting:`DEBUG` is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Ní úsáidtear tuairimí ``bad_request`` ach amháin nuair:setting: `DEBUG` "
"``False``."
